{"parentUuid":"b0b157cb-e448-4934-b0ec-af4d45b78849","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuiya6USah7sHhjQrtnF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new CI rule conflicts with invariant 8. That invariant, in `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/technical-design/invariants.md`, says the three deployables ship independently and no CI pipeline reaches into another's tree. If deploying the pipeline type-checks `api/`, or deploying the API type-checks `pipeline/`, the pipeline reaches into another tree. Branch 9 already has a change to `common/` run both Workers' type checks, which stays within the invariant because `common/` is shared.\n\nI added the rule to branch 10 as an open leaf, marked with the conflict. Keeping it means amending invariant 8 in both places, and dropping it leaves branch 9 as it is. Tell me which.\n\nI also took the rule as separate from Q16. A type check runs on the code before a deploy. Q16 is about values at runtime, such as a row read back from D1 or a response from Modal, which a type check can't see. Q16 and Q17 stay open."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1068,"cache_read_input_tokens":496801,"output_tokens":391,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":73},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1068,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":496801,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1068},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ad0a00c2-2a6a-4835-a53f-a755db86a8ab","apiBlockIndex":1,"reques