{"parentUuid":"9bf08149-5b00-4a5b-8161-5b92429e8104","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfujFnATNSo8ZGQpdbvzH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":614,"cache_read_input_tokens":514775,"output_tokens":1251,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":614,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":514775,"cache_creation_input_tokens":614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":614},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7137,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"0852783e-2c06-411c-8e4d-d721213334c1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfujFmfSicsDHMecupCAn","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"704579e6-5d39-418e-ac99-827cd4b5380f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:20:35.027Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"704579e6-5d39-418e-ac99-827cd4b5380f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfujFnATNSo8ZGQpdbvzH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The design tree is complete: all ten branches are settled and every leaf is ✓. I've stopped the canvas and saved it in `canvas/design.tldr.json`. The full tree, with each branch's prose and diagrams, is in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/design.md`.\n\n```\nSystem design\n├─ 1 Stored data                     settled\n├─ 2 Components and bindings         settled\n├─ 3 Contracts between deployables   settled\n│  ├─ 3.1 API Worker and item Workflow\n│  └─ 3.2 item Workflow and Modal\n├─ 4 Item lifecycle                  settled\n├─ 5 Item Workflow                   settled\n├─ 6 Image handling                  settled\n├─ 7 Delivery to clients             settled\n├─ 8 Local development               settled\n├─ 9 Deployment and switchover       settled\n└─ 10 The common/ package            settled\n```\n\n## Recording\n\n### Existing notes the change touches\n\nFrom what I read during the session, these notes in `docs/technical-design/` contradict the design:\n\n| Note | What it would need |\n|---|---|\n| `persistence-and-storage.md` | Postgres, SQLite, the ORM and Alembic become D1 with SQL migrations in `common/`. Two buckets and two storage implementations become one R2 bucket with a prefix per type. The item row gains `workflow_instance_id`, `updated_at`, `current_step` and an always-set `status`. The ledger gains `cached`. |\n| `item-lifecycle.md` | The step machine, `queued_at`, `extraction_handle`, `enriched_at` and `modal_call_id` give way to the item Workflow, the step wrapper, the status writes and retry by restarting the instance from `current_step`. |\n| `the-describer.md` | The \"no describer cache\" callout no longer holds, because AI Gateway's cache is on and the ledger records `cached`. Describing an SVG from its markup is new. |\n| `article-extraction.md` | Raster validation moves from Pillow to the Images binding, and SVGs are stored as SVG with scripts stripped. |\n| `recipes.md` | Recipe versions live in D1 and are read by the pipeline. |\n| `invariants.md` + the summary in `CLAUDE.md` | Invariant 5 (BackgroundTasks and `queued_at`), invariant 7 (Alembic) and the Python-only parts of 6 and 8 change. Invariant 8 gains the `common/` type-check rule. |\n\nThese I know only by name, so I don't know what each would need: `deployment-and-ci.md`, `extraction-service.md`, `tts-service.md`, `item-contract.md` and `authentication.md`. The touched set is incomplete. A `mahou:docs-scout` can find every note that refers to Railway, Postgres, Alembic, BackgroundTasks, the job index or the job routes.\n\nFor each note, decide: update it, add the minimum and point to the new note, or skip it.\n\n### New notes\n\nThe design has several parts that no note covers today: the item Workflow with its wrapper, the `common/` package, and local development with the tunnel. Tell me how to split them into notes: one note for the whole migration, one per new part, or another split.\n\nOnce the existing notes and the split are settled, I'll run mahou:write-documentation once with the tree and every amendment."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":614,"cache_read_input_tokens":514775,"output_tokens":1251,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":614,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":514775,"cache_creation_input_tokens":614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":614},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0852783e-2c06-411c-8e4d-d721213334c1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfujFmfSicsDHMecupCAn","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"04603256-bacf-4498-985b-046dcff53ee4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:20:38.504Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
