{"parentUuid":"da322919-85b7-4434-941b-c4e173bec3e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfujXLmvuCBxEj9BVh38o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The scout is running. It's checking every note under `docs/` and the docs sections of `CLAUDE.md` against `design.md`.\n\nYou asked for my view on the split. I think it works, with one point to settle.\n\n**The Workflow and the wrapper in `item-lifecycle.md`.** That fits. The note already covers the four statuses, the routes and the step machine that drives an item. The flattened Workflow replaces that step machine, and the wrapper writes the statuses the note describes.\n\n**What overlaps is `extraction-service.md`.** It describes extraction as a separate service on Cloudflare: the Worker entrypoint with `POST /jobs` and `GET /jobs`, a domain-queue Durable Object, one Workflow per job, the job index and the Flue agents, all called by the Python API through spawn-and-resolve. After the migration there are no job routes, no job index and no Workflow per job. DomainQueue, the recipe runtime and the agents become what the lease and recipe steps call. If `item-lifecycle.md` describes the steps, that note loses its subject as written. It could either:\n- become the note on the pipeline Worker's parts that the steps call: DomainQueue's lease, the recipe runtime and the agents, which `item-lifecycle.md` links to for those steps, or\n- fold into `item-lifecycle.md`.\n\n**`common/` with a note of its own.** Having each part describe its piece and link to that note also fits. The R2 key layout and presigning would sit in `persistence-and-storage.md`, the shared types next to the item contract, and the migrations in deployment.\n\n**Local development in its own note.** Also fits. None of the current notes covers it.\n\nTell me what happens to `extraction-service.md`. I'll bring the scout's list when it reports back."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1287,"cache_read_input_tokens":518197,"output_tokens":811,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":230},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1287,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":811,"cache_read_input_tokens":518197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1287},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9440426b-5ab8-4590-865f-5a1037c74bc0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfujXLCThwEZEG6zVbAL2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c13e83b3-039d-44ed-a4e0-23c345cc6b01","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:24:07.023Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
