{"parentUuid":"12f565e1-eb52-46b3-8be7-b213d1746fa7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfujbgDLVmeVsKYQ9stDx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015tpZovZjbHiQz7oH28Trbp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p13 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); m=d.get('message'); print(m); open('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-impact.md','w').write('# Docs impact (docs-scout, 2026-10-11)\\n\\n'+(m or ''))\"; $H close w30:tR >/dev/null"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":520295,"output_tokens":248,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":422,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":248,"cache_read_input_tokens":520295,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":422},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015tpZovZjbHiQz7oH28Trbp":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p13 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); m=d.get('message'); print(m); open('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-impact.md','w').write('# Docs impact (docs-scout, 2026-10-11)\\n\\n'+(m or ''))\"; $H close w30:tR >/dev/null"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"eb197d2a-6239-4069-8a12-984a1d208f95","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfujbfeMFqBJkCRRmcVeV","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8b18478f-a359-49cf-9cd2-7988f667f1f9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:24:59.683Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"8b18478f-a359-49cf-9cd2-7988f667f1f9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1493d69-5415-4215-94d9-95d05c935d65","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015tpZovZjbHiQz7oH28Trbp","type":"tool_result","content":"done\nAlmost every technical note changes. I found no product-design note that needs a change beyond one stale status list. Paths are under `docs/` unless noted.\n\n## Technical notes\n\n**`technical-design/item-lifecycle.md`** (nearly all of it)\n- Summary and Overview: \"mortal in-process task\", \"every later step runs on poll\".\n- Modeling table: `queued_at`, `extraction_handle`, `enriched_at` and `modal_call_id` go. `updated_at`, `current_step` and `workflow_instance_id` are new. `retry_count` is still capped at 3.\n- States diagram: \"queued, poll … past the ceiling\" and all poll-driven transitions. `generating` now starts when the Workflow holds the lease.\n- \"Enqueue … `advance_queued_item` as a `BackgroundTasks` handler\".\n- \"Poll … advances a `generating` item in place\" and its flowchart.\n- The Flow section: `pipeline.advance`, the step table (FetchStep through StoreStep), the `Fetcher`/`Describer`/`Synthesizer` interface table, and the notes on `enriched_at` and on why the working context copies the row.\n- The whole \"Deferred work is mortal\" section: the ceiling, `_write_if_queued`, \"Why nothing sweeps\".\n- \"Retry resumes from the phase that failed\": the table keyed on units and `enriched_at`, handle re-attach, `queued_at` rewrite, the `modal_call_id` warning, \"Retry does not re-fetch\".\n- The retry-claim note describes a conditional SQL `UPDATE`. The design says the retry route writes `queued`, then restarts the instance.\n- Failure-prefix table (`fetch:`, `extraction:`, `enrichment:`, `spawn:`, `store:`, `tts:`) and \"Stranded work … `enrichment: no result after 300s`\". Error naming now comes from `current_step`.\n- \"Async endpoints over bridged sync libraries\" (`run_in_threadpool`, boto3, firecrawl SDK, `asyncpg`/`aiosqlite`): none of it applies to a TypeScript Worker.\n\n**`technical-design/extraction-service.md`**\n- Summary and Overview: \"called by the API with spawn-and-resolve\", \"separate from the item pipeline\", \"Python API\".\n- Architecture diagram: \"POST /jobs, GET /jobs\", the Index Durable Object, one Workflow per job. The Worker \"owns the HTTP endpoints\" and \"Access authenticates at the edge\".\n- \"What the service exposes\": the `POST /jobs` and `GET /jobs/{job_id}` table, the job state machine (`queued`/`running`/`complete`/`not_article`/`error`) and the `JobStatus` class diagram.\n- \"A job's path\": the sequence diagram, plus \"last step releases the lease … lease alarm\" (the Workflow now has steps lease and release).\n- \"The job index\": the whole section.\n- \"The calling side\": the thin client, the extraction handle, \"Fetching stays API-side\", the 300 s ceiling from `queued_at`, and the \"ceiling can kill an item mid-authoring\" note.\n- \"Platform limits\": the 1 MiB instance-parameter statement, if it assumes HTML as a param.\n- The \"Dynamic Worker\" warning and the runtime and agents sections stay valid.\n\n**`technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md`**\n- Summary and Overview: \"Railway serverless for the API\", three-deployables wording.\n- \"How the API deploys\": the whole section (Railway resources, `railway.toml` table, `preDeployCommand = \"alembic upgrade head\"`, dashboard-only Root Directory and Watch Paths, the DNS-only CNAME and port-8080 warnings, the rejected-PaaS tip).\n- \"How the extraction service deploys\": the Access warning and the API holding the token's halves.\n- CI: the diagram and \"three independent, path-filtered pipelines\". The `api` workflow gains a deploy, there is a new `common/` job, and the order is migrations, pipeline, API.\n- \"Two deploy models coexist by design\".\n- \"What is not built yet\": \"`web/` and `api/` are served from separate hosts\" may need a recheck.\n\n**`technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md`**\n- Summary and Overview: \"ORM row\", \"Alembic\", \"the two backends … selected from configuration\".\n- Modeling: \"SQLAlchemy ORM row … SQLite and Postgres\".\n- The Alembic section: \"applied before the app serves (Railway's pre-deploy step)\", the autogenerate-check note, the SQLite cross-thread and Postgres `NullPool` paragraph, \"The store swaps by connection string\", and \"Rejected: Postgres everywhere\".\n- Storage: `StorageBase` with the boto3 client, the `s3_configured` row, \"four S3 settings\", and the \"half-supplied credential set\" warning. Local file stores become local R2.\n- Image keying by \"content hash of the re-encoded WebP bytes\". The design keys SVGs by hash too.\n- \"Serving audio and an image\": `FileResponse` locally, the `image_dir` diagram, and `s3_url_ttl`. The 1 h presigned GET is now signed by the API Worker.\n- Ledger: add the `cached` flag and describe cache-hit rows. The three-point commit table (\"`tts` rides the finalize-to-`ready` write\") changes, and so does \"Prices … on `Settings`\".\n- Ledger `type` map (`CostType` `Literal`) is Python.\n- \"Audio caching … not built yet\" is unaffected.\n\n**`technical-design/item-contract.md`**\n- \"pydantic discriminated union\" and \"persisted `Unit`\": the shapes move to TypeScript types in `common/`.\n- Route table: `POST /items` (\"a background task then fetches\"), `GET /items/{id}` (\"Advances a `generating` item … Fails a `queued` item … once its work age has passed the ceiling\"), and the audio and image rows (\"a file locally, a short-lived presigned URL in the bucket\").\n- \"Poll persists the units when the extraction job resolves\" and the \"units null until timed\" note. Recheck against the Workflow's store step.\n- \"Image serving\" and \"Why the backends are allowed to disagree\": the 404 asymmetry (file locally, store 404 in the bucket) no longer exists, because local is R2 too.\n- \"The `url` string … `fetch: no response`\" prefix.\n- \"Retry\": \"rewrites `queued_at`, advances `retry_count`\", the conditional-`UPDATE` note, and \"two Modal spawns\".\n- Voice selection path `api/app/service/tts.py`.\n\n**`technical-design/authentication.md`**\n- `require_key` as a FastAPI dependency and the Python snippet `settings.api_key`.\n- \"in development it streams the local file directly\" and the sequence diagram's \"bytes (dev)\": audio is a 307 in both environments.\n- The `?key=` and \"mints one only for a `ready` item\" wording needs a check against the design.\n\n**`technical-design/tts-service.md`**\n- Summary and \"spawn, persist the handle, resolve lazily\".\n- \"What it exposes\": `synthesize(paragraphs, voice)` returning `audio_base64`. The design adds two web endpoints with proxy auth and a destination URL, and the result drops the audio bytes.\n- Flow: \"return audio_base64 + timeline\", and the \"Opus, WAV fallback\" encode path is unchanged except for the upload.\n- \"How the API invokes it\": `modal.Cls.from_name(...).spawn`, persisting `object_id`, `fc.get(timeout=0)`, and the notes \"compute platform is the async layer, no broker\", \"Rejected: a broker\" and \"Clients poll; the API never pushes\".\n- \"The API's item-contract models the return shape as `SynthesisResult`\" now names a `common/` type.\n\n**`technical-design/article-extraction.md`**\n- Summary and Overview: \"the API fetches … hands it to the extraction service … when the job resolves\".\n- \"Fetching the page\": the firecrawl scrape is now the Workflow's own fetch client, the `Fetcher` interface and \"API writes what each scrape bills\" change, and \"`proxy=\"auto\"`\" stays only if the call fields are unchanged.\n- The `fetch:` prefix.\n- \"The extraction step runs … on the poll that resolves a `complete` job\", step 8, and \"Why the display list is persisted\" (\"when the job resolves\").\n- Acquisition: \"Pillow\", \"re-encoded to WebP\", \"10 MB cap … per-host semaphore\", and \"SVG … rasterised to PNG at 768 px … 200 px filter does not apply\". Rasters go through the Images binding, and SVGs stay SVG with scripts stripped.\n- The `cairosvg` warning and `RAILPACK_DEPLOY_APT_PACKAGES`: delete.\n- \"An image that … fails SVG rasterisation is dropped\" and \"svg rasterise failed\" (also in persistence's degradation table).\n- \"The API derives it\": `api/app/service/extract.py` moves to TypeScript, which also affects CLAUDE.md's \"When adding something\".\n\n**`technical-design/the-describer.md`**\n- \"`gemini-3.5-flash-lite` on Google's paid API (never through a gateway)\": now AI Gateway with the response cache.\n- \"`ImageDescribeRequest` … the WebP `image` bytes\": SVG now goes as `text/plain` markup, with no size cap.\n- Python-specific parts: `asyncio.gather`, `Semaphore`, `NAGARA_DESCRIBE_CONCURRENCY`, `stamina`, google-genai, `_RETRY_STATUS`. The Workflow step retry (3 attempts, 5 min) replaces them.\n- The `NAGARA_GEMINI_API_KEY` warning mentions \"the Railway dashboard\".\n- `on_describe` callback \"one `describer` cost entry\": add the cached flag.\n- \"No describer cache\": now false.\n- The cap of 25 and per-unit degradation rules hold.\n\n**`technical-design/recipes.md`**\n- ER diagram: `extraction_handle` is gone from `ITEM`.\n- \"in the item database alongside the items\": D1.\n- \"The item pipeline\" actor, \"The recipe store\" and \"Insert as the new highest version\" need a recheck for who writes the version. The Workflow writes recipe versions in D1.\n- \"the API drops a unit whose spoken form has no letter or digit\" and the \"Firecrawl's rawHtml … The fetch\" provenance table.\n\n**`technical-design/invariants.md`**\n- Rows 5 (\"API never imports TTS … `BackgroundTasks` handler … `queued_at` ceiling\"), 6 (verify), 7 (\"autogenerate check\", Alembic), 8 (\"Railway watch paths\") and 10 (check \"the workflow\"). Overview and Related are fine.\n\n## Notes checked, no change\n`technical-design/README.md` needs changes only to its index summaries (item-lifecycle, extraction-service, persistence, deployment rows, \"Reading order\" item 1) and the invariants count. `technical-design/read-along-timing.md`, `technical-design/markdown-units.md`, `product-design/what-nagara-is.md`, `product-design/listening-experience.md`, `product-design/what-gets-read-aloud.md` and `_templates/note.md` need nothing. `README.md` (the charter) needs nothing. `product-design/queue.md` line 26 lists three states, while the design's poll route has four. That was already stale before this design.\n\n## CLAUDE.md (project)\n- Layout table: `api/` row (\"The queue API: … single-key auth\"), `pipeline/` row (\"one Worker routing the job endpoints … singleton job index … one Workflow per job\"), and `common/` is missing.\n- Commands block: the `api/` line (`uv sync · alembic · uvicorn · pytest · ruff · ty`) becomes pnpm and wrangler. Add `common/` and the vite dev plus wrangler dev plus tunnel flow.\n- \"Both `api/` and `tts/` are pinned to Python 3.12\": only `tts/` now.\n- CI paragraph: \"`api/` auto-deploys … via Railway's connected source: two dashboard-only Railway settings\". New order is common migrations, pipeline, API. Also the `deployment-and-ci` pointer.\n- Invariants 5 (API Worker, `BackgroundTasks`, `queued_at` ceiling), 7 (Alembic) and 8 (check). 6 and 10 hold.\n- Code style: \"pydantic\" for payloads (the design makes shared types compile-time only, departing from the style rule), and \"`api/app/` is `models` / `schemas` / `service` / `endpoints`\".\n- \"When adding something\": \"endpoint module + a pydantic schema\", the `api/app/service/extract.py` spoken-form bullet, and \"A change to the item JSON … a migration … `Item.units` is a `JSON` column\" (now a hand-written SQL migration in `common/`).\n- Checks line (`uv run pytest · ruff · ty` for `api/`/`tts/`): `api/` is no longer uv. \"Seeing it work\" holds.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8cf68fb1-488f-4c82-83cf-0a2f60b9d4a3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:25:00.890Z","toolUseResu