{"parentUuid":"38a58b2f-e705-4c75-b078-02ed048434c5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfujk8pDE6bbudeKPLnF3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013oTQpXPRhmNK9Dq2vTYoHQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts; cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; cat > briefs/docs-common.md <<'EOF'\n## How to work (shared by every docs drafter)\n\nYou draft updates to nagara's documentation for the Cloudflare migration. You write drafts only; you never edit anything under /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs or CLAUDE.md, and you commit nothing.\n\nRead first, in this order:\n1. /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/README.md (the charter: naming, frontmatter, callouts, house style, emoji headings, no hard wrapping, `---` then a `Related:` line at the end).\n2. /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/_templates/note.md (the section menu).\n3. /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/README.md (the folder index).\n4. /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/design.md: the settled design tree with each branch's prose and mermaid diagrams. It is the source of truth for what the system is after the migration. Most of the new text is this prose moved into place and fitted to the note.\n5. /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-impact.md: a scout's list of which statements in each note no longer hold.\n6. The notes you are assigned.\n\nRules for the content:\n- A note explains how a part works, in the present tense. Overview first, then the mechanism. Reasoning goes in `> [!NOTE]`, `> [!WARNING]` or `> [!TIP]` callouts beside the mechanism it justifies.\n- Change only what changed. A section that still describes the system correctly stays exactly as it is, word for word. Delete behaviour that is gone; never annotate it as removed. No \"used to\", \"previously\", \"no longer\", \"replaced by\", \"now\", \"migrated\", \"instead of Railway\". No sentence compares the design with how things worked before the migration. Railway, Postgres, Alembic, SQLAlchemy, FastAPI, BackgroundTasks, boto3, Pillow, cairosvg, the job index and the job routes are not mentioned unless a callout explains a choice against them (\"considered and not chosen, because…\").\n- Name roles rather than products where the design is generic; Cloudflare's products (Workers, Workflows, D1, R2, Durable Objects, AI Gateway, the Images binding), Modal, Firecrawl and Gemini are the actual platform and are named.\n- Explain the code, do not reprint it: tables for surfaces, prose or mermaid for behaviour, snippets only of two to four lines where the code is the insight. There is no code yet for the new parts, so write no snippets for them.\n- Every mermaid diagram must validate: pipe each block through `bash /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/superpowers/skills/mermaid-validation/scripts/validate-mermaid.sh` and fix until valid. Text inside a flowchart node, a state note or an entity box is clipped past about 24 characters per line: break with `<br/>`. Never put `;` in state diagram text. Keep sequence-diagram messages plain (no braces, no `<br/>`).\n- Fixed names across all notes: the API Worker (in api/), the pipeline Worker (in pipeline/), the item Workflow, the step wrapper, DomainQueue, the recipe runtime, the Flue author and revision agents, the common/ package, D1, the R2 bucket with its audio/ and images/ prefixes. New and renamed notes, use these exact file names in links: `technical-design/common-package.md` (\"The common/ package\"), `technical-design/local-development.md` (\"Local development\"), `technical-design/image-and-code-describer.md` (\"Image and code describer\", the renamed the-describer.md). `technical-design/extraction-service.md` is deleted: its still-valid content (DomainQueue's lease, the recipe runtime, the Dynamic Worker warning, the Flue agents) moves into item-lifecycle.md, so links to extraction-service.md point to item-lifecycle.md instead. Links to the-describer.md point to image-and-code-describer.md.\n- Each part that uses a piece of common/ describes that piece where it is used and links to common-package.md.\n- Shared types are checked when the code builds, not at runtime; this departs from CLAUDE.md's code-style rule about pydantic, and CLAUDE.md's code style is updated to the TypeScript equivalent of the rule as the design settles it.\n\nOutput, for each assigned note, two files in /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/:\n- `<file-name>.md`: the complete note as it will read after your edits (for CLAUDE.md, name it `CLAUDE.md`).\n- `<file-name>.edits.md`: the edits in this exact form, and nothing else: for an updated note, one line of prose per edit naming where it lands, using the section names as they read in the note (\"Replace the Overview:\", \"Replace the second paragraph of <section>:\", \"New section before <section>:\", \"Delete the section <section>.\", \"<table>, <row>, <column>:\"), followed by the edit exactly as it will read in the file, headings and mermaid blocks included; for a new note, the whole note with no location lines.\n\nThen run an editing pass over your own new and changed prose against these rules: no em dashes, colons only before lists or examples, no \"serves as / stands as / features\", no filler (\"in order to\", \"it is important to note\"), active voice with the actor named, no restating a sentence, no metaphors or figurative verbs, no \"not X but Y\" framing, pronouns that resolve to one thing. Fix what you find.\n\nReply with: the files you wrote, and any point where design.md left you unsure what to write (as a question; do not invent the answer). Under 250 words.\nEOF\nspawn() { local label=$1 f=$2 notes=$3; { echo \"<supervisor-agent>\"; cat briefs/docs-common.md; echo; echo \"## Your assignment\"; echo; echo \"$notes\"; echo \"</supervisor-agent>\"; } > briefs/$f; /home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper spawn --kind claude --label \"$label\" --model opus --body-file briefs/$f; }\nspawn \"docs: item lifecycle\" docs-1.md \"docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md, folding in the still-valid parts of docs/technical-design/extraction-service.md (read it; do not draft a replacement for it, it is deleted). item-lifecycle.md becomes the note on how an item moves from enqueue to ready or failed: the statuses (branch 4), the item Workflow and its nine steps with the step wrapper (branch 5), DomainQueue's lease, the recipe runtime with its Dynamic Worker warning, the Flue agents, retry from current_step, and the failure handling. Keep its existing sections that still hold.\"\nspawn \"docs: storage contract auth\" docs-2.md \"docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md (branches 1 and 7, the ledger), docs/technical-design/item-contract.md (routes unchanged for clients; shapes in common/; retry; image serving), docs/technical-design/authentication.md (key on every item route; audio and images are a 307 in every environment).\"\nspawn \"docs: deploy invariants claude\" docs-3.md \"docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md (branch 9 and the common/ CI rule from branch 10), docs/technical-design/invariants.md (invariants 5, 7 and 8 change; check 6 and 10), the technical-design/README.md index (rows for the new, renamed and deleted notes, summaries, reading order, invariants count), docs/product-design/queue.md (its status list: four statuses), and /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/CLAUDE.md (layout table with common/, commands, Python pinning, the CI paragraph, the invariants summary, code style, When adding something, Docs checks). Keep CLAUDE.md's invariants and invariants.md in agreement.\"\nspawn \"docs: tts extraction recipes describer\" docs-4.md \"docs/technical-design/tts-service.md (branch 3.2: two web endpoints, proxy auth, destination URL, result without audio bytes, polled by the item Workflow), docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md (fetch inside the item Workflow, images through the Images binding, SVG kept with scripts stripped, branch 6), docs/technical-design/recipes.md (recipes in D1, written by the item Workflow), and the-describer.md renamed: draft it as image-and-code-describer.md titled 'Image and code describer' (AI Gateway with its response cache, SVG markup as text/plain, the cached ledger flag, the step's retries; the budget and per-unit rules stay).\"\nspawn \"docs: new notes\" docs-5.md \"Two new notes. technical-design/common-package.md, 'The common/ package', from branch 10: what it holds, who uses each piece (each piece's detail lives in the note of the part that uses it; link to those notes: persistence-and-storage, item-contract, item-lifecycle, deployment-and-ci), the build-time type check and the CI rule. technical-design/local-development.md, 'Local development', from branch 8, with its diagram. Set created to 2026-10-11.\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3109,"cache_read_input_tokens":529957,"output_tokens":3496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":202},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3109,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3496,"cache_read_input_tokens":529957,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3109},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013oTQpXPRhmNK9Dq2vTYoHQ":{"command":"mk