{"parentUuid":"38697e37-0ec9-4f8c-896e-11d88b6f58c5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfukikiWpP33F6R8ogW92","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0143HDQBJPuxPEcdA43ZwhtN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins; ls mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/references 2>/dev/null; sed -n 1,60p mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md; grep -n \"top of\\|Questions go\\|opening tree\\|pending, with no\" mahou/skills/*-with-canvas/SKILL.md; sed -n 80,140p mahou/skills/canvas/scripts/canvas.sh; ls superpowers/skills/mermaid-validation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2285,"cache_read_input_tokens":544517,"output_tokens":1226,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":981},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2285,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1226,"cache_read_input_tokens":544517,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2285},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0143HDQBJPuxPEcdA43ZwhtN":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins; ls mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/references 2>/dev/null; sed -n 1,60p mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md; grep -n \"top of\\|Questions go\\|opening tree\\|pending, with no\" mahou/skills/*-with-canvas/SKILL.md; sed -n 80,140p mahou/skills/canvas/scripts/canvas.sh; ls superpowers/skills/mermaid-validation"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5665a206-b5b4-456f-9a27-511daf2c3cdf","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfukie1CQ4EtYGafMc7fd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7660fd9-11ba-45c8-bc41-ebb26227659c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:39:55.290Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"d7660fd9-11ba-45c8-bc41-ebb26227659c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f67a4013-5f46-42cd-af28-2ccfd43d035b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0143HDQBJPuxPEcdA43ZwhtN","type":"tool_result","content":"mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas:\nmockups\nreferences\nSKILL.md\n\nmahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/references:\nrepresentations\n---\nname: program-design-with-canvas\ndescription: Runs the program-design skill on a canvas. Each part of a branch (screen layout, component tree, state) is drawn on the canvas for the user to correct, while the record file keeps the text representation. Use when the user wants to work a program design on a canvas.\nargument-hint: <the scope or change to program-design>\n---\n\nLoad mahou:program-design first, then mahou:canvas. Then read `.mahou/program-design-with-canvas.md` if present.\n\n# Program design with canvas\n\n`program-design` and the skills it loads keep their opening, tree, branch order, parts, standards, record and ending.\n\nThe document is `canvas/<name>.tldr.json` in the change's scratch folder, named after what the program design covers, such as `settings-screen.tldr.json`. The record stays `program-design/<root>.md`. Each time a part settles on the canvas, write it into the record in the text representation from `program-design`'s references.\n\n## The canvas\n\n- **The tree goes at the top**, in monospace text, with `design-tree`'s marks. Update it whenever you propose a part or the user settles one.\n- **Each part gets its own `area`**, labelled `<root> · <branch> · <n> <part> · <status>`, with the status `proposed` or `settled`. A new part goes under the previous one. A settled part stays on the canvas.\n- **Draw each part as its reference under `references/representations/` describes.** Work out a part with no canvas reference with the user before drawing it.\n\nEach canvas reference describes how to draw one of `program-design`'s representations, and has the same file name as that representation's reference under `program-design/references/representations/`:\n\n| The part | `program-design` reference | Canvas reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| Screen layout | `screen-layout.md` | `references/representations/screen-layout.md` |\n| Component tree | `component-tree.md` | `references/representations/component-tree.md` |\n| State, as a derivation ledger | `derivation-ledger.md` | `references/representations/derivation-ledger.md` |\n\n## Mockups\n\nThe canvas references use the mockups in this skill's `mockups/` folder: `screen-wireframe`, `component-cards`, `state-card` and `hook-card`. Before drawing a part, copy the mockups it uses into the canvas folder's `mockups/`, unless they are already there. Each file's props are its `data`.\nmahou/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md:27:The opening tree goes on the canvas as the branch areas, each one pending, with no leaves yet. A branch's opening statement goes on the canvas as its leaves and its prose. When a branch settles, draw its representation and prose in its section and ask the user to approve it there.\nmahou/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md:31:Questions go in the open branch, at the top of its right side, above its write-up.\nmahou/skills/shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md:17:The root goes at the top of the canvas as a title, `Problem: <one line>`. Each top-level branch is an `area` labelled `<n> <title> · <status>`, and Out of scope is always the last one.\nmahou/skills/shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md:27:The opening tree goes on the canvas as the branch areas, each one pending, with the ✓ leaves the user brought under their areas and no prose yet. When a branch opens, its statement of what is settled goes on the canvas as its prose. When a branch settles, ask the user to approve it there.\nmahou/skills/shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md:33:Questions go in the open branch, at the top of its right side, above its prose.\n  if [[ -n \"$current\" ]]; then\n    echo \"stopping the canvas for $current\" >&2\n    stop\n  fi\n\n  if curl -s -o /dev/null \"$URL\"; then\n    echo \"port $PORT is taken by another server; set CANVAS_PORT to use another port\" >&2\n    exit 1\n  fi\n\n  # An older document would be served in a format the app no longer reads, and its edits saved over it\n  if ! document_cli check; then\n    exit 1\n  fi\n\n  scaffold\n\n  # Detached, so the server outlives the shell that started it and any background time limit\n  CANVAS_DOC=\"$DOC\" setsid nohup \"$APP/node_modules/.bin/vite\" --config \"$APP/vite.config.ts\" --port \"$PORT\" --strictPort \\\n    >\"$CACHE/server.log\" 2>&1 </dev/null &\n  echo $! >\"$PID_FILE\"\n\n  for _ in $(seq 60); do\n    [[ \"$(serving)\" == \"$DOC\" ]] && { echo \"$URL\"; return; }\n    sleep 0.5\n  done\n\n  echo \"the server did not come up; its log is $CACHE/server.log\" >&2\n  exit 1\n}\n\ncase \"$COMMAND\" in\n  start)\n    start\n    ;;\n  watch)\n    start >/dev/null\n    curl -sN \"$URL/api/events\" | sed -u -n 's/^data: //p'\n    ;;\n  export)\n    start >/dev/null\n    # Its own browser session, so the export leaves Claude's open tab alone\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export open \"$URL?user=export\" >/dev/null\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export wait --fn \"window.editor != null\" >/dev/null\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export eval \"(async () => { await document.fonts.ready; const e = window.editor; e.selectNone(); const r = await e.getSvgString([...e.getCurrentPageShapeIds()], { background: true, padding: 64 }); return await fetch('/api/export', { method: 'POST', body: r.svg }).then((response) => response.text()) })()\"\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export close >/dev/null\n    ;;\n  texts)\n    document_cli texts\n    ;;\n  migrate)\n    if [[ \"$(serving)\" == \"$DOC\" ]]; then\n      echo \"stop the canvas before migrating its document\" >&2\n      exit 1\n    fi\n\n    document_cli migrate\n    ;;\n  stop)\n    stop\n    ;;\nscripts\nSKILL.md\nShell cwd was reset to /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0fefc05d-3784-4f48-b13e-34238ba7be76","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:39:55.903Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas:\nmockups\nreferences\nSKILL.md\n\nmahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/references:\nrepresentations\n---\nname: program-design-with-canvas\ndescription: Runs the program-design skill on a canvas. Each part of a branch (screen layout, component tree, state) is drawn on the canvas for the user to correct, while the record file keeps the text representation. Use when the user wants to work a program design on a canvas.\nargument-hint: <the scope or change to program-design>\n---\n\nLoad mahou:program-design first, then mahou:canvas. Then read `.mahou/program-design-with-canvas.md` if present.\n\n# Program design with canvas\n\n`program-design` and the skills it loads keep their opening, tree, branch order, parts, standards, record and ending.\n\nThe document is `canvas/<name>.tldr.json` in the change's scratch folder, named after what the program design covers, such as `settings-screen.tldr.json`. The record stays `program-design/<root>.md`. Each time a part settles on the canvas, write it into the record in the text representation from `program-design`'s references.\n\n## The canvas\n\n- **The tree goes at the top**, in monospace text, with `design-tree`'s marks. Update it whenever you propose a part or the user settles one.\n- **Each part gets its own `area`**, labelled `<root> · <branch> · <n> <part> · <status>`, with the status `proposed` or `settled`. A new part goes under the previous one. A settled part stays on the canvas.\n- **Draw each part as its reference under `references/representations/` describes.** Work out a part with no canvas reference with the user before drawing it.\n\nEach canvas reference describes how to draw one of `program-design`'s representations, and has the same file name as that representation's reference under `program-design/references/representations/`:\n\n| The part | `program-design` reference | Canvas reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| Screen layout | `screen-layout.md` | `references/representations/screen-layout.md` |\n| Component tree | `component-tree.md` | `references/representations/component-tree.md` |\n| State, as a derivation ledger | `derivation-ledger.md` | `references/representations/derivation-ledger.md` |\n\n## Mockups\n\nThe canvas references use the mockups in this skill's `mockups/` folder: `screen-wireframe`, `component-cards`, `state-card` and `hook-card`. Before drawing a part, copy the mockups it uses into the canvas folder's `mockups/`, unless they are already there. Each file's props are its `data`.\nmahou/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md:27:The opening tree goes on the canvas as the branch areas, each one pending, with no leaves yet. A branch's opening statement goes on the canvas as its leaves and its prose. When a branch settles, draw its representation and prose in its section and ask the user to approve it there.\nmahou/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md:31:Questions go in the open branch, at the top of its right side, above its write-up.\nmahou/skills/shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md:17:The root goes at the top of the canvas as a title, `Problem: <one line>`. Each top-level branch is an `area` labelled `<n> <title> · <status>`, and Out of scope is always the last one.\nmahou/skills/shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md:27:The opening tree goes on the canvas as the branch areas, each one pending, with the ✓ leaves the user brought under their areas and no prose yet. When a branch opens, its statement of what is settled goes on the canvas as its prose. When a branch settles, ask the user to approve it there.\nmahou/skills/shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md:33:Questions go in the open branch, at the top of its right side, above its prose.\n  if [[ -n \"$current\" ]]; then\n    echo \"stopping the canvas for $current\" >&2\n    stop\n  fi\n\n  if curl -s -o /dev/null \"$URL\"; then\n    echo \"port $PORT is taken by another server; set CANVAS_PORT to use another port\" >&2\n    exit 1\n  fi\n\n  # An older document would be served in a format the app no longer reads, and its edits saved over it\n  if ! document_cli check; then\n    exit 1\n  fi\n\n  scaffold\n\n  # Detached, so the server outlives the shell that started it and any background time limit\n  CANVAS_DOC=\"$DOC\" setsid nohup \"$APP/node_modules/.bin/vite\" --config \"$APP/vite.config.ts\" --port \"$PORT\" --strictPort \\\n    >\"$CACHE/server.log\" 2>&1 </dev/null &\n  echo $! >\"$PID_FILE\"\n\n  for _ in $(seq 60); do\n    [[ \"$(serving)\" == \"$DOC\" ]] && { echo \"$URL\"; return; }\n    sleep 0.5\n  done\n\n  echo \"the server did not come up; its log is $CACHE/server.log\" >&2\n  exit 1\n}\n\ncase \"$COMMAND\" in\n  start)\n    start\n    ;;\n  watch)\n    start >/dev/null\n    curl -sN \"$URL/api/events\" | sed -u -n 's/^data: //p'\n    ;;\n  export)\n    start >/dev/null\n    # Its own browser session, so the export leaves Claude's open tab alone\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export open \"$URL?user=export\" >/dev/null\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export wait --fn \"window.editor != null\" >/dev/null\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export eval \"(async () => { await document.fonts.ready; const e = window.editor; e.selectNone(); const r = await e.getSvgString([...e.getCurrentPageShapeIds()], { background: true, padding: 64 }); return await fetch('/api/export', { method: 'POST', body: r.svg }).then((response) => response.text()) })()\"\n    agent-browser --session canvas-export close >/dev/null\n    ;;\n  texts)\n    document_cli texts\n    ;;\n  migrate)\n    if [[ \"$(serving)\" == \"$DOC\" ]]; then\n      echo \"stop the canvas before migrating its document\" >&2\n      exit 1\n    fi\n\n    document_cli migrate\n    ;;\n  stop)\n    stop\n    ;;\nscripts\nSKILL.md","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","interrupted"