{"parentUuid":"3fd4109c-7d6d-4705-b511-799231c9ccbb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfukkySYh7o3sydMwf8G6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"These are the items you kept, each with what it does and where it lands. Correct anything I've read wrong before I draft.\n\n1. **Several canvases at once.** Each document gets its own server on its own port, the first free one from 5190 up. The server's PID is tracked per document, and start, watch, export and stop act only on that document's server. This drops \"one server runs at a time\".\n   - Lands in: `canvas/scripts/canvas.sh` and its section in `canvas/SKILL.md`. Global.\n2. **Default font.** Every text on the canvas uses tldraw's default font, the hand font. That includes prose, Claude notes and question cards. Monospace is kept only where a skill asks for it, such as the leaves.\n   - Lands in: `canvas/SKILL.md`, Drawing. Global.\n3. **Stale `growY`.** After a script sets a geo shape's `h`, tldraw doesn't recompute `growY`. So set `growY: 0` together with `h`, and measure the label's height from its DOM element before stacking shapes inside it.\n   - Lands in: `canvas/SKILL.md`. Global.\n4. **Questions under the write-up.** Question cards go under the branch's prose, not at the top of the right side.\n   - Lands in: `design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`.\n5. **Explaining the opening tree.** Each pending area in the opening tree carries one line on what the branch settles.\n   - Lands in: `design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`.\n6. **Proposing an obvious answer.** When a decision has one plausible answer, propose it and ask the user to confirm. That covers an answer that follows from decisions already settled, or from how the code already works. It's an exception to rule 2.\n   - Lands in: `basics/SKILL.md` rule 2, plus the question rules in `design-tree/SKILL.md`, where the proposal needs a form.\n   - Draft wording for rule 2: \"When a decision follows from what is already settled, or from how the code already works, so that only one answer is plausible, propose that answer and ask the user to confirm it instead of asking the question open.\"\n   - In design-tree, a proposed answer would sit in the tree as a leaf marked as proposed. It stays proposed until the user confirms it.\n7. **Contract representation and canvas references.**\n   - Change `design/references/types/contract.md`'s representation to the form the session settled: one mermaid flowchart per member. The call is a solid arrow through a braces box with the interface it sends, giving each field's name, type and meaning. The return is a dashed arrow through a braces box with the interface returned.\n   - Add `design-with-canvas/references/types/`, shaped like program-design-with-canvas: a table in `design-with-canvas/SKILL.md` mapping a design type to its canvas reference. The first reference is `contract.md`.\n8. **Colours and shapes per kind in mermaid.** The palette is blue rectangle for the API, green for the pipeline's parts with the Workflow as a framed rectangle, orange cylinders for stores, violet clouds for outside services, a grey pill for the client and amber braces for interfaces. Each kind is styled with `classDef` and drawn with an `@{ shape: … }`.\n9. **Mermaid rendering problems.**\n   - In general: after a diagram validates, render it and look at the image before showing it, because a diagram that parses can still draw wrong.\n   - Add to the list of rendering rules the validator can't catch:\n     - a `;` inside state-diagram text ends the statement\n     - markdown inside an `@{ label }` draws as plain text\n     - a subgraph's `direction` is ignored when edges cross its border, so set the layout direction on the whole flowchart\n   - Specific to the canvas: its mermaid shape draws sequence diagrams with labels out of place. That one goes in `canvas/SKILL.md`, where the mermaid kind is described.\n10. **Workflows facts.** Add the restart-resolve and researcher facts to `cloudflare/workflows.md`:\n    - `restart()` resolves on acceptance, then about 3.4 s pass before the step starts.\n    - `restart()` with no arguments runs every step again.\n    - No step hook exists, and code outside a step runs again on resume.\n    - `wrangler delete` leaves the Workflow behind.\n    - The REST API needs a token.\n\n    These are global.\n\nOpen questions:\n\n- **Items 4 and 5:** shape-with-canvas has the same rule as item 4, cards \"at the top of its right side, above its prose\", and the same pending-areas opening as item 5. Do these changes apply to shape-with-canvas too, or only to design-with-canvas?\n- **Item 7:** you said \"adjust the existing design types\", plural. Does any type besides contract change? The session also drew data flows (branches 2, 7 and 8), a lifecycle (4) and rules (6) in the coloured style.\n- **Item 8:** does the palette go in superpowers:mermaid-validation, in a new skill about drawing diagrams, or somewhere else? Is it the same palette in every project, or a pattern of one colour and shape per kind with this palette as the example?\n- **Item 9:** do the general rule and the three rendering problems go in superpowers:mermaid-validation's \"Rendering rules the validator cannot catch\", or with item 8 wherever that lands?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1301,"cache_read_input_tokens":550191,"output_tokens":1790,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":19},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1301,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1790,"cache_read_input_tokens":550191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1301},"type":"message"}]