{"parentUuid":"e0e0e93d-3049-4708-9714-4cbdef0c612c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfukshqsy4rJMnuiXx2Gk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012uGZ2wZd6t6dZ5C45Ga3bS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; for p in w30:p14 w30:p15 w30:p16 w30:p17 w30:p18; do echo \"=== $p\"; $H collect $p | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['label'], d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\"; done; ls /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":553282,"output_tokens":238,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":238,"cache_read_input_tokens":553282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012uGZ2wZd6t6dZ5C45Ga3bS":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; for p in w30:p14 w30:p15 w30:p16 w30:p17 w30:p18; do echo \"=== $p\"; $H collect $p | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['label'], d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\"; done; ls /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e1cb2d8a-1cac-4214-9718-37b54e22d01d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfuksgv4fqTbzK2LmtTjq","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"66862c01-38db-4dda-bcbd-fae15dffd922","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:41:44.132Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"66862c01-38db-4dda-bcbd-fae15dffd922","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"98a2819c-5e51-4d39-816d-1a07b6b12f77","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012uGZ2wZd6t6dZ5C45Ga3bS","type":"tool_result","content":"=== w30:p14\ndocs: item lifecycle idle\nI wrote the `item-lifecycle.md` draft and its edits file. The three mermaid diagrams pass the validator, and I ran the editing pass over the new prose.\n\n**Files** (in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`):\n- `item-lifecycle.md`\n- `item-lifecycle.edits.md`\n\nThe kept parts of extraction-service.md are DomainQueue's lease and alarm, the recipe runtime with its Dynamic Worker warning, the Flue agents, and the platform limits. Four sections are deleted: Flow, \"Deferred work is mortal\", \"Async endpoints\" and the failure-prefix table.\n\n**Questions where design.md left me unsure:**\n1. Does a failed item's `error` still start with a phase prefix (`fetch:`, `extraction:`…), or does `current_step` replace the prefix? I left prefixes out.\n2. Does a restarted step read the earlier steps' results, such as the fetched HTML and the units? I assumed it does, in a NOTE callout (\"Why fetch's output is a step result and not a column\") and in the retry section. Please confirm.\n3. Branch 5 says \"keep today's handling\" for a retry from lease or earlier while an earlier attempt still holds the lease. What is that handling? I described only the alarm sweeping the lease of an ended instance.\n4. What is an agent conversation keyed by: the item id, or the instance id? And is a retry's conversation still a fresh one under a suffixed id? I wrote \"a conversation of its own\".\n5. Does the lease step's 3 × 1 h limit fail an item that waits too long behind its domain? I wrote that it does.\n6. Does a not-article verdict skip the step's retries? I wrote only that the recipe step fails the item.\n=== w30:p15\ndocs: storage contract auth idle\nI wrote all three drafts and their edit files in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`: `persistence-and-storage.md`, `item-contract.md` and `authentication.md`, each with its `.edits.md`. Every mermaid block passes the validator, and I ran the editing pass over the new prose. Where design.md is silent I kept wording that commits to as little as possible. These points need a decision:\n\n1. **Ledger `tts` row:** which step writes it? I put \"the store step\"; design.md only says each step that makes a metered call writes its own row.\n2. **Prices:** where are they configured in the pipeline Worker? I wrote only \"Prices are configuration per invariant 6\".\n3. **Image hash:** is it taken over the stored bytes (the WebP, or the SVG after its scripts are stripped)? I wrote \"the stored bytes\".\n4. **Double-submitted retry:** does the retry route still claim the item with one conditional `UPDATE` (status still `failed`, count under the cap)? I kept that callout and only changed its cost to \"restarts one instance twice\".\n5. **`retry_count`:** I assumed the retry route still increments it alongside writing `queued`. Is that right?\n6. **Error text:** the `fetch: no response` error string came out. Do errors keep a prefix, maybe derived from `current_step`, or is it the step's raw error?\n7. **Tests and the schema:** do the Workers' tests apply common/'s migrations, or build the schema some other way? I deleted the test-schema warning and wrote nothing in its place.\n8. **Units before `ready`:** I wrote that the units first reach the row with the finished state, going by branch 4, so `units` is null until `ready`. Does no earlier step write a partial list?\n9. **Degradations:** I wrote that the images and describe steps collect them and they are written with the finished state. Do they instead pass between steps or get written to the row step by step?\n=== w30:p16\ndocs: deploy invariants claude done\nI wrote all five drafts with their edits files in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`, and nothing under `docs/` or the root `CLAUDE.md` changed. The CI diagram passes the mermaid validator, and the editing pass found nothing else to fix.\n\n- `deployment-and-ci.md` / `.edits.md`\n- `invariants.md` / `.edits.md` (rules 5, 7, 8 and 10)\n- `README.md` / `.edits.md`: this is the `technical-design/` index, not the docs charter.\n- `queue.md` / `.edits.md`\n- `CLAUDE.md` / `CLAUDE.edits.md`\n\nCLAUDE.md's invariants now say the same as invariants.md. I left the switchover out (no copying from Railway, then deleting Railway and Access), because it is a one-time event, not how the system works.\n\nQuestions where design.md left me unsure:\n1. Does a push that touches only `api/` still apply `common/`'s migrations and redeploy the pipeline first? And is the chain one workflow file or three? I wrote \"in a fixed order, after the checks pass\" without settling either.\n2. Invariant 6 keeps \"a half-supplied credential set counts as not configured.\" Does that still apply to the R2 API tokens, or does it go?\n3. Invariant 7 used to say how tests guard the migration path. What guards it now: do the tests apply `common/`'s migrations?\n4. I copied the pipeline's commands for `api/` and `common/` (`pnpm dev` runs wrangler dev, `pnpm deploy` and the checks). Are those the real script names, and is the repo a pnpm workspace?\n5. Where does the spoken-form derivation live? I wrote \"in `pipeline/`\".\n6. The charter's \"without opening `api/app` or `tts/app.py`\" is now stale. Whose draft fixes it?\n=== w30:p17\ndocs: tts extraction recipes describer idle\nI've drafted all four notes in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`, each with its `.edits.md`. Every mermaid block passes the validator, and the editing pass is done.\n\n- `tts-service.md`\n- `article-extraction.md`\n- `recipes.md`\n- `image-and-code-describer.md` (its edits file starts with the rename from the-describer.md)\n\n**Questions where design.md left me unsure:**\n\n1. **Spoken form and drop rule:** which step runs them? I wrote \"the item Workflow\" without naming a step.\n2. **Units between steps:** I wrote that the units travel from step to step as Workflow step results, and that a retry reuses the results of earlier steps. design.md doesn't say this directly. Is it right?\n3. **Synthesis result type:** where does its TypeScript type live? It isn't in common/'s list, so I put it in the pipeline Worker. I also didn't name its fields.\n4. **Image download limits:** do the per-host limit (2), global limit (10), 10 s timeout and 10 MB cap still hold? I kept them unchanged.\n5. **Describe retries:** I wrote that a failed describe call is not retried on its own; only the whole step is retried, 3 attempts of 5 min. Is there still a per-call retry for 408, 429 and 5xx?\n6. **Cache hits:** is there a reason a cache hit is billed at the full flat price? I stated the rule without one.\n7. **`extraction_domain` on the item row:** design.md doesn't remove it, so I left it in the recipes diagram. Does it stay?\n8. **Recipe step timeout:** the recipe step gets 15 min per attempt, but authoring allows 100 turns plus retries. Does that limit belong in recipes.md?\n=== w30:p18\ndocs: new notes done\nI wrote both notes. Each one is in two files in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`; for a new note the edits file holds the whole note.\n\n- `common-package.md` and `common-package.edits.md`: \"The common/ package\".\n- `local-development.md` and `local-development.edits.md`: \"Local development\". It uses the design's branch 8 diagram.\n\nBoth diagrams pass the mermaid validator. I ran the editing pass on both notes. Nothing under `docs/` was touched and nothing is committed.\n\nQuestions where design.md left me unsure:\n\n1. **Invariant 8:** it says \"no CI pipeline reaches into another's tree\". A change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/. Does invariant 8 get reworded, or is common/ an exception to it? I left this out of the note.\n2. **Cassette matching:** design.md says \"today's matching rules and filters\". I described the rules concretely: method, scheme, host, port, query, and path and body with item ids normalized. Do the item-id normalization and the Access-header filter really carry over unchanged?\n3. **Tunnel hostname:** how does the pipeline Worker learn the current quick tunnel's hostname? From a config value, an env file, or something else? The note only says it must hand Modal the hostname of the tunnel that is running.\n4. **Local migrations:** the spike learnings, not design.md, say local D1 gets its schema by applying common/'s migrations with wrangler against the shared folder. I added one sentence saying so. Should it stay?\n5. **Reload while an item runs:** the learnings also say a Workflow instance that is running during a dev-server reload never resumes. I left this out because design.md only covers the \"pipeline not running\" case. Should the note have a warning about it?\n6. **Stuck items:** I described the stuck state as \"stays queued, the instance never starts or ends in error\". That wording comes from the spike learnings.\narticle-extraction.edits.md\narticle-extraction.md\nauthentication.edits.md\nauthentication.md\nCLAUDE.edits.md\nCLAUDE.md\ncommon-package.edits.md\ncommon-package.md\ndeployment-and-ci.edits.md\ndeployment-and-ci.md\nimage-and-code-describer.edits.md\nimage-and-code-describer.md\ninvariants.edits.md\ninvariants.md\nitem-contract.edits.md\nitem-contract.md\nitem-lifecycle.edits.md\nitem-lifecycle.md\nlocal-development.edits.md\nlocal-development.md\npersistence-and-storage.edits.md\npersistence-and-storage.md\nqueue.edits.md\nqueue.md\nREADME.edits.md\nREADME.md\nrecipes.edits.md\nrecipes.md\ntts-service.edits.md\ntts-service.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d535e8a0-90c5-422c-a3b7-992aebea3b36","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:41:44.886Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== w30:p14\ndocs: item lifecycle idle\nI wrote the `item-lifecycle.md` draft and its edits file. The three mermaid diagrams pass the validator, and I ran the editing pass over the new prose.\n\n**Files** (in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`):\n- `item-lifecycle.md`\n- `item-lifecycle.edits.md`\n\nThe kept parts of extraction-service.md are DomainQueue's lease and alarm, the recipe runtime with its Dynamic Worker warning, the Flue agents, and the platform limits. Four sections are deleted: Flow, \"Deferred work is mortal\", \"Async endpoints\" and the failure-prefix table.\n\n**Questions where design.md left me unsure:**\n1. Does a failed item's `error` still start with a phase prefix (`fetch:`, `extraction:`…), or does `current_step` replace the prefix? I left prefixes out.\n2. Does a restarted step read the earlier steps' results, such as the fetched HTML and the units? I assumed it does, in a NOTE callout (\"Why fetch's output is a step result and not a column\") and in the retry section. Please confirm.\n3. Branch 5 says \"keep today's handling\" for a retry from lease or earlier while an earlier attempt still holds the lease. What is that handling? I described only the alarm sweeping the lease of an ended instance.\n4. What is an agent conversation keyed by: the item id, or the instance id? And is a retry's conversation still a fresh one under a suffixed id? I wrote \"a conversation of its own\".\n5. Does the lease step's 3 × 1 h limit fail an item that waits too long behind its domain? I wrote that it does.\n6. Does a not-article verdict skip the step's retries? I wrote only that the recipe step fails the item.\n=== w30:p15\ndocs: storage contract auth idle\nI wrote all three drafts and their edit files in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`: `persistence-and-storage.md`, `item-contract.md` and `authentication.md`, each with its `.edits.md`. Every mermaid block passes the validator, and I ran the editing pass over the new prose. Where design.md is silent I kept wording that commits to as little as possible. These points need a decision:\n\n1. **Ledger `tts` row:** which step writes it? I put \"the store step\"; design.md only says each step that makes a metered call writes its own row.\n2. **Prices:** where are they configured in the pipeline Worker? I wrote only \"Prices are configuration per invariant 6\".\n3. **Image hash:** is it taken over the stored bytes (the WebP, or the SVG after its scripts are stripped)? I wrote \"the stored bytes\".\n4. **Double-submitted retry:** does the retry route still claim the item with one conditional `UPDATE` (status still `failed`, count under the cap)? I kept that callout and only changed its cost to \"restarts one instance twice\".\n5. **`retry_count`:** I assumed the retry route still increments it alongside writing `queued`. Is that right?\n6. **Error text:** the `fetch: no response` error string came out. Do errors keep a prefix, maybe derived from `current_step`, or is it the step's raw error?\n7. **Tests and the schema:** do the Workers' tests apply common/'s migrations, or build the schema some other way? I deleted the test-schema warning and wrote nothing in its place.\n8. **Units before `ready`:** I wrote that the units first reach the row with the finished state, going by branch 4, so `units` is null until `ready`. Does no earlier step write a partial list?\n9. **Degradations:** I wrote that the images and describe steps collect them and they are written with the finished state. Do they instead pass between steps or get written to the row step by step?\n=== w30:p16\ndocs: deploy invariants claude done\nI wrote all five drafts with their edits files in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`, and nothing under `docs/` or the root `CLAUDE.md` changed. The CI diagram passes the mermaid validator, and the editing pass found nothing else to fix.\n\n- `deployment-and-ci.md` / `.edits.md`\n- `invariants.md` / `.edits.md` (rules 5, 7, 8 and 10)\n- `README.md` / `.edits.md`: this is the `technical-design/` index, not the docs charter.\n- `queue.md` / `.edits.md`\n- `CLAUDE.md` / `CLAUDE.edits.md`\n\nCLAUDE.md's invariants now say the same as invariants.md. I left the switchover out (no copying from Railway, then deleting Railway and Access), because it is a one-time event, not how the system works.\n\nQuestions where design.md left me unsure:\n1. Does a push that touches only `api/` still apply `common/`'s migrations and redeploy the pipeline first? And is the chain one workflow file or three? I wrote \"in a fixed order, after the checks pass\" without settling either.\n2. Invariant 6 keeps \"a half-supplied credential set counts as not configured.\" Does that still apply to the R2 API tokens, or does it go?\n3. Invariant 7 used to say how tests guard the migration path. What guards it now: do the tests apply `common/`'s migrations?\n4. I copied the pipeline's commands for `api/` and `common/` (`pnpm dev` runs wrangler dev, `pnpm deploy` and the checks). Are those the real script names, and is the repo a pnpm workspace?\n5. Where does the spoken-form derivation live? I wrote \"in `pipeline/`\".\n6. The charter's \"without opening `api/app` or `tts/app.py`\" is now stale. Whose draft fixes it?\n=== w30:p17\ndocs: tts extraction recipes describer idle\nI've drafted all four notes in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`, each with its `.edits.md`. Every mermaid block passes the validator, and the editing pass is done.\n\n- `tts-service.md`\n- `article-extraction.md`\n- `recipes.md`\n- `image-and-code-describer.md` (its edits file starts with the rename from the-describer.md)\n\n**Questions where design.md left me unsure:**\n\n1. **Spoken form and drop rule:** which step runs them? I wrote \"the item Workflow\" without naming a step.\n2. **Units between steps:** I wrote that the units travel from step to step as Workflow step results, and that a retry reuses the results of earlier steps. design.md doesn't say this directly. Is it right?\n3. **Synthesis result type:** where does its TypeScript type live? It isn't in common/'s list, so I put it in the pipeline Worker. I also didn't name its fields.\n4. **Image download limits:** do the per-host limit (2), global limit (10), 10 s timeout and 10 MB cap still hold? I kept them unchanged.\n5. **Describe retries:** I wrote that a failed describe call is not retried on its own; only the whole step is retried, 3 attempts of 5 min. Is there still a per-call retry for 408, 429 and 5xx?\n6. **Cache hits:** is there a reason a cache hit is billed at the full flat price? I stated the rule without one.\n7. **`extraction_domain` on the item row:** design.md doesn't remove it, so I left it in the recipes diagram. Does it stay?\n8. **Recipe step timeout:** the recipe step gets 15 min per attempt, but authoring allows 100 turns plus retries. Does that limit belong in recipes.md?\n=== w30:p18\ndocs: new notes done\nI wrote both notes. Each one is in two files in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/`; for a new note the edits file holds the whole note.\n\n- `common-package.md` and `common-package.edits.md`: \"The common/ package\".\n- `local-development.md` and `local-development.edits.md`: \"Local development\". It uses the design's branch 8 diagram.\n\nBoth diagrams pass the mermaid validator. I ran the editing pass on both notes. Nothing under `docs/` was touched and nothing is committed.\n\nQuestions where design.md left me unsure:\n\n1. **Invariant 8:** it says \"no CI pipeline reaches into another's tree\". A change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/. Does invariant 8 get reworded, or is common/ an exception to it? I left this out of the note.\n2. **Cassette matching:** design.md says \"today's matching rules and filters\". I described the rules concretely: method, scheme, host, port, query, and path and body with item ids normalized. Do the item-id normalization and the Access-header filter really carry over unchanged?\n3. **Tunnel hostname:** how does the pipeline Worker learn the current quick tunnel's hostname? From a config value, an env file, or something else? The note only says it must hand Modal the hostname of the tunnel that is running.\n4. **Local migrations:** the spike learnings, not design.md, say local D1 gets its schema by applying common/'s migrations with wrangler against the shared folder. I added one sentence saying so. Should it stay?\n5. **Reload while an item runs:** the learnings also say a Workflow instance that is running during a dev-server reload never resumes. I left this out because design.md only covers the \"pipeline not running\" case. Should the note have a warning about it?\n6. **Stuck items:** I described the stuck state as \"stays queued, the instance never starts or ends in error\". That wording comes from the spike learnings.\narticle-extraction.edits.md\narticle-extraction.md\nauthentication.edits.md\nauthentication.md\nCLAUDE.edits.md\nCLAUDE.md\ncommon-package.edits.md\ncommon-package.md\ndeployment-and-ci.edits.md\ndeployment-and-ci.md\nimage-and-code-describer.edits.md\nimage-and-code-describer.md\ninvariants.edits.md\ninvariants.md\nitem-contract.edits.md\nitem-contract.md\nitem-lifecycle.edits.md\nitem-lifecycle.md\nlocal-development.edits.md\nlocal-development.md\npersistence-and-storage.edits.md\npersistence-and-storage.md\nqueue.edits.md\nqueue.md\nREADME.edits.md\nREADME.md\nrecipes.edits.md\nrecipes.md\ntts-service.edits.md\ntts-service.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e1cb2d8a-1cac-4214-9718-37b54e22d01d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.