30.281Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace/plugins","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"2841008c-0fef-4ac6-b4db-060f17c22dc9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93123f5c-2014-4df8-8796-cbf57f61f75a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013PymSVrcZSL6rcGjfWYJnK","type":"tool_result","content":"experimental-dev/skills/design/SKILL.md:9:Load `filadd-experimental-dev:basics` first, then `filadd-experimental-dev:design-tree` and `filadd-experimental-dev:mermaid`. The tree, the rounds, the question format, the facts rule and how answers grow the tree come from `design-tree` and apply here as written. Diagrams go through `mermaid` for syntax and validation.\nexperimental-dev/skills/design/SKILL.md:40:5. **Render when settled.** Once every leaf is ✓, produce the branch's representation in the reference's form when one matches: the diagram validated with `mermaid`, or the prototype reconciled through `prototype`. The user asks for a different form when they want one, and when they want to compare, render the candidates side by side. When no reference matches, ask which form before rendering. The prose under the representation is the opening statement extended with the new leaves, not a new draft, and explains what the representation does not show. Numbered steps in prose refer to the diagram's numbers. When another document or an earlier branch already settles a behaviour, reference it in one sentence and do not draw it again; the representation shows only what this branch adds. Show the whole tree with the branch settled and stop. Open the next branch when the user approves.\nexperimental-dev/skills/design/SKILL.md:83:**How a draft is shown.** Plain markdown in the reply, never quoted, never as a code block, never in the browser. One paragraph of prose first: what changes and why. Then, per document, a bold line with the document's title, and for each edit one line of prose naming where it lands (\"Replace the last sentence of <section>:\", \"New section before <section>:\", \"Append to <section>:\", \"<table>, <row>, <column>:\"), with the section names as they read in the document, followed by the edit itself exactly as it will read in Notion, headings and mermaid blocks included. A horizontal rule separates documents. A new document is shown whole under its title line with no location lines. The location lines are the only prose between edits; everything else after the opening paragraph is draft.\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:40:  lead with the answer, diagram what reads clearer as a picture (via `mermaid`), separate verified\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:161:  `mermaid` shapes once the branch settles. Questions are violet cards in the open\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:184:  messages, tied to a shape by sitting on it or by an arrow, and \"Send to Claude\" notifies through a watch. Unslops the canvas texts before every export. Mermaid stays the\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:185:  choice for diagrams that live as text in a document, and the built-in `mermaid` kind draws the same source on the canvas. Typed for a one-off mockup or sketch, or loaded\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:231:**Capability** — `code-search` (+ `search-strategy`), `doc-search`, `data-search`, `mermaid`,\nexperimental-dev/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md:11:The document is `canvas/design.tldr.json` in the change's scratch folder. `design.md` in the same folder keeps the tree, each branch's prose and its mermaid diagrams, updated whenever the canvas changes; the canvas draws from it.\nexperimental-dev/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md:19:- **Use `design`'s types for the representations.** While a branch is open, draw its diagrams with tldraw shapes, which are easier to change as answers come in. Once the branch settles, replace each diagram with a `mermaid` shape that holds the source the final document uses. Size the shape to the diagram's own proportions, at one canvas unit per diagram unit. Draw a screen as a mockup copied from its prototype.\ncommons/skills:\ncreate-claude-artifact\n\nexperimental-dev/skills:\naddress-pr-review\nagentic-review\narchitecture-exploration\nbasics\ncanvas\nchangeset\ncode-blast-radius\ncode-search\ncommit-changes\ncreate-pull-request\ncreate-scopes\ndata-search\ndesign\ndesign-tree\ndesign-with-canvas\ndev-standards\ndoc-search\nexplore\nexplore-with-canvas\nguide\nhuman-review\nimplement\nimplement-with-tdd\nland\nlearn\nlocal-services\nlookup\nmermaid\nobservability\none-page-design\nprepare-repo\nprogram-design\nprogram-design-with-canvas\nproject-knowledge\nprototype\nrebase\nrelease-check\nrelease-repo\nreplicate-user-data\nreport\nscope-tasks\nsearch-strategy\nshape\nshape-up-entities\nshape-with-canvas\nspike\ntest-design\nupdate-pitch-context\nupdate-pull-request\nvalidate-feature\nvalidate-pitch","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ce3b20b4-e5f3-4b09-9c4d-bce2cde41236","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:42:30.694Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"experimental-dev/skills/design/SKILL.md:9:Load `filadd-experimental-dev:basics` first, then `filadd-experimental-dev:design-tree` and `filadd-experimental-dev:mermaid`. The tree, the rounds, the question format, the facts rule and how answers grow the tree come from `design-tree` and apply here as written. Diagrams go through `mermaid` for syntax and validation.\nexperimental-dev/skills/design/SKILL.md:40:5. **Render when settled.** Once every leaf is ✓, produce the branch's representation in the reference's form when one matches: the diagram validated with `mermaid`, or the prototype reconciled through `prototype`. The user asks for a different form when they want one, and when they want to compare, render the candidates side by side. When no reference matches, ask which form before rendering. The prose under the representation is the opening statement extended with the new leaves, not a new draft, and explains what the representation does not show. Numbered steps in prose refer to the diagram's numbers. When another document or an earlier branch already settles a behaviour, reference it in one sentence and do not draw it again; the representation shows only what this branch adds. Show the whole tree with the branch settled and stop. Open the next branch when the user approves.\nexperimental-dev/skills/design/SKILL.md:83:**How a draft is shown.** Plain markdown in the reply, never quoted, never as a code block, never in the browser. One paragraph of prose first: what changes and why. Then, per document, a bold line with the document's title, and for each edit one line of prose naming where it lands (\"Replace the last sentence of <section>:\", \"New section before <section>:\", \"Append to <section>:\", \"<table>, <row>, <column>:\"), with the section names as they read in the document, followed by the edit itself exactly as it will read in Notion, headings and mermaid blocks included. A horizontal rule separates documents. A new document is shown whole under its title line with no location lines. The location lines are the only prose between edits; everything else after the opening paragraph is draft.\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:40:  lead with the answer, diagram what reads clearer as a picture (via `mermaid`), separate verified\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:161:  `mermaid` shapes once the branch settles. Questions are violet cards in the open\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:184:  messages, tied to a shape by sitting on it or by an arrow, and \"Send to Claude\" notifies through a watch. Unslops the canvas texts before every export. Mermaid stays the\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:185:  choice for diagrams that live as text in a document, and the built-in `mermaid` kind draws the same source on the canvas. Typed for a one-off mockup or sketch, or loaded\nexperimental-dev/CLAUDE.md:231:**Capability** — `code-search` (+ `search-strategy`), `doc-search`, `data-search`, `mermaid`,\nexperimental-dev/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md:11:The document is `canvas/design.tldr.json` in the change's scratch folder. `design.md` in the same folder keeps the tree, each branch's prose and its