{"parentUuid":"308fd4d3-77ae-4686-be04-fba6c98319f5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93123f5c-2014-4df8-8796-cbf57f61f75a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013H17u8z72khkG1hTBesFAn","type":"tool_result","content":"10:- Use these node shapes: `A[Rectangle]` (process/step), `B{Diamond}` (decision), `E((Circle))` (start/end), `F[/Parallelogram/]` (I/O). For any other element use an expanded shape, `A@{ shape: cyl, label: \"…\" }`, chosen from the Shapes section below.\n34:    classDef error fill:#F88,stroke:#F22,stroke-width:2px\n40:- **Color to distinguish concerns or states.** Define a reusable class once and apply it, rather than repeating inline styles:\n42:  classDef error fill:#F88,stroke:#F22,stroke-width:2px\n43:  classDef active fill:#0CF,stroke:#09F,stroke-width:3px\n48:- **One-off node styling**: `style C fill:greenyellow,stroke:green,stroke-width:4px`.\n49:- **Highlight a path**: color specific edges by their declaration order (0-indexed): `linkStyle 0,1,4 stroke:gold,stroke-width:4px`. Use `linkStyle default color:Sienna` for all edges.\n54:## Shapes\n56:Give each kind of element the same shape in every diagram, so a reader who has seen one diagram reads the next one without a legend.\n60:Declare an expanded shape on the node's first use, with the label inside the braces:\n63:DB@{ shape: cyl, label: \"Base de datos<br/>de <servicio>\" }\n68:### Which shape for each element\n70:| Element | Shape |\n85:### Shapes Notion renders\n87:Notion runs mermaid 11.15 or 11.16. It renders every shape up to 11.16, `datastore` included, and none of those added in 11.17: `person`, `browser`, `bucket`, `folder`. The validator rejects any shape outside `scripts/notion-shapes.txt`.\nmermaid","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2d7bc2ce-8994-4273-bed0-212d0e41d6a9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:42:40.645Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"10:- Use these node shapes: `A[Rectangle]` (process/step), `B{Diamond}` (decision), `E((Circle))` (start/end), `F[/Pa