{"parentUuid":"5f695558-c57a-4876-bf17-386beaa0d700","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93123f5c-2014-4df8-8796-cbf57f61f75a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017t3HVKxzZjtCZ8vhbJnXZ7","type":"tool_result","content":"    BFF -->|no| Reject[Return 401]\n    BFF -->|yes| DataAPI\n\n    subgraph internal[\"Data API\"]\n        DataAPI[Fetch courses] --> DB[Postgres]\n    end\n\n    DataAPI --> Resp[Return courses]\n\n    classDef error fill:#F88,stroke:#F22,stroke-width:2px\n    class Reject error\n```\n\n## UX / styling guidance\n\n- **Color to distinguish concerns or states.** Define a reusable class once and apply it, rather than repeating inline styles:\n  ```\n  classDef error fill:#F88,stroke:#F22,stroke-width:2px\n  classDef active fill:#0CF,stroke:#09F,stroke-width:3px\n  class Reject error\n  class BFF,DataAPI active\n  ```\n  Apply one class to several nodes with a comma list: `class B,C,F active`.\n- **One-off node styling**: `style C fill:greenyellow,stroke:green,stroke-width:4px`.\n- **Highlight a path**: color specific edges by their declaration order (0-indexed): `linkStyle 0,1,4 stroke:gold,stroke-width:4px`. Use `linkStyle default color:Sienna` for all edges.\n- **`subgraph` to group** by service / layer / repo — this is the primary way to convey architecture boundaries in a flow. Give the subgraph a quoted title when it contains spaces: `subgraph consumer[\"Consumer API (BFF)\"]`.\n- **Line breaks** inside labels: `A[\"Line one<br/>Line two\"]`.\n- Keep direction consistent with meaning: `LR` reads as a pipeline; `TD` reads as a decision tree.\n\n## Shapes\n\nGive each kind of element the same shape in every diagram, so a reader who has seen one diagram reads the next one without a legend.\n\n### Syntax\n\nDeclare an expanded shape on the node's first use, with the label inside the braces:\n\n```\nDB@{ shape: cyl, label: \"Base de datos<br/>de <servicio>\" }\n```\n\nLater references use the bare id. The `<br/>` rule from `SKILL.md` applies to the label.\n\n### Which shape for each element\n\n| Element | Shape |\n|---|---|\n| A person: a user, an admin | `rect` |\n| A screen or a frontend | `rect` |\n| A service, a module, a step | `rect` |\n| A shared piece several components use: a library, a set of rules | `hex` |\n| A background job, a scheduled task | `st-rect` |\n| A wait: a timeout, a period without activity | `delay` |\n| A database, a table, stored state | `cyl` |\n| A store outside the system you query: a BI tool, a warehouse | `cyl` |\n| An external service: a SaaS, a third-party API | `cloud` |\n| A decision | `diam` |\n\nA service's boundary is a `subgraph`, and its storage sits outside the subgraph.\n\n### Shapes Notion renders\n\nNotion runs mermaid 11.15 or 11.16. It renders every shape up to 11.16, `datastore` included, and none of those added in 11.17: `person`, `browser`, `bucket`, `folder`. The validator rejects any shape outside `scripts/notion-shapes.txt`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"06034fb7-68dc-44c4-afbe-c34f781ccd3e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:42:44.263Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"    BFF -->|no| Reject[Return 401]\n    BFF -->|yes| DataAPI\n\n    subgraph internal[\"Data API\"]\n        DataAPI[Fetch courses] --> DB[Postgres]\n    end\n\n    DataAPI --> Resp[Return courses]\n\n    classDef error fill:#F88,stroke:#F22,stroke-width:2px\n    class Reject error\n```\n\n## UX / styling guidance\n\n- **Color to distinguish concerns or states.** Define a reusable class once and apply it, rather than repeating inline styles:\n  ```\n  classDef error fill:#F88,stroke:#F22,stroke-width:2px\n  classDef active fill:#0CF,stroke:#09F,stroke-width:3px\n  class Reject error\n  class BFF,DataAPI active\n  ```\n  Apply one class to several nodes with a comma list: `class B,C,F active`.\n- **One-off node styling**: `style C fill:greenyellow,stroke:green,stroke-width:4px`.\n- **Highlight a path**: color specific edges by their declaration order (0-indexed): `linkStyle 0,1,4 stroke:gold,stroke-width:4px`. Use `linkStyle default color:Sienna` for all edges.\n- **`subgraph` to group** by service / layer / repo — this is the primary way to convey architecture boundaries in a flow. Give the subgraph a quoted title when it contains spaces: `subgraph consumer[\"Consumer API (BFF)\"]`.\n- **Line breaks** inside labels: `A[\"Line one<br/>Line two\"]`.\n- Keep direction consistent with meaning: `LR` reads as a pipeline; `TD` reads as a decision tree.\n\n## Shapes\n\nGive each kind of element the same shape in every diagram, so a reader who has seen one diagram reads the next one without a legend.\n\n### Syntax\n\nDeclare an expanded shape on the node's first use, with the label inside the braces:\n\n```\nDB@{ shape: cyl, label: \"Base de datos<br/>de <servicio>\" }\n```\n\nLater references use the bare id. The `<br/>` rule from `SKILL.md` applies to the label.\n\n### Which shape for each element\n\n| Element | Shape |\n|---|---|\n| A person: a user, an admin | `rect` |\n| A screen or a frontend | `rect` |\n| A service, a module, a step | `rect` |\n| A shared piece several components use: a library, a set of rules | `hex` |\n| A background job, a scheduled task | `st-rect` |\n| A wait: a timeout, a period without activity | `delay` |\n| A database, a table, stored state | `cyl` |\n| A store outside the system you query: a BI tool, a warehouse | `cyl` |\n| An external service: a SaaS, a third-party API | `cloud` |\n| A decision | `diam` |\n\nA service's boundary is a `subgraph`, and its storage sits outside the subgraph.\n\n### Shapes Notion renders\n\nNotion runs mermaid 11.15 or 11.16. It renders every shape up to 11.16, `datastore` included, and none of those added in 11.17: `person`, `browser`, `bucket`, `folder`. The validator rejects any shape outside `scripts/notion-shapes.txt`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b2bc1556-d697-4397-a7da-8100e9b8eff1","contex