{"parentUuid":"b74e0cb3-e41b-4e75-8c5c-eaaf1a582869","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93123f5c-2014-4df8-8796-cbf57f61f75a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013V8bsZdR6nANRPGxoaPwbT","type":"tool_result","content":"66:| `superpowers:unslop`, `superpowers:mermaid-validation` | `filadd-docs:unslop`, `filadd-docs:unslop-pass`, `filadd-experimental-dev:mermaid` |\n81:- **mermaid-validation**: Validate mermaid diagram syntax after writing code blocks using bundled merval-based script (~552KB, auto-installs on first run)\n283:- Durable docs are **lore**: mechanism first, reasoning in a callout beside the thing it justifies, a what-is-not-built-yet section, and no ceremony. **Lore explains the code, it never reprints it** — a declaration belongs in the file where it is typechecked; the surface goes in a table of what each member answers, behaviour goes in prose or a diagram, a snippet survives only where the code *is* the insight at two to four lines. **Use mermaid whenever the subject has a shape.** A quest's `## Design` is most of the lore draft already, minus the signatures.\n301:*Entry points and tooling:* `guide` (matches a goal against skill descriptions dynamically, no routing table; hands off without summarizing or chaining), `init` (typed only; seeds the docs charter, per-folder READMEs with a hand-kept index table, `_templates/note.md` carrying the overview-plus-menu shape adapted from filadd-docs's section menu minus Issue, Possible Solutions and Edge Cases, emoji heading prefixes kept, and a `## Docs` CLAUDE.md block; never overwrites, re-run to add a folder; `init/seeds/` is the only place a template body lives), `wiki`, `learn` (typed only; discovery mode collects the session's friction points and gives a take on each, directed mode works the ask; drafts every item in one reply, each under its heading, written to the scratch folder and passed through `superpowers:unslop` before being shown, approved per item; fidelity rule: reproduce the session's patterns exactly; since 2026-10-10 a code example in a wiki entry is named after a generic resource, never the session's feature). Asked for by name: `canvas` (added 2026-10: a tldraw app under `scripts/app/` run by `scripts/canvas.sh` over one `<name>.tldr.json` document, installed with npm into `~/.cache/mahou-canvas`; the agent draws through `agent-browser` in its own tab, one awaited `canvas.step` per element so the user sees the drawing grow, every tab edits live, mockups are `mockups/<kind>.tsx` files rendered by a custom `mock` shape, a sticky note is the user's message to the agent, \"Send to Claude\" is read through `canvas.sh watch`, documents carry a `canvasVersion` that `canvas.sh migrate` upgrades, each cohesive element is one tldraw group made with `editor.groupShapes` and an `area` boxes only the parts of one thing (2026-10-04), and the texts go through `superpowers:unslop` before `canvas.sh export` writes the SVG; since 2026-10-04 the skill carries drawing rules (one shape per kind of part, arrows labelled with their payload, flows left to right, nothing overlapping), an `area` has no natural width so its border and label keep their size, and `canvas.sh watch` runs under a monitor so each click arrives; since 2026-10-10 a built-in `mermaid` kind holds a finished diagram drawn in the canvas's ink and hand font, Ctrl+. sends like the button, holding the mic button or Ctrl+, sends a voice message that `watch` prints as `voice: <message> | selected: …`, mockups redraw through hot reload instead of reloading the page, and the skill carries rules for sizing a mock to its content, `null` over `undefined` in `data`, pointing an arrow inside a mock, placing notes so no arrow crosses the diagram, resizing areas, restarting after app edits, and talking in the chat or on the canvas as the loading skill says), `explore-with-canvas`, `shape-with-canvas`, `design-with-canvas`, `program-design-with-canvas` (added 2026-10-10: each runs the skill it names on a `canvas` in the scratch folder's `canvas/`; explore lays answers out freely beside a `Decisions` log; shape and design draw the tree as one area per branch, leaves on the left and prose and representations on the right, questions as violet cards with follow-ups inside them, two kept open, Claude notes in place of chat text; design swaps a settled branch's diagrams for `mermaid` shapes and records in the chat; program design draws each part in its own area from bundled mockups and canvas references while `program-design/<root>.md` keeps the text form), `architecture-exploration` (added 2026-10-04: a system's architecture drawn on a `canvas` in the scratch folder's `canvas/`, parts named as the code and docs name them, one area per platform or deployable; when options are asked for, `references/exploration.md` lays them out as a grid with one square per combination of independent dimensions, draws a shared part once step by step, and redraws the chosen option whole beside the earlier one after each decision; picks nothing, removes no drawing unasked; also loaded by `explore`), `one-page-design` (added 2026-10: a settled design as one page on a `canvas` in the scratch folder's `one-page/`, one element largest in the centre, small supporting views, a legend card for the arrow colours; since 2026-10-04 the page is a journey or an anatomy, each a reference under `references/types/` with its centre, layout, patterns and what it leaves out, read from the context or asked when more than one fits, and `references/patterns/` holds one file per visual pattern, routed from a table in the skill), `create-pull-request` (opens one PR, base found by commit distance, title and body from every commit on the branch, waits for confirmation before creating), `rebase` (brings a branch up to date with its base, verifies against the suite, never pushes; ported 2026-09 for `land`), `telepathy` (a mode, added 2026-09: the conversation moves out of the chat into markdown files in the change's scratch folder, served by a Bun server under `scripts/` that the agent starts as a Claude Code background process with the folder's slug; the user edits block by block in the browser (click to edit, `+` to write under, Enter or blur sends, Shift+Enter a new line) and each commit reaches the agent's pane through `herdr agent prompt` as a `[telepathy]` message carrying the file, the lines and a diff, never a block id; the server is the only writer on the user's behalf, so authorship is known, and it is kept per block in `<root>/.meta.json` together with each file's last snapshot; agent writes are picked up by a line diff against that snapshot, which carries block ids and authors forward, plus a positional pass so a block rewritten in place keeps its id; a user edit to a block the agent also changed is three-way merged, and the merge editor opens only when the same lines changed; a prompt to an agent blocked on a dialog waits and retries, everything else goes straight into its input queue; the mode overrides every loaded skill's \"reply\", and the agent ends each turn without chat text).\n303:*Loaded, never typed:* `basics`, `docs`, `design-tree` (frontier rounds, numbered questions across the session, questions written straight into the reply and never through a tool, a section on what a question carries: the context the user needs (earlier answers that bear on it, what the answer changes) and never the ways to answer it, with what counts as a proposed answer and a reread before every round, settled decisions stated as ✓ leaves and never re-asked, a Scope section that gates hypotheticals (a missing value, a failing step, a later feature) behind one \"do we consider X?\" question per branch with deferred ones recorded where the loading skill says, and since 2026-10-10 raised only when a noticed situation would change what the branch defines, the whole tree shown when a branch opens or settles and the worked branch alone between rounds, facts only on request), `changeset` (repos by absolute path and `git -C`, never `cd`; base from `@{u}`, then `origin/HEAD`, then `git remote show origin`, then ask, never guess between `main` and `master`; three-dot diff; introduced vs pre-existing), `prototype` (one self-contained HTML file in the change's scratch folder at `prototypes/`, reopened in place each round; a control strip switches states, alternatives lettered on one page in the first round, corrections applied as given afterwards, reconciled against the settled leaves before a UI branch renders; loaded by `explore` when a screen question comes up and by the `ui` design type, brought over from `filadd-experimental-dev` 2026-09 with no Filadd dependency to strip), `lookup` (where a fact comes from: routing between `code-scout` per repository, `docs-scout` against the project's docs folder, `researcher` for anything outside the project, or a direct trial; verified vs asserted kept apart in the reporting; loaded by `explore` and `design-tree`, ported 2026-09), `report` (the shape of what a skill hands the user when the work is done: findings, an investigation's answer, a change summary; loads the unslop rules and holds them while writing rather than running the pass, leads with the answer, diagrams what reads clearer as a picture, separates the verified from the claimed, cuts what does not bear on the ask, structures by reader need rather than by source; ported from `filadd-experimental-dev` 2026-10 with the unslop and mermaid loads re-pointed at superpowers).\n307:**Cross-plugin dependencies:** `superpowers:unslop` (the writing pass in `write-documentation`, the rules held while writing in `report`) and `superpowers:mermaid-validation` (diagrams in `design`, `write-documentation` and `report`). Both degrade to \"say so and continue\" when absent. External CLIs: `plannotator` (`human-review`) and `agent-browser` (`validate`'s browser reference loads its skill content via `agent-browser skills get core --full`; `canvas` drives its tab with it), plus Node and npm for `canvas`.\n370:`superpowers` and `lesserpowers` are sibling plugins. `superpowers` keeps the curated, most-used surface (agent-browser, herdr, bro, mermaid-validation, show-markdown, unslop, the three `using-` skills, plus the situation-state and process-directives commands); `lesserpowers` holds everything else that was split out (systematic-debugging, self-maintaining-claude-md, hunk-review, agent-communication, financial-summary, and the evolve commands). They have no cross-references — the split is clean.\n398:- Plugin-specific skills (using-live-documentation, self-maintaining-claude-md, using-antigravity, agent-communication, financial-summary, using-code-directives, mermaid-validation, show-markdown) have no upstream and are never modified during sync\nShell cwd was reset to /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3ad9840c-4633-4653-b948-991b515271fb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:43:00.545Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"66:| `superpowers:unslop`, `superpowers:mermaid-validation` | `filadd-docs:unslop`, `filadd-docs:unslop-pass`, `filadd-experimental-dev:mermaid` |\n81:- **mermaid-validation**: Validate mermaid diagram syntax after writing code blocks using bundled merval-based script (~552KB, auto-installs on first run)\n283:- Durable docs are **lore**: mechanism first, reasoning in a callout beside the thing it justifies, a what-is-not-built-yet section, and no ceremony. **Lore explains the code, it never reprints it** — a declaration belongs in the file where it is typechecked; the surface goes in a table of what each member answers, behaviour goes in prose or a diagram, a snippet survives only where the code *is* the insight at two to four lines. **Use mermaid whenever the subject has a shape.** A quest's `## Design` is most of the lore draft already, minus the signatures.\n301:*Entry points and tooling:* `guide` (matches a goal against skill descriptions dynamically, no routing table; ha