st in the centre, small supporting views, a legend card for the arrow colours; since 2026-10-04 the page is a journey or an anatomy, each a reference under `references/types/` with its centre, layout, patterns and what it leaves out, read from the context or asked when more than one fits, and `references/patterns/` holds one file per visual pattern, routed from a table in the skill), `create-pull-request` (opens one PR, base found by commit distance, title and body from every commit on the branch, waits for confirmation before creating), `rebase` (brings a branch up to date with its base, verifies against the suite, never pushes; ported 2026-09 for `land`), `telepathy` (a mode, added 2026-09: the conversation moves out of the chat into markdown files in the change's scratch folder, served by a Bun server under `scripts/` that the agent starts as a Claude Code background process with the folder's slug; the user edits block by block in the browser (click to edit, `+` to write under, Enter or blur sends, Shift+Enter a new line) and each commit reaches the agent's pane through `herdr agent prompt` as a `[telepathy]` message carrying the file, the lines and a diff, never a block id; the server is the only writer on the user's behalf, so authorship is known, and it is kept per block in `<root>/.meta.json` together with each file's last snapshot; agent writes are picked up by a line diff against that snapshot, which carries block ids and authors forward, plus a positional pass so a block rewritten in place keeps its id; a user edit to a block the agent also changed is three-way merged, and the merge editor opens only when the same lines changed; a prompt to an agent blocked on a dialog waits and retries, everything else goes straight into its input queue; the mode overrides every loaded skill's \"reply\", and the agent ends each turn without chat text).\n303:*Loaded, never typed:* `basics`, `docs`, `design-tree` (frontier rounds, numbered questions across the session, ques