{"parentUuid":"12abffbc-0088-4be7-ad9a-640374631615","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfukyeFjnwwy1DDBVYPQQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Filadd experimental-dev plugin has `filadd-experimental-dev:mermaid`. Your `sync-to-filadd` skill maps it to `superpowers:mermaid-validation`. It's a fuller skill than ours:\n\n- **Chart table:** a table that picks the chart type for what you're documenting, with one reference file per chart. The flowchart, sequence, class and ER references exist. The table links a state-diagram reference that isn't in the folder.\n- **Common syntax rules:** these include the 24-character `<br/>` rule, plus validation through a temp file with the same mermaid-ast validator.\n- **Fixed shapes:** a Shapes section in `references/flowchart.md` gives each kind of element the same shape in every diagram, \"so a reader who has seen one diagram reads the next one without a legend\". For example:\n  - `rect` for a service, step, screen or person\n  - `hex` for a shared library\n  - `st-rect` for a background job\n  - `cyl` for stores\n  - `cloud` for external services\n  - `diam` for a decision\n- **Notion check:** a whitelist of the shapes Notion renders, which the validator enforces.\n- **Colour:** guidance only, \"colour to distinguish concerns or states\" with `classDef`. It has no palette per kind.\n\nThat fits your idea. Replace `superpowers:mermaid-validation` with a `superpowers:mermaid` skill ported from Filadd's, with these additions:\n- **Colour per kind:** a colour column in the shapes table, plus the shapes this session used that Filadd's table lacks: `subproc` for a durable job such as a Workflow, `braces` for an interface or payload crossing a boundary, and `stadium` for the client.\n- **Rendering rules:** the validator can't catch these. It gets a \"render it and look\" step, plus the three problems this session hit: `;` in state-diagram text, markdown inside `@{ label }`, and a subgraph `direction` ignored when edges cross its border.\n\nBecause this replaces a skill, the item also covers removing `mermaid-validation` and updating every reference to it:\n- in mahou: `design`, `program-design`, `write-documentation`, `report` and `lookup`\n- `mahou/README.md`\n- the root `CLAUDE.md`\n- the root and superpowers READMEs\n- the mapping table in the `sync-to-filadd` and `sync-upstream` skills\n\nI took your other answers this way:\n- items 4 and 5 also apply to shape-with-canvas\n- item 7 changes every design type the session drew in the coloured style: contract, data flow, component architecture, lifecycle and rules\n\n**Questions for the mermaid item:**\n\n- **Name:** `superpowers:mermaid`, or another name?\n- **Notion whitelist:** does it come along, or stay Filadd-only?\n- **Person's shape:** Filadd draws a person as `rect`, and this session drew the client as `stadium`. Which goes in the table?\n- **Fixed palette:** does the colour column hold this session's colours (blue API, green pipeline, orange stores, violet external, grey client, amber interfaces), or neutral colours per kind that any project uses?\n\nThe docs drafters' questions from before (P1–P13 and D1–D9) are also still waiting for your answers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3806,"cache_read_input_tokens":570365,"output_tokens":1563,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":478},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3806,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":570365,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3806},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"inpu