{"parentUuid":"4bafe630-4034-427b-801f-74d22c9306f0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"287199b2-c9a3-4397-9619-039a07127cf3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"\n\n<pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n# Annotations on claude · last message\n\n## Annotation 1 (line 21)\nLooks good: \"or is it the step's own error, with `current_step` naming the step?\"\n\n## Annotation 2 (line 22)\nComment on: \"- **D2 Results between steps:** do the fetched HTML, the units and the degradations travel from step to step as Workflow step results? A restarted step would then read them, and they would reach the row only when the store step runs.\"\n> is it necessary to pass on the values? won't the important bits get saved on the DB anyway?\n\n## Annotation 3 (line 23)\nComment on: \"**D3 Spoken-form step:** which step derives the spoken form and drops empty units?\"\n> hmm which step does it fit? should we add a new one?\n\n## Annotation 4 (line 24)\nComment on: \"D4 Describe retries:** does describe keep a retry per call for 408, 429 and 5xx, or does it rely only on the step's 3 attempts?\"\n> hmm does it make sense (and does the workflow have support for) making this a step that spawns nested steps for each item to describe?\n\n## Annotation 5 (line 25)\nLooks good: \"D5 Tests and migrations:** do the Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying `common/`'s migrations?\"\n\n## Annotation 6 (line 26)\nComment on: \"D6 CI scope:** does a push that touches only `api/` still apply the migrations and deploy the pipeline first? Is the chain one workflow or three?\"\n> the migrations are applied by the common CI worklow, the others might need to depend on that one tho to continue\n\n## Annotation 7 (line 27)\nComment on: \"**D7 Credentials rule:** does invariant 6's \"a half-supplied credential set counts as not configured\" still apply, now to the R2 tokens, or does it go?\"\n> let's drop it\n\n## Annotation 8 (line 28)\nComment on: \"**D8 Recipe step timeout:** does the 15-minute limit on the recipe step belong in `recipes.md`, given that authoring allows up to 100 turns?\"\n> are they contradictory? otherwise it sounds good to keep it there\n\n## Annotation 9 (line 29)\nLooks good: \"Can I send a scout to read today's code for both?\"\n\n</pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n"},"uuid":"e686fea2-bb28-4720-8413-0915d42c1113","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:47:34.831Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":58,"turnIndex":195},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
