{"parentUuid":"531441a4-0ddb-4545-a26e-183521819494","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumMGvTyLXPyS6nwcKVe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EueojwQaUPyDs8BEiaPHYf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; python3 - <<'EOF'\na=open('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/agents/code-scout.md').read()\nbody=a.split('---',2)[2].strip()\ntask=\"\"\"\n\n## Task\n\nRepository: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara (read-only). Today's code: api/ (Python) and pipeline/ (TypeScript on Cloudflare).\n\nAnswer four questions about how the code works today, with file:line references:\n1. DomainQueue (pipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts and callers): when a job fails or its Workflow instance ends while holding its domain's lease, what frees the lease (the alarm, a release call, something else) and after how long? And what happens when the same item or job is enqueued or retried again while an earlier attempt still holds the lease (is the earlier holder detected, replaced, waited on)?\n2. The Flue author and revision agents (pipeline/src/agents/): what is a conversation keyed by (job id, item id, domain, something else)? When the API retries an item and a new extraction job runs, does the agent start a fresh conversation, and how is its id formed?\n3. The spoken form: in api/app/service/ (extract.py and the lifecycle steps), in what order do these happen for an item: deriving each unit's spoken form from its markdown, describing images and code (enrichment), dropping a unit whose spoken form has no letter or digit, and spawning synthesis? Name the function and the step for each.\n4. Authoring duration: is there anything in the code, tests, cassettes, docs (docs/technical-design/recipes.md, extraction-service.md) or .scratch spikes that records how long a recipe authoring or revision run takes, or a timeout or turn limit on it (for example 100 turns)? Report the numbers found and where.\n\nMark anything inferred as inferred. Under 500 words. Make no edits.\n\"\"\"\nopen('briefs/scout-today-handling.md','w').write(\"<supervisor-agent>\\n\"+body+task+\"</supervisor-agent>\\n\")\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"scout: today handling\" --model sonnet --body-file briefs/scout-today-handling.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3256,"cache_read_input_tokens":576530,"output_tokens":1079,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":88},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3256,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1079,"cache_read_input_tokens":576530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3256},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EueojwQaUPyDs8BEiaPHYf":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; python3 - <<'EOF'\na=open('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/agents/code-scout.md').read()\nbody=a.split('---',2)[2].strip()\ntask=\"\"\"\n\n## Task\n\nRepository: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara (read-only). Today's code: api/ (Python) and pipeline/ (TypeScript on Cloudflare).\n\nAnswer four questions about how the code works today, with file:line references:\n1. DomainQueue (pipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts and callers): when a job fails or its Workflow instance ends while holding its domain's lease, what frees the lease (the alarm, a release call, something else) and after how long? And what happens when the same item or job is enqueued or retried again while an earlier attempt still holds the lease (is the earlier holder detected, replaced, waited on)?\n2. The Flue author and revision agents (pipeline/src/agents/): what is a conversation keyed by (job id, item id, domain, something else)? When the API retries an item and a new extraction job runs, does the agent start a fresh conversation, and how is its id formed?\n3. The spoken form: in api/app/service/ (extract.py and the lifecycle steps), in what order do these happen for an item: deriving each unit's spoken form from its markdown, describing images and code (enrichment), dropping a unit whose spoken form has no letter or digit, and spawning synthesis? Name the function and the step for each.\n4. Authoring duration: is there anything in the code, tests, cassettes, docs (docs/technical-design/recipes.md, extraction-service.md) or .scratch spikes that records how long a recipe authoring or revision run takes, or a timeout or turn limit on it (for example 100 turns)? Report the numbers found and where.\n\nMark anything inferred as inferred. Under 500 words. Make no edits.\n\"\"\"\nopen('briefs/scout-today-handling.md','w').write(\"<supervisor-agent>\\n\"+body+task+\"</supervisor-agent>\\n\")\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"scout: today handling\" --model sonnet --body-file briefs/scout-today-handling.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"950e9401-0cdb-4498-8015-7e7add73c261","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfumMGMjcwHxJc3KTooWC","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15034095-4573-40b7-a90f-d6f74b365a9f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:48:04.978Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace