{"parentUuid":"9c6c5c45-8676-48f6-b7e0-8e644956a64e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumNtuhNUpmcerz7Qj7e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":581179,"output_tokens":1654,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":721},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1654,"cache_read_input_tokens":581179,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13682,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"e0b53c5b-416e-4adb-91b9-3af428452a9c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfumNtNCrJ4Q5Vz8Mx8aa","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"603df186-570b-4627-83c3-2156c6316a0a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:48:31.750Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"603df186-570b-4627-83c3-2156c6316a0a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumNtuhNUpmcerz7Qj7e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recorded your answers:\n\n- **D1:** an error is the step's own error, and `current_step` names the step.\n- **D5:** the Workers' tests apply `common/`'s migrations.\n- **D6:** `common/`'s CI workflow applies the migrations. The pipeline and API workflows wait for it to succeed before they continue.\n- **D7:** the credentials rule is dropped.\n- **D9:** a scout is reading today's code. Its questions are what frees a held lease, what happens on a retry while an earlier attempt still holds it, how agent conversations are keyed, the order of spoken form, describe and drop, and how long authoring takes.\n\nYou left P1 to P13 unmarked, so I'm taking them as confirmed. Tell me if any isn't.\n\nThe facts for your questions:\n\n**D2: passing values between steps.** Workflows stores each step's return value and replays it when the instance resumes or restarts. A step that restarts can only read an earlier step's output if that step returned it or wrote it somewhere. The values that cross steps are:\n- the fetched HTML, up to the 1 MiB cap\n- the units, around 150 to 250 KB\n- the degradations\n- the descriptions\n- Modal's call id and its result\n\nOf these, only the units and degradations have a column on the row, and the HTML has no stored home at all. A step result is documented as capped at 1 MiB, which is where the HTML cap also sits. Writing the units to the row before ready makes a poll see them, unless the API holds them back. So the question is which of these values live as step results and which go to the row, or elsewhere, as soon as they exist.\n\n**D3: which step derives the spoken form.** Describe fills the spoken form of images and code. Dropping a unit whose spoken form has no letter or digit has to come after describe and before start synthesis. The scout is checking where each piece happens today, and I'll put that next to this question when it reports back.\n\n**D4: one step per description.** Workflows supports it:\n- a loop can call `step.do` once per item, as long as each step name carries a counter\n- an instance allows 10,000 steps, and the shared budget caps describes at 25 per item\n- each describe step then gets its own retries and timeout, and writes its own ledger row\n- a restart replays the describes that already finished\n\nWhether those steps can run concurrently, by awaiting several `step.do` calls at once, isn't in the wiki and wasn't tested. I can look it up.\n\n**D8: the recipe step's timeout.** The 15-minute timeout applies to each attempt. It conflicts with authoring only if an authoring run can take longer than 15 minutes, because the step would then time out and start the authoring over. The scout is looking for recorded authoring times and turn limits.\n\nYour four questions on the mermaid skill from the learn session are still open: its name, the Notion whitelist, the person shape, and the fixed palette."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":581179,"output_tokens":1654,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":721},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1654,"cache_read_input_tokens":581179,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e0b53c5b-416e-4adb-91b9-3af428452a9c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011