{"parentUuid":"a5fc607b-799d-490c-95e8-9b9f131153a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumSMBb74pTK5q5zJwTr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016ZdwtWB3Rpe4XHgv5jksXx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p1D | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\"; $H close w30:tY >/dev/null"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2081,"cache_read_input_tokens":582060,"output_tokens":165,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2081,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":165,"cache_read_input_tokens":582060,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2081},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016ZdwtWB3Rpe4XHgv5jksXx":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p1D | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\"; $H close w30:tY >/dev/null"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"90163636-45bc-4e6e-9ea3-576f3c278478","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfumSLZ8tuGYPD1zpYYjc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"48cb65e2-78aa-49be-906f-57424fd52418","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:49:06.311Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"48cb65e2-78aa-49be-906f-57424fd52418","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2b352530-d5b0-4577-8121-7a793d4f90e4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ZdwtWB3Rpe4XHgv5jksXx","type":"tool_result","content":"done\n**Answers.** The workflow's last step releases the lease at once. The 60 s alarm frees it if that step never runs. A repeat enqueue of the same job id is rejected with 409, and nothing replaces or waits on the earlier holder. Conversations are keyed by job id, with a `-N` suffix on in-job re-attempts. The agent loops are bounded at 100 turns (prompt-level, see Q4) and the one measured authoring run took 97 s.\n\n## 1. DomainQueue lease\n- **Normal path:** `pipeline/src/workflow/extraction.ts:137-144` runs a final `release lease` step that calls `DomainQueue.release(jobId)` (`domain-queue.ts:85-94`). It deletes the lease only if `lease.jobId === jobId`, then `advance()` creates the next waiting job. A failed release is swallowed as `{released:false}`.\n- **Error terminals:** agent `error`, `not_article` and exhausted retries are returned values, not throws (`extraction.ts:74-95`), so they still reach the release step.\n- **Backstop:** a lease is set with `setAlarm(now + leaseAlarmMs)` (`domain-queue.ts:62,126`), and `leaseAlarmMs` is 60000 (`wrangler.jsonc:28`). `alarm()` (`:133-154`) calls `EXTRACTION.get(jobId).status()`. If the status is `complete`, `errored` or `terminated`, or `get` throws, it deletes the lease and calls `advance()`. Otherwise it re-arms 60 s later. A dead holder is therefore freed 60 s or less after its alarm next fires (inferred: up to 60 s after the instance ended).\n- **Same job id again:** `enqueue` (`:40-50`) returns `{conflict:true}` if the id is the lease holder or already waiting. It also conflicts if the write-once job index already knows the id. `routes.ts:61-63` turns that into a 409. The earlier holder is not detected as dead, replaced or waited on.\n- **API side:** a retry mints a new handle, `item_id-{retry_count}` (`api/app/service/extraction.py:30-42`). It avoids the conflict, but joins the domain's FIFO behind the old lease until release or alarm (inferred from the code).\n\n## 2. Flue agents\n- Conversations are keyed by an id string, `init(agentFor(kind), { id: conversationId })` (`pipeline/src/agents/gateway.ts:38,47`). Domain and item id are not part of the key.\n- `extraction.ts:56` forms the id as `jobId` on attempt 1 and `${jobId}-${attempt}` after that.\n- `jobId` is `event.instanceId`, which is the API's handle (`item_id`, or `item_id-{retry_count}`).\n- An API retry that reminted the handle produces a new job id, so the agent starts a fresh conversation.\n- A reused handle would fail on enqueue with a 409 (`mint_handle` docstring says only an `error` terminal clears the handle).\n- `author.ts` and `revisor.ts` carry no other key. The domain and recipe go in the message and `initialData`.\n\n## 3. Order in `api/`\nThe step list is `api/app/service/pipeline/__init__.py:27-36`.\n1. **Spoken form and drop (one pass):**\n   - `ExtractionResolveStep` (`steps.py:143-183`) calls `enrich_declared_images` (`images.py:~81-85`).\n   - For each non-image unit it derives `spoken = to_spoken(display)` (`extract.py:60`, markdown to spoken via `sanitize_spoken`).\n   - It then drops the unit if `is_unspeakable(spoken)` (`extract.py:120`, no alphanumeric). The unit is dropped before it becomes a `ParagraphUnit` or `CodeUnit`, with no degradation recorded.\n   - Image units are acquired afterwards and interleaved. An image's spoken form comes from its alt.\n   - If no units survive, it raises \"no surviving units\".\n2. **Enrichment (describing images and code):** `DescribeStep` (`steps.py:186-226`, name \"enrichment\") calls `enrich_with_descriptions` and sets `enriched_at`. It runs in the generating phase, after extraction has resolved. `describe.py` re-sanitises with `sanitize_spoken` (`:91`) and never drops (`:272`).\n3. **Synthesis spawn:** `SynthesizeStep` (`steps.py:228-248`, name \"spawn\") runs only when `enriched_at` is set and no `modal_call_id` exists. It spawns synthesis over `[unit.spoken ...]`.\n\n## 4. Authoring duration and limits\n- **Turn limit:** `agentMaxTurns: 100` (`pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:25`). It appears only in the prompt text, \"about ${maxTurns} turns\" (`prompts.ts:54,72`). I found no code that enforces a turn cap (inferred; I did not read the Flue runtime).\n- **Docs on turns:** `docs/technical-design/recipes.md:80` and `:101` say \"within 100 turns, then two retries\" for the revision loop.\n- **Retries:** `authoringRetries: 1` and `revisionRetries: 2` (`wrangler.jsonc:26-27`).\n- **No timeout:** `extraction-service.md:163` says a workflow instance has no wall-clock limit and the agent loops stay far inside the CPU bound. `recipeCpuMs: 2000` is the recipe run's CPU cap (`wrangler.jsonc:30`), not the agent's.\n- **Measured run:** `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/spikes/local-dev-real/FINDINGS.md:39` records `jvns-author-1`, no recipe, as complete, with the author settling on attempt 1, in **97 s**. The recipe-provided run took 1.3 s (`:40`). I did not check which model produced the 97 s, and found no revision run timing.\n- **Not found:** no per-run duration in `pipeline/test/` (no agent-duration matches), and no authoring or revision timing in `docs/`.\n\nNo edits made.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e589a92e-9e7b-439d-a0cc-960fae873fb4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:49:07.464Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\n**Answers.** The workflow's last step releases the lease at once. The 60 s alarm frees it if that step never runs. A repeat enqueue of the same job id is rejected with 409, and nothing replaces or waits on the earlier holder. Conversations are keyed by job id, with a `-N` suffix on in-job re-attempts. The agent loops are bounded at 100 turns (prompt-level, see Q4) and the one measured authoring run took 97 s.\n\n## 1. DomainQueue lease\n- **Normal path:** `pipeline/src/workflow/extraction.ts:137-144` runs a final `release lease` step that calls `DomainQueue.release(jobId)` (`domain-queue.ts:85-94`). It deletes the lease only if `lease.jobId === jobId`, then `advance()` creates the next waiting job. A failed release is swallowed as `{released:false}`.\n- **Error terminals:** agent `error`, `not_article` and exhausted retries are returned values, not throws (`extraction.ts:74-95`), so they still reach the release step.\n- **Backstop:** a lease is set with `setAlarm(now + leaseAlarmMs)` (`domain-queue.ts:62,126`), and `leaseAlarmMs` is 60000 (`wrangler.jsonc:28`). `alarm()` (`:133-154`) calls `EXTRACTION.get(jobId).status()`. If the status is `complete`, `errored` or `terminated`, or `get` throws, it deletes the lease and calls `advance()`. Otherwise it re-arms 60 s later. A dead holder is therefore freed 60 s or less after its alarm next fires (inferred: up to 60 s after the instance ended).\n- **Same job id again:** `enqueue` (`:40-50`) returns `{conflict:true}` if the id is the lease holder or already waiting. It also conflicts if the write-once job index already knows the id. `routes.ts:61-63` turns that into a 409. The earlier holder is not detected as dead, replaced or waited on.\n- **API side:** a retry mints a new handle, `item_id-{retry_count}` (`api/app/service/extraction.py:30-42`). It avoids the conflict, but joins the domain's FIFO behind the old lease until release or alarm (inferred from the code).\n\n## 2. Flue agents\n- Conversations are keyed by an id string, `init(agentFor(kind), { id: conversationId })` (`pipeline/src/agents/gateway.ts:38,47`). Domain and item id are not part of the key.\n- `extraction.ts:56` forms the id as `jobId` on attempt 1 and `${jobId}-${attempt}` after that.\n- `jobId` is `event.instanceId`, which is the API's handle (`item_id`, or `item_id-{retry_count}`).\n- An API retry that reminted the handle produces a new job id, so the agent starts a fresh conversation.\n- A reused handle would fail on enqueue with a 409 (`mint_handle` docstring says only an `error` terminal clears the handle).\n- `author.ts` and `revisor.ts` carry no other key. The domain and recipe go in the message and `initialData`.\n\n## 3. Order in `api/`\nThe step list is `api/app/service/pipeline/__init__.py:27-36`.\n1. **Spoken form and drop (one pass):**\n   - `ExtractionResolveStep` (`steps.py:143-183`) calls `enrich_declared_images` (`images.py:~81-85`).\n   - For each non-image unit it derives `spoken = to_spoken(display)` (`extract.py:60`, markdown to spoken via `sanitize_spoken`).\n   - It then drops the unit if `is_unspeakable(spoken)` (`extract.py:120`, no alphanumeric). The unit is dropped before it becomes a `ParagraphUnit` or `CodeUnit`, with no degradation recorded.\n   - Image units are acquired afterwards and interleaved. An image's spoken form comes from its alt.\n   - If no units survive, it raises \"no surviving units\".\n2. **Enrichment (describing images and code):** `DescribeStep` (`steps.py:186-226`, name \"enrichment\") calls `enrich_with_descriptions` and sets `enriched_at`. It runs in the generating phase, after extraction has resolved. `describe.py` re-sanitises with `sanitize_spoken` (`:91`) and never drops (`:272`).\n3. **Synthesis spawn:** `SynthesizeStep` (`steps.py:228-248`, name \"spawn\") runs only when `enriched_at` is set and no `modal_call_id` exists. It spawns synthesis over `[unit.spoken ...]`.\n\n## 4. Authoring duration and limits\n- **Turn limit:** `agentMaxTurns: 100` (`pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:25`). It appears only in the prompt text, \"about ${maxTurns} turns\" (`prompts.ts:54,72`). I found no code that enforces a turn cap (inferred; I did not read the Flue runtime).\n- **Docs on turns:** `docs/technical-design/recipes.md:80` and `:101` say \"within 100 turns, then two retries\" for the revision loop.\n- **Retries:** `authoringRetries: 1` and `revisionRetries: 2` (`wrangler.jsonc:26-27`).\n- **No timeout:** `extraction-service.md:163` says a workflow instance has no wall-clock limit and the agent loops stay far inside the CPU bound. `recipeCpuMs: 2000` is the recipe run's CPU cap (`wrangler.jsonc:30`), not the agent's.\n- **Measured run:** `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/spikes/local-dev-real/FINDINGS.md:39` records `jvns-author-1`, no recipe, as complete, with the author settling on attempt 1, in **97 s**. The recipe-provided run took 1.3 s (`:40`). I did not check which model produced the 97 s, and found no revision run timing.\n- **Not found:** no per-run duration in `pipeline/test/` (no agent-duration matches), and no authoring or revision timing in `docs/`.\n\nNo edits made.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"90163636-45bc-4e6e-9ea3-576f3c278478","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"48cb65e2-78aa-49be-906f-57424fd52418","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitB