{"parentUuid":"05c026ff-0d90-4252-a5b7-e795414f8f0d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumShPWkaBpNJDmmAb3L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2298,"cache_read_input_tokens":584141,"output_tokens":1744,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":768},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2298,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":584141,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2298},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14257,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"0edacc37-1477-45cb-ae32-e1c0bff9f1c0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfumSgjpsxLm2FAiWfsvf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"592f7824-d3e8-4678-a4f2-a3c61738e46a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:49:24.099Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"592f7824-d3e8-4678-a4f2-a3c61738e46a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumShPWkaBpNJDmmAb3L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The scout is back with how today's code handles these.\n\n**D9: the domain lease today.**\n- **The last step releases the lease.** Agent errors and not-an-article verdicts come back as returned values, not thrown errors, so the release step runs even when extraction fails.\n- **An alarm backs that up.** Every 60 s it checks the holder's instance and frees the lease once the instance has completed, errored or been terminated.\n- **A retry gets a new job id today.** The new id is `<item id>-<retry count>`, so the retry queues behind the old holder. Enqueuing the same job id again is rejected as a conflict.\n\nThe new design restarts the same instance, so \"today's handling\" doesn't carry over cleanly, in two ways:\n- **Restarting from recipe:** if recipe fails after the lease is taken, the alarm frees the lease within about 60 s of the instance erroring. A restart from recipe then replays the lease step's cached result, and recipe runs without holding the lease.\n- **Restarting from fetch or lease:** the item asks for the lease again under the same id, the instance id. Today DomainQueue rejects a repeated id as a conflict.\n\n**D9: agent conversations today.** They're keyed by the job id, with `-<attempt>` added for retries inside one job. The job id is the instance id. Today a retry gets a fresh conversation because it gets a fresh job id. With a restart the instance id stays the same, so a retried authoring run would reuse the earlier conversation's id.\n\n**D3: spoken form today.** Each unit's spoken form is derived, and units with no letter or digit are dropped, in one pass right after extraction resolves, before describe. An image takes its spoken form from its alt text. Describe cleans the text again but never drops a unit. In the new design that pass sits at the end of the recipe step, or in a step of its own between recipe and images.\n\n**D8: authoring time.** The one measured authoring run took 97 s and settled on its first attempt. The 100-turn limit appears only in the prompt, and nothing in the code enforces it. Authoring gets 1 retry, revision gets 2. No revision run has been timed. On that one measurement, the 15-minute timeout per attempt doesn't conflict, so I'll keep the limit in `recipes.md` unless you say otherwise.\n\n**Still open:**\n- **D2:** which values that cross steps live as step results, and which go to the row or elsewhere.\n- **D3:** spoken form and drop at the end of recipe, or in a new step.\n- **D4:** one step per description. I can look up whether those steps can run concurrently.\n- **New, on restart and the lease:**\n  - what keeps the lease for an item restarted from recipe\n  - what happens when a restarted item asks for the lease again under the same id\n- **New, on restart and conversations:** how a retried authoring run gets its conversation.\n- **The mermaid skill (learn session):** its name, the Notion whitelist, the shape for a person, and the fixed palette."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2298,"cache_read_input_tokens":584141,"output_tokens":1744,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":768},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2298,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":584141,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2298},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0edacc37