{"parentUuid":"9a99a1a8-8f8d-4e97-9df8-ff23201c58b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumeTpmb5j2y4XSipwLL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N1weRwpkJETTA8PSbYAsxu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; python3 - <<'EOF'\na=open('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/agents/researcher.md').read()\nbody=a.split('---',2)[2].strip()\ntask=\"\"\"\n\n## Task\n\nPlatform: Cloudflare Workflows, Workers binding API in TypeScript, as of October 2026.\n\nQuestion: can one Workflow instance run several steps at the same time, and can a step contain steps?\n\nContext: an item Workflow describes up to 25 images and code blocks, one Gemini call each. The design wants one `step.do` per description, each with its own retries and timeout, run concurrently, and a failing description must not fail the instance.\n\nReport, with source URLs and the date of each source:\n1. Whether awaiting several `step.do` calls at once (for example `Promise.all` or `Promise.allSettled` over them) is documented as supported, and any limit on concurrent steps per instance.\n2. Whether a `step.do` callback can itself call `step.do` (nested steps), or whether the docs forbid or say nothing about it.\n3. How a step that throws after exhausting its retries behaves when awaited inside `Promise.allSettled`: does catching it keep the instance running, or does any exhausted step fail the instance? Quote the docs on catching step errors.\n4. Any naming rule for steps created in a loop (deterministic names) and how replay treats concurrent steps after a restart or a deploy.\n5. Any official example or guide that fans out steps in parallel.\n\nMark anything you could not confirm as unconfirmed. Under 450 words. Write nothing outside /tmp.\n\"\"\"\nopen('briefs/research-parallel-steps.md','w').write(\"<supervisor-agent>\\n\"+body+task+\"</supervisor-agent>\\n\")\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"research: parallel steps\" --model sonnet --body-file briefs/research-parallel-steps.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":933,"cache_read_input_tokens":588504,"output_tokens":1168,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":404},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":933,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1168,"cache_read_input_tokens":588504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":933},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01N1weRwpkJETTA8PSbYAsxu":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; python3 - <<'EOF'\na=open('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/agents/researcher.md').read()\nbody=a.split('---',2)[2].strip()\ntask=\"\"\"\n\n## Task\n\nPlatform: Cloudflare Workflows, Workers binding API in TypeScript, as of October 2026.\n\nQuestion: can one Workflow instance run several steps at the same time, and can a step contain steps?\n\nContext: an item Workflow describes up to 25 images and code blocks, one Gemini call each. The design wants one `step.do` per description, each with its own retries and timeout, run concurrently, and a failing description must not fail the instance.\n\nReport, with source URLs and the date of each source:\n1. Whether awaiting several `step.do` calls at once (for example `Promise.all` or `Promise.allSettled` over them) is documented as supported, and any limit on concurrent steps per instance.\n2. Whether a `step.do` callback can itself call `step.do` (nested steps), or whether the docs forbid or say nothing about it.\n3. How a step that throws after exhausting its retries behaves when awaited inside `Promise.allSettled`: does catching it keep the instance running, or does any exhausted step fail the instance? Quote the docs on catching step errors.\n4. Any naming rule for steps created in a loop (deterministic names) and how replay treats concurrent steps after a restart or a deploy.\n5. Any official example or guide that fans out steps in parallel.\n\nMark anything you could not confirm as unconfirmed. Under 450 words. Write nothing outside /tmp.\n\"\"\"\nopen('briefs/research-parallel-steps.md','w').write(\"<supervisor-agent>\\n\"+body+task+\"</supervisor-agent>\\n\")\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"research: parallel steps\" --model sonnet --body-file briefs/research-parallel-steps.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"39c41e42-1a85-429b-b842-60f9c4d3eed9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfumeSiYcz2f3Ckt48RQG","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d3a9d61d-4364-435a-b8a5-4c9654596f63","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:51:59.719Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
