{"parentUuid":"ccad14d0-7584-41e2-8fa8-bdb6fbc83bcb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14998190 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d3f19165-b788-46ab-b02e-9a77e374682c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:52:09.052Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14998190 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"d3f19165-b788-46ab-b02e-9a77e374682c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfumg5Mic62AX7ep8QZNN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stadium goes in the shapes table for a person or client. All the mermaid questions are now settled, so that learn item is ready to draft.\n\n**D2.** I read your answer this way:\n- **Written to the row:** units and degradations go to the row as soon as a step produces them, and later steps read them from there.\n- **Passed as step results:** only values with no column on the row and that a later step needs. That's the fetched HTML, Modal's call id and the synthesis result.\n- **The poll:** with units on the row before ready, the API has to hold them back until the item is ready. Today's contract keeps units null until the item is timed.\n\n**D4.** A researcher is checking whether several `step.do` calls can run at once, and whether steps can be nested. If the docs don't settle it, a spike will.\n\nOne conflict with something already settled. You want the parent step not to fail even when every child fails. Branch 6 kept today's rule that the item fails when every code block within the describe budget failed. Under today's rule, an item made only of images never fails because of describe, since an image always has its alt text to fall back on. Does the parent-never-fails rule replace the code-block rule, or does the code-block rule still apply after the children finish?\n\nStill open:\n- **D3:** spoken form and drop at the end of the recipe step, or in a new step.\n- **Restart and the lease:** what keeps the lease for an item restarted from recipe, and what happens when a restarted item asks for the lease again under the same id.\n- **Restart and conversations:** how a retried authoring run gets its conversation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":287,"cache_read_input_tokens":590770,"output_tokens":496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":287,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":496,"cache_read_input_tokens":590770,"cache_creation_input_tokens":287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":287},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8e3bf469-e01e-4eed-8866-76e9265cf29c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfumg4sTSZBC4MMvSwEg6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e30da360-edc3-466c-a48d-9bb2bad3fa71","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:52:15.883Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
