{"parentUuid":"dd211dca-7f88-42b9-9feb-bd25fcdb8dec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfumif4Z2MXsh8MHZaDgS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013LbYVv5SaqmoYDCbrgo7d8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p1F | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\"; $H close w30:tZ >/dev/null"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":591553,"output_tokens":166,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":427,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":166,"cache_read_input_tokens":591553,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":427},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013LbYVv5SaqmoYDCbrgo7d8":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p1F | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\"; $H close w30:tZ >/dev/null"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a5faa36d-7bd8-44fd-9c01-6dc4cbcc871e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfumieU66uJ2L3ia3Sngg","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"195b322c-4644-46b9-83dd-177e925ccd43","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:52:47.495Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"195b322c-4644-46b9-83dd-177e925ccd43","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"26211e23-3579-4ea7-8a84-f90dfedeaa3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013LbYVv5SaqmoYDCbrgo7d8","type":"tool_result","content":"done\n**Cloudflare Workflows: concurrent and nested steps** (Workers binding API, TypeScript). Checked 2026-10-11. All claims below come from documentation fetches. I ran no trial.\n\n**Sources**\n- Rules of Workflows: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/ (no date shown on the page)\n- Workers API: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/workers-api/ (no date shown)\n- Limits: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/reference/limits/ (last updated 2026-09-21)\n- Sleeping and retrying: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/sleeping-and-retrying/ (no date shown)\n- Visualizer: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/visualizer/ (reached only as a search snippet from a preview mirror; I did not fetch the page)\n\n**1. Concurrent steps**\n- The Rules page says: \"Workflows allows the usage steps within the `Promise.race()` or `Promise.any()` methods as a way to achieve concurrent steps execution.\"\n- The same page has a state example that uses `await Promise.all([...])` over two `step.do` calls. It is only an example of state handling. No rule is stated about it.\n- `Promise.allSettled` is not mentioned on any page I fetched.\n- The Limits page has no row for concurrent steps per instance. Its only concurrency limits are on instances: 100 on Free, 50,000 on Paid.\n- Other limits that apply to 25 steps:\n  - 10,000 steps per instance (Paid, default).\n  - 10,000 subrequests per instance (Paid, default).\n  - 1 MiB maximum result per step.\n- A search snippet says the dashboard visualizer shows `Promise.all()` steps as a \"ParallelNode\". This is unconfirmed because I did not fetch that page.\n\n**2. Nested steps**\n- The docs don't address a `step.do` callback calling `step.do`. Nothing forbids it and nothing permits it. I could not confirm either way.\n- The only nesting example is a `step.do` wrapped around a `Promise.race` of steps. The comment on it says: \"The `Promise.race` is surrounded by a `step.do`, ensuring deterministic caching behavior.\"\n\n**3. A step that throws after exhausting retries**\n- Quote: \"Any error not handled at this top level will cause the Workflow instance to fail.\" (Workers API)\n- Quote: \"surround the intended steps that are allowed to fail with a `try...catch` block.\" The example comment says \"the Workflow will not fail and will continue its execution.\" (Sleeping and retrying)\n- The docs only demonstrate try/catch around a single awaited `step.do`. They say nothing about `Promise.allSettled`.\n- The Rules page warns about a step that is not awaited: \"exceptions being swallowed (and not terminating the Workflow).\"\n- Whether `Promise.allSettled` catches an exhausted step and keeps the instance running is unconfirmed. By the documented pattern it should. A trial would settle it.\n\n**4. Naming and replay**\n- Quote: \"Steps should be named deterministically (that is, not using the current date/time, randomness, etc).\" (Rules)\n- Quote: \"Step names act as the 'cache key' in your Workflow.\"\n- The loop example is commented \"it's fine to dynamically name steps (e.g: create a step per list entry)\", with the name `` `get cat: ${cat}` ``.\n- Replay:\n  - \"If the engine restarts, the step logic will be preserved, but logic outside of the steps may be duplicated.\"\n  - A restarted step \"will start over from the beginning of that step.\"\n- For `Promise.race`, the step returned first \"may not be the actual cached step\", which is why it should be wrapped in a `step.do`.\n- Behavior of concurrent steps across a deploy is unconfirmed. Nothing in the fetched pages covers it.\n\n**5. Official parallel fan-out example**\n- I found none with `Promise.all` or `Promise.allSettled` over a list of steps.\n- The only official code is the two-step `Promise.all` state example and the `Promise.race` example, both on the Rules page.\n- The search surfaced no official Cloudflare guide beyond the pages above.\n\n**Not verified**\n- No trial run on workerd or deployed.\n- The Workers API page didn't mention `Promise.all`.\n- I did not look at the changelog or the `cloudflare/workers-sdk` or `workflows` repos for behavior or release notes.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ecb2b162-9c78-4e3f-9df2-59e46e6bbb7d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:52:48.665Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\n**Cloudflare Workflows: concurrent and nested steps** (Workers binding API, TypeScript). Checked 2026-10-11. All claims below come from documentation fetches. I ran no trial.\n\n**Sources**\n- Rules of Workflows: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/ (no date shown on the page)\n- Workers API: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/workers-api/ (no date shown)\n- Limits: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/reference/limits/ (last updated 2026-09-21)\n- Sleeping and retrying: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/sleeping-and-retrying/ (no date shown)\n- Visualizer: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/visualizer/ (reached only as a search snippet from a preview mirror; I did not fetch the page)\n\n**1. Concurrent steps**\n- The Rules page says: \"Workflows allows the usage steps within the `Promise.race()` or `Promise.any()` methods as a way to achieve concurrent steps execution.\"\n- The same page has a state example that uses `await Promise.all([...])` over two `step.do` calls. It is only an example of state handling. No rule is stated about it.\n- `Promise.allSettled` is not mentioned on any page I fetched.\n- The Limits page has no row for concurrent steps per instance. Its only concurrency limits are on instances: 100 on Free, 50,000 on Paid.\n- Other limits that apply to 25 steps:\n  - 10,000 steps per instance (Paid, default).\n  - 10,000 subrequests per instance (Paid, default).\n  - 1 MiB maximum result per step.\n- A search snippet says the dashboard visualizer shows `Promise.all()` steps as a \"ParallelNode\". This is unconfirmed because I did not fetch that page.\n\n**2. Nested steps**\n- The docs don't address a `step.do` callback calling `step.do`. Nothing forbids it and nothing permits it. I could not confirm either way.\n- The only nesting example is a `step.do` wrapped around a `Promise.race` of steps. The comment on it says: \"The `Promise.race` is surrounded by a `step.do`, ensuring deterministic caching behavior.\"\n\n**3. A step that throws after exhausting retries**\n- Quote: \"Any error not handled at this top level will cause the Workflow instance to fail.\" (Workers API)\n- Quote: \"surround the intended steps that are allowed to fail with a `try...catch` block.\" The example comment says \"the Workflow will not fail and will continue its execution.\" (Sleeping and retrying)\n- The docs only demonstrate try/catch around a single awaited `step.do`. They say nothing about `Promise.allSettled`.\n- The Rules page warns about a step that is not awaited: \"exceptions being swallowed (and not terminating the Workflow).\"\n- Whether `Promise.allSettled` catches an exhausted step and keeps the instance running is unconfirmed. By the documented pattern it should. A trial would settle it.\n\n**4. Naming and replay**\n- Quote: \"Steps should be named deterministically (that is, not using the current date/time, randomness, etc).\" (Rules)\n- Quote: \"Step names act as the 'cache key' in your Workflow.\"\n- The loop example is commented \"it's fine to dynamically name steps (e.g: create a step per list entry)\", with the name `` `get cat: ${cat}` ``.\n- Replay:\n  - \"If the engine restarts, the step logic will be preserved, but logic outside of the steps may be duplicated.\"\n  - A restarted step \"will start over from the beginning of that step.\"\n- For `Promise.race`, the step returned first \"may not be the actual cached step\", which is why it should be wrapped in a `step.do`.\n- Behavior of concurrent steps across a deploy is unconfirmed. Nothing in the fetched pages covers it.\n\n**5. Official parallel fan-out example**\n- I found none with `Promise.all` or `Promise.allSettled` over a list of steps.\n- The only official code is the two-step `Promise.all` state example and the `Promise.race` example, both on the Rules page.\n- The search surfaced no official Cloudflare guide beyond the pages above.\n\n**Not verified**\n- No trial run on workerd or deployed.\n- The Workers API page didn't mention `Promise.all`.\n- I did not look at the changelog or the `cloudflare/workers-sdk` or `workflows` repos for behavior or release notes.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a5faa36d-7bd8-44fd-9c01-6dc4cbcc871e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"195b322c-4644-46b9-83dd-177e925ccd43","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd