{"parentUuid":"ee6e8ee0-9573-4c6f-9695-a21f58d52cb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfumj1EGECeRPs4GmcUhP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1721,"cache_read_input_tokens":591980,"output_tokens":1545,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":172},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1721,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1545,"cache_read_input_tokens":591980,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1721,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1721},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1834,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"ab5d8e4a-6563-4c75-b7c0-848de7218759","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfumizNfU3c7CtygVt8gD","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c8bf6a0-aa86-4c15-9e9b-d7e5ec00715e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:52:53.095Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"4c8bf6a0-aa86-4c15-9e9b-d7e5ec00715e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfumj1EGECeRPs4GmcUhP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KHjGFVMgvm9ekaFnbGLPqV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('briefs/spike-restart-resolve.md').read()\nhead=s.split(\"## Question\")[0]\ntask=\"\"\"## Question\n\nCan one Cloudflare Workflow instance run many `step.do` calls concurrently, keep running when some or all of them fail after exhausting their retries, and can a `step.do` callback contain `step.do` calls?\n\nWhy it matters: the item Workflow's describe phase makes up to 25 Gemini calls, one per image or code block. The design wants each call to be its own step with its own retries and timeout, run concurrently, and the instance (the parent) must not fail even if every child fails.\n\n## What to build\n\nWork in /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/spikes/parallel-steps/ (create it). Reference sibling spikes `item-workflow/` and `restart-resolve/` for wrangler, bindings and D1 setup; their resources are deleted.\n\n- One Worker `nagara-spike-parallel-wf` with a Workflow and routes to create an instance with params (how many children, which ones fail, child duration), read its status and an event log, and restart it from a named step.\n- Children: `describe 0` … `describe N-1`, each `step.do` with `retries: { limit: 1, delay: '1 second' }` and a timeout, sleeping a configurable time with a fetch to a slow public URL or `scheduler.wait`, then succeeding or throwing per params. Each child writes start and end rows to D1 (`instance, step, attempt, event, at_ms`).\n- Variants to run, one variable per round:\n  1. `Promise.allSettled` over 25 children, all succeed: are they concurrent (overlapping start/end times) and how many at once?\n  2. Same, 5 children fail on every attempt: does the instance continue past the fan-out and complete?\n  3. All 25 fail: does it still continue and complete?\n  4. `Promise.all` instead with one failing child, and a try/catch around it: does the instance continue?\n  5. A parent `step.do` whose callback runs the children `step.do` calls: is it accepted, are the children recorded as steps, and what does a child failure do to the parent?\n  6. Add a step `after` following the fan-out that fails once (flag in D1); restart from `after`: do the finished children replay from cache (no new D1 start rows)?\n- One D1 database `nagara-spike-parallel-db`.\n\nDeployed, not wrangler dev. Record status() and the REST step list if reachable with the existing OAuth wrangler session (do not create tokens).\n\n## Output\n\nWrite FINDINGS.md in the spike folder: Question, Answer (one paragraph per variant, with numbers), What was run, Measurements, Surprises, New questions, Cleanup (every resource created and confirmation it was deleted, including `wrangler workflows delete`, since `wrangler delete` leaves the Workflow behind). Reply with the answers and a short table, under 400 words.\n</supervisor-agent>\n\"\"\"\nopen('briefs/spike-parallel-steps.md','w').write(head+task)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"nagara-spike-\" briefs/spike-parallel-steps.md; H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"spike: parallel steps\" --model opus --body-file briefs/spike-parallel-steps.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1721,"cache_read_input_tokens":591980,"output_tokens":1545,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":172},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1721,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","ite