{"parentUuid":"7153fb9a-d6e2-43a6-afa4-6b2e82a8c265","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfumwna7G8BTpWeURfouP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":595495,"output_tokens":1156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":566},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1156,"cache_read_input_tokens":595495,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5816,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"59d94193-67ac-46e8-ac12-f0d8723d971c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfumwmwuiFPtX8s2PSbfV","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"71df3de4-4a22-462c-ad3c-14e5b42c2fe8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:55:50.599Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"71df3de4-4a22-462c-ad3c-14e5b42c2fe8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfumwna7G8BTpWeURfouP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recorded:\n- **Describe never fails the item.** The parent step finishes even when every child fails, so the code-block rule goes.\n- **D3:** the spoken form and the drop get a step of their own. Today they run right after extraction and before image acquisition, so I'm placing the new step after release and before images: fetch, lease, recipe, release, **spoken**, images, describe, start synthesis, poll, store. Tell me if it belongs elsewhere.\n\n**The lease, with an example.** Item A's recipe step fails after A took example.com's lease. A's instance ends errored, and DomainQueue's alarm sees that within 60 s and frees the lease, so item B, waiting behind A, gets it and starts extracting. Then a client retries A, and A restarts from recipe. The lease step doesn't run again, because its result is cached. So A runs recipe while B holds the lease, and two items from example.com extract at once. That's the gap.\n\nYour rule, that the same id asking again gets the lease, covers a restart from fetch or lease, because then A asks again and is granted. A restart from recipe never asks. What should happen there?\n\n**Conversations, for a domain with no recipe.** Workflows stores a step's return value, not the agent's conversation. The conversation lives in the Flue agent's own Durable Object, keyed by a conversation id. Today that id is the instance id, plus `-<attempt>` for the step's own retries.\n- **A step retrying on its own:** the attempt number changes, so each attempt gets a new conversation.\n- **After a restart:** the instance id is the same, and the attempt count starts again at 1. The retried authoring run gets the same conversation id as the first run, so it reattaches to that conversation with its history.\n\nShould a retried authoring run continue the earlier conversation, or start a fresh one?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":595495,"output_tokens":1156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":566},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1156,"cache_read_input_tokens":595495,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"59d94193-67ac-46e8-ac12-f0d8723d971c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfumwmwuiFPtX8s2PSbfV","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8baf3b81-c634-4d6a-a5a4-463113b210c3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:55:55.793Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
