{"parentUuid":"34431582-a17d-4550-886f-5d4797bdddb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfun93Q9en84WvYVoDPAy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012UxBXogWtPLXKYFEiGgVJu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > recording-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# Decisions made while recording the design (2026-10-11)\n\nThese settle gaps the docs drafters raised. They amend design.md where noted.\n\n## Proposals confirmed\n- P1 An item that waits longer than the lease step's 1 h timeout × 3 attempts fails like any step out of attempts.\n- P2 A not-an-article verdict fails the item without retrying the step.\n- P3 The tts ledger row is written by the store step, with the finished state.\n- P4 An image's hash is taken over the stored bytes (the WebP, or the SVG after its scripts are stripped).\n- P5 The retry route claims the item with one conditional write (status still failed, count under the cap) that also increments retry_count.\n- P6 The synthesis result type lives in the pipeline Worker.\n- P7 Image download limits stay: 2 per host, 10 overall, 10 s timeout, 10 MB cap.\n- P8 extraction_domain stays on the item row.\n- P9 Cassette matching rules and filters carry over; the Access-header filter goes.\n- P10 The pipeline Worker reads the tunnel hostname from configuration.\n- P11 Local D1 gets its schema from common/'s migrations applied with wrangler against the shared folder.\n- P12 The local-development note warns that a Workflow instance running during a dev-server reload never resumes; restart it through the retry route.\n- P13 The charter's \"without opening api/app or tts/app.py\" is updated.\n\n## Answers\n- D1 A failed item's error is the step's own error; current_step names the step. No phase prefixes.\n- D2 Only values the Workflow needs and the row does not hold pass between steps as step results (the fetched HTML, Modal's call id, the synthesis result). Units and degradations are written to the row as soon as a step produces them, and later steps read them from there. The API shows units only once the item is ready.\n- D3 The spoken form and the drop of units with no letter or digit run at the end of the recipe step.\n- D4 describe fans out one step per description (pending the parallel-steps spike on concurrency and nesting). The describe phase never fails the item, even when every description fails; the rule that an item fails when every code block failed goes.\n- D5 The Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying common/'s migrations.\n- D6 common/'s CI workflow applies the migrations; the pipeline and API workflows wait for it to succeed before continuing.\n- D7 Invariant 6's half-supplied-credentials rule is dropped.\n- D8 The recipe step's 15-minute timeout stays in recipes.md (one measured authoring run took 97 s).\n- Lease on retry: a retry whose failed step is recipe or release restarts from the lease step, so the item asks for its domain's lease again and recipe re-reads the domain's current recipe. The same instance id asking for the lease again is granted it.\n- Agent conversations are keyed by the instance id alone, with no attempt suffix, so a step's own retries and a restart continue the same conversation.\n\n## Today's behaviour (scout, for reference)\n- The release step runs on every terminal today because agent errors and verdicts are returned values; DomainQueue's alarm (60 s) frees the lease of an instance that completed, errored or was terminated.\n- Today the spoken form is derived and empty units dropped right after extraction resolves, before describe; describe never drops.\n- One measured authoring run took 97 s; the 100-turn limit is in the prompt only.\nEOF\necho ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":598000,"output_tokens":1944,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":698},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1944,"cache_read_input_tokens":598000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012UxBXogWtPLXKYFEiGgVJu":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration && cat > recording-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# Decisions made while recording the design (2026-10-11)\n\nThese settle gaps the docs drafters raised. They amend design.md where noted.\n\n## Proposals confirmed\n- P1 An item that waits longer than the lease step's 1 h timeout × 3 attempts fails like any step out of attempts.\n- P2 A not-an-article verdict fails the item without retrying the step.\n- P3 The tts ledger row is written by the store step, with the finished state.\n- P4 An image's hash is taken over the stored bytes (the WebP, or the SVG after its scripts are stripped).\n- P5 The retry route claims the item with one conditional write (status still failed, count under the cap) that also increments retry_count.\n- P6 The synthesis result type lives in the pipeline Worker.\n- P7 Image download limits stay: 2 per host, 10 overall, 10 s timeout, 10 MB cap.\n- P8 extraction_domain stays on the item row.\n- P9 Cassette matching rules and filters carry over; the Access-header filter goes.\n- P10 The pipeline Worker reads the tunnel hostname from configuration.\n- P11 Local D1 gets its schema from common/'s migrations applied with wrangler against the shared folder.\n- P12 The local-development note warns that a Workflow instance running during a dev-server reload never resumes; restart it through the retry route.\n- P13 The charter's \"without opening api/app or tts/app.py\" is updated.\n\n## Answers\n- D1 A failed item's error is the step's own error; current_step names the step. No phase prefixes.\n- D2 Only values the Workflow needs and the row does not hold pass between steps as step results (the fetched HTML, Modal's call id, the synthesis result). Units and degradations are written to the row as soon as a step produces them, and later steps read them from there. The API shows units only once the item is ready.\n- D3 The spoken form and the drop of units with no letter or digit run at the end of the recipe step.\n- D4 describe fans out one step per description (pending the parallel-steps spike on concurrency and nesting). The describe phase never fails the item, even when every description fails; the rule that an item fails when every code block failed goes.\n- D5 The Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying common/'s migrations.\n- D6 common/'s CI workflow applies the migrations; the pipeline and API workflows wait for it to succeed before continuing.\n- D7 Invariant 6's half-supplied-credentials rule is dropped.\n- D8 The recipe step's 15-minute timeout stays in recipes.md (one measured authoring run took 97 s).\n- Lease on retry: a retry whose failed step is recipe or release restarts from the lease step, so the item asks for its domain's lease again and recipe re-reads the domain's current recipe. The same instance id asking for the lease again is granted it.\n- Agent conversations are keyed by the instance id alone, with no attempt suffix, so a step's own retries and a restart continue the same conversation.\n\n## Today's behaviour (scout, for reference)\n- The release step runs on every terminal today because agent errors and verdicts are returned values; DomainQueue's alarm (60 s) frees the lease of an instance that completed, errored or was terminated.\n- Today the spoken form is derived and empty units dropped right after extraction resolves, before describe; describe never drops.\n- One measured authoring run took 97 s; the 100-turn limit is in the prompt only.\nEOF\necho ok"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_012UxBXogWtPLXKYFEiGgVJu":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a010d5b1-f071-4afb-823a-bd936ff91a84","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfun92hE4JhHw8fncZigd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2da1280b-67ec-4198-80f8-402c036d0d01","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:58:34.095Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
