{"parentUuid":"e1812b58-a53a-4941-8855-089c27b61b29","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfunKMSdhgeDcpSo1oTn3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019gV3rKZbNfXSNAJxVW7fst","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; tail -2 /tmp/claude-1000/-home-agus-workspace-asermax-nagara/f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e/tasks/btbg9bjkq.output; $H collect w30:p1H | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_read_input_tokens":600612,"output_tokens":227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":600612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":426},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019gV3rKZbNfXSNAJxVW7fst":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; tail -2 /tmp/claude-1000/-home-agus-workspace-asermax-nagara/f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e/tasks/btbg9bjkq.output; $H collect w30:p1H | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message'))\""}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6160525b-bba1-4eaa-aff2-fc5ee68658ea","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfunKLtPotchBzuzdJzfm","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e72d7484-9ae4-4e5f-878e-192cdf0b840f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:00:40.571Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"e72d7484-9ae4-4e5f-878e-192cdf0b840f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d9e00f24-2908-4c0a-98e9-596935c1bcfc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019gV3rKZbNfXSNAJxVW7fst","type":"tool_result","content":"[exited with code 0]\ndone\nAll three answers are yes. One instance runs 25 `step.do` calls at once, finishes normally when some or all of them fail after their retries, and accepts `step.do` calls inside a `step.do` callback. Every variant ran on the deployed Worker, and every instance ended `complete` (v6 after its restart).\n\n1. **25 children, all succeed:** all 25 started within 96 ms of each other and all 25 ran at the same time. The fan-out took 5.3 s with 5 s children. When each child made a 5 s `fetch` instead of sleeping, the 25 steps still started together, but the requests completed in batches of 6 and the last finished at 26 s. This matches the Workers limit of 6 open outbound connections, which applies to the whole instance, across all its steps.\n2. **5 of 25 fail on every attempt:** the 5 retries started about 1.1 s after the failures. The fan-out returned 20 ok and 5 failed at 7.7 s, and `status()` showed `complete` with `error: null`.\n3. **All 25 fail:** 25 first attempts and 25 retries ran, the fan-out returned 0 ok at 7.7 s, and the instance still completed.\n4. **`Promise.all` with one failing child, in a try/catch:** the catch ran and the instance completed. I added one variation (4b): the failing child fails after 500 ms, the others sleep 8 s, and the catch does not wait for them. The instance reported `complete` at 2.3 s while 24 children were still running. They finished at 8.2 s and showed up later in the step list as `success: true`.\n5. **Nested `step.do`:** accepted. The children run concurrently and the step list records them as ordinary top-level steps next to `parent-1`. If the parent throws because a child failed, the parent step fails and the instance continues. If the parent has a retry, the retry runs all 25 children again as new steps (`describe i-2`): 52 child starts in total, none reused.\n6. **Restart from `after`:** the 25 finished children came back from cache in 337 ms with no new D1 start rows. The 2 failed children were not retried either, because a failed step is cached the same way as a successful one.\n\n| Variant | Failing | Concurrent | Fan-out done | Final status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| v1 timer / fetch | 0 | 25 / 6 fetches | 5.3 s / 26.0 s | complete |\n| v2 allSettled | 5 | 25 | 7.7 s | complete |\n| v3 allSettled | 25 | 25 | 7.7 s | complete |\n| v4 all + catch | 1 | 25 | 7.3 s | complete |\n| v4b no wait in catch | 1 | 25 | 2.3 s (children end 8.2 s) | complete |\n| v5 nested | 0 / 5 / 1 + parent throws | 25 | 3.6 / 7.8 / 7.6 s | complete |\n| v5e nested, parent retry | 1 | 25 | 16.4 s | complete, 52 child starts |\n| v6 restart from `after` | 2 | 25 | replay 0.34 s | errored → complete, 0 new starts |\n\nOne run (v5d) started seconds after a deploy and still ran the previous version; I discarded it and re-ran it as v5e.\n\n**New questions:**\n- Do D1 and AI Gateway calls count against the 6-connection limit?\n- Does time spent waiting for a free connection count toward a step's `timeout`? The last fetch child took 26 s of its 60 s timeout.\n- How many concurrent steps can one instance run before Workflows throttles them? Only 25 were tried.\n\n**Cleanup:** I deleted Worker `nagara-spike-parallel-wf` (its URL now returns 404), the Workflow of the same name with `wrangler workflows delete`, and D1 database `nagara-spike-parallel-db`. None of them appear in the wrangler lists anymore.\n\nEverything is in `spikes/parallel-steps/`; open `FINDINGS.md` first, and the raw output is in `results/`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1d5b95d4-964a-4f69-842d-21225786bdbd","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:00:41.144Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"[exited with code 0]\ndone\nAll three answers are yes. One instance runs 25 `step.do` calls at once, finishes normally when some or all of them fail after their retries, and accepts `step.do` calls inside a `step.do` callback. Every variant ran on the deployed Worker, and every instance ended `complete` (v6 after its restart).\n\n1. **25 children, all succeed:** all 25 started within 96 ms of each other and all 25 ran at the same time. The fan-out took 5.3 s with 5 s children. When each child made a 5 s `fetch` instead of sleeping, the 25 steps still started together, but the requests completed in batches of 6 and the last finished at 26 s. This matches the Workers limit of 6 open outbound connections, which applies to the whole instance, across all its steps.\n2. **5 of 25 fail on every attempt:** the 5 retries started about 1.1 s after the failures. The fan-out returned 20 ok and 5 failed at 7.7 s, and `status()` showed `complete` with `error: null`.\n3. **All 25 fail:** 25 first attempts and 25 retries ran, the fan-out returned 0 ok at 7.7 s, and the instance still completed.\n4. **`Promise.all` with one failing child, in a try/catch:** the catch ran and the instance completed. I added one variation (4b): the failing child fails after 500 ms, the others sleep 8 s, and the catch does not wait for them. The instance reported `complete` at 2.3 s while 24 children were still running. They finished at 8.2 s and showed up later in the step list as `success: true`.\n5. **Nested `step.do`:** accepted. The children run concurrently and the step list records them as ordinary top-level steps next to `parent-1`. If the parent throws because a child failed, the parent step fails and the instance continues. If the parent has a retry, the retry runs all 25 children again as new steps (`describe i-2`): 52 child starts in total, none reused.\n6. **Restart from `after`:** the 25 finished children came back from cache in 337 ms with no new D1 start rows. The 2 failed children were not retried either, because a failed step is cached the same way as a successful one.\n\n| Variant | Failing | Concurrent | Fan-out done | Final status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| v1 timer / fetch | 0 | 25 / 6 fetches | 5.3 s / 26.0 s | complete |\n| v2 allSettled | 5 | 25 | 7.7 s | complete |\n| v3 allSettled | 25 | 25 | 7.7 s | complete |\n| v4 all + catch | 1 | 25 | 7.3 s | complete |\n| v4b no wait in catch | 1 | 25 | 2.3 s (children end 8.2 s) | complete |\n| v5 nested | 0 / 5 / 1 + parent throws | 25 | 3.6 / 7.8 / 7.6 s | complete |\n| v5e nested, parent retry | 1 | 25 | 16.4 s | complete, 52 child starts |\n| v6 restart from `after` | 2 | 25 | replay 0.34 s | errored → complete, 0 new starts |\n\nOne run (v5d) started seconds after a deploy and still ran the previous version; I discarded it and re-ran it as v5e.\n\n**New questions:**\n- Do D1 and AI Gateway calls count against the 6-connection limit?\n- Does time spent waiting for a free connection count toward a step's `timeout`? The last fetch child took 26 s of its 60 s timeout.\n- How many concurrent steps can one instance run before Workflows throttles them? Only 25 were tried.\n\n**Cleanup:** I deleted Worker `nagara-spike-parallel-wf` (its URL now returns 404), the Workflow of the same name with `wrangler workflows delete`, and D1 database `nagara-spike-parallel-db`. None of them appear in the wrangler lists anymore.\n\nEverything is in `spikes/parallel-steps/`; open `FINDINGS.md` first, and the raw output is in `results/`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6160525b-bba1-4eaa-aff2-fc5ee68658ea","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remo