{"parentUuid":"75601387-8182-4566-8a72-4e33531a5416","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfunkGXf8qNAc8asktFHT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018GBGL2g5bkMgUQDvRTvBHw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w30:p14 --body \"<supervisor-agent>\nOne addition to item-lifecycle.md: the note needs one end-to-end mermaid diagram of the whole pipeline, placed near the top after the Overview. It shows, in one picture: the client enqueueing through the API Worker (the row written with queued, the instance created), the item Workflow's steps in order (fetch, lease, recipe with the spoken form and drop at its end, release, images, describe as a parent step fanning out to child describe steps, start synthesis, poll, store), the service or store each step reaches (Firecrawl, DomainQueue, the recipe runtime and Flue agents, the Images binding, AI Gateway, Modal, R2, D1), where the status moves (queued for fetch and lease, generating after, ready or failed at the end), the retry path (the retry route writes queued and restarts the instance from current_step, or from lease when the failed step is recipe or release), and the client reading the ready item and its audio. Use the colour and shape palette the design's diagrams use (classDef: blue rect API Worker, green pipeline parts with the Workflow as subproc, orange cyl stores, violet cloud outside services, grey stadium client). Validate it, keep node text under 24 characters per line, and add it to both item-lifecycle.md and item-lifecycle.edits.md. Reply in under 100 words.\n</supervisor-agent>\"; $H wait w30:p14 --timeout 5000 >/dev/null 2>&1; echo"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":608554,