job or workflow: subproc, green; a shared piece several components use: hex, amber; an interface or payload crossing a boundary: braces, amber (#fef3c7 / #d97706); a store: cyl, orange (#ffedd5 / #ea580c); an external service: cloud, violet (#ede9fe / #7c3aed); a decision: diam, blue; a failure or dropped outcome: rect, red (#fee2e2 / #dc2626). Keep Filadd's other rows (background job st-rect, wait delay) with a colour. Show the classDef block once as a copyable example. Say the same palette applies to state diagrams through classDef.\n- Keep superpowers' existing \"Rendering rules the validator cannot catch\" (long lines clipped at about 24 characters in containers; braces and <br/> in sequence messages) and add: after a diagram validates, render it and look at the image before showing it, since a diagram that parses can still draw wrong; a `;` inside state-diagram text (a note, a transition label) ends the statement and the rest renders as stray states, so use a comma; markdown such as **bold** inside an `@{ shape, label }` label renders as plain text; a subgraph's `direction` is ignored when edges cross its border, so set the layout direction on the whole flowchart, and a flowchart that grows too wide in one direction is redrawn in the other.\n- The description says it is loaded to choose, write, style and validate mermaid diagrams; the skill name is `mermaid`.\n\nAlso draft the list of every reference to update (do not edit them): grep /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins for `mermaid-validation` and list each file with the line and the replacement text, including the two sync skills under .claude/skills/ (sync-to-filadd's mapping row becomes superpowers:mermaid -> filadd-experimental-dev:mermaid, and sync-to-filadd gains one instruction: when syncing this skill to Filadd, keep Filadd's Notion shape whitelist, its check in the validator and the Notion sections, which superpowers does not carry).\n\nOutput: the full skill tree as files in learn/round2/mermaid/ (SKILL.md, references/*.md; for the script, a note saying it stays as is or the diff), plus learn/round2/mermaid/REFERENCES.md with the reference updates. Then an editing pass on your prose: no em dashes, no filler, active voice, no metaphors, plain words. Reply with the files written, under 150 words.\n</supervisor-agent>\nEOF\ncat > briefs/learn-canvas-ports.md <<'EOF'\n<supervisor-agent>\nDraft a change to a script. Write drafts only, under /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2/canvas/ ; edit nothing in the plugin, commit nothing.\n\nScript: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/skills/canvas/scripts/canvas.sh (read it whole, and the server code it starts under scripts/app/ only as far as needed to see how the port and the health check work). Today one server runs at a time: one PID file in the cache, `start` stops whatever document is served on the port, and CANVAS_PORT picks another port by hand.\n\nJob: several canvases can run at once, one server per document. `start` for a document already served returns its URL. Otherwise it picks the first free port from 5190 up, starts the server there, and records the document, port and PID in a per-document state file in the cache (for example keyed by a hash of the document's absolute path). `watch`, `export` and `stop` act on that document's own server, found through its state file and confirmed by the health check, which answers with the served document's path. `stop` stops only that document's server. Stale state files (dead PID, or the port serving another document) are cleaned up. CANVAS_PORT, when set, is still honoured as the port to use. The server log moves to a per-document file. No `pkill` or killing by pattern anywhere.\n\nOutput: learn/round2/canvas/canvas.sh (the full new script) and learn/round2/canvas/canvas.sh.diff (unified diff against the current one). Test it without touching any running canvas: run two documents under /tmp at once on free ports, check both URLs answer with their own document, stop one and confirm the other still answers, then stop the second; stop only the processes you started, by PID. Report the test in two lines. Reply under 150 words.\n</supervisor-agent>\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"learn: mermaid skill\" --model opus --body-file briefs/learn-mermaid.md; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"learn: canvas ports\" --model opus --body-file briefs/learn-canvas-ports.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":609854,"output_tokens":2461,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":104},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2461,"cache_read_input_tokens":609854,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018KCCrvzfiqp4h5nLgWnLmp":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2; cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; cat > briefs/learn-mermaid.md <<'EOF'\n<supervisor-agent>\nDraft a replacement skill. Write drafts only, under /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2/mermaid/ ; edit nothing in any plugin, commit nothing.\n\nJob: `superpowers:mermaid` replaces `superpowers:mermaid-validation` (/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/superpowers/skills/mermaid-validation/). Port