{"parentUuid":"a90e301d-75f8-4b73-8f79-ba9cbd433316","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfunuYwt3HiFSm5wSsiEd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DDDESezRpQcwCri16oK1m3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2; sed -n '/^Interface: a table/,/^Outputs: a class/p' /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/skills/design/references/types/contract.md | head -3; cat > 07-design-types-and-canvas-refs.md <<'EOF'\n# 07 Design types draw in the mermaid palette; contract interfaces per member; canvas references for design-with-canvas\n\nLands in: `mahou/skills/design/references/types/contract.md`, `component-architecture.md`, `data-flow.md`, `lifecycle.md`, `rules.md`; new `mahou/skills/design-with-canvas/references/types/contract.md` and `data-flow.md`; a table in `mahou/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`.\n\n## contract.md, Representation: replace the Interface paragraph, its table, and the Outputs paragraph with its class diagram\n\nOld: \"Interface: a table of what each member answers and who asks, the same form the note template uses for what a part exposes.\" with its table, and \"Outputs: a class diagram, one class per part of the value, then prose per part. …\" with its class diagram.\n\nNew:\n\nInterface and outputs: one flowchart per member, captioned `<member> · <when it is called>`. The caller and the component sit at the two ends. The call is a solid arrow from the caller through a braces box holding what the call sends, to the component; the return is a dashed arrow from the component through a braces box holding what comes back, to the caller, labelled `returns`. A member that returns nothing has no return arrow. Each braces box lists its interface's name, then one line per field with its type, then in parentheses what the values mean. A value nested in another gets its own braces box, joined to its parent by a plain line. Style it with superpowers:mermaid's palette.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  caller@{ shape: rect, label: \"Caller\" } -->|\"create\"| inp@{ shape: braces, label: \"CreateParams\n  resourceId: string\n  (the row the caller just wrote)\" }\n  inp --> comp@{ shape: subproc, label: \"Component\" }\n  comp -.-> out@{ shape: braces, label: \"Instance\n  id: string\n  (stored on the row)\" }\n  out -.->|\"returns\"| caller\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef payload fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  class caller worker\n  class comp flow\n  class inp,out payload\n```\n\nThe prose for each member states what the diagram cannot: when the member is called, what an absent field means, who validates the value and what an invalid one does to the caller.\n\n## component-architecture.md, Representation, append\n\nDraw each component, store and outside service with its kind's shape and colour from superpowers:mermaid's palette, so the diagram reads without a legend.\n\n## data-flow.md, Representation, append\n\nStyle the participants and nodes with superpowers:mermaid's palette.\n\n## lifecycle.md, Representation, append\n\nColour each state by what it means for whoever reads it, with `classDef`: a waiting state amber, a working state blue, a done state green, a failed state red. Keep `;` out of notes and transition labels.\n\n## rules.md, Representation, append\n\nColour the flowchart with superpowers:mermaid's palette: steps green, decisions blue, an outcome that drops or fails red, what gets stored orange.\n\n## design-with-canvas/SKILL.md, after \"Use `design`'s types for the representations…\"\n\nNew paragraph and table:\n\nDraw a representation as its canvas reference under `references/types/` describes, when one exists; otherwise as `design`'s type describes. Each canvas reference has the same file name as the type it adapts.\n\n| The branch is about | `design` type | Canvas reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| What a component agrees with the rest of the system | `contract.md` | `references/types/contract.md` |\n| How a value moves between components | `data-flow.md` | `references/types/data-flow.md` |\n\n## New file: design-with-canvas/references/types/contract.md\n\n# Contract on the canvas\n\nDraw one `mermaid` shape per member, in the form `design`'s contract type gives, each under a caption `<member> · <when it is called>` in the hand font, stacked in the order the members are called. A branch with several boundaries draws each boundary's members under that boundary's sub-branch heading. Draw no table and no separate class diagram: the braces boxes inside each flowchart carry the interfaces.\n\n## New file: design-with-canvas/references/types/data-flow.md\n\n# Data flow on the canvas\n\nThe canvas's `mermaid` shape draws sequence diagrams with their labels out of place. Draw a data flow as a left-to-right flowchart instead: the components as nodes in the palette's shapes, each arrow numbered in the order of the path (`1 GET the audio`, `2 the item exists?`), and the prose naming the steps by number. Use a sequence diagram in the final document only when the document's renderer draws it correctly.\nEOF\necho done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3462,"cache_read_input_tokens":620889,"output_tokens":2227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":291},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3462,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2227,"cache_read_input_tokens":620889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3462},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"i