estamp":"2026-10-11T04:14:00.494Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"bcc3cd9d-b41d-45ff-bc30-e6468731016f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ece8269f-7650-4df3-a0c3-c4fd69b081ab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AAzDRCXRqbcB7NHdks4mBe","type":"tool_result","content":"learn: mermaid skill\nI wrote the drafts under `learn/round2/mermaid/`. Nothing in any plugin was edited and nothing was committed.\n\n- **`SKILL.md`**: name `mermaid`, ported from Filadd's skill with the Notion parts removed. It keeps the superpowers validator, which reads the diagram on stdin, and adds the new rendering rules plus a step to render the diagram and look at it.\n- **`references/flowchart.md`**: the shape table now has a colour column and is the default palette, with one copyable `classDef` block.\n- **`references/state-diagram.md`**: new, in the same shape as the others, and it uses the same palette.\n- **`references/class-diagram.md`, `er-diagram.md`, `sequence-diagram.md`**: ported and edited (no em dashes, no filler).\n- **`scripts/README.md`**: `validate-mermaid.sh` moves to the new directory unchanged.\n- **`REFERENCES.md`**: every `mermaid-validation` match with its line and replacement text, including both sync skills and the Notion instruction for sync-to-filadd.\n\nBoth worked examples pass the validator and rendered correctly. The render command (mermaid-cli) fails until a headless Chrome is installed and `PUPPETEER_EXECUTABLE_PATH` points to it, so `SKILL.md` includes that setup. I installed that browser into `~/.cache/puppeteer`.\nlearn: canvas ports\nI wrote both drafts under `learn/round2/canvas/`: the new `canvas.sh` and `canvas.sh.diff`. Nothing in the plugin was edited and nothing was committed.\n\n- **State:** each document gets `servers/<sha256-16>.state` (document, port, PID) and its own `.log` in the cache.\n- **Start:** it returns the URL if the document's server is already up. Otherwise it takes the first free port from 5190, or `CANVAS_PORT` if set. If vite fails because another server grabbed the port, it tries the next one.\n- **Stale files:** they are removed when the PID is dead or the port serves another document.\n- **Stop:** it kills only the PID in the state file, after the health check confirms the document.\n\nTest: two `/tmp` documents came up on 5191 and 5192, and each URL answered with its own path. Your canvas on 5190 was skipped and left running. Stopping A left B answering; stopping B ended its PID. I removed the test files afterwards.\n\n**Open risks:**\n- All servers share vite's dependency cache in the app folder, so first-time startups running together could collide.\n- A canvas started by the current script has no state file. The new `start` reuses it, but the new `stop` can't stop it.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dd1c59d7-6569-4d85-b571-c71cfd93ef0b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:14:02.340Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"learn: mermaid skill\nI wrote the drafts under `learn/round2/mermaid/`. Nothing in any plugin was edited and nothing was committed.\n\n- **`SKILL.md`**: name `mermaid`, ported from Filadd's skill with the Notion parts removed. It keeps the superpowers validator, which reads the diagram on stdin, and adds the new rendering rules plus a step to render the diagram and look at it.\n- **`references/flowchart.md`**: the shape table now has a colour column and is the default palette, with one copyable `classDef` block.\n- **`references/state-diagram.md`**: new, in the same shape as the others, and it uses the same palette.\n- **`references/class-diagram.md`, `er-diagram.md`, `sequence-diagram.md`**: ported and edited (no em dashes, no filler).\n- **`scripts/README.md`**: `validate-mermaid.sh` moves to the new directory unchanged.\n- **`REFERENCES.md`**: every `mermaid-validation` match with its line and replacement text, including both sync skills and the Notion instruction for sync-to-filadd.\n\nBoth worked examples pass the validator and rendered correctly. The render command (mermaid-cli) fails until a headless Chrome is installed and `PUPPETEER_EXECUTABLE_PATH` points to it, so `SKILL.md` includes that setup. I installed that browser into `~/.cache/puppeteer`.\nlearn: canvas ports\nI wrote both drafts under `learn/round2/canvas/`: the new `canvas.sh` and `canvas.sh.diff`. Nothing in the plugin was edited and nothing was committed.\n\n- **State:** each document gets `servers/<sha256-16>.state` (document, port, PID) and its own `.log` in the cache.\n- **Start:** it returns the URL if the document's server is already up. Otherwise it takes the first free port from 5190, or `CANVAS_PORT` if set. If vite fails because another server grabbed the port, it tries the next one.\n- **Stale files:** they are removed when the PID is dead or the port serves another document.\n- **Stop:** it kills only the PID in the state file, after the health check confirms the document.\n\nTest: two `/tmp` documents came up on 5191 and 5192, and each URL answered with its own path. Your canvas on 5190 was skipped and left running. Stopping A left B answering; stopping B ended its PID. I removed the test files afterwards.\n\n**Open risks:**\n- All servers share vite's dependency cache in the app folder, so first-time startups running together could collide.\n- A canvas started by the current script has no state file. The new `start` reuses it, but the new `stop` can't stop it.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fb3118cf-aa27-4828-bbf9-223c686251ad","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"gi