{"parentUuid":"5f473251-1b0c-4b2c-8b27-17f11ae07d92","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_015DyPACK4VNB7sZzitbgevt","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"af43642b-6931-46f2-b866-46e463db390d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:14:30.574Z","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"af43642b-6931-46f2-b866-46e463db390d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuoNTvWQdd7tazjcPyon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recorded:\n- **Title:** the recipe step writes it together with the units.\n- **Describe children:** each child step gets 1 minute per attempt.\n\n**The 15-minute auto-fail has two open points.**\n- **Who fails the item.** Nothing in the design runs on a timer. The candidates are the poll route, which can fail a queued item when it reads one older than 15 minutes, as today's `queued_at` ceiling does, or a scheduled sweep. Whichever it is needs a time to measure from: `queued_at` is gone, and `updated_at` is the last write to the row.\n- **The lease wait.** An item waiting for its domain's lease behind another article stays queued, and the lease step allows up to 1 hour per attempt, 3 attempts. A 15-minute queued limit would fail items that are legitimately waiting their turn. Does the limit count from enqueue, or from the last status write? Does it apply while an item waits for the lease?\n\n**The command lines.** `CLAUDE.md` has a \"Layout and commands\" block listing the commands for each tree. Today the `api/` line is `uv sync · alembic upgrade head · uvicorn …`. After the migration `api/` is TypeScript, and `common/` is new. The drafter wrote pnpm and wrangler commands for both, copied from the pipeline's, because that code doesn't exist yet. Should I keep those guessed lines, or leave `api/` and `common/` out of the block until their commands exist?\n\nThe unslop pass over the learn drafts is running. I'll show you all the drafts in one message when it's done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_tokens":635757,"output_tokens":517,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_f