{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:25:12.947Z","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","content":"Plannotator: Claude's recent messages (pn-8ef4d9) — Feedback · 4 comments.\n\n# Message Annotations\n\n# Message Feedback\n\nThe following feedback spans 1 assistant message. Each section includes an excerpt of the message it applies to.\n\n## Message 1\n\nMessage excerpt:\n```markdown\nAll the learn drafts are below, each written to `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2/` and through both unslop rounds. Approve, correct or drop each one separately.\n\n## 1. Every text in tldraw's default font\n\n**`mahou/skills/canvas/SKILL.md`, Drawing**\n\nOld:\n\n- Text is black, arrow labels included.\n\nNew:\n\n- Text is black, arrow labels included, and written in tldraw's default font, the hand font (`font: 'draw'`): prose, notes, labels and cards alike. Use the monospace font only where the loading skill asks for it, such as a tree of leaves.\n\n## 2. Sizing a geo shape set from a script\n\n**`mahou/skills/canvas/SKILL.md`, Drawing, a new bullet after \"Resize an area whenever what it holds grows or moves\"**\n\n- **Set `growY: 0` whenever a script sets a geo shape's `h`.** tldraw keeps the `growY` it computed for the earlier size, and the shape stays taller than what it holds. To stack shapes inside a geo shape under its label, read the label's height first: the height of the shape's `.tl-rich-text` element divided by the zoom level.\n\n## 3. Questions under the write-up\n\n**`mahou/skills/design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, Questions**\n\nOld: Questions go in the open branch, at the top of its r...\n```\n\n# Feedback for Message 1\n\nI've reviewed this message and have 4 pieces of feedback:\n\n## 1. (line 331) Feedback on: \"mahou:program-design is an exception: it proposes the details of a design whose decisions are already settled, grounded in the code and the conventions, and the user corrects each proposal. \"\n> thtis should be on the program design skill, not here\n\n## 2. (line 335) Feedback on: \"When an open decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions the tree already settled or from how the code works today, do not ask it as a question. List it as a proposal, with the decision or the behaviour it follows from, and ask the user to confirm or correct each proposal. A confirmed proposal becomes a ✓ leaf; a corrected one becomes a ✓ leaf with the user’s answer. A decision that more than one answer could reasonably settle stays a question.\"\n> it should still show as a question on the tree, what changes is the way it's deliveerd to the user\n\n## 3. (line 337) Remove this\n```\nmahou/skills/design-tree/SKILL.md, What a question carries, a new sentence after the list of things that propose an answer\n\nThese rules do not apply to a proposal made under the paragraph on decisions with one plausible answer.\n```\n> I don't want this in the message.\n\n## 4. (line 377) Feedback on: \"Draw a representation as its canvas reference under references/types/ describes, when one exists; otherwise as design‘s type describes. Each canvas reference has the same file name as the type it adapts.\"\n> it should read both the design and this skills representation for context, and use the canvas one for the canvvas and the design one for the final text\n\n---\n\nPlease address the annotation feedback above."}
