conventions, and the user corrects each proposal. \"\n> thtis should be on the program design skill, not here\n\n## 2. (line 335) Feedback on: \"When an open decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions the tree already settled or from how the code works today, do not ask it as a question. List it as a proposal, with the decision or the behaviour it follows from, and ask the user to confirm or correct each proposal. A confirmed proposal becomes a ✓ leaf; a corrected one becomes a ✓ leaf with the user’s answer. A decision that more than one answer could reasonably settle stays a question.\"\n> it should still show as a question on the tree, what changes is the way it's deliveerd to the user\n\n## 3. (line 337) Remove this\n```\nmahou/skills/design-tree/SKILL.md, What a question carries, a new sentence after the list of things that propose an answer\n\nThese rules do not apply to a proposal made under the paragraph on decisions with one plausible answer.\n```\n> I don't want this in the message.\n\n## 4. (line 377) Feedback on: \"Draw a representation as its canvas reference under references/types/ describes, when one exists; otherwise as design‘s type describes. Each canvas reference has the same file name as the type it adapts.\"\n> it should read both the design and this skills representation for context, and use the canvas one for the canvvas and the design one for the final text\n\n---\n\nPlease address the annotation feedback above.\n\nThis is how Claude Code surfaces a prompt a plugin submits between turns — it starts this turn in the user's place. Address the message above."},"uuid":"2da57f9f-bef9-4071-a22e-4d73f5da1cea","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:25:12.992Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"plugin","name":"plannotator"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"system","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":69,"turnIndex":210},"queuePriority":"later","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.