{"parentUuid":"5f71f329-4316-443c-9901-f4410c1d50d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfupD8eWdCn4f9G625VBB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012mNRDsEuq8xYUsZkxmqrYq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2; cat > 06-propose-the-obvious.md <<'EOF'\n# 06 Proposing an answer when only one is plausible\n\nLands in: `mahou/skills/basics/SKILL.md` rule 2, `mahou/skills/program-design/SKILL.md` (one phrase), and `mahou/skills/design-tree/SKILL.md`.\n\n## basics, rule 2\n\nOld:\n\n2. **Never decide for the user.** Map the state, then ask. No recommendations, no leaning toward an option, no answering for them. Give a recommendation only when the user asks for one. mahou:program-design is the one exception: it proposes the details of a design whose decisions are already settled, grounded in the code and the conventions, and the user corrects each proposal.\n\nNew:\n\n2. **Never decide for the user.** Map the state, then ask. No recommendations, no leaning toward an option, no answering for them. Give a recommendation only when the user asks for one. When a decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions already settled or from how the code already works, propose that answer with the fact it follows from and ask the user to confirm or correct it, instead of asking the question open.\n\n## program-design, \"What this skill does\" paragraph\n\nOld: That is why this skill is the one exception to the rule in `basics` against recommending: a proposal grounded in the code and the conventions is a fact for the user to correct, not a choice made for them.\n\nNew: That is why this skill proposes, against the rule in `basics` against recommending: a proposal grounded in the code and the conventions is a fact for the user to correct, not a choice made for them.\n\n## design-tree, after \"State a decision the user already made…\"\n\nNew paragraph:\n\nWhen an open decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions the tree already settled or from how the code works today, it stays a ❔ leaf in the tree like any other question, and it is asked as a proposal: the round states the answer and the decision or the behaviour it follows from, and asks the user to confirm or correct it. The leaf becomes ✓ with the answer the user confirms or gives. A decision that more than one answer could reasonably settle is asked open.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='07-design-types-and-canvas-refs.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"Draw a representation as its canvas reference under `references/types/` describes, when one exists; otherwise as `design`'s type describes. Each canvas reference has the same file name as the type it adapts.\",\"For a branch whose type has a canvas reference under `references/types/`, read both the type in `design` and the canvas reference: draw the canvas as the canvas reference describes, and write `design.md` and the final documentation in the type's own form. A type with no canvas reference is drawn in its own form. Each canvas reference has the same file name as the type it adapts.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"read both\" 07-design-types-and-canvas-refs.md | cut -c1-80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_read_input_tokens":677797,"output_tokens":1360,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":304},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1928,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1360,"cache_read_input_tokens":677797,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012mNRDsEuq8xYUsZkxmqrYq":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2; cat > 06-propose-the-obvious.md <<'EOF'\n# 06 Proposing an answer when only one is plausible\n\nLands in: `mahou/skills/basics/SKILL.md` rule 2, `mahou/skills/program-design/SKILL.md` (one phrase), and `mahou/skills/design-tree/SKILL.md`.\n\n## basics, rule 2\n\nOld:\n\n2. **Never decide for the user.** Map the state, then ask. No recommendations, no leaning toward an option, no answering for them. Give a recommendation only when the user asks for one. mahou:program-design is the one exception: it proposes the details of a design whose decisions are already settled, grounded in the code and the conventions, and the user corrects each proposal.\n\nNew:\n\n2. **Never decide for the user.** Map the state, then ask. No recommendations, no leaning toward an option, no answering for them. Give a recommendation only when the user asks for one. When a decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions already settled or from how the code already works, propose that answer with the fact it follows from and ask the user to confirm or correct it, instead of asking the question open.\n\n## program-design, \"What this skill does\" paragraph\n\nOld: That is why this skill is the one exception to the rule in `basics` against recommending: a proposal grounded in the code and the conventions is a fact for the user to correct, not a choice made for them.\n\nNew: That is why this skill proposes, against the rule in `basics` against recommending: a proposal grounded in the code and the conventions is a fact for the user to correct, not a choice made for them.\n\n## design-tree, after \"State a decision the user already made…\"\n\nNew paragraph:\n\nWhen an open decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions the tree already settled or from how the code works today, it stays a ❔ leaf in the tree like any other question, and it is asked as a proposal: the round states the answer and the decision or the behaviour it follows from, and asks the user to confirm or correct it. The leaf becomes ✓ with the answer the user confirms or gives. A decision that more than one answer could reasonably settle is asked open.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='07-design-types-and-canvas-refs.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"Draw a representation as its canvas reference under `references/types/` describes, when one exists; otherwise as `design`'s type describes. Each canvas reference has the same file name as the type it adapts.\",\"For a branch whose type has a canvas reference under `references/types/`, read both the type in `design` and the canvas reference: draw the canvas as the canvas reference describes, and write `design.md` and the final documentation in the type's own form. A type with no canvas reference is drawn in its own form. Each canvas reference has the same file name as the type it adapts.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"read both\" 07-design-types-and-canvas-refs.md | cut -c1-80"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dae023ac-bc67-4cb3-a3d7-fe346ba173ba","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfupD7xLTd5qw8h8BDQ4s","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"67298fef-a527-4b07-9c6c-80ca5c966a99","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:25:36.534Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round2","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
