{"parentUuid":"f370e2ba-c9ca-49ea-ab38-b17e25d4b70a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfupGEQMu2SwVbnzs11sc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Md1dwTAqJGEmcgDEtCrGmx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins && git status --short | head; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,os\nM='mahou/skills/'\ndef rep(path, pairs):\n    s=open(path).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        if a not in s: print(\"MISSING in\",path,\":\",a[:70]); continue\n        s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n    open(path,'w').write(s)\n# 1 font, 3 growY (canvas)\nrep(M+'canvas/SKILL.md',[\n(\"- Text is black, arrow labels included.\",\"- Text is black, arrow labels included, and written in tldraw's default font, the hand font (`font: 'draw'`): prose, notes, labels and cards alike. Use the monospace font only where the loading skill asks for it, such as a tree of leaves.\"),\n(\"- `start` installs the app on first run, starts the server detached and prints the URL to give the user. One server runs at a time: starting another document stops the server for the first, whose document is already on disk. It refuses a document saved in an older format and names the `migrate` command.\",\"- `start` installs the app on first run, starts a detached server for the document on the first free port from 5190 and prints the URL to give the user. A document that already has a server gets its URL back. Each document has its own server, so several canvases run at once, in one project or in several; `CANVAS_PORT` picks the port instead. It refuses a document saved in an older format and names the `migrate` command.\"),\n(\"- `stop` stops the server.\",\"- `stop` stops the document's own server and leaves every other canvas running.\"),\n])\ns=open(M+'canvas/SKILL.md').read()\ni=s.index(\"- **Resize an area whenever\")\nj=s.index(\"\\n\",i)\ns=s[:j+1]+\"- **Set `growY: 0` whenever a script sets a geo shape's `h`.** tldraw keeps the `growY` it computed for the earlier size, and the shape stays taller than what it holds. To stack shapes inside a geo shape under its label, read the label's height first: the height of the shape's `.tl-rich-text` element divided by the zoom level.\\n\"+s[j+1:]\nopen(M+'canvas/SKILL.md','w').write(s)\n# 4,5 questions & opening tree\nrep(M+'design-with-canvas/SKILL.md',[\n(\"Questions go in the open branch, at the top of its right side, above its write-up.\",\"Questions go in the open branch, on its right side, under its write-up. The branch's Claude note goes under the questions.\"),\n(\"The opening tree goes on the canvas as the branch areas, each one pending, with no leaves yet.\",\"The opening tree goes on the canvas as the branch areas, each one pending, with no leaves yet. Above the areas, a Claude note says in one line per branch what that branch settles.\"),\n])\nrep(M+'shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md',[\n(\"Questions go in the open branch, at the top of its right side, above its prose.\",\"Questions go in the open branch, on its right side, under its prose. The branch's Claude note goes under the questions.\"),\n(\"with the ✓ leaves the user brought under their areas and no prose yet.\",\"with the ✓ leaves the user brought under their areas and no prose yet. Above the areas, a Claude note says in one line per branch what that branch settles.\"),\n])\n# 7 basics, program-design, design-tree\nrep(M+'basics/SKILL.md',[(\"Give a recommendation only when the user asks for one. mahou:program-design is the one exception: it proposes the details of a design whose decisions are already settled, grounded in the code and the conventions, and the user corrects each proposal.\",\"Give a recommendation only when the user asks for one. When a decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions already settled or from how the code already works, propose that answer with the fact it follows from and ask the user to confirm or correct it, instead of asking the question open.\")])\nrep(M+'program-design/SKILL.md',[(\"That is why this skill is the one exception to the rule in `basics` against recommending:\",\"That is why this skill proposes, against the rule in `basics` against recommending:\")])\nrep(M+'design-tree/SKILL.md',[(\"The user corrects a leaf that is wrong; the corrected leaf goes back to ❔ and joins the next frontier.\",\"The user corrects a leaf that is wrong; the corrected leaf goes back to ❔ and joins the next frontier.\\n\\nWhen an open decision has only one plausible answer, because it follows from decisions the tree already settled or from how the code works today, it stays a ❔ leaf in the tree like any other question, and it is asked as a proposal: the round states the answer and the decision or the behaviour it follows from, and asks the user to confirm or correct it. The leaf becomes ✓ with the answer the user confirms or gives. A decision that more than one answer could reasonably settle is asked open.\")])\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42,"cache_read_input_tokens":682198,"output_tokens":1806,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":138},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1806,"cache_read_input_tokens":682198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Md1dwTAqJGEmcgDEtCrGmx":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins && git status --short | head; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,os\