:"2026-10-11T04:27:15.330Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"5eab99a1-e71b-4ae8-87e9-51bd07397747","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"100ff23d-76c2-456a-9c05-6aa0096c8be8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VAfxTFpY1h9JxxnQ87upsy","type":"tool_result","content":"== docs: item lifecycle done\nI updated `item-lifecycle.md` and regenerated `item-lifecycle.edits.md`:\n- **Title:** the recipe step now writes it with the units, so `ready` writes only the timed units, duration and format.\n- **Describe children:** each child step gets 3 attempts of 1 minute.\n- **Stuck `queued` items:** the note now says nothing fails them automatically.\n\nThe decisions conflict on one point. The retry route returns 409 for a `queued` item, yet the note also says the route restarts a local item stuck in `queued`. Should retry accept a stuck `queued` item?\n== docs: storage contract auth done\nI changed one sentence in `persistence-and-storage.md` and its `.edits.md`: the recipe step now writes the title together with the units. None of my three notes mentions the describe children's per-attempt timeout or stuck queued items, so `item-contract` and `authentication` stay as they were. The CLAUDE.md and charter items are for the drafter that owns CLAUDE.md, not me.\n== docs: deploy invariants claude done\nI updated `CLAUDE.md` and its edits file: the commands block no longer has the `api/` and `common/` lines. I also drafted `README-charter.md` and its edits file, where the line now reads \"without opening `api/`, `pipeline/` or `tts/app.py` first.\"\n\nThe other three second-round decisions (title written with the units, describe children's 1-minute attempts, no automatic failure of queued items) change nothing in my notes.\n\nThe charter still cites markdown-it-py, a Python library, in its folder example. I left that line alone because it was not in the brief.\n== docs: tts extraction recipes describer done\nI applied the second-round decisions to the full notes and their `.edits.md` files:\n\n- **article-extraction:** the recipe step now writes the title into the row together with its units.\n- **image-and-code-describer:** each describe child step gets 3 attempts of 1 minute each. The connection-wait warning now names that 1-minute timeout.\n\nNothing in my four notes says queued items fail automatically, so that decision needed no change. The CLAUDE.md commands block and the charter fix belong to the CLAUDE.md drafter, so I left them alone.\n== docs: new notes done\nI made no changes: none of the second-round decisions changes a statement in `common-package.md` or `local-development.md`. Neither note mentions the title, the units write or describe timeouts. Stuck queued items still fit, because the local-development note only has the developer restart them by hand.\n\nMy earlier question is still open. P5 lets the retry route claim only failed items, so it would refuse a stuck queued item, yet the notes restart those items through it.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8b037213-efd1-42df-ab1f-ff2238efec6e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:27:16.136Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"== docs: item lifecycle done\nI updated `item-lifecycle.md` and regenerated `item-lifecycle.edits.md`:\n- **Title:** the recipe step now writes it with the units, so `ready` writes only the timed units, duration and format.\n- **Describe children:** each child step gets 3 attempts of 1 minute.\n- **Stuck `queued` items:** the note now says nothing fails them automatically.\n\nThe decisions conflict on one point. The retry route returns 409 for a `queued` item, yet the note also says the route restarts a local item stuck in `queued`. Should retry accept a stuck `queued` item?\n== docs: storage contract auth done\nI changed one sentence in `persistence-and-storage.md` and its `.edits.md`: the recipe step now writes the title together with the units. None of my three notes mentions the describe children's per-attempt timeout or stuck queued items, so `item-contract` and `authentication` stay as they were. The CLAUDE.md and charter items are for the drafter that owns CLAUDE.md, not me.\n== docs: deploy invariants claude done\nI updated `CLAUDE.md` and its edits file: the commands block no longer has the `api/` and `common/` lines. I also drafted `README-charter.md` and its edits file, where the line now reads \"without opening `api/`, `pipeline/` or `tts/app.py` first.\"\n\nThe other three second-round decisions (title written with the units, describe children's 1-minute attempts, no automatic failure of queued items) change nothing in my notes.\n\nThe charter still cites markdown-it-py, a Python library, in its folder example. I left that line alone because it was not in the brief.\n== docs: tts extraction recipes describer done\nI applied the second-round decisions to the full notes and their `.edits.md` files:\n\n- **article-extraction:** the recipe step now writes the title into the row together with its units.\n- **image-and-code-describer:** each describe child step gets 3 attempts of 1 minute each. The connection-wait warning now names that 1-minute timeout.\n\nNothing in my four notes says queued items fail automatically, so that decision needed no change. The CLAUDE.md commands block and the charter fix belong to the CLAUDE.md drafter, so I left them alone.\n== docs: new notes done\nI made no changes: none of the second-round decisions changes a statement in `common-package.md` or `local-development.md`. Neither note mentions the title, the units write or describe timeouts. Stuck queued items still fit, because the local-development note only has the developer restart them by hand.\n\nMy earlier question is still open. P5 lets the retry route claim only failed items, so it would refuse a stuck queued item, yet the notes restart those items through it.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d63d31d8-5769-459a-bbbf-73c23cc773f7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/a