{"parentUuid":"6311c44f-d576-4e83-ada9-74acc7d9077f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfupYHZKAJds8quGEwDkb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MYHtgoFzv3JZAL6xC5KQF1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration && cat >> recording-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Third round\n- An item queued for more than 15 minutes is retried automatically. The item row keeps queued_at again: set when the item is enqueued and rewritten whenever it is queued again. When the API reads an item whose status is queued and whose queued_at is more than 15 minutes old, it queues the item again: it restarts the item's instance (creates one when the row holds no instance id), and rewrites queued_at. This applies to items stuck locally as well, so a developer does not restart them by hand.\n- The charter's examples name whatever the code uses after the migration (the pipeline's markdown parser instead of markdown-it-py, the TypeScript trees instead of api/app).\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper\nfor p in w30:p14 w30:p15 w30:p16 w30:p17 w30:p18; do $H prompt $p --body \"<supervisor-agent>\nrecording-decisions.md has a Third round section (read it). Apply what bears on your notes, in the full notes and their .edits.md: queued_at comes back on the item row; the API re-queues an item queued for more than 15 minutes when it reads it (restarting its instance, or creating one when the row has no instance id) and rewrites queued_at; this also covers items stuck locally. Do not state whether an automatic re-queue counts toward the 3 client retries. The drafter of CLAUDE.md and the charter also updates the charter's examples to what the code uses after the migration: read pipeline/package.json and pipeline/src for the markdown parser the pipeline uses and name it instead of markdown-it-py. Reply under 80 words.\n</supervisor-agent>\" >/dev/null && echo \"sent $p\"; done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":140,"cache_read_input_tokens":695680,"output_tokens":2001,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":140,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2001,"cache_read_input_tokens":695680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":140},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MYHtgoFzv3JZAL6xC5KQF1":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration && cat >> recording-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Third round\n- An item queued for more than 15 minutes is retried automatically. The item row keeps queued_at again: set when the item is enqueued and rewritten whenever it is queued again. When the API reads an item whose status is queued and whose queued_at is more than 15 minutes old, it queues the item again: it restarts the item's instance (creates one when the row holds no instance id), and rewrites queued_at. This applies to items stuck locally as well, so a developer does not restart them by hand.\n- The charter's examples name whatever the code uses after the migration (the pipeline's markdown parser instead of markdown-it-py, the TypeScript trees instead of api/app).\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper\nfor p in w30:p14 w30:p15 w30:p16 w30:p17 w30:p18; do $H prompt $p --body \"<supervisor-agent>\nrecording-decisions.md has a Third round section (read it). Apply what bears on your notes, in the full notes and their .edits.md: queued_at comes back on the item row; the API re-queues an item queued for more than 15 minutes when it reads it (restarting its instance, or creating one when the row has no instance id) and rewrites queued_at; this also covers items stuck locally. Do not state whether an automatic re-queue counts toward the 3 client retries. The drafter of CLAUDE.md and the charter also updates the charter's examples to what the code uses after the migration: read pipeline/package.json and pipeline/src for the markdown parser the pipeline uses and name it instead of markdown-it-py. Reply under 80 words.\n</supervisor-agent>\" >/dev/null && echo \"sent $p\"; done"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2c08a5f3-9a94-4f2c-a632-e4b865517c29","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfupYGMtWDUGtJCpdroMg","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"841669a1-b2bc-44aa-a453-00be6bc35ce4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:30:04.629Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
