011CfupdHsZLnynn8kFxFiy7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"27e137d7-af2f-4fd6-8c13-637624d675cc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:30:56.032Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"27e137d7-af2f-4fd6-8c13-637624d675cc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3f9cb8ec-eb40-495b-a663-78b8faa3e833","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QyTuLMyPaMHHzqHq6zVUQK","type":"tool_result","content":"== docs: item lifecycle\nI updated `item-lifecycle.md` and regenerated `item-lifecycle.edits.md`:\n- `queued_at` is back in Modeling. Enqueue sets it and a retry rewrites it.\n- Poll re-queues an item `queued` for more than 15 minutes, which also covers items stuck locally. The diagram shows this re-queue too.\n- The retry and failure sections now point to the re-queue, not to a manual retry.\n- I did not say whether a re-queue counts toward the 3 retries.\n\nThe validator script now lives at `superpowers/skills/mermaid/scripts/validate-mermaid.sh`; all four diagrams pass.\n\nIs it intended that an item waiting over 15 minute\n== docs: storage contract auth\nI updated both notes and their `.edits.md`. The ER diagram still validates; the validator now lives under `skills/mermaid/`.\n\n- **persistence-and-storage:** the ER diagram has `queued_at` back. The modeling paragraph says it is set at enqueue and rewritten whenever the item is queued again. A `queued` item older than 15 minutes is re-queued when the API reads it: the API restarts its instance, or creates one when the row has no instance id.\n- **item-contract:** the poll row describes that re-queue, and retry also rewrites `queued_at`.\n\nNeither note says whether a re-queue counts toward the 3 r\n== docs: deploy invariants claude\nInvariant 5 now adds that the API re-queues an item when it reads one queued for more than 15 minutes. That's in `invariants.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, both with their `.edits.md`.\n\nThe pipeline has no markdown parser. Its dependencies are turndown (HTML to markdown), cheerio and domino. So the charter now reads \"the spoken-form derivation that produces that placeholder\" instead of naming a library.\n\nShould the charter name the library that does the spoken-form derivation once it exists?\n== docs: tts extraction recipes describer\nThe Third round needs no changes to my notes. None of the four (tts-service, article-extraction, recipes, image-and-code-describer) mentions queued items, stuck items, the queued-for-15-minutes re-queue or the retry route, so `queued_at` and the automatic re-queue have nothing to replace. I left the files unchanged. The charter's examples belong to the drafter of CLAUDE.md and the charter, so I did not touch them.\n== docs: new notes\nI updated `local-development.md` and its `.edits.md`. The renamed \"Re-queuing a stuck item\" section has the API re-queue an item queued over 15 minutes when it reads it: restart or create the instance, rewrite queued_at. The reload warning now says the same for an item stranded in queued. `common-package.md` is unchanged.\n\nOpen: an instance stranded by a reload in generating gets no re-queue. Should the warning say how that item recovers?\narticle-extraction.edits.md\narticle-extraction.md\nauthentication.edits.md\nauthentication.md\nCLAUDE.edits.md\nCLAUDE.md\ncommon-package.edits.md\ncommon-package.md\ndeployment-and-ci.edits.md\ndeployment-and-ci.md\nimage-and-code-describer.edits.md\nimage-and-code-describer.md\ninvariants.edits.md\ninvariants.md\nitem-contract.edits.md\nitem-contract.md\nitem-lifecycle.edits.md\nitem-lifecycle.md\nlocal-development.edits.md\nlocal-development.md\npersistence-and-storage.edits.md\npersistence-and-storage.md\nqueue.edits.md\nqueue.md\nREADME-charter.edits.md\nREADME-charter.md\nREADME.edits.md\nREADME.md\nrecipes.edits.md\nrecipes.md\ntts-service.edits.md\ntts-service.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"59127102-3d57-4c22-b77e-5b06383e7707","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:30:56.839Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"== docs: item lifecycle\nI updated `item-lifecycle.md` and regenerated `item-lifecycle.edits.md`:\n- `queued_at` is back in Modeling. Enqueue sets it and a retry rewrites it.\n- Poll re-queues an item `queued` for more than 15 minutes, which also covers items stuck locally. The diagram shows this re-queue too.\n- The retry and failure sections now point to the re-queue, not to a manual retry.\n- I did not say whether a re-queue counts toward the 3 retries.\n\nThe validator script now lives at `superpowers/skills/mermaid/scripts/validate-mermaid.sh`; all four diagrams pass.\n\nIs it intended that an item waiting over 15 minute\n== docs: storage contract auth\nI updated both notes and their `.edits.md`. The ER diagram still validates; the validator now lives under `skills/mermaid/`.\n\n- **persistence-and-storage:** the ER diagram has `queued_at` back. The modeling paragraph says it is set at enqueue and rewritten whenever the item is queued again. A `queued` item older than 15 minutes is re-queued when the API reads it: the API restarts its instance, or creates one when the row has no instance id.\n- **item-contract:** the poll row describes that re-queue, and retry also rewrites `queued_at`.\n\nNeither note says whether a re-queue counts toward the 3 r\n== docs: deploy invariants claude\nInvariant 5 now adds that the API re-queues an item when it reads one queued for more than 15 minutes. That's in `invariants.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, both with their `.edits.md`.\n\nThe pipeline has no markdown parser. Its dependencies are turndown (HTML to markdown), cheerio and domino. So the charter now reads \"the spoken-form derivation that produces that placeholder\" instead of naming a library.\n\nShould the charter name the library that does the spoken-form derivation once it exists?\n== docs: tts extraction recipes describer\nThe Third round needs no changes to my notes. None of the four (tts-service, article-extraction, recipes, image-and-code-describer) mentions queued items, stuck items, the queued-for-15-minutes re-queue or the retry route, so `queued_at` and the automatic re-queue have nothing to replace. I left the files unchanged. The charter's examples belong to the drafter of CLAUDE.md and the charter, so I did not touch them.\n== docs: new notes\nI updated `local-development.md` and its `.edits.md`. The renamed \"Re-queuing a stuck item\" section has the API re-queue an item queued over 15 minutes when it reads it: restart or create the instance, rewrite queued_at. The reload warning now says the same for an item stranded in queued. `common-package.md` is unchanged.\n\nOpen: an instance stranded by a reload in generating gets no re-queue. Should the warning say how that item recovers?\narticle-extraction.edits.md\narticle-extraction.md\nauthentication.edits.md\nauthentication.md\nCLAUDE.edits.md\nCLAUDE.md\ncommon-package.edits.md\ncommon-package.md\ndeployment-and-ci.edits.md\ndeployment-and-ci.md\nimage-and-code-describer.edits.md\nimage-and-code-describer.md\ninvariants.edits.md\ninvariants.md\nitem-contract.edits.md\nitem-contract.md\nitem-lifecycle.edits.md\nitem-lifecycle.md\nlocal-development.edits.md\nlocal-development.md\npersistence-and-storage.edits.md\npersistence-and-storage.md\nqueue.edits.md\nqueue.md\nREADME-charter.edits.md\nREADME-charter.md\nREADME.edits.md\nREADME.md\nrecipes.edits.md\nrecipes.md\ntts-service.edits.md\ntts-service.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"14de74e2-929f-4fdf-8336-cdbee972e6c9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github