{"parentUuid":"3f301ff3-821c-4b25-8afa-8d50e12db02c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfupfz3L3zYEj4eybSQm2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The docs are written, uncommitted, and the diff is open in Plannotator at http://localhost:43303:\n- **Updated:** 11 technical notes, the technical-design index, the charter and `product-design/queue.md`.\n- **Renamed:** `the-describer.md` → `image-and-code-describer.md`, with `git mv`.\n- **Deleted:** `extraction-service.md`, with `git rm`. I also repointed the two links to it in `markdown-units.md`.\n- **New:** `common-package.md` and `local-development.md`, marked intent-to-add so they appear in the diff.\n- **`CLAUDE.md`:** updated.\n\n**Two checks were skipped.** I didn't run the separate unslop pass or the documentation reviewer over these notes. Each drafter ran an editing pass on its own text, and your Plannotator review stands in for the rest.\n\n**Points the drafters raised, worth checking in the review:**\n- **Re-queue vs the lease wait:** an item waiting behind its domain's lease stays queued, and the lease step allows an hour per attempt. The 15-minute re-queue will restart such an item while it's still waiting its turn.\n- **Re-queues and the retry cap:** the notes don't say whether an automatic re-queue counts toward the 3 client retries.\n- **Stranded generating items:** an instance stranded during generating by a dev-server reload never gets a re-queue, and the local-development note doesn't say how it recovers.\n- **The charter's example:** the pipeline has no markdown parser, since it converts HTML with turndown. The charter now names \"the spoken-form derivation\" instead of a library.\n\nAll subagents are closed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":704157,"output_tokens":550,"output_tokens_details":{