{"parentUuid":"c2bd4198-f2d6-4461-8b9b-144eff154b78","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuq6gLuhe5iTn6ZYckwH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked the extraction-v2 branches. Local `feat/extraction-v2` and `origin/feat/extraction-v2` both point at `26473be` (\"shorten the lease alarm to one minute\", 2026-09-22), and neither has any commit that isn't on `main`. Deleting them loses nothing. I'll delete the local one with `git branch -d` and the remote one with `git push origin --delete feat/extraction-v2`.\n\nFor the new branch I'd use `feat/cloudflare-migration`, following `CLAUDE.md`'s `feat/<feature-name>` rule. It starts from `main` and carries the working-tree changes.\n\nThe proposed commits:\n\n**1. `docs: describe nagara on Cloudflare`**\n- Updated: `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/README.md`, `docs/product-design/queue.md`, `docs/technical-design/README.md`, `article-extraction.md`, `authentication.md`, `deployment-and-ci.md`, `invariants.md`, `item-contract.md`, `item-lifecycle.md`, `markdown-units.md`, `persistence-and-storage.md`, `recipes.md`, `tts-service.md`\n- New: `common-package.md`, `local-development.md`\n- Renamed: `the-describer.md` → `image-and-code-describer.md`\n- Deleted: `extraction-service.md`\n\n**2. `chore: add local spike rules`**\n- `.mahou/spike.md`, which is untracked. These are the project's spike rules from the earlier learn session: muted audio, and the `nagara-spike-` prefix with cleanup.\n\nProceed with both commits as listed, or merge them into one? I'll also delete the two extraction-v2 branches once you confirm."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":486,"cache_read_input_tokens":707895,"output_tokens":812,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":231},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation"