{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"f1a01712-21e5-4f75-8b83-2596ead2bb1d","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"manual","preTokens":711468,"postTokens":41983,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":1198503,"durationMs":122596,"preCompactDiscoveredTools":["Monitor","TaskStop","mcp__linear-server__get_issue","mcp__linear-server__get_milestone","mcp__linear-server__list_issues","mcp__linear-server__list_milestones","mcp__plannotator__plannotator"],"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"641a4a20-3ca6-49f5-903e-8c9f15c127a4","anchorUuid":"7b509959-cd81-4783-9a86-d370bfebbfea","tailUuid":"f1a01712-21e5-4f75-8b83-2596ead2bb1d"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"7b509959-cd81-4783-9a86-d370bfebbfea","uuids":["641a4a20-3ca6-49f5-903e-8c9f15c127a4","f1a01712-21e5-4f75-8b83-2596ead2bb1d"],"allUuids":["641a4a20-3ca6-49f5-903e-8c9f15c127a4","f1a01712-21e5-4f75-8b83-2596ead2bb1d"]}},"uuid":"4e06f449-8837-41de-a50c-b7fd20100931","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:42:16.227Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"4e06f449-8837-41de-a50c-b7fd20100931","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b65c0465-5f64-49cc-83fb-90531a66bc11","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - `/mahou:design-with-canvas` for the Cloudflare migration milestone (nagara): \"let's proceed with the design details; same approach as before, we have decided quite a bit so don't bring up something unless we really haven't decided on the topic already.\"\n   - Afterwards, record the design in `docs/` per design's Recording, via mahou:write-documentation:\n     - a scout checks every note\n     - the item Workflow and wrapper go in item-lifecycle\n     - drop `extraction-service.md` and merge it \"together with the rest of the pipeline\" (item-lifecycle)\n     - rename the describer to \"image and code describer\"\n     - a new `common-package` note, which other notes link to for their part\n     - a new `local-development` note\n     - then \"write all our docs and run a plannotator review\" and close the subagents\n   - `/mahou:learn` round 2 on the session since the last learn: apply all items, uncommitted.\n   - `/mahou:commit-changes` \"into a new branch and let's also drop the extraction v2 local and remote branches, those are stale\". This is done.\n   - Security and operational constraints carried over (verbatim intent, still in effect):\n     - never print secrets\n     - a credential the user must create is written by the user to a scratch file with `!`, and the spike deletes it\n     - stop processes by PID only, never `pkill` or `killall` or kill by pattern\n     - spike resources are prefixed `nagara-spike-` and deleted\n     - never touch the production `nagara` Worker, its Workflows and Durable Objects, the `nagara` AI Gateway's settings or the `nagara-tts` Modal app\n     - the user deletes the Modal proxy token and the R2 tokens in the dashboards\n     - commit nothing unless asked\n     - no pushing unless asked\n   - The user also said \"close all the subagents if we're done with those\". All herdr children are closed now.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Cloudflare Workers:\n     - API Worker (api/) and pipeline Worker (pipeline/)\n     - a cross-script Workflow binding (`script_name`)\n     - Workflows: `restart({from:{name}})`, `step.do`, `waitForEvent`, `Promise.allSettled` fan-out, nested steps, 10,000 steps per instance, a 6-outbound-connection limit, retention 30 days\n     - D1, R2 presigning (aws4fetch), the Images binding, AI Gateway's cache, DomainQueue DO (lease plus a 60 s alarm)\n     - Flue agents, conversations keyed by instance id\n   - Modal web endpoints with proxy auth; result without audio bytes.\n   - tldraw canvas via agent-browser:\n     - `canvas.step`, geo `growY`, measuring `.tl-rich-text`\n     - the mermaid mock shape, sized from the viewBox\n   - Mermaid:\n     - `@{ shape }`, braces, subproc, stadium, cyl, cloud, classDef palette\n     - state-diagram `;` pitfall\n     - subgraph direction ignored when edges cross its border\n     - the validator `superpowers/skills/mermaid/scripts/validate-mermaid.sh` (stdin)\n   - herdr subagents (`herdr-helper spawn/prompt/wait/collect/close`); the mahou agent body is pasted into the brief.\n   - The design tree, design types, plannotator.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Scratch folder** `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/`:\n     - `design.md`: the full settled tree, 10 branches with prose and mermaid. Later amended: `queued_at` is kept again, plus the 15-minute re-queue leaf.\n     - `status.md`:\n       - Stage: \"design recorded in `docs/`, committed on branch `feat/cloudflare-migration` (not pushed). Next: the user's review of the docs, then mahou:tasks.\"\n       - Tracking: delete the Modal proxy token and revoke the R2 tokens.\n     - `recording-decisions.md`: P1–P13, D1–D9, lease and conversation rules, Second and Third rounds.\n       - Key decisions:\n         - errors are the step's own error, with no prefixes\n         - only values not on the row pass as step results; units and degradations are written as produced, and the API shows units only when ready\n         - spoken form and drop at the end of the recipe step\n         - describe is a wrapped parent step with children under allSettled, children return results and the parent writes once; children get 1 min per attempt; describe never fails the item\n         - tests apply common/ migrations\n         - pipeline and API CI wait for common's workflow\n         - invariant 6's credential rule is dropped\n         - a retry of recipe or release restarts from lease; the same id re-asking the lease is granted\n         - agent conversation id = instance id, no attempt suffix\n         - the recipe step writes the title with the units\n         - `queued_at` is back; the API re-queues an item queued >15 min on read (restarts the instance, or creates one when there's no id) and rewrites `queued_at`\n         - CLAUDE.md commands block omits api/ and common/\n         - the charter examples name what the code uses\n     - `docs-impact.md` (scout report), `docs-drafts/` (all drafts plus `.edits.md`).\n     - `canvas/design.tldr.json`: the design canvas, stopped.\n     - `spikes/restart-resolve/`: `restart()` resolves on acceptance in 0.4–0.6 s, status queued; the step starts 3.1–3.8 s later; no-arg restart reruns all steps.\n     - `spikes/parallel-steps/`:\n       - 25 concurrent steps; fetches are capped at 6 per instance\n       - with allSettled, failed children don't fail the instance\n       - nested children are recorded top-level, and a parent retry reruns all children\n       - a restart replays the cached children\n     - `README.md` spike table: both spikes added.\n     - `learn/round2/`: drafts plus unslop reports. `briefs/`: all briefs.\n   - **nagara repo, committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration`:**\n     - `c0dbdba docs: describe nagara on Cloudflare`:\n       - updated: CLAUDE.md, docs/README.md (charter), product-design/queue.md, technical-design README, article-extraction, authentication, deployment-and-ci, invariants, item-contract, item-lifecycle (with the end-to-end \"🗺️ How an item moves through the system\" diagram), markdown-units (links repointed from extraction-service to item-lifecycle), persistence-and-storage, recipes, tts-service\n       - new: common-package.md, local-development.md\n       - the-describer.md renamed to image-and-code-describer.md\n       - extraction-service.md deleted\n     - `54cb15d chore: add local spike rules` (`.mahou/spike.md`).\n     - Local and remote `feat/extraction-v2` deleted. Not pushed.\n   - **claude-plugins, uncommitted:**\n     - `mahou/skills/canvas/SKILL.md`:\n       - multi-server start/stop text\n       - \"Text is black, arrow labels included, and written in tldraw's default font, the hand font (`font: 'draw'`)…\"\n       - a `growY: 0` bullet\n     - `mahou/skills/canvas/scripts/canvas.sh`:\n       - a per-document state in `$CACHE/servers/<sha256-16>.state` holding doc, port and PID, plus a per-doc log\n       - first free port from 5190 to 5289, or `CANVAS_PORT`\n       - `find_server`, `launch`, `sweep`\n       - stop by PID\n     - `design-with-canvas/SKILL.md` and `shape-with-canvas/SKILL.md`:\n       - questions under the write-up or prose, with the Claude note under the questions\n       - an opening-tree Claude note with one line per branch\n       - design-with-canvas only: a \"read both type and canvas reference\" paragraph and a table\n     - New `design-with-canvas/references/types/contract.md` and `data-flow.md`. The data-flow one says to use a numbered flowchart on the canvas, because sequence diagrams misrender there.\n     - `basics/SKILL.md` rule 2: the program-design sentence is removed, and an obvious-answer proposal is added.\n     - `program-design/SKILL.md`: \"That is why this skill proposes, against the rule in `basics` against recommending:\".\n     - `design-tree/SKILL.md`: a new paragraph saying a one-plausible-answer decision stays a ❔ leaf and is asked as a proposal.\n     - `design/references/types/contract.md`: Interface and outputs become one flowchart per member, with braces boxes and a dashed `returns`.\n     - Palette sentences appended to component-architecture, data-flow, lifecycle and rules.\n     - `wiki/references/cloudflare/workflows.md`:\n       - restart details and timings\n       - no hooks\n       - concurrency and the 6-connection limit\n       - nesting\n       - `wrangler workflows delete`\n     - `superpowers/skills/mermaid/`: `git mv` from mermaid-validation (rename staged).\n       - new SKILL.md with a render step through mmdc and puppeteer, and the extra rendering rules\n       - `references/` (flowchart with the palette table and colours, state-diagram new, class, er, sequence)\n       - the script is unchanged\n     - Reference updates:\n       - CLAUDE.md, README.md, superpowers/README.md, mahou/README.md\n       - report, program-design, write-documentation, design and lookup skills\n       - sync-upstream\n       - sync-to-filadd: split mapping row, renamed pair, git log path, Notion divergence bullet\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Port collision with the filadd canvas.** I used `CANVAS_PORT=5191`, which led to learn item 1 (multi-server).\n   - **Sans font used for prose.** The user asked why; I switched to `draw`. This became learn item 2.\n   - **Geo growY stale, cards overlapping.** Set `growY: 0` and measure the label via the DOM. Learn item 3.\n   - **Representations in branch 3.** The user rejected several forms in turn: monospace tables, a single class diagram, sequence diagrams (misrendered in the canvas), context diagrams. It ended with per-method mermaid flowcharts with braces, colours and shapes, and the first shape changes didn't apply until I fixed the script injection. Learn items 7 and 8.\n   - **`;` in a state note** created stray states. Replaced with a comma.\n   - **LR flowchart with a TB subgraph** came out too wide. Switched to flowchart TB.\n   - **Mannered or rule-breaking text.** A metaphor (\"phone book\") was removed, and so was a candidate list in Q17. Question placement was overridden by the user.\n   - **Questions the user saw as unnecessary** (job index, Modal payloads). The user said to propose obvious answers; this became the learn rule.\n   - **CDP \"Promise was collected\".** I verified the state afterwards.\n   - **Wrong herdr pane id.** I re-armed the wait with the correct id.\n   - **git add of an already-staged rename path failed.** Re-ran without those paths.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Gaps between the design and the docs were resolved through the P and D rounds, two spikes (restart-resolve, parallel-steps), a researcher pass and scouts. The scouts covered the job index and today's lease, conversation and spoken-form handling, plus authoring time (97 s).\n   - Conflicts flagged and resolved:\n     - the CI rule vs invariant 8: scoped to common/ changes, and a failure stops the whole deploy\n     - the code-block failure rule, replaced by \"describe never fails\"\n     - retry vs stuck items, settled with the 15-minute re-queue\n   - Still open, from the drafters, unresolved:\n     - an item waiting >15 min for its domain lease gets re-queued\n     - whether a re-queue counts toward the 3 retries\n     - how an instance stranded during generating by a dev reload recovers locally\n\n6. All user messages (condensed, in order):\n   - `/mahou:design-with-canvas` \"let's proceed with the design details; same approach as before, we have decided quite a bit so don't bring up something unless we really haven't decided on the topic already\"\n   - Voice messages during the canvas design:\n     - Tree and approvals: \"can you give me a short explanation of each of the topics\", \"this looks fine let's move on\", \"why is the text using a different font than the normal canvas one\", \"the questions should go under the summary\".\n     - Q1: keep the workflow ID and derive state from it, keep `updated_at`. Q1.1: use the instance id while running and the item's finished state after.\n     - Q2: alternatives? advantages? Single bucket with prefixes. Reuse for the same article? \"use only the item ID\". Extension on the image key, then \"keep the content hash only\". A bucket usage diagram?\n     - Q3: \"add a cash property\". Q5: the API writes at creation and the pipeline updates the final state. Q6: use the scout, \"I don't understand…\", \"if the new process… doesn't need the job index then we can just drop it\". Q7: the pipeline should sign.\n     - Q8: the API creates the item instance, the workflow writes its id. Q9: \"what do we need… other than the current status\", then \"keep returning the same output\", later \"drop it\". Q8.1: no instance id means queued, and how long can an item wait. Q10: \"do you need to ask this… previous implementation\", \"do we need to poll\", \"keep the polling and move on\".\n     - Branch 3 representation: a better interface view; a table from canvas elements; split the branch; a small context diagram; keep only the interacting components; one diagram for all, then \"pretty bad\", then two separate diagrams, one per method plus class diagrams, clearer, \"understandable on its own\", \"a lot better… use mermaid… include the actual interfaces\", include the class diagram, braces shape and colours, different shapes, \"nevermind they changed now\".\n     - Branch 2: apply the colours.\n     - Branch 4: status lives on the item, the workflow updates it. Q12: easy retry? token? Look it up. The workflow keeps track of the current step. Q13: back to generating; not sure API or workflow; a middleware? A wrapper with generic step logic; avoid showing failed. Wait for the start? Validate when the promise resolves. \"keep moving while we wait for the spike\". Retry endpoint sets queued.\n     - Branch 5: no output needed. Q14: keep queued, wrapper configurable per step. Q15: keep today's handling, skip deploy and buffered event.\n     - Branches 6–9 approved. Branch 10 for common: CI check (only when common is modified, and the whole deployment fails); move everything common in; no runtime checks.\n   - Docs recording:\n     - \"send a scout… workflow and wrapper on item lifecycle… common package… local deployment needs its own document\"\n     - \"drop the extraction service and put it together with the rest of the pipeline; rename 'the describer' to 'image and code describer'; the rest looks good\"\n     - Annotations on P and D:\n       - error = the step's own error\n       - D2: is it necessary to pass on values? Then \"only pass through stuff that's necessary… not already saved on the row\"\n       - D3: which step? Then \"at the end of the recipe step\"\n       - D4: nested steps? Look it up and spike; the parent should not fail even if all children fail; replace the code-block rule\n       - D5 ok\n       - D6: the common CI applies the migrations, the others depend on it\n       - D7 drop\n       - D8: if not contradictory, keep\n       - D9: scout ok\n       - lease: re-get the lease and recheck the recipe on every retry\n       - conversation: the same one for step retries too\n     - \"promise all sounds good; write current step outside the step, steps only write unit info\", then \"it makes sense to have a parent step… wrapped… write the result from all 25 substeps\"\n     - \"confirm (title); 1 minute per children; auto fail stuck >15 min; idk what api and common command lines are about; show me all the learn drafts\"\n     - \"leave them out until they exist; drop the 15 minute auto fail\"\n     - \"an item queued for 15 minutes gets an actual retry; the API checks queued_at, re-queues and updates queued_at; update the charter to match; write all our docs and run a plannotator review; close all the subagents\"\n   - Learn:\n     - `/mahou:learn` \"let's do a learn session while we wait…\"\n     - Annotations on the friction points:\n       - multiple ports and drop the one-server rule\n       - default tldraw font\n       - questions under the write-up ok\n       - opening-tree explanation ok\n       - the obvious-answer rule (wording to think about)\n       - adjust the design types and add design-with-canvas references\n       - mermaid palette in the mermaid skill\n       - generalize the rendering problems\n       - remove the branch-split, common-late and recording-notes points\n       - wiki facts ok\n       - growY ok\n     - Later answers:\n       - shape-with-canvas too\n       - \"all that apply\"\n       - rethink mermaid-validation into a mermaid skill like Filadd's\n       - same location for the rendering rules\n       - name ok\n       - Notion Filadd-only, adjust the sync skill\n       - \"stadium? what's that?\", then \"i like the stadium\"\n       - current palette as the default\n       - \"stop any unused subagents, draft the learnings too and do we have a full diagram of the whole pipeline somewhere?\"\n     - Plannotator feedback on the drafts:\n       - the program-design exception goes on the program-design skill\n       - a proposal still shows as a question in the tree\n       - remove the \"What a question carries\" sentence\n       - read both the design and canvas representations, canvas form for the canvas and design form for the final text\n     - \"apply all of them; what's the state of the docs?\"\n   - `/mahou:commit-changes` \"into a new branch and let's also drop the extraction v2 local and remote branches, those are stale\"; \"go ahead with both\".\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Await the user's plannotator review feedback (session pn-bb5f09; the diff it showed is now committed) and apply any annotations to the docs.\n   - Open questions to raise if relevant:\n     - the 15-minute re-queue vs items waiting for the domain lease\n     - whether re-queues count toward the 3 client retries\n     - recovery of an instance stranded during generating by a dev reload\n   - The claude-plugins learn changes are uncommitted, with the mermaid rename staged by `git mv`. Commit only if asked.\n   - Remind the user: delete the Modal proxy auth token, and revoke the R2 API tokens from the spikes (r2-presigned, svg-display). The stopped Modal apps `nagara-tts-spike` and `nagara-spike-upload` remain.\n   - Next stage per status.md: mahou:tasks, only when the user asks.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished `/mahou:commit-changes`.\n   - Created branch `feat/cloudflare-migration` from main.\n   - Committed `c0dbdba docs: describe nagara on Cloudflare` (all docs plus CLAUDE.md) and `54cb15d chore: add local spike rules` (`.mahou/spike.md`).\n   - Deleted the local `feat/extraction-v2` (\"Deleted branch feat/extraction-v2 (was 26473be)\") and the remote (\"[deleted] feat/extraction-v2\").\n   - Updated the scratch `status.md`: Stage is design recorded and committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration`, not pushed, and the local artifacts list now includes `recording-decisions.md`, `docs-drafts/` and `docs-impact.md`.\n   - The commit report to the user had not been sent yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Report the commit outcome to the user:\n   - the two commits on `feat/cloudflare-migration`\n   - both extraction-v2 branches deleted\n   - nothing pushed\n   - the plannotator review (pn-bb5f09) is still open; its diff is now committed, so feedback would land as follow-up edits\n\n   Then wait for the plannotator feedback or the user's next instruction. Start no new work unprompted. The last user instruction was: \"go ahead with both\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/agus/.claude/projects/-home-agus-workspace-asermax-nagara/f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"7b509959-cd81-4783-9a86-d370bfebbfea","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:42:15.763Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":73,"turnIndex":215},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
