{"parentUuid":"14faa471-103d-4e9d-b78b-3511a17bded9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bfa32ed9-babd-4bb0-92a6-0867b6b276d3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TMyFmqCxbQ57jVFT8BvYMx","type":"tool_result","content":"# testing\n\n- [`cassettes-over-mocks`](cassettes-over-mocks.md): replaying HTTP boundaries from cassettes, fabricating them from a contract, and what stays mocked\n# cloudflare\n\n- [`local-pipeline`](local-pipeline.md): running the pipeline and its agents locally, and the key the AI Gateway accepts\n# References\n\n- [`cloudflare`](cloudflare/INDEX.md): running jobs, gates, agents, containers and data on Cloudflare's platform\n- [`firecrawl`](firecrawl/INDEX.md): calling Firecrawl from runtimes its SDK does not support\n- [`gemini`](gemini/INDEX.md): what the Gemini API accepts as input and how it describes it\n- [`markdown`](markdown/INDEX.md): parsing markdown into a syntax tree outside a renderer\n- [`modal`](modal/INDEX.md): calling Modal functions from outside its Python client\n- [`node`](node/INDEX.md): running and distributing a Node program\n- [`testing`](testing/INDEX.md): how test runners are built and what they expose\n# Cloudflare\n\n- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\n- [`cf-cli`](cf-cli.md): the beta `cf` CLI against wrangler for D1 migrations, deploys and CI\n- [`containers`](containers.md): running an existing image behind a Durable Object, reaching bindings, sizes, sleep and cost\n- [`d1`](d1.md): SQLite on Cloudflare, its limits, wrangler migrations, and why SQLAlchemy and Alembic do not drive it\n- [`durable-objects`](durable-objects.md): serializing work per key with a gate object\n- [`flue`](flue.md): agents as functions, dispatch from Workflows, the Vite-only build, and the DOM dependency on Workers\n- [`images`](images.md): the Images binding against WebAssembly in a Worker: SVG, the 10 MP memory ceiling, fonts and pricing\n- [`local-dev`](local-dev.md): running Workers that bind each other locally, shared state, local R2 over S3 and tunnels to it\n- [`python-workers`](python-workers.md): running a Python web app as a Worker, the Pyodide package gaps and the limits\n- [`r2`](r2.md): S3 access, presigned URLs in a browser, serving SVG safely, and pricing\n- [`vitest-plugin`](vitest-plugin.md): testing Workflows with introspection and step mocks, and outbound HTTP after `fetchMock`\n- [`workflows`](workflows.md): running a long job in a spawn-and-resolve shape, its limits, retries, behaviour across deploys, and the languages that can write one\n# Workflow testing: which test double replaces Firecrawl, Gemini and Modal\n\n## Question\n\nFor a Workflow shaped like the item Workflow (fetch page, describe image, spawn TTS, sleep and poll TTS, write result, with D1 and R2 bindings), running under vitest and `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin` in workerd, which test double fits replacing Firecrawl, Gemini and Modal: step mocking through introspection, MSW intercepting `fetch` inside a step, or a code seam like today's `WORLD_SEAM`?\n\n## Answer\n\nAll three work, with caveats, and they cover different things. Interception at the HTTP layer is the only kind that replays the existing cassettes, and it comes in two forms: MSW, and a fourth option found during the spike, miniflare's `outboundService`.\n\n| | Step body runs | D1/R2 writes in the step | Client serialization and parsing | Replays `api/tests/cassettes` | Skips sleeps and retry delays |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Introspection `mockStepResult` / `mockStepError` / `forceStepTimeout` | no | no | no | no | yes, `disableSleeps` and `disableRetryDelays` |\n| MSW in the test file | yes | yes | yes | yes, with a replayer, header stripping and URL rewriting | no, it needs introspection beside it |\n| `outboundService` in the vitest config (Node side) | yes | yes | yes | yes, read straight from disk in Node | no, it needs introspection beside it |\n| Code seam (`WORLD_SEAM`-style `ItemWorld`) | yes | yes | no, the double replaces the client | no | no, it needs introspection beside it |\n\nEvery combination ran green on plugin 1.1.13 (the repo's version) and on 1.3.6, three runs each with no flakes. Their behaviour did not differ.\n\nWhatever double fills the step bodies, the plugin's introspection API is what removes the waits: `disableSleeps` and `disableRetryDelays` are the only way found to skip a `step.sleep` or a retry backoff. Without them a 30 s sleep takes 30 s of wall clock.\n\n## What was run\n\nThe code is in `app/` (plugin 1.1.13, vitest 4.1.0, wrangler 4.135.0, workers-types 5.20260919.1, as in `pipeline/package.json`). `app-1.3.6/` is a copy with plugin 1.3.6, which brings in wrangler 4.147.0 and miniflare 5.20261001.\n\n- `src/item-workflow.ts` holds `ItemWorkflow`. It runs `fetch page` (retries 2, 5 s constant), `describe image` (retries 3, 10 s exponential) and `spawn tts`, then loops `step.sleep(\"wait for tts\", \"30 seconds\")` plus `poll tts`, which puts the audio in R2 when it is ready, and ends with `write result`. Every step updates the `items` row in D1.\n- `src/clients.ts` holds plain `fetch` clients: Firecrawl `POST /v2/scrape`, Gemini `generateContent` with the image prompt from `api/`, and Modal `POST /submit` and `GET /result/{call_id}`, where 202 means still running.\n- `src/world.ts` holds the `ItemWorld` seam, copied from the shape of `pipeline/src/workflow/world.ts`.\n- `test/cassette.ts` holds a vcrpy YAML loader and an in-order replayer that matches on method and URI, with optional JSON body matching and URI rewriting.\n- `test/fixtures.ts` imports three repo cassettes with Vite `?raw`: `test_firecrawl_fetch/test_firecrawl_http_surface`, `test_describe_images/test_image_describe_returns_a_clean_sentence` and `test_describe/test_a_429_retries_then_succeeds`. It also imports one fabricated Modal cassette, `test/cassettes/modal_tts_fabricated.yaml` (submit, 202, 202, 200 with an `X-Duration` header), because the repo has no Modal cassette: modal is mocked in the Python suite today.\n- Tests: `test/introspection.test.ts`, `test/msw.test.ts` (msw 3.0.2), `test/msw2.test.ts` (msw 2.15.0), `test/seam.test.ts`, and `test/outbound/outbound.test.ts` under its own config, `vitest.outbound.config.ts`.\n\n```\ncd .scratch/cloudflare-migration/spikes/workflow-testing/app        # or app-1.3.6\npnpm install\npnpm vitest run --reporter=verbose --silent=false                   # 19 tests\npnpm vitest run -c vitest.outbound.config.ts --reporter=verbose     # 1 test\npnpm tsc --noEmit\n```\n\nNo test reaches a real service, and no cloud resource was created.\n\n## Measurements\n\n| Test | Elapsed |\n|---|---|\n| Everything mocked through introspection, sleeps disabled | 22 ms |\n| Two mocked errors on `describe image` with `disableRetryDelays` | 13–20 ms |\n| One mocked error on `fetch page` without `disableRetryDelays` (5 s constant delay) | 5016 ms |\n| One 30 s sleep not disabled (introspection test and seam test alike) | 30013 / 30024 ms |\n| MSW replaying Firecrawl, Gemini and Modal through the real step bodies | 44–76 ms |\n| `outboundService` replaying the same set | 61–117 ms |\n| Whole suite, 19 tests, files in parallel | 38.6 s on both plugin versions, almost all of it the two deliberate 30 s sleeps |\n\nMSW replay produced the same D1 row as the Python cassettes would imply: `title` \"Herman Melville - Moby-Dick\", `image_spoken` holding Gemini's recorded sentence about the Python logo, `tts_call_id` \"fc-01SPIKE\", status `ready`, and the R2 object holding the fabricated WAV bytes. The introspection run ended with `status = ready` while `title`, `image_spoken` and `tts_call_id` stayed `NULL`: only `write result`, the one step left unmocked, wrote to D1.\n\nWhen a step exhausts its retries, the engine attempts it 1 + 5 times under the default retry config (counted from MSW misses on the unmatched Modal submit).\n\n## Surprises\n\n- **A falsy mocked result is ignored.** In miniflare's workflow engine, `mockStepResult` is applied by `else if (replaceResult)`, so a mocked `null`, `false`, `0` or `\"\"` falls through and the real step body runs. In the first run, the step body made a real request to `nagara-tts-spike.modal.run` and got a 404. The spike's `poll tts` first returned `null` for \"not yet\"; it now returns `{ ready: false }` so it can be mocked. The behaviour is the same on both plugin versions.\n- **An unmocked step reaches the real internet.** Introspection, MSW without a catch-all handler, and the seam all let anything they do not cover fall through to the network. One test sent the placeholder key to the live Gemini endpoint and got 400. Only `outboundService` sits in front of every outbound request.\n- **`mockStepError` must come before `mockStepResult` on the same step.** In the other order, the modifier throws \"Trying to mock error on step ... after mocking its result\".\n- **`getError()` drops the message of a `NonRetryableError`.** It returns `WorkflowFatalError: ... a step threw an NonRetryableError and it was not handled`; a plain error keeps its message, for example `{\"message\":\"firecrawl 503\"}`.\n- **msw 3's `setupServer` from `msw/node` does not start in workerd.** Its `ClientRequest` interceptor reads `llhttp.wasm` from disk, and workerd's virtual filesystem cannot open the file (ENOENT). This holds on both plugin versions. msw 2.15's `msw/node` works as-is. msw 3 works through `msw/experimental`: `defineNetwork` with an `InterceptorSource` holding only `FetchInterceptor` (from `@mswjs/interceptors`, which has to be a direct dependency).\n- **MSW and Workflow code share one global per test file.** The Workflow's `run()` executes in the test file's isolate, the same reason `WORLD_SEAM` on `globalThis` works today, so a patched `fetch` reaches inside `step.do`. Test files run in separate isolates: two files patching `fetch` concurrently did not interfere.\n- **The Python cassettes do not replay verbatim.** vcrpy stores the decoded body next to the wire's `Content-Encoding: gzip` and `Content-Length`. Replaying both made workerd's `fetch` fail with \"Decompression failed\", and the Firecrawl step then burned through its retries. The replayer strips `content-encoding`, `content-length` and `transfer-encoding`.\n- **Body matching works for Gemini and fails for Firecrawl.** The Gemini request rebuilt in TS from the same prompt and image matches the recorded body as JSON. The Firecrawl body does not, because the Python SDK sends nine fields the TS client does not (`origin: python-sdk@4.34.0`, `proxy`, `maxAge`, `blockAds` and others). Matching on URI alone is unsafe: in the `outboundService` run, the second interaction of the 429 cassette (a code-block describe) answered the image describe request, and the item went `ready` with \"A Python function that wraps a single request.\" as its image description.\n- **Going through the AI Gateway changes the URL.** The cassettes are recorded against `generativelanguage.googleapis.com`, and the Worker calls `gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/{account}/{gateway}/google-ai-studio`. The replayer has to rewrite the URI.\n- **`env` is shared and mutable between the test and the Workflow.** Overwriting `env.GEMINI_BASE` in a test changed the URL the step called.\n- **msw's request type does not fit workers-types' `Request`.** Passing the request on needs `as unknown as Request`.\n- **1.1.13 and 1.3.6 behave identically for every case above.** Neither exports a `fetchMock` from `cloudflare:test`. The undici `MockScope` types are still in the `.d.ts` file, but nothing exports them.\n\n## Design decisions this raises\n\n- Should the item Workflow's tests replay cassettes through the real step bodies (MSW or `outboundService`), stub at the step (introspection), stub behind a seam, or mix them per test? Today the API suite replays HTTP cassettes and the pipeline suite uses a seam.\n- If cassettes: are the Python cassettes reused through a translating replayer (header stripping, URI rewrite, relaxed matching for Firecrawl), or re-recorded from the TS clients so that body matching holds?\n- If interception: MSW in the test file, where handlers are per test and the module graph is the worker's, or `outboundService` in the config, where it runs in Node, reads cassettes from disk, blocks every unmatched request, and is controlled through a fake control host?\n- If MSW: msw 2.15 with stock `msw/node`, or msw 3 with the experimental `defineNetwork` API?\n- Is a test that lets an unmatched request reach the real network acceptable, or must the suite block unmatched requests the way `outboundService` does?","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2031f3fb-2b1d-4ca1-8e14-061c348c46e7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:48:37.123Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# testing\n\n- [`cassettes-over-mocks`](cassettes-over-mocks.md): replaying HTTP boundaries from cassettes, fabricating them from a contract, and what stays mocked\n# cloudflare\n\n- [`local-pipeline`](local-pipeline.md): running the pipeline and its agents locally, and the key the AI Gateway accepts\n# References\n\n- [`cloudflare`](cloudflare/INDEX.md): running jobs, gates, agents, containers and data on Cloudflare's platform\n- [`firecrawl`](firecrawl/INDEX.md): calling Firecrawl from runtimes its SDK does not support\n- [`gemini`](gemini/INDEX.md): what the Gemini API accepts as input and how it describes it\n- [`markdown`](markdown/INDEX.md): parsing markdown into a syntax tree outside a renderer\n- [`modal`](modal/INDEX.md): calling Modal functions from outside its Python client\n- [`node`](node/INDEX.md): running and distributing a Node program\n- [`testing`](testing/INDEX.md): how test runners are built and what they expose\n# Cloudflare\n\n- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\n- [`cf-cli`](cf-cli.md): the beta `cf` CLI against wrangler for D1 migrations, deploys and CI\n- [`containers`](containers.md): running an existing image behind a Durable Object, reaching bindings, sizes, sleep and cost\n- [`d1`](d1.md): SQLite on Cloudflare, its limits, wrangler migrations, and why SQLAlchemy and Alembic do not drive it\n- [`durable-objects`](durable-objects.md): serializing work per key with a gate object\n- [`flue`](flue.md): agents as functions, dispatch from Workflows, the Vite-only build, and the DOM dependency on Workers\n- [`images`](images.md): the Images binding against WebAssembly in a Worker: SVG, the 10 MP memory ceiling, fonts and pricing\n- [`local-dev`](local-dev.md): running Workers that bind each other locally, shared state, local R2 over S3 and tunnels to it\n- [`python-workers`](python-workers.md): running a Python web app as a Worker, the Pyodide package gaps and the limits\n- [`r2`](r2.md): S3 access, presigned URLs in a browser, serving SVG safely, and pricing\n- [`vitest-plugin`](vitest-plugin.md): testing Workflows with introspection and step mocks, and outbound HTTP after `fetchMock`\n- [`workflows`](workflows.md): running a long job in a spawn-and-resolve shape, its limits, retries, behaviour across deploys, and the languages that can write one\n# Workflow testing: which test double replaces Firecrawl, Gemini and Modal\n\n## Question\n\nFor a Workflow shaped like the item Workflow (fetch page, describe image, spawn TTS, sleep and poll TTS, write result, with D1 and R2 bindings), running under vitest and `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin` in workerd, which test double fits replacing Firecrawl, Gemini and Modal: step mocking through introspection, MSW intercepting `fetch` inside a step, or a code seam like today's `WORLD_SEAM`?\n\n## Answer\n\nAll three work, with caveats, and they cover different things. Interception at the HTTP layer is the only kind that replays the existing cassettes, and it comes in two forms: MSW, and a fourth option found during the spike, miniflare's `outboundS