{"parentUuid":"2e3235c6-0437-4a51-afa2-c950a27a94c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfur9mYeJSmL22cXr4BC6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5462,"cache_read_input_tokens":187977,"output_tokens":16908,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":23},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5462,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":16908,"cache_read_input_tokens":187977,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5462},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":437,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"b6b87393-bea4-4731-b9e4-7474e9612d8b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfur9m9bHxu6XGn9qQt8F","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:program-design","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"c6d7ed81-9920-496b-b464-1dc8d554f99f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:50:53.953Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"c6d7ed81-9920-496b-b464-1dc8d554f99f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfur9mYeJSmL22cXr4BC6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014U1Ejk8czyaC5w3Wd55rSe","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md","content":"# Program design: nagara on Cloudflare\n\nRepository: `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara`, branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`, clean.\n\nCovers how the Cloudflare migration lands in the code: the pnpm workspace, `common/`, the new TypeScript `api/`, the item Workflow and DomainQueue in `pipeline/`, the two web endpoints in `tts/`, local development and CI. Source: the notes under `docs/technical-design/` committed in `c0dbdba`, plus `design.md` and `recording-decisions.md` in this folder. Leaves out the test cases and manual validations (mahou:test-design), and `web/`.\n\nStatus: **proposed**, every part. The user reads the whole proposal on the canvas and points out what does not match.\n\n```\nProgram design\n└─ nagara                                                        proposed\n   ├─ 1 Workspace and packages                                   proposed\n   │  └─ 1.1 Package layout\n   ├─ 2 common/                                                  proposed\n   │  ├─ 2.1 What each module exposes (interfaces)\n   │  └─ 2.2 Module list\n   ├─ 3 api/: the routes                                         proposed\n   │  ├─ 3.1 Callstacks: enqueue, poll with re-queue, retry, media\n   │  ├─ 3.2 Interfaces and module list\n   │  └─ 3.3 Critical behaviour: the re-queue and the restart point\n   ├─ 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow                             proposed\n   │  ├─ 4.1 Control flow: the nine steps and the wrapper\n   │  ├─ 4.2 Interfaces: the step wrapper, step results, modules\n   │  ├─ 4.3 Critical behaviour: lease, poll loop, describe fan-out\n   │  └─ 4.4 Module list\n   ├─ 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue                                   proposed\n   │  └─ 5.1 Interfaces and module list\n   ├─ 6 tts/: the two web endpoints                              proposed\n   │  └─ 6.1 Interfaces and module list\n   ├─ 7 Local development                                        proposed\n   │  └─ 7.1 Module list and launch\n   ├─ 8 CI                                                       proposed\n   │  └─ 8.1 Control flow and module list\n   └─ 9 Standards                                                proposed\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1 Workspace and packages\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```\nnagara/\n├── package.json                 new   private root, no scripts of its own\n├── pnpm-workspace.yaml          new   packages: common, api, pipeline; carries pipeline's allowBuilds and overrides\n├── pnpm-lock.yaml               new   one lockfile for the three TypeScript packages\n├── common/                      new   @nagara/common, source only: exports .ts, never built\n│   ├── package.json             exports \".\", \"./testing\"\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           the D1 binding and migrations_dir, for `wrangler d1 migrations apply`\n│   ├── migrations/              hand-written SQL, applied by CI, locally, and by both Workers' tests\n│   ├── src/                     types, keys, presigning, item row, sanitize\n│   ├── testing/                 the cassette replay library (vitest only)\n│   └── test/\n├── api/                         replaced: the Python tree goes, a Worker takes its place\n│   ├── package.json             @nagara/api; depends on @nagara/common: workspace:*\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           name nagara-api, route nagara.asermax.com, D1, R2, the item Workflow by script_name\n│   ├── src/\n│   └── test/\n├── pipeline/                    touched\n│   ├── package.json             depends on @nagara/common: workspace:*; own pnpm-lock.yaml and pnpm-workspace.yaml go\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           workflow renamed item, JobIndex deleted, D1 and R2 bound, workers_dev false\n│   ├── src/\n│   └── test/                    cassettes/ moves here from api/tests/cassettes\n├── tts/                         touched: two web endpoints, no package change\n└── .github/workflows/           cloudflare.yml replaces api.yml and pipeline.yml; tts.yml unchanged\n```\n\n`common/` is a workspace package because both Workers import it at build time and its migrations are the one thing it deploys. It ships no build step: Vite (pipeline) and wrangler's esbuild (api) compile its `.ts` sources directly, the way `pipeline/` already imports its own `.ts` paths. The `./testing` export keeps the cassette library and its YAML parser out of the Workers' runtime bundles.\n\nOne root workspace and lockfile replace `pipeline/`'s own, so `workspace:*` links resolve without publishing. `pnpm install` from any of the three folders installs the workspace. `tts/` stays outside the workspace, under uv as today.\n\nNew dependencies: `aws4fetch` in `common/` for presigning (the r2-presigned spike signed with it), `markdown-it` in `common/` for the sanitize tail's partner, the spoken-form derivation (wiki `markdown`), `yaml` in `common/` dev for cassette parsing, `msw@2.15` as a dev dependency of both Workers (msw 3's `msw/node` does not start in workerd, workflow-testing spike). `valibot` stays in `pipeline/` and joins `api/` for the enqueue body.\n\n---\n\n## 2 common/\n\n### 2.1 What each module exposes\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/item.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"The item row and its statuses.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"ITEM_STATUS\": { \"enum\": [\"queued\", \"generating\", \"ready\", \"failed\"], \"description\": \"Constant map; ItemStatus derives from it.\" },\n    \"ItemRow\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"itm_ plus 8 hex characters.\" },\n        \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"title\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"voice\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"status\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ITEM_STATUS\" },\n        \"created_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"updated_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"queued_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"workflow_instance_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"current_step\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"A STEP name, or a poll step's numbered name.\" },\n        \"extraction_domain\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"recipe_version_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"retry_count\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n        \"duration\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n        \"audio_format\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"units\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/units.ts#/$defs/RowUnit\" } },\n        \"degradations\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/units.ts#/$defs/Degradation\" } },\n        \"error\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/units.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"The unit union the display, spoken form and timing ride on.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"Unit\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphUnit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CodeUnit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ImageUnit\" }] },\n    \"ParagraphUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"paragraph\" }, \"display\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"spoken\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"start\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"end\": { \"type\": \"number\" } }, \"required\": [\"type\", \"display\", \"spoken\"] },\n    \"CodeUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"code\" }, \"display\": {}, \"spoken\": {}, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } },\n    \"ImageUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"image\" }, \"display\": { \"description\": \"![<raw alt>](/items/<id>/images/<hash>): the describe step reads the alt back from here.\" }, \"spoken\": {}, \"image\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The content hash.\" }, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } },\n    \"DeclaredImageUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"declared-image\" }, \"src\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"alt\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"description\": \"An image the recipe declared and the images step has not acquired yet; never survives the images step.\" },\n    \"RowUnit\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Unit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DeclaredImageUnit\" }] },\n    \"DEGRADATION_REASON\": { \"enum\": [\"404\", \"timeout\", \"undecodable\", \"describe failed\", \"describe cap reached\"] },\n    \"Degradation\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"enum\": [\"image\", \"code\"] }, \"reason\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DEGRADATION_REASON\" }, \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Origin URL, acquisition failures only.\" } }, \"required\": [\"type\", \"reason\"] }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/workflow.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"What the API and the item Workflow agree on.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"ItemWorkflowParams\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"itemId\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"required\": [\"itemId\"] },\n    \"STEP\": { \"enum\": [\"fetch\", \"lease\", \"recipe\", \"release\", \"images\", \"describe\", \"start synthesis\", \"poll\", \"store\"], \"description\": \"Constant map of step names. A poll step runs as `poll <n>`.\" },\n    \"restartPoint\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"currentStep\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] } } },\n        \"output\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"The step name restart() starts from: lease for recipe and release, the step itself otherwise, null (restart every step) when empty.\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/row.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"Reads and writes of the item row both Workers make.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"readItem\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"db\": { \"description\": \"D1Database\" }, \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"ItemRow with units and degradations decoded, or null.\" } } },\n    \"writeStatus\": {\n      \"description\": \"One UPDATE: status, current_step, error = null, updated_at = now. Used by the API for queued and by the step wrapper for every status.\",\n      \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"db\": {}, \"id\": {}, \"status\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/item.ts#/$defs/ITEM_STATUS\" }, \"currentStep\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] }, \"error\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Set only with failed.\" } }, \"required\": [\"db\", \"id\", \"status\"] }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"nothing\" } }\n    },\n    \"encodeJson / decodeJson\": { \"description\": \"The JSON column codec for units and degradations.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/keys.ts and common/src/presign.ts\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"audioKey\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"itemId\": {} } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"audio/<itemId>\" } } },\n    \"imageKey\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"hash\": {} } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"images/<hash>\" } } },\n    \"presign\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n          \"endpoint\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The S3 endpoint the URL is signed for: R2's in production, the local S3 endpoint locally.\" },\n          \"bucket\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"key\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"method\": { \"enum\": [\"GET\", \"PUT\"] },\n          \"accessKeyId\": {}, \"secretAccessKey\": {},\n          \"expiresIn\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"description\": \"Seconds; 3600 for both callers.\" }\n        } },\n        \"output\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The signed URL.\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/ledger.ts, common/src/recipe.ts, common/src/sanitize.ts\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"COST_TYPE\": { \"enum\": [\"firecrawl\", \"describer\", \"tts\"] },\n    \"COST_UNIT\": { \"enum\": [\"credits\", \"calls\", \"seconds\"] },\n    \"CostEntryRow\": { \"properties\": { \"id\": {}, \"item_id\": {}, \"type\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/COST_TYPE\" }, \"quantity\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"unit\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/COST_UNIT\" }, \"dollars\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"cached\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }, \"detail\": { \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"] }, \"created_at\": {} } },\n    \"RecipeVersionRow\": { \"properties\": { \"id\": {}, \"domain\": {}, \"version\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }, \"script\": {}, \"created_at\": {} } },\n    \"sanitizeSpoken\": { \"description\": \"The sanitize tail: markers touching text, tags to words, comparison operators to words. Used by the spoken-form derivation and the describer, two pipeline modules.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/testing: replayCassettes\",\n  \"description\": \"Our TypeScript copy of vcrpy, replay only, run through msw in both Workers' tests.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"cassette\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The YAML text, imported with ?raw.\" },\n      \"rewrite\": { \"description\": \"Host rewrites, such as generativelanguage.googleapis.com to the gateway's URL.\" }\n    } },\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"msw handlers: match on method, scheme, host, port, query, and path and JSON body with item ids normalized; credential headers stripped before matching; content-encoding, content-length and transfer-encoding stripped from the replayed response; repeated identical requests answer in recorded order; an unmatched request throws.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe D1 test schema comes from `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`'s `readD1Migrations(\"../common/migrations\")` in each Worker's vitest config and `applyD1Migrations` in a setup file, so `common/testing` holds only the cassette library.\n\n`sanitizeSpoken` and the row reads and writes are in `common/` because the project's rule puts there everything more than one module uses: the sanitize tail serves the spoken-form module and the describer module, the row writes serve the API and the pipeline.\n\n### 2.2 Module list\n\n```\ncommon/package.json                      new\ncommon/tsconfig.json                     new\ncommon/biome.json                        new   copied from pipeline/\ncommon/wrangler.jsonc                    new   D1 binding \"DB\", database nagara, migrations_dir migrations\ncommon/migrations/0001_initial.sql       new   items, recipe_versions, cost_entries, with the indexes for recipe lookup\ncommon/src/item.ts                       new\ncommon/src/units.ts                      new\ncommon/src/workflow.ts                   new\ncommon/src/row.ts                        new\ncommon/src/keys.ts                       new\ncommon/src/presign.ts                    new\ncommon/src/ledger.ts                     new\ncommon/src/recipe.ts                     new\ncommon/src/sanitize.ts                   new   ported from api/app/service/extract.py, sanitize_spoken and its helpers\ncommon/src/index.ts                      new   re-exports src/\ncommon/testing/cassettes.ts              new   ported from api/tests/conftest.py's matchers and filters\ncommon/testing/index.ts                  new\ncommon/test/presign.test.ts              new\ncommon/test/sanitize.test.ts             new\ncommon/test/row.test.ts                  new\ncommon/test/cassettes.test.ts            new\n```\n\nThe SQL starts from the D1 schema at migration 0001 because the move starts empty; the Alembic history is not carried over.\n\n---\n\n## 3 api/: the routes\n\n### 3.1 Callstacks\n\n```\nPOST /items\ngiven X-API-Key, {url, voice?}\n│\n└─ index.fetch → guard.requireKey                               401 on a missing or wrong key\n   └─ routes/enqueue\n      ├─ valibot parse {url: string, voice?: string}            400 when malformed\n      ├─ voices.pick(voice)                                     random from the curated pool when absent\n      ├─ items/create.insertQueued(db, {id = itm_ + 8 hex, url, voice, status queued, queued_at = now})\n      ├─ env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({params: {itemId}})           instance id left to Cloudflare\n      │  └─ when create throws: log it, answer 202 anyway       the re-queue on read recovers the item\n      └─ 202 response.toItemResponse(row)\n```\n\n```\nGET /items/{id}\ngiven X-API-Key, id\n│\n└─ routes/poll\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null\n   ├─ when status queued and queued_at older than 15 min\n   │  └─ items/requeue.requeue(env, row)\n   │     ├─ claim: UPDATE items SET queued_at = now, updated_at = now\n   │     │         WHERE id = ? AND status = 'queued' AND queued_at < now - 15 min\n   │     ├─ when no row changed: another poll claimed it, nothing more\n   │     ├─ when workflow_instance_id is null\n   │     │  └─ env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({params: {itemId}})\n   │     └─ otherwise\n   │        └─ (await env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.get(instance id)).restart(from restartPoint(current_step))\n   └─ 200 response.toItemResponse(row)\n```\n\n```\nPOST /items/{id}/retry\ngiven X-API-Key, id\n│\n└─ routes/retry\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null\n   ├─ items/retry-claim.claim(db, id, retryMax)\n   │  └─ UPDATE items SET status = 'queued', error = null, queued_at = now, updated_at = now,\n   │     retry_count = retry_count + 1\n   │     WHERE id = ? AND status = 'failed' AND retry_count < ?  409 when no row changed; the pre-read picks the message\n   ├─ (await env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.get(workflow_instance_id)).restart(from restartPoint(current_step))\n   │  └─ when the row holds no instance id: create({params: {itemId}})\n   └─ 202 response.toItemResponse(claimed row)\n```\n\n```\nGET /items/{id}/audio · GET /items/{id}/images/{hash}\ngiven X-API-Key, id[, hash]\n│\n└─ routes/audio | routes/images\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null; audio also 404 unless ready with audio_format\n   ├─ common.presign({endpoint: R2_S3_ENDPOINT, bucket, key: audioKey(id) | imageKey(hash),\n   │                  method GET, R2 GET token, expiresIn 3600})\n   └─ 307 to the signed URL\n\nGET /health → 200 \"ok\", before the guard\n```\n\n### 3.2 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"api/ wrangler bindings and configuration\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"DB\": { \"description\": \"D1 nagara, shared with the pipeline.\" },\n    \"ITEM_WORKFLOW\": { \"description\": \"workflows: {binding ITEM_WORKFLOW, name item, class_name ItemWorkflow, script_name nagara}.\" },\n    \"vars\": { \"properties\": { \"R2_S3_ENDPOINT\": {}, \"R2_BUCKET\": {}, \"RETRY_MAX\": { \"const\": 3 }, \"REQUEUE_AFTER_MS\": { \"const\": 900000 } } },\n    \"secrets\": { \"properties\": { \"API_KEY\": {}, \"R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID\": {}, \"R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\": {} } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"api/src/response.ts: toItemResponse\",\n  \"description\": \"The wire projection, unchanged for clients: drops spoken, adds index, holds units back until ready.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"description\": \"ItemRow\" },\n    \"output\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"id\": {}, \"url\": {}, \"title\": {}, \"status\": {}, \"voice\": {}, \"created_at\": {},\n      \"duration\": { \"description\": \"Absent until ready.\" },\n      \"units\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"properties\": { \"index\": {}, \"type\": {}, \"display\": {}, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {}, \"image\": {} } }, \"description\": \"null unless ready.\" },\n      \"error\": {},\n      \"audio_url\": { \"description\": \"/items/<id>/audio, only when ready.\" }\n    } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```\napi/                                     the Python tree goes: app/, migrations/, tests/, data/, prototype_cache/,\n                                         alembic.ini, pyproject.toml, uv.lock, railway.toml        deleted\napi/tests/cassettes/                     moved to pipeline/test/cassettes/\napi/package.json                         new\napi/tsconfig.json                        new\napi/biome.json                           new\napi/wrangler.jsonc                       new\napi/vitest.config.ts                     new   readD1Migrations(\"../common/migrations\")\napi/src/index.ts                         new   fetch handler: /health, the key guard, the route table (plain matching, as pipeline/src/http/routes.ts does)\napi/src/guard.ts                         new\napi/src/voices.ts                        new   the curated pool, ported from api/app/service/tts.py pick_voice\napi/src/response.ts                      new\napi/src/routes/enqueue.ts                new\napi/src/routes/poll.ts                   new\napi/src/routes/retry.ts                  new\napi/src/routes/audio.ts                  new\napi/src/routes/images.ts                 new\napi/src/items/create.ts                  new   insertQueued and the id mint\napi/src/items/requeue.ts                 new\napi/src/items/retry-claim.ts             new\napi/test/setup.ts                        new   applies the migrations\napi/test/helpers/workflow-stand-in.ts    new   the stand-in for ITEM_WORKFLOW: records create, get and restart calls\napi/test/*.test.ts                       new   one file per route, cases from test-design\n```\n\n### 3.3 Critical behaviour\n\nThe re-queue claims the row with one conditional UPDATE before it touches the instance, the same pattern as the retry claim, so two polls landing together restart the instance once. It does not increment `retry_count`: the cap bounds client retries of failed items, and a re-queue recovers an item that never failed. It restarts from `restartPoint(current_step)`, so an item waiting for its domain's lease (current_step `lease`) asks for the lease again, and DomainQueue keeps an id that is already in its FIFO at its position (5.1); a re-queue never sends a waiting item to the back.\n\nThe retry route reaches the same `restartPoint`. `recipe` and `release` map to `lease`; `poll <n>` restarts at that poll step, so the poll steps before it replay from cache and Modal is not asked to synthesize again; an empty `current_step` restarts every step.\n\nNeither route reads the instance's status: the row is the only state the API reads, as the design says.\n\n---\n\n## 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow\n\n### 4.1 Control flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"ItemWorkflow.run<br/>params {itemId}\"]) --> s1[\"1 fetch · queued<br/>writes instance id,<br/>domain, ledger row<br/>returns {html}\"]\n    s1 --> s2[\"2 lease · queued<br/>ask DomainQueue,<br/>waitForEvent lease-granted\"]\n    s2 --> s3[\"3 recipe · generating<br/>run, author or revise;<br/>spoken form and drop;<br/>writes title, units\"]\n    s3 --> s4[\"4 release · generating<br/>give the lease back\"]\n    s4 --> s5[\"5 images · generating<br/>acquire declared images;<br/>writes units, degradations\"]\n    s5 --> s6[\"6 describe · generating<br/>child steps, allSettled;<br/>one write at the end\"]\n    s6 --> s7[\"7 start synthesis<br/>· generating<br/>sign PUT, call Modal<br/>returns {callId}\"]\n    s7 --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"8 poll · generating\"]\n        direction TB\n        p[\"poll n: fetch result\"] --> r{\"ready?\"}\n        r -->|\"no: sleep 10 s,<br/>n + 1\"| p\n    end\n    r -->|\"yes, returns the result\"| s9[\"9 store · generating<br/>join timings; writes<br/>ready, units, duration,<br/>format, tts ledger row\"]\n    s9 --> done([\"ready\"])\n    s1 -. \"last attempt fails\" .-> fail([\"wrapper writes failed,<br/>the step's error;<br/>run() rethrows\"])\n    s2 -. \"3 waits of 1 h\" .-> fail\n    s3 -. \"not an article: at once\" .-> fail\n    s5 -.-> fail\n    s7 -.-> fail\n    loop -. \"failed or expired\" .-> fail\n    s9 -. \"length mismatch\" .-> fail\n```\n\nEvery box is one call to the wrapper (4.2), which runs the body inside `step.do` with the step's retries and timeout. The order is required throughout: the lease comes before recipe and goes right after it; images come before describe because describe reads the acquired images from R2; describe comes before start synthesis because synthesis reads the described spoken forms from the row.\n\nA failed step ends the run: the wrapper writes `failed` with the step's own error and rethrows, so the instance ends `errored`, which DomainQueue's alarm reads when the failed step held the lease. describe never fails because a child failed (4.3). The Workflow returns nothing.\n\n### 4.2 Interfaces\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts: runStep\",\n  \"description\": \"The logic every step shares.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"ctx\": { \"properties\": { \"step\": { \"description\": \"WorkflowStep\" }, \"db\": {}, \"itemId\": {} } },\n      \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The step name: a STEP value, or poll <n>.\" },\n      \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"queued\", \"generating\"], \"description\": \"queued for fetch and lease, generating after.\" },\n      \"config\": { \"properties\": { \"retries\": { \"const\": 3, \"description\": \"limit 3, 5 s exponential delay\" }, \"timeout\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n      \"body\": { \"description\": \"The step's work; returns its step result or nothing.\" }\n    } },\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"The body's step result.\" }\n  },\n  \"$comment\": \"Inside step.do, first thing in every attempt: writeStatus(status, current_step = name), which also clears error. When step.do throws (its last attempt failed, or a NonRetryableError): step.do('<name> failed') writes failed with error.message, then rethrows. An attempt that fails with attempts left writes nothing.\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Step results\",\n  \"description\": \"Only what the Workflow needs and the row does not hold.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"fetch\": { \"properties\": { \"html\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n    \"start synthesis\": { \"properties\": { \"callId\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n    \"poll <n>\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"properties\": { \"ready\": { \"const\": false } } }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SynthesisResult\" }], \"description\": \"{ready: false}, never null: a falsy mocked step result is ignored by the test engine.\" }\n  },\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"SynthesisResult\": { \"properties\": { \"ready\": { \"const\": true }, \"format\": { \"enum\": [\"audio/ogg\", \"audio/wav\"] }, \"duration\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"timings\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"properties\": { \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } } } } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/ domain modules: what each step calls\",\n  \"description\": \"Each module returns values; only the step files write to D1 and R2.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"firecrawl.scrape(url)\": { \"description\": \"→ {html, finalUrl, creditsUsed, proxy}. Our fetch client, the Python SDK's fields; rawHtml + markdown at proxy auto. Throws on no HTML; the step throws NonRetryableError over maxHtmlBytes.\" },\n    \"recipes.currentRecipe(db, domain) / recipes.saveVersion(db, domain, script)\": { \"description\": \"→ RecipeVersionRow | null; the insert as the next version.\" },\n    \"recipes.settle(env, {instanceId, domain, html, recipe?})\": { \"description\": \"→ {kind: 'ok', title, units, script, isNew} | {kind: 'not-article'} | {kind: 'gave-up', reason}. Runs the recipe; on failure dispatches the revision agent, or the author when there is no recipe; conversation id = instance id; authoring 1 retry, revision 2, every settled script re-run through the runtime.\" },\n    \"spoken.toTypedUnits(recipeUnits, title)\": { \"description\": \"→ RowUnit[]: spoken form derived, empty-of-letters units dropped, declared images anchored after the last kept text unit.\" },\n    \"images.acquire(env, units, itemId)\": { \"description\": \"→ {units, degradations}: download under per-host 2 / global 10 semaphores, 10 s, 10 MB; sniff <svg; SVG scripts stripped with HTMLRewriter; rasters through env.IMAGES, kept when min side ≥ 200, re-encoded to WebP; sha256 of the stored bytes; R2 put under imageKey with its content type; spoken Image: <alt> or the floor.\" },\n    \"describe.jobs(units, title)\": { \"description\": \"→ the document-ordered jobs: every code unit, every image whose alt (read from display) fails the good-alt filter; the cap of 25 splits them into described and capped.\" },\n    \"describe.describeOne(env, job, image?)\": { \"description\": \"→ {spoken, cached}: one Gemini call through AI Gateway, structured output {spoken}, sanitized; cached from cf-aig-cache-status.\" },\n    \"tts.start(env, {paragraphs, voice, destination}) / tts.result(env, callId)\": { \"description\": \"→ callId; → {ready: false} | SynthesisResult. Proxy-auth headers Modal-Key and Modal-Secret. 500 and 410 throw.\" },\n    \"ledger.record(db, entry)\": { \"description\": \"Inserts one CostEntryRow at the configured price.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/ wrangler bindings and configuration\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"workflows\": { \"description\": \"{binding ITEM_WORKFLOW, name item, class_name ItemWorkflow}.\" },\n    \"DB / BUCKET / IMAGES / LOADER / DOMAIN_QUEUE\": { \"description\": \"D1 nagara, R2 nagara, the Images binding, the Worker Loader, the DomainQueue DO.\" },\n    \"vars\": { \"properties\": { \"R2_S3_ENDPOINT\": { \"description\": \"The endpoint PUT URLs are signed for.\" }, \"R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\": { \"description\": \"What Modal is handed in its place; equal to R2_S3_ENDPOINT in production, the tunnel's https://<host>/s3 locally.\" }, \"R2_BUCKET\": {}, \"MODAL_START_URL\": {}, \"MODAL_RESULT_URL\": {}, \"describeMaxPerItem\": { \"const\": 25 }, \"imageFetchPerHost\": { \"const\": 2 }, \"imageFetchConcurrency\": { \"const\": 10 }, \"pollIntervalSeconds\": { \"const\": 10 }, \"prices\": { \"description\": \"firecrawl per credit, describer per call, tts per second\" }, \"existing\": { \"description\": \"agentModel, agentMaxTurns, authoringRetries, revisionRetries, leaseAlarmMs, recipeCpuMs, maxHtmlBytes, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, CLOUDFLARE_GATEWAY_ID\" } } },\n    \"secrets\": { \"properties\": { \"FIRECRAWL_API_KEY\": {}, \"GEMINI_API_KEY\": {}, \"CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY\": { \"description\": \"The AI Gateway token, the name the agents already read.\" }, \"MODAL_PROXY_KEY\": {}, \"MODAL_PROXY_SECRET\": {}, \"R2_PUT_ACCESS_KEY_ID\": {}, \"R2_PUT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\": {} } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 4.3 Critical behaviour\n\n**The lease.** The `lease` step asks `DomainQueue.acquire(instanceId)` and returns `{granted}`. When not granted, the Workflow waits with `step.waitForEvent(\"lease wait <n>\", {type: \"lease-granted\", timeout: \"1 hour\"})`, up to 3 waits; after a wait times out, a `lease recheck <n>` step asks again, since a grant can be lost to a deploy. An event sent before the wait begins is kept (item-workflow spike). After the third timeout the wrapper's failure path writes `failed`. The waits sit between wrapper calls and write nothing, so `current_step` stays `lease` throughout.\n\n**The poll loop.** Step `poll <n>` asks Modal for the result; when it is not ready, `step.sleep(\"poll sleep <n>\", pollIntervalSeconds)` and `n + 1`. Each name carries its counter, because a repeated name replays the cached result. Each poll step has 3 attempts of 1 min; Modal's 500 (the synthesis crashed) and 410 (the result expired after 7 days) throw, so a crashed synthesis uses the poll step's attempts and fails the item. At 10 s, the 10,000-step limit covers about 27 h of synthesis; a 70-minute article took 176 s.\n\n**The describe fan-out.** The wrapper's body for `describe` reads the units and title from the row, builds the jobs, and starts `step.do(\"describe <unit index>\", {retries 3, timeout 1 min}, …)` for each job within the cap, awaited with `Promise.allSettled`. An image job reads its stored object from R2 inside its child step. Then, still inside the parent's body, it applies every fulfilled result (`Code: …` or `Image: …`), floors every rejected or capped job (code to `Code with no description.`, image keeps its fallback), and makes one D1 batch: the units, the degradations, and one describer ledger row per fulfilled child.\n\n**The spoken form and the title** are set at the end of the recipe step: `spoken.toTypedUnits` runs on the settled units, a new script is saved as the next version first, and one UPDATE writes `title`, `units`, `recipe_version_id`. No surviving unit throws NonRetryableError (`no surviving units`).\n\n**Store** joins `timings[i]` onto the i-th unit; a length mismatch throws NonRetryableError (invariant 2). One D1 batch writes the timed units, `duration`, `audio_format`, the tts ledger row, and `status = ready`, `current_step = null`, so the item turns ready in the same write that makes it readable.\n\n### 4.4 Module list\n\n```\npipeline/package.json                         touched   @nagara/common workspace:*, markdown-it via common, msw dev; build:bundle unchanged\npipeline/pnpm-lock.yaml                       deleted   the root lockfile replaces it\npipeline/pnpm-workspace.yaml                  deleted   its allowBuilds and overrides move to the root\npipeline/wrangler.jsonc                       touched   workflow item/ItemWorkflow, D1, R2, IMAGES, JobIndex removed (a deleted_classes migration), new vars, workers_dev false\npipeline/vitest.config.ts                     touched   readD1Migrations, R2 and D1 bindings for tests\npipeline/src/cloudflare.ts                    touched   exports ItemWorkflow and DomainQueue\npipeline/src/app.ts                           touched   the default export answers 404 to every request\npipeline/src/http/                            deleted   routes.ts, read.ts, job-status.ts: no public routes\npipeline/src/queue/job-index.ts               deleted\npipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts            touched   see 5.1\npipeline/src/workflow/extraction.ts           deleted   its settle loop moves to recipes/settle.ts\npipeline/src/workflow/world.ts                deleted   the tests replay HTTP with msw instead of the seam\npipeline/src/workflow/item.ts                 new       ItemWorkflow.run: the nine wrapper calls in order\npipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts              new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/fetch.ts          new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/lease.ts          new       the ask, the waits, the rechecks\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/recipe.ts         new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/release.ts        new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/images.ts         new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/describe.ts       new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/synthesis.ts      new       start synthesis, the poll loop, store\npipeline/src/workflow/ledger.ts               new       only the steps write ledger rows\npipeline/src/firecrawl/client.ts              new       ported from api/app/service/fetch.py\npipeline/src/recipes/store.ts                 new       ported from api/app/service/recipes.py\npipeline/src/recipes/settle.ts                new       from workflow/extraction.ts, conversation id without suffix\npipeline/src/runtime/                         unchanged\npipeline/src/agents/                          unchanged\npipeline/src/spoken/derive.ts                 new       ported from extract.py: to_spoken, the token walk, tables\npipeline/src/spoken/typed-units.ts            new       drop rule, image anchoring\npipeline/src/images/acquire.ts                new       ported from api/app/service/images.py\npipeline/src/images/svg.ts                    new       sniff and script stripping\npipeline/src/images/alt.ts                    new       spoken form from alt, good-alt filter, cruft test\npipeline/src/describe/core.ts                 new       ported from api/app/service/describe.py\npipeline/src/describe/prompts.ts              new\npipeline/src/describe/jobs.ts                 new\npipeline/src/tts/modal.ts                     new       ported from api/app/service/tts.py, over HTTP\npipeline/test/cassettes/                      new       moved from api/tests/cassettes\npipeline/test/helpers/world.ts                deleted\npipeline/test/helpers/http.ts                 deleted\npipeline/test/extraction-workflow.test.ts     deleted   replaced by item-workflow tests\npipeline/test/http.test.ts, read-path.test.ts, job-index.test.ts   deleted\npipeline/test/*.test.ts                       new       cases from test-design\n```\n\n`images/alt.ts` holds the good-alt filter, which the describe module also needs. Both reach it: the images step speaks the alt and the describe step decides from it. By the project rule that puts it in `common/`; it stays in `pipeline/` here because only pipeline modules use it, and moving pipeline-only code into the package both Workers build is the opposite of the rule's purpose. This is the one placement that departs from a literal reading of CLAUDE.md, flagged for the user.\n\n---\n\n## 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue\n\n### 5.1 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"DomainQueue\",\n  \"$comment\": \"exists; one instance per domain via idFromName(domain)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"acquire\": { \"$comment\": \"added, replaces enqueue\", \"properties\": {\n      \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"instanceId\": {} } },\n      \"output\": { \"properties\": { \"granted\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" } }, \"description\": \"true when the id holds the lease, or the lease is free and the FIFO is empty; otherwise the id is appended once, keeping its place if already waiting.\" } } },\n    \"release\": { \"$comment\": \"changed: keyed on instance id; drops the id from the FIFO too\", \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"instanceId\": {} } } } },\n    \"advance\": { \"$comment\": \"changed: no create; shifts the next id, checks status(), writes the lease, sendEvent({type: 'lease-granted'}); a terminal or throwing id is skipped\" },\n    \"alarm\": { \"$comment\": \"unchanged: 60 s, sweeps an ended or unaddressable holder\" },\n    \"enqueue, stateOf\": { \"$comment\": \"removed\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe FIFO holds instance ids only, since the Workflow carries its own HTML as a step result; the per-key params storage and the job index go. State moves to the synchronous `ctx.storage.kv` as in the item-workflow spike, so `acquire` has no `await` and nothing interleaves.\n\n```\npipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts       touched\npipeline/test/domain-queue.test.ts       touched\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6 tts/: the two web endpoints\n\n### 6.1 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"tts/app.py: start (POST, requires_proxy_auth)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"paragraphs\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"voice\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"af_heart\" }, \"destination\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Presigned PUT URL.\" } }, \"required\": [\"paragraphs\", \"destination\"] },\n    \"output\": { \"properties\": { \"call_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"tts/app.py: result (GET ?call_id=, requires_proxy_auth)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"202 {status: running} while it runs; 200 {format, duration, timings[{start, end}]} when done; 500 {error} when the synthesis raised; 410 when Modal no longer holds the result.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`Kokoro.synthesize` gains `destination`, PUTs the encoded audio there with its content type through httpx, and returns the result without `audio_base64`. Both endpoints live on a small CPU `web` function in the same app that spawns `Kokoro().synthesize` and reads `FunctionCall.from_id(call_id).get(timeout=0)`. Request and response shapes are pydantic models, per CLAUDE.md.\n\n```\ntts/app.py                               touched   the endpoints, destination upload, pydantic models\ntts/pyproject.toml                       touched   fastapi[standard] and httpx for the endpoints\ntts/tests/test_endpoints.py              new\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7 Local development\n\n### 7.1 Module list and launch\n\n```\n.wrangler-state/                         git-ignored: the shared state folder at the repository root\n.gitignore                               touched\napi/wrangler.jsonc                       dev: port 8787\napi/package.json                         dev = wrangler dev --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\npipeline/vite.config.ts                  touched   cloudflare({persistState: {path: \"../.wrangler-state\"}, ...}); experimental local S3 credentials\npipeline/.dev.vars.example               new       secrets plus R2_S3_ENDPOINT = http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3 and R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT = https://<tunnel>/s3\npipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs        new       Node proxy: /s3/<bucket>/<key> to localhost /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/<bucket>/<key>, host rewritten\npipeline/package.json                    touched   dev:proxy = node scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs\ncommon/package.json                      migrate:local = wrangler d1 migrations apply nagara --local --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\n```\n\nLaunch: `pnpm --filter @nagara/common migrate:local`, then `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`, `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`, `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:<proxy port>` by hand, the tunnel host into `.dev.vars`, and `pnpm dev` in `api/`. `cloudflared` is a tool on the developer's machine, not a dependency.\n\n---\n\n## 8 CI\n\n### 8.1 Control flow and module list\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    push([\"push to main\"]) --> ch[\"changes:<br/>paths-filter for<br/>common, pipeline, api\"]\n    ch --> cc[\"common checks:<br/>test, lint, types,<br/>api and pipeline types\"]\n    ch --> pc[\"pipeline checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    ch --> ac[\"api checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    cc --> mig[\"migrate: wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply --remote\"]\n    mig --> pd[\"deploy pipeline:<br/>pnpm build,<br/>deploy dist config\"]\n    pc --> pd\n    pd --> ad[\"deploy api\"]\n    ac --> ad\n    cc -. \"a check fails\" .-> stop([\"nothing deploys\"])\n```\n\nOne `cloudflare.yml` replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`: the jobs a tree did not change are skipped, and every deploy job runs on `!failure() && !cancelled()` with its own tree changed or an upstream deploy run, so a pipeline-only push deploys the pipeline without waiting for a migration that never ran, and a failed common check stops everything after it. Three separate workflows cannot wait on each other within one push without polling, which is why this is one file; the docs say three workflows and would change to one workflow with a job group per tree.\n\n```\n.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml         new\n.github/workflows/api.yml                deleted\n.github/workflows/pipeline.yml           deleted\n.github/workflows/tts.yml                unchanged\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9 Standards\n\n```\n- CLAUDE.md, \"Code style\": common/ holds the shared types; payloads crossing a boundary are typed; pydantic models for tts/'s endpoints\n- CLAUDE.md, \"Invariants\" 2, 3: store's length guard; 4: the key guard ahead of every /items route; 5: Modal over HTTP, retry from the failed step, the 15-minute re-queue; 6: R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT and the other vars instead of any environment branch; 7: migrations in common/ and the tests' schema from them; 8: the CI order\n- CLAUDE.md, \"When adding something\": the spoken-form and drop functions at the end of the recipe step; anything more than one module uses in common/\n- ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md: == null checks, constant maps instead of enums, one function per module by default, named exports, arrow functions, airy blocks\n- .mahou/basics.md and mahou:basics \"Code\": no comments inside object literals, configs or fixtures\n- wiki cloudflare/workflows: step names with counters, restart({from}), the 6-connection limit, idempotent bodies\n- wiki cloudflare/vitest-plugin and .mahou/wiki/testing/cassettes-over-mocks: msw replay, introspection to skip sleeps, unmatched requests fail\n- wiki cloudflare/r2 and cloudflare/local-dev: presigning with aws4fetch, the local S3 endpoint and the tunnel proxy\n- wiki cloudflare/images: rasters through the binding, SVG kept\n- wiki cloudflare/ai-gateway and gemini: the cache header, the gateway URL, text/plain SVG parts\n- wiki firecrawl: the fetch client in place of the SDK\n- wiki modal: proxy-auth headers on web endpoints\n- wiki cloudflare/flue and cloudflare/durable-objects: agents dispatched from a step, the DO's synchronous kv\n- wiki markdown: markdown-it's token tree for the spoken form\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5462,"cache_read_input_tokens":187977,"output_tokens":16908,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":23},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5462,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":16908,"cache_read_input_tokens":187977,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5462},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014U1Ejk8czyaC5w3Wd55rSe":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md","content":"# Program design: nagara on Cloudflare\n\nRepository: `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara`, branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`, clean.\n\nCovers how the Cloudflare migration lands in the code: the pnpm workspace, `common/`, the new TypeScript `api/`, the item Workflow and DomainQueue in `pipeline/`, the two web endpoints in `tts/`, local development and CI. Source: the notes under `docs/technical-design/` committed in `c0dbdba`, plus `design.md` and `recording-decisions.md` in this folder. Leaves out the test cases and manual validations (mahou:test-design), and `web/`.\n\nStatus: **proposed**, every part. The user reads the whole proposal on the canvas and points out what does not match.\n\n```\nProgram design\n└─ nagara                                                        proposed\n   ├─ 1 Workspace and packages                                   proposed\n   │  └─ 1.1 Package layout\n   ├─ 2 common/                                                  proposed\n   │  ├─ 2.1 What each module exposes (interfaces)\n   │  └─ 2.2 Module list\n   ├─ 3 api/: the routes                                         proposed\n   │  ├─ 3.1 Callstacks: enqueue, poll with re-queue, retry, media\n   │  ├─ 3.2 Interfaces and module list\n   │  └─ 3.3 Critical behaviour: the re-queue and the restart point\n   ├─ 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow                             proposed\n   │  ├─ 4.1 Control flow: the nine steps and the wrapper\n   │  ├─ 4.2 Interfaces: the step wrapper, step results, modules\n   │  ├─ 4.3 Critical behaviour: lease, poll loop, describe fan-out\n   │  └─ 4.4 Module list\n   ├─ 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue                                   proposed\n   │  └─ 5.1 Interfaces and module list\n   ├─ 6 tts/: the two web endpoints                              proposed\n   │  └─ 6.1 Interfaces and module list\n   ├─ 7 Local development                                        proposed\n   │  └─ 7.1 Module list and launch\n   ├─ 8 CI                                                       proposed\n   │  └─ 8.1 Control flow and module list\n   └─ 9 Standards                                                proposed\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1 Workspace and packages\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```\nnagara/\n├── package.json                 new   private root, no scripts of its own\n├── pnpm-workspace.yaml          new   packages: common, api, pipeline; carries pipeline's allowBuilds and overrides\n├── pnpm-lock.yaml               new   one lockfile for the three TypeScript packages\n├── common/                      new   @nagara/common, source only: exports .ts, never built\n│   ├── package.json             exports \".\", \"./testing\"\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           the D1 binding and migrations_dir, for `wrangler d1 migrations apply`\n│   ├── migrations/              hand-written SQL, applied by CI, locally, and by both Workers' tests\n│   ├── src/                     types, keys, presigning, item row, sanitize\n│   ├── testing/                 the cassette replay library (vitest only)\n│   └── test/\n├── api/                         replaced: the Python tree goes, a Worker takes its place\n│   ├── package.json             @nagara/api; depends on @nagara/common: workspace:*\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           name nagara-api, route nagara.asermax.com, D1, R2, the item Workflow by script_name\n│   ├── src/\n│   └── test/\n├── pipeline/                    touched\n│   ├── package.json             depends on @nagara/common: workspace:*; own pnpm-lock.yaml and pnpm-workspace.yaml go\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           workflow renamed item, JobIndex deleted, D1 and R2 bound, workers_dev false\n│   ├── src/\n│   └── test/                    cassettes/ moves here from api/tests/cassettes\n├── tts/                         touched: two web endpoints, no package change\n└── .github/workflows/           cloudflare.yml replaces api.yml and pipeline.yml; tts.yml unchanged\n```\n\n`common/` is a workspace package because both Workers import it at build time and its migrations are the one thing it deploys. It ships no build step: Vite (pipeline) and wrangler's esbuild (api) compile its `.ts` sources directly, the way `pipeline/` already imports its own `.ts` paths. The `./testing` export keeps the cassette library and its YAML parser out of the Workers' runtime bundles.\n\nOne root workspace and lockfile replace `pipeline/`'s own, so `workspace:*` links resolve without publishing. `pnpm install` from any of the three folders installs the workspace. `tts/` stays outside the workspace, under uv as today.\n\nNew dependencies: `aws4fetch` in `common/` for presigning (the r2-presigned spike signed with it), `markdown-it` in `common/` for the sanitize tail's partner, the spoken-form derivation (wiki `markdown`), `yaml` in `common/` dev for cassette parsing, `msw@2.15` as a dev dependency of both Workers (msw 3's `msw/node` does not start in workerd, workflow-testing spike). `valibot` stays in `pipeline/` and joins `api/` for the enqueue body.\n\n---\n\n## 2 common/\n\n### 2.1 What each module exposes\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/item.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"The item row and its statuses.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"ITEM_STATUS\": { \"enum\": [\"queued\", \"generating\", \"ready\", \"failed\"], \"description\": \"Constant map; ItemStatus derives from it.\" },\n    \"ItemRow\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"itm_ plus 8 hex characters.\" },\n        \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"title\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"voice\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"status\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ITEM_STATUS\" },\n        \"created_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"updated_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"queued_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"workflow_instance_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"current_step\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"A STEP name, or a poll step's numbered name.\" },\n        \"extraction_domain\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"recipe_version_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"retry_count\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n        \"duration\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n        \"audio_format\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"units\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/units.ts#/$defs/RowUnit\" } },\n        \"degradations\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/units.ts#/$defs/Degradation\" } },\n        \"error\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/units.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"The unit union the display, spoken form and timing ride on.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"Unit\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphUnit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CodeUnit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ImageUnit\" }] },\n    \"ParagraphUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"paragraph\" }, \"display\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"spoken\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"start\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"end\": { \"type\": \"number\" } }, \"required\": [\"type\", \"display\", \"spoken\"] },\n    \"CodeUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"code\" }, \"display\": {}, \"spoken\": {}, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } },\n    \"ImageUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"image\" }, \"display\": { \"description\": \"![<raw alt>](/items/<id>/images/<hash>): the describe step reads the alt back from here.\" }, \"spoken\": {}, \"image\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The content hash.\" }, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } },\n    \"DeclaredImageUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"declared-image\" }, \"src\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"alt\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"description\": \"An image the recipe declared and the images step has not acquired yet; never survives the images step.\" },\n    \"RowUnit\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Unit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DeclaredImageUnit\" }] },\n    \"DEGRADATION_REASON\": { \"enum\": [\"404\", \"timeout\", \"undecodable\", \"describe failed\", \"describe cap reached\"] },\n    \"Degradation\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"enum\": [\"image\", \"code\"] }, \"reason\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DEGRADATION_REASON\" }, \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Origin URL, acquisition failures only.\" } }, \"required\": [\"type\", \"reason\"] }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/workflow.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"What the API and the item Workflow agree on.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"ItemWorkflowParams\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"itemId\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"required\": [\"itemId\"] },\n    \"STEP\": { \"enum\": [\"fetch\", \"lease\", \"recipe\", \"release\", \"images\", \"describe\", \"start synthesis\", \"poll\", \"store\"], \"description\": \"Constant map of step names. A poll step runs as `poll <n>`.\" },\n    \"restartPoint\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"currentStep\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] } } },\n        \"output\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"The step name restart() starts from: lease for recipe and release, the step itself otherwise, null (restart every step) when empty.\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/row.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"Reads and writes of the item row both Workers make.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"readItem\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"db\": { \"description\": \"D1Database\" }, \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"ItemRow with units and degradations decoded, or null.\" } } },\n    \"writeStatus\": {\n      \"description\": \"One UPDATE: status, current_step, error = null, updated_at = now. Used by the API for queued and by the step wrapper for every status.\",\n      \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"db\": {}, \"id\": {}, \"status\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/item.ts#/$defs/ITEM_STATUS\" }, \"currentStep\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] }, \"error\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Set only with failed.\" } }, \"required\": [\"db\", \"id\", \"status\"] }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"nothing\" } }\n    },\n    \"encodeJson / decodeJson\": { \"description\": \"The JSON column codec for units and degradations.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/keys.ts and common/src/presign.ts\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"audioKey\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"itemId\": {} } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"audio/<itemId>\" } } },\n    \"imageKey\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"hash\": {} } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"images/<hash>\" } } },\n    \"presign\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n          \"endpoint\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The S3 endpoint the URL is signed for: R2's in production, the local S3 endpoint locally.\" },\n          \"bucket\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"key\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"method\": { \"enum\": [\"GET\", \"PUT\"] },\n          \"accessKeyId\": {}, \"secretAccessKey\": {},\n          \"expiresIn\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"description\": \"Seconds; 3600 for both callers.\" }\n        } },\n        \"output\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The signed URL.\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/ledger.ts, common/src/recipe.ts, common/src/sanitize.ts\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"COST_TYPE\": { \"enum\": [\"firecrawl\", \"describer\", \"tts\"] },\n    \"COST_UNIT\": { \"enum\": [\"credits\", \"calls\", \"seconds\"] },\n    \"CostEntryRow\": { \"properties\": { \"id\": {}, \"item_id\": {}, \"type\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/COST_TYPE\" }, \"quantity\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"unit\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/COST_UNIT\" }, \"dollars\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"cached\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }, \"detail\": { \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"] }, \"created_at\": {} } },\n    \"RecipeVersionRow\": { \"properties\": { \"id\": {}, \"domain\": {}, \"version\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }, \"script\": {}, \"created_at\": {} } },\n    \"sanitizeSpoken\": { \"description\": \"The sanitize tail: markers touching text, tags to words, comparison operators to words. Used by the spoken-form derivation and the describer, two pipeline modules.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/testing: replayCassettes\",\n  \"description\": \"Our TypeScript copy of vcrpy, replay only, run through msw in both Workers' tests.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"cassette\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The YAML text, imported with ?raw.\" },\n      \"rewrite\": { \"description\": \"Host rewrites, such as generativelanguage.googleapis.com to the gateway's URL.\" }\n    } },\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"msw handlers: match on method, scheme, host, port, query, and path and JSON body with item ids normalized; credential headers stripped before matching; content-encoding, content-length and transfer-encoding stripped from the replayed response; repeated identical requests answer in recorded order; an unmatched request throws.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe D1 test schema comes from `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`'s `readD1Migrations(\"../common/migrations\")` in each Worker's vitest config and `applyD1Migrations` in a setup file, so `common/testing` holds only the cassette library.\n\n`sanitizeSpoken` and the row reads and writes are in `common/` because the project's rule puts there everything more than one module uses: the sanitize tail serves the spoken-form module and the describer module, the row writes serve the API and the pipeline.\n\n### 2.2 Module list\n\n```\ncommon/package.json                      new\ncommon/tsconfig.json                     new\ncommon/biome.json                        new   copied from pipeline/\ncommon/wrangler.jsonc                    new   D1 binding \"DB\", database nagara, migrations_dir migrations\ncommon/migrations/0001_initial.sql       new   items, recipe_versions, cost_entries, with the indexes for recipe lookup\ncommon/src/item.ts                       new\ncommon/src/units.ts                      new\ncommon/src/workflow.ts                   new\ncommon/src/row.ts                        new\ncommon/src/keys.ts                       new\ncommon/src/presign.ts                    new\ncommon/src/ledger.ts                     new\ncommon/src/recipe.ts                     new\ncommon/src/sanitize.ts                   new   ported from api/app/service/extract.py, sanitize_spoken and its helpers\ncommon/src/index.ts                      new   re-exports src/\ncommon/testing/cassettes.ts              new   ported from api/tests/conftest.py's matchers and filters\ncommon/testing/index.ts                  new\ncommon/test/presign.test.ts              new\ncommon/test/sanitize.test.ts             new\ncommon/test/row.test.ts                  new\ncommon/test/cassettes.test.ts            new\n```\n\nThe SQL starts from the D1 schema at migration 0001 because the move starts empty; the Alembic history is not carried over.\n\n---\n\n## 3 api/: the routes\n\n### 3.1 Callstacks\n\n```\nPOST /items\ngiven X-API-Key, {url, voice?}\n│\n└─ index.fetch → guard.requireKey                               401 on a missing or wrong key\n   └─ routes/enqueue\n      ├─ valibot parse {url: string, voice?: string}            400 when malformed\n      ├─ voices.pick(voice)                                     random from the curated pool when absent\n      ├─ items/create.insertQueued(db, {id = itm_ + 8 hex, url, voice, status queued, queued_at = now})\n      ├─ env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({params: {itemId}})           instance id left to Cloudflare\n      │  └─ when create throws: log it, answer 202 anyway       the re-queue on read recovers the item\n      └─ 202 response.toItemResponse(row)\n```\n\n```\nGET /items/{id}\ngiven X-API-Key, id\n│\n└─ routes/poll\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null\n   ├─ when status queued and queued_at older than 15 min\n   │  └─ items/requeue.requeue(env, row)\n   │     ├─ claim: UPDATE items SET queued_at = now, updated_at = now\n   │     │         WHERE id = ? AND status = 'queued' AND queued_at < now - 15 min\n   │     ├─ when no row changed: another poll claimed it, nothing more\n   │     ├─ when workflow_instance_id is null\n   │     │  └─ env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({params: {itemId}})\n   │     └─ otherwise\n   │        └─ (await env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.get(instance id)).restart(from restartPoint(current_step))\n   └─ 200 response.toItemResponse(row)\n```\n\n```\nPOST /items/{id}/retry\ngiven X-API-Key, id\n│\n└─ routes/retry\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null\n   ├─ items/retry-claim.claim(db, id, retryMax)\n   │  └─ UPDATE items SET status = 'queued', error = null, queued_at = now, updated_at = now,\n   │     retry_count = retry_count + 1\n   │     WHERE id = ? AND status = 'failed' AND retry_count < ?  409 when no row changed; the pre-read picks the message\n   ├─ (await env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.get(workflow_instance_id)).restart(from restartPoint(current_step))\n   │  └─ when the row holds no instance id: create({params: {itemId}})\n   └─ 202 response.toItemResponse(claimed row)\n```\n\n```\nGET /items/{id}/audio · GET /items/{id}/images/{hash}\ngiven X-API-Key, id[, hash]\n│\n└─ routes/audio | routes/images\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null; audio also 404 unless ready with audio_format\n   ├─ common.presign({endpoint: R2_S3_ENDPOINT, bucket, key: audioKey(id) | imageKey(hash),\n   │                  method GET, R2 GET token, expiresIn 3600})\n   └─ 307 to the signed URL\n\nGET /health → 200 \"ok\", before the guard\n```\n\n### 3.2 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"api/ wrangler bindings and configuration\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"DB\": { \"description\": \"D1 nagara, shared with the pipeline.\" },\n    \"ITEM_WORKFLOW\": { \"description\": \"workflows: {binding ITEM_WORKFLOW, name item, class_name ItemWorkflow, script_name nagara}.\" },\n    \"vars\": { \"properties\": { \"R2_S3_ENDPOINT\": {}, \"R2_BUCKET\": {}, \"RETRY_MAX\": { \"const\": 3 }, \"REQUEUE_AFTER_MS\": { \"const\": 900000 } } },\n    \"secrets\": { \"properties\": { \"API_KEY\": {}, \"R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID\": {}, \"R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\": {} } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"api/src/response.ts: toItemResponse\",\n  \"description\": \"The wire projection, unchanged for clients: drops spoken, adds index, holds units back until ready.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"description\": \"ItemRow\" },\n    \"output\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"id\": {}, \"url\": {}, \"title\": {}, \"status\": {}, \"voice\": {}, \"created_at\": {},\n      \"duration\": { \"description\": \"Absent until ready.\" },\n      \"units\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"properties\": { \"index\": {}, \"type\": {}, \"display\": {}, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {}, \"image\": {} } }, \"description\": \"null unless ready.\" },\n      \"error\": {},\n      \"audio_url\": { \"description\": \"/items/<id>/audio, only when ready.\" }\n    } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```\napi/                                     the Python tree goes: app/, migrations/, tests/, data/, prototype_cache/,\n                                         alembic.ini, pyproject.toml, uv.lock, railway.toml        deleted\napi/tests/cassettes/                     moved to pipeline/test/cassettes/\napi/package.json                         new\napi/tsconfig.json                        new\napi/biome.json                           new\napi/wrangler.jsonc                       new\napi/vitest.config.ts                     new   readD1Migrations(\"../common/migrations\")\napi/src/index.ts                         new   fetch handler: /health, the key guard, the route table (plain matching, as pipeline/src/http/routes.ts does)\napi/src/guard.ts                         new\napi/src/voices.ts                        new   the curated pool, ported from api/app/service/tts.py pick_voice\napi/src/response.ts                      new\napi/src/routes/enqueue.ts                new\napi/src/routes/poll.ts                   new\napi/src/routes/retry.ts                  new\napi/src/routes/audio.ts                  new\napi/src/routes/images.ts                 new\napi/src/items/create.ts                  new   insertQueued and the id mint\napi/src/items/requeue.ts                 new\napi/src/items/retry-claim.ts             new\napi/test/setup.ts                        new   applies the migrations\napi/test/helpers/workflow-stand-in.ts    new   the stand-in for ITEM_WORKFLOW: records create, get and restart calls\napi/test/*.test.ts                       new   one file per route, cases from test-design\n```\n\n### 3.3 Critical behaviour\n\nThe re-queue claims the row with one conditional UPDATE before it touches the instance, the same pattern as the retry claim, so two polls landing together restart the instance once. It does not increment `retry_count`: the cap bounds client retries of failed items, and a re-queue recovers an item that never failed. It restarts from `restartPoint(current_step)`, so an item waiting for its domain's lease (current_step `lease`) asks for the lease again, and DomainQueue keeps an id that is already in its FIFO at its position (5.1); a re-queue never sends a waiting item to the back.\n\nThe retry route reaches the same `restartPoint`. `recipe` and `release` map to `lease`; `poll <n>` restarts at that poll step, so the poll steps before it replay from cache and Modal is not asked to synthesize again; an empty `current_step` restarts every step.\n\nNeither route reads the instance's status: the row is the only state the API reads, as the design says.\n\n---\n\n## 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow\n\n### 4.1 Control flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"ItemWorkflow.run<br/>params {itemId}\"]) --> s1[\"1 fetch · queued<br/>writes instance id,<br/>domain, ledger row<br/>returns {html}\"]\n    s1 --> s2[\"2 lease · queued<br/>ask DomainQueue,<br/>waitForEvent lease-granted\"]\n    s2 --> s3[\"3 recipe · generating<br/>run, author or revise;<br/>spoken form and drop;<br/>writes title, units\"]\n    s3 --> s4[\"4 release · generating<br/>give the lease back\"]\n    s4 --> s5[\"5 images · generating<br/>acquire declared images;<br/>writes units, degradations\"]\n    s5 --> s6[\"6 describe · generating<br/>child steps, allSettled;<br/>one write at the end\"]\n    s6 --> s7[\"7 start synthesis<br/>· generating<br/>sign PUT, call Modal<br/>returns {callId}\"]\n    s7 --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"8 poll · generating\"]\n        direction TB\n        p[\"poll n: fetch result\"] --> r{\"ready?\"}\n        r -->|\"no: sleep 10 s,<br/>n + 1\"| p\n    end\n    r -->|\"yes, returns the result\"| s9[\"9 store · generating<br/>join timings; writes<br/>ready, units, duration,<br/>format, tts ledger row\"]\n    s9 --> done([\"ready\"])\n    s1 -. \"last attempt fails\" .-> fail([\"wrapper writes failed,<br/>the step's error;<br/>run() rethrows\"])\n    s2 -. \"3 waits of 1 h\" .-> fail\n    s3 -. \"not an article: at once\" .-> fail\n    s5 -.-> fail\n    s7 -.-> fail\n    loop -. \"failed or expired\" .-> fail\n    s9 -. \"length mismatch\" .-> fail\n```\n\nEvery box is one call to the wrapper (4.2), which runs the body inside `step.do` with the step's retries and timeout. The order is required throughout: the lease comes before recipe and goes right after it; images come before describe because describe reads the acquired images from R2; describe comes before start synthesis because synthesis reads the described spoken forms from the row.\n\nA failed step ends the run: the wrapper writes `failed` with the step's own error and rethrows, so the instance ends `errored`, which DomainQueue's alarm reads when the failed step held the lease. describe never fails because a child failed (4.3). The Workflow returns nothing.\n\n### 4.2 Interfaces\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts: runStep\",\n  \"description\": \"The logic every step shares.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"ctx\": { \"properties\": { \"step\": { \"description\": \"WorkflowStep\" }, \"db\": {}, \"itemId\": {} } },\n      \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The step name: a STEP value, or poll <n>.\" },\n      \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"queued\", \"generating\"], \"description\": \"queued for fetch and lease, generating after.\" },\n      \"config\": { \"properties\": { \"retries\": { \"const\": 3, \"description\": \"limit 3, 5 s exponential delay\" }, \"timeout\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n      \"body\": { \"description\": \"The step's work; returns its step result or nothing.\" }\n    } },\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"The body's step result.\" }\n  },\n  \"$comment\": \"Inside step.do, first thing in every attempt: writeStatus(status, current_step = name), which also clears error. When step.do throws (its last attempt failed, or a NonRetryableError): step.do('<name> failed') writes failed with error.message, then rethrows. An attempt that fails with attempts left writes nothing.\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Step results\",\n  \"description\": \"Only what the Workflow needs and the row does not hold.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"fetch\": { \"properties\": { \"html\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n    \"start synthesis\": { \"properties\": { \"callId\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n    \"poll <n>\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"properties\": { \"ready\": { \"const\": false } } }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SynthesisResult\" }], \"description\": \"{ready: false}, never null: a falsy mocked step result is ignored by the test engine.\" }\n  },\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"SynthesisResult\": { \"properties\": { \"ready\": { \"const\": true }, \"format\": { \"enum\": [\"audio/ogg\", \"audio/wav\"] }, \"duration\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"timings\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"properties\": { \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } } } } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/ domain modules: what each step calls\",\n  \"description\": \"Each module returns values; only the step files write to D1 and R2.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"firecrawl.scrape(url)\": { \"description\": \"→ {html, finalUrl, creditsUsed, proxy}. Our fetch client, the Python SDK's fields; rawHtml + markdown at proxy auto. Throws on no HTML; the step throws NonRetryableError over maxHtmlBytes.\" },\n    \"recipes.currentRecipe(db, domain) / recipes.saveVersion(db, domain, script)\": { \"description\": \"→ RecipeVersionRow | null; the insert as the next version.\" },\n    \"recipes.settle(env, {instanceId, domain, html, recipe?})\": { \"description\": \"→ {kind: 'ok', title, units, script, isNew} | {kind: 'not-article'} | {kind: 'gave-up', reason}. Runs the recipe; on failure dispatches the revision agent, or the author when there is no recipe; conversation id = instance id; authoring 1 retry, revision 2, every settled script re-run through the runtime.\" },\n    \"spoken.toTypedUnits(recipeUnits, title)\": { \"description\": \"→ RowUnit[]: spoken form derived, empty-of-letters units dropped, declared images anchored after the last kept text unit.\" },\n    \"images.acquire(env, units, itemId)\": { \"description\": \"→ {units, degradations}: download under per-host 2 / global 10 semaphores, 10 s, 10 MB; sniff <svg; SVG scripts stripped with HTMLRewriter; rasters through env.IMAGES, kept when min side ≥ 200, re-encoded to WebP; sha256 of the stored bytes; R2 put under imageKey with its content type; spoken Image: <alt> or the floor.\" },\n    \"describe.jobs(units, title)\": { \"description\": \"→ the document-ordered jobs: every code unit, every image whose alt (read from display) fails the good-alt filter; the cap of 25 splits them into described and capped.\" },\n    \"describe.describeOne(env, job, image?)\": { \"description\": \"→ {spoken, cached}: one Gemini call through AI Gateway, structured output {spoken}, sanitized; cached from cf-aig-cache-status.\" },\n    \"tts.start(env, {paragraphs, voice, destination}) / tts.result(env, callId)\": { \"description\": \"→ callId; → {ready: false} | SynthesisResult. Proxy-auth headers Modal-Key and Modal-Secret. 500 and 410 throw.\" },\n    \"ledger.record(db, entry)\": { \"description\": \"Inserts one CostEntryRow at the configured price.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/ wrangler bindings and configuration\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"workflows\": { \"description\": \"{binding ITEM_WORKFLOW, name item, class_name ItemWorkflow}.\" },\n    \"DB / BUCKET / IMAGES / LOADER / DOMAIN_QUEUE\": { \"description\": \"D1 nagara, R2 nagara, the Images binding, the Worker Loader, the DomainQueue DO.\" },\n    \"vars\": { \"properties\": { \"R2_S3_ENDPOINT\": { \"description\": \"The endpoint PUT URLs are signed for.\" }, \"R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\": { \"description\": \"What Modal is handed in its place; equal to R2_S3_ENDPOINT in production, the tunnel's https://<host>/s3 locally.\" }, \"R2_BUCKET\": {}, \"MODAL_START_URL\": {}, \"MODAL_RESULT_URL\": {}, \"describeMaxPerItem\": { \"const\": 25 }, \"imageFetchPerHost\": { \"const\": 2 }, \"imageFetchConcurrency\": { \"const\": 10 }, \"pollIntervalSeconds\": { \"const\": 10 }, \"prices\": { \"description\": \"firecrawl per credit, describer per call, tts per second\" }, \"existing\": { \"description\": \"agentModel, agentMaxTurns, authoringRetries, revisionRetries, leaseAlarmMs, recipeCpuMs, maxHtmlBytes, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, CLOUDFLARE_GATEWAY_ID\" } } },\n    \"secrets\": { \"properties\": { \"FIRECRAWL_API_KEY\": {}, \"GEMINI_API_KEY\": {}, \"CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY\": { \"description\": \"The AI Gateway token, the name the agents already read.\" }, \"MODAL_PROXY_KEY\": {}, \"MODAL_PROXY_SECRET\": {}, \"R2_PUT_ACCESS_KEY_ID\": {}, \"R2_PUT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\": {} } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 4.3 Critical behaviour\n\n**The lease.** The `lease` step asks `DomainQueue.acquire(instanceId)` and returns `{granted}`. When not granted, the Workflow waits with `step.waitForEvent(\"lease wait <n>\", {type: \"lease-granted\", timeout: \"1 hour\"})`, up to 3 waits; after a wait times out, a `lease recheck <n>` step asks again, since a grant can be lost to a deploy. An event sent before the wait begins is kept (item-workflow spike). After the third timeout the wrapper's failure path writes `failed`. The waits sit between wrapper calls and write nothing, so `current_step` stays `lease` throughout.\n\n**The poll loop.** Step `poll <n>` asks Modal for the result; when it is not ready, `step.sleep(\"poll sleep <n>\", pollIntervalSeconds)` and `n + 1`. Each name carries its counter, because a repeated name replays the cached result. Each poll step has 3 attempts of 1 min; Modal's 500 (the synthesis crashed) and 410 (the result expired after 7 days) throw, so a crashed synthesis uses the poll step's attempts and fails the item. At 10 s, the 10,000-step limit covers about 27 h of synthesis; a 70-minute article took 176 s.\n\n**The describe fan-out.** The wrapper's body for `describe` reads the units and title from the row, builds the jobs, and starts `step.do(\"describe <unit index>\", {retries 3, timeout 1 min}, …)` for each job within the cap, awaited with `Promise.allSettled`. An image job reads its stored object from R2 inside its child step. Then, still inside the parent's body, it applies every fulfilled result (`Code: …` or `Image: …`), floors every rejected or capped job (code to `Code with no description.`, image keeps its fallback), and makes one D1 batch: the units, the degradations, and one describer ledger row per fulfilled child.\n\n**The spoken form and the title** are set at the end of the recipe step: `spoken.toTypedUnits` runs on the settled units, a new script is saved as the next version first, and one UPDATE writes `title`, `units`, `recipe_version_id`. No surviving unit throws NonRetryableError (`no surviving units`).\n\n**Store** joins `timings[i]` onto the i-th unit; a length mismatch throws NonRetryableError (invariant 2). One D1 batch writes the timed units, `duration`, `audio_format`, the tts ledger row, and `status = ready`, `current_step = null`, so the item turns ready in the same write that makes it readable.\n\n### 4.4 Module list\n\n```\npipeline/package.json                         touched   @nagara/common workspace:*, markdown-it via common, msw dev; build:bundle unchanged\npipeline/pnpm-lock.yaml                       deleted   the root lockfile replaces it\npipeline/pnpm-workspace.yaml                  deleted   its allowBuilds and overrides move to the root\npipeline/wrangler.jsonc                       touched   workflow item/ItemWorkflow, D1, R2, IMAGES, JobIndex removed (a deleted_classes migration), new vars, workers_dev false\npipeline/vitest.config.ts                     touched   readD1Migrations, R2 and D1 bindings for tests\npipeline/src/cloudflare.ts                    touched   exports ItemWorkflow and DomainQueue\npipeline/src/app.ts                           touched   the default export answers 404 to every request\npipeline/src/http/                            deleted   routes.ts, read.ts, job-status.ts: no public routes\npipeline/src/queue/job-index.ts               deleted\npipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts            touched   see 5.1\npipeline/src/workflow/extraction.ts           deleted   its settle loop moves to recipes/settle.ts\npipeline/src/workflow/world.ts                deleted   the tests replay HTTP with msw instead of the seam\npipeline/src/workflow/item.ts                 new       ItemWorkflow.run: the nine wrapper calls in order\npipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts              new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/fetch.ts          new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/lease.ts          new       the ask, the waits, the rechecks\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/recipe.ts         new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/release.ts        new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/images.ts         new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/describe.ts       new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/synthesis.ts      new       start synthesis, the poll loop, store\npipeline/src/workflow/ledger.ts               new       only the steps write ledger rows\npipeline/src/firecrawl/client.ts              new       ported from api/app/service/fetch.py\npipeline/src/recipes/store.ts                 new       ported from api/app/service/recipes.py\npipeline/src/recipes/settle.ts                new       from workflow/extraction.ts, conversation id without suffix\npipeline/src/runtime/                         unchanged\npipeline/src/agents/                          unchanged\npipeline/src/spoken/derive.ts                 new       ported from extract.py: to_spoken, the token walk, tables\npipeline/src/spoken/typed-units.ts            new       drop rule, image anchoring\npipeline/src/images/acquire.ts                new       ported from api/app/service/images.py\npipeline/src/images/svg.ts                    new       sniff and script stripping\npipeline/src/images/alt.ts                    new       spoken form from alt, good-alt filter, cruft test\npipeline/src/describe/core.ts                 new       ported from api/app/service/describe.py\npipeline/src/describe/prompts.ts              new\npipeline/src/describe/jobs.ts                 new\npipeline/src/tts/modal.ts                     new       ported from api/app/service/tts.py, over HTTP\npipeline/test/cassettes/                      new       moved from api/tests/cassettes\npipeline/test/helpers/world.ts                deleted\npipeline/test/helpers/http.ts                 deleted\npipeline/test/extraction-workflow.test.ts     deleted   replaced by item-workflow tests\npipeline/test/http.test.ts, read-path.test.ts, job-index.test.ts   deleted\npipeline/test/*.test.ts                       new       cases from test-design\n```\n\n`images/alt.ts` holds the good-alt filter, which the describe module also needs. Both reach it: the images step speaks the alt and the describe step decides from it. By the project rule that puts it in `common/`; it stays in `pipeline/` here because only pipeline modules use it, and moving pipeline-only code into the package both Workers build is the opposite of the rule's purpose. This is the one placement that departs from a literal reading of CLAUDE.md, flagged for the user.\n\n---\n\n## 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue\n\n### 5.1 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"DomainQueue\",\n  \"$comment\": \"exists; one instance per domain via idFromName(domain)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"acquire\": { \"$comment\": \"added, replaces enqueue\", \"properties\": {\n      \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"instanceId\": {} } },\n      \"output\": { \"properties\": { \"granted\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" } }, \"description\": \"true when the id holds the lease, or the lease is free and the FIFO is empty; otherwise the id is appended once, keeping its place if already waiting.\" } } },\n    \"release\": { \"$comment\": \"changed: keyed on instance id; drops the id from the FIFO too\", \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"instanceId\": {} } } } },\n    \"advance\": { \"$comment\": \"changed: no create; shifts the next id, checks status(), writes the lease, sendEvent({type: 'lease-granted'}); a terminal or throwing id is skipped\" },\n    \"alarm\": { \"$comment\": \"unchanged: 60 s, sweeps an ended or unaddressable holder\" },\n    \"enqueue, stateOf\": { \"$comment\": \"removed\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe FIFO holds instance ids only, since the Workflow carries its own HTML as a step result; the per-key params storage and the job index go. State moves to the synchronous `ctx.storage.kv` as in the item-workflow spike, so `acquire` has no `await` and nothing interleaves.\n\n```\npipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts       touched\npipeline/test/domain-queue.test.ts       touched\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6 tts/: the two web endpoints\n\n### 6.1 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"tts/app.py: start (POST, requires_proxy_auth)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"paragraphs\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"voice\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"af_heart\" }, \"destination\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Presigned PUT URL.\" } }, \"required\": [\"paragraphs\", \"destination\"] },\n    \"output\": { \"properties\": { \"call_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"tts/app.py: result (GET ?call_id=, requires_proxy_auth)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"202 {status: running} while it runs; 200 {format, duration, timings[{start, end}]} when done; 500 {error} when the synthesis raised; 410 when Modal no longer holds the result.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`Kokoro.synthesize` gains `destination`, PUTs the encoded audio there with its content type through httpx, and returns the result without `audio_base64`. Both endpoints live on a small CPU `web` function in the same app that spawns `Kokoro().synthesize` and reads `FunctionCall.from_id(call_id).get(timeout=0)`. Request and response shapes are pydantic models, per CLAUDE.md.\n\n```\ntts/app.py                               touched   the endpoints, destination upload, pydantic models\ntts/pyproject.toml                       touched   fastapi[standard] and httpx for the endpoints\ntts/tests/test_endpoints.py              new\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7 Local development\n\n### 7.1 Module list and launch\n\n```\n.wrangler-state/                         git-ignored: the shared state folder at the repository root\n.gitignore                               touched\napi/wrangler.jsonc                       dev: port 8787\napi/package.json                         dev = wrangler dev --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\npipeline/vite.config.ts                  touched   cloudflare({persistState: {path: \"../.wrangler-state\"}, ...}); experimental local S3 credentials\npipeline/.dev.vars.example               new       secrets plus R2_S3_ENDPOINT = http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3 and R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT = https://<tunnel>/s3\npipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs        new       Node proxy: /s3/<bucket>/<key> to localhost /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/<bucket>/<key>, host rewritten\npipeline/package.json                    touched   dev:proxy = node scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs\ncommon/package.json                      migrate:local = wrangler d1 migrations apply nagara --local --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\n```\n\nLaunch: `pnpm --filter @nagara/common migrate:local`, then `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`, `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`, `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:<proxy port>` by hand, the tunnel host into `.dev.vars`, and `pnpm dev` in `api/`. `cloudflared` is a tool on the developer's machine, not a dependency.\n\n---\n\n## 8 CI\n\n### 8.1 Control flow and module list\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    push([\"push to main\"]) --> ch[\"changes:<br/>paths-filter for<br/>common, pipeline, api\"]\n    ch --> cc[\"common checks:<br/>test, lint, types,<br/>api and pipeline types\"]\n    ch --> pc[\"pipeline checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    ch --> ac[\"api checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    cc --> mig[\"migrate: wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply --remote\"]\n    mig --> pd[\"deploy pipeline:<br/>pnpm build,<br/>deploy dist config\"]\n    pc --> pd\n    pd --> ad[\"deploy api\"]\n    ac --> ad\n    cc -. \"a check fails\" .-> stop([\"nothing deploys\"])\n```\n\nOne `cloudflare.yml` replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`: the jobs a tree did not change are skipped, and every deploy job runs on `!failure() && !cancelled()` with its own tree changed or an upstream deploy run, so a pipeline-only push deploys the pipeline without waiting for a migration that never ran, and a failed common check stops everything after it. Three separate workflows cannot wait on each other within one push without polling, which is why this is one file; the docs say three workflows and would change to one workflow with a job group per tree.\n\n```\n.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml         new\n.github/workflows/api.yml                deleted\n.github/workflows/pipeline.yml           deleted\n.github/workflows/tts.yml                unchanged\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9 Standards\n\n```\n- CLAUDE.md, \"Code style\": common/ holds the shared types; payloads crossing a boundary are typed; pydantic models for tts/'s endpoints\n- CLAUDE.md, \"Invariants\" 2, 3: store's length guard; 4: the key guard ahead of every /items route; 5: Modal over HTTP, retry from the failed step, the 15-minute re-queue; 6: R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT and the other vars instead of any environment branch; 7: migrations in common/ and the tests' schema from them; 8: the CI order\n- CLAUDE.md, \"When adding something\": the spoken-form and drop functions at the end of the recipe step; anything more than one module uses in common/\n- ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md: == null checks, constant maps instead of enums, one function per module by default, named exports, arrow functions, airy blocks\n- .mahou/basics.md and mahou:basics \"Code\": no comments inside object literals, configs or fixtures\n- wiki cloudflare/workflows: step names with counters, restart({from}), the 6-connection limit, idempotent bodies\n- wiki cloudflare/vitest-plugin and .mahou/wiki/testing/cassettes-over-mocks: msw replay, introspection to skip sleeps, unmatched requests fail\n- wiki cloudflare/r2 and cloudflare/local-dev: presigning with aws4fetch, the local S3 endpoint and the tunnel proxy\n- wiki cloudflare/images: rasters through the binding, SVG kept\n- wiki cloudflare/ai-gateway and gemini: the cache header, the gateway URL, text/plain SVG parts\n- wiki firecrawl: the fetch client in place of the SDK\n- wiki modal: proxy-auth headers on web endpoints\n- wiki cloudflare/flue and cloudflare/durable-objects: agents dispatched from a step, the DO's synchronous kv\n- wiki markdown: markdown-it's token tree for the spoken form\n```\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b6b87393-bea4-4731-b9e4-7474e9612d8b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfur9m9bHxu6XGn9qQt8F","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:program-design","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"9322fcf7-e563-4391-9220-a36845344a5e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:53:10.557Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"9322fcf7-e563-4391-9220-a36845344a5e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bfa32ed9-babd-4bb0-92a6-0867b6b276d3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014U1Ejk8czyaC5w3Wd55rSe","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"5d71cbf7-c915-484f-b344-af29feb3b2b3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:53:10.627Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md","content":"# Program design: nagara on Cloudflare\n\nRepository: `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara`, branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`, clean.\n\nCovers how the Cloudflare migration lands in the code: the pnpm workspace, `common/`, the new TypeScript `api/`, the item Workflow and DomainQueue in `pipeline/`, the two web endpoints in `tts/`, local development and CI. Source: the notes under `docs/technical-design/` committed in `c0dbdba`, plus `design.md` and `recording-decisions.md` in this folder. Leaves out the test cases and manual validations (mahou:test-design), and `web/`.\n\nStatus: **proposed**, every part. The user reads the whole proposal on the canvas and points out what does not match.\n\n```\nProgram design\n└─ nagara                                                        proposed\n   ├─ 1 Workspace and packages                                   proposed\n   │  └─ 1.1 Package layout\n   ├─ 2 common/                                                  proposed\n   │  ├─ 2.1 What each module exposes (interfaces)\n   │  └─ 2.2 Module list\n   ├─ 3 api/: the routes                                         proposed\n   │  ├─ 3.1 Callstacks: enqueue, poll with re-queue, retry, media\n   │  ├─ 3.2 Interfaces and module list\n   │  └─ 3.3 Critical behaviour: the re-queue and the restart point\n   ├─ 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow                             proposed\n   │  ├─ 4.1 Control flow: the nine steps and the wrapper\n   │  ├─ 4.2 Interfaces: the step wrapper, step results, modules\n   │  ├─ 4.3 Critical behaviour: lease, poll loop, describe fan-out\n   │  └─ 4.4 Module list\n   ├─ 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue                                   proposed\n   │  └─ 5.1 Interfaces and module list\n   ├─ 6 tts/: the two web endpoints                              proposed\n   │  └─ 6.1 Interfaces and module list\n   ├─ 7 Local development                                        proposed\n   │  └─ 7.1 Module list and launch\n   ├─ 8 CI                                                       proposed\n   │  └─ 8.1 Control flow and module list\n   └─ 9 Standards                                                proposed\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1 Workspace and packages\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```\nnagara/\n├── package.json                 new   private root, no scripts of its own\n├── pnpm-workspace.yaml          new   packages: common, api, pipeline; carries pipeline's allowBuilds and overrides\n├── pnpm-lock.yaml               new   one lockfile for the three TypeScript packages\n├── common/                      new   @nagara/common, source only: exports .ts, never built\n│   ├── package.json             exports \".\", \"./testing\"\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           the D1 binding and migrations_dir, for `wrangler d1 migrations apply`\n│   ├── migrations/              hand-written SQL, applied by CI, locally, and by both Workers' tests\n│   ├── src/                     types, keys, presigning, item row, sanitize\n│   ├── testing/                 the cassette replay library (vitest only)\n│   └── test/\n├── api/                         replaced: the Python tree goes, a Worker takes its place\n│   ├── package.json             @nagara/api; depends on @nagara/common: workspace:*\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           name nagara-api, route nagara.asermax.com, D1, R2, the item Workflow by script_name\n│   ├── src/\n│   └── test/\n├── pipeline/                    touched\n│   ├── package.json             depends on @nagara/common: workspace:*; own pnpm-lock.yaml and pnpm-workspace.yaml go\n│   ├── wrangler.jsonc           workflow renamed item, JobIndex deleted, D1 and R2 bound, workers_dev false\n│   ├── src/\n│   └── test/                    cassettes/ moves here from api/tests/cassettes\n├── tts/                         touched: two web endpoints, no package change\n└── .github/workflows/           cloudflare.yml replaces api.yml and pipeline.yml; tts.yml unchanged\n```\n\n`common/` is a workspace package because both Workers import it at build time and its migrations are the one thing it deploys. It ships no build step: Vite (pipeline) and wrangler's esbuild (api) compile its `.ts` sources directly, the way `pipeline/` already imports its own `.ts` paths. The `./testing` export keeps the cassette library and its YAML parser out of the Workers' runtime bundles.\n\nOne root workspace and lockfile replace `pipeline/`'s own, so `workspace:*` links resolve without publishing. `pnpm install` from any of the three folders installs the workspace. `tts/` stays outside the workspace, under uv as today.\n\nNew dependencies: `aws4fetch` in `common/` for presigning (the r2-presigned spike signed with it), `markdown-it` in `common/` for the sanitize tail's partner, the spoken-form derivation (wiki `markdown`), `yaml` in `common/` dev for cassette parsing, `msw@2.15` as a dev dependency of both Workers (msw 3's `msw/node` does not start in workerd, workflow-testing spike). `valibot` stays in `pipeline/` and joins `api/` for the enqueue body.\n\n---\n\n## 2 common/\n\n### 2.1 What each module exposes\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/item.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"The item row and its statuses.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"ITEM_STATUS\": { \"enum\": [\"queued\", \"generating\", \"ready\", \"failed\"], \"description\": \"Constant map; ItemStatus derives from it.\" },\n    \"ItemRow\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"itm_ plus 8 hex characters.\" },\n        \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"title\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"voice\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"status\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ITEM_STATUS\" },\n        \"created_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"updated_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"queued_at\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"workflow_instance_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"current_step\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"A STEP name, or a poll step's numbered name.\" },\n        \"extraction_domain\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"recipe_version_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"retry_count\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n        \"duration\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n        \"audio_format\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n        \"units\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/units.ts#/$defs/RowUnit\" } },\n        \"degradations\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/units.ts#/$defs/Degradation\" } },\n        \"error\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/units.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"The unit union the display, spoken form and timing ride on.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"Unit\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphUnit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CodeUnit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ImageUnit\" }] },\n    \"ParagraphUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"paragraph\" }, \"display\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"spoken\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"start\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"end\": { \"type\": \"number\" } }, \"required\": [\"type\", \"display\", \"spoken\"] },\n    \"CodeUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"code\" }, \"display\": {}, \"spoken\": {}, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } },\n    \"ImageUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"image\" }, \"display\": { \"description\": \"![<raw alt>](/items/<id>/images/<hash>): the describe step reads the alt back from here.\" }, \"spoken\": {}, \"image\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The content hash.\" }, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } },\n    \"DeclaredImageUnit\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"const\": \"declared-image\" }, \"src\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"alt\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"description\": \"An image the recipe declared and the images step has not acquired yet; never survives the images step.\" },\n    \"RowUnit\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Unit\" }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DeclaredImageUnit\" }] },\n    \"DEGRADATION_REASON\": { \"enum\": [\"404\", \"timeout\", \"undecodable\", \"describe failed\", \"describe cap reached\"] },\n    \"Degradation\": { \"properties\": { \"type\": { \"enum\": [\"image\", \"code\"] }, \"reason\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DEGRADATION_REASON\" }, \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Origin URL, acquisition failures only.\" } }, \"required\": [\"type\", \"reason\"] }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/workflow.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"What the API and the item Workflow agree on.\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"ItemWorkflowParams\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"itemId\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"required\": [\"itemId\"] },\n    \"STEP\": { \"enum\": [\"fetch\", \"lease\", \"recipe\", \"release\", \"images\", \"describe\", \"start synthesis\", \"poll\", \"store\"], \"description\": \"Constant map of step names. A poll step runs as `poll <n>`.\" },\n    \"restartPoint\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"currentStep\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] } } },\n        \"output\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"The step name restart() starts from: lease for recipe and release, the step itself otherwise, null (restart every step) when empty.\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/row.ts\",\n  \"description\": \"Reads and writes of the item row both Workers make.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"readItem\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"db\": { \"description\": \"D1Database\" }, \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"ItemRow with units and degradations decoded, or null.\" } } },\n    \"writeStatus\": {\n      \"description\": \"One UPDATE: status, current_step, error = null, updated_at = now. Used by the API for queued and by the step wrapper for every status.\",\n      \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"db\": {}, \"id\": {}, \"status\": { \"$ref\": \"common/src/item.ts#/$defs/ITEM_STATUS\" }, \"currentStep\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] }, \"error\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Set only with failed.\" } }, \"required\": [\"db\", \"id\", \"status\"] }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"nothing\" } }\n    },\n    \"encodeJson / decodeJson\": { \"description\": \"The JSON column codec for units and degradations.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/keys.ts and common/src/presign.ts\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"audioKey\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"itemId\": {} } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"audio/<itemId>\" } } },\n    \"imageKey\": { \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"hash\": {} } }, \"output\": { \"description\": \"images/<hash>\" } } },\n    \"presign\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n          \"endpoint\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The S3 endpoint the URL is signed for: R2's in production, the local S3 endpoint locally.\" },\n          \"bucket\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"key\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"method\": { \"enum\": [\"GET\", \"PUT\"] },\n          \"accessKeyId\": {}, \"secretAccessKey\": {},\n          \"expiresIn\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"description\": \"Seconds; 3600 for both callers.\" }\n        } },\n        \"output\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The signed URL.\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/src/ledger.ts, common/src/recipe.ts, common/src/sanitize.ts\",\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"COST_TYPE\": { \"enum\": [\"firecrawl\", \"describer\", \"tts\"] },\n    \"COST_UNIT\": { \"enum\": [\"credits\", \"calls\", \"seconds\"] },\n    \"CostEntryRow\": { \"properties\": { \"id\": {}, \"item_id\": {}, \"type\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/COST_TYPE\" }, \"quantity\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"unit\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/COST_UNIT\" }, \"dollars\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"cached\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }, \"detail\": { \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"] }, \"created_at\": {} } },\n    \"RecipeVersionRow\": { \"properties\": { \"id\": {}, \"domain\": {}, \"version\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }, \"script\": {}, \"created_at\": {} } },\n    \"sanitizeSpoken\": { \"description\": \"The sanitize tail: markers touching text, tags to words, comparison operators to words. Used by the spoken-form derivation and the describer, two pipeline modules.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"common/testing: replayCassettes\",\n  \"description\": \"Our TypeScript copy of vcrpy, replay only, run through msw in both Workers' tests.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"cassette\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The YAML text, imported with ?raw.\" },\n      \"rewrite\": { \"description\": \"Host rewrites, such as generativelanguage.googleapis.com to the gateway's URL.\" }\n    } },\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"msw handlers: match on method, scheme, host, port, query, and path and JSON body with item ids normalized; credential headers stripped before matching; content-encoding, content-length and transfer-encoding stripped from the replayed response; repeated identical requests answer in recorded order; an unmatched request throws.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe D1 test schema comes from `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`'s `readD1Migrations(\"../common/migrations\")` in each Worker's vitest config and `applyD1Migrations` in a setup file, so `common/testing` holds only the cassette library.\n\n`sanitizeSpoken` and the row reads and writes are in `common/` because the project's rule puts there everything more than one module uses: the sanitize tail serves the spoken-form module and the describer module, the row writes serve the API and the pipeline.\n\n### 2.2 Module list\n\n```\ncommon/package.json                      new\ncommon/tsconfig.json                     new\ncommon/biome.json                        new   copied from pipeline/\ncommon/wrangler.jsonc                    new   D1 binding \"DB\", database nagara, migrations_dir migrations\ncommon/migrations/0001_initial.sql       new   items, recipe_versions, cost_entries, with the indexes for recipe lookup\ncommon/src/item.ts                       new\ncommon/src/units.ts                      new\ncommon/src/workflow.ts                   new\ncommon/src/row.ts                        new\ncommon/src/keys.ts                       new\ncommon/src/presign.ts                    new\ncommon/src/ledger.ts                     new\ncommon/src/recipe.ts                     new\ncommon/src/sanitize.ts                   new   ported from api/app/service/extract.py, sanitize_spoken and its helpers\ncommon/src/index.ts                      new   re-exports src/\ncommon/testing/cassettes.ts              new   ported from api/tests/conftest.py's matchers and filters\ncommon/testing/index.ts                  new\ncommon/test/presign.test.ts              new\ncommon/test/sanitize.test.ts             new\ncommon/test/row.test.ts                  new\ncommon/test/cassettes.test.ts            new\n```\n\nThe SQL starts from the D1 schema at migration 0001 because the move starts empty; the Alembic history is not carried over.\n\n---\n\n## 3 api/: the routes\n\n### 3.1 Callstacks\n\n```\nPOST /items\ngiven X-API-Key, {url, voice?}\n│\n└─ index.fetch → guard.requireKey                               401 on a missing or wrong key\n   └─ routes/enqueue\n      ├─ valibot parse {url: string, voice?: string}            400 when malformed\n      ├─ voices.pick(voice)                                     random from the curated pool when absent\n      ├─ items/create.insertQueued(db, {id = itm_ + 8 hex, url, voice, status queued, queued_at = now})\n      ├─ env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({params: {itemId}})           instance id left to Cloudflare\n      │  └─ when create throws: log it, answer 202 anyway       the re-queue on read recovers the item\n      └─ 202 response.toItemResponse(row)\n```\n\n```\nGET /items/{id}\ngiven X-API-Key, id\n│\n└─ routes/poll\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null\n   ├─ when status queued and queued_at older than 15 min\n   │  └─ items/requeue.requeue(env, row)\n   │     ├─ claim: UPDATE items SET queued_at = now, updated_at = now\n   │     │         WHERE id = ? AND status = 'queued' AND queued_at < now - 15 min\n   │     ├─ when no row changed: another poll claimed it, nothing more\n   │     ├─ when workflow_instance_id is null\n   │     │  └─ env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({params: {itemId}})\n   │     └─ otherwise\n   │        └─ (await env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.get(instance id)).restart(from restartPoint(current_step))\n   └─ 200 response.toItemResponse(row)\n```\n\n```\nPOST /items/{id}/retry\ngiven X-API-Key, id\n│\n└─ routes/retry\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null\n   ├─ items/retry-claim.claim(db, id, retryMax)\n   │  └─ UPDATE items SET status = 'queued', error = null, queued_at = now, updated_at = now,\n   │     retry_count = retry_count + 1\n   │     WHERE id = ? AND status = 'failed' AND retry_count < ?  409 when no row changed; the pre-read picks the message\n   ├─ (await env.ITEM_WORKFLOW.get(workflow_instance_id)).restart(from restartPoint(current_step))\n   │  └─ when the row holds no instance id: create({params: {itemId}})\n   └─ 202 response.toItemResponse(claimed row)\n```\n\n```\nGET /items/{id}/audio · GET /items/{id}/images/{hash}\ngiven X-API-Key, id[, hash]\n│\n└─ routes/audio | routes/images\n   ├─ common.readItem(db, id)                                   404 when null; audio also 404 unless ready with audio_format\n   ├─ common.presign({endpoint: R2_S3_ENDPOINT, bucket, key: audioKey(id) | imageKey(hash),\n   │                  method GET, R2 GET token, expiresIn 3600})\n   └─ 307 to the signed URL\n\nGET /health → 200 \"ok\", before the guard\n```\n\n### 3.2 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"api/ wrangler bindings and configuration\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"DB\": { \"description\": \"D1 nagara, shared with the pipeline.\" },\n    \"ITEM_WORKFLOW\": { \"description\": \"workflows: {binding ITEM_WORKFLOW, name item, class_name ItemWorkflow, script_name nagara}.\" },\n    \"vars\": { \"properties\": { \"R2_S3_ENDPOINT\": {}, \"R2_BUCKET\": {}, \"RETRY_MAX\": { \"const\": 3 }, \"REQUEUE_AFTER_MS\": { \"const\": 900000 } } },\n    \"secrets\": { \"properties\": { \"API_KEY\": {}, \"R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID\": {}, \"R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\": {} } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"api/src/response.ts: toItemResponse\",\n  \"description\": \"The wire projection, unchanged for clients: drops spoken, adds index, holds units back until ready.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"description\": \"ItemRow\" },\n    \"output\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"id\": {}, \"url\": {}, \"title\": {}, \"status\": {}, \"voice\": {}, \"created_at\": {},\n      \"duration\": { \"description\": \"Absent until ready.\" },\n      \"units\": { \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"], \"items\": { \"properties\": { \"index\": {}, \"type\": {}, \"display\": {}, \"start\": {}, \"end\": {}, \"image\": {} } }, \"description\": \"null unless ready.\" },\n      \"error\": {},\n      \"audio_url\": { \"description\": \"/items/<id>/audio, only when ready.\" }\n    } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```\napi/                                     the Python tree goes: app/, migrations/, tests/, data/, prototype_cache/,\n                                         alembic.ini, pyproject.toml, uv.lock, railway.toml        deleted\napi/tests/cassettes/                     moved to pipeline/test/cassettes/\napi/package.json                         new\napi/tsconfig.json                        new\napi/biome.json                           new\napi/wrangler.jsonc                       new\napi/vitest.config.ts                     new   readD1Migrations(\"../common/migrations\")\napi/src/index.ts                         new   fetch handler: /health, the key guard, the route table (plain matching, as pipeline/src/http/routes.ts does)\napi/src/guard.ts                         new\napi/src/voices.ts                        new   the curated pool, ported from api/app/service/tts.py pick_voice\napi/src/response.ts                      new\napi/src/routes/enqueue.ts                new\napi/src/routes/poll.ts                   new\napi/src/routes/retry.ts                  new\napi/src/routes/audio.ts                  new\napi/src/routes/images.ts                 new\napi/src/items/create.ts                  new   insertQueued and the id mint\napi/src/items/requeue.ts                 new\napi/src/items/retry-claim.ts             new\napi/test/setup.ts                        new   applies the migrations\napi/test/helpers/workflow-stand-in.ts    new   the stand-in for ITEM_WORKFLOW: records create, get and restart calls\napi/test/*.test.ts                       new   one file per route, cases from test-design\n```\n\n### 3.3 Critical behaviour\n\nThe re-queue claims the row with one conditional UPDATE before it touches the instance, the same pattern as the retry claim, so two polls landing together restart the instance once. It does not increment `retry_count`: the cap bounds client retries of failed items, and a re-queue recovers an item that never failed. It restarts from `restartPoint(current_step)`, so an item waiting for its domain's lease (current_step `lease`) asks for the lease again, and DomainQueue keeps an id that is already in its FIFO at its position (5.1); a re-queue never sends a waiting item to the back.\n\nThe retry route reaches the same `restartPoint`. `recipe` and `release` map to `lease`; `poll <n>` restarts at that poll step, so the poll steps before it replay from cache and Modal is not asked to synthesize again; an empty `current_step` restarts every step.\n\nNeither route reads the instance's status: the row is the only state the API reads, as the design says.\n\n---\n\n## 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow\n\n### 4.1 Control flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"ItemWorkflow.run<br/>params {itemId}\"]) --> s1[\"1 fetch · queued<br/>writes instance id,<br/>domain, ledger row<br/>returns {html}\"]\n    s1 --> s2[\"2 lease · queued<br/>ask DomainQueue,<br/>waitForEvent lease-granted\"]\n    s2 --> s3[\"3 recipe · generating<br/>run, author or revise;<br/>spoken form and drop;<br/>writes title, units\"]\n    s3 --> s4[\"4 release · generating<br/>give the lease back\"]\n    s4 --> s5[\"5 images · generating<br/>acquire declared images;<br/>writes units, degradations\"]\n    s5 --> s6[\"6 describe · generating<br/>child steps, allSettled;<br/>one write at the end\"]\n    s6 --> s7[\"7 start synthesis<br/>· generating<br/>sign PUT, call Modal<br/>returns {callId}\"]\n    s7 --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"8 poll · generating\"]\n        direction TB\n        p[\"poll n: fetch result\"] --> r{\"ready?\"}\n        r -->|\"no: sleep 10 s,<br/>n + 1\"| p\n    end\n    r -->|\"yes, returns the result\"| s9[\"9 store · generating<br/>join timings; writes<br/>ready, units, duration,<br/>format, tts ledger row\"]\n    s9 --> done([\"ready\"])\n    s1 -. \"last attempt fails\" .-> fail([\"wrapper writes failed,<br/>the step's error;<br/>run() rethrows\"])\n    s2 -. \"3 waits of 1 h\" .-> fail\n    s3 -. \"not an article: at once\" .-> fail\n    s5 -.-> fail\n    s7 -.-> fail\n    loop -. \"failed or expired\" .-> fail\n    s9 -. \"length mismatch\" .-> fail\n```\n\nEvery box is one call to the wrapper (4.2), which runs the body inside `step.do` with the step's retries and timeout. The order is required throughout: the lease comes before recipe and goes right after it; images come before describe because describe reads the acquired images from R2; describe comes before start synthesis because synthesis reads the described spoken forms from the row.\n\nA failed step ends the run: the wrapper writes `failed` with the step's own error and rethrows, so the instance ends `errored`, which DomainQueue's alarm reads when the failed step held the lease. describe never fails because a child failed (4.3). The Workflow returns nothing.\n\n### 4.2 Interfaces\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts: runStep\",\n  \"description\": \"The logic every step shares.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": {\n      \"ctx\": { \"properties\": { \"step\": { \"description\": \"WorkflowStep\" }, \"db\": {}, \"itemId\": {} } },\n      \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The step name: a STEP value, or poll <n>.\" },\n      \"status\": { \"enum\": [\"queued\", \"generating\"], \"description\": \"queued for fetch and lease, generating after.\" },\n      \"config\": { \"properties\": { \"retries\": { \"const\": 3, \"description\": \"limit 3, 5 s exponential delay\" }, \"timeout\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n      \"body\": { \"description\": \"The step's work; returns its step result or nothing.\" }\n    } },\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"The body's step result.\" }\n  },\n  \"$comment\": \"Inside step.do, first thing in every attempt: writeStatus(status, current_step = name), which also clears error. When step.do throws (its last attempt failed, or a NonRetryableError): step.do('<name> failed') writes failed with error.message, then rethrows. An attempt that fails with attempts left writes nothing.\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Step results\",\n  \"description\": \"Only what the Workflow needs and the row does not hold.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"fetch\": { \"properties\": { \"html\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n    \"start synthesis\": { \"properties\": { \"callId\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n    \"poll <n>\": { \"oneOf\": [{ \"properties\": { \"ready\": { \"const\": false } } }, { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SynthesisResult\" }], \"description\": \"{ready: false}, never null: a falsy mocked step result is ignored by the test engine.\" }\n  },\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"SynthesisResult\": { \"properties\": { \"ready\": { \"const\": true }, \"format\": { \"enum\": [\"audio/ogg\", \"audio/wav\"] }, \"duration\": { \"type\": \"number\" }, \"timings\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"properties\": { \"start\": {}, \"end\": {} } } } } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/ domain modules: what each step calls\",\n  \"description\": \"Each module returns values; only the step files write to D1 and R2.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"firecrawl.scrape(url)\": { \"description\": \"→ {html, finalUrl, creditsUsed, proxy}. Our fetch client, the Python SDK's fields; rawHtml + markdown at proxy auto. Throws on no HTML; the step throws NonRetryableError over maxHtmlBytes.\" },\n    \"recipes.currentRecipe(db, domain) / recipes.saveVersion(db, domain, script)\": { \"description\": \"→ RecipeVersionRow | null; the insert as the next version.\" },\n    \"recipes.settle(env, {instanceId, domain, html, recipe?})\": { \"description\": \"→ {kind: 'ok', title, units, script, isNew} | {kind: 'not-article'} | {kind: 'gave-up', reason}. Runs the recipe; on failure dispatches the revision agent, or the author when there is no recipe; conversation id = instance id; authoring 1 retry, revision 2, every settled script re-run through the runtime.\" },\n    \"spoken.toTypedUnits(recipeUnits, title)\": { \"description\": \"→ RowUnit[]: spoken form derived, empty-of-letters units dropped, declared images anchored after the last kept text unit.\" },\n    \"images.acquire(env, units, itemId)\": { \"description\": \"→ {units, degradations}: download under per-host 2 / global 10 semaphores, 10 s, 10 MB; sniff <svg; SVG scripts stripped with HTMLRewriter; rasters through env.IMAGES, kept when min side ≥ 200, re-encoded to WebP; sha256 of the stored bytes; R2 put under imageKey with its content type; spoken Image: <alt> or the floor.\" },\n    \"describe.jobs(units, title)\": { \"description\": \"→ the document-ordered jobs: every code unit, every image whose alt (read from display) fails the good-alt filter; the cap of 25 splits them into described and capped.\" },\n    \"describe.describeOne(env, job, image?)\": { \"description\": \"→ {spoken, cached}: one Gemini call through AI Gateway, structured output {spoken}, sanitized; cached from cf-aig-cache-status.\" },\n    \"tts.start(env, {paragraphs, voice, destination}) / tts.result(env, callId)\": { \"description\": \"→ callId; → {ready: false} | SynthesisResult. Proxy-auth headers Modal-Key and Modal-Secret. 500 and 410 throw.\" },\n    \"ledger.record(db, entry)\": { \"description\": \"Inserts one CostEntryRow at the configured price.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"pipeline/ wrangler bindings and configuration\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"workflows\": { \"description\": \"{binding ITEM_WORKFLOW, name item, class_name ItemWorkflow}.\" },\n    \"DB / BUCKET / IMAGES / LOADER / DOMAIN_QUEUE\": { \"description\": \"D1 nagara, R2 nagara, the Images binding, the Worker Loader, the DomainQueue DO.\" },\n    \"vars\": { \"properties\": { \"R2_S3_ENDPOINT\": { \"description\": \"The endpoint PUT URLs are signed for.\" }, \"R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\": { \"description\": \"What Modal is handed in its place; equal to R2_S3_ENDPOINT in production, the tunnel's https://<host>/s3 locally.\" }, \"R2_BUCKET\": {}, \"MODAL_START_URL\": {}, \"MODAL_RESULT_URL\": {}, \"describeMaxPerItem\": { \"const\": 25 }, \"imageFetchPerHost\": { \"const\": 2 }, \"imageFetchConcurrency\": { \"const\": 10 }, \"pollIntervalSeconds\": { \"const\": 10 }, \"prices\": { \"description\": \"firecrawl per credit, describer per call, tts per second\" }, \"existing\": { \"description\": \"agentModel, agentMaxTurns, authoringRetries, revisionRetries, leaseAlarmMs, recipeCpuMs, maxHtmlBytes, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, CLOUDFLARE_GATEWAY_ID\" } } },\n    \"secrets\": { \"properties\": { \"FIRECRAWL_API_KEY\": {}, \"GEMINI_API_KEY\": {}, \"CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY\": { \"description\": \"The AI Gateway token, the name the agents already read.\" }, \"MODAL_PROXY_KEY\": {}, \"MODAL_PROXY_SECRET\": {}, \"R2_PUT_ACCESS_KEY_ID\": {}, \"R2_PUT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\": {} } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 4.3 Critical behaviour\n\n**The lease.** The `lease` step asks `DomainQueue.acquire(instanceId)` and returns `{granted}`. When not granted, the Workflow waits with `step.waitForEvent(\"lease wait <n>\", {type: \"lease-granted\", timeout: \"1 hour\"})`, up to 3 waits; after a wait times out, a `lease recheck <n>` step asks again, since a grant can be lost to a deploy. An event sent before the wait begins is kept (item-workflow spike). After the third timeout the wrapper's failure path writes `failed`. The waits sit between wrapper calls and write nothing, so `current_step` stays `lease` throughout.\n\n**The poll loop.** Step `poll <n>` asks Modal for the result; when it is not ready, `step.sleep(\"poll sleep <n>\", pollIntervalSeconds)` and `n + 1`. Each name carries its counter, because a repeated name replays the cached result. Each poll step has 3 attempts of 1 min; Modal's 500 (the synthesis crashed) and 410 (the result expired after 7 days) throw, so a crashed synthesis uses the poll step's attempts and fails the item. At 10 s, the 10,000-step limit covers about 27 h of synthesis; a 70-minute article took 176 s.\n\n**The describe fan-out.** The wrapper's body for `describe` reads the units and title from the row, builds the jobs, and starts `step.do(\"describe <unit index>\", {retries 3, timeout 1 min}, …)` for each job within the cap, awaited with `Promise.allSettled`. An image job reads its stored object from R2 inside its child step. Then, still inside the parent's body, it applies every fulfilled result (`Code: …` or `Image: …`), floors every rejected or capped job (code to `Code with no description.`, image keeps its fallback), and makes one D1 batch: the units, the degradations, and one describer ledger row per fulfilled child.\n\n**The spoken form and the title** are set at the end of the recipe step: `spoken.toTypedUnits` runs on the settled units, a new script is saved as the next version first, and one UPDATE writes `title`, `units`, `recipe_version_id`. No surviving unit throws NonRetryableError (`no surviving units`).\n\n**Store** joins `timings[i]` onto the i-th unit; a length mismatch throws NonRetryableError (invariant 2). One D1 batch writes the timed units, `duration`, `audio_format`, the tts ledger row, and `status = ready`, `current_step = null`, so the item turns ready in the same write that makes it readable.\n\n### 4.4 Module list\n\n```\npipeline/package.json                         touched   @nagara/common workspace:*, markdown-it via common, msw dev; build:bundle unchanged\npipeline/pnpm-lock.yaml                       deleted   the root lockfile replaces it\npipeline/pnpm-workspace.yaml                  deleted   its allowBuilds and overrides move to the root\npipeline/wrangler.jsonc                       touched   workflow item/ItemWorkflow, D1, R2, IMAGES, JobIndex removed (a deleted_classes migration), new vars, workers_dev false\npipeline/vitest.config.ts                     touched   readD1Migrations, R2 and D1 bindings for tests\npipeline/src/cloudflare.ts                    touched   exports ItemWorkflow and DomainQueue\npipeline/src/app.ts                           touched   the default export answers 404 to every request\npipeline/src/http/                            deleted   routes.ts, read.ts, job-status.ts: no public routes\npipeline/src/queue/job-index.ts               deleted\npipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts            touched   see 5.1\npipeline/src/workflow/extraction.ts           deleted   its settle loop moves to recipes/settle.ts\npipeline/src/workflow/world.ts                deleted   the tests replay HTTP with msw instead of the seam\npipeline/src/workflow/item.ts                 new       ItemWorkflow.run: the nine wrapper calls in order\npipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts              new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/fetch.ts          new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/lease.ts          new       the ask, the waits, the rechecks\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/recipe.ts         new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/release.ts        new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/images.ts         new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/describe.ts       new\npipeline/src/workflow/steps/synthesis.ts      new       start synthesis, the poll loop, store\npipeline/src/workflow/ledger.ts               new       only the steps write ledger rows\npipeline/src/firecrawl/client.ts              new       ported from api/app/service/fetch.py\npipeline/src/recipes/store.ts                 new       ported from api/app/service/recipes.py\npipeline/src/recipes/settle.ts                new       from workflow/extraction.ts, conversation id without suffix\npipeline/src/runtime/                         unchanged\npipeline/src/agents/                          unchanged\npipeline/src/spoken/derive.ts                 new       ported from extract.py: to_spoken, the token walk, tables\npipeline/src/spoken/typed-units.ts            new       drop rule, image anchoring\npipeline/src/images/acquire.ts                new       ported from api/app/service/images.py\npipeline/src/images/svg.ts                    new       sniff and script stripping\npipeline/src/images/alt.ts                    new       spoken form from alt, good-alt filter, cruft test\npipeline/src/describe/core.ts                 new       ported from api/app/service/describe.py\npipeline/src/describe/prompts.ts              new\npipeline/src/describe/jobs.ts                 new\npipeline/src/tts/modal.ts                     new       ported from api/app/service/tts.py, over HTTP\npipeline/test/cassettes/                      new       moved from api/tests/cassettes\npipeline/test/helpers/world.ts                deleted\npipeline/test/helpers/http.ts                 deleted\npipeline/test/extraction-workflow.test.ts     deleted   replaced by item-workflow tests\npipeline/test/http.test.ts, read-path.test.ts, job-index.test.ts   deleted\npipeline/test/*.test.ts                       new       cases from test-design\n```\n\n`images/alt.ts` holds the good-alt filter, which the describe module also needs. Both reach it: the images step speaks the alt and the describe step decides from it. By the project rule that puts it in `common/`; it stays in `pipeline/` here because only pipeline modules use it, and moving pipeline-only code into the package both Workers build is the opposite of the rule's purpose. This is the one placement that departs from a literal reading of CLAUDE.md, flagged for the user.\n\n---\n\n## 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue\n\n### 5.1 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"DomainQueue\",\n  \"$comment\": \"exists; one instance per domain via idFromName(domain)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"acquire\": { \"$comment\": \"added, replaces enqueue\", \"properties\": {\n      \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"instanceId\": {} } },\n      \"output\": { \"properties\": { \"granted\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" } }, \"description\": \"true when the id holds the lease, or the lease is free and the FIFO is empty; otherwise the id is appended once, keeping its place if already waiting.\" } } },\n    \"release\": { \"$comment\": \"changed: keyed on instance id; drops the id from the FIFO too\", \"properties\": { \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"instanceId\": {} } } } },\n    \"advance\": { \"$comment\": \"changed: no create; shifts the next id, checks status(), writes the lease, sendEvent({type: 'lease-granted'}); a terminal or throwing id is skipped\" },\n    \"alarm\": { \"$comment\": \"unchanged: 60 s, sweeps an ended or unaddressable holder\" },\n    \"enqueue, stateOf\": { \"$comment\": \"removed\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe FIFO holds instance ids only, since the Workflow carries its own HTML as a step result; the per-key params storage and the job index go. State moves to the synchronous `ctx.storage.kv` as in the item-workflow spike, so `acquire` has no `await` and nothing interleaves.\n\n```\npipeline/src/queue/domain-queue.ts       touched\npipeline/test/domain-queue.test.ts       touched\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6 tts/: the two web endpoints\n\n### 6.1 Interfaces and module list\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"tts/app.py: start (POST, requires_proxy_auth)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": { \"properties\": { \"paragraphs\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }, \"voice\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"af_heart\" }, \"destination\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Presigned PUT URL.\" } }, \"required\": [\"paragraphs\", \"destination\"] },\n    \"output\": { \"properties\": { \"call_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"tts/app.py: result (GET ?call_id=, requires_proxy_auth)\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"output\": { \"description\": \"202 {status: running} while it runs; 200 {format, duration, timings[{start, end}]} when done; 500 {error} when the synthesis raised; 410 when Modal no longer holds the result.\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`Kokoro.synthesize` gains `destination`, PUTs the encoded audio there with its content type through httpx, and returns the result without `audio_base64`. Both endpoints live on a small CPU `web` function in the same app that spawns `Kokoro().synthesize` and reads `FunctionCall.from_id(call_id).get(timeout=0)`. Request and response shapes are pydantic models, per CLAUDE.md.\n\n```\ntts/app.py                               touched   the endpoints, destination upload, pydantic models\ntts/pyproject.toml                       touched   fastapi[standard] and httpx for the endpoints\ntts/tests/test_endpoints.py              new\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7 Local development\n\n### 7.1 Module list and launch\n\n```\n.wrangler-state/                         git-ignored: the shared state folder at the repository root\n.gitignore                               touched\napi/wrangler.jsonc                       dev: port 8787\napi/package.json                         dev = wrangler dev --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\npipeline/vite.config.ts                  touched   cloudflare({persistState: {path: \"../.wrangler-state\"}, ...}); experimental local S3 credentials\npipeline/.dev.vars.example               new       secrets plus R2_S3_ENDPOINT = http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3 and R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT = https://<tunnel>/s3\npipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs        new       Node proxy: /s3/<bucket>/<key> to localhost /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/<bucket>/<key>, host rewritten\npipeline/package.json                    touched   dev:proxy = node scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs\ncommon/package.json                      migrate:local = wrangler d1 migrations apply nagara --local --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\n```\n\nLaunch: `pnpm --filter @nagara/common migrate:local`, then `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`, `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`, `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:<proxy port>` by hand, the tunnel host into `.dev.vars`, and `pnpm dev` in `api/`. `cloudflared` is a tool on the developer's machine, not a dependency.\n\n---\n\n## 8 CI\n\n### 8.1 Control flow and module list\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    push([\"push to main\"]) --> ch[\"changes:<br/>paths-filter for<br/>common, pipeline, api\"]\n    ch --> cc[\"common checks:<br/>test, lint, types,<br/>api and pipeline types\"]\n    ch --> pc[\"pipeline checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    ch --> ac[\"api checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    cc --> mig[\"migrate: wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply --remote\"]\n    mig --> pd[\"deploy pipeline:<br/>pnpm build,<br/>deploy dist config\"]\n    pc --> pd\n    pd --> ad[\"deploy api\"]\n    ac --> ad\n    cc -. \"a check fails\" .-> stop([\"nothing deploys\"])\n```\n\nOne `cloudflare.yml` replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`: the jobs a tree did not change are skipped, and every deploy job runs on `!failure() && !cancelled()` with its own tree changed or an upstream deploy run, so a pipeline-only push deploys the pipeline without waiting for a migration that never ran, and a failed common check stops everything after it. Three separate workflows cannot wait on each other within one push without polling, which is why this is one file; the docs say three workflows and would change to one workflow with a job group per tree.\n\n```\n.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml         new\n.github/workflows/api.yml                deleted\n.github/workflows/pipeline.yml           deleted\n.github/workflows/tts.yml                unchanged\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9 Standards\n\n```\n- CLAUDE.md, \"Code style\": common/ holds the shared types; payloads crossing a boundary are typed; pydantic models for tts/'s endpoints\n- CLAUDE.md, \"Invariants\" 2, 3: store's length guard; 4: the key guard ahead of every /items route; 5: Modal over HTTP, retry from the failed step, the 15-minute re-queue; 6: R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT and the other vars instead of any environment branch; 7: migrations in common/ and the tests' schema from them; 8: the CI order\n- CLAUDE.md, \"When adding something\": the spoken-form and drop functions at the end of the recipe step; anything more than one module uses in common/\n- ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md: == null checks, constant maps instead of enums, one function per module by default, named exports, arrow functions, airy blocks\n- .mahou/basics.md and mahou:basics \"Code\": no comments inside object literals, configs or fixtures\n- wiki cloudflare/workflows: step names with counters, restart({from}), the 6-connection limit, idempotent bodies\n- wiki cloudflare/vitest-plugin and .mahou/wiki/testing/cassettes-over-mocks: msw replay, introspection to skip sleeps, unmatched requests fail\n- wiki cloudflare/r2 and cloudflare/local-dev: presigning with aws4fetch, the local S3 endpoint and the tunnel proxy\n- wiki cloudflare/images: rasters through the binding, SVG kept\n- wiki cloudflare/ai-gateway and gemini: the cache header, the gateway URL, text/plain SVG parts\n- wiki firecrawl: the fetch client in place of the SDK\n- wiki modal: proxy-auth headers on web endpoints\n- wiki cloudflare/flue and cloudflare/durable-objects: agents dispatched from a step, the DO's synchronous kv\n- wiki markdown: markdown-it's token tree for the spoken form\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9322fcf7-e563-4391-9220-a36845344a5e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
