{"parentUuid":"09b56729-522a-4063-957f-cb07d6fc2da5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfurhBY9TFZJJ46FnR4gy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015uVQsBRfDwvx76pHuEYRrx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/canvas.md","content":"# Program design canvas: visual parts\n\nThe canvas draws these diagrams; `nagara.md` keeps the text representations.\n\n## 1 Workspace and packages\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  ws@{ shape: doc, label: \"pnpm workspace:<br/>root package.json,<br/>one lockfile\" }\n  subgraph cf [\"Built by pnpm, deployed by wrangler\"]\n    direction LR\n    api@{ shape: rect, label: \"api/<br/>@nagara/api<br/>Worker nagara-api\" }\n    common@{ shape: rect, label: \"common/<br/>@nagara/common<br/>source only, no build\" }\n    pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline/<br/>Worker nagara<br/>built by Vite + Flue\" }\n  end\n  tts@{ shape: rect, label: \"tts/<br/>uv, outside<br/>the workspace\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" }\n  ws --- api\n  ws --- common\n  ws --- pipe\n  api -->|\"workspace:*<br/>types, keys, presign, row\"| common\n  pipe -->|\"workspace:*<br/>types, keys, presign,<br/>row, sanitize\"| common\n  common -->|\"migrations/\"| d1\n  tts -->|\"modal deploy\"| modal\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class common shared\n  class d1 store\n  class modal ext\n  class ws,tts tool\n```\n\nThe Python api/ goes and a TypeScript Worker takes its place. common/ is compiled into each Worker; only its migrations deploy. New dependencies: aws4fetch (common), markdown-it (pipeline), msw 2.15 (tests of both Workers), valibot joins api/.\n\n## 2 common/\n\n### 2.1 What it holds\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n  direction LR\n  class ItemRow {\n    id, url, title, voice\n    status: ItemStatus\n    created_at, updated_at, queued_at\n    workflow_instance_id?\n    current_step?\n    extraction_domain?, recipe_version_id?\n    retry_count\n    duration?, audio_format?\n    units: RowUnit[]\n    degradations: Degradation[]\n    error?\n  }\n  class RowUnit {\n    <<union>>\n  }\n  class Unit {\n    <<union: paragraph, code, image>>\n    type, display, spoken\n    image hash: image only\n    start?, end?: set by store\n  }\n  class DeclaredImageUnit {\n    <<until the images step>>\n    type declared-image\n    src, alt\n  }\n  class Degradation {\n    type: image or code\n    reason\n    url?\n  }\n  class CostEntryRow {\n    item_id, type, quantity, unit\n    dollars, cached, detail?\n  }\n  class RecipeVersionRow {\n    id, domain, version, script\n  }\n  class ItemWorkflowParams {\n    itemId\n  }\n  ItemRow --> RowUnit\n  RowUnit <|-- Unit\n  RowUnit <|-- DeclaredImageUnit\n  ItemRow --> Degradation\n  ItemRow ..> RecipeVersionRow : recipe_version_id\n  CostEntryRow ..> ItemRow : item_id\n```\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph common [\"common/src\"]\n    direction TB\n    row@{ shape: rect, label: \"row.ts<br/>readItem, writeStatus,<br/>JSON codec\" }\n    wf@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow.ts<br/>STEP names,<br/>restartPoint\" }\n    keys@{ shape: rect, label: \"keys.ts<br/>audioKey, imageKey\" }\n    sign@{ shape: rect, label: \"presign.ts<br/>GET or PUT URL\" }\n    san@{ shape: rect, label: \"sanitize.ts<br/>the sanitize tail\" }\n  end\n  subgraph testing [\"common/testing\"]\n    vcr@{ shape: rect, label: \"replayCassettes<br/>to msw handlers\" }\n  end\n  mig@{ shape: cyl, label: \"common/migrations<br/>0001_initial.sql\" }\n  api@{ shape: rect, label: \"API Worker\" }\n  pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline Worker\" }\n  tests@{ shape: rect, label: \"both Workers' tests\" }\n  api --> row\n  api --> wf\n  api --> keys\n  api -->|\"GET\"| sign\n  pipe --> row\n  pipe --> wf\n  pipe --> keys\n  pipe -->|\"PUT\"| sign\n  pipe --> san\n  tests --> vcr\n  tests -->|\"readD1Migrations\"| mig\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class row,wf,keys,sign,san,vcr shared\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class mig store\n  class tests tool\n```\n\nwriteStatus sets status, current_step and updated_at and clears error in one UPDATE; restartPoint maps recipe and release to lease, keeps any other step, and returns null (restart every step) when current_step is empty. Statuses, cost types and units are constant maps.\n\n## 3 api/: the routes\n\n### 3.1 Enqueue and poll\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  e([\"POST /items<br/>{url, voice?}\"]) --> g{\"key valid?\"}\n  g -->|no| e401([\"401\"])\n  g -->|yes| v{\"body valid?\"}\n  v -->|no| e400([\"400\"])\n  v -->|yes| ins[\"insert row: queued,<br/>queued_at now,<br/>voice picked if absent\"]\n  ins --> cr[\"ITEM_WORKFLOW.create<br/>{itemId}\"]\n  cr --> ok([\"202 item\"])\n  cr -. \"throws: log it\" .-> ok\n  p([\"GET /items/{id}\"]) --> r{\"row exists?\"}\n  r -->|no| n404([\"404\"])\n  r -->|yes| q{\"queued and<br/>queued_at > 15 min?\"}\n  q -->|no| pok([\"200 item\"])\n  q -->|yes| claim{\"claim: UPDATE<br/>queued_at WHERE still<br/>queued and stale\"}\n  claim -->|\"0 rows: another<br/>poll got it\"| pok\n  claim -->|\"1 row\"| has{\"instance id<br/>on the row?\"}\n  has -->|no| c2[\"create {itemId}\"]\n  has -->|yes| rs[\"restart from<br/>restartPoint(current_step)\"]\n  c2 --> pok\n  rs --> pok\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  classDef done fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class ins,cr,c2,rs worker\n  class e401,e400,n404 broken\n  class ok,pok done\n```\n\n### 3.2 Retry and media\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  t([\"POST /items/{id}/retry\"]) --> r{\"row exists?\"}\n  r -->|no| n404([\"404\"])\n  r -->|yes| claim{\"claim: UPDATE to queued,<br/>retry_count + 1, error null<br/>WHERE failed and<br/>retry_count < 3\"}\n  claim -->|\"0 rows\"| c409([\"409\"])\n  claim -->|\"1 row\"| rs[\"restart from<br/>restartPoint(current_step)\"]\n  rs --> ok([\"202 item\"])\n  m([\"GET audio · GET images/{hash}\"]) --> mr{\"row exists?<br/>audio: ready with<br/>audio_format?\"}\n  mr -->|no| m404([\"404\"])\n  mr -->|yes| sign[\"presign GET for<br/>audioKey or imageKey,<br/>1 h, API's R2 token\"]\n  sign --> redirect([\"307\"])\n  h([\"GET /health\"]) --> hok([\"200, no key\"])\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  classDef done fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class rs,sign worker\n  class n404,c409,m404 broken\n  class ok,redirect,hok done\n```\n\nThe re-queue does not count toward the 3 retries. The API never reads the instance's status; the row is all it reads.\n\n### 3.3 Modules\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  idx@{ shape: rect, label: \"index.ts<br/>route table\" }\n  guard@{ shape: rect, label: \"guard.ts<br/>X-API-Key\" }\n  subgraph routes [\"routes/\"]\n    direction TB\n    en@{ shape: rect, label: \"enqueue\" }\n    po@{ shape: rect, label: \"poll\" }\n    re@{ shape: rect, label: \"retry\" }\n    au@{ shape: rect, label: \"audio, images\" }\n  end\n  subgraph items [\"items/\"]\n    direction TB\n    cr@{ shape: rect, label: \"create.ts<br/>insertQueued, id mint\" }\n    rq@{ shape: rect, label: \"requeue.ts\" }\n    rc@{ shape: rect, label: \"retry-claim.ts\" }\n  end\n  resp@{ shape: rect, label: \"response.ts<br/>toItemResponse\" }\n  voices@{ shape: rect, label: \"voices.ts\" }\n  common@{ shape: rect, label: \"common/\" }\n  wf@{ shape: cloud, label: \"ITEM_WORKFLOW<br/>script_name nagara\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  idx --> guard --> routes\n  en --> cr\n  en --> voices\n  po --> rq\n  re --> rc\n  routes --> resp\n  routes --> common\n  cr --> d1\n  rq --> d1\n  rc --> d1\n  en --> wf\n  rq --> wf\n  re --> wf\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  class idx,guard,en,po,re,au,cr,rq,rc,resp,voices worker\n  class common shared\n  class d1 store\n  class wf ext\n```\n\ntoItemResponse keeps today's wire shape: units are null until ready, spoken is dropped, audio_url appears only when ready. Secrets: API_KEY and the GET R2 token.\n\n## 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow\n\n### 4.1 The nine steps\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"ItemWorkflow.run<br/>params {itemId}\"]) --> s1[\"1 fetch · queued<br/>writes instance id,<br/>domain, ledger row<br/>returns {html}\"]\n    s1 --> s2[\"2 lease · queued<br/>ask DomainQueue,<br/>waitForEvent lease-granted\"]\n    s2 --> s3[\"3 recipe · generating<br/>run, author or revise;<br/>spoken form and drop;<br/>writes title, units\"]\n    s3 --> s4[\"4 release · generating<br/>give the lease back\"]\n    s4 --> s5[\"5 images · generating<br/>acquire declared images;<br/>writes units, degradations\"]\n    s5 --> s6[\"6 describe · generating<br/>child steps, allSettled;<br/>one write at the end\"]\n    s6 --> s7[\"7 start synthesis<br/>· generating<br/>sign PUT, call Modal<br/>returns {callId}\"]\n    s7 --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"8 poll · generating\"]\n        direction TB\n        p[\"poll n: fetch result\"] --> r{\"ready?\"}\n        r -->|\"no: sleep 10 s,<br/>n + 1\"| p\n    end\n    r -->|\"yes, returns the result\"| s9[\"9 store · generating<br/>join timings; writes<br/>ready, units, duration,<br/>format, tts ledger row\"]\n    s9 --> done([\"ready\"])\n    s1 -. \"last attempt fails\" .-> fail([\"wrapper writes failed,<br/>the step's error;<br/>run() rethrows\"])\n    s2 -. \"3 waits of 1 h\" .-> fail\n    s3 -. \"not an article: at once\" .-> fail\n    s5 -.-> fail\n    s7 -.-> fail\n    loop -. \"failed or expired\" .-> fail\n    s9 -. \"length mismatch\" .-> fail\n```\n\n### 4.2 The step wrapper\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  call([\"runStep(name, status,<br/>retries 3, timeout, body)\"]) --> sd\n  subgraph sd [\"step.do(name), each attempt\"]\n    direction TB\n    ws[\"writeStatus: status,<br/>current_step = name,<br/>error cleared\"] --> body[\"the step's body\"]\n  end\n  body -->|\"returns\"| res([\"the step result,<br/>to the next step\"])\n  body -. \"throws, attempts left:<br/>nothing written\" .-> ws\n  sd -. \"last attempt failed,<br/>or NonRetryableError\" .-> fs[\"step.do(name failed):<br/>writes failed and<br/>error.message\"]\n  fs --> th([\"rethrow: instance<br/>ends errored\"])\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class ws,body flow\n  class fs,th broken\n```\n\nThe status write runs inside the step so a restart from that step writes it again. Step results carry only what the row does not hold: fetch's html, start synthesis's callId, and a poll's {ready: false} or the synthesis result.\n\n### 4.3 What each step calls\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph steps [\"workflow/steps\"]\n    direction TB\n    f@{ shape: rect, label: \"fetch\" }\n    l@{ shape: rect, label: \"lease, release\" }\n    rc@{ shape: rect, label: \"recipe\" }\n    im@{ shape: rect, label: \"images\" }\n    de@{ shape: rect, label: \"describe\" }\n    sy@{ shape: rect, label: \"start synthesis,<br/>poll, store\" }\n  end\n  subgraph mods [\"pipeline modules, return values only\"]\n    direction TB\n    fc@{ shape: rect, label: \"firecrawl/client\" }\n    dq@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/DomainQueue\" }\n    rs@{ shape: rect, label: \"recipes/<br/>store, settle\" }\n    rt@{ shape: rect, label: \"runtime/, agents/<br/>(unchanged)\" }\n    sp@{ shape: rect, label: \"spoken/<br/>derive, typed-units\" }\n    ia@{ shape: rect, label: \"images/<br/>acquire, svg, alt\" }\n    dm@{ shape: rect, label: \"describe/<br/>jobs, core, prompts\" }\n    tm@{ shape: rect, label: \"tts/modal\" }\n  end\n  led@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/ledger\" }\n  fcx@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Firecrawl\" }\n  aig@{ shape: cloud, label: \"AI Gateway\" }\n  imgb@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Images binding\" }\n  mx@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" }\n  r2@{ shape: cyl, label: \"R2\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  f --> fc --> fcx\n  l --> dq\n  rc --> rs --> rt --> aig\n  rc --> sp\n  im --> ia\n  ia --> imgb\n  ia --> r2\n  de --> dm --> aig\n  sy --> tm --> mx\n  steps -->|\"row writes\"| d1\n  f --> led\n  de --> led\n  sy --> led\n  led --> d1\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  class f,l,rc,im,de,sy,fc,dq,rs,rt,sp,ia,dm,tm,led flow\n  class r2,d1 store\n  class fcx,aig,imgb,mx ext\n```\n\nOnly the step files write to D1. The good-alt filter sits in images/alt and describe reads it too; a literal reading of CLAUDE.md would put it in common/.\n\n### 4.4 The lease\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  a[\"lease step:<br/>DomainQueue.acquire(id)\"] --> g{\"granted?\"}\n  g -->|yes| rec([\"recipe step\"])\n  g -->|no| w[\"waitForEvent<br/>lease wait n,<br/>lease-granted, 1 h\"]\n  w -->|\"event\"| rec\n  w -->|\"timeout, n < 3\"| rck[\"lease recheck n:<br/>acquire again\"]\n  rck --> g\n  w -. \"third timeout\" .-> fail([\"failed\"])\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class a,w,rck flow\n  class fail broken\n```\n\n### 4.5 The describe fan-out\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  rd[\"read units and title<br/>from the row\"] --> jobs[\"jobs in document order:<br/>code units, images whose<br/>alt fails the filter\"]\n  jobs --> cap{\"within the<br/>cap of 25?\"}\n  cap -->|no| floor[\"capped: floor or<br/>keep the fallback\"]\n  cap -->|yes| kids@{ shape: procs, label: \"step.do(describe i)<br/>3 x 1 min each,<br/>Promise.allSettled\" }\n  kids --> st{\"per child\"}\n  st -->|fulfilled| sent[\"Code: or Image:<br/>sentence\"]\n  st -->|rejected| floor\n  sent --> w[\"one D1 batch: units,<br/>degradations, a ledger<br/>row per success\"]\n  floor --> w\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class rd,jobs,kids,sent,floor,w flow\n```\n\n### 4.6 Files\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph del [\"deleted\"]\n    direction TB\n    d1@{ shape: rect, label: \"http/ routes, read,<br/>job-status\" }\n    d2@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/job-index\" }\n    d3@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/extraction,<br/>workflow/world\" }\n    d4@{ shape: rect, label: \"own lockfile and<br/>pnpm-workspace\" }\n    d5@{ shape: rect, label: \"tests: http, read-path,<br/>job-index, extraction,<br/>helpers/world, http\" }\n  end\n  subgraph tch [\"touched\"]\n    direction TB\n    t1@{ shape: rect, label: \"wrangler.jsonc: item<br/>workflow, D1, R2, IMAGES,<br/>workers_dev false\" }\n    t2@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/domain-queue\" }\n    t3@{ shape: rect, label: \"cloudflare.ts, app.ts,<br/>vitest.config.ts,<br/>vite.config.ts\" }\n  end\n  subgraph nw [\"new\"]\n    direction TB\n    n1@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/item, wrapper,<br/>ledger, steps/*\" }\n    n2@{ shape: rect, label: \"firecrawl/, recipes/,<br/>spoken/, images/,<br/>describe/, tts/\" }\n    n3@{ shape: rect, label: \"test/cassettes<br/>(moved from api/)\" }\n  end\n  classDef new fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef touched fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef gone fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class n1,n2,n3 new\n  class t1,t2,t3 touched\n  class d1,d2,d3,d4,d5 gone\n```\n\nPorted from Python: firecrawl from fetch.py, recipes/store from recipes.py, spoken/ from extract.py, images/ from images.py, describe/ from describe.py, tts/ from tts.py. runtime/ and agents/ stay as they are.\n\n## 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue\n\n### 5.1 acquire, release, advance\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  acq([\"acquire(id)\"]) --> h{\"id holds<br/>the lease?\"}\n  h -->|yes| gt([\"granted\"])\n  h -->|no| fr{\"lease free and<br/>FIFO empty?\"}\n  fr -->|yes| take[\"write lease = id,<br/>alarm in 60 s\"] --> gt\n  fr -->|no| inq{\"id already<br/>in the FIFO?\"}\n  inq -->|yes| keep([\"not granted,<br/>keeps its place\"])\n  inq -->|no| app[\"append id\"] --> keep\n  rel([\"release(id)\"]) --> drop[\"drop id from FIFO;<br/>if it holds the lease,<br/>delete it\"] --> adv\n  alarm([\"alarm, 60 s\"]) --> st{\"holder ended<br/>or gone?\"}\n  st -->|yes| adv[\"advance: next id,<br/>status() check, lease,<br/>sendEvent lease-granted\"]\n  st -->|no| re[\"re-arm\"]\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class take,app,drop,adv,re flow\n```\n\nThe FIFO holds instance ids only, in the synchronous ctx.storage.kv, so acquire has no await. enqueue, stateOf, the params storage and the job index go.\n\n## 6 tts/: the two web endpoints\n\n### 6.1 start and result\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  wf@{ shape: rect, label: \"item Workflow\" }\n  subgraph modal [\"Modal app nagara-tts\"]\n    direction TB\n    web@{ shape: rect, label: \"web function, CPU:<br/>POST start,<br/>GET result\" }\n    k@{ shape: rect, label: \"Kokoro.synthesize<br/>(paragraphs, voice,<br/>destination)\" }\n  end\n  r2@{ shape: cyl, label: \"R2 audio/\" }\n  wf -->|\"start: paragraphs,<br/>voice, PUT URL<br/>Modal-Key, Modal-Secret\"| web\n  web -->|\"spawn\"| k\n  web -->|\"call_id\"| wf\n  k -->|\"PUT encoded audio\"| r2\n  wf -->|\"result?call_id\"| web\n  web -->|\"202 running · 200 format,<br/>duration, timings ·<br/>500 failed · 410 expired\"| wf\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  class wf flow\n  class web,k ext\n  class r2 store\n```\n\nBoth endpoints require proxy auth and take pydantic models. The result carries no audio bytes.\n\n## 7 Local development\n\n### 7.1 Launch\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  mig[\"1 common:<br/>migrate:local\"] --> st@{ shape: cyl, label: \".wrangler-state/<br/>D1, R2, DOs\" }\n  pipe[\"2 pipeline: pnpm dev<br/>vite, persistState\"] --- st\n  proxy[\"3 pipeline: dev:proxy<br/>/s3 to /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3\"] --> pipe\n  tun@{ shape: cloud, label: \"4 cloudflared<br/>quick tunnel\" } --> proxy\n  vars@{ shape: doc, label: \"pipeline/.dev.vars<br/>R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT =<br/>https://tunnel/s3\" }\n  vars -.-> pipe\n  api[\"5 api: pnpm dev<br/>wrangler --persist-to\"] --- st\n  api -->|\"create, restart\"| pipe\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" } -->|\"PUT\"| tun\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class mig,proxy,vars tool\n  class st store\n  class tun,modal ext\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n```\n\nThe pipeline signs PUT URLs for R2_S3_ENDPOINT and swaps in R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT for Modal; in production the two are equal, so no code checks the environment.\n\n## 8 CI\n\n### 8.1 One Cloudflare workflow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    push([\"push to main\"]) --> ch[\"changes:<br/>paths-filter for<br/>common, pipeline, api\"]\n    ch --> cc[\"common checks:<br/>test, lint, types,<br/>api and pipeline types\"]\n    ch --> pc[\"pipeline checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    ch --> ac[\"api checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    cc --> mig[\"migrate: wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply --remote\"]\n    mig --> pd[\"deploy pipeline:<br/>pnpm build,<br/>deploy dist config\"]\n    pc --> pd\n    pd --> ad[\"deploy api\"]\n    ac --> ad\n    cc -. \"a check fails\" .-> stop([\"nothing deploys\"])\n```\n\ncloudflare.yml replaces api.yml and pipeline.yml; tts.yml stays. A skipped job does not block the jobs after it, so a pipeline-only push deploys without a migration. The docs say three workflows.\n\n## 9 Standards\n\n### 9.1 Sources\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  cm@{ shape: doc, label: \"CLAUDE.md\" }\n  gl@{ shape: doc, label: \"global CLAUDE.md,<br/>mahou basics\" }\n  wk@{ shape: doc, label: \"wiki entries\" }\n  a1[\"shared types in common/,<br/>pydantic in tts/,<br/>invariants 2 to 8\"]\n  a2[\"== null, constant maps,<br/>one function per module,<br/>no comments in literals\"]\n  a3[\"workflows, vitest-plugin,<br/>r2, local-dev, images,<br/>ai-gateway, gemini,<br/>firecrawl, modal, flue,<br/>durable-objects, markdown,<br/>cassettes-over-mocks\"]\n  cm --> a1\n  gl --> a2\n  wk --> a3\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class cm,gl,wk tool\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":231232,"output_tokens":10551,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":734},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":10551,"cache_read_input_tokens":231232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015uVQsBRfDwvx76pHuEYRrx":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/canvas.md","content":"# Program design canvas: visual parts\n\nThe canvas draws these diagrams; `nagara.md` keeps the text representations.\n\n## 1 Workspace and packages\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  ws@{ shape: doc, label: \"pnpm workspace:<br/>root package.json,<br/>one lockfile\" }\n  subgraph cf [\"Built by pnpm, deployed by wrangler\"]\n    direction LR\n    api@{ shape: rect, label: \"api/<br/>@nagara/api<br/>Worker nagara-api\" }\n    common@{ shape: rect, label: \"common/<br/>@nagara/common<br/>source only, no build\" }\n    pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline/<br/>Worker nagara<br/>built by Vite + Flue\" }\n  end\n  tts@{ shape: rect, label: \"tts/<br/>uv, outside<br/>the workspace\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" }\n  ws --- api\n  ws --- common\n  ws --- pipe\n  api -->|\"workspace:*<br/>types, keys, presign, row\"| common\n  pipe -->|\"workspace:*<br/>types, keys, presign,<br/>row, sanitize\"| common\n  common -->|\"migrations/\"| d1\n  tts -->|\"modal deploy\"| modal\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class common shared\n  class d1 store\n  class modal ext\n  class ws,tts tool\n```\n\nThe Python api/ goes and a TypeScript Worker takes its place. common/ is compiled into each Worker; only its migrations deploy. New dependencies: aws4fetch (common), markdown-it (pipeline), msw 2.15 (tests of both Workers), valibot joins api/.\n\n## 2 common/\n\n### 2.1 What it holds\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n  direction LR\n  class ItemRow {\n    id, url, title, voice\n    status: ItemStatus\n    created_at, updated_at, queued_at\n    workflow_instance_id?\n    current_step?\n    extraction_domain?, recipe_version_id?\n    retry_count\n    duration?, audio_format?\n    units: RowUnit[]\n    degradations: Degradation[]\n    error?\n  }\n  class RowUnit {\n    <<union>>\n  }\n  class Unit {\n    <<union: paragraph, code, image>>\n    type, display, spoken\n    image hash: image only\n    start?, end?: set by store\n  }\n  class DeclaredImageUnit {\n    <<until the images step>>\n    type declared-image\n    src, alt\n  }\n  class Degradation {\n    type: image or code\n    reason\n    url?\n  }\n  class CostEntryRow {\n    item_id, type, quantity, unit\n    dollars, cached, detail?\n  }\n  class RecipeVersionRow {\n    id, domain, version, script\n  }\n  class ItemWorkflowParams {\n    itemId\n  }\n  ItemRow --> RowUnit\n  RowUnit <|-- Unit\n  RowUnit <|-- DeclaredImageUnit\n  ItemRow --> Degradation\n  ItemRow ..> RecipeVersionRow : recipe_version_id\n  CostEntryRow ..> ItemRow : item_id\n```\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph common [\"common/src\"]\n    direction TB\n    row@{ shape: rect, label: \"row.ts<br/>readItem, writeStatus,<br/>JSON codec\" }\n    wf@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow.ts<br/>STEP names,<br/>restartPoint\" }\n    keys@{ shape: rect, label: \"keys.ts<br/>audioKey, imageKey\" }\n    sign@{ shape: rect, label: \"presign.ts<br/>GET or PUT URL\" }\n    san@{ shape: rect, label: \"sanitize.ts<br/>the sanitize tail\" }\n  end\n  subgraph testing [\"common/testing\"]\n    vcr@{ shape: rect, label: \"replayCassettes<br/>to msw handlers\" }\n  end\n  mig@{ shape: cyl, label: \"common/migrations<br/>0001_initial.sql\" }\n  api@{ shape: rect, label: \"API Worker\" }\n  pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline Worker\" }\n  tests@{ shape: rect, label: \"both Workers' tests\" }\n  api --> row\n  api --> wf\n  api --> keys\n  api -->|\"GET\"| sign\n  pipe --> row\n  pipe --> wf\n  pipe --> keys\n  pipe -->|\"PUT\"| sign\n  pipe --> san\n  tests --> vcr\n  tests -->|\"readD1Migrations\"| mig\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class row,wf,keys,sign,san,vcr shared\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class mig store\n  class tests tool\n```\n\nwriteStatus sets status, current_step and updated_at and clears error in one UPDATE; restartPoint maps recipe and release to lease, keeps any other step, and returns null (restart every step) when current_step is empty. Statuses, cost types and units are constant maps.\n\n## 3 api/: the routes\n\n### 3.1 Enqueue and poll\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  e([\"POST /items<br/>{url, voice?}\"]) --> g{\"key valid?\"}\n  g -->|no| e401([\"401\"])\n  g -->|yes| v{\"body valid?\"}\n  v -->|no| e400([\"400\"])\n  v -->|yes| ins[\"insert row: queued,<br/>queued_at now,<br/>voice picked if absent\"]\n  ins --> cr[\"ITEM_WORKFLOW.create<br/>{itemId}\"]\n  cr --> ok([\"202 item\"])\n  cr -. \"throws: log it\" .-> ok\n  p([\"GET /items/{id}\"]) --> r{\"row exists?\"}\n  r -->|no| n404([\"404\"])\n  r -->|yes| q{\"queued and<br/>queued_at > 15 min?\"}\n  q -->|no| pok([\"200 item\"])\n  q -->|yes| claim{\"claim: UPDATE<br/>queued_at WHERE still<br/>queued and stale\"}\n  claim -->|\"0 rows: another<br/>poll got it\"| pok\n  claim -->|\"1 row\"| has{\"instance id<br/>on the row?\"}\n  has -->|no| c2[\"create {itemId}\"]\n  has -->|yes| rs[\"restart from<br/>restartPoint(current_step)\"]\n  c2 --> pok\n  rs --> pok\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  classDef done fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class ins,cr,c2,rs worker\n  class e401,e400,n404 broken\n  class ok,pok done\n```\n\n### 3.2 Retry and media\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  t([\"POST /items/{id}/retry\"]) --> r{\"row exists?\"}\n  r -->|no| n404([\"404\"])\n  r -->|yes| claim{\"claim: UPDATE to queued,<br/>retry_count + 1, error null<br/>WHERE failed and<br/>retry_count < 3\"}\n  claim -->|\"0 rows\"| c409([\"409\"])\n  claim -->|\"1 row\"| rs[\"restart from<br/>restartPoint(current_step)\"]\n  rs --> ok([\"202 item\"])\n  m([\"GET audio · GET images/{hash}\"]) --> mr{\"row exists?<br/>audio: ready with<br/>audio_format?\"}\n  mr -->|no| m404([\"404\"])\n  mr -->|yes| sign[\"presign GET for<br/>audioKey or imageKey,<br/>1 h, API's R2 token\"]\n  sign --> redirect([\"307\"])\n  h([\"GET /health\"]) --> hok([\"200, no key\"])\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  classDef done fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class rs,sign worker\n  class n404,c409,m404 broken\n  class ok,redirect,hok done\n```\n\nThe re-queue does not count toward the 3 retries. The API never reads the instance's status; the row is all it reads.\n\n### 3.3 Modules\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  idx@{ shape: rect, label: \"index.ts<br/>route table\" }\n  guard@{ shape: rect, label: \"guard.ts<br/>X-API-Key\" }\n  subgraph routes [\"routes/\"]\n    direction TB\n    en@{ shape: rect, label: \"enqueue\" }\n    po@{ shape: rect, label: \"poll\" }\n    re@{ shape: rect, label: \"retry\" }\n    au@{ shape: rect, label: \"audio, images\" }\n  end\n  subgraph items [\"items/\"]\n    direction TB\n    cr@{ shape: rect, label: \"create.ts<br/>insertQueued, id mint\" }\n    rq@{ shape: rect, label: \"requeue.ts\" }\n    rc@{ shape: rect, label: \"retry-claim.ts\" }\n  end\n  resp@{ shape: rect, label: \"response.ts<br/>toItemResponse\" }\n  voices@{ shape: rect, label: \"voices.ts\" }\n  common@{ shape: rect, label: \"common/\" }\n  wf@{ shape: cloud, label: \"ITEM_WORKFLOW<br/>script_name nagara\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  idx --> guard --> routes\n  en --> cr\n  en --> voices\n  po --> rq\n  re --> rc\n  routes --> resp\n  routes --> common\n  cr --> d1\n  rq --> d1\n  rc --> d1\n  en --> wf\n  rq --> wf\n  re --> wf\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  class idx,guard,en,po,re,au,cr,rq,rc,resp,voices worker\n  class common shared\n  class d1 store\n  class wf ext\n```\n\ntoItemResponse keeps today's wire shape: units are null until ready, spoken is dropped, audio_url appears only when ready. Secrets: API_KEY and the GET R2 token.\n\n## 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow\n\n### 4.1 The nine steps\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"ItemWorkflow.run<br/>params {itemId}\"]) --> s1[\"1 fetch · queued<br/>writes instance id,<br/>domain, ledger row<br/>returns {html}\"]\n    s1 --> s2[\"2 lease · queued<br/>ask DomainQueue,<br/>waitForEvent lease-granted\"]\n    s2 --> s3[\"3 recipe · generating<br/>run, author or revise;<br/>spoken form and drop;<br/>writes title, units\"]\n    s3 --> s4[\"4 release · generating<br/>give the lease back\"]\n    s4 --> s5[\"5 images · generating<br/>acquire declared images;<br/>writes units, degradations\"]\n    s5 --> s6[\"6 describe · generating<br/>child steps, allSettled;<br/>one write at the end\"]\n    s6 --> s7[\"7 start synthesis<br/>· generating<br/>sign PUT, call Modal<br/>returns {callId}\"]\n    s7 --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"8 poll · generating\"]\n        direction TB\n        p[\"poll n: fetch result\"] --> r{\"ready?\"}\n        r -->|\"no: sleep 10 s,<br/>n + 1\"| p\n    end\n    r -->|\"yes, returns the result\"| s9[\"9 store · generating<br/>join timings; writes<br/>ready, units, duration,<br/>format, tts ledger row\"]\n    s9 --> done([\"ready\"])\n    s1 -. \"last attempt fails\" .-> fail([\"wrapper writes failed,<br/>the step's error;<br/>run() rethrows\"])\n    s2 -. \"3 waits of 1 h\" .-> fail\n    s3 -. \"not an article: at once\" .-> fail\n    s5 -.-> fail\n    s7 -.-> fail\n    loop -. \"failed or expired\" .-> fail\n    s9 -. \"length mismatch\" .-> fail\n```\n\n### 4.2 The step wrapper\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  call([\"runStep(name, status,<br/>retries 3, timeout, body)\"]) --> sd\n  subgraph sd [\"step.do(name), each attempt\"]\n    direction TB\n    ws[\"writeStatus: status,<br/>current_step = name,<br/>error cleared\"] --> body[\"the step's body\"]\n  end\n  body -->|\"returns\"| res([\"the step result,<br/>to the next step\"])\n  body -. \"throws, attempts left:<br/>nothing written\" .-> ws\n  sd -. \"last attempt failed,<br/>or NonRetryableError\" .-> fs[\"step.do(name failed):<br/>writes failed and<br/>error.message\"]\n  fs --> th([\"rethrow: instance<br/>ends errored\"])\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class ws,body flow\n  class fs,th broken\n```\n\nThe status write runs inside the step so a restart from that step writes it again. Step results carry only what the row does not hold: fetch's html, start synthesis's callId, and a poll's {ready: false} or the synthesis result.\n\n### 4.3 What each step calls\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph steps [\"workflow/steps\"]\n    direction TB\n    f@{ shape: rect, label: \"fetch\" }\n    l@{ shape: rect, label: \"lease, release\" }\n    rc@{ shape: rect, label: \"recipe\" }\n    im@{ shape: rect, label: \"images\" }\n    de@{ shape: rect, label: \"describe\" }\n    sy@{ shape: rect, label: \"start synthesis,<br/>poll, store\" }\n  end\n  subgraph mods [\"pipeline modules, return values only\"]\n    direction TB\n    fc@{ shape: rect, label: \"firecrawl/client\" }\n    dq@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/DomainQueue\" }\n    rs@{ shape: rect, label: \"recipes/<br/>store, settle\" }\n    rt@{ shape: rect, label: \"runtime/, agents/<br/>(unchanged)\" }\n    sp@{ shape: rect, label: \"spoken/<br/>derive, typed-units\" }\n    ia@{ shape: rect, label: \"images/<br/>acquire, svg, alt\" }\n    dm@{ shape: rect, label: \"describe/<br/>jobs, core, prompts\" }\n    tm@{ shape: rect, label: \"tts/modal\" }\n  end\n  led@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/ledger\" }\n  fcx@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Firecrawl\" }\n  aig@{ shape: cloud, label: \"AI Gateway\" }\n  imgb@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Images binding\" }\n  mx@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" }\n  r2@{ shape: cyl, label: \"R2\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  f --> fc --> fcx\n  l --> dq\n  rc --> rs --> rt --> aig\n  rc --> sp\n  im --> ia\n  ia --> imgb\n  ia --> r2\n  de --> dm --> aig\n  sy --> tm --> mx\n  steps -->|\"row writes\"| d1\n  f --> led\n  de --> led\n  sy --> led\n  led --> d1\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  class f,l,rc,im,de,sy,fc,dq,rs,rt,sp,ia,dm,tm,led flow\n  class r2,d1 store\n  class fcx,aig,imgb,mx ext\n```\n\nOnly the step files write to D1. The good-alt filter sits in images/alt and describe reads it too; a literal reading of CLAUDE.md would put it in common/.\n\n### 4.4 The lease\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  a[\"lease step:<br/>DomainQueue.acquire(id)\"] --> g{\"granted?\"}\n  g -->|yes| rec([\"recipe step\"])\n  g -->|no| w[\"waitForEvent<br/>lease wait n,<br/>lease-granted, 1 h\"]\n  w -->|\"event\"| rec\n  w -->|\"timeout, n < 3\"| rck[\"lease recheck n:<br/>acquire again\"]\n  rck --> g\n  w -. \"third timeout\" .-> fail([\"failed\"])\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class a,w,rck flow\n  class fail broken\n```\n\n### 4.5 The describe fan-out\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  rd[\"read units and title<br/>from the row\"] --> jobs[\"jobs in document order:<br/>code units, images whose<br/>alt fails the filter\"]\n  jobs --> cap{\"within the<br/>cap of 25?\"}\n  cap -->|no| floor[\"capped: floor or<br/>keep the fallback\"]\n  cap -->|yes| kids@{ shape: procs, label: \"step.do(describe i)<br/>3 x 1 min each,<br/>Promise.allSettled\" }\n  kids --> st{\"per child\"}\n  st -->|fulfilled| sent[\"Code: or Image:<br/>sentence\"]\n  st -->|rejected| floor\n  sent --> w[\"one D1 batch: units,<br/>degradations, a ledger<br/>row per success\"]\n  floor --> w\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class rd,jobs,kids,sent,floor,w flow\n```\n\n### 4.6 Files\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph del [\"deleted\"]\n    direction TB\n    d1@{ shape: rect, label: \"http/ routes, read,<br/>job-status\" }\n    d2@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/job-index\" }\n    d3@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/extraction,<br/>workflow/world\" }\n    d4@{ shape: rect, label: \"own lockfile and<br/>pnpm-workspace\" }\n    d5@{ shape: rect, label: \"tests: http, read-path,<br/>job-index, extraction,<br/>helpers/world, http\" }\n  end\n  subgraph tch [\"touched\"]\n    direction TB\n    t1@{ shape: rect, label: \"wrangler.jsonc: item<br/>workflow, D1, R2, IMAGES,<br/>workers_dev false\" }\n    t2@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/domain-queue\" }\n    t3@{ shape: rect, label: \"cloudflare.ts, app.ts,<br/>vitest.config.ts,<br/>vite.config.ts\" }\n  end\n  subgraph nw [\"new\"]\n    direction TB\n    n1@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/item, wrapper,<br/>ledger, steps/*\" }\n    n2@{ shape: rect, label: \"firecrawl/, recipes/,<br/>spoken/, images/,<br/>describe/, tts/\" }\n    n3@{ shape: rect, label: \"test/cassettes<br/>(moved from api/)\" }\n  end\n  classDef new fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef touched fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef gone fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class n1,n2,n3 new\n  class t1,t2,t3 touched\n  class d1,d2,d3,d4,d5 gone\n```\n\nPorted from Python: firecrawl from fetch.py, recipes/store from recipes.py, spoken/ from extract.py, images/ from images.py, describe/ from describe.py, tts/ from tts.py. runtime/ and agents/ stay as they are.\n\n## 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue\n\n### 5.1 acquire, release, advance\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  acq([\"acquire(id)\"]) --> h{\"id holds<br/>the lease?\"}\n  h -->|yes| gt([\"granted\"])\n  h -->|no| fr{\"lease free and<br/>FIFO empty?\"}\n  fr -->|yes| take[\"write lease = id,<br/>alarm in 60 s\"] --> gt\n  fr -->|no| inq{\"id already<br/>in the FIFO?\"}\n  inq -->|yes| keep([\"not granted,<br/>keeps its place\"])\n  inq -->|no| app[\"append id\"] --> keep\n  rel([\"release(id)\"]) --> drop[\"drop id from FIFO;<br/>if it holds the lease,<br/>delete it\"] --> adv\n  alarm([\"alarm, 60 s\"]) --> st{\"holder ended<br/>or gone?\"}\n  st -->|yes| adv[\"advance: next id,<br/>status() check, lease,<br/>sendEvent lease-granted\"]\n  st -->|no| re[\"re-arm\"]\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class take,app,drop,adv,re flow\n```\n\nThe FIFO holds instance ids only, in the synchronous ctx.storage.kv, so acquire has no await. enqueue, stateOf, the params storage and the job index go.\n\n## 6 tts/: the two web endpoints\n\n### 6.1 start and result\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  wf@{ shape: rect, label: \"item Workflow\" }\n  subgraph modal [\"Modal app nagara-tts\"]\n    direction TB\n    web@{ shape: rect, label: \"web function, CPU:<br/>POST start,<br/>GET result\" }\n    k@{ shape: rect, label: \"Kokoro.synthesize<br/>(paragraphs, voice,<br/>destination)\" }\n  end\n  r2@{ shape: cyl, label: \"R2 audio/\" }\n  wf -->|\"start: paragraphs,<br/>voice, PUT URL<br/>Modal-Key, Modal-Secret\"| web\n  web -->|\"spawn\"| k\n  web -->|\"call_id\"| wf\n  k -->|\"PUT encoded audio\"| r2\n  wf -->|\"result?call_id\"| web\n  web -->|\"202 running · 200 format,<br/>duration, timings ·<br/>500 failed · 410 expired\"| wf\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  class wf flow\n  class web,k ext\n  class r2 store\n```\n\nBoth endpoints require proxy auth and take pydantic models. The result carries no audio bytes.\n\n## 7 Local development\n\n### 7.1 Launch\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  mig[\"1 common:<br/>migrate:local\"] --> st@{ shape: cyl, label: \".wrangler-state/<br/>D1, R2, DOs\" }\n  pipe[\"2 pipeline: pnpm dev<br/>vite, persistState\"] --- st\n  proxy[\"3 pipeline: dev:proxy<br/>/s3 to /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3\"] --> pipe\n  tun@{ shape: cloud, label: \"4 cloudflared<br/>quick tunnel\" } --> proxy\n  vars@{ shape: doc, label: \"pipeline/.dev.vars<br/>R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT =<br/>https://tunnel/s3\" }\n  vars -.-> pipe\n  api[\"5 api: pnpm dev<br/>wrangler --persist-to\"] --- st\n  api -->|\"create, restart\"| pipe\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" } -->|\"PUT\"| tun\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class mig,proxy,vars tool\n  class st store\n  class tun,modal ext\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n```\n\nThe pipeline signs PUT URLs for R2_S3_ENDPOINT and swaps in R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT for Modal; in production the two are equal, so no code checks the environment.\n\n## 8 CI\n\n### 8.1 One Cloudflare workflow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    push([\"push to main\"]) --> ch[\"changes:<br/>paths-filter for<br/>common, pipeline, api\"]\n    ch --> cc[\"common checks:<br/>test, lint, types,<br/>api and pipeline types\"]\n    ch --> pc[\"pipeline checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    ch --> ac[\"api checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    cc --> mig[\"migrate: wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply --remote\"]\n    mig --> pd[\"deploy pipeline:<br/>pnpm build,<br/>deploy dist config\"]\n    pc --> pd\n    pd --> ad[\"deploy api\"]\n    ac --> ad\n    cc -. \"a check fails\" .-> stop([\"nothing deploys\"])\n```\n\ncloudflare.yml replaces api.yml and pipeline.yml; tts.yml stays. A skipped job does not block the jobs after it, so a pipeline-only push deploys without a migration. The docs say three workflows.\n\n## 9 Standards\n\n### 9.1 Sources\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  cm@{ shape: doc, label: \"CLAUDE.md\" }\n  gl@{ shape: doc, label: \"global CLAUDE.md,<br/>mahou basics\" }\n  wk@{ shape: doc, label: \"wiki entries\" }\n  a1[\"shared types in common/,<br/>pydantic in tts/,<br/>invariants 2 to 8\"]\n  a2[\"== null, constant maps,<br/>one function per module,<br/>no comments in literals\"]\n  a3[\"workflows, vitest-plugin,<br/>r2, local-dev, images,<br/>ai-gateway, gemini,<br/>firecrawl, modal, flue,<br/>durable-objects, markdown,<br/>cassettes-over-mocks\"]\n  cm --> a1\n  gl --> a2\n  wk --> a3\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class cm,gl,wk tool\n```\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd707c1c-0ddf-4141-923e-36f2c540b672","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfurhAcaqZNVbgDcgcgqd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e67d15bd-7083-47ad-a4f9-840672d71e44","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:59:19.601Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"e67d15bd-7083-47ad-a4f9-840672d71e44","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"db309e29-deb6-4554-ab0e-a079114120e1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015uVQsBRfDwvx76pHuEYRrx","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/canvas.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e1b53777-fa57-42bb-b89e-093e100b5940","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:59:19.677Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/canvas.md","content":"# Program design canvas: visual parts\n\nThe canvas draws these diagrams; `nagara.md` keeps the text representations.\n\n## 1 Workspace and packages\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  ws@{ shape: doc, label: \"pnpm workspace:<br/>root package.json,<br/>one lockfile\" }\n  subgraph cf [\"Built by pnpm, deployed by wrangler\"]\n    direction LR\n    api@{ shape: rect, label: \"api/<br/>@nagara/api<br/>Worker nagara-api\" }\n    common@{ shape: rect, label: \"common/<br/>@nagara/common<br/>source only, no build\" }\n    pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline/<br/>Worker nagara<br/>built by Vite + Flue\" }\n  end\n  tts@{ shape: rect, label: \"tts/<br/>uv, outside<br/>the workspace\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" }\n  ws --- api\n  ws --- common\n  ws --- pipe\n  api -->|\"workspace:*<br/>types, keys, presign, row\"| common\n  pipe -->|\"workspace:*<br/>types, keys, presign,<br/>row, sanitize\"| common\n  common -->|\"migrations/\"| d1\n  tts -->|\"modal deploy\"| modal\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class common shared\n  class d1 store\n  class modal ext\n  class ws,tts tool\n```\n\nThe Python api/ goes and a TypeScript Worker takes its place. common/ is compiled into each Worker; only its migrations deploy. New dependencies: aws4fetch (common), markdown-it (pipeline), msw 2.15 (tests of both Workers), valibot joins api/.\n\n## 2 common/\n\n### 2.1 What it holds\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n  direction LR\n  class ItemRow {\n    id, url, title, voice\n    status: ItemStatus\n    created_at, updated_at, queued_at\n    workflow_instance_id?\n    current_step?\n    extraction_domain?, recipe_version_id?\n    retry_count\n    duration?, audio_format?\n    units: RowUnit[]\n    degradations: Degradation[]\n    error?\n  }\n  class RowUnit {\n    <<union>>\n  }\n  class Unit {\n    <<union: paragraph, code, image>>\n    type, display, spoken\n    image hash: image only\n    start?, end?: set by store\n  }\n  class DeclaredImageUnit {\n    <<until the images step>>\n    type declared-image\n    src, alt\n  }\n  class Degradation {\n    type: image or code\n    reason\n    url?\n  }\n  class CostEntryRow {\n    item_id, type, quantity, unit\n    dollars, cached, detail?\n  }\n  class RecipeVersionRow {\n    id, domain, version, script\n  }\n  class ItemWorkflowParams {\n    itemId\n  }\n  ItemRow --> RowUnit\n  RowUnit <|-- Unit\n  RowUnit <|-- DeclaredImageUnit\n  ItemRow --> Degradation\n  ItemRow ..> RecipeVersionRow : recipe_version_id\n  CostEntryRow ..> ItemRow : item_id\n```\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph common [\"common/src\"]\n    direction TB\n    row@{ shape: rect, label: \"row.ts<br/>readItem, writeStatus,<br/>JSON codec\" }\n    wf@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow.ts<br/>STEP names,<br/>restartPoint\" }\n    keys@{ shape: rect, label: \"keys.ts<br/>audioKey, imageKey\" }\n    sign@{ shape: rect, label: \"presign.ts<br/>GET or PUT URL\" }\n    san@{ shape: rect, label: \"sanitize.ts<br/>the sanitize tail\" }\n  end\n  subgraph testing [\"common/testing\"]\n    vcr@{ shape: rect, label: \"replayCassettes<br/>to msw handlers\" }\n  end\n  mig@{ shape: cyl, label: \"common/migrations<br/>0001_initial.sql\" }\n  api@{ shape: rect, label: \"API Worker\" }\n  pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline Worker\" }\n  tests@{ shape: rect, label: \"both Workers' tests\" }\n  api --> row\n  api --> wf\n  api --> keys\n  api -->|\"GET\"| sign\n  pipe --> row\n  pipe --> wf\n  pipe --> keys\n  pipe -->|\"PUT\"| sign\n  pipe --> san\n  tests --> vcr\n  tests -->|\"readD1Migrations\"| mig\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class row,wf,keys,sign,san,vcr shared\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class mig store\n  class tests tool\n```\n\nwriteStatus sets status, current_step and updated_at and clears error in one UPDATE; restartPoint maps recipe and release to lease, keeps any other step, and returns null (restart every step) when current_step is empty. Statuses, cost types and units are constant maps.\n\n## 3 api/: the routes\n\n### 3.1 Enqueue and poll\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  e([\"POST /items<br/>{url, voice?}\"]) --> g{\"key valid?\"}\n  g -->|no| e401([\"401\"])\n  g -->|yes| v{\"body valid?\"}\n  v -->|no| e400([\"400\"])\n  v -->|yes| ins[\"insert row: queued,<br/>queued_at now,<br/>voice picked if absent\"]\n  ins --> cr[\"ITEM_WORKFLOW.create<br/>{itemId}\"]\n  cr --> ok([\"202 item\"])\n  cr -. \"throws: log it\" .-> ok\n  p([\"GET /items/{id}\"]) --> r{\"row exists?\"}\n  r -->|no| n404([\"404\"])\n  r -->|yes| q{\"queued and<br/>queued_at > 15 min?\"}\n  q -->|no| pok([\"200 item\"])\n  q -->|yes| claim{\"claim: UPDATE<br/>queued_at WHERE still<br/>queued and stale\"}\n  claim -->|\"0 rows: another<br/>poll got it\"| pok\n  claim -->|\"1 row\"| has{\"instance id<br/>on the row?\"}\n  has -->|no| c2[\"create {itemId}\"]\n  has -->|yes| rs[\"restart from<br/>restartPoint(current_step)\"]\n  c2 --> pok\n  rs --> pok\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  classDef done fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class ins,cr,c2,rs worker\n  class e401,e400,n404 broken\n  class ok,pok done\n```\n\n### 3.2 Retry and media\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  t([\"POST /items/{id}/retry\"]) --> r{\"row exists?\"}\n  r -->|no| n404([\"404\"])\n  r -->|yes| claim{\"claim: UPDATE to queued,<br/>retry_count + 1, error null<br/>WHERE failed and<br/>retry_count < 3\"}\n  claim -->|\"0 rows\"| c409([\"409\"])\n  claim -->|\"1 row\"| rs[\"restart from<br/>restartPoint(current_step)\"]\n  rs --> ok([\"202 item\"])\n  m([\"GET audio · GET images/{hash}\"]) --> mr{\"row exists?<br/>audio: ready with<br/>audio_format?\"}\n  mr -->|no| m404([\"404\"])\n  mr -->|yes| sign[\"presign GET for<br/>audioKey or imageKey,<br/>1 h, API's R2 token\"]\n  sign --> redirect([\"307\"])\n  h([\"GET /health\"]) --> hok([\"200, no key\"])\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  classDef done fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class rs,sign worker\n  class n404,c409,m404 broken\n  class ok,redirect,hok done\n```\n\nThe re-queue does not count toward the 3 retries. The API never reads the instance's status; the row is all it reads.\n\n### 3.3 Modules\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  idx@{ shape: rect, label: \"index.ts<br/>route table\" }\n  guard@{ shape: rect, label: \"guard.ts<br/>X-API-Key\" }\n  subgraph routes [\"routes/\"]\n    direction TB\n    en@{ shape: rect, label: \"enqueue\" }\n    po@{ shape: rect, label: \"poll\" }\n    re@{ shape: rect, label: \"retry\" }\n    au@{ shape: rect, label: \"audio, images\" }\n  end\n  subgraph items [\"items/\"]\n    direction TB\n    cr@{ shape: rect, label: \"create.ts<br/>insertQueued, id mint\" }\n    rq@{ shape: rect, label: \"requeue.ts\" }\n    rc@{ shape: rect, label: \"retry-claim.ts\" }\n  end\n  resp@{ shape: rect, label: \"response.ts<br/>toItemResponse\" }\n  voices@{ shape: rect, label: \"voices.ts\" }\n  common@{ shape: rect, label: \"common/\" }\n  wf@{ shape: cloud, label: \"ITEM_WORKFLOW<br/>script_name nagara\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  idx --> guard --> routes\n  en --> cr\n  en --> voices\n  po --> rq\n  re --> rc\n  routes --> resp\n  routes --> common\n  cr --> d1\n  rq --> d1\n  rc --> d1\n  en --> wf\n  rq --> wf\n  re --> wf\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  class idx,guard,en,po,re,au,cr,rq,rc,resp,voices worker\n  class common shared\n  class d1 store\n  class wf ext\n```\n\ntoItemResponse keeps today's wire shape: units are null until ready, spoken is dropped, audio_url appears only when ready. Secrets: API_KEY and the GET R2 token.\n\n## 4 pipeline/: the item Workflow\n\n### 4.1 The nine steps\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"ItemWorkflow.run<br/>params {itemId}\"]) --> s1[\"1 fetch · queued<br/>writes instance id,<br/>domain, ledger row<br/>returns {html}\"]\n    s1 --> s2[\"2 lease · queued<br/>ask DomainQueue,<br/>waitForEvent lease-granted\"]\n    s2 --> s3[\"3 recipe · generating<br/>run, author or revise;<br/>spoken form and drop;<br/>writes title, units\"]\n    s3 --> s4[\"4 release · generating<br/>give the lease back\"]\n    s4 --> s5[\"5 images · generating<br/>acquire declared images;<br/>writes units, degradations\"]\n    s5 --> s6[\"6 describe · generating<br/>child steps, allSettled;<br/>one write at the end\"]\n    s6 --> s7[\"7 start synthesis<br/>· generating<br/>sign PUT, call Modal<br/>returns {callId}\"]\n    s7 --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"8 poll · generating\"]\n        direction TB\n        p[\"poll n: fetch result\"] --> r{\"ready?\"}\n        r -->|\"no: sleep 10 s,<br/>n + 1\"| p\n    end\n    r -->|\"yes, returns the result\"| s9[\"9 store · generating<br/>join timings; writes<br/>ready, units, duration,<br/>format, tts ledger row\"]\n    s9 --> done([\"ready\"])\n    s1 -. \"last attempt fails\" .-> fail([\"wrapper writes failed,<br/>the step's error;<br/>run() rethrows\"])\n    s2 -. \"3 waits of 1 h\" .-> fail\n    s3 -. \"not an article: at once\" .-> fail\n    s5 -.-> fail\n    s7 -.-> fail\n    loop -. \"failed or expired\" .-> fail\n    s9 -. \"length mismatch\" .-> fail\n```\n\n### 4.2 The step wrapper\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  call([\"runStep(name, status,<br/>retries 3, timeout, body)\"]) --> sd\n  subgraph sd [\"step.do(name), each attempt\"]\n    direction TB\n    ws[\"writeStatus: status,<br/>current_step = name,<br/>error cleared\"] --> body[\"the step's body\"]\n  end\n  body -->|\"returns\"| res([\"the step result,<br/>to the next step\"])\n  body -. \"throws, attempts left:<br/>nothing written\" .-> ws\n  sd -. \"last attempt failed,<br/>or NonRetryableError\" .-> fs[\"step.do(name failed):<br/>writes failed and<br/>error.message\"]\n  fs --> th([\"rethrow: instance<br/>ends errored\"])\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class ws,body flow\n  class fs,th broken\n```\n\nThe status write runs inside the step so a restart from that step writes it again. Step results carry only what the row does not hold: fetch's html, start synthesis's callId, and a poll's {ready: false} or the synthesis result.\n\n### 4.3 What each step calls\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph steps [\"workflow/steps\"]\n    direction TB\n    f@{ shape: rect, label: \"fetch\" }\n    l@{ shape: rect, label: \"lease, release\" }\n    rc@{ shape: rect, label: \"recipe\" }\n    im@{ shape: rect, label: \"images\" }\n    de@{ shape: rect, label: \"describe\" }\n    sy@{ shape: rect, label: \"start synthesis,<br/>poll, store\" }\n  end\n  subgraph mods [\"pipeline modules, return values only\"]\n    direction TB\n    fc@{ shape: rect, label: \"firecrawl/client\" }\n    dq@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/DomainQueue\" }\n    rs@{ shape: rect, label: \"recipes/<br/>store, settle\" }\n    rt@{ shape: rect, label: \"runtime/, agents/<br/>(unchanged)\" }\n    sp@{ shape: rect, label: \"spoken/<br/>derive, typed-units\" }\n    ia@{ shape: rect, label: \"images/<br/>acquire, svg, alt\" }\n    dm@{ shape: rect, label: \"describe/<br/>jobs, core, prompts\" }\n    tm@{ shape: rect, label: \"tts/modal\" }\n  end\n  led@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/ledger\" }\n  fcx@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Firecrawl\" }\n  aig@{ shape: cloud, label: \"AI Gateway\" }\n  imgb@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Images binding\" }\n  mx@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" }\n  r2@{ shape: cyl, label: \"R2\" }\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }\n  f --> fc --> fcx\n  l --> dq\n  rc --> rs --> rt --> aig\n  rc --> sp\n  im --> ia\n  ia --> imgb\n  ia --> r2\n  de --> dm --> aig\n  sy --> tm --> mx\n  steps -->|\"row writes\"| d1\n  f --> led\n  de --> led\n  sy --> led\n  led --> d1\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  class f,l,rc,im,de,sy,fc,dq,rs,rt,sp,ia,dm,tm,led flow\n  class r2,d1 store\n  class fcx,aig,imgb,mx ext\n```\n\nOnly the step files write to D1. The good-alt filter sits in images/alt and describe reads it too; a literal reading of CLAUDE.md would put it in common/.\n\n### 4.4 The lease\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  a[\"lease step:<br/>DomainQueue.acquire(id)\"] --> g{\"granted?\"}\n  g -->|yes| rec([\"recipe step\"])\n  g -->|no| w[\"waitForEvent<br/>lease wait n,<br/>lease-granted, 1 h\"]\n  w -->|\"event\"| rec\n  w -->|\"timeout, n < 3\"| rck[\"lease recheck n:<br/>acquire again\"]\n  rck --> g\n  w -. \"third timeout\" .-> fail([\"failed\"])\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class a,w,rck flow\n  class fail broken\n```\n\n### 4.5 The describe fan-out\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  rd[\"read units and title<br/>from the row\"] --> jobs[\"jobs in document order:<br/>code units, images whose<br/>alt fails the filter\"]\n  jobs --> cap{\"within the<br/>cap of 25?\"}\n  cap -->|no| floor[\"capped: floor or<br/>keep the fallback\"]\n  cap -->|yes| kids@{ shape: procs, label: \"step.do(describe i)<br/>3 x 1 min each,<br/>Promise.allSettled\" }\n  kids --> st{\"per child\"}\n  st -->|fulfilled| sent[\"Code: or Image:<br/>sentence\"]\n  st -->|rejected| floor\n  sent --> w[\"one D1 batch: units,<br/>degradations, a ledger<br/>row per success\"]\n  floor --> w\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class rd,jobs,kids,sent,floor,w flow\n```\n\n### 4.6 Files\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph del [\"deleted\"]\n    direction TB\n    d1@{ shape: rect, label: \"http/ routes, read,<br/>job-status\" }\n    d2@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/job-index\" }\n    d3@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/extraction,<br/>workflow/world\" }\n    d4@{ shape: rect, label: \"own lockfile and<br/>pnpm-workspace\" }\n    d5@{ shape: rect, label: \"tests: http, read-path,<br/>job-index, extraction,<br/>helpers/world, http\" }\n  end\n  subgraph tch [\"touched\"]\n    direction TB\n    t1@{ shape: rect, label: \"wrangler.jsonc: item<br/>workflow, D1, R2, IMAGES,<br/>workers_dev false\" }\n    t2@{ shape: rect, label: \"queue/domain-queue\" }\n    t3@{ shape: rect, label: \"cloudflare.ts, app.ts,<br/>vitest.config.ts,<br/>vite.config.ts\" }\n  end\n  subgraph nw [\"new\"]\n    direction TB\n    n1@{ shape: rect, label: \"workflow/item, wrapper,<br/>ledger, steps/*\" }\n    n2@{ shape: rect, label: \"firecrawl/, recipes/,<br/>spoken/, images/,<br/>describe/, tts/\" }\n    n3@{ shape: rect, label: \"test/cassettes<br/>(moved from api/)\" }\n  end\n  classDef new fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef touched fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef gone fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class n1,n2,n3 new\n  class t1,t2,t3 touched\n  class d1,d2,d3,d4,d5 gone\n```\n\nPorted from Python: firecrawl from fetch.py, recipes/store from recipes.py, spoken/ from extract.py, images/ from images.py, describe/ from describe.py, tts/ from tts.py. runtime/ and agents/ stay as they are.\n\n## 5 pipeline/: DomainQueue\n\n### 5.1 acquire, release, advance\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  acq([\"acquire(id)\"]) --> h{\"id holds<br/>the lease?\"}\n  h -->|yes| gt([\"granted\"])\n  h -->|no| fr{\"lease free and<br/>FIFO empty?\"}\n  fr -->|yes| take[\"write lease = id,<br/>alarm in 60 s\"] --> gt\n  fr -->|no| inq{\"id already<br/>in the FIFO?\"}\n  inq -->|yes| keep([\"not granted,<br/>keeps its place\"])\n  inq -->|no| app[\"append id\"] --> keep\n  rel([\"release(id)\"]) --> drop[\"drop id from FIFO;<br/>if it holds the lease,<br/>delete it\"] --> adv\n  alarm([\"alarm, 60 s\"]) --> st{\"holder ended<br/>or gone?\"}\n  st -->|yes| adv[\"advance: next id,<br/>status() check, lease,<br/>sendEvent lease-granted\"]\n  st -->|no| re[\"re-arm\"]\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class take,app,drop,adv,re flow\n```\n\nThe FIFO holds instance ids only, in the synchronous ctx.storage.kv, so acquire has no await. enqueue, stateOf, the params storage and the job index go.\n\n## 6 tts/: the two web endpoints\n\n### 6.1 start and result\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  wf@{ shape: rect, label: \"item Workflow\" }\n  subgraph modal [\"Modal app nagara-tts\"]\n    direction TB\n    web@{ shape: rect, label: \"web function, CPU:<br/>POST start,<br/>GET result\" }\n    k@{ shape: rect, label: \"Kokoro.synthesize<br/>(paragraphs, voice,<br/>destination)\" }\n  end\n  r2@{ shape: cyl, label: \"R2 audio/\" }\n  wf -->|\"start: paragraphs,<br/>voice, PUT URL<br/>Modal-Key, Modal-Secret\"| web\n  web -->|\"spawn\"| k\n  web -->|\"call_id\"| wf\n  k -->|\"PUT encoded audio\"| r2\n  wf -->|\"result?call_id\"| web\n  web -->|\"202 running · 200 format,<br/>duration, timings ·<br/>500 failed · 410 expired\"| wf\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  class wf flow\n  class web,k ext\n  class r2 store\n```\n\nBoth endpoints require proxy auth and take pydantic models. The result carries no audio bytes.\n\n## 7 Local development\n\n### 7.1 Launch\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  mig[\"1 common:<br/>migrate:local\"] --> st@{ shape: cyl, label: \".wrangler-state/<br/>D1, R2, DOs\" }\n  pipe[\"2 pipeline: pnpm dev<br/>vite, persistState\"] --- st\n  proxy[\"3 pipeline: dev:proxy<br/>/s3 to /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3\"] --> pipe\n  tun@{ shape: cloud, label: \"4 cloudflared<br/>quick tunnel\" } --> proxy\n  vars@{ shape: doc, label: \"pipeline/.dev.vars<br/>R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT =<br/>https://tunnel/s3\" }\n  vars -.-> pipe\n  api[\"5 api: pnpm dev<br/>wrangler --persist-to\"] --- st\n  api -->|\"create, restart\"| pipe\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" } -->|\"PUT\"| tun\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  class mig,proxy,vars tool\n  class st store\n  class tun,modal ext\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n```\n\nThe pipeline signs PUT URLs for R2_S3_ENDPOINT and swaps in R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT for Modal; in production the two are equal, so no code checks the environment.\n\n## 8 CI\n\n### 8.1 One Cloudflare workflow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    push([\"push to main\"]) --> ch[\"changes:<br/>paths-filter for<br/>common, pipeline, api\"]\n    ch --> cc[\"common checks:<br/>test, lint, types,<br/>api and pipeline types\"]\n    ch --> pc[\"pipeline checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    ch --> ac[\"api checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]\n    cc --> mig[\"migrate: wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply --remote\"]\n    mig --> pd[\"deploy pipeline:<br/>pnpm build,<br/>deploy dist config\"]\n    pc --> pd\n    pd --> ad[\"deploy api\"]\n    ac --> ad\n    cc -. \"a check fails\" .-> stop([\"nothing deploys\"])\n```\n\ncloudflare.yml replaces api.yml and pipeline.yml; tts.yml stays. A skipped job does not block the jobs after it, so a pipeline-only push deploys without a migration. The docs say three workflows.\n\n## 9 Standards\n\n### 9.1 Sources\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  cm@{ shape: doc, label: \"CLAUDE.md\" }\n  gl@{ shape: doc, label: \"global CLAUDE.md,<br/>mahou basics\" }\n  wk@{ shape: doc, label: \"wiki entries\" }\n  a1[\"shared types in common/,<br/>pydantic in tts/,<br/>invariants 2 to 8\"]\n  a2[\"== null, constant maps,<br/>one function per module,<br/>no comments in literals\"]\n  a3[\"workflows, vitest-plugin,<br/>r2, local-dev, images,<br/>ai-gateway, gemini,<br/>firecrawl, modal, flue,<br/>durable-objects, markdown,<br/>cassettes-over-mocks\"]\n  cm --> a1\n  gl --> a2\n  wk --> a3\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class cm,gl,wk tool\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e67d15bd-7083-47ad-a4f9-840672d71e44","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
