{"parentUuid":"e376d823-7a6e-40c2-9d34-92bad63aa667","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuszUauuA3kfB7SuiWZU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I applied all nine answers, and the program design is now settled. That covers the record in `program-design/nagara.md`, the diagram sources in `canvas.md`, and the canvas itself, where every part is now marked settled.\n\n**How I applied each answer:**\n- **2. Enqueue.** If creating the Workflow instance fails, the route marks the item `failed` with the create error and still returns the item. The row has no instance id, so a retry creates one.\n- **3. Poll steps.** Before, the Python API asked Modal for the result each time a client polled. Numbered `poll <n>` steps come from the item-workflow spike, which polled every 5 s. I set the interval back to 5 s to match the spike, which covers about 13.8 h of synthesis before the step limit. 10 s was my own number.\n- **4. Lease wait.** Each wait is now 5 minutes, with up to 3 waits and a re-check after each. An item now fails after about 15 minutes behind its domain's lease. If an earlier article's recipe step runs longer than that, for example a long authoring run plus retries, the item waiting behind it fails.\n- **5. Declared images.** That type didn't exist before. The Python code kept declared images in a private helper class inside one process, so they never reached the database. I've dropped the new type. The recipe step now hands the unacquired images to the images step as its step result, each with its src, alt and the text unit it follows. The row only ever holds finished units.\n- **6. Shared code.** I edited CLAUDE.md (uncommitted): `common/` now holds what both Workers use. Code that only pipeline modules share stays in the pipeline module it belongs to, and the others import it from there. The sanitize step that cleans up spoken text moved from `common/` to `pipeline/spoken/sanitize`, next to the alt-text filter in `images/alt`.\n\n**Docs these decisions contradict or don't cover yet.** Tell me which to update and I'll run one documentation pass:\n\n1. **item-lifecycle**\n   - the step wrapper writes the status as each attempt starts\n   - poll steps are named `poll <n>` and run every 5 s\n   - lease waits are 3 × 5 min with re-checks; the steps table now says 1 h\n   - the recipe step passes the declared images to the images step as its result\n   - the re-queue claims the row first, doesn't count toward the 3 retries, and restarts from `current_step`\n   - DomainQueue keeps an already-waiting item at its place in the queue\n   - an item whose instance can't be created fails at enqueue\n2. **item-contract:** `POST /items` returns the item as `failed` when the instance can't be created.\n3. **article-extraction:** the images not yet acquired pass from the recipe step to the images step as its step result, not on the row.\n4. **deployment-and-ci, plus the CI paragraph and invariant 8 in CLAUDE.md:** one `cloudflare.yml` with a job group per tree replaces the three workflows.\n5. **common-package:** it holds everything both Workers use, which replaces \"everything more than one module uses\".\n6. **tts-service:** the result endpoint answers 202 while running, 200 with the result, 500 when the synthesis failed, and 410 when the result has expired.\n7. **local-development:** the launch steps, meaning the local migration, the tunnel proxy, `cloudflared`, and `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` in `.dev.vars`.\n\nAfter the docs, I'll run /test-design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_read_input_tokens":279806,"output_tokens":1150,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1150,"cache_read_input_tokens":279806,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":519},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a94790c1-f9c2-4d91-8952-836e0b56be0d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuszUD6rHjbuL6CMpnRi","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d8e47da1-a5ac-44ac-a08b-67633f10392b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:15:11.341Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
