s, the whole deploy stops: common/'s CI workflow applies no migration, and neither W\ndocs/technical-design/invariants.md:23:| 5 | **No Worker imports the TTS code.** `tts/` is an image definition uploaded to Modal, not a library; the item Workflow reaches it over HTTP through two web endpoints behind Modal's proxy\ndocs/technical-design/item-contract.md:43:> A wire element carries `start` and `end`, and timing only exists once synthesis finishes. The item Workflow's recipe step writes the units into the row with `type`/`display`/`spoken` but\ndocs/technical-design/item-contract.md:50:| `GET /items/{id}` | Poll. Reads the item row and returns the current item; it never reads the Workflow instance. Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes: it \ndocs/technical-design/item-contract.md:81:`POST /items/{id}/retry` re-drives a failed item in place rather than re-enqueuing the URL. It refuses anything but a `failed` item, and a `failed` item past the retry cap, with `409`; `40\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:40:      s8@{ shape: rect, label: \"8 poll\" }\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:79:  read -.->|\"re-queue, queued<br/>over 15 min\"| wf\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:97:The client enqueues through the API Worker, which writes the row as `queued` and creates the item Workflow. fetch and lease run with the item `queued`; every later step runs with it `gene\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:110:| `queued_at` | when the item was last queued: set at enqueue and rewritten whenever the item is queued again, by a retry or by the re-queue of a stale `queued` item |\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:121:`units` and `degradations` are JSON columns, and common/ encodes and decodes them for both Workers. Audio bytes are never a column on this row; they live in the R2 bucket under the `audi\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:152:**Poll** reads the row and never the Workflow instance. When the row is `queued`