ra/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"8a0d9aa4-e2a8-47ad-85fe-5b6ea91117fa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b2952e36-1570-4ab7-9574-b5a0d1c40917","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SmWUguzr3dyxur6MhKC3J2","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:17 | rule 36 | \"the API queues the item again as it reads it\" | the API queues the item again when it reads the row\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:17 | rule 28 | \"It first claims the row with one conditional write that rewrites `queued_at` only while the row is still `queued` and its `queued_at` still that old, so two polls that arrive together queue it once.\" | It first claims the row with one conditional write. The write rewrites `queued_at` only if the row is still `queued` and `queued_at` is still more than 15 minutes old, so two polls that arrive together queue the item once.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:43 | rule 29 | \"the status the step is given\" | the status the Workflow passes to the step\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:51 | rule 28 | \"The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error, then restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, and returns `202`.\" | The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error. Through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, it restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates an instance when the row holds no instance id. It returns `202`.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:73 | rule 14 | \"Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes: one conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue it once, then the API restarts...\" | Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes. One conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue the item once. The API then restarts the item's instance from the step `current_step` names, or creates one when the row holds no instance id.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:97 | rule 28 | \"The wait for synthesis step asks the result endpoint for the call id every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5), and the store step writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length\" | The wait for synthesis step asks the result endpoint for the call id every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5). The store step then writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:97 | rule 14 | \"Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and wait for synthesis 15 minutes.\" | Each step gets 3 attempts. Start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt, and wait for synthesis has 15 minutes.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:101 | rule 32 | \"A result Modal has discarded, 7 days after the call, answers `410` and fails the item at once.\" | Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:150 | rule 28 | \"A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed; a job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the ones after it, so a push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys the pipeline without a migration.\" | A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed. A job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the jobs after it, so a push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys the pipeline without a migration.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:150 | rule 15 | \"with a **`deploy` job that depends on all three of its checks**, runs `modal deploy` and authenticates\" | `tts` keeps its own workflow. Its `deploy` job depends on all three of its checks, runs `modal deploy` and authenticates with `MODAL_TOKEN_ID` and `MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET`.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:208 | rule 33 | \"write its hostname into `pipeline/.dev.vars` as `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, `https://<hostname>/s3`\" | write `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<hostname>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`, with the tunnel's hostname in place of `<hostname>`\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:213 | rule 28 | \"It hands that URL to Modal with the endpoint in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>, in place of localhost's.\" | It hands that URL to Modal with localhost's endpoint replaced by the one in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The URL then holds the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:217 | rule 14 | \"the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes: when it reads the item, it restarts the item's instance and rewrites queued_at\" | the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes. When the API reads the item, it restarts the item's instance and rewrites queued_at\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:217 | rule 36 | \"the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item\" | the API re-queues the item the way the API re-queues any item\nTOTAL: 14","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"193fdf4a-e90c-4413-b514-9d993ccc5bde","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:24:05.686Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:17 | rule 36 | \"the API queues the item again as it reads it\" | the API queues the item again when it reads the row\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:17 | rule 28 | \"It first claims the row with one conditional write that rewrites `queued_at` only while the row is still `queued` and its `queued_at` still that old, so two polls that arrive together queue it once.\" | It first claims the row with one conditional write. The write rewrites `queued_at` only if the row is still `queued` and `queued_at` is still more than 15 minutes old, so two polls that arrive together queue the item once.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:43 | rule 29 | \"the status the step is given\" | the status the Workflow passes to the step\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:51 | rule 28 | \"The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error, then restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, and returns `202`.\" | The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error. Through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, it restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates an instance when the row holds no instance id. It returns `202`.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:73 | rule 14 | \"Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes: one conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue it once, then the API restarts...\" | Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes. One conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue the item once. The API then restarts the item's instance from the step `current_step` names, or creates one when the row holds no instance id.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:97 | rule 28 | \"The wait for synthesis step asks the result endpoint for the call id every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5), and the store step writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length\" | The wait for synthesis step asks the result endpoint for the call id every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5). The store step then writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:97 | rule 14 | \"Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and wait for synthesis 15 minutes.\" | Each step gets 3 attempts. Start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt, and wait for synthesis has 15 minutes.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:101 | rule 32 | \"A result Modal has discarded, 7 days after the call, answers `410` and fails the item at once.\" | Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:150 | rule 28 | \"A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed; a job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the ones after it, so a push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys the pipeline without a migration.\" | A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed. A job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the jobs after it, so a push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys the pipeline without a migration.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:150 | rule 15 | \"with a **`deploy` job that depends on all three of its checks**, runs `modal deploy` and authenticates\" | `tts` keeps its own workflow. Its `deploy` job depends on all three of its checks, runs `modal deploy` and authenticates with `MODAL_TOKEN_ID` and `MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET`.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:208 | rule 33 | \"write its hostname into `pipeline/.dev.vars` as `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, `https://<hostname>/s3`\" | write `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<hostname>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`, with the tunnel's hostname in place of `<hostname>`\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:213 | rule 28 | \"It hands that URL to Modal with the endpoint in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>, in place of localhost's.\" | It hands that URL to Modal with localhost's endpoint replaced by the one in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The URL then holds the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>.\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:217 | rule 14 | \"the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes: when it reads the item, it restarts the item's instance and rewrites queued_at\" | the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes. When the API reads the item, it restarts the item's instance and rewrites queued_at\n/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md:217 | rule 36 | \"the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item\" | the API re-queues the item the way the API re-queues any item\nTOTAL: 14","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a971096d-f844-4ccb-8672-89b998a6c73e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a0d9aa4-e2a8-47ad-85fe-5b6ea91117fa","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
