{"parentUuid":"e721bf01-8b73-439d-bc07-05bb67cc4d90","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfutgjJZC4JLE8rnxKYyt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U16PEvcfTA8wkk9nu62d2K","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='program-design-amendments.md'; s=open(p).read()\nR=[\n(\"When the row is `queued` and its `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, the API queues the item again as it reads it. It first claims the row with one conditional write that rewrites `queued_at` only while the row is still `queued` and its `queued_at` still that old, so two polls that arrive together queue it once.\",\n \"When the row is `queued` and its `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, the API queues the item again when it reads the row. It first claims the row with one conditional write. The write rewrites `queued_at` only if the row is still `queued` and `queued_at` is still more than 15 minutes old, so two polls that arrive together queue the item once.\"),\n(\"The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error, then restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, and returns `202`.\",\n \"The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error. Through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, it restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates an instance when the row holds no instance id. It returns `202`.\"),\n(\"Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes: one conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue it once, then the API restarts the item's instance from the step `current_step` names, or creates one when the row holds no instance id.\",\n \"Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes. One conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue the item once. The API then restarts the item's instance from the step `current_step` names, or creates one when the row holds no instance id.\"),\n(\"every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5), and the store step writes\",\"every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5). The store step then writes\"),\n(\"Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and wait for synthesis 15 minutes.\",\"Each step gets 3 attempts. Start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt, and wait for synthesis has 15 minutes.\"),\n(\"A result Modal has discarded, 7 days after the call, answers `410` and fails the item at once.\",\"Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.\"),\n(\"A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed; a job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the ones after it,\",\"A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed. A job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the jobs after it,\"),\n(\"and write its hostname into `pipeline/.dev.vars` as `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, `https://<hostname>/s3`.\",\"and write `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<hostname>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`, with the tunnel's hostname in place of `<hostname>`.\"),\n(\"2. It hands that URL to Modal with the endpoint in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>, in place of localhost's.\",\"2. It hands that URL to Modal with localhost's endpoint replaced by the one in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The URL then holds the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>.\"),\n(\"and the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes: when it reads the item, it restarts\",\"and the API re-queues the item the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes. When the API reads the item, it restarts\"),\n]\nfor a,b in R:\n    assert a in s, a[:50]; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\necho ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2490,"cache_read_input_tokens":313733,"output_tokens":1562,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":123},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2490,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1562,"cache_read_input_tokens":313733,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2490},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01U16PEvcfTA8wkk9nu62d2K":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='program-design-amendments.md'; s=open(p).read()\nR=[\n(\"When the row is `queued` and its `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, the API queues the item again as it reads it. It first claims the row with one conditional write that rewrites `queued_at` only while the row is still `queued` and its `queued_at` still that old, so two polls that arrive together queue it once.\",\n \"When the row is `queued` and its `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, the API queues the item again when it reads the row. It first claims the row with one conditional write. The write rewrites `queued_at` only if the row is still `queued` and `queued_at` is still more than 15 minutes old, so two polls that arrive together queue the item once.\"),\n(\"The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error, then restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, and returns `202`.\",\n \"The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error. Through the same Workflow binding enqueue uses, it restarts the item's instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates an instance when the row holds no instance id. It returns `202`.\"),\n(\"Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes: one conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue it once, then the API restarts the item's instance from the step `current_step` names, or creates one when the row holds no instance id.\",\n \"Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes. One conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue the item once. The API then restarts the item's instance from the step `current_step` names, or creates one when the row holds no instance id.\"),\n(\"every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5), and the store step writes\",\"every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5). The store step then writes\"),\n(\"Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and wait for synthesis 15 minutes.\",\"Each step gets 3 attempts. Start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt, and wait for synthesis has 15 minutes.\"),\n(\"A result Modal has discarded, 7 days after the call, answers `410` and fails the item at once.\",\"Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.\"),\n(\"A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed; a job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the ones after it,\",\"A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed. A job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the jobs after it,\"),\n(\"and write its hostname into `pipeline/.dev.vars` as `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, `https://<hostname>/s3`.\",\"and write `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<hostname>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`, with the tunnel's hostname in place of `<hostname>`.\"),\n(\"2. It hands that URL to Modal with the endpoint in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`, the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>, in place of localhost's.\",\"2. It hands that URL to Modal with localhost's endpoint replaced by the one in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The URL then holds the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>.\"),\n(\"and the API re-queues it the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes: when it reads the item, it restarts\",\"and the API re-queues the item the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes. When the API reads the item, it restarts\"),\n]\nfor a,b in R:\n    assert a in s, a[:50]; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\necho ok"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a15aa11-b239-4bdf-9255-27629eb62f09","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfutgirXDy59kLGdbPSYL","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1af2505b-989b-4b09-8275-ce7dda90d626","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:24:17.656Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
