{"parentUuid":"1f96e9e2-c369-4d48-8e5f-c338d8c644aa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"768b5f33-50c6-49f2-88f3-4be4e3a8fdd2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014vZwdXt49ULmayY4XsLRFr","type":"tool_result","content":"**Findings** (11, ordered by how much each affects)\n\n1. **common-package.md, \"Checking the shared types at build time\"**: the location line does not match. \"Second and third sentences of the first paragraph\" is wrong. The first paragraph (line 72) has two sentences, and \"When either check fails…\" and \"When both pass…\" are sentences 2 and 3 of the second paragraph (line 74).\n\n2. **tts-service.md, paragraph after the sequence diagram**: the location line does not match. The paragraph has five sentences, and \"Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and each poll 1 minute\" is the fifth. Replacing only the third and fourth sentences leaves that sentence in place next to the replacement's own \"Each step gets 3 attempts…\" sentence. The target should be sentences 3 to 5.\n\n3. **invariants.md lines 25 and 26 are not amended.** Invariants 7 and 8 still say \"`common/`'s CI workflow applies them\" and describe three workflows. The draft changes the CLAUDE.md CI paragraph, but not the invariants. The root `CLAUDE.md` says that if the two disagree, fix both. The `deployment-and-ci` row in `technical-design/README.md` is still accurate.\n\n4. **item-lifecycle.md, \"The step wrapper\"**: the replacement for sentences 2 and 3 drops the sentence saying fetch and lease are given `queued` and every later step `generating`. The new text refers to \"the status the step is given\", and nothing in the note now defines it. Charter, \"A note explains how one part works\": the mechanism has to stay in the note.\n\n5. **item-lifecycle.md, \"🟢 States\" diagram**: not amended. The new enqueue failure writes `failed` directly, but the diagram has only `[*] --> queued`, and `queued --> failed` is described as \"fetch or lease uses all its attempts\". The same gap appears in the \"What a failure names\" intro, which says `current_step` names the failed step, while the new \"Instance not created\" bullet leaves it empty. Charter, \"A note describes the present\": the note should be consistent with itself.\n\n6. **article-extraction.md, images edit**: the replacement makes the images step a separate Workflow step with its own step result. The surrounding text still says steps 1 to 5 run at the end of the recipe step, and the flowchart still places 6 to 8 in one flow (\"Write the units into the item row\" is step 8). The edit does not say which Workflow step runs steps 7 and 8. The flowchart and the surrounding paragraph need the same change.\n\n7. **item-lifecycle.md, \"What a failure names\"**: \"add one after them\" is ambiguous. Below \"Result expired\" there is also a \"Storage failure on finalize\" bullet. The draft should say where the new bullet goes.\n\n8. **item-lifecycle.md, Modeling edit**: the target sentence is in the paragraph after the field table, which is the third paragraph under the heading, not \"the first paragraph under Modeling\". The sentence text itself matches.\n\n9. **item-lifecycle.md, callout \"Why waiting for synthesis is one step\"**: this describes an alternative not taken (a loop of separate polling steps) under a NOTE. The charter's TIP kind is for \"an alternative considered and not taken\". Split it into a NOTE for the choice and a TIP for the rejected loop.\n\n10. **deployment-and-ci.md, callout \"Why one workflow for the Cloudflare side\"**: same issue. The \"separate workflows cannot [wait]\" clause is a rejected alternative, so it belongs in a TIP.\n\n11. **local-development.md, new \"🚀 Starting it\" section**: the heading names an action, where the charter prefers \"a heading that could answer a question someone typed into search\". The numbered command list is a runbook, and the charter says a note explains how a part works. I could not check `pnpm migrate:local`, `pnpm dev:proxy` or `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` against the code, because `common/` and the `package.json` scripts are not in this working tree.\n\nThe other locations match the current text: the item-lifecycle edits (enqueue, poll, DomainQueue, retry, steps table), the item-contract rows and \"Retry\" paragraph, the deployment-and-ci replacements and warning, the common-package overview, diagram, table and paragraph targets, the persistence-and-storage sentence, the local-development step 2 and \"Re-queuing a stuck item\" paragraph, and the CLAUDE.md span. The new headings keep the emoji, the callout kinds are the charter's three, and mermaid is used for the new diagram. The edits are in the present tense, one line per paragraph, with no history language.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d9c8fe1d-9822-4270-accb-1a19fd7db12c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:24:48.731Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**Findings** (11, ordered by how much each affects)\n\n1. **common-package.md, \"Checking the shared types at build time\"**: the location line does not match. \"Second and third sentences of the first paragraph\" is wrong. The first paragraph (line 72) has two sentences, and \"When either check fails…\" and \"When both pass…\" are sentences 2 and 3 of the second paragraph (line 74).\n\n2. **tts-service.md, paragraph after the sequence diagram**: the location line does not match. The paragraph has five sentences, and \"Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and each poll 1 minute\" is the fifth. Replacing only the third and fourth sentences leaves that sentence in place next to the replacement's own \"Each step gets 3 attempts…\" sentence. The target should be sentences 3 to 5.\n\n3. **invariants.md lines 25 and 26 are not amended.** Invariants 7 and 8 still say \"`common/`'s CI workflow applies them\" and describe three workflows. The draft changes the CLAUDE.md CI paragraph, but not the invariants. The root `CLAUDE.md` says that if the two disagree, fix both. The `deployment-and-ci` row in `technical-design/README.md` is still accurate.\n\n4. **item-lifecycle.md, \"The step wrapper\"**: the replacement for sentences 2 and 3 drops the sentence saying fetch and lease are given `queued` and every later step `generating`. The new text refers to \"the status the step is given\", and nothing in the note now defines it. Charter, \"A note explains how one part works\": the mechanism has to stay in the note.\n\n5. **item-lifecycle.md, \"🟢 States\" diagram**: not amended. The new enqueue failure writes `failed` directly, but the diagram has only `[*] --> queued`, and `queued --> failed` is described as \"fetch or lease uses all its attempts\". The same gap appears in the \"What a failure names\" intro, which says `current_step` names the failed step, while the new \"Instance not created\" bullet leaves it empty. Charter, \"A note describes the present\": the note should be consistent with itself.\n\n6. **article-extraction.md, images edit**: the replacement makes the images step a separate Workflow step with its own step result. The surrounding text still says steps 1 to 5 run at the end of the recipe step, and the flowchart still places 6 to 8 in one flow (\"Write the units into the item row\" is step 8). The edit does not say which Workflow step runs steps 7 and 8. The flowchart and the surrounding paragraph need the same change.\n\n7. **item-lifecycle.md, \"What a failure names\"**: \"add one after them\" is ambiguous. Below \"Result expired\" there is also a \"Storage failure on finalize\" bullet. The draft should say where the new bullet goes.\n\n8. **item-lifecycle.md, Modeling edit**: the target sentence is in the paragraph after the field table, which is the third paragraph under the heading, not \"the first paragraph under Modeling\". The sentence text itself matches.\n\n9. **item-lifecycle.md, callout \"Why waiting for synthesis is one step\"**: this describes an alternative not taken (a loop of separate polling steps) under a NOTE. The charter's TIP kind is for \"an alternative considered and not taken\". Split it into a NOTE for the choice and a TIP for the rejected loop.\n\n10. **deployment-and-ci.md, callout \"Why one workflow for the Cloudflare side\"**: same issue. The \"separate workflows cannot [wait]\" clause is a rejected alternative, so it belongs in a TIP.\n\n11. **local-development.md, new \"🚀 Starting it\" section**: the heading names an action, where the charter prefers \"a heading that could answer a question someone typed into search\". The numbered command list is a runbook, and the charter says a note explains how a part works. I could not check `pnpm migrate:local`, `pnpm dev:proxy` or `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` against the code, because `common/` and the `package.json` scripts are not in this working tree.\n\nThe other locations match the current text: the item-lifecycle edits (enqueue, poll, DomainQueue, retry, steps table), the item-contract rows and \"Retry\" paragraph, the deployment-and-ci replacements and warning, the common-package overview, diagram, table and paragraph targets, the persistence-and-storage sentence, the local-development step 2 and \"Re-queuing a stuck item\" paragraph, and the CLAUDE.md span. The new headings keep the emoji, the callout kinds are the charter's three, and mermaid is used for the new diagram. The edits are in the present tense, one line per paragraph, with no history language.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ceb0076a-f21e-4ba7-850b-4951d2f818c4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"