m","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"9131de13-d609-4aa2-8243-4cdb9fd778c4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"768b5f33-50c6-49f2-88f3-4be4e3a8fdd2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012RLbY4Eo86zbGSWvREwwer","type":"tool_result","content":"| 7 | **A schema change is a migration.** Hand-written SQL migrations in `common/` own the D1 schema, and `common/`'s CI workflow applies them with wrangler before either Worker deploys. The Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying the same migrations, so the suite exercises the migration path itself. | [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md), [common-package](common-package.md) |\n| 8 | **The three deployables ship separately, and no CI pipeline runs on another's tree except `common/`'s.** GitHub Actions path filters enforce this. A change to `common/` runs the type checks of both Workers, and the Cloudflare side deploys in a fixed order: `common/`'s migrations, then the pipeline Worker, then the API Worker. | [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md) |\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> queued : the API writes it at enqueue\n    queued --> generating : the Workflow holds its domain's lease\n    generating --> ready : store finishes\n    queued --> failed : fetch or lease uses all its attempts\n    generating --> failed : a step uses all its attempts, or the page is not an article\n    failed --> queued : a client retries, at most 3 times\n    ready --> [*]\n## 🏷️ What a failure names\n\nEvery `failed` item carries the failed step's own error, with no phase prefix, and its `current_step` names the step that failed, so a reader can place a failure without a stack trace. An item fails when a step uses all 3 of its attempts, and in these cases:\n\nThe shared types are checked when the code builds and deploys, never at runtime. A value read back from D1 or received from Modal is trusted to match its type, and nothing parses it against a schema.\n\nA change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/ against it in CI. When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: common/'s CI workflow applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys. When both pass, common/'s CI workflow applies the migrations to D1 with wrangler, and the pipeline and API workflows wait for it to succeed before they continue; the pipeline Worker deploys before the API Worker. [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md) holds that order.\nThe item Workflow's start synthesis step signs the PUT URL and calls the start endpoint, which spawns the synthesis and answers with Modal's call id at once (1, 2). Modal uploads the audio to the bucket when the synthesis finishes (3). The poll step asks the result endpoint for the call id until the result is ready (4, 5), and the store step writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). The call id and the result pass from step to step as step results; the item row holds neither. Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and each poll 1 minute.\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"The recipe returns<br/>a title and<br/>display units\"]) --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"For each recipe unit,<br/>in document order\"]\n        direction TB\n        kind{\"Image unit?\"}\n        kind -->|No| spoken[\"1 Derive the spoken<br/>form from the display\"]\n        spoken --> test{\"2 Drop rule<br/>matches?\"}\n        test -->|Yes| drop[\"3 Drop: no typed unit\"]\n        test -->|No| keep[\"4 Keep as a typed<br/>paragraph or code unit\"]\n        kind -->|Yes| stash[\"5 Hold it after the<br/>last kept text unit\"]\n    end\n    loop --> acquire[\"6 Acquire held images,<br/>interleave with kept units\"]\n    acquire --> any{\"7 Any unit survives?\"}\n    any -. no .-> fail([\"Fail the item:<br/>no surviving units\"])\n    any -->|Yes| write[\"8 Write the units<br/>into the item row\"]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"699195f2-e61c-4014-a5f3-6a5f610890da","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:25:02.714Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"| 7 | **A schema change is a migration.** Hand-written SQL migrations in `common/` own the D1 schema, and `common/`'s CI workflow applies them with wrangler before either Worker deploys. The Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying the same migrations, so the suite exercises the migration path itself. | [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md), [common-package](common-package.md) |\n| 8 | **The three deployables ship separately, and no CI pipeline runs on another's tree except `common/`'s.** GitHub Actions path filters enforce this. A change to `common/` runs the type checks of both Workers, and the Cloudflare side deploys in a fixed order: `common/`'s migrations, then the pipeline Worker, then the API Worker. | [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md) |\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> queued : the API writes it at enqueue\n    queued --> generating : the Workflow holds its domain's lease\n    generating --> ready : store finishes\n    queued --> failed : fetch or lease uses all its attempts\n    generating --> failed : a step uses all its attempts, or the page is not an article\n    failed --> queued : a client retries, at most 3 times\n    ready --> [*]\n## 🏷️ What a failure names\n\nEvery `failed` item carries the failed step's own error, with no phase prefix, and its `current_step` names the step that failed, so a reader can place a failure without a stack trace. An item fails when a step uses all 3 of its attempts, and in these cases:\n\nThe shared types are checked when the code builds and deploys, never at runtime. A value read back from D1 or received from Modal is trusted to match its type, and nothing parses it against a schema.\n\nA change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/ against it in CI. When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: common/'s CI workflow applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys. When both pass, common/'s CI workflow applies the migrations to D1 with wrangler, and the pipeline and API workflows wait for it to succeed before they continue; the pipeline Worker deploys before the API Worker. [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md) holds that order.\nThe item Workflow's start synthesis step signs the PUT URL and calls the start endpoint, which spawns the synthesis and answers with Modal's call id at once (1, 2). Modal uploads the audio to the bucket when the synthesis finishes (3). The poll step asks the result endpoint for the call id until the result is ready (4, 5), and the store step writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). The call id and the result pass from step to step as step results; the item row holds neither. Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and each poll 1 minute.\nflowchart TD\n    start([\"The recipe returns<br/>a title and<br/>display units\"]) --> loop\n    subgraph loop [\"For each recipe unit,<br/>in document order\"]\n        direction TB\n        kind{\"Image unit?\"}\n        kind -->|No| spoken[\"1 Derive the spoken<br/>form from the display\"]\n        spoken --> test{\"2 Drop rule<br/>matches?\"}\n        test -->|Yes| drop[\"3 Drop: no typed unit\"]\n        test -->|No| keep[\"4 Keep as a typed<br/>paragraph or code unit\"]\n        kind -->|Yes| stash[\"5 Hold it after the<br/>last kept text unit\"]\n    end\n    loop --> acquire[\"6 Acquire held images,<br/>interleave with kept units\"]\n    acquire --> any{\"7 Any unit survives?\"}\n    any -. no .-> fail([\"Fail the item:<br/>no surviving units\"])\n    any -->|Yes| write[\"8 Write the units<br/>into the item row\"]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"43424533-78a4-407b-bb4d-fa0f90e9922c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9131de13-d609-4aa2-8243-4cdb9fd778c4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
