{"parentUuid":"f1f540f5-356d-479d-8607-9d079b3b07ba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfutkwd5ZNf8f5zMEebvr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LQ8F17Z4CWxsVAPFSqFA6J","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='program-design-amendments.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]; s=s.replace(a,b)\n# 8\nrep(\"Replace the last sentence of the first paragraph under \\\"Modeling\\\" (after the field table):\",\"Replace the last sentence of the third paragraph under \\\"Modeling\\\", after the field table:\")\n# 4\nrep(\"\"\"Replace the second and third sentences of the first paragraph under \"The step wrapper\":\n\nAt the start of each attempt, inside the step, the wrapper writes `current_step` and the status the step is given, and clears the error, so a restart from that step writes them again.\"\"\",\"\"\"Replace the second sentence of the first paragraph under \"The step wrapper\", keeping the sentence after it:\n\nAt the start of each attempt, inside the step, the wrapper writes `current_step` and the status the step is given, and clears the error, so a restart from that step writes them again.\"\"\")\n# 5 states diagram\nrep(\"\"\"New callout after the \"Poll\" paragraph:\"\"\",\"\"\"\"States\" diagram, a transition added after `[*] --> queued`:\n\n    [*] --> failed : creating the Workflow instance fails\n\nNew callout after the \"Poll\" paragraph:\"\"\")\n# 7 + 5 failure intro\nrep('''\"What a failure names\", replace the \"Synthesis that fails every time\" and \"Result expired\" bullets and add one after them:''','''\"What a failure names\", replace the first sentence of the paragraph under the heading:\n\nEvery `failed` item carries the failed step's own error, with no phase prefix, and its `current_step` names the step that failed, so a reader can place a failure without a stack trace; `current_step` is empty only when the instance was never created.\n\n\"What a failure names\", replace the \"Synthesis that fails every time\" and \"Result expired\" bullets, and add the \"Instance not created\" bullet between \"Result expired\" and \"Storage failure on finalize\":''')\n# 9\nrep(\"\"\"> [!NOTE] Why waiting for synthesis is one step\n> The Workflow replays a step's stored result by the step's name, so a loop of separate polling steps would need a new name for every round. One step that asks Modal every 5 seconds inside its own body keeps one name in `current_step`, and a retry restarts it without starting a second synthesis.\"\"\",\"\"\"> [!NOTE] Why waiting for synthesis is one step\n> One step that asks Modal every 5 seconds inside its own body keeps one name in `current_step`, and a retry restarts it without starting a second synthesis.\n\n> [!TIP] Rejected: a loop of polling steps\n> The Workflow replays a step's stored result by the step's name, so each round of a polling loop needs a step name of its own, and `current_step` would carry a round number instead of the step's name.\"\"\")\n# 10\nrep(\"\"\"> [!NOTE] Why one workflow for the Cloudflare side\n> The deploys depend on each other: the migrations go first and the API Worker last. Jobs in one workflow can wait on each other within a push, and separate workflows cannot without polling one another.\"\"\",\"\"\"> [!NOTE] Why one workflow for the Cloudflare side\n> The deploys depend on each other: the migrations go first and the API Worker last. Jobs in one workflow wait on each other within a push.\n\n> [!TIP] Rejected: one workflow per tree\n> Separate workflows cannot wait on each other within a push without polling one another, so the pipeline and API deploys could not wait for the migrations.\"\"\")\n# 2\nrep(\"Replace the third and fourth sentences of the paragraph after the sequence diagram:\",\"Replace the third, fourth and fifth sentences of the paragraph after the sequence diagram:\")\n# 1\nrep('Replace the second and third sentences of the first paragraph under \"Checking the shared types at build time\":','Replace the second and third sentences of the second paragraph under \"Checking the shared types at build time\":')\n# 11\nrep(\"## 🚀 Starting it\",\"## 🚀 How to run both Workers locally\")\n# 6 article-extraction\nrep(\"\"\"Replace the sentence \"Step 6, the images step, acquires the held images and drops any that will not acquire (see below).\" in the paragraph after the units flowchart:\n\nThe recipe step hands the held images to the images step as its step result, each with its src, its alt and the kept unit it follows, so the row holds only finished units. Step 6, the images step, acquires them, places each after its unit and drops any that will not acquire (see below).\"\"\",\"\"\"Units flowchart, the loop's label and steps 6 to 8 grouped as the images step:\n\n    subgraph loop [\"Recipe step: each recipe<br/>unit, in document order\"]\n\n    subgraph images [\"Images step\"]\n        direction TB\n        acquire[\"6 Acquire held images,<br/>interleave with kept units\"]\n        acquire --> any{\"7 Any unit survives?\"}\n        any -->|Yes| write[\"8 Write the units<br/>into the item row\"]\n    end\n    loop --> acquire\n    any -. no .-> fail([\"Fail the item:<br/>no surviving units\"])\n\nReplace the sentences from \"Step 6, the images step, acquires\" to \"the later steps read them from there.\" in the paragraph after the units flowchart:\n\nThe recipe step writes the kept text units into the item row and hands the held images to the images step as its step result, each with its src, its alt and the kept unit it follows, so the row holds only finished units. Steps 6 to 8 run in the images step. It acquires the held images, places each after its unit and drops any that will not acquire (see below). It fails the item when no unit survives. It writes the full list and the degradations into the item row, and the later steps read them from there.\"\"\")\n# 3 invariants\nrep(\"\"\"---\n\n**CLAUDE.md**\"\"\",\"\"\"---\n\n**docs/technical-design/invariants.md**\n\nTable, row 7, replace \"and `common/`'s CI workflow applies them with wrangler before either Worker deploys\" with:\n\nand the Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job applies them with wrangler before either Worker deploys\n\nTable, row 8, replace the last sentence of the invariant column:\n\nA change to `common/` runs the type checks of both Workers, and one Cloudflare workflow deploys in a fixed order: `common/`'s migrations, then the pipeline Worker, then the API Worker.\n\n---\n\n**CLAUDE.md**\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^    subgraph\\|loop -->\" program-design-amendments.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2695,"cache_read_input_tokens":322560,"output_tokens":2512,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":288},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2512,"cache_read_input_tokens":322560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LQ8F17Z4CWxsVAPFSqFA6J":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='program-design-amendments.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]; s=s.replace(a,b)\n# 8\nrep(\"Replace the last sentence of the first paragraph under \\\"Modeling\\\" (after the field table):\",\"Replac