t fails every time\\|Result expired\\|Storage failure on finalize\\|longer than the lease step\\|s8@\" item-lifecycle.md | cut -c1-140; sed -n 223,226p item-lifecycle.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1cf8c5d5-156d-4f4b-8e43-da656df10226","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfutyqx93cp1MEDNnJEaN","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0b647fb3-20fc-4b62-9d3e-a64b9e3a1da2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:28:02.696Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"0b647fb3-20fc-4b62-9d3e-a64b9e3a1da2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"75d77dd3-3a53-474d-af79-0de70ba1a2eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019fGDnuubYjsw2p7gxWd7mm","type":"tool_result","content":"40:      s8@{ shape: rect, label: \"8 poll\" }\n121:`units` and `degradations` are JSON columns, and common/ encodes and decodes them for both Workers. Audio bytes are never a column on th\n176:    s8@{ shape: rect, label: \"8 poll\" }\n211:| lease | waits for the domain's lease from DomainQueue through `waitForEvent` | 1 h |\n217:| poll | asks Modal for the result until it is ready | 1 min per poll |\n222:> [!NOTE] Why the units live on the row and the HTML in a step result\n230:Every step runs inside one wrapper holding the logic common to all of them. As a step starts, the wrapper writes `current_step` and the \n273:The release step is the fast path; the alarm is the backstop for an item whose Workflow never runs it. Acquiring the lease sets an alarm\n295:`POST /items/{id}/retry` re-drives a `failed` item. The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error, then restarts \n311:Every `failed` item carries the failed step's own error, with no phase prefix, and its `current_step` names the step that failed, so a r\n315:- **Synthesis that fails every time**: the poll step uses its attempts on a crashed synthesis and fails the item.\n316:- **Result expired**: Modal holds a synthesis result for 7 days; a poll after that fails the item.\n317:- **Storage failure on finalize**: synthesis completes, but writing the finished state fails; the store step fails the item rather than \n319:No time limit bounds a whole item. An item that waits for its domain's lease longer than the lease step's 3 attempts of 1 h each fails l\n> A step result is capped near 1 MiB, and the Workflow keeps it so a later step, and a restart from a later step, can read it. The fetched HTML is needed only by the recipe step, so it rides as fetch's step result. The units are read and changed by several steps, so they sit on the row, and each step that changes them writes them there.\n\n> [!WARNING] A step can run twice\n> A deploy can interrupt a step mid-attempt, and the Workflow runs it again. Modal accepts no idempotency key, so a start synthesis that runs again synthesizes a second time; the second upload overwrites the same audio key, because the key is the item id. The duplicate costs one synthesis and is accepted.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a8b7a00f-bd56-4804-9405-b8a4c8d5ad94","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:28:03.251Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"40:      s8@{ shape: rect, label: \"8 poll\" }\n121:`units` and `degradations` are JSON columns, and common/ encodes and decodes them for both Workers. Audio bytes are never a column on th\n176:    s8@{ shape: rect, label: \"8 poll\" }\n211:| lease | waits for the domain's lease from DomainQueue through `waitForEvent` | 1 h |\n217:| poll | asks Modal for the result until it is ready | 1 min per poll |\n222:> [!NOTE] Why the units live on the row and the HTML in a step result\n230:Every step runs inside one wrapper holding the logic common to all of them. As a step starts, the wrapper writes `current_step` and the \n273:The release step is the fast path; the alarm is the backstop for an item whose Workflow never runs it. Acquiring the lease sets an alarm\n295:`POST /items/{id}/retry` re-drives a `failed` item. The route writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at` and clears the error, then restarts \n311:Every `failed` item carries the failed step's own error, with no phase prefix, and its `current_step` names the step that failed, so a r\n315:- **Synthesis that fails every time**: the poll step uses its attempts on a crashed synthesis and fails the item.\n316:- **Result expired**: Modal holds a synthesis result for 7 days; a poll after that fails the item.\n317:- **Storage failure on finalize**: synthesis completes, but writing the finished state fails; the store step fails the item rather than \n319:No time limit bounds a whole item. An item that waits for its domain's lease longer than the lease step's 3 attempts of 1 h each fails l\n> A step result is capped near 1 MiB, and the Workflow keeps it so a later step, and a restart from a later step, can read it. The fetched HTML is needed only by the recipe step, so it rides as fetch's step result. The units are read and changed by several steps, so they sit on the row, and each step that changes them writes them there.\n\n> [!WARNING] A step can run twice\n> A deploy can interrupt a step mid-attempt, and the Workflow runs it again. Modal accepts no idempotency key, so a start synthesis that runs again synthesizes a second time; the second upload overwrites the same audio key, because the key is the item id. The duplicate costs one synthesis and is accepted.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1cf8c5d5-156d-4f4b-8e43-da656df10226","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0b647fb3-20fc-4b62-9d3e-a64b9e3a1da2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"s