{"parentUuid":"30893543-69c5-4db1-aa56-cd43d0e1712b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"75d77dd3-3a53-474d-af79-0de70ba1a2eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3cW5CMiEnSg9HGkL9F2RW","type":"tool_result","content":"49:| `POST /items` | Create an item from `{url, voice?}`. Writes the item row at `queued`, then creates the item's Workflow instance with the item id, and returns `202` with the item at `queued`; the item Workflow does the rest (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)). |\n81:`POST /items/{id}/retry` re-drives a failed item in place rather than re-enqueuing the URL. It refuses anything but a\nThe schema is a set of hand-written SQL migrations in [common/](common-package.md). common/'s own CI job applies them to D1 with wrangler before the pipeline Worker and the API Worker deploy, and the pipeline and API workflows wait for that job to succeed, so neither Worker ever runs against a schema older than its code (see [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md)). Deploys are not made twice in quick succession, so two migration runs never overlap. Locally, the developer applies the same migrations with wrangler to the D1 database in the shared state folder (see [local-development](local-development.md)), and the Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying them too.\n11:common/ is the TypeScript package that api/ and pipeline/ both build from, and it holds everything more than one module uses: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, item row reads and writes, the hand-written SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library the integration tests us\n32:  mig -->|\"applied by common/'s CI job\"| d1\n47:The API Worker and the pipeline Worker import common/ at build time. common/'s CI workflow applies the SQL migrations to D1, and both Workers' tests apply the same migrations to build their own D1 schema. The replay library runs only inside both Workers' integration tests.\n63:| SQL migrations | the D1 schema, as hand-written SQL files | common/'s CI workflow, both Workers' tests, local development | [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md), [local-development](local-development.md) |\n74:A change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/ against it in CI. When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: common/'s CI workflow applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys. When both pass, common/'s CI workflow applies the migrations to D1 with wrangler, and the pipel\n> The API Worker creates and restarts the item Workflow through the cross-script Workflow binding, and nothing else calls the pipeline. With no route to reach, the pipeline Worker carries no authentication of its own and no edge policy guards it.\n95:Each tree runs **test, lint and types as three parallel jobs** on pushes to `main`, path-filtered\n100:> Nothing serializes two runs of `common/`'s workflow, so two pushes to `main` in quick successi\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal TTS\" }\n  ext@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Firecrawl,<br/>AI Gateway\" }\n  api -->|\"create, restart\"| pipe\n  api --- state\n  pipe --- state\n  pipe -->|\"scrape, describe,<br/>agents\"| ext\n  pipe -->|\"start: PUT URL with<br/>the tunnel's hostname\"| modal\n59:2. It hands that URL to Modal with the quick tunnel's hostname, which it reads from its configuration, in place of localhost and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a9b3725f-ae68-4b5a-ad9e-a197de70a74b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:28:27.244Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"49:| `POST /items` | Create an item from `{url, voice?}`. Writes the item row at `queued`, then creates the item's Workflow instance with the item id, and returns `202` with the item at `queued`; the item Workflow does the rest (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)). |\n81:`POST /items/{id}/retry` re-drives a failed item in place rather than re-enqueuing the URL. It refuses anything but a\nThe schema is a set of hand-written SQL migrations in [common/](common-package.md). common/'s own CI job applies them to D1 with wrangler before the pipeline Worker and the API Worker deploy, and the pipeline and API workflows wait for that job to succeed, so neither Worker ever runs against a schema older than its code (see [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md)). Deploys are not made twice in quick succession, so two migration runs never overlap. Locally, the developer applies the same migrations with wrangler to the D1 database in the shared state folder (see [local-development](local-development.md)), and the Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying them too.\n11:common/ is the TypeScript package that api/ and pipeline/ both build from, and it holds everything more than one module uses: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, item row reads and writes, the hand-written SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library the integration tests us\n32:  mig -->|\"applied by common/'s CI job\"| d1\n47:The API Worker and the pipeline Worker import common/ at build time. common/'s CI workflow applies the SQL migrations to D1, and both Workers' tests apply the same migrations to build their own D1 schema. The replay library runs only inside both Workers' integration tests.\n63:| SQL migrations | the D1 schema, as hand-written SQL files | common/'s CI workflow, both Workers' tests, local development | [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md), [local-development](local-development.md) |\n74:A change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/ against it in CI. When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: common/'s CI workflow applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys. When both pass, common/'s CI workflow applies the migrations to D1 with wrangler, and the pipel\n> The API Worker creates and restarts the item Workflow through the cross-script Workflow binding, and nothing else calls the pipeline. With no route to reach, the pipeline Worker carries no authentication of its own and no edge policy guards it.\n95:Each tree runs **test, lint and types as three parallel jobs** on pushes to `main`, path-filtered\n100:> Nothing serializes two runs of `common/`'s workflow, so two pushes to `main` in quick successi\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal TTS\" }\n  ext@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Firecrawl,<br/>AI Gateway\" }\n  api -->|\"create, restart\"| pipe\n  api --- state\n  pipe --- state\n  pipe -->|\"scrape, describe,<br/>agents\"| ext\n  pipe -->|\"start: PUT URL with<br/>the tunnel's hostname\"| modal\n59:2. It hands that URL to Modal with the quick tunnel's hostname, which it reads from its configuration, in place of localhost and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"cdcdb42b-5f60-484d-bef8-3ff7e1cff917","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30893543-69c5-4db1-aa56-cd43d0e1712b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudfla