y (4, 5). The store step then writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). The call id and the result pass from step to step as step results; the item row holds neither. Each step gets 3 attempts. Start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt, and wait for synthesis has 15 minutes.\"),\n(\"A synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the poll step has used its attempts, and so does a result Modal has discarded, which happens 7 days after the call.\",\"A synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the wait for synthesis step has used its attempts. Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.\"),\n])\n# deployment\ndraft=open('.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md').read()\ndiag=re.search(r\"## 🔁 CI: path-filtered checks per tree, deploys in a fixed order\\n\\n```mermaid\\n.*?```\\n\",draft,re.S).group(0)\ns=open(T+'deployment-and-ci.md').read()\nm=re.search(r\"## 🔁 CI: one path-filtered workflow per tree, deploys in a fixed order\\n\\n```mermaid\\n.*?```\\n\",s,re.S); assert m\ns=s.replace(m.group(0),diag)\nopen(T+'deployment-and-ci.md','w').write(s)\nedit(T+'deployment-and-ci.md',[\n(re.compile(r\"`common/` deploys nothing but its SQL migrations, which its own CI workflow applies to D1 with wrangler;\"),\"`common/` deploys nothing but its SQL migrations, which the Cloudflare workflow's migrate job applies to D1 with wrangler;\"),\n(\"inside `common/`'s workflow\",\"in `common/`'s checks\"),\n(re.compile(r\"Three workflows ship the Cloudflare side.*?All four are GitHub Actions secrets\\.\"),\"One workflow ships the Cloudflare side with `cloudflare/wrangler-action`. A paths filter decides which of `common/`, `pipeline/` and `api/` changed, and each changed tree's checks run. The deploy chain runs in a fixed order: the migrate job applies `common/`'s SQL migrations to D1, the pipeline job runs `pnpm build` and deploys `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`, and the API job deploys the API Worker. A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed. A job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the jobs after it, so a push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys the pipeline without a migration. A failed `common/` check stops all three: no migration, no pipeline deploy and no API deploy. A failed `pipeline/` check stops both Worker deploys, and a failed `api/` check stops the API deploy. The jobs authenticate with `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`. `tts` keeps its own workflow, with a **`deploy` job that depends on all three of its checks**, runs `modal deploy` and authenticates with `MODAL_TOKEN_ID` / `MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET`. All four are GitHub Actions secrets.\\n\\n> [!NOTE] Why one workflow for the Cloudflare side\\n> The deploys depend on each other: the migrations go first and the API Worker last. Jobs in one workflow wait on each other within a push.\\n\\n> [!TIP] Rejected: one workflow per tree\\n> Separate workflows cannot wait on each other within a push without polling one another, so the pipeline and API deploys could not wait for the migrations.\"),\n(\"Nothing serializes two runs of `common/`'s workflow,\",\"Nothing serializes two runs of the Cloudflare workflow,\"),\n])\n# common-package\nedit(T+'common-package.md',[\n(\"and it holds everything more than one module uses: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, item row reads and writes, the hand-written SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library the integration tests use.\",\"and it holds everything both Workers use: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, item row reads and writes, the hand-written SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library the integration tests use. Code that only the pipeline's own modules share stays in pipeline/.\"),\n(\"by common/'s own CI workflow\",\"by the Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job\"),\n('mig -->|\"applied by common/\\'s CI job\"| d1','mig -->|\"applied by the migrate job\"| d1'),\n(\"common/'s CI workflow applies the SQL migrations to D1, and both\",\"The Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job applies the SQL migrations to D1, and both\"),\n(\"| common/'s CI workflow, both Workers' tests, local development |\",\"| the Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job, both Workers' tests, local development |\"),\n(re.compile(r\"When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: common/'s CI workflow applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys\\. When both pass, .*?the pipeline Worker deploys before the API Worker\\.\"),\"When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: the migrate job applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys. When both pass, the migrate job applies the migrations to D1 with wrangler, then the pipeline Worker deploys and then the API Worker, all in one CI workflow.\"),\n])\nedit(T+'persistence-and-storage.md',[\n(\"common/'s own CI job applies them to D1 with wrangler before the pipeline Worker and the API Worker deploy, and the pipeline and API workflows wait for that job to succeed, so neither\",\"The Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job applies them to D1 with wrangler before the pipeline Worker and the API Worker deploy, in the same workflow, so neither\"),\n])\n# local-development\ns=open(T+'local-development.md').read()\ni=s.index('## 🏗️ Architecture')\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"## 🚀 How to run both Workers locally\n\n1. Apply common/'s migrations to the shared state folder: `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`.\n2. Start the pipeline Worker: `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`.\n3. Start the Node proxy: `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`.\n4. Start a quick tunnel to the proxy's port with `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:<port>`, and write `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<hostname>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`, with the tunnel's hostname in place of `<hostname>`.\n5. Start the API Worker: `pnpm dev` in `api/`.\n\n\"\"\"+s[i:]\ns=s.replace(\"2. It hands that URL to Modal with the quick tunnel's hostname, which it reads from its configuration, in place of localhost and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>.\",\"2. It hands that URL to Modal with localhost's endpoint replaced by the one in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The URL then holds the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>. In production both endpoints are R2's, so the same code runs in both places.\")\nm=re.search(r\"An item enqueued while the pipeline Worker is not running gets stuck in queued:.*?and the item starts again\\.\",s); assert m\ns=s.replace(m.group(0),\"An item enqueued while the pipeline Worker is not running cannot start. When the API fails to create its Workflow instance, the item fails at enqueue, and a retry once the pipeline Worker is running creates the instance. When the instance is created but never starts, or ends in error, the item stays queued, and the API re-queues the item the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes. When the API reads the item, it restarts the item's instance and rewrites queued_at (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)). The developer polls the item once the pipeline Worker is running, and the item starts again.\")\nopen(T+'local-development.md','w').write(s)\nedit(T+'invariants.md',[\n(\"and `common/`'s CI workflow applies them with wrangler before either Worker deploys\",\"and the Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job applies them with wrangler before either Worker deploys\"),\n(\"A change to `common/` runs the type checks of both Workers, and the Cloudflare side deploys in a fixed order: `common/`'s migrations, then the pipeline Worker, then the API Worker.\",\"A change to `common/` runs the type checks of both Workers, and one Cloudflare workflow deploys in a fixed order: `common/`'s migrations, then the pipeline Worker, then the API Worker.\"),\n])\ns=open('CLAUDE.md').read()\nm=re.search(r\"CI runs test/lint/types as three parallel jobs per subproject.*?stops all\\nthree\\.\",s,re.S); assert m\ns=s.replace(m.group(0),\"\"\"CI runs test/lint/types as three parallel jobs per subproject, each path-filtered to its own directory,\non pushes to `main`; a change to `common/` also runs the type checks of `api/` and `pipeline/`. One\nCloudflare workflow deploys with wrangler in a fixed order: it applies `common/`'s migrations to D1, then\ndeploys the pipeline Worker from the built `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`, then the API Worker; a job runs\nonly when no job before it failed, so a failed check in `common/` stops all three.\"\"\")\nopen('CLAUDE.md','w').write(s)\nprint('all ok')\nEOF\ngit diff --stat"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1a18633e-d813-4088-bb1a-ab30162cc267","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfuu2148ELEKr61c9tGUv","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ced67c1a-3562-44e9-b79c-9f8b0da25c3f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:28:59.908Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"ced67c1a-3562-44e9-b79c-9f8b0da25c3f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"75d77dd3-3a53-474d-af79-0de70ba1a2eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012eXq5ncchqtS3cQefqDMQX","type":"tool_result","content":"all ok\n CLAUDE.md                                        | 16 ++---\n docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md      | 14 ++--\n docs/technical-design/common-package.md          | 10 +--\n docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md       | 90 ++++++++++--------------\n docs/technical-design/invariants.md              |  4 +-\n docs/technical-design/item-contract.md           |  6 +-\n docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md          | 39 ++++++----\n docs/technical-design/local-development.md       | 12 +++-\n docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md |  2 +-\n docs/technical-design/tts-service.md             |  6 +-\n 10 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 96 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a08052b1-304b-4ea1-a656-b19b989d4dca","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:29:00.376Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"all ok\n CLAUDE.md                                        | 16 ++---\n docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md      | 14 ++--\n docs/technical-design/common-package.md          | 10 +--\n docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md       | 90 ++++++++++--------------\n docs/technical-design/invariants.md              |  4 +-\n docs/technical-design/item-contract.md           |  6 +-\n docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md          | 39 ++++++----\n docs/technical-design/local-development.md       | 12 +++-\n docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md |  2 +-\n docs/technical-design/tts-service.md             |  6 +-\n 10 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 96 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/item-contract.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":8,"newStart":46,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," | Route | Does |"," |---|---|","-| `POST /items` | Create an item from `{url, voice?}`. Writes the item row at `queued`, then creates the item's Workflow instance with the item id, and returns `202` with the item at `queued`; the item Workflow does the rest (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)). |","-| `GET /items/{id}` | Poll. Reads the item row and returns the current item; it never reads the Workflow instance. Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes: it restarts the item's instance, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, and rewrites `queued_at`. `404` for an unknown id. |","+| `POST /items` | Create an item from `{url, voice?}`. Writes the item row at `queued`, then creates the item's Workflow instance with the item id, and returns `202` with the item at `queued`; the item Workflow does the rest (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)). When creating the instance fails, the API writes the item as `failed` with that error and returns it; a retry creates the instance. |","+| `GET /items/{id}` | Poll. Reads the item row and returns the current item; it never reads the Workflow instance. Queues again an item that has been `queued` for more than 15 minutes. One conditional write claims the row and rewrites `queued_at`, so concurrent polls queue the item once. The API then restarts the item's instance from the step `current_step` names, or creates one when the row holds no instance id. The re-queue does not count toward the retry cap. `404` for an unknown id. |"," | `GET /items/{id}/audio` | Serve audio for a `ready` item: a `307` to a GET URL for the item's audio key in the R2 bucket, signed for one hour (see [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). `404` if the item is not `ready`, has no audio format yet, or is unknown: no link is ever minted for a non-ready item. |"," | `GET /items/{id}/images/{hash}` | Serve an image for the item, keyed by the content hash carried on an image unit. A `307` to a GET URL for the hash's key in the R2 bucket, signed fresh at read time for one hour. `404` for an unknown item. An unknown *hash* gets the `307` too, and R2 answers the signed URL with its own `404`; see below. Behind the same key as everything else. |"," | `POST /items/{id}/retry` | Re-drive a `failed` item in place, restarting its Workflow instance from the step that failed. `202` with the item back at `queued`; `409` unless the item is `failed` and under the retry cap, `404` for an unknown id. See the section below and [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md). |"]},{"oldStart":78,"oldLines":7,"newStart":78,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 🔁 Retry"," ","-`POST /items/{id}/retry` re-drives a failed item in place rather than re-enqueuing the URL. It refuses anything but a `failed` item, and a `failed` item past the retry cap, with `409`; `404` for an unknown id. An accepted retry writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at`, increments `retry_count` and clears the old error in one conditional write, then restarts the item's existing Workflow instance from the step named in `current_step`. The steps before it do not run again. A retry whose failed step is `recipe` or `release` restarts from `lease` instead, so the item asks for its domain's lease again and the recipe step reads the domain's current recipe. The Workflow moves the item to `generating` once it holds the lease, as on its first run; [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) carries the steps and what each one costs.","+`POST /items/{id}/retry` re-drives a failed item in place rather than re-enqueuing the URL. It refuses anything but a `failed` item, and a `failed` item past the retry cap, with `409`; `404` for an unknown id. An accepted retry writes `queued`, rewrites `queued_at`, increments `retry_count` and clears the old error in one conditional write, then restarts the item's existing Workflow instance from the step named in `current_step`, or creates one when the row holds no instance id. The steps before it do not run again. A retry whose failed step is `recipe` or `release` restarts from `lease` instead, so the item asks for its domain's lease again and the recipe step reads the domain's current recipe. The Workflow moves the item to `generating` once it holds the lease, as on its first run; [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) carries the steps and what each one costs."," "," > [!NOTE] Double-submitting is refused by the write, not by the read"," > The transition is one conditional `UPDATE` gating on status still `failed` and `retry_count` under the cap, incrementing the count in SQL. A rowcount of zero is the `409`. Reading the row first and then writing would let two concurrent retries both pass the guard, which restarts one instance twice and increments the count once, so the cap would read tighter than it is. The pre-read only picks which refusal message to send."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":7,"newStart":25,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ```mermaid"," flowchart TD","     start([\"The recipe returns<br/>a title and<br/>display units\"]) --> loop","-    subgraph loop [\"For each recipe unit,<br/>in document order\"]","+    subgraph loop [\"Recipe step: each recipe<br/>unit, in document order\"]","         direction TB","         kind{\"Image unit?\"}","         kind -->|No| spoken[\"1 Derive the spoken<br/>form from the display\"]"]},{"oldStart":34,"oldLines":14,"newStart":34,"newLines":18,"lines":["         test -->|No| keep[\"4 Keep as a typed<br/>paragraph or code unit\"]","         kind -->|Yes| stash[\"5 Hold it after the<br/>last kept text unit\"]","     end","-    loop --> acquire[\"6 Acquire held images,<br/>interleave with kept units\"]","-    acquire --> any{\"7 Any unit survives?\"}","+    subgraph images [\"Images step\"]","+        direction TB","+        acquire[\"6 Acquire held images,<br/>interleave with kept units\"]","+        acquire --> any{\"7 Any unit survives?\"}","+        any -->|Yes| write[\"8 Write the units<br/>into the item row\"]","+    end","+    loop --> acquire","     any -. no .-> fail([\"Fail the item:<br/>no surviving units\"])","-    any -->|Yes| write[\"8 Write the units<br/>into the item row\"]","     write --> next([\"Describe, synthesis,<br/>store: survivors only\"])"," ```"," ","-Steps 1 to 5 run at the end of the item Workflow's recipe step, on the units the recipe returns. Steps 1 and 2 are in a required order, because the drop rule reads the spoken form. The loop must also run in document order, because step 5 anchors an image to the last text unit kept so far. When that unit is dropped, the image anchors to the kept unit before it. An image that comes before every text unit goes first in the list. Step 6, the images step, acquires the held images and drops any that will not acquire (see below). Step 7 fails the item when nothing survives, before the list is written. Step 8 writes the survivors and the degradations into the item row as soon as the step has them, and the later steps read them from there. The recipe step writes the title into the row together with its units. A recipe the agents authored or revised is written as its next version by the item Workflow itself (see [recipes](recipes.md)).","+Steps 1 to 5 run at the end of the item Workflow's recipe step, on the units the recipe returns. Steps 1 and 2 are in a required order, because the drop rule reads the spoken form. The loop must also run in document order, because step 5 anchors an image to the last text unit kept so far. When that unit is dropped, the image anchors to the kept unit before it. An image that comes before every text unit goes first in the list. The recipe step writes the kept text units into the item row and hands the held images to the images step as its step result, each with its src, its alt and the kept unit it follows, so the row holds only finished units. Steps 6 to 8 run in the images step. It acquires the held images, places each after its unit and drops any that will not acquire (see below). It fails the item when no unit survives. It writes the full list and the degradations into the item row, and the later steps read them from there. The recipe step writes the title into the row together with its units. A recipe the agents authored or revised is written as its next version by the item Workflow itself (see [recipes](recipes.md))."," "," From step 8 on, describe, synthesis and store work on the survivors only and never drop a unit, so the length guard at store compares one list against its own timeline (invariant 2)."," "]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/tts-service.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":7,"newStart":20,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Endpoint | Takes | Answers |"," |---|---|---|"," | start synthesis | the spoken forms, one string per read-along unit in unit order; the Kokoro voice, defaulting to `af_heart`; the destination URL, a presigned R2 PUT URL for the item's audio key | Modal's call id for this synthesis, at once |","-| fetch result | the call id | not ready while the synthesis runs; once it is done, the result below |","+| fetch result | the call id | `202` while the synthesis runs; `200` with the result below once it is done; `500` when the synthesis raised; `410` once Modal no longer holds the result |"," "," | Result field | Answers |"," |---|---|"]},{"oldStart":75,"oldLines":9,"newStart":75,"newLines":9,"lines":["     end"," ```"," ","-The item Workflow's start synthesis step signs the PUT URL and calls the start endpoint, which spawns the synthesis and answers with Modal's call id at once (1, 2). Modal uploads the audio to the bucket when the synthesis finishes (3). The poll step asks the result endpoint for the call id until the result is ready (4, 5), and the store step writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). The call id and the result pass from step to step as step results; the item row holds neither. Each step gets 3 attempts: start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt and each poll 1 minute.","+The item Workflow's start synthesis step signs the PUT URL and calls the start endpoint, which spawns the synthesis and answers with Modal's call id at once (1, 2). Modal uploads the audio to the bucket when the synthesis finishes (3). The wait for synthesis step asks the result endpoint for the call id every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5). The store step then writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). The call id and the result pass from step to step as step results; the item row holds neither. Each step gets 3 attempts. Start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt, and wait for synthesis has 15 minutes."," ","-A synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the poll step has used its attempts, and so does a result Modal has discarded, which happens 7 days after the call.","+A synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the wait for synthesis step has used its attempts. Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once."," "," > [!WARNING] A start repeated after a deploy synthesizes twice"," > Modal accepts no idempotency key and no caller-chosen call id, so a start synthesis step that runs again after a deploy spawns a second synthesis. Both upload to the same audio key, keyed by the item id, so the second upload overwrites the first and the item still has one audio file. The cost is one extra synthesis, which is accepted."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":21,"oldLines":7,"newStart":21,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," `pipeline/` deploys with `pnpm deploy`, from within `pipeline/` or via CI below; see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) for what runs on it. That script builds before it ships: `pnpm build` runs Vite with the Flue and Cloudflare plugins, writing the bundled Worker and a generated `wrangler.json` into `dist/nagara/`, and `wrangler deploy -c dist/nagara/wrangler.json` ships that generated config rather than the hand-written `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc`. The Flue plugin adds the author and revision agents' Durable Object bindings at build time, so the source config alone would ship a Worker without them."," ","-`common/` deploys nothing but its SQL migrations, which its own CI workflow applies to D1 with wrangler; see [common-package](common-package.md) for the rest of the package.","+`common/` deploys nothing but its SQL migrations, which the Cloudflare workflow's migrate job applies to D1 with wrangler; see [common-package](common-package.md) for the rest of the package."," "," > [!NOTE] Why migrations, then the pipeline, then the API"," > Both Workers read and write D1, so the schema they build against is applied before either deploys. The API Worker's Workflow binding fails with `workflow.not_found` until the pipeline Worker that holds the item Workflow is deployed, so the pipeline always goes before the API."]},{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":65,"newStart":39,"newLines":49,"lines":[" "," `tts/` is pushed independently with `modal deploy`, from within `tts/` or via CI below; see [tts-service](tts-service.md) for what actually runs on Modal."," ","-## 🔁 CI: one path-filtered workflow per tree, deploys in a fixed order","+## 🔁 CI: path-filtered checks per tree, deploys in a fixed order"," "," ```mermaid","-flowchart LR","-  push@{ shape: stadium, label: \"Push to main\" }","-  subgraph cw [\"common workflow\"]","-    direction TB","-    cchk@{ shape: rect, label: \"test, lint, types,<br/>both Workers' types\" }","-    mig@{ shape: rect, label: \"1 apply common/<br/>migrations to D1\" }","-    cchk --> mig","-  end","-  subgraph pw [\"pipeline workflow\"]","-    direction TB","-    pchk@{ shape: rect, label: \"test, lint, types<br/>(parallel)\" }","-    pdep@{ shape: rect, label: \"2 deploy the<br/>pipeline Worker\" }","-    pchk --> pdep","-  end","-  subgraph aw [\"api workflow\"]","-    direction TB","-    achk@{ shape: rect, label: \"test, lint, types<br/>(parallel)\" }","-    adep@{ shape: rect, label: \"3 deploy the<br/>API Worker\" }","-    achk --> adep","-  end","-  subgraph tw [\"tts workflow\"]","-    direction TB","-    tchk@{ shape: rect, label: \"test, lint, types<br/>(parallel)\" }","-    tdep@{ shape: rect, label: \"deploy tts/<br/>to Modal\" }","-    tchk --> tdep","-  end","-  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1\" }","-  cfw@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Cloudflare<br/>Workers\" }","-  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal\" }","-  push -->|\"common/\"| cchk","-  push -->|\"pipeline/\"| pchk","-  push -->|\"api/\"| achk","-  push -->|\"tts/\"| tchk","-  mig -.->|\"waits for\"| pdep","-  mig -.->|\"waits for\"| adep","-  pdep -.->|\"waits for\"| adep","-  mig -->|\"wrangler\"| d1","-  pdep -->|\"wrangler\"| cfw","-  adep -->|\"wrangler\"| cfw","-  tdep -->|\"modal deploy\"| modal","-  classDef step fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a","-  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c","-  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed","-  classDef person fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563","-  class cchk,mig,pchk,pdep,achk,adep,tchk,tdep step","-  class d1 store","-  class cfw,modal ext","-  class push person","+flowchart TD","+    push([\"push to main\"]) --> ch[\"changes:<br/>paths-filter for<br/>common, pipeline, api\"]","+    ch -->|\"common/ changed\"| cc[\"common checks:<br/>test, lint, types,<br/>api and pipeline types\"]","+    ch -->|\"pipeline/ changed\"| pc[\"pipeline checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]","+    ch -->|\"api/ changed\"| ac[\"api checks:<br/>test, lint, types\"]","+    subgraph chain [\"deploy chain: a job runs only when no job before it failed\"]","+        direction TB","+        mig[\"1 migrate: wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply --remote\"]","+        pd[\"2 deploy pipeline:<br/>pnpm build,<br/>deploy dist config\"]","+        ad[\"3 deploy api\"]","+        mig --> pd --> ad","+    end","+    cc --> mig","+    pc --> pd","+    ac --> ad","+    cc -. \"fails\" .-> s1([\"1, 2 and 3 do not run:<br/>no migration, no<br/>Worker deploys\"])","+    pc -. \"fails\" .-> s2([\"2 and 3 do not run\"])","+    ac -. \"fails\" .-> s3([\"3 does not run\"])","+    tw[\"tts workflow: test, lint,<br/>types, then modal deploy\"]","+    push -->|\"tts/ changed\"| tw","+    classDef step fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a","+    classDef broken fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626","+    classDef person fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563","+    class ch,cc,pc,ac,mig,pd,ad,tw step","+    class s1,s2,s3 broken","+    class push person"," ```"," ","-Each tree runs **test, lint and types as three parallel jobs** on pushes to `main`, path-filtered to its own directory (`api/**`, `pipeline/**`, `common/**`, `tts/**`), so a docs-only push, or a change to one tree, runs neither another tree's checks nor its deploy. A change to `common/` also runs the type checks of `api/` and `pipeline/` against the changed package, inside `common/`'s workflow. The `api`, `pipeline` and `common` jobs install with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` on Node 24 and run `pnpm test`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm types`; the `tts` jobs provision the pinned toolchain (uv/ruff/ty/pytest, see the repository's `CLAUDE.md`) with `uv sync --frozen` against `tts/`'s lockfile.","+Each tree runs **test, lint and types as three parallel jobs** on pushes to `main`, path-filtered to its own directory (`api/**`, `pipeline/**`, `common/**`, `tts/**`), so a docs-only push, or a change to one tree, runs neither another tree's checks nor its deploy. A change to `common/` also runs the type checks of `api/` and `pipeline/` against the changed package, in `common/`'s checks. The `api`, `pipeline` and `common` jobs install with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` on Node 24 and run `pnpm test`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm types`; the `tts` jobs provision the pinned toolchain (uv/ruff/ty/pytest, see the repository's `CLAUDE.md`) with `uv sync --frozen` against `tts/`'s lockfile."," ","-Three workflows ship the Cloudflare side with `cloudflare/wrangler-action`, each after its own checks pass: `common/`'s workflow applies its SQL migrations to D1, the pipeline's workflow runs `pnpm build` and deploys `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`, and the API's workflow deploys the API Worker. The pipeline and API workflows wait for `common/`'s workflow to succeed before they deploy, and the API deploys after the pipeline. When a check in `common/`'s workflow fails, nothing deploys: no migration, no pipeline deploy and no API deploy. The three authenticate with `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`. `tts` adds a **`deploy` job that depends on all three of its checks**, runs `modal deploy` and authenticates with `MODAL_TOKEN_ID` / `MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET`. All four are GitHub Actions secrets.","+One workflow ships the Cloudflare side with `cloudflare/wrangler-action`. A paths filter decides which of `common/`, `pipeline/` and `api/` changed, and each changed tree's checks run. The deploy chain runs in a fixed order: the migrate job applies `common/`'s SQL migrations to D1, the pipeline job runs `pnpm build` and deploys `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`, and the API job deploys the API Worker. A job in the chain runs only when no job before it failed. A job skipped because its tree did not change does not stop the jobs after it, so a push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys the pipeline without a migration. A failed `common/` check stops all three: no migration, no pipeline deploy and no API deploy. A failed `pipeline/` check stops both Worker deploys, and a failed `api/` check stops the API deploy. The jobs authenticate with `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`. `tts` keeps its own workflow, with a **`deploy` job that depends on all three of its checks**, runs `modal deploy` and authenticates with `MODAL_TOKEN_ID` / `MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET`. All four are GitHub Actions secrets."," ","+> [!NOTE] Why one workflow for the Cloudflare side","+> The deploys depend on each other: the migrations go first and the API Worker last. Jobs in one workflow wait on each other within a push.","+","+> [!TIP] Rejected: one workflow per tree","+> Separate workflows cannot wait on each other within a push without polling one another, so the pipeline and API deploys could not wait for the migrations.","+"," > [!WARNING] Two migration runs at once are not guarded","-> Nothing serializes two runs of `common/`'s workflow, so two pushes to `main` in quick succession can apply `common/`'s migrations twice at the same time. The chain relies on deploys never being made twice in quick succession.","+> Nothing serializes two runs of the Cloudflare workflow, so two pushes to `main` in quick succession can apply `common/`'s migrations twice at the same time. The chain relies on deploys never being made twice in quick succession."," "," The `tts` check jobs install the full dev dependency group (torch-cpu, kokoro, numpy) because `ty` needs them to resolve `app.py`'s image-runtime imports locally; the deploy job installs only the Modal client (`--no-dev`). uv's lockfile-keyed cache absorbs most of the repeat install cost."," "]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/common-package.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":7,"newStart":8,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 🔭 Overview"," ","-common/ is the TypeScript package that api/ and pipeline/ both build from, and it holds everything more than one module uses: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, item row reads and writes, the hand-written SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library the integration tests use. Of its contents only the migrations are deployed, by common/'s own CI workflow; the rest is compiled into each Worker. The shared types are checked when the code builds, never at runtime.","+common/ is the TypeScript package that api/ and pipeline/ both build from, and it holds everything both Workers use: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, item row reads and writes, the hand-written SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library the integration tests use. Code that only the pipeline's own modules share stays in pipeline/. Of its contents only the migrations are deployed, by the Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job; the rest is compiled into each Worker. The shared types are checked when the code builds, never at runtime."," "," ## 🏗️ Architecture"," "]},{"oldStart":29,"oldLines":7,"newStart":29,"newLines":7,"lines":["   tests@{ shape: rect, label: \"Both Workers'<br/>integration tests\" }","   api -->|\"types, keys, GET signing,<br/>row, queued write\"| common","   pipe -->|\"types, keys, PUT signing,<br/>row, status writes\"| common","-  mig -->|\"applied by common/'s CI job\"| d1","+  mig -->|\"applied by the migrate job\"| d1","   tests -->|\"replay cassettes\"| vcr","   tests -->|\"build the test schema\"| mig","   classDef shared fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706"]},{"oldStart":44,"oldLines":7,"newStart":44,"newLines":7,"lines":["   class tests tool"," ```"," ","-The API Worker and the pipeline Worker import common/ at build time. common/'s CI workflow applies the SQL migrations to D1, and both Workers' tests apply the same migrations to build their own D1 schema. The replay library runs only inside both Workers' integration tests.","+The API Worker and the pipeline Worker import common/ at build time. The Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job applies the SQL migrations to D1, and both Workers' tests apply the same migrations to build their own D1 schema. The replay library runs only inside both Workers' integration tests."," "," ## 📦 What it holds"," "]},{"oldStart":60,"oldLines":7,"newStart":60,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | R2 key layout | the bucket's audio/ and images/ prefixes, and the functions that build an audio key from an item id and an image key from a content hash | the API Worker, the item Workflow | [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) |"," | Presigning | one function that signs a GET or a PUT URL for a key with a given R2 token and lifetime | the API Worker for GET, the pipeline Worker for PUT | [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) |"," | Item row reads and writes | encoding and decoding the JSON columns, and the status write that sets a status, clears the error and stamps updated_at | the API Worker for queued, the step wrapper for every later status | [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) |","-| SQL migrations | the D1 schema, as hand-written SQL files | common/'s CI workflow, both Workers' tests, local development | [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md), [local-development](local-development.md) |","+| SQL migrations | the D1 schema, as hand-written SQL files | the Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job, both Workers' tests, local development | [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md), [local-development](local-development.md) |"," | Cassette replay library | our TypeScript copy of vcrpy, replay only | both Workers' integration tests | this note |"," "," ## 📼 Replaying cassettes in tests"]},{"oldStart":71,"oldLines":7,"newStart":71,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," The shared types are checked when the code builds and deploys, never at runtime. A value read back from D1 or received from Modal is trusted to match its type, and nothing parses it against a schema."," ","-A change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/ against it in CI. When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: common/'s CI workflow applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys. When both pass, common/'s CI workflow applies the migrations to D1 with wrangler, and the pipeline and API workflows wait for it to succeed before they continue; the pipeline Worker deploys before the API Worker. [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md) holds that order.","+A change to common/ runs the type checks of api/ and pipeline/ against it in CI. When either check fails, the whole deploy stops: the migrate job applies no migration, and neither Worker deploys. When both pass, the migrate job applies the migrations to D1 with wrangler, then the pipeline Worker deploys and then the API Worker, all in one CI workflow. [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md) holds that order."," "," > [!NOTE] Why the types are not validated at runtime"," > Both Workers are type-checked against the same common/ before anything deploys, so a shape the two Workers disagree on stops the deploy before it reaches production. This departs from the code style's rule that a payload crossing a service boundary validates at runtime."]}]}],"moreFiles":4,"changedFiles":["/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/item-contract.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/tts-service.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/common-package.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/local-development.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/invariants.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/CLAUDE.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1a18633e-d813-4088-bb1a-ab30162cc267","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked"