{"parentUuid":"1a100db5-e22d-4bfc-90f9-b63603bed451","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuu6Bdz1RWPjhSoDDrD2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lssh9bSskAhKCi8osXEPob","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/skills/wiki/references; cat $W/testing/INDEX.md; sed -n 1,200p $W/cloudflare/vitest-plugin.md | head -80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2866,"cache_read_input_tokens":355888,"output_tokens":783,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":654},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":355888,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Lssh9bSskAhKCi8osXEPob":{"command":"W=/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou/skills/wiki/references; cat $W/testing/INDEX.md; sed -n 1,200p $W/cloudflare/vitest-plugin.md | head -80"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b58a5dd6-e9f0-4b56-991e-b7c6cf201705","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfuu6BEv3ypdAf5bPdavZ","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:test-design","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"0bba7186-c90d-45c9-aa46-3b15dc4019c2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:29:33.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"0bba7186-c90d-45c9-aa46-3b15dc4019c2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"75d77dd3-3a53-474d-af79-0de70ba1a2eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lssh9bSskAhKCi8osXEPob","type":"tool_result","content":"# testing\n\n- [`runner-reporters`](runner-reporters.md): how a test runner hands results to a pluggable reporter, and who computes the exit code\n# Testing Workers and Workflows with the vitest plugin\n\nverified: 2026-10-10\n\nAnswers how Cloudflare's vitest integration tests Workflows and outbound HTTP, what replaced its removed fetch mock, and which approach replays recorded HTTP. Distilled from the plugin's type declarations, changelog and examples, the docs, and a spike that ran every approach on plugin 1.1.13 and 1.3.6 under vitest 4.1.\n\n## Knowledge\n\n- `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin` is the renamed `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` (renamed in 1.0.0; the old name stopped at 0.22.0). Tests run inside workerd with the project's wrangler bindings.\n- Workflow introspection is documented and supported. `introspectWorkflowInstance(binding, id)` gives `waitForStepResult`, `waitForStatus`, the output and error, and `modify(fn)` with `disableSleeps`, `disableRetryDelays`, `mockStepResult`, `mockStepError`, `forceStepTimeout` and `mockEvent`. `introspectWorkflow(binding)` applies the same `modify` to every instance created afterwards, for ids the test does not control. Both support `await using`.\n- `modify` works on whole steps. A mocked step never runs its callback, so the HTTP calls and the binding writes inside it never happen; steps that are not mocked run their real code, `fetch` included. `modify` needs a Workflow binding. A Workflow taken from `ctx.exports` raises an error that explains how to add the binding.\n- Introspection gotchas: a falsy mocked result (`null`, `false`, `0`, `\"\"`) is ignored and the real step body runs; `mockStepError` must come before `mockStepResult` on the same step; `getError()` drops a `NonRetryableError`'s message. Only introspection skips sleeps and retry delays; an undisabled 30 s sleep takes 30 s.\n- `fetchMock` from `cloudflare:test` was removed in 0.13.0 and the `miniflare.fetchMock` option in 0.20.0. The changelog points to mocking `globalThis.fetch` or MSW (\"recommended\"), and the examples include an MSW fixture set up through `setupFiles`. The prose docs mention neither.\n- MSW intercepts a `fetch` made inside a Workflow step, because the Workflow's `run()` executes in the test file's isolate. That is also why a global the test sets is visible to the Workflow. msw 2.15 works as is; msw 3's `msw/node` does not start in workerd (it cannot read `llhttp.wasm`) and works only through the experimental `defineNetwork` with the fetch interceptor.\n- Miniflare's `outboundService`, set in the vitest config's miniflare options, replaces all of a Worker's outbound requests with one handler, which can read recorded responses from disk in Node. Nothing reaches the network unless the handler forwards it. Introspection, MSW without a catch-all, and a code seam all let unmatched requests reach the real network.\n- Only HTTP interception (MSW or `outboundService`) runs the real step bodies, including the client's request building and response parsing and the step's binding writes, while replaying recorded responses.\n- Replaying vcrpy (Python) cassettes needs translation: strip `content-encoding` and `content-length` from recorded responses (otherwise \"Decompression failed\"), rewrite URLs that changed (such as a provider now reached through a gateway), and compare bodies as JSON rather than bytes. Matching on URL alone serves the wrong recorded response when several share a URL.\n- Code-level seams, such as a global symbol the code reads for a test double, are not a documented Workflow-testing method; they put the test hook in production code paths, and the double replaces the client code, so the client's serialization never runs.\n\n## Sources\n\n- https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/test-apis/\n- https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/test-workflows/\n- https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk (vitest-plugin CHANGELOG, `fixtures/vitest-plugin-examples/request-mocking`, `fixtures/vitest-plugin-examples/workflows`)\n- Spike, 2026-10-04: introspection, MSW, `outboundService` and a global seam raced on one Workflow, replaying recorded Firecrawl and Gemini responses","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1c51c872-6248-41fb-a1ef-915289676019","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:29:33.755Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# testing\n\n- [`runner-reporters`](runner-reporters.md): how a test runner hands results to a pluggable reporter, and who computes the exit code\n# Testing Workers and Workflows with the vitest plugin\n\nverified: 2026-10-10\n\nAnswers how Cloudflare's vitest integration tests Workflows and outbound HTTP, what replaced its removed fetch mock, and which approach replays recorded HTTP. Distilled from the plugin's type declarations, changelog and examples, the docs, and a spike that ran every approach on plugin 1.1.13 and 1.3.6 under vitest 4.1.\n\n## Knowledge\n\n- `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin` is the renamed `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` (renamed in 1.0.0; the old name stopped at 0.22.0). Tests run inside workerd with the project's wrangler bindings.\n- Workflow introspection is documented and supported. `introspectWorkflowInstance(binding, id)` gives `waitForStepResult`, `waitForStatus`, the output and error, and `modify(fn)` with `disableSleeps`, `disableRetryDelays`, `mockStepResult`, `mockStepError`, `forceStepTimeout` and `mockEvent`. `introspectWorkflow(binding)` applies the same `modify` to every instance created afterwards, for ids the test does not control. Both support `await using`.\n- `modify` works on whole steps. A mocked step never runs its callback, so the HTTP calls and the binding writes inside it never happen; steps that are not mocked run their real code, `fetch` included. `modify` needs a Workflow binding. A Workflow taken from `ctx.exports` raises an error that explains how to add the binding.\n- Introspection gotchas: a falsy mocked result (`null`, `false`, `0`, `\"\"`) is ignored and the real step body runs; `mockStepError` must come before `mockStepResult` on the same step; `getError()` drops a `NonRetryableError`'s message. Only introspection skips sleeps and retry delays; an undisabled 30 s sleep takes 30 s.\n- `fetchMock` from `cloudflare:test` was removed in 0.13.0 and the `miniflare.fetchMock` option in 0.20.0. The changelog points to mocking `globalThis.fetch` or MSW (\"recommended\"), and the examples include an MSW fixture set up through `setupFiles`. The prose docs mention neither.\n- MSW intercepts a `fetch` made inside a Workflow step, because the Workflow's `run()` executes in the test file's isolate. That is also why a global the test sets is visible to the Workflow. msw 2.15 works as is; msw 3's `msw/node` does not start in workerd (it cannot read `llhttp.wasm`) and works only through the experimental `defineNetwork` with the fetch interceptor.\n- Miniflare's `outboundService`, set in the vitest config's miniflare options, replaces all of a Worker's outbound requests with one handler, which can read recorded responses from disk in Node. Nothing reaches the network unless the handler forwards it. Introspection, MSW without a catch-all, and a code seam all let unmatched requests reach the real network.\n- Only HTTP interception (MSW or `outboundService`) runs the real step bodies, including the client's request building and response parsing and the step's binding writes, while replaying recorded responses.\n- Replaying vcrpy (Python) cassettes needs translation: strip `content-encoding` and `content-length` from recorded responses (otherwise \"Decompression failed\"), rewrite URLs that changed (such as a provider now reached through a gateway), and compare bodies as JSON rather than bytes. Matching on URL alone serves the wrong recorded response when several share a URL.\n- Code-level seams, such as a global symbol the code reads for a test double, are not a documented Workflow-testing method; they put the test hook in production code paths, and the double replaces the client code, so the client's serialization never runs.\n\n## Sources\n\n- https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/test-apis/\n- https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/test-workflows/\n- https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk (vitest-plugin CHANGELOG, `fixtures/vitest-plugin-examples/request-mocking`, `fixtures/vitest-plugin-examples/workflows`)\n- Spike, 2026-10-04: introspection, MSW, `outboundService` and a global seam raced on one Workflow, replaying recorded Firecrawl and Gemini responses","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b58a5dd6-e9f0-4b56-991e-b7c6cf201705","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0bba7186-c90d-45c9-aa46-3b15dc4019c2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
