{"parentUuid":"c09efe74-77e5-4256-a262-28a175814044","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuuBVFXQBUFZpKLDes1M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I committed the doc changes as one commit, `4930ea1 docs: record the program design of the Cloudflare migration`, covering CLAUDE.md and the ten notes. I also stopped both canvases: the program-design one, and the stuck one, which was a canvas from your filadd project (`scope1-components`) on port 5190.\n\nThe new test-design canvas is at **http://localhost:5190**. It shows one tree per deployable, each with its candidate starting points to test (roots), worked in this order:\n\n- **A, common/:** presign, writeStatus with readItem, restartPoint, replayCassettes. Migrations get no root of their own; they're checked by hand by reading an item back after migrating.\n- **B, tts/:** POST start and GET result. The audio upload is a variant of start, not a separate root.\n- **C, pipeline/:** ItemWorkflow.run as one root, with a branch per step group: wrapper, fetch, lease and release, recipe, images, describe, start synthesis, wait for synthesis, store. DomainQueue (acquire, release, alarm) is the second root.\n- **D, api/:** POST /items, GET /items/{id}, retry, audio and images, health and the key guard.\n\nThe Claude note on the canvas describes how I plan to draw each branch. It's the usual classification-tree picture: the root at the top, the factors that change the outcome under it, and the cases of each factor under those. Below that comes a grid with one line per test row and a dot under each case the row picks, so you can see at a glance what each row covers.\n\nCorrect the roots there with sticky notes or by voice. I'll open the first branch once you confirm them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":367959,"output_tokens":535,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":392,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":535,"cache_read_input_tokens":367959,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":392},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"187b7e05-68c9-48e8-82ae-3c01fe28e735","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuuBUqiwszzQNHhjrmQ7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:test-design","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"a137d548-0c92-45e1-8c4c-8fa625b39b29","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:30:42.854Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
