{"parentUuid":"aad515b4-cc09-4ce4-b058-dd5fc4281b20","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuvJJ49FAD9b3Z5DQdas","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I applied both of your notes on writeStatus:\n\n- **Two overloads.** `writeStatus` is now two overloads. One takes queued or generating and accepts no error, so it clears it. The other takes failed and requires the error. I changed the record's interface in `program-design/nagara.md` to match.\n- **Split branch.** writeStatus and readItem are now separate branches:\n  - **A2 writeStatus:** writing generating over a row with an error clears the error, writing queued clears it too, and writing failed stores its error. A note under the branch says why there are no rows for queued or generating with an error, or failed without one: the compiler rejects both.\n  - **A3 readItem:** a row with no units yet, a row whose JSON columns decode, and an unknown id.\n- **Renumbering.** restartPoint and replayCassettes moved to A4 and A5, and the rows renumbered, so tree A runs A1–A17. The other trees didn't change.\n\nI redrew the trees and removed the leftover connector lines the first redraw left behind. When the trees are done, I'll list the overloads as an amendment for the common-package note."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":438,"cache_read_input_tokens":414063,"output_tokens":364,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":438,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":414063,"cache_creation_input_tokens":438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":438},"type":"message"}],"speed":"stan