{"parentUuid":"714265d1-0da1-48c8-864f-cd302b655142","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14911270 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b9acb83c-dd88-4adc-8c68-a185ceedd68a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:51:30.461Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14911270 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"b9acb83c-dd88-4adc-8c68-a185ceedd68a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuvmyKYKS5BvfVi6YEcH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've marked all four trees settled on the canvas and in `test-design/nagara.md`:\n\n| Tree | Rows | Also run by hand |\n|---|---|---|\n| A common/ | A1–A17 | none |\n| B tts/ | B1–B9 | B1 |\n| C pipeline/ | C1–C28 | C1, C5, C7, C9, C11 |\n| D api/ | D1–D27 | D1, D4, D5, D13, D16, D20, D21, D25 |\n\nFour questions are still open, and each one changes a row or adds an implementation task:\n\n1. **C11, small images:** a raster under 200 px is dropped. Should it record a degradation, or be dropped silently like the empty-unit drop rule?\n2. **C7–C10, agent stand-in:** the Flue agents run in their own Durable Objects, so how do the tests stand in for them? My proposal is an implementation task: replay the agents' AI Gateway calls with msw if those objects run inside the test, otherwise fake the agent's reply.\n3. **C1 and C11, Images binding:** I haven't checked whether the Images binding works in local tests. I can check it now, or record it as an implementation task.\n4. **B tree, unknown call id:** what should the result endpoint return for an unknown or malformed call id? The design only names 202, 200, 500 and 410.\n\nThe trees also changed one thing the docs describe. The status write is now two overloads: queued and generating take no error and clear it, and failed requires one. That belongs in item-lifecycle's step wrapper section and in common-package. Once you've answered the questions, I'll record it together with anything the answers add."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":431987,"output_tokens":538,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":431987,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7e53f0ea-e549-4e4e-96e0-ae7614cdec54","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuvmxwUevSqyAA4DUu1G","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ea33102-7a6a-416d-9397-dbaa003e933e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:51:36.478Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
