{"parentUuid":"43c369f1-b78a-4c64-b63d-56a44ce0943a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuw4eq2WZsktUygaTLmT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XzhZmCnV1qFjhQNLNBZJH5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; cat > docs-drafts/test-design-amendments.md <<'EOF'\n**docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md**\n\nReplace the paragraph after the first paragraph under \"The step wrapper\":\n\nThe status write sets the status and `current_step` and stamps `updated_at` in one statement. It has two forms: `queued` or `generating` takes no error and clears it, and `failed` requires the error, so the type checker rejects a `failed` write without one. It belongs to the [common/ package](common-package.md), and the API uses the same write for `queued` at enqueue and on retry, and for `failed` when the instance cannot be created.\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/common-package.md**\n\n\"What it holds\" table, row Item row reads and writes, \"Holds\" and \"Used by\" columns:\n\n| Item row reads and writes | encoding and decoding the JSON columns, and the status write that sets a status and stamps updated_at, clearing the error for queued and generating and requiring one for failed | the API Worker for queued and for a failed enqueue, the step wrapper for every later status | [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) |\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/tts-service.md**\n\n\"What it exposes\", endpoint table, row fetch result, append to the \"Answers\" column:\n\n; `422` for an id Modal never issued or one that is not a call id\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md**\n\nInsert after the sentence ending \"measured on the decoded file.\" in the paragraph beginning \"Validation runs on the **decoded bytes**\":\n\nA smaller raster is dropped silently, with no degradation: it is an avatar or a tracking pixel, not content the item lost.\nEOF\nD=$PWD/docs-drafts/test-design-amendments.md\npython3 - \"$D\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys,re\nd=sys.argv[1]\ns=open('briefs/unslop-pd-r1.md').read()\ns=s.replace('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md',d)\nopen('briefs/unslop-td-r1.md','w').write(s)\ns=open('briefs/docreview-pd.md').read().replace('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/docs-drafts/program-design-amendments.md',d).replace(' and one edit to /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/CLAUDE.md','')\nopen('briefs/docreview-td.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"test-design-amendments\" briefs/unslop-td-r1.md briefs/docreview-td.md\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper\n$H spawn --kind claude --label \"unslop td amendments r1\" --model opus --body-file briefs/unslop-td-r1.md; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"doc review td amendments\" --model sonnet --body-file briefs/docreview-td.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":435537,"output_tokens":1113,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1089,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1113,"cache_read_input_tokens":435537,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1089},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XzhZmCnV1qFjhQNLNBZJH5":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; cat > docs-drafts/test-design-amendments.md <<