. With the two-form write, the API also writes `failed` with the error. The charter says a note describes the present, and the notes should agree. The same applies to `common-package.md`'s summary row in the folder README.\n6. **Edit 2, `common-package.md`:** \"the step wrapper for every later status\" includes `failed`, which the same cell also gives to the API Worker for a failed enqueue. Both writers then appear to own `failed`. Say \"the step wrapper for every status after enqueue, including `failed` after a step's last attempt\".\n7. **Edit 3, `tts-service.md`:** `422` appears only in the table. The prose at `tts-service.md:80` explains `410` and its consequence, the item failing at once. The draft does not say what the Workflow does on a `422`, so a reader of the note cannot tell whether it retries or fails the item.\n\n**What the draft gets right:** every edit is in the present tense, reprints no code, uses no ASCII diagrams and links no issue, and the table row keeps the template's column count and link convention. The edits add no headings, so the emoji rule is not tested here.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1f1018ff-a3fe-427b-84ec-c928be56a316","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home