c76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"ab54a7e0-d43c-48f8-b3a9-e550db648a4a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b0c29400-5764-47e0-b7f6-3520658235fc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011jPwh6rr6qXegZjkTCGzak","type":"tool_result","content":"The row always holds the item's status. The API Worker writes `queued` at enqueue; the item Workflow's step wrapper writes every later status together with `current_step` as each step starts. The Workflow writes the finished state when it ends, and a failed item's `error` is the failing step's own error, with `current_step` naming that step. `workflow_instance_id` names the item's Workflow instance, which the retry route restarts; `updated_at` records the last write. `queued_at` is set at enqueue and rewritten whenever the item is queued again: when the API reads a `queued` item whose `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, it restarts the item's instance, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, and rewrites `queued_at`. The poll reads only the row and never the instance, so an item stays readable after Cloudflare drops the instance at the end of its retention window. Both writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status, clears the error and stamps `updated_at`.\n34:| [common-package](common-package.md) | The package both Workers build from: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, the item row's reads and writes, the SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library. |\nA synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the wait for synthesis step has used its attempts. Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0fa97e31-d3f7-4562-b270-ec08abda8b88","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:56:23.841Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"The row always holds the item's status. The API Worker writes `queued` at enqueue; the item Workflow's step wrapper writes every later status together with `current_step` as each step starts. The Workflow writes the finished state when it ends, and a failed item's `error` is the failing step's own error, with `current_step` naming that step. `workflow_instance_id` names the item's Workflow instance, which the retry route restarts; `updated_at` records the last write. `queued_at` is set at enqueue and rewritten whenever the item is queued again: when the API reads a `queued` item whose `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, it restarts the item's instance, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, and rewrites `queued_at`. The poll reads only the row and never the instance, so an item stays readable after Cloudflare drops the instance at the end of its retention window. Both writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status, clears the error and stamps `updated_at`.\n34:| [common-package](common-package.md) | The package both Workers build from: the shared types, the R2 key layout, presigning, the item row's reads and writes, the SQL migrations for D1 and the cassette replay library. |\nA synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the wait for synthesis step has used its attempts. Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f3109fba-9387-4db1-b64b-29c453ebb32f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","re