{"parentUuid":"290c001a-33e3-48b2-8938-91a2bf88b5f2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b0c29400-5764-47e0-b7f6-3520658235fc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019N9o34WBNwDrSdiAhoWP54","type":"tool_result","content":"**docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md**\n\nReplace the paragraph after the first paragraph under \"The step wrapper\":\n\nThe status write sets the status and `current_step` and stamps `updated_at` in one statement. It has two forms: `queued` or `generating` takes no error and clears it, and `failed` requires the error, so the type checker rejects a `failed` write without one. The status write belongs to the [common/ package](common-package.md). The API uses the same write for `queued` at enqueue and on retry, and for `failed` when it cannot create the instance.\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/common-package.md**\n\n\"What it holds\" table, row Item row reads and writes, \"Holds\" and \"Used by\" columns:\n\n| Item row reads and writes | encoding and decoding the JSON columns, and the status write that sets a status and stamps updated_at, clearing the error for queued and generating and requiring one for failed | the API Worker for queued and for a failed enqueue, the step wrapper for every status after enqueue, including `failed` after a step's last attempt | [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) |\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md**\n\nReplace the second sentence of the paragraph beginning \"The row always holds the item's status\":\n\nThe API Worker writes `queued` at enqueue, or `failed` with the error when it cannot create the instance; the item Workflow's step wrapper writes every later status together with `current_step` as each step starts.\n\nReplace the last sentence of that paragraph:\n\nBoth writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status and stamps `updated_at`, clearing the error for `queued` and `generating` and requiring one for `failed`.\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/tts-service.md**\n\n\"What it exposes\", endpoint table, row fetch result, append to the \"Answers\" column:\n\n; `422` for an id Modal never issued or one that is not a call id\n\nReplace the last sentence of the paragraph beginning \"A synthesis that fails every time\":\n\nAfter that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once; a `422` for a call id Modal does not recognise fails it at once too.\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md**\n\nInsert after the sentence ending \"measured on the decoded file.\" in the paragraph beginning \"Validation runs on the **decoded bytes**\":\n\nA smaller raster is dropped and records no degradation.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0ad8256f-e99b-4887-b77e-8152f91ac28d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:56:33.518Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md**\n\nReplace the paragraph after the first paragraph under \"The step wrapper\":\n\nThe status write sets the status and `current_step` and stamps `updated_at` in one statement. It has two forms: `queued` or `generating` takes no error and clears it, and `failed` requires the error, so the type checker rejects a `failed` write without one. The status write belongs to the [common/ package](common-package.md). The API uses the same write for `queued` at enqueue and on retry, and for `failed` when it cannot create the instance.\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/common-package.md**\n\n\"What it holds\" table, row Item row reads and writes, \"Holds\" and \"Used by\" columns:\n\n| Item row reads and writes | encoding and decoding the JSON columns, and the status write that sets a status and stamps updated_at, clearing the error for queued and generating and requiring one for failed | the API Worker for queued and for a failed enqueue, the step wrapper for every status after enqueue, including `failed` after a step's last attempt | [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) |\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md**\n\nReplace the second sentence of the paragraph beginning \"The row always holds the item's status\":\n\nThe API Worker writes `queued` at enqueue, or `failed` with the error when it cannot create the instance; the item Workflow's step wrapper writes every later status together with `current_step` as each step starts.\n\nReplace the last sentence of that paragraph:\n\nBoth writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status and stamps `updated_at`, clearing the error for `queued` and `generating` and requiring one for `failed`.\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/tts-service.md**\n\n\"What it exposes\", endpoint table, row fetch result, append to the \"Answers\" column:\n\n; `422` for an id Modal never issued or one that is not a call id\n\nReplace the last sentence of the paragraph beginning \"A synthesis that fails every time\":\n\nAfter that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once; a `422` for a call id Modal does not recognise fails it at once too.\n\n---\n\n**docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md**\n\nInsert after the sentence ending \"measured on the decoded file.\" in the paragraph beginning \"Validation runs on the **decoded bytes**\":\n\nA smaller raster is dropped and records no degradation.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4bd279a4-2a28-4b1f-8c32-12d0fbe4e839","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibi