s each step starts.\"),\n(\"Both writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status, clears the error and stamps `updated_at`.\",\"Both writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status and stamps `updated_at`, clearing the error for `queued` and `generating` and requiring one for `failed`.\"),\n])\nedit('tts-service.md',[\n(\"`410` once Modal no longer holds the result |\",\"`410` once Modal no longer holds the result; `422` for an id Modal never issued or one that is not a call id |\"),\n(\"After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.\",\"After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once; a `422` for a call id Modal does not recognise fails it at once too.\"),\n])\nedit('article-extraction.md',[(re.compile(r\"(measured on the decoded file\\.)\"),r\"\\1 A smaller raster is dropped and records no degradation.\")])\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ngit diff --stat; git add docs && git commit -q -m \"docs: record what the Cloudflare migration test design settled\" && git log --oneline -1"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6c0ec487-744a-4b8c-8bcf-38885cd58f33","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuwBjJMZgRDZwcBqPEPY","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e35aa61-d6ec-4cc9-a5e7-e8c864f12564","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:57:01.866Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"9e35aa61-d6ec-4cc9-a5e7-e8c864f12564","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b3f0753f-71bb-4af5-adba-c6fa786180ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LErWC2v4oTvmBymawzMrXU","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\n docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md      | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/common-package.md          | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md          | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/tts-service.md             | 4 ++--\n 5 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\nfdc0c1a docs: record what the Cloudflare migration test design settled","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4d68dd7b-03a7-4bd6-af7f-d6f821e1232c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:57:02.407Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok\n docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md      | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/common-package.md          | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md          | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md | 2 +-\n docs/technical-design/tts-service.md             | 4 ++--\n 5 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\nfdc0c1a docs: record what the Cloudflare migration test design settled","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":239,"oldLines":7,"newStart":239,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Every step runs inside one wrapper holding the logic common to all of them. At the start of each attempt, inside the step, the wrapper writes `current_step` and the status the step is given, and clears the error, so a restart from that step writes them again. fetch and lease are given `queued`; every later step is given `generating`, so the item shows `generating` from the moment the lease is held. When a step's last attempt fails, the wrapper writes `failed` and the step's own error. A not-article verdict fails the recipe step at once, without its remaining attempts. An attempt that fails while attempts remain writes nothing, so a step's automatic retries never show `failed`."," ","-The status write sets the status, clears the error and stamps `updated_at` in one statement. It belongs to the [common/ package](common-package.md), and the API uses the same write for `queued` at enqueue and on retry.","+The status write sets the status and `current_step` and stamps `updated_at` in one statement. It has two forms: `queued` or `generating` takes no error and clears it, and `failed` requires the error, so the type checker rejects a `failed` write without one. The status write belongs to the [common/ package](common-package.md). The API uses the same write for `queued` at enqueue and on retry, and for `failed` when it cannot create the instance."," "," ### 🗣️ The describe fan-out"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/common-package.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":59,"oldLines":7,"newStart":59,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Workflow params type | the item id the API Worker creates and restarts the item Workflow with | the API Worker, the item Workflow | [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) |"," | R2 key layout | the bucket's audio/ and images/ prefixes, and the functions that build an audio key from an item id and an image key from a content hash | the API Worker, the item Workflow | [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) |"," | Presigning | one function that signs a GET or a PUT URL for a key with a given R2 token and lifetime | the API Worker for GET, the pipeline Worker for PUT | [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) |","-| Item row reads and writes | encoding and decoding the JSON columns, and the status write that sets a status, clears the error and stamps updated_at | the API Worker for queued, the step wrapper for every later status | [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) |","+| Item row reads and writes | encoding and decoding the JSON columns, and the status write that sets a status and stamps updated_at, clearing the error for queued and generating and requiring one for failed | the API Worker for queued and for a failed enqueue, the step wrapper for every status after enqueue, including `failed` after a step's last attempt | [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) |"," | SQL migrations | the D1 schema, as hand-written SQL files | the Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job, both Workers' tests, local development | [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md), [local-development](local-development.md) |"," | Cassette replay library | our TypeScript copy of vcrpy, replay only | both Workers' integration tests | this note |"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":41,"oldLines":7,"newStart":41,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," The database has three tables: `items`, one row per enqueued article; `recipe_versions`, one row per version of a domain's recipe; and `cost_entries`, one row per metered call. The item row's full field list is in [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md); the diagram shows the fields this note is about. Audio bytes are never a column; they live in the bucket below, keyed by item id, so a multi-megabyte file never bloats the row."," ","-The row always holds the item's status. The API Worker writes `queued` at enqueue; the item Workflow's step wrapper writes every later status together with `current_step` as each step starts. The Workflow writes the finished state when it ends, and a failed item's `error` is the failing step's own error, with `current_step` naming that step. `workflow_instance_id` names the item's Workflow instance, which the retry route restarts; `updated_at` records the last write. `queued_at` is set at enqueue and rewritten whenever the item is queued again: when the API reads a `queued` item whose `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, it restarts the item's instance, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, and rewrites `queued_at`. The poll reads only the row and never the instance, so an item stays readable after Cloudflare drops the instance at the end of its retention window. Both writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status, clears the error and stamps `updated_at`.","+The row always holds the item's status. The API Worker writes `queued` at enqueue, or `failed` with the error when it cannot create the instance; the item Workflow's step wrapper writes every later status together with `current_step` as each step starts. The Workflow writes the finished state when it ends, and a failed item's `error` is the failing step's own error, with `current_step` naming that step. `workflow_instance_id` names the item's Workflow instance, which the retry route restarts; `updated_at` records the last write. `queued_at` is set at enqueue and rewritten whenever the item is queued again: when the API reads a `queued` item whose `queued_at` is more than 15 minutes old, it restarts the item's instance, or creates one when the row holds no instance id, and rewrites `queued_at`. The poll reads only the row and never the instance, so an item stays readable after Cloudflare drops the instance at the end of its retention window. Both writers go through the status write in [common/](common-package.md), which sets a status and stamps `updated_at`, clearing the error for `queued` and `generating` and requiring one for `failed`."," "," The Workflow writes `units` and `degradations` into the row as soon as a step produces them, and later steps read them back from the row. The recipe step writes the title together with the units, which carry their display and spoken forms; the images step rewrites them, and the describe step writes every described unit's spoken form, with its degradations and ledger rows, in one write at its end. Its child steps, one per description and run concurrently, only return their results to it. The API returns the units to a client only once the item is `ready`."," "]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/tts-service.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":7,"newStart":20,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Endpoint | Takes | Answers |"," |---|---|---|"," | start synthesis | the spoken forms, one string per read-along unit in unit order; the Kokoro voice, defaulting to `af_heart`; the destination URL, a presigned R2 PUT URL for the item's audio key | Modal's call id for this synthesis, at once |","-| fetch result | the call id | `202` while the synthesis runs; `200` with the result below once it is done; `500` when the synthesis raised; `410` once Modal no longer holds the result |","+| fetch result | the call id | `202` while the synthesis runs; `200` with the result below once it is done; `500` when the synthesis raised; `410` once Modal no longer holds the result; `422` for an id Modal never issued or one that is not a call id |"," "," | Result field | Answers |"," |---|---|"]},{"oldStart":77,"oldLines":7,"newStart":77,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," The item Workflow's start synthesis step signs the PUT URL and calls the start endpoint, which spawns the synthesis and answers with Modal's call id at once (1, 2). Modal uploads the audio to the bucket when the synthesis finishes (3). The wait for synthesis step asks the result endpoint for the call id every 5 seconds until the result is ready (4, 5). The store step then writes the finished state into the item row together with the tts ledger row, priced by the audio's length (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). The call id and the result pass from step to step as step results; the item row holds neither. Each step gets 3 attempts. Start synthesis has 2 minutes per attempt, and wait for synthesis has 15 minutes."," ","-A synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the wait for synthesis step has used its attempts. Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once.","+A synthesis that fails every time fails the item once the wait for synthesis step has used its attempts. Modal discards a result 7 days after the call. After that the result endpoint answers `410`, and the item fails at once; a `422` for a call id Modal does not recognise fails it at once too."," "," > [!WARNING] A start repeated after a deploy synthesizes twice"," > Modal accepts no idempotency key and no caller-chosen call id, so a start synthesis step that runs again after a deploy spawns a second synthesis. Both upload to the same audio key, keyed by the item id, so the second upload overwrites the first and the item still has one audio file. The cost is one extra synthesis, which is accepted."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":95,"oldLines":7,"newStart":95,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," A declared image is downloaded under a per-host semaphore (default 2) beneath a global one (default 10), with a 10-second timeout and a 10 MB streamed size cap. The per-host bound is the one that matters: one article's many same-host images must never open that many connections to a server nagara has no relationship with. A Workers instance holds 6 outbound connections at a time, so at most 6 downloads run at once whatever the global bound."," ","-Validation runs on the **decoded bytes**, never on HTTP or HTML metadata. The bytes are sniffed for an `<svg` root. A raster image goes through Cloudflare's Images binding, which decodes it outside the Worker, and is **kept when `min(width, height) >= 200`**, measured on the decoded file. What survives is re-encoded to WebP through the same binding. Each kept image is stored once per content hash, taken over the stored bytes, under the images prefix of the R2 bucket, with its content type on the object, and the hash becomes the unit's image reference, so no origin URL leaks into persisted markdown. common/'s image key function builds the object's key from the hash (see [common-package](common-package.md), and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) for the bucket layout).","+Validation runs on the **decoded bytes**, never on HTTP or HTML metadata. The bytes are sniffed for an `<svg` root. A raster image goes through Cloudflare's Images binding, which decodes it outside the Worker, and is **kept when `min(width, height) >= 200`**, \\1 A smaller raster is dropped and records no degradation. What survives is re-encoded to WebP through the same binding. Each kept image is stored once per content hash, taken over the stored bytes, under the images prefix of the R2 bucket, with its content type on the object, and the hash becomes the unit's image reference, so no origin URL leaks into persisted markdown. common/'s image key function builds the object's key from the hash (see [common-package](common-package.md), and [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) for the bucket layout)."," "," > [!NOTE] Why validate by decoding, not by trusting the attributes or the Content-Type"," > Most of the corpus omits `width`/`height` entirely (all four New Yorker contact sheets carry neither), and a Content-Type header can lie, so the only trustworthy size and format come from decoding the file itself. The 200 px floor sits in a gap in the corpus: avatars and tracking pixels cluster around 40 px and every legitimate figure is 305 px or larger. Two square brand logos survive it, accepted rather than chased, because a square-ratio rule has no legitimate square image in the corpus to test against and a false positive costs only one cheap describe call."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/common-package.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/tts-service.md","/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c0ec487-744a-4b8c-8bcf-38885cd58f33","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e35aa61-d6ec-4cc9-a5e7-e8c864f12564","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
