{"parentUuid":"f0bde3e3-793b-483e-89fe-e72ec03e9fe4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuwMifSWPWF3kmXZiTQs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12020,"cache_read_input_tokens":457739,"output_tokens":2840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1259},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12020,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2840,"cache_read_input_tokens":457739,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12020,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12020},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":18593,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"18b1c588-2847-42be-8149-64dadbe7fc68","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfuwMiAfUwzMz5pKo227R","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:tasks","attributionPlugin":"mahou","attributionMcpServer":"linear-server","attributionMcpTool":"list_issues","type":"assistant","uuid":"47280170-77ba-417f-9af6-b0ea2fbe88d4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:59:28.777Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"47280170-77ba-417f-9af6-b0ea2fbe88d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuwMifSWPWF3kmXZiTQs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker is Linear: project nagara, milestone **Cloudflare migration**. The milestone has no issues yet. I've drawn the candidates from the docs notes, `program-design/nagara.md` and `test-design/nagara.md`. The test rows go into each task's brief and don't become tasks of their own. They're in the order the work would run, and all are on `feat/cloudflare-migration`:\n\n| # | Candidate task | What it requires | Notes | Test rows |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Workspace and the common/ package** | Root pnpm workspace with one lockfile. common/ gets the types, keys, presign, the two-form writeStatus, readItem, restartPoint, the `0001_initial.sql` migration, and the cassette replay library under `./testing`. | common-package, persistence-and-storage | A1–A17 |\n| 2 | **tts/: start and result web endpoints** | Proxy-auth endpoints with pydantic models. Synthesize uploads to the destination URL. The result endpoint answers 202, 200, 500, 410 or 422. | tts-service | B1–B10 |\n| 3 | **pipeline/: DomainQueue as a lease for the item Workflow** | acquire, release and advance on the synchronous KV store, with `sendEvent` lease-granted. A waiting id keeps its place. JobIndex is removed. | item-lifecycle (DomainQueue) | C22–C28 |\n| 4 | **pipeline/: the item Workflow through recipe** | The ItemWorkflow, the step wrapper, the Firecrawl client and fetch, lease and release, and the recipe step (settle, spoken form, sanitize, title and units, declared images as the step result). The public routes and the extraction Workflow go. Includes the fake agent reply for tests (test-design task). | item-lifecycle, article-extraction, recipes | fetch, lease and recipe rows of C1–C21 |\n| 5 | **pipeline/: the images step** | Downloads under the semaphores, SVG script stripping, rasters through the Images binding, R2 storage by hash, degradations. Includes checking whether the Images binding works under the vitest plugin (test-design task). | article-extraction | C11, C12 |\n| 6 | **pipeline/: the describe step** | The ported describer core and prompts, the good-alt filter, the child-step fan-out with the cap, one write at the end, and ledger rows with the cache flag. | image-and-code-describer | C13, C14 |\n| 7 | **pipeline/: start synthesis, wait for synthesis, store** | PUT signing with the upload endpoint swap, the Modal client, polling inside one step, store's length guard and the tts ledger row. The whole-run rows land here once every step exists. | tts-service, item-lifecycle | C1, C15–C21 |\n| 8 | **api/: the TypeScript API Worker** | Replaces the Python tree: guard, enqueue with failure on a failed create, poll with the claimed re-queue, the retry claim, media 307s, and a stand-in for the Workflow binding. Cassettes move to `pipeline/test/`. | item-contract, authentication, item-lifecycle | D1–D27 |\n| 9 | **Local development setup** | Shared state folder, `migrate:local`, the tunnel proxy, `.dev.vars.example`, and `persistState` in the Vite config. | local-development | manual parts of C1, D4, D5 |\n| 10 | **CI: one Cloudflare workflow** | `cloudflare.yml` with a paths filter and the migrate, pipeline, api chain. It replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`. | deployment-and-ci | none |\n| 11 | **Switchover to Cloudflare** | Create the production D1, R2, tokens and secrets. Deploy, point `nagara.asermax.com` at the API Worker, remove the Access app and its service token, run the manual checks, then delete the Railway resources. | deployment-and-ci, shape \"Switching over\" | every \"test + manual\" row, by hand |\n\nTwo existing loose issues are superseded by these rows. I propose canceling each with a comment naming the row that covers it:\n- ASE-28, \"spawn failure inside create_item lands the item in failed\", is covered by D4 in task 8.\n- ASE-29, \"poll route rejects a missing or wrong API key\", is covered by D25 in task 8.\n\nThe rest of the backlog stays as it is. That includes ASE-19 (describe budget) and ASE-27 (footnote markers), which touch code these tasks port, but neither design changed them.\n\nFor each candidate, tell me whether to create it, reshape it or drop it. Also confirm the two cancellations."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12020,"cache_read_input_tokens":457739,"output_tokens":2840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1259},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12020,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2840,"cache_read_input_tokens":457739,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12020,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12020},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"18b1c588-2847-42be-8149-64dadbe7fc68","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfuwMiAfUwzMz5pKo227R","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:tasks","attributionPlugin":"mahou","attributionMcpServer":"linear-server","attributionMcpTool":"list_issues","type":"assistant","uuid":"844c9089-2a6e-4338-a539-2c2fb7f4b74b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:59:35.904Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
