{"parentUuid":"dd25bb68-77dd-4815-8a24-053757bf33a6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuwT8exkWYyPn3FB1WwL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011XEvYA6eUFLa5BtbfAXLrG","name":"mcp__linear-server__save_issue","input":{"team":"ASE","project":"nagara","milestone":"Cloudflare migration","title":"pipeline/: DomainQueue as a lease for the item Workflow","labels":["Feature"],"priority":2,"description":"Turn DomainQueue from the creator of extraction instances into a lease the item Workflow asks for:\n\n- `acquire(instanceId)` → granted when the id holds the lease, or the lease is free and the FIFO empty; otherwise the id is appended once, keeping its place when it is already waiting\n- `release(instanceId)` drops the id from the FIFO and, when it holds the lease, hands the lease on\n- `advance` checks the next id's status, writes the lease and sends `lease-granted`; a terminal or throwing id is skipped\n- `alarm` (60 s) sweeps an ended or unaddressable holder, re-arms for a running one\n\nState moves to the synchronous `ctx.storage.kv`; the FIFO holds instance ids only. `enqueue`, `stateOf`, the params storage and the JobIndex Durable Object go (with a `deleted_classes` migration).\n\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md` (\"One extraction per domain: DomainQueue\").\n\nTest rows C22–C28 from the test design.\n\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1884,"cache_read_input_tokens":472637,"output_tokens":5866,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1884,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5866,"cache_read_input_tokens":472637,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1884},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011XEvYA6eUFLa5BtbfAXLrG":{"team":"ASE","project":"nagara","milestone":"Cloudflare migration","title":"pipeline/: DomainQueue as a lease for the item Workflow","labels":["Feature"],"priority":2,"description":"Turn DomainQueue from the creator of extraction instances into a lease the item Workflow asks for:\n\n- `acquire(instanceId)` → granted when the id holds the lease, or the lease is free and the FIFO empty; otherwise the id is appended once, keeping its place when it is already waiting\n- `release(instanceId)` drops the id from the FIFO and, when it holds the lease, hands the lease on\n- `advance` checks the next id's status, writes the lease and sends `lease-granted`; a terminal or throwing id is skipped\n- `alarm` (60 s) sweeps an ended or unaddressable holder, re-arms for a running one\n\nState moves to the synchronous `ctx.storage.kv`; the FIFO holds instance ids only. `enqueue`, `stateOf`, the params storage and the JobIndex Durable Object go (with a `deleted_classes` migration).\n\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md` (\"One extraction per domain: DomainQueue\").\n\nTest rows C22–C28 from the test design.\n\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a8661d95-feda-4eae-a12a-324a6fd99f6c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfuwT8BRxMziRW9fuBjht","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"linear-server","attributionMcpTool":"save_issue","type":"assistant","uuid":"754c2f8c-260a-495a-b605-608984b16d4c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:00:31.518Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"754c2f8c-260a-495a-b605-608984b16d4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuwT8exkWYyPn3FB1WwL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L9qHD3vMjCqd6bNhpJX59S","name":"mcp__linear-server__save_issue","input":{"team":"ASE","project":"nagara","milestone":"Cloudflare migration","title":"pipeline/: the item Workflow through the recipe step","labels":["Feature"],"priority":2,"description":"Build the item Workflow and its first four steps:\n\n- `ItemWorkflow` (binding `ITEM_WORKFLOW`, params `{itemId}`) and the step wrapper: the status write inside each attempt, the step's own error on the last attempt, rethrow\n- fetch through our own Firecrawl client (the Python SDK's fields, `rawHtml` and `markdown` at `proxy: auto`): instance id, domain, ledger row, the HTML as the step result, the 1 MiB cap\n- lease (ask DomainQueue, up to 3 waits of 5 minutes for `lease-granted`, a re-check after each) and release\n- recipe: run, author or revise (conversation id = instance id), save a new version, then the spoken-form derivation and sanitize tail (ported from `api/app/service/extract.py`), the drop rule, title and units on the row, the declared images as the step result\n\nThe public routes (`http/`), the extraction Workflow and the `WORLD_SEAM` test seam go. Includes the test design's task: the tests configure the agents to answer with a scripted reply (a script, a not-article verdict, or giving up) through configuration, not an environment branch.\n\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md`, `docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md`, `docs/technical-design/recipes.md`, `docs/technical-design/markdown-units.md`.\n\nTest rows: the fetch, lease and recipe rows of C1–C21 (C2–C10, C20); C7 and C9 are also run by hand.\n\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1884,"cache_read_input_tokens":472637,"output_tokens":5866,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1884,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5866,"cache_read_input_tokens":472637,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1884},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L9qHD3vMjCqd6bNhpJX59S":{"team":"ASE","project":"nagara","milestone":"Cloudflare migration","title":"pipeline/: the item Workflow through the recipe step","labels":["Feature"],"priority":2,"description":"Build the item Workflow and its first four steps:\n\n- `ItemWorkflow` (binding `ITEM_WORKFLOW`, params `{itemId}`) and the step wrapper: the status write inside each attempt, the step's own error on the last attempt, rethrow\n- fetch through our own Firecrawl client (the Python SDK's fields, `rawHtml` and `markdown` at `proxy: auto`): instance id, domain, ledger row, the HTML as the step result, the 1 MiB cap\n- lease (ask DomainQueue, up to 3 waits of 5 minutes for `lease-granted`, a re-check after each) and release\n- recipe: run, author or revise (conversation id = instance id), save a new version, then the spoken-form derivation and sanitize tail (ported from `api/app/service/extract.py`), the drop rule, title and units on the row, the declared images as the step result\n\nThe public routes (`http/`), the extraction Workflow and the `WORLD_SEAM` test seam go. Includes the test design's task: the tests configure the agents to answer with a scripted reply (a script, a not-article verdict, or giving up) through configuration, not an environment branch.\n\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md`, `docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md`, `docs/technical-design/recipes.md`, `docs/technical-design/markdown-units.md`.\n\nTest rows: the fetch, lease and recipe rows of C1–C21 (C2–C10, C20); C7 and C9 are also run by hand.\n\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a8661d95-feda-4eae-a12a-324a6fd99f6c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfuwT8BRxMziRW9fuBjht","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"linear-server","attributionMcpTool":"save_issue","type":"assistant","uuid":"7d2db710-9753-41de-97fe-35b1bed4e1b4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:00:37.319Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"7d2db710-9753-41de-97fe-35b1bed4e1b4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuwT8exkWYyPn3FB1WwL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kb7kSrHt27jJgorS35kL6Y","name":"mcp__linear-server__save_issue","input":{"team":"ASE","project":"nagara","milestone":"Cloudflare migration","title":"pipeline/: the images step","labels":["Feature"],"priority":2,"description":"Acquire the images the recipe step hands over as its step result, ported from `api/app/service/images.py`:\n\n- download under the per-host (2) and global (10) semaphores, 10 s, 10 MB\n- sniff `<svg`: an SVG keeps its markup with scripts stripped, the SVG content type, no size floor\n- rasters through the Images binding: kept when the shorter side is at least 200 px (a smaller one drops with no degradation), re-encoded to WebP\n- store under `images/<sha256 of the stored bytes>`; the unit goes after its anchor with display `![alt](/items/<id>/images/<hash>)` and spoken `Image: <alt>` or the floor\n- a failed acquisition drops the unit with a degradation; no surviving unit fails the item\n\nIncludes the test design's task: check that the Images binding works under the vitest plugin locally; if it does not, give the tests a stand-in binding through configuration, or move those rows to manual.\n\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md` (\"Article images\").\n\nTest rows C11 and C12 from the test design; C11 is also run by hand.\n\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1884,"cache_read_input_tokens":472637,"output_tokens":5866,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1884,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inf