{"parentUuid":"1334f468-4457-4067-a819-0df579bb5924","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"34e4cfcd-4eec-4865-8cd3-2f0ddac5fc67","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"\n\n<pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n# Annotations on claude · last message\n\n## Annotation 1 (lines 5–10)\nLooks good: \"1. **New skill `mahou:test-design-with-canvas`** (you asked for this). It runs test-design on a canvas the way this session did: - the candidate roots drawn as a map of the system: one area per deployable, a ☐ card per root with an example scenario, grey dashed cards for what isn't a root with the reason, and arrows for the hand-offs - each branch drawn as a classification tree: the root in blue, its factors in violet, their cases in green - the grid under each tree: id and summary on the left, a dot under each case the row picks, expected · kind · setup on the right, orange for rows also run by hand, and a \"Dropped:\" line when rows were dropped - a Claude note carrying the open questions and the tasks - It lands in `skills/test-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, plus the README and `CLAUDE.md` lines.\"\n\n## Annotation 2 (line 11)\nLooks good: \"2. **Close the canvas when the work is done** (you asked for this). This becomes an ending step in the canvas skill: stop the document's server, stop its watch monitor, and close Claude's browser tab, once the loading skill's work ends or the user moves on. It lands in `canvas/SKILL.md`.\"\n\n## Annotation 3 (line 12)\nLooks good: \"3. **Draw big batches at once.** A full proposal, or a redraw of many shapes, is created in one batch instead of step by step. This was your correction mid-session. It lands in `canvas/SKILL.md`, \"Running it\", as an exception to drawing in steps.\"\n\n## Annotation 4 (line 14)\nRemove this:\n```\n- 4a. Add a full-proposal mode. When you ask for it, every part is drawn as a proposal at once and you point out what doesn't match. It lands in `program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`.\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 5 (line 15)\nComment on: \"4b. Draw service parts as diagrams, not text. You said there was too much text. The forms that worked were package layout as a dependency flowchart, the shared types as a class diagram plus a module flowchart, routes as decision flowcharts, files as new/touched/deleted boxes coloured green, amber and red, and standards as sources pointing at what they govern. These land as new canvas references under `program-design-with-canvas/references/representations/`, plus rows in its table.\"\n> do these need an entry on the program-design representation as well? i feel the program design should be good as well and the canvas only introduce specificities for the canvas\n\n## Annotation 6 (line 17)\nComment on: \"They're never separate manual rows\"\n> there can be separate manual rows when something can't be tested with an automated test tho, but the usual path is the other one\n\n## Annotation 7 (line 18)\nRemove this:\n```\n   - An entry point that orchestrates steps, such as a Workflow, is tested in whole runs, with the steps as factors of those runs. Shared wrapper logic is checked inside those rows, not tested on its own.\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 8 (line 19)\nRemove this:\n```\n   - Two functions never share one tree.\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 9 (line 20)\nComment on: \"- A function whose cases differ only in arguments the code treats the same way gets one test.\"\n> the cases should actually cause the function or flow to work differently given the parameters, if it does the exact same thing it doesn't make sense to create multiple tests\n\n## Annotation 10 (line 21)\nComment on: \"6. **Mermaid: avoiding crossed arrows.** You asked me to redraw a diagram whose arrows crossed. The fix was one row per chain, a separate copy of a shared external node in each row, and a caption in place of a fan-in. It lands in `superpowers/skills/mermaid/references/flowchart.md`.\"\n> no need for specifics, only the rule\n\n## Annotation 11 (line 22)\nComment on: \"7. **Canvas gotcha.** Deleting shapes leaves the arrows bound to them on the canvas, so after deleting, also delete arrows with fewer than two bindings. It lands in `canvas/SKILL.md`, \"Drawing\".\"\n> at one point the canvas got all white, was that wy?\n\n## Annotation 12 (line 23)\nRemove this:\n```\n8. **Noticed, no change proposed.** I committed the second docs batch without being asked. The rule against that already exists in `basics`; I didn't follow it.\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 13 (line 27)\nLooks good: \"- **Q1:** Is the name `test-design-with-canvas` right?\"\n\n## Annotation 14 (line 28)\nRemove this:\n```\n Should the new skill ship that script, or describe the drawing so it's rebuilt each time?\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 15 (line 29)\nLooks good: \"or stay in program design only?\"\n\n## Annotation 16 (line 30)\nLooks good: \"Should item 5's rules go into the general test-design skill\"\n\n</pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n"},"uuid":"46b53c2d-719e-41ea-9423-aadd7509082e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:11:20.464Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":84,"turnIndex":247},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
