{"parentUuid":"b55b0f89-3b37-4e93-8104-a8a0de85de05","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"34e4cfcd-4eec-4865-8cd3-2f0ddac5fc67","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011oXCnbW12VvNFa2R7VFLtG","type":"tool_result","content":"## Styling guidance\n\n- **Colour through the palette's classes**, not inline styles. Apply one class to several nodes with a comma list: `class B,C,F green`.\n- **One-off node styling**, for a node the palette does not cover: `style C fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:3px`.\n- **Highlight a path**: colour edges by their declaration order (0-indexed): `linkStyle 0,1,4 stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:3px`. `linkStyle default` styles every edge.\n- **Use `subgraph` to group** by service, layer or repository. It is the main way to show architecture boundaries in a flow.\n- **Line breaks** inside labels: `A[\"Line one<br/>Line two\"]`.\n- **Match the direction to the content**: `LR` reads as a pipeline, `TD` as a decision tree. Set it on the whole flowchart, not on a subgraph.\n- `mahou:one-page-design`. Draws a settled design as one page on a `canvas`, as a journey (what the user sees step by step, what gets stored on the way and how it is read back) or an anatomy (what one thing is made of and where each part comes from). One element largest in the centre, small supporting views, and a legend for the arrows. The type comes from the context, or from you when more than one fits, and a catalogue of visual patterns backs both types.\n- `mahou:architecture-exploration`. Draws a system's architecture on a `canvas` and explores ways to change it with you. It lays the options out as a grid of small drawings, one per combination, and draws a part they share step by step. After each decision it redraws the chosen one whole, beside the earlier ones, until one architecture remains. Loaded by `explore` when a question is about an architecture.\n- `mahou:explore-with-canvas`, `mahou:shape-with-canvas`, `mahou:design-with-canvas`, `mahou:program-design-with-canvas`. Run the skill they name on a `canvas` instead of in the chat. Explore lays the answers out freely next to a decision log. Shape and design draw the tree as one area per branch, leaves on the left and prose and representations on the right, with questions as violet cards and two kept open at a time; design turns a settled branch's diagrams into `mermaid` shapes and records in the chat at the end. Program design draws each part of a branch (screen layout, component tree, derivation ledger) in its own area from bundled mockups, while the record file keeps the text form.\n- `mahou:telepathy`. A mode: the conversation moves out of the chat and into markdown files in the change's scratch folder, served as a page you edit in the browser. Click a block to edit it or `+` to write under it; Enter or clicking away sends, and each edit reaches the agent's pane through herdr as a message, which the agent answers by writing in the files. The server tracks who wrote each block in `.meta.json`, picks up the agent's writes by diffing against its last snapshot, and merges your edit with the agent's when both touched the same block, opening a merge editor only when the same lines changed. Requires herdr and Bun.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"93854a92-b7fb-4ef0-9eda-03093dc9b29b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:12:22.336Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Styling guidance\n\n- **Colour through the palette's classes**, not inline styles. Apply one class to several nodes with a comma list: `class B,C,F green`.\n- **One-off node styling**, for a node the palette does not cover: `style C fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:3px`.\n- **Highlight a path**: colour edges by their declaration order (0-indexed): `linkStyle 0,1,4 stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:3px`. `linkStyle default` styles every edge.\n- **Use `subgraph` to group** by service, layer or repository. It is the main way to show architecture boundaries in a flow.\n- **Line breaks** inside labels: `A[\"Line one<br/>Line two\"]`.\n- **Match the direction to the content**: `LR` reads as a pipeline, `TD` as a decision tree. Set it on the whole flowchart, not on a subgraph.\n- `mahou:one-page-design`. Draws a settled design as one page on a `canvas`, as a journey (what the user sees step by step, what gets stored on the way and how it is read back) or an anatomy (what one thing is made of and where each part comes from). One element largest in the centre, small supporting views, and a legend for the arrows. The type comes from the context, or from you when more than one fits, and a catalogue of visual patterns backs both types.\n- `mahou:architecture-exploration`. Draws a system's architecture on a `canvas` and explores ways to change it with you. It lays the options out as a grid of small drawings, one per combination, and draws a part they share step by step. After each decision it redraws the chosen one whole, beside the earlier ones, until one architecture remains. Loaded by `explore` when a question is about an architecture.\n- `mahou:explore-with-canvas`, `mahou:shape-with-canvas`, `mahou:design-with-canvas`, `mahou:program-design-with-canvas`. Run the skill they name on a `canvas` instead of in the chat. Explore lays the answers out freely next to a decision log. Shape and design draw the tree as one area per branch, leaves on the left and prose and representations on the right, with questions as violet cards and two kept open at a time; design turns a settled branch's diagrams into `mermaid` shapes and records in the chat at the end. Program design draws each part of a branch (screen layout, component tree, derivation ledger) in its own area from bundled mockups, while the record file keeps the text form.\n- `mahou:telepathy`. A mode: the conversation moves out of the chat and into markdown files in the change's scratch folder, served as a page you edit in the browser. Click a block to edit it or `+` to write under it; Enter or clicking away sends, and each edit reaches the agent's pane through herdr as a message, which the agent answers by writing in the files. The server tracks who wrote each block in `.meta.json`, picks up the agent's writes by diffing against its last snapshot, and merges your edit with the agent's when both touched the same block, opening a merge editor only when the same lines changed. Requires herdr and Bun.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bec084c7-9eb3-44b4-b88f-e8aa35c80b17","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b55b0f89-3b37-4e93-8104-a8a0de85de05","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
