{"parentUuid":"88888ef3-52aa-4ff2-9f5a-51160560fb73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuxxKgussULiiiUCbTdL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018cmJWJSCXbGLZ8wKbLKXww","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round3 && cat > /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round3/item4.md <<'EOF'\n# Item 4: canvas references for program design's service representations\n\nEach lands in `mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/references/representations/`, with a row in the skill's table.\n\n## package-layout.md\n\n# Package layout on the canvas\n\n`program-design`'s package layout reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the annotated file tree.\n\n## Representation\n\nOne `mermaid` shape holding a flowchart of the packages. Each package is a node labelled with its folder, its package name and how it is built or run. The workspace is a document node joined to the packages it holds, and a target a package deploys to is a store or a cloud. Label each edge between packages with what one imports from the other, and colour each package by the deployable it belongs to, with the palette in superpowers:mermaid.\n\nUnder the shape, one or two lines: what is published or built, and the dependencies the change adds.\n\n## interfaces.md\n\n# Interfaces on the canvas\n\n`program-design`'s interfaces reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the JSON Schemas.\n\n## Representation\n\nTwo `mermaid` shapes. The first holds a class diagram of the shapes that cross between parts: one class per shape, its members with `?` on the optional ones, a stereotype for a union, and an edge for each shape that holds another. The second holds a flowchart of who calls what: the parts the branch adds or changes as nodes grouped by module, each labelled with the operations it exposes, and an edge from each caller to the part it calls, labelled when the call carries a direction or a mode, such as `GET` and `PUT`.\n\nUnder the shapes, one or two lines on what the diagrams cannot show, such as what an operation answers in a case the record spells out.\n\n## callstack.md\n\n# Callstack on the canvas\n\n`program-design`'s callstack reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the text tree.\n\n## Representation\n\nOne `mermaid` shape per entry, holding a top-to-bottom flowchart from the request and what it is given to every response it can give. A check is a diamond, an action a rectangle coloured by the deployable that runs it, a refusal a red terminal with its status, and a success a green one. A failure the entry absorbs is a dotted edge labelled with what went wrong. Two entries that share their parts may share one shape.\n\nUnder the shape, one or two lines stating the rule the flowchart implements.\n\n## module-list.md\n\n# Module list on the canvas\n\n`program-design`'s module list reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the paths.\n\n## Representation\n\nOne `mermaid` shape holding a flowchart with three subgraphs: deleted, touched and new. Each node is a file or a set of files in one folder, labelled with the path and, when the path alone does not say it, why it changes. New nodes are green, touched amber and deleted red.\n\nUnder the shape, one or two lines on the placement decisions.\n\n## standards.md\n\n# Standards on the canvas\n\n`program-design`'s standards reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the list.\n\n## Representation\n\nOne `mermaid` shape holding a flowchart: each source of conventions is a document node, joined to a node listing what it governs in this root.\n\n## Table rows in program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md\n\n| Package layout | `package-layout.md` | `references/representations/package-layout.md` |\n| Interfaces | `interfaces.md` | `references/representations/interfaces.md` |\n| Callstack | `callstack.md` | `references/representations/callstack.md` |\n| Module list | `module-list.md` | `references/representations/module-list.md` |\n| Standards | `standards.md` | `references/representations/standards.md` |\nEOF\ncd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; python3 - \"$PWD/learn/round3/item4.md\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\nd=sys.argv[1]\ns=open('briefs/unslop-learn2-r1.md').read()\na=s.index('Read ')+5; b=s.index('. Do not edit anything.')\nopen('briefs/unslop-learn3b-r1.md','w').write(s[:a]+d+s[b:])\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"unslop learn3 item4\" --model opus --body-file briefs/unslop-learn3b-r1.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1528,"cache_read_input_tokens":537399,"output_tokens":1730,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":59},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1528,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":537399,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1528,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1528},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018cmJWJSCXbGLZ8wKbLKXww":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round3 && 