{"parentUuid":"90ec90c6-74dd-4a90-95cf-36f1582da1b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuxz3i2nFi8MrnGdEH5T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015keUPQPSkPCzH8JitZNyyd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"P=/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins; M=$P/mahou/skills; mkdir -p $M/test-design-with-canvas && cat > $M/test-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: test-design-with-canvas\ndescription: Runs the test-design skill on a canvas instead of in the chat. The candidate roots are drawn on a map of the system for the user to pick, and each branch is drawn as a classification tree with its combination matrix under it; the user corrects with sticky notes or by voice. Use when the user wants to design the test cases and manual validations of a settled change on a canvas.\nargument-hint: <the settled design to prove>\n---\n\nLoad mahou:test-design first, then mahou:canvas. Then read `.mahou/test-design-with-canvas.md` if present.\n\n# Test design with canvas\n\n`test-design` and the skills it loads keep their procedure: roots, branches, classifications, partitions, matrices, facts, dropped rows, recording and ending.\n\nThe document is `canvas/test-design.tldr.json` in the change's scratch folder. The record stays `test-design/<repo>.md`; write a tree's change into it whenever the canvas changes, and draw the canvas from it.\n\n## Roots on a map of the system\n\nThe candidate roots go on the canvas as a map of the system, under a title naming the change and the order the trees are worked in.\n\n- **Each tree is an `area`**, labelled with its letter, its repository or deployable, and what it is to the rest of the system, such as `B <service>/: what a client calls`. Lay the areas out in the order work flows through them, whoever starts it on the left; put the tree that every other one imports along the bottom.\n- **Each candidate root is a blue card** inside its tree's area. Its first line is an empty checkbox, `☐`, for the user to tick, then the root's id and its entry point; its second line is `e.g. <scenario>`, one or two scenarios through that entry point, an error case among them.\n- **A candidate that is not a root is a grey dashed card** with the reason, such as a piece that runs only inside another entry point, or a migration validated through a read.\n- **Arrows join the cards that hand work to each other**, each labelled with the action one card asks of the other, such as `create` or `start`.\n\nTell the user to tick or cross out cards with sticky notes or by voice.\n\n## Each branch is a classification tree\n\nEach branch is an `area` labelled `<id> <root> · <status>`, inside its tree's area. Branches stack down their tree's area, and the trees sit side by side.\n\n- **The root is a blue box** at the top, with the entry point and what it is given.\n- **Each classification is a violet box** under the root, joined to it by a line with no arrowheads.\n- **Each partition is a green box** under its classification, joined the same way, with a short label.\n- **The matrix goes under the tree.** A header line reads `row · what the test does` on the left and `expected · kind · setup` on the right, both in grey. Each row is one line: its id and summary on the left, a filled dot under the centre of each partition it picks, and its expected outcome, kind and setup on the right. Dotted grey lines run between the rows and down each partition's column.\n- **A row run by hand is orange**, its text and its dots, whether it is `test + manual` or `manual`. Its expected outcome adds what the check observes by hand.\n- **Dropped rows get a grey line under the matrix**, `Dropped: <reason>`.\n- **A branch with one row** draws its root and that row, with no classifications.\n\n## Messages from Claude\n\nWrite what you would say in the chat as one Claude note at the top of the canvas: how to read the drawing, the open questions, and the implementation tasks the trees surfaced. Replace its text each round.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nP='/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(P+p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert a in s,(p,a[:60]); s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n    open(P+p,'w').write(s)\nedit('mahou/README.md',[(\"`mahou:program-design-with-canvas`. Run the skill they name\",\"`mahou:program-design-with-canvas`, `mahou:test-design-with-canvas`. Run the skill they name\"),\n (\"while the record file keeps the text form.\",\"while the record file keeps the text form. Test design draws the candidate roots on a map of the system for you to pick, then each branch as a classification tree with its matrix under it, a dot under each partition that a row picks.\")])\ns=open(P+'CLAUDE.md').read()\nanchor=\"while `program-design/<root>.md` keeps the text form)\"\nassert anchor in s\ns=s.replace(anchor, anchor+\", `test-design-with-canvas` (added 2026-10-11: runs test-design on a canvas; the candidate roots as ☐ cards on a map of the system, one area per tree, grey dashed cards for what is not a root; each branch a classification tree, root blue, classifications violet, partitions green, with the matrix under it as dots under the partitions and orange rows for those run by hand; `test-design/<repo>.md` keeps the record)\",1)\nopen(P+'CLAUDE.md','w').write(s)\nedit('mahou/skills/canvas/SKILL.md',[\n(\"## What this skill is not\",\"## Ending\\n\\nWhen the loading skill's work is done, or the user moves on to other work, stop the canvas: run `canvas.sh stop` on the document, stop the monitor running `canvas.sh watch`, and close your `agent-browser` tab.\\n\\n## What this skill is not\"),\n(\"- A note goes right after the element it describes, and its arrow right after the note.\\n\",\"- A note goes right after the element it describes, and its arrow right after the note.\\n\\nDraw a large batch in one script instead, without `canvas.step`, when a change creates or redraws many shapes at once, such as every tree rebuilt from a revised record. Stepping through hundreds of shapes makes the user wait for a drawing they will read only once it is finished.\\n\"),\n(\"- **Group what moves together.**\",\"- **Delete the arrows of the shapes you delete.** An arrow bound to a deleted shape stays on the canvas where it was drawn. After deleting shapes, delete every arrow with fewer than two bindings.\\n- **Group what moves together.**\"),\n])\nedit('mahou/skills/test-design/SKILL.md',[\n(\"Two partitions that the code treats identically are one partition.\",\"Two partitions that the code treats identically are one partition. When every input takes the code down the same path, the root is one row.\"),\n(\"The manual picks on a service always include the most common flows, error cases included. Schema rejections are not manual picks.\",\"Pick the manual checks from the test rows: a picked row's kind becomes `test + manual`, and its expected outcome adds what the check observes by hand. On a service they always include the most common flows and the most common error cases. A row is `manual` alone only when no automated test can check it. Schema rejections are not manual picks.\"),\n])\ns=open(P+'superpowers/skills/mermaid/references/flowchart.md').read()\na=\"- **Match the direction to the content**: `LR` reads as a pipeline, `TD` as a decision tree. Set it on the whole flowchart, not on a subgraph.\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a, a+\"\\n- **Keep edges from crossing where the layout allows.** When edges cross, try reordering the nodes or restructuring the diagram; some diagrams cross anyway.\",1)\nopen(P+'superpowers/skills/mermaid/references/flowchart.md','w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ncd $P && git status --short | grep -v \"^ M\\|^RM\\|^R \" "},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284,"cache_read_input_tokens":540732,"output_tokens":269