{"parentUuid":"62d5f69e-f62f-4271-a404-0cae487bae4d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuy54Qqn1za8tPWaDUxD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written items 1, 2, 3, 5, 6 and 7 to claude-plugins with your corrections. None of it is committed.\n\n- **1. `mahou/skills/test-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, new.**\n  - The example tree label is generic: `B <service>/: what a client calls`.\n  - The ☐ is now explained as an empty checkbox for you to tick. That's what the symbol was: the empty ballot-box character.\n  - The arrow labels read \"such as `create` or `start`\", so they come across as examples.\n  - The Ending section is gone. Stopping the canvas is covered by item 2.\n  - The mahou README and the claude-plugins `CLAUDE.md` now list the skill.\n- **2 and 3. `canvas/SKILL.md`.** It gets a new Ending section that stops the server and the watch monitor and closes the tab. \"Running it\" gets the exception for drawing a large batch in one script.\n- **5. `test-design/SKILL.md`.** It gets the one-row rule and the rule for picking manual checks from the test rows.\n- **6. `superpowers/skills/mermaid/references/flowchart.md`.** The rule now reads \"Keep edges from crossing where the layout allows. When edges cross, try reordering the nodes or restructuring the diagram; some diagrams cross anyway.\"\n- **7. `canvas/SKILL.md`, \"Drawing\".** It gets the rule to delete arrows left behind by deleted shapes.\n\nFor item 4, the program-design representations stay as they are. The diagram forms become canvas-only references in `program-design-with-canvas/references/representations/`, with one row each in that skill's table. These drafts went through both cleanup rounds. Approve them and I'll write them:\n\n**`package-layout.md`**\n> # Package layout on the canvas\n>\n> `program-design`'s package layout reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the annotated file tree.\n>\n> ## Representation\n>\n> One `mermaid` shape holding a flowchart of the packages. Each package is a node labelled with its folder, its package name and how it is built or run. The workspace is a document node joined to the packages it holds, and a target that a package deploys to is a store or a cloud. Label each edge between packages with the names one package imports from the other, and colour each package by the deployable it belongs to, with the palette in superpowers:mermaid.\n>\n> Under the shape, one or two lines: the artifacts the change publishes or builds, and the dependencies it adds.\n\n**`interfaces.md`**\n> # Interfaces on the canvas\n>\n> `program-design`'s interfaces reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the JSON Schemas.\n>\n> ## Representation\n>\n> Two `mermaid` shapes. The first holds a class diagram of the shapes that cross between parts: one class per shape, its members with `?` on the optional ones, a stereotype for a union, and an edge for each shape that holds another. The second holds a flowchart of the calls between parts. Each part the branch adds or changes is a node, grouped by module and labelled with the operations it exposes. An edge runs from each caller to the part it calls, labelled with the call's direction or mode when it has one, such as `GET` or `PUT`.\n>\n> Under the shapes, one or two lines on what the diagrams cannot show, such as the response an operation returns in a case that the record describes.\n\n**`callstack.md`**\n> # Callstack on the canvas\n>\n> `program-design`'s callstack reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the text tree.\n>\n> ## Representation\n>\n> One `mermaid` shape per entry, holding a top-to-bottom flowchart from the request and its inputs to every response the entry can return. A check is a diamond, an action a rectangle coloured by the deployable that runs it, a refusal a red terminal with its status, and a success a green one. A failure that the entry handles without refusing the request is a dotted edge labelled with the error. Two entries that share their parts may share one shape.\n>\n> Under the shape, one or two lines stating the rule the flowchart implements.\n\n**`module-list.md`**\n> # Module list on the canvas\n>\n> `program-design`'s module list reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the paths.\n>\n> ## Representation\n>\n> One `mermaid` shape holding a flowchart with three subgraphs: deleted, touched and new. Each node is a file or a set of files in one folder, labelled with the path, plus the reason the file changes when the path does not make it clear. New nodes are green, touched amber and deleted red.\n>\n> Under the shape, one or two lines on the placement decisions.\n\n**`standards.md`**\n> # Standards on the canvas\n>\n> `program-design`'s standards reference still says what the part covers, what to read before proposing it and when it fits. The record keeps the list.\n>\n> ## Representation\n>\n> One `mermaid` shape holding a flowchart: each source of conventions is a document node, joined to a node listing the parts of the change it governs in this root.\n\n**New rows in the table in `program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`**\n\n| The part | `program-design` reference | Canvas reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| Package layout | `package-layout.md` | `references/representations/package-layout.md` |\n| Interfaces | `interfaces.md` | `references/representations/interfaces.md` |\n| Callstack | `callstack.md` | `references/representations/callstack.md` |\n| Module list | `module-list.md` | `references/representations/module-list.md` |\n| Standards | `standards.md` | `references/representations/standards.md` |"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":550323,"output_tokens":1911,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1911,"cache_read_input_tokens":550323,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5f503d69-ef53-4ab0-b3cc-d6fd12cf9903","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfuy53z3ebvhByg279bXp","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"301bb057-d5cd-4e7a-8ba3-dea4b5e94dbc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:21:50.655Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
