{"parentUuid":"3a94230f-b6a8-40fd-b9ef-700e20ab7e98","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__plannotator__plannotator_inbox","description":"The Plannotator Inbox on this machine: message the person and get their answer without holding this session open. Set `action` to one of the Inbox's tools below and pass that tool's fields; the project and this session are filled in for you.\n\n- send_message: Message the person in the Plannotator Inbox (markdown), in your session's open thread (see `thread`).\n- read_thread: Read one Inbox thread (thread_id or message_id): every message with its questions and the person's answers.\n- wait_for_reply: Wait for the person's reply in a thread (thread_id or message_id), or in any open thread you asked when neither is given.\n- resolve_message: Close the thread a message belongs to once you have what you needed (resolved: false reopens it).\n- list_decisions: List the decisions that hold in this project (state \"current\", the default), or the replaced, retired or all of them, oldest first.\n- record_decision: Record a decision that now holds in this project, one you settled with the person (it shows on their Decisions page as recorded by you).\n- submit_guide: Send the person a guided review of a code change.\n- get_guide_brief: Get what you need to write a guided review of a code change for the person: Plannotator's method, the JSON shape of the guide, how to read the diff, the rules, and a worked submit_guide call.\n\nWhen the person replies to a message you sent, their reply arrives in this session by itself once the session is idle, as a message with the line `Plannotator Inbox: <subject> (<reply id>)`: you can end your turn instead of waiting with wait_for_reply.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"action":{"type":"string","enum":["send_message","read_thread","wait_for_reply","resolve_message","list_decisions","record_decision","submit_guide","get_guide_brief"],"description":"Which Inbox tool to call."},"body":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"(send_message, submit_guide) The message, markdown. Question blocks render as answerable cards.\n\nMessage the person in the Plannotator Inbox (markdown), in your session's open thread (see `thread`). The answer comes back via wait_for_reply.\n\n## Asking the reviewer questions\n\nWhen a decision needs the reviewer (a trade-off you cannot settle from the code or the conversation), write it as a question block. The reviewer answers in place, and the answers come back to you in an \"Answers to your questions\" section at the top of their feedback, with the questions they left open listed under \"Unanswered\".\n\n```markdown\n:::question\nWhere should losing conflict versions be kept?\n\nLast-write-wins silently drops the loser unless we keep it somewhere.\n\n- [ ] Local only, purged after 30 days — cheap, no server change\n- [ ] Server-side per user — survives reinstall, needs a retention policy\n- [ ] Nowhere — accept silent loss for v1\n\nRecommended: Local only, purged after 30 days\n:::\n```\n\n- `:::question` picks one choice, `:::question-multi` picks any number, `:::question-text` asks for free text (a block with no choices is free text too).\n- The first line is the question. Other prose lines are context. Most reviewers answer faster with a sentence or two of it: what the choice affects and what you already know. Context can include an image (`![alt](path)`), which helps when the question is about something visual, such as a screen.\n- Choices are task-list items: `- [ ] label`, optionally `- [ ] label — why`. The reviewer can always answer \"Other\", add a note, or skip.\n- `Recommended: <label>` marks your recommendation. Text that matches no choice is offered as a suggested answer.\n- `- [x]` means the choice is already settled. Use it when you resubmit: keep an answered question with the chosen choice checked, or remove the block and write the decision into the prose.\n- Leave blank lines between the parts so the block also reads well on GitHub.\n- Ask only what you cannot decide alone, and keep a round short (about 8 questions at most). Do not ask rhetorical questions or questions the codebase answers.\n- Each answer comes back under its question (`### Q2. <question> (line N)`) as `Answer: <choice>`, marked `(your recommendation)` when the reviewer took yours, or as `Other: ...`, free text in a quote, or `Skipped`, plus any `Note:`. A question you marked `- [x]` is settled and only comes back if the reviewer changed it or added a note."},"subject":{"description":"(send_message, submit_guide) A short subject when this starts a thread (ignored when it joins one). Default: the first question's prompt, else the first line.","type":"string"},"thread":{"description":"(send_message, submit_guide) A short thread name (1-120 characters, one line). Without it, your messages join your session's open thread in this project (a new one the first time, or once the person resolved it; a thread keeps its first subject). With it, the same name in this project is the same open thread, across sessions (compared without case, spacing or invisible characters). Use it to split separate work, or to join another session's thread. Ignored with reply_to.","type":"string"},"reply_to":{"description":"(send_message, submit_guide) A message id: post this as a reply in that message's thread.","type":"string"},"idempotency_key":{"description":"(send_message, record_decision, submit_guide) Any unique string; sending again with the same key answers the first message instead of posting twice.","type":"string"},"attachments":{"description":"(send_message) Files for the person to open and annotate beside your message, e.g. [\"docs/plan.md\", \"proto/admin.html\", \"flow.mmd\"]: absolute, or relative to project_path, inside the project. Markdown, plain text, config and data files, Mermaid and Graphviz sources, and HTML (its relative images and frames load from its folder); .env is refused. The Inbox keeps the version you sent and shows the file as it is now, saying when it changed. The person's annotations come back in their reply.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"thread_id":{"type":"string","description":"(read_thread, wait_for_reply)"},"message_id":{"type":"string","description":"(read_thread, wait_for_reply, resolve_message)"},"asked_by":{"description":"(read_thread) Default \"me\" when your session is known.","type":"string","enum":["me","anyone"]},"include_resolved":{"type":"boolean","description":"(read_thread)"},"limit":{"description":"(read_thread) Threads to list (default 20).","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100},"cursor":{"description":"(wait_for_reply) The cursor a previous call returned.","type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"timeout_seconds":{"description":"(wait_for_reply) Wait at most this long (default 50).","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":50},"resolved":{"description":"(resolve_message) Default true.","type":"boolean"},"state":{"description":"(list_decisions) Default \"current\".","type":"string","enum":["current","replaced","retired","all"]},"text":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"(record_decision) The decision, one statement."},"reason":{"description":"(record_decision) Why it holds.","type":"string"},"guide":{"description":"(submit_guide) The guide: { title, intent, sections: [{ title, overview, diffs: [{ file, summary }] }], unplacedFiles?, review?: { gitRef, base }, source?, generator? } (get_guide_brief's output_schema), as an object or its JSON.","anyOf":[{"type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"additionalProperties":{}},{"type":"string"}]},"patch":{"description":"(submit_guide) The exact unified diff the guide describes (get_guide_brief's diff_steps).","type":"string"},"snapshot":{"description":"(submit_guide) Instead of guide and patch: a complete Plannotator guide snapshot, as an object or its JSON.","anyOf":[{"type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"additionalProperties":{}},{"type":"string"}]}},"required":["action"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fa2e5bf6-25ea-4926-a079-e9af3f5bc8dd","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:26:39.757Z","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
