,"attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9366134-50f4-47e5-8068-e41057bd020e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:32:05.680Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"d9366134-50f4-47e5-8068-e41057bd020e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fa24657c-a4b7-4b9d-9c50-2e639d9c0f75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FtakJxnaGFJjGuzsyF1oUT","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ntitle: \"Local development\"\nsummary: \"How the API Worker and the pipeline Worker run locally on one shared state folder, call the real Firecrawl, AI Gateway and Modal, and receive Modal's audio upload through a quick tunnel and a local proxy.\"\ncreated: \"2026-10-11\"\n---\n\n# Local development\n\n## 🔭 Overview\n\nLocally, the pipeline Worker runs under vite dev and the API Worker under its own wrangler dev, and both keep their state in one shared folder, so they see the same D1 database and the same R2 bucket on disk. The Workers call the real Firecrawl, the real AI Gateway for Gemini and the Flue agents, and the same Modal app production uses. Modal uploads the audio into the local bucket through a Cloudflare quick tunnel and a small local Node proxy.\n\n## 🚀 How to run both Workers locally\n\n1. Apply common/'s migrations to the shared state folder: `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`.\n2. Start the pipeline Worker: `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`.\n3. Start the Node proxy: `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`.\n4. Start a quick tunnel to the proxy's port with `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:<port>`, and write `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<hostname>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`, with the tunnel's hostname in place of `<hostname>`.\n5. Start the API Worker: `pnpm dev` in `api/`.\n\n## 🏗️ Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph laptop [\"Developer machine\"]\n    direction TB\n    api@{ shape: rect, label: \"API Worker<br/>(wrangler dev)\" }\n    pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline Worker<br/>(vite dev)\" }\n    state@{ shape: cyl, label: \"Shared state folder:<br/>D1 and R2 on disk\" }\n    s3@{ shape: rect, label: \"Local S3 endpoint<br/>/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/\" }\n    proxy@{ shape: rect, label: \"Node proxy\" }\n  end\n  tunnel@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Cloudflare<br/>quick tunnel\" }\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal TTS\" }\n  ext@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Firecrawl,<br/>AI Gateway\" }\n  api -->|\"create, restart\"| pipe\n  api --- state\n  pipe --- state\n  pipe -->|\"scrape, describe,<br/>agents\"| ext\n  pipe -->|\"start: PUT URL with<br/>the tunnel's hostname\"| modal\n  modal -->|\"PUT /s3/bucket/key\"| tunnel\n  tunnel --> proxy\n  proxy -->|\"rewrites to<br/>/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/\"| s3\n  s3 --- state\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class state store\n  class tunnel,modal,ext ext\n  class s3,proxy tool\n```\n\nThe API Worker creates and restarts the item Workflow through the same cross-script Workflow binding it uses in production; the two dev servers find each other locally. Both Workers point at the same state folder, so D1, R2 and the Durable Objects are one set of files on disk. Locally, D1's schema comes from common/'s migrations, applied with wrangler against that folder (see [the common/ package](common-package.md)).\n\n> [!WARNING] A Worker that does not share the state folder sees an empty database\n> Each dev server keeps its state under its own config directory unless it is pointed at the shared folder. A Worker started without it finds no tables and an empty bucket.\n\n## 📤 How Modal's audio reaches the local bucket\n\nModal runs in the cloud and uploads the audio to a presigned PUT URL, as in production. Locally that URL points at wrangler's experimental local S3 endpoint, which the pipeline Worker's dev server serves at /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/ and which checks the URL's signature.\n\n1. The pipeline Worker signs the PUT URL for localhost with the same presigning function it uses against R2 in production (see [the common/ package](common-package.md)).\n2. It hands that URL to Modal with localhost's endpoint replaced by the one in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The URL then holds the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>. In production both endpoints are R2's, so the same code runs in both places.\n3. Modal PUTs the audio to the tunnel, which forwards it to the Node proxy.\n4. The proxy maps /s3/<bucket>/<key> to /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/<bucket>/<key> with localhost as the host, so the signature matches, and the local endpoint writes the object into the shared state folder.\n\nThe API Worker then reads the audio through its own R2 binding, from the same folder.\n\n> [!NOTE] Why a proxy sits behind the tunnel\n> Cloudflare's edge answers every /cdn-cgi/ path on trycloudflare.com itself, so a request for /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/ never reaches the dev server. The proxy gives the tunnel a path outside /cdn-cgi/ and restores the endpoint's path and host locally.\n\n> [!WARNING] The tunnel's hostname can change on every start\n> A quick tunnel gets a new random hostname each time it starts. The pipeline Worker reads the hostname from its configuration, so the configuration has to name the tunnel that is running; an upload to an old hostname never reaches the local bucket.\n\n## 🔁 Re-queuing a stuck item\n\nAn item enqueued while the pipeline Worker is not running cannot start. When the API fails to create its Workflow instance, the item fails at enqueue, and a retry once the pipeline Worker is running creates the instance. When the instance is created but never starts, or ends in error, the item stays queued, and the API re-queues the item the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes. When the API reads the item, it restarts the item's instance and rewrites queued_at (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)). The developer polls the item once the pipeline Worker is running, and the item starts again.\n\n> [!WARNING] A dev-server reload strands the running Workflow instance\n> An edit reloads the dev server, and a Workflow instance that is running during the reload never resumes: its item stays in the status it had. An item stranded in queued is re-queued once its queued_at is more than 15 minutes old.\n\n---\n\nRelated: [the common/ package](common-package.md) · [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) · [tts-service](tts-service.md) · [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) · [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md)\n----\n## Still to delete by hand\n\nThese credentials were created in dashboards for the spikes and can only be removed there:\n\n- The Modal proxy auth token (Modal, Settings, Proxy Auth Tokens), if not deleted yet.\n- The R2 API tokens created for `r2-presigned` and `svg-display` (Cloudflare, R2, Manage API tokens), if not revoked yet. `svg-display` printed one token's access key ID inside a URL; revoking the token covers it.\n\nThe stopped Modal apps `nagara-tts-spike` and `nagara-spike-upload` still appear in `modal app list`; the CLI cannot remove a stopped app.\napi:\n.\n..\nalembic.ini\napp\ndata\n.env\n.env.example\nmigrations\nprototype_cache\npyproject.toml\n.pytest_cache\n.python-version\n.railwayignore\nrailway.toml\n.ruff_cache\ntests\nuv.lock\n.venv\n\npipeline:\n.\n..\nbiome.json\n.claude\n.dev.vars\ndist\n.gitignore\nnode_modules\npackage.json\npnpm-lock.yaml\npnpm-workspace.yaml\nscripts\nsrc\ntest\ntsconfig.json\nvite.config.ts\nvitest.config.ts\nworker-configuration.d.ts\n.wrangler\nwrangler.jsonc\n\ntts:\n.\n..\napp.py\npyproject.toml\n.python-version\ntests\nuv.lock\n.venv\n/home/agus/.modal.toml","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"12892e79-3b18-400b-9f89-38e3671b0d37","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:32:06.141Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\ntitle: \"Local development\"\nsummary: \"How the API Worker and the pipeline Worker run locally on one shared state folder, call the real Firecrawl, AI Gateway and Modal, and receive Modal's audio upload through a quick tunnel and a local proxy.\"\ncreated: \"2026-10-11\"\n---\n\n# Local development\n\n## 🔭 Overview\n\nLocally, the pipeline Worker runs under vite dev and the API Worker under its own wrangler dev, and both keep their state in one shared folder, so they see the same D1 database and the same R2 bucket on disk. The Workers call the real Firecrawl, the real AI Gateway for Gemini and the Flue agents, and the same Modal app production uses. Modal uploads the audio into the local bucket through a Cloudflare quick tunnel and a small local Node proxy.\n\n## 🚀 How to run both Workers locally\n\n1. Apply common/'s migrations to the shared state folder: `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`.\n2. Start the pipeline Worker: `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`.\n3. Start the Node proxy: `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`.\n4. Start a quick tunnel to the proxy's port with `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:<port>`, and write `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<hostname>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`, with the tunnel's hostname in place of `<hostname>`.\n5. Start the API Worker: `pnpm dev` in `api/`.\n\n## 🏗️ Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph laptop [\"Developer machine\"]\n    direction TB\n    api@{ shape: rect, label: \"API Worker<br/>(wrangler dev)\" }\n    pipe@{ shape: rect, label: \"pipeline Worker<br/>(vite dev)\" }\n    state@{ shape: cyl, label: \"Shared state folder:<br/>D1 and R2 on disk\" }\n    s3@{ shape: rect, label: \"Local S3 endpoint<br/>/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/\" }\n    proxy@{ shape: rect, label: \"Node proxy\" }\n  end\n  tunnel@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Cloudflare<br/>quick tunnel\" }\n  modal@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Modal TTS\" }\n  ext@{ shape: cloud, label: \"Firecrawl,<br/>AI Gateway\" }\n  api -->|\"create, restart\"| pipe\n  api --- state\n  pipe --- state\n  pipe -->|\"scrape, describe,<br/>agents\"| ext\n  pipe -->|\"start: PUT URL with<br/>the tunnel's hostname\"| modal\n  modal -->|\"PUT /s3/bucket/key\"| tunnel\n  tunnel --> proxy\n  proxy -->|\"rewrites to<br/>/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/\"| s3\n  s3 --- state\n  classDef worker fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef flow fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef ext fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class api worker\n  class pipe flow\n  class state store\n  class tunnel,modal,ext ext\n  class s3,proxy tool\n```\n\nThe API Worker creates and restarts the item Workflow through the same cross-script Workflow binding it uses in production; the two dev servers find each other locally. Both Workers point at the same state folder, so D1, R2 and the Durable Objects are one set of files on disk. Locally, D1's schema comes from common/'s migrations, applied with wrangler against that folder (see [the common/ package](common-package.md)).\n\n> [!WARNING] A Worker that does not share the state folder sees an empty database\n> Each dev server keeps its state under its own config directory unless it is pointed at the shared folder. A Worker started without it finds no tables and an empty bucket.\n\n## 📤 How Modal's audio reaches the local bucket\n\nModal runs in the cloud and uploads the audio to a presigned PUT URL, as in production. Locally that URL points at wrangler's experimental local S3 endpoint, which the pipeline Worker's dev server serves at /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/ and which checks the URL's signature.\n\n1. The pipeline Worker signs the PUT URL for localhost with the same presigning function it uses against R2 in production (see [the common/ package](common-package.md)).\n2. It hands that URL to Modal with localhost's endpoint replaced by the one in `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The URL then holds the quick tunnel's hostname and the path /s3/<bucket>/<key>. In production both endpoints are R2's, so the same code runs in both places.\n3. Modal PUTs the audio to the tunnel, which forwards it to the Node proxy.\n4. The proxy maps /s3/<bucket>/<key> to /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/<bucket>/<key> with localhost as the host, so the signature matches, and the local endpoint writes the object into the shared state folder.\n\nThe API Worker then reads the audio through its own R2 binding, from the same folder.\n\n> [!NOTE] Why a proxy sits behind the tunnel\n> Cloudflare's edge answers every /cdn-cgi/ path on trycloudflare.com itself, so a request for /cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/ never reaches the dev server. The proxy gives the tunnel a path outside /cdn-cgi/ and restores the endpoint's path and host locally.\n\n> [!WARNING] The tunnel's hostname can change on every start\n> A quick tunnel gets a new random hostname each time it starts. The pipeline Worker reads the hostname from its configuration, so the configuration has to name the tunnel that is running; an upload to an old hostname never reaches the local bucket.\n\n## 🔁 Re-queuing a stuck item\n\nAn item enqueued while the pipeline Worker is not running cannot start. When the API fails to create its Workflow instance, the item fails at enqueue, and a retry once the pipeline Worker is running creates the instance. When the instance is created but never starts, or ends in error, the item stays queued, and the API re-queues the item the way it re-queues any item queued for more than 15 minutes. When the API reads the item, it restarts the item's instance and rewrites queued_at (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)). The developer polls the item once the pipeline Worker is running, and the item starts again.\n\n> [!WARNING] A dev-server reload strands the running Workflow instance\n> An edit reloads the dev server, and a Workflow instance that is running during the reload never resumes: its item stays in the status it had. An item stranded in queued is re-queued once its queued_at is more than 15 minutes old.\n\n---\n\nRelated: [the common/ package](common-package.md) · [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md) · [tts-service](tts-service.md) · [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md) · [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md)\n----\n## Still to delete by hand\n\nThese credentials were created in dashboards for the spikes and can only be removed there:\n\n- The Modal proxy auth token (Modal, Settings, Proxy Auth Tokens), if not deleted yet.\n- The R2 API tokens created for `r2-presigned` and `svg-display` (Cloudflare, R2, Manage API tokens), if not revoked yet. `svg-display` printed one token's access key ID inside a URL; revoking the token covers it.\n\nThe stopped Modal apps `nagara-tts-spike` and `nagara-spike-upload` still appear in `modal app list`; the CLI cannot remove a stopped app.\napi:\n.\n..\nalembic.ini\napp\ndata\n.env\n.env.example\nmigrations\nprototype_cache\npyproject.toml\n.pytest_cache\n.python-version\n.railwayignore\nrailway.toml\n.ruff_cache\ntests\nuv.lock\n.venv\n\npipeline:\n.\n..\nbiome.json\n.claude\n.dev.vars\ndist\n.gitignore\nnode_modules\npackage.json\npnpm-lock.yaml\npnpm-workspace.yaml\nscripts\nsrc\ntest\ntsconfig.json\nvite.config.ts\nvitest.config.ts\nworker-configuration.d.ts\n.wrangler\nwrangler.jsonc\n\ntts:\n.\n..\napp.py\npyproject.toml\n.python-version\ntests\nuv.lock\n.venv\n/home/agus/.modal.toml","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c9f276d4-d2d1-4e9a-94e6-9bc77f608b69","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":