,"attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ced7f3e-2db5-4772-b6ae-1b4b02543f37","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:32:33.460Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"3ced7f3e-2db5-4772-b6ae-1b4b02543f37","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fa24657c-a4b7-4b9d-9c50-2e639d9c0f75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JtEEUEYgdBsMFGASjSKFLh","type":"tool_result","content":"spikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:18:  - `wrangler.jsonc` is the receiver. Its bucket `nagara-spike-audio` carries `local_dev.experimental_s3_credentials` with dummy keys.\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:19:  - `wrangler.api.jsonc` is the \"API\": the same bucket, no S3 credentials.\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:65:- On the API Worker side, sharing works for a bucket with no S3 credentials. Only the Worker that serves the endpoint needs `experimental_s3_credentials`. If two Workers bind the same bucket with *different* credentials, miniflare throws `ERR_DIFFERENT_S3_CREDENTIALS`. I saw this in the code and did not run it.\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:70:- The local S3 credentials are dummy values in the wrangler config. Should the presigner read its access key and secret from configuration (invariant 6), so that local and production differ only in values?\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:74:- I did not verify that the same presign code is accepted by a real R2 bucket for a **PUT**: it needs S3 credentials and a bucket, and the brief let me skip it. The `r2-presigned` spike verified aws4fetch presigned **GETs** against real R2. The PUT path differs only in method and base URL, but it is unverified.\nspikes/svg-display/FINDINGS.md:64:Remaining: the R2 API token the user created in the dashboard (the user must revoke it), and the local `spikes/svg-display/` folder. The R2 Access Key ID was printed once in the terminal output (inside a presigned URL); the secret was never printed. Revoking the token covers it.\ncross-script-binding\nfirecrawl-gemini\nimage-processing\nitem-workflow\nlocal-audio-tunnel\nlocal-audio-upload\nlocal-dev\nlocal-dev-b\nlocal-dev-real\nmodal-http\nparallel-steps\nr2-presigned\nREPORT.md\nrestart-resolve\nshared-d1\nsvg-describe\nsvg-display\nworkflow-testing\n\n- **route**: audio · image\n- **item**: ready · not ready · missing\n- **hash**: stored · unknown\n\n| Row | What the test does | route | item | hash | Expected | Kind | Setup |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D20 | asks for a ready item's audio | audio | ready | stored | 307 to a URL signed for audio/<id>, X-Amz-Expires=3600. By hand: the URL plays and seeks in a browser audio element | test + manual |  |\n| D21 | asks for a generating item's audio | audio | not ready | stored | 404. By hand: the audio route of an item still generating answers 404 | test + manual |  |\n| D22 | asks for a stored image | image | not ready | stored | 307 to a URL signed for images/<hash> | test |  |\n| D23 | asks for an image of an unknown item | image | missing | stored | 404 | test |  |\n| D24 | asks for an unknown hash | image | ready | unknown | 307 anyway | test |  |\n\n### D5 the key guard and /health\n\nRoot: `every route`\n\n- **key**: missing · wrong · right\n- **route**: an /items route · /health\n\n| Row | What the test does | key | route | Expected | Kind | Setup |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D25 | calls every /items route without a key | missing | an /items route | 401. By hand on the deployed API: a poll without the key answers 401 | test + manual |  |\n| D26 | calls every /items route with a wrong key | wrong | an /items route | 401 | test |  |\n| D27 | calls /health without a key | missing | /health | 200 | test |  |\n\n## Implementation tasks\n\n- C7 to C10: a fake agent for the tests. The agents run in their own Durable Objects and the program design drops the WORLD_SEAM seam, so the tests configure the agents to answer with a scripted reply (a script, a not-article verdict, or giving up), through configuration rather than an environment branch (invariant 6).\n- C1 and C11: check that the Images binding works under the vitest plugin locally; if it does not, give the tests a stand-in binding through configuration, or move those rows to manual.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"52adc1e7-48de-4182-abd9-8eeb7e66298d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:32:33.937Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"spikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:18:  - `wrangler.jsonc` is the receiver. Its bucket `nagara-spike-audio` carries `local_dev.experimental_s3_credentials` with dummy keys.\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:19:  - `wrangler.api.jsonc` is the \"API\": the same bucket, no S3 credentials.\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:65:- On the API Worker side, sharing works for a bucket with no S3 credentials. Only the Worker that serves the endpoint needs `experimental_s3_credentials`. If two Workers bind the same bucket with *different* credentials, miniflare throws `ERR_DIFFERENT_S3_CREDENTIALS`. I saw this in the code and did not run it.\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:70:- The local S3 credentials are dummy values in the wrangler config. Should the presigner read its access key and secret from configuration (invariant 6), so that local and production differ only in values?\nspikes/local-audio-upload/FINDINGS.md:74:- I did not verify that the same presign code is accepted by a real R2 bucket for a **PUT**: it needs S3 credentials and a bucket, and the brief let me skip it. The `r2-presigned` spike verified aws4fetch presigned **GETs** against real R2. The PUT path differs only in method and base URL, but it is unverified.\nspikes/svg-display/FINDINGS.md:64:Remaining: the R2 API token the user created in the dashboard (the user must revoke it), and the local `spikes/svg-display/` folder. The R2 Access Key ID was printed once in the terminal output (inside a presigned URL); the secret was never printed. Revoking the token covers it.\ncross-script-binding\nfirecrawl-gemini\nimage-processing\nitem-workflow\nlocal-audio-tunnel\nlocal-audio-upload\nlocal-dev\nlocal-dev-b\nlocal-dev-real\nmodal-http\nparallel-steps\nr2-presigned\nREPORT.md\nr