{"parentUuid":"17c8ae1a-530d-43ab-b34a-1ff801a48397","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuz5kZBsrEYKCeEMwGhw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017iLLqusES8V72ftzQC9VXc","name":"mcp__linear-server__list_issues","input":{"project":"nagara","query":"Cloudflare","fields":["id","title","description","status"],"limit":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7011,"cache_read_input_tokens":88566,"output_tokens":138,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7011,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":138,"cache_read_input_tokens":88566,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7011},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017iLLqusES8V72ftzQC9VXc":{"project":"nagara","query":"Cloudflare","fields":["id","title","description","status"],"limit":30}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5e409d76-8354-4d70-b2a5-29ce7476e353","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfuz5kDMcBGcMUV7Yp22m","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:implement","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"7df991b9-8f52-46c5-a250-db75645f2ea2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:34:54.356Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"7df991b9-8f52-46c5-a250-db75645f2ea2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fa24657c-a4b7-4b9d-9c50-2e639d9c0f75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017iLLqusES8V72ftzQC9VXc","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\":[{\"id\":\"ASE-83\",\"title\":\"Switch nagara over to Cloudflare and retire Railway\",\"description\":\"Bring the migrated stack up in production and remove what it replaces:\\n\\n* create the production D1 database, R2 bucket and the two R2 API tokens (GET for the API, PUT for the pipeline); set each Worker's secrets\\n* deploy (migrations, pipeline, API) and point `nagara.asermax.com` at the API Worker\\n* remove the Cloudflare Access application and its service token from the pipeline\\n* run every \\\"test + manual\\\" row of the test design by hand against t… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-61\",\"title\":\"Extraction service: the pipeline deployable on Cloudflare\",\"description\":\"The third deployable, pipeline/: the Worker entrypoint (POST /jobs and GET /jobs/{job_id}, Access authenticating at the edge, 413 at the \\\\~1 MiB cap with no job created), the domain-queue Durable Object (lease plus FIFO, create-before-persist, the five-minute alarm that sweeps or re-arms), the singleton index Durable Object (job id to domain in SQLite, written by the queues at enqueue, swept every 24h, nothing deletes on read or create), and the… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Done\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-82\",\"title\":\"CI: one Cloudflare workflow for common, pipeline and api\",\"description\":\"Replace `.github/workflows/api.yml` and `pipeline.yml` with one `cloudflare.yml`:\\n\\n* a paths filter decides which of `common/`, `pipeline/` and `api/` changed; each changed tree runs test, lint and types; a change to `common/` also runs both Workers' type checks\\n* the deploy chain: migrate (`wrangler d1 migrations apply --remote`), then the pipeline (`pnpm build`, deploy `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`), then the API\\n* a job runs only when no job be… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-18\",\"title\":\"Serve the web frontend and the API from one origin\",\"description\":\"Design decision: serve the web frontend and the API from one origin (for example `nagara.asermax.com`) instead of separate hosts. Same-origin removes CORS, simplifies the cookie/session story for the future player's authentication, and gives a clean presigned-audio flow.\\n\\nThe constraint: Railway maps a domain to one service, so one surface must own the domain and route to the other over private networking. The question to settle is which surface… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-81\",\"title\":\"Local development setup for both Workers\",\"description\":\"Make both Workers run together locally, as `docs/technical-design/local-development.md` describes:\\n\\n* the shared state folder `.wrangler-state/` at the repository root (git-ignored): `persistState` in `pipeline/vite.config.ts`, `--persist-to` in `api/`'s dev script\\n* `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`\\n* `pipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs` (`/s3/<bucket>/<key>` to `/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/...` with localhost as host) and `pnpm dev:proxy`\\n* the experi… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-63\",\"title\":\"API integration: extraction client, handle and the recipe_version migration\",\"description\":\"The api side of the boundary: the thin client (spawn(html, recipe or none, job id, domain) and resolve(job id)) behind CLOUDFLARE\\\\_\\\\* configuration, the source step swapped to fetch-and-spawn with firecrawl always, poll mapping the five states to outcomes with extraction:-prefixed errors, the retry rules (handle stable across retries, a new id only after error, not_article accepted under the cap), and the alembic migration adding the recipe_vers… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Done\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-28\",\"title\":\"Test: spawn failure inside create_item lands the item in failed\",\"description\":\"Add an endpoint-level test for the path where `spawn_synthesis` raises inside `create_item`.\\n\\nThe enqueue-to-audio API spec (R4) requires that a URL which cannot be turned into audio at enqueue time, including the case where synthesis cannot be dispatched, returns an enqueue response that is already the item in `failed`.\\n\\n`api/app/endpoints/items.py::create_item` wraps `spawn_synthesis(...)` (defined in `api/app/service/tts.py`) in a `try`/`exce… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Canceled\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-29\",\"title\":\"Test: the poll route rejects a missing or wrong API key\",\"description\":\"Add a test that `GET /items/{id}` rejects a request with a missing or incorrect `X-API-Key`.\\n\\nThe enqueue-to-audio API spec (R8) says a request with a missing or incorrect credential to any route (enqueue, poll, or audio) is rejected as unauthorized. `test_post_requires_key` and `test_audio_requires_key` cover two of the three routes; there is no `test_get_requires_key` for the poll route.\\n\\nThe guard is `require_key` in `api/app/security.py`, wi… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Canceled\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-78\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: the describe step\",\"description\":\"Port the describer (`api/app/service/describe.py`) into the describe step:\\n\\n* the core call: Gemini through AI Gateway with structured output `{spoken}`, then the sanitize tail; a raster as the stored WebP, an SVG as its markup in a `text/plain` part\\n* the code and image prompts, and the good-alt filter (reading the alt back from the unit's display)\\n* jobs in document order, capped at 25 combined; one child step per job (3 attempts of 1 minute),… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-74\",\"title\":\"tts/: start and result web endpoints\",\"description\":\"Give the Modal app two web endpoints behind Modal's proxy auth, on a CPU web function in the same app:\\n\\n* **start** (POST): paragraphs, voice (default `af_heart`), destination (a presigned PUT URL). Spawns `Kokoro.synthesize` and answers `{call_id}` at once.\\n* **result** (GET `?call_id=`): `202` while running; `200` with format, duration, timings once done; `500` when the synthesis raised; `410` once Modal no longer holds the result; `422` for a… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-75\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: DomainQueue as a lease for the item Workflow\",\"description\":\"Turn DomainQueue from the creator of extraction instances into a lease the item Workflow asks for:\\n\\n* `acquire(instanceId)` → granted when the id holds the lease, or the lease is free and the FIFO empty; otherwise the id is appended once, keeping its place when it is already waiting\\n* `release(instanceId)` drops the id from the FIFO and, when it holds the lease, hands the lease on\\n* `advance` checks the next id's status, writes the lease and sen… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-79\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: start synthesis, wait for synthesis, store\",\"description\":\"The last three steps of the item Workflow:\\n\\n* start synthesis: sign a PUT URL for the item's audio key against `R2_S3_ENDPOINT`, hand Modal the URL with `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` in its place, the spoken forms and the voice; the call id as the step result\\n* wait for synthesis: one step asking the result endpoint every `pollIntervalSeconds` (5 s) until ready, 15 minutes per attempt; `500` fails the attempt, `410` and `422` fail the item at once\\n* stor… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-73\",\"title\":\"Workspace and the common/ package\",\"description\":\"Create the root pnpm workspace (one lockfile for `common/`, `api/`, `pipeline/`; `pipeline/`'s own lockfile and workspace file go, their allowBuilds and overrides move to the root) and the `@nagara/common` package, source only, imported by both Workers.\\n\\n`common/` holds:\\n\\n* the shared types: item row, unit union, degradations, statuses and the cost and unit constant maps, recipe version row, ledger row, `ItemWorkflowParams`, the `STEP` names\\n* `… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-77\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: the images step\",\"description\":\"Acquire the images the recipe step hands over as its step result, ported from `api/app/service/images.py`:\\n\\n* download under the per-host (2) and global (10) semaphores, 10 s, 10 MB\\n* sniff `<svg`: an SVG keeps its markup with scripts stripped, the SVG content type, no size floor\\n* rasters through the Images binding: kept when the shorter side is at least 200 px (a smaller one drops with no degradation), re-encoded to WebP\\n* store under `images/… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-80\",\"title\":\"api/: the TypeScript API Worker\",\"description\":\"Replace the Python `api/` tree with a TypeScript Worker (`nagara-api`) serving the same routes and item JSON:\\n\\n* the `X-API-Key` guard ahead of every `/items` route; `/health` open\\n* `POST /items`: the queued row, then `ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({itemId})`; a create that throws writes the item failed with its error\\n* `GET /items/{id}`: the wire projection (units only once ready, no spoken, `audio_url`); an item queued over 15 minutes is claimed with … (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-76\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: the item Workflow through the recipe step\",\"description\":\"Build the item Workflow and its first four steps:\\n\\n* `ItemWorkflow` (binding `ITEM_WORKFLOW`, params `{itemId}`) and the step wrapper: the status write inside each attempt, the step's own error on the last attempt, rethrow\\n* fetch through our own Firecrawl client (the Python SDK's fields, `rawHtml` and `markdown` at `proxy: auto`): instance id, domain, ledger row, the HTML as the step result, the 1 MiB cap\\n* lease (ask DomainQueue, up to 3 waits… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}]}]},"uuid":"6cfb0cd9-44d5-42b6-b246-af10ca97b01f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:34:56.232Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\":[{\"id\":\"ASE-83\",\"title\":\"Switch nagara over to Cloudflare and retire Railway\",\"description\":\"Bring the migrated stack up in production and remove what it replaces:\\n\\n* create the production D1 database, R2 bucket and the two R2 API tokens (GET for the API, PUT for the pipeline); set each Worker's secrets\\n* deploy (migrations, pipeline, API) and point `nagara.asermax.com` at the API Worker\\n* remove the Cloudflare Access application and its service token from the pipeline\\n* run every \\\"test + manual\\\" row of the test design by hand against t… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-61\",\"title\":\"Extraction service: the pipeline deployable on Cloudflare\",\"description\":\"The third deployable, pipeline/: the Worker entrypoint (POST /jobs and GET /jobs/{job_id}, Access authenticating at the edge, 413 at the \\\\~1 MiB cap with no job created), the domain-queue Durable Object (lease plus FIFO, create-before-persist, the five-minute alarm that sweeps or re-arms), the singleton index Durable Object (job id to domain in SQLite, written by the queues at enqueue, swept every 24h, nothing deletes on read or create), and the… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Done\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-82\",\"title\":\"CI: one Cloudflare workflow for common, pipeline and api\",\"description\":\"Replace `.github/workflows/api.yml` and `pipeline.yml` with one `cloudflare.yml`:\\n\\n* a paths filter decides which of `common/`, `pipeline/` and `api/` changed; each changed tree runs test, lint and types; a change to `common/` also runs both Workers' type checks\\n* the deploy chain: migrate (`wrangler d1 migrations apply --remote`), then the pipeline (`pnpm build`, deploy `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`), then the API\\n* a job runs only when no job be… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-18\",\"title\":\"Serve the web frontend and the API from one origin\",\"description\":\"Design decision: serve the web frontend and the API from one origin (for example `nagara.asermax.com`) instead of separate hosts. Same-origin removes CORS, simplifies the cookie/session story for the future player's authentication, and gives a clean presigned-audio flow.\\n\\nThe constraint: Railway maps a domain to one service, so one surface must own the domain and route to the other over private networking. The question to settle is which surface… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-81\",\"title\":\"Local development setup for both Workers\",\"description\":\"Make both Workers run together locally, as `docs/technical-design/local-development.md` describes:\\n\\n* the shared state folder `.wrangler-state/` at the repository root (git-ignored): `persistState` in `pipeline/vite.config.ts`, `--persist-to` in `api/`'s dev script\\n* `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`\\n* `pipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs` (`/s3/<bucket>/<key>` to `/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/...` with localhost as host) and `pnpm dev:proxy`\\n* the experi… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-63\",\"title\":\"API integration: extraction client, handle and the recipe_version migration\",\"description\":\"The api side of the boundary: the thin client (spawn(html, recipe or none, job id, domain) and resolve(job id)) behind CLOUDFLARE\\\\_\\\\* configuration, the source step swapped to fetch-and-spawn with firecrawl always, poll mapping the five states to outcomes with extraction:-prefixed errors, the retry rules (handle stable across retries, a new id only after error, not_article accepted under the cap), and the alembic migration adding the recipe_vers… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Done\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-28\",\"title\":\"Test: spawn failure inside create_item lands the item in failed\",\"description\":\"Add an endpoint-level test for the path where `spawn_synthesis` raises inside `create_item`.\\n\\nThe enqueue-to-audio API spec (R4) requires that a URL which cannot be turned into audio at enqueue time, including the case where synthesis cannot be dispatched, returns an enqueue response that is already the item in `failed`.\\n\\n`api/app/endpoints/items.py::create_item` wraps `spawn_synthesis(...)` (defined in `api/app/service/tts.py`) in a `try`/`exce… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Canceled\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-29\",\"title\":\"Test: the poll route rejects a missing or wrong API key\",\"description\":\"Add a test that `GET /items/{id}` rejects a request with a missing or incorrect `X-API-Key`.\\n\\nThe enqueue-to-audio API spec (R8) says a request with a missing or incorrect credential to any route (enqueue, poll, or audio) is rejected as unauthorized. `test_post_requires_key` and `test_audio_requires_key` cover two of the three routes; there is no `test_get_requires_key` for the poll route.\\n\\nThe guard is `require_key` in `api/app/security.py`, wi… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Canceled\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-78\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: the describe step\",\"description\":\"Port the describer (`api/app/service/describe.py`) into the describe step:\\n\\n* the core call: Gemini through AI Gateway with structured output `{spoken}`, then the sanitize tail; a raster as the stored WebP, an SVG as its markup in a `text/plain` part\\n* the code and image prompts, and the good-alt filter (reading the alt back from the unit's display)\\n* jobs in document order, capped at 25 combined; one child step per job (3 attempts of 1 minute),… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-74\",\"title\":\"tts/: start and result web endpoints\",\"description\":\"Give the Modal app two web endpoints behind Modal's proxy auth, on a CPU web function in the same app:\\n\\n* **start** (POST): paragraphs, voice (default `af_heart`), destination (a presigned PUT URL). Spawns `Kokoro.synthesize` and answers `{call_id}` at once.\\n* **result** (GET `?call_id=`): `202` while running; `200` with format, duration, timings once done; `500` when the synthesis raised; `410` once Modal no longer holds the result; `422` for a… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-75\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: DomainQueue as a lease for the item Workflow\",\"description\":\"Turn DomainQueue from the creator of extraction instances into a lease the item Workflow asks for:\\n\\n* `acquire(instanceId)` → granted when the id holds the lease, or the lease is free and the FIFO empty; otherwise the id is appended once, keeping its place when it is already waiting\\n* `release(instanceId)` drops the id from the FIFO and, when it holds the lease, hands the lease on\\n* `advance` checks the next id's status, writes the lease and sen… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-79\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: start synthesis, wait for synthesis, store\",\"description\":\"The last three steps of the item Workflow:\\n\\n* start synthesis: sign a PUT URL for the item's audio key against `R2_S3_ENDPOINT`, hand Modal the URL with `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` in its place, the spoken forms and the voice; the call id as the step result\\n* wait for synthesis: one step asking the result endpoint every `pollIntervalSeconds` (5 s) until ready, 15 minutes per attempt; `500` fails the attempt, `410` and `422` fail the item at once\\n* stor… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-73\",\"title\":\"Workspace and the common/ package\",\"description\":\"Create the root pnpm workspace (one lockfile for `common/`, `api/`, `pipeline/`; `pipeline/`'s own lockfile and workspace file go, their allowBuilds and overrides move to the root) and the `@nagara/common` package, source only, imported by both Workers.\\n\\n`common/` holds:\\n\\n* the shared types: item row, unit union, degradations, statuses and the cost and unit constant maps, recipe version row, ledger row, `ItemWorkflowParams`, the `STEP` names\\n* `… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-77\",\"title\":\"pipeline/: the images step\",\"description\":\"Acquire the images the recipe step hands over as its step result, ported from `api/app/service/images.py`:\\n\\n* download under the per-host (2) and global (10) semaphores, 10 s, 10 MB\\n* sniff `<svg`: an SVG keeps its markup with scripts stripped, the SVG content type, no size floor\\n* rasters through the Images binding: kept when the shorter side is at least 200 px (a smaller one drops with no degradation), re-encoded to WebP\\n* store under `images/… (truncated, use `get_issue` for full description)\",\"status\":\"Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"ASE-80\",\"title\":\"api/: the TypeScript API Worker\",\"description\":\"Replace the Python `api/` tree with a TypeScript Worker (`nagara-api`) serving the same routes and item JSON:\\n\\n* the `X-API-Key` guard ahead of every `/items` route; `/health` open\\n* `POST /items`: the queued row, then `ITEM_WORKFLOW.create({itemId})`; a create that throws writes the item failed with its error\\n* `GET /items/{id}`: the wire projection (units only once ready, no spoken, `audio_url`); an item