{"parentUuid":"6c717964-6826-4837-be13-b70656d824a2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuzBUcuLQTEBsKaa3SHA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation has started: two subagents are running, one on the workspace and `common/` (ASE-73), the other on the tts endpoints (ASE-74, in its own worktree).\n\n**Do I need another key?** Only the Modal proxy auth token, and it isn't in place yet: `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env` doesn't exist. Please create it before you leave, with `MODAL_PROXY_KEY=` and `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET=` lines. Everything else is already on the machine:\n- Firecrawl and Gemini keys in `api/.env`\n- the AI Gateway token in `pipeline/.dev.vars`\n- the Modal CLI login in `~/.modal.toml`, for the `modal serve` dev copy\n- wrangler logged in\n- cloudflared installed\n\nThe local S3 endpoint takes dummy keys. Without the token, everything still gets built and tested except the live calls to Modal.\n\n**Order of work:**\n1. Once `common/` is committed, the pipeline (ASE-75 to 79) and API (ASE-80) work start in parallel, each in its own worktree.\n2. I merge each worktree into `feat/cloudflare-migration` as it finishes.\n3. Then come local dev (ASE-81), CI (ASE-82), the code reviews and the manual rows, run locally.\n\nThe end-to-end runs will use small articles only. Questions and progress will reach you in the Plannotator Inbox. Nothing gets deployed or pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":106712,"output_tokens":538,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":34},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":585,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":538,"cache_read_