{"parentUuid":"5fbf706e-c8b4-4310-a224-f186f74cbe90","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"13a22853-87f6-4b33-9be7-aa27e0225bbb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PaZEt6nJFgemEtAayFbUTC","type":"tool_result","content":"  uv run ruff check  All checks passed!\n  uv run ty check    All checks passed!\n\n  Serving the dev copy\n\n  - Run cd tts && uv run modal serve app.py. It prints one web function URL: https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run.\n  - MODAL_START_URL is https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run/start (POST, JSON {paragraphs, voice?, destination}).\n  - MODAL_RESULT_URL is https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run/result (GET ?call_id=).\n  - Both need the Modal-Key and Modal-Secret headers. The deployed app should be https://asermax--nagara-tts-web.modal.run/{start,result}; I derived that from the dev URL without deploying.\n  - Modal disables memory snapshots for ephemeral apps, so cold starts on the dev copy will be slower.\n\n  Cleanup:\n  - I stopped the dev server by the PID I recorded. SIGINT sent to the uv process did not stop it; SIGTERM sent to its child process did.\n  - The ephemeral app ap-eEdbl27EyXzJF1NfCSNDH9 was still listed afterwards, so I stopped it with modal app stop -y on that id.\n  - The deployed nagara-tts was not touched.\n\n  Design drift and details the design did not fix\n\n  - One web function, two routes: the endpoints are /start and /result on a single web function, matching \"a small CPU web function\". The note's \"two web endpoints\" means two routes, not two Modal\n    functions.\n  - Result fields dropped: sample_rate and the per-entry index and text are no longer returned. The program design specifies only {format, duration, timings[{start, end}]}.\n  - synthesize returns a dict: the endpoint rebuilds the result with SynthesisResult.model_validate. Unpickling a pydantic class across containers would depend on how each container names the\n    module.\n  - Malformed ids: for an id without the fc- prefix, Modal raises a generic ExecutionError (I checked this against Modal). The endpoint checks the prefix itself so the answer is 422, not 500. An\n    unissued fc-… id raises NotFoundError, which maps to 422.\n  - Function timeout: Modal's FunctionTimeoutError, raised when the synthesis runs out of time, is answered 500, the same as any other failed synthesis.\n  - Error bodies: the design gives no body for 410 and 422. Both answer {error}.\n  - Extra GPU image layer: the program design does not mention it. It is needed because app.py imports fastapi and httpx when the module loads, in every container.\n\n  No decisions were taken without the user, and I sent no questions.\n\n  Linear\n\n  ASE-74 went to In Progress, then Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n  Unresolved\n\n  - No authenticated or synthesis check: the proxy token file is missing, so neither the endpoints with credentials nor a real synthesis uploading to a presigned R2 URL has run.\n  - New GPU image layer unbuilt: the dev copy got no authenticated call, so it never spawned Kokoro, and the new layer has never been built on Modal.\n  - B1's by-hand part (audio landing in R2 and playing) is left for the manual validation.\n\n✻ Sautéed for 5m 45s · done 3:41 AM\n\n❯ <supervisor-agent>An added safety rule: never run rm -rf. A user rule turns it into a permission dialog that blocks you while the user is away. Delete with rm -r <named path>, or leave\n  temporary folders in /tmp.</supervisor-agent>\n\n● Got it, I won't use rm -rf from now on. I never ran it in this task: the only deletions were rm /tmp/nagara-tts-serve.pid and rm -f /tmp/nagara-tts-serve.log, two files I had created myself. If\n  I need to delete anything else, I'll use rm -r on a named path or leave temporary folders in /tmp.\n\n✻ Churned for 2s · done 3:41 AM\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n❯ The proxy token is in modal-proxy.env now, run the live check\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  🤖 Opus 5.5 | 🟢 108k/1000k (10%) | 📍 ~/.herdr/worktrees/nagara/feat-cloudflare-migration-tts | 🌿 feat/cloudflare-migration-tts\n  -- INSERT -- ⏵⏵ auto mode on (shift+tab to cycle)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"be1643a5-ad60-4b37-b789-9efe1cac7203","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:42:07.079Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  uv run ruff check  All checks passed!\n  uv run ty check    All checks passed!\n\n  Serving the dev copy\n\n  - Run cd tts && uv run modal serve app.py. It prints one web function URL: https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run.\n  - MODAL_START_URL is https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run/start (POST, JSON {paragraphs, voice?, destination}).\n  - MODAL_RESULT_URL is https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run/result (GET ?call_id=).\n  - Both need the Modal-Key and Modal-Secret headers. The deployed app should be https://asermax--nagara-tts-web.modal.run/{start,result}; I derived that from the dev URL without deploying.\n  - Modal disables memory snapshots for ephemeral apps, so cold starts on the dev copy will be slower.\n\n  Cleanup:\n  - I stopped the dev server by the PID I recorded. SIGINT sent to the uv process did not stop it; SIGTERM sent to its child process did.\n  - The ephemeral app ap-eEdbl27EyXzJF1NfCSNDH9 was still listed afterwards, so I stopped it with modal app stop -y on that id.\n  - The deployed nagara-tts was not touched.\n\n  Design drift and details the design did not fix\n\n  - One web function, two routes: the endpoints are /start and /result on a single web function, matching \"a small CPU web function\". The note's \"two web endpoints\" means two routes, not two Modal\n    functions.\n  - Result fields dropped: sample_rate and the per-entry index and text are no longer returned. The program design specifies only {format, duration, timings[{start, end}]}.\n  - synthesize returns a dict: the endpoint rebuilds the result with SynthesisResult.model_validate. Unpickling a pydantic class across containers would depend on how each container names the\n    module.\n  - Malformed ids: for an id without the fc- prefix, Modal raises a generic ExecutionError (I checked this against Modal). The endpoint checks the prefix itself so the answer is 422, not 500. An\n    unissued fc-… id raises NotFoundError, which maps to 422.\n  - Function timeout: Modal's FunctionTimeoutError, raised when the synthesis runs out of time, is answered 500, the same as any other failed synthesis.\n  - Error bodies: the design gives no body for 410 and 422. Both answer {error}.\n  - Extra GPU image layer: the program design does not mention it. It is needed because app.py imports fastapi and httpx when the module loads, in every container.\n\n  No decisions were taken without the user, and I sent no questions.\n\n  Linear\n\n  ASE-74 went to In Progress, then Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n  Unresolved\n\n  - No authenticated or synthesis check: the proxy token file is missing, so neither the endpoints with credentials nor a real synthesis uploading to a presigned R2 URL has run.\n  - New GPU image layer unbuilt: the dev copy got no authenticated call, so it never spawned Kokoro, and the new layer has never been built on Modal.\n  - B1's by-hand part (audio landing in R2 and playing) is left for the manual validation.\n\n✻ Sautéed for 5m 45s · done 3:41 AM\n\n❯ <supervisor-agent>An added safety rule: never run rm -rf. A user rule turns it into a permission dialog that blocks you while the user is away. Delete with rm -r <named path>, or leave\n  temporary folders in /tmp.</supervisor-agent>\n\n● Got it, I won't use rm -rf from now on. I never ran it in this task: the only deletions 