{"parentUuid":"f49159ae-d45b-44c4-b774-48d2c1059b1a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"07bf287a-26cc-4e27-ac2f-fcd1aa1d06a5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C6S1riixWBtcW1kxYFM3bu","type":"tool_result","content":"  ├─────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ A15 │ › replays a response recorded with gzip headers without decompressing it                                                                                                               │\n  ├─────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ A16 │ › answers repeated identical requests with the recorded responses in order                                                                                                             │\n  ├─────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ A17 │ › fails a request the cassette does not hold                                                                                                                                           │\n  └─────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n  The Gemini fixture is a copy of api/tests/cassettes/test_describe/test_a_real_code_describe_parses_and_is_clean.yaml, because api/ is about to be deleted. synthesis-poll.yaml is a fabricated\n  two-response poll sequence.\n\n  Check output\n\n  common/   Test Files 4 passed (4) · Tests 17 passed (17)\n            biome check: Checked 22 files. No fixes applied.\n            tsc --noEmit: clean\n  pipeline/ Test Files 11 passed (11) · Tests 55 passed | 1 skipped (56)\n            biome check: Checked 49 files. No fixes applied.\n            types (build:bundle && tsc --noEmit): clean · vite build: ✓ built in 1.41s\n\n  During the pipeline run, workerd prints \"uncaught exception … code had hung\" several times. The messages appear around job-index.test.ts, http.test.ts and read-path.test.ts, all of which still\n  pass. The two runtime packages that execute the tests, workerd and miniflare, are the same versions as before the move. I did not run the old tree to compare.\n\n  Design drift\n\n  - database_id is a placeholder. common/wrangler.jsonc uses 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 because wrangler d1 list shows no D1 database on the account. Local D1 state is keyed by this id,\n    so api/wrangler.jsonc and pipeline/wrangler.jsonc must use the same value to share the database in .wrangler-state. The real id replaces it in all three files once the production D1 is\n    created, which is a remote action I did not take.\n  - An unmatched request reaches the client as a 500, not a rejected fetch. msw 2 turns the handler's thrown error into a 500 response whose body says no cassette interaction matches <METHOD>\n    <url>. A client that recovers from a 500 on its own, such as a describe child that falls back to the floor, would hide the miss. Only an assertion on the outcome would catch it. The pipeline's\n    tests should assert results, such as the described spoken form, not just ready.\n  - Credential headers are never compared. The note says they are \"removed before matching\". Since no header takes part in a match, a request that carries credentials still matches, which gives\n    the same result.\n  - CostEntryRow.cached is typed boolean as the program design says, but D1 stores it as 0 or 1 and returns it that way.\n  - Not done here: .gitignore and .wrangler-state/ belong to the local-development part (section 7 of the program design). I added only common/.gitignore with .wrangler/. I did not add\n    @nagara/common as a dependency of the pipeline; the pipeline subagent adds it.\n\n  Decisions taken without the user\n\n  None.\n\n  Linear\n\n  ASE-73 is moved to In Progress and then Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n  Unresolved\n\n  The production D1 database does not exist yet. Someone has to create it and put its id in place of the placeholder.\n\n✻ Worked for 7m 22s · done 3:45 AM\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n❯\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  🤖 Opus 5.5 | 🟢 155k/1000k (15%) | 📍 ~/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs | 🌿 feat/cloudflare-migration\n  -- INSERT -- ⏵⏵ auto mode on (shift+tab to cycle)\n\n624387d chore: move to one root pnpm workspace\nee21dae feat(common): add the @nagara/common package\nfdc0c1a docs: record what the Cloudflare migration test design settled\n4930ea1 docs: record the program design of the Cloudflare migration\n54cb15d chore: add local spike rules","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cc95b71c-e3c1-4d96-aabe-2e85cac48885","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:45:12.178Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  ├─────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ A15 │ › replays a response recorded with gzip headers without decompressing it                                                                                                               │\n  ├─────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ A16 │ › answers repeated identical requests with the recorded responses in order                                                                                                             │\n  ├─────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ A17 │ › fails a request the cassette does not hold                                                                                                                                           │\n  └─────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n  The Gemini fixture is a copy of api/tests/cassettes/test_describe/test_a_real_code_describe_parses_and_is_clean.yaml, because api/ is about to be deleted. synthesis-poll.yaml is a fabricated\n  two-response poll sequence.\n\n  Check output\n\n  common/   Test Files 4 passed (4) · Tests 17 passed (17)\n            biome check: Checked 22 files. No fixes applied.\n            tsc --noEmit: clean\n  pipeline/ Test Files 11 passed (11) · Tests 55 passed | 1 skipped (56)\n            biome check: Checked 49 files. No fixes applied.\n            types (build:bundle && tsc --noEmit): clean · vite build: ✓ built in 1.41s\n\n  During the pipeline run, workerd prints \"uncaught exception … code had hung\" several times. The messages appear around job-index.test.ts, http.test.ts and read-path.test.ts, all of which still\n  pass. The two runtime packages that execute the tests, workerd and miniflare, are the same versions as before the move. I did not run the old tree to compare.\n\n  Design drift\n\n  - database_id is a placeholder. common/wrangler.jsonc uses 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 because wrangler d1 list shows no D1 database on the account. Local D1 state is keyed by this id,\n    so api/wrangler.jsonc and pipeline/wrangler.jsonc must use the same value to share the database in .wrangler-state. The real id replaces it in all three files once the production D1 is\n    created, which is a remote action I did not take.\n  - An unmatched request reaches the client as a 500, not a rejected fetch. msw 2 turns the handler's thrown error into a 500 response whose body says no cassette interaction matches <METHOD>\n    <url>. A client that recovers from a 500 on its own, such as a describe child that falls back to the floor, would hide the miss. Only an assertion on the outcome would catch it. The pipeline's\n    tests should assert results, such as the described spoken form, not just ready.\n  - Credential headers are never compared. The note says they are \"removed before matching\". Since no header takes part in a match, a request that carries credentials still matches, which gives\n    the same result.\n  - CostEntryRow.cached is typed boolean as the program design says, but D1 stores it as 0 or 1 and returns it that way.\n  - Not done here: .gitignore and .wrangler-state/ belong to the local-development part (section 7 of the program design). I added only common/.gitignore with .wrangler/. I did not add\n    @nagara/common as a dependency of the pipeline; the pipeline subagent adds it.\n\n  Decisions taken without the user\n\n  None.\n\n  Linear\n\n  ASE-73 is moved to In Progress and then Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n  Unresolved\n\n  The production D1 database does not exist yet. Someone has to create it and put its id in place of the placeholder.\n\n✻ Worked for 7m 22s · done 3:45 AM\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n❯\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────