{"parentUuid":"4d91038c-dfbc-4888-bc0f-aa1c0a7bf299","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuzsTc1GafZstVwkKASo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RsnhzoYMASpX4dmYPGnBZk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs\ncp implement-common.md implement-pipeline.md; cat >> implement-pipeline.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Your part: pipeline/ (ASE-75 to ASE-79)\n\nTasks, in this order: ASE-75 (DomainQueue as a lease), ASE-76 (the item Workflow through the recipe step, plus the fake agent for tests), ASE-77 (the images step, plus the Images binding check), ASE-78 (the describe step), ASE-79 (start synthesis, wait for synthesis, store). You work in a worktree on branch `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline`, forked from `feat/cloudflare-migration` after the workspace and `common/` landed (commits ee21dae, 624387d). Touch only `pipeline/`, plus the root lockfile and workspace file when you add a dependency. Do not edit `common/`. When `common/` is missing something you need or has a bug, say so in a question to the orchestrator (see below) and work around it locally until answered.\n\n- Add `@nagara/common` as a workspace dependency of `pipeline/`.\n- The pipeline's existing extraction-service code (POST /jobs, GET /jobs, the job index, the extraction Workflow) is replaced as the program design's module list says: new, touched and deleted files.\n- Your tests: tree C (C1 to C28) of the test design. The two \"Implementation tasks\" at its end are yours: the fake agent for C7 to C10 (configured through configuration, no environment branch) and the Images binding check for C1 and C11.\n- From the common/ subagent: an unmatched cassette request reaches the client as a 500 response, not a rejected fetch, so a step that recovers from a 500 (a describe child falling back to the floor) would hide the miss. Assert the outcomes (the described spoken form, the stored keys), not only that the item reached `ready`.\n- `common/wrangler.jsonc` uses the placeholder D1 `database_id` 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000. Use the same value in `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc` so the local state is shared.\n- Do not run the dev server against real services; local end-to-end runs come later in another task. Your tests replay cassettes.\n- Questions about `common/` or about how your part fits with the api's part go to the orchestrator, not to the user: end your turn with the question wrapped in `<subagent-ask>…</subagent-ask>`. Design questions only the user can answer go to the Inbox as above.\n- Commit each task as it goes green, so the work survives.\nEOF\ncp implement-common.md implement-api.md; cat >> implement-api.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Your part: api/ (ASE-80)\n\nTask: ASE-80 \"api/: the TypeScript API Worker\". You work in a worktree on branch `feat/cloudflare-migration-api`, forked from `feat/cloudflare-migration` after the workspace and `common/` landed (commits ee21dae, 624387d). Touch only `api/`, plus the root workspace file (add `api/`) and the root lockfile. Do not edit `common/` or `pipeline/`.\n\n- Replace the Python `api/` tree with the TypeScript Worker `nagara-api` as the program design's module list says. Delete the Python tree (FastAPI app, alembic, pyproject, tests, Railway files). Before deleting, copy nothing secret anywhere; `api/.env` is git-ignored: leave the file itself on disk untouched (the local-development task reads its keys later), and make sure the new `.gitignore` keeps ignoring it and `.dev.vars`.\n- The `ITEM_WORKFLOW` binding is cross-script (`script_name: nagara`, class `ItemWorkflow`); in tests, stand it in through configuration as the program design and the spikes (`cross-script-binding/`, `workflow-testing/`) say.\n- `common/wrangler.jsonc` uses the placeholder D1 `database_id` 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000. Use the same value in `api/wrangler.jsonc` so the local state is shared.\n- Your tests: tree D (D1 to D27) of the test design.\n- Do not run the dev server against real services; local end-to-end runs come later in another task.\n- Questions about `common/` or about how your part fits with the pipeline's part go to the orchestrator: end your turn with the question wrapped in `<subagent-ask>…</subagent-ask>`. Design questions only the user can answer go to the Inbox as above.\n- Commit as you go green.\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper\n$H spawn --kind claude --label \"impl: pipeline (ASE-75..79)\" --model opus --worktree --branch feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline --base feat/cloudflare-migration --body \"<supervisor-agent>Read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/implement-pipeline.md. It is your full brief.</supervisor-agent>\"\n$H spawn --kind claude --label \"impl: api Worker (ASE-80)\" --model opus --worktree --branch feat/cloudflare-migration-api --base feat/cloudflare-migration --body \"<supervisor-agent>Read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/implement-api.md. It is your full brief.</supervisor-agent>\"\n$H prompt w30:p24 --body \"/mahou:agentic-review <supervisor-agent>Run the agentic review on your changeset: commits ee21dae and 624387d on feat/cloudflare-migration, measured against fdc0c1a (the integration branch before your work; do not measure against main). Fix inside the review's own bounds and leave the fixes uncommitted. Report what it fixed and what it skipped, with reasons. Two other subagents now work in worktrees forked from 624387d, on pipeline/ and api/, so keep fixes inside common/ and the root workspace files, and list any fix that changes a common/ export's shape or name.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Spawn pipeline and api subagents, dispatch the common review"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_d