{"parentUuid":"ebfa71cf-95f6-443a-90b2-37f7d914b2a0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"61746d9a-6f29-413a-be1a-758064f564ed","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L65HvRA6rVM9CEYkDh3BeL","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"pane_id\":\"w30:p24\",\"status\":\"done\"}\n\n[exited with code 0]\ndone\n# Agentic review of the `common/` changeset\n\nThe review ran three rounds against `fdc0c1a` and stopped with no findings left. Four fixes are in the working tree, uncommitted, and none of them changes the name or shape of a `common/` export. Nothing outside `common/` was touched.\n\n## How it ran\n\n- **Round 1:** twelve reviewers ran:\n  - reuse, simplification, efficiency and altitude;\n  - one conventions reviewer per source: the project `CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, mahou basics, and the wiki entries `cloudflare/vitest-plugin`, `d1`, `r2`, `local-dev` and the local `testing/cassettes-over-mocks`.\n- **Round 2:** all twelve were resumed. The only finding came from the `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` reviewer, about a round-1 fix.\n- **Round 3:** only that reviewer was resumed, and it returned nothing.\n\nI left `.mahou/basics.md` out of the sources: its only rule is about how subagents are spawned, so there is nothing in the code for it to check.\n\n## Fixed\n\n| Round | File | Fix | Raised by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `common/src/units.ts` | `ParagraphUnit`, `CodeUnit` and `ImageUnit` now build on a non-exported `TextUnit` base (`UnitWindow & {display, spoken}`) instead of repeating those two fields. | simplification, altitude, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` |\n| 1 | `common/testing/cassettes.ts` | `sortKeys` and the query sort in `requestKey` share one `byKey` comparator, and the `query` variable is inlined. | reuse, simplification, altitude |\n| 1 | `common/src/presign.ts` | The `signed` variable is inlined into the return. | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` |\n| 2 | `common/testing/cassettes.ts` | Restored the blank line before the `return` in `requestKey`, which the round-1 edit had removed. | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` |\n\nOn exports: the three unit types keep their names and resolve to the same structure. `TextUnit` is new but not exported. The other fixes only touch internals.\n\n## Skipped\n\n- **One root `biome.json`, `tsconfig.base.json` and pnpm `catalog:` instead of the per-package copies** (reuse, altitude). Each needs a new root file and edits to `pipeline/package.json` and `pipeline/`'s configs. Creating files is outside this review's bounds, and the other subagents own `pipeline/`.\n- **Splitting `row.ts` and `testing/cassettes.ts` into one module per function** (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`). The settled program design names these modules with these contents.\n- **Removing `encodeJson`, which has no caller yet** (simplification). The program design defines it as half of the JSON column codec, and the Workers' writers will use it. Removing it would change the export list.\n- **Reusing one `AwsClient` across calls** (efficiency). That changes `presign`'s signature. The reviewer itself rated the cost low, since building the client is cheap next to signing.\n- **Replacing the hand-written `*.yaml?raw` declaration with `vite/client` types** (simplification). `vite` is not a direct dependency of `common/`, and pnpm's strict layout would not resolve it.\n\nThe two pipeline-side skips (the root config files and the catalog) can only be done once the pipeline and api branches merge back.\n\n## Checks after the last fix\n\nIn `common/`:\n- `biome check`: 22 files, no fixes needed.\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean.\n- `vitest run`: 4 files, 17 tests passed.\n\nThe reviewers' findings files are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/agentic-review-common/`, and all reviewer tabs are closed. The next step is mahou:human-review.\n M common/src/presign.ts\n M common/src/units.ts\n M common/testing/cassettes.ts","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"33726f41-cb2d-48e8-ba85-0b3aee6548a1","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:49:29.533Z","toolUseResult":{"s