**One root `biome.json`, `tsconfig.base.json` and pnpm `catalog:` instead of the per-package copies** (reuse, altitude). Each needs a new root file and edits to `pipeline/package.json` and `pipeline/`'s configs. Creating files is outside this review's bounds, and the other subagents own `pipeline/`.\n- **Splitting `row.ts` and `testing/cassettes.ts` into one module per function** (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`). The settled program design names these modules with these contents.\n- **Removing `encodeJson`, which has no caller yet** (simplification). The program design defines it as half of the JSON column codec, and the Workers' writers will use it. Removing it would change the export list.\n- **Reusing one `AwsClient` across calls** (efficiency). That changes `presign`'s signature. The reviewer itself rated the cost low, since building the client is cheap next to signing.\n- **Replacing the hand-written `*.yaml?raw` declaration with `vite/client` types** (simplification). `vite` is not a direct dependency of `common/`, and pnpm's strict layout would not resolve it.\n\nThe two pipeline-side skips (the root config files and the catalog) can only be done once the pipeline and api branches merge back.\n\n## Checks after the last fix\n\nIn `common/`:\n- `biome check`: 22 files, no fixes needed.\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean.\n- `vitest run`: 4 files, 17 tests passed.\n\nThe reviewers' findings files are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/agentic-review-common/`, and all reviewer tabs are closed. The next step is mahou:human-review.\n M common/src/presign.ts\n M common/src/units.ts\n M common/testing/cassettes.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0245f8fb-7f2b-4241-94dc-105fcf5f86c9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,