{"parentUuid":"4372136b-1da0-4590-9144-b84891921d70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv1CRjfqZXvcNkxpfr6C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UHVX64uQzWFctXczXaS8dU","name":"mcp__plannotator__plannotator_inbox","input":{"action":"send_message","thread":"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator","subject":"common/ review fixes: commit them?","body":"The agentic review of `common/` (ASE-73) finished after three rounds with no findings left. It left four small fixes uncommitted in the main checkout, and none of them changes a `common/` export:\n\n- `units.ts`: the paragraph, code and image units build on a shared non-exported `TextUnit` base instead of repeating `display` and `spoken`.\n- `testing/cassettes.ts`: one shared key comparator, an inlined variable, and a blank line restored.\n- `presign.ts`: an intermediate variable is inlined.\n\nSkipped, with reasons:\n- **Root configs:** one root biome, tsconfig base and pnpm catalog. They need pipeline/ edits, so they wait until the branches merge.\n- **Module split:** splitting `row.ts` and `cassettes.ts` into a module per function. The program design names those modules.\n- **`encodeJson`:** removing it. The Workers will use it.\n- **`AwsClient`:** reusing one client. It would change `presign`'s signature for a negligible gain.\n- **vite types:** using `vite/client` types. `common/` doesn't depend on vite.\n\nChecks: 17 tests pass, and biome and tsc are clean.\n\nIf you haven't answered by the time the manual validation is due, the fixes stay uncommitted in the working tree, and I'll run the validation on the committed code.\n\n:::question\nCommit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\n\n- [ ] Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\n- [ ] No, discard them\n\nRecommended: Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\n:::"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":133824,"output_tokens":889,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":205},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":889,"cache_read_input_tokens":133824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UHVX64uQzWFctXczXaS8dU":{"action":"send_message","thread":"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator","subject":"common/ review fixes: commit them?","body":"The agentic review of `common/` (ASE-73) finished after three rounds with no findings left. It left four small fixes uncommitted in the main checkout, and none of them changes a `common/` export:\n\n- `units.ts`: the paragraph, code and image units build on a shared non-exported `TextUnit` base instead of repeating `display` and `spoken`.\n- `testing/cassettes.ts`: one shared key comparator, an inlined variable, and a blank line restored.\n- `presign.ts`: an intermediate variable is inlined.\n\nSkipped, with reasons:\n- **Root configs:** one root biome, tsconfig base and pnpm catalog. They need pipeline/ edits, so they wait until the branches merge.\n- **Module split:** splitting `row.ts` and `cassettes.ts` into a module per function. The program design names those modules.\n- **`encodeJson`:** removing it. The Workers will use it.\n- **`AwsClient`:** reusing one client. It would change `presign`'s signature for a negligible gain.\n- **vite types:** using `vite/client` types. `common/` doesn't depend on vite.\n\nChecks: 17 tests pass, and biome and tsc are clean.\n\nIf you haven't answered by the time the manual validation is due, the fixes stay uncommitted in the working tree, and I'll run the validation on the committed code.\n\n:::question\nCommit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\n\n- [ ] Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\n- [ ] No, discard them\n\nRecommended: Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\n:::"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b31cc5c9-c2c7-4a59-b03f-73e532f5951e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfv1CRN6QFicY6TwD8ZPR","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9934c51a-41ad-4ca1-8255-de2cb3e0fb8f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:49:39.292Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
