{"parentUuid":"b1ecd84c-32cd-40ef-b33e-5be1f379084a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e6e94b49-5d1f-4775-90e5-464723d48de0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011eAX8os4nSnDD9wTgASEaN","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"pane_id\":\"w47:p2\",\"status\":\"done\"}\n\n[exited with code 0]\ndone\n# Report: api/ (ASE-80)\n\nThe Python API is replaced by the TypeScript Worker `nagara-api`. All 35 tests pass, and lint and type checks are clean. ASE-80 is in Linear as Done. One part of the task is not done: the cassettes did not move to `pipeline/` (see \"Not resolved\" below).\n\n## Branch and commit\n\n`feat/cloudflare-migration-api`, one commit on top of 624387d, not pushed:\n- `79ed096 feat(api): replace the Python API with the nagara-api Worker`\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Python tree deleted:** `app/`, `migrations/`, `alembic.ini`, `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, Railway files, `.python-version`, `.env.example`, and the tests apart from `tests/cassettes/`. `api/.env` is git-ignored and was never in this worktree, so nothing touched it. The new `api/.gitignore` ignores `.dev.vars`, `.wrangler/` and `node_modules/`; the root `.gitignore` still ignores `.env`.\n- **Config files:**\n  - `api/package.json` is `@nagara/api`, with `dev = wrangler dev --persist-to ../.wrangler-state`.\n  - `tsconfig.json` and `biome.json` are copied from `common/`.\n  - `wrangler.jsonc` sets:\n    - D1 `DB` with the placeholder id `00000000-…` and `migrations_dir ../common/migrations`.\n    - `ITEM_WORKFLOW` as `{name item, class_name ItemWorkflow, script_name nagara}`.\n    - The custom domain `nagara.asermax.com` and dev port 8787.\n    - Vars: `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` (the account's `r2.cloudflarestorage.com` URL), `R2_BUCKET` set to `nagara`, `RETRY_MAX` 3, `REQUEUE_AFTER_MS` 900000.\n  - Secrets are typed in `src/env.d.ts`: `API_KEY`, `R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`.\n  - `wrangler deploy --dry-run` bundles the Worker (28 KiB) and lists every binding.\n- **Source:**\n  - `src/index.ts`: answers `/health` before the guard, then the key guard, then the route table.\n  - `src/guard.ts`: compares the key with `timingSafeEqual`.\n  - `src/voices.ts`, `src/response.ts`.\n  - `src/routes/{enqueue,poll,retry,audio,images}.ts`.\n  - `src/items/{create,requeue,retry-claim}.ts`.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `test/setup.ts` applies `../common/migrations`.\n  - `test/helpers/workflow-stand-in.ts` records `create`, `get` and `restart` calls.\n  - `test/helpers/api.ts` calls the Worker's `fetch` with `{...env, ITEM_WORKFLOW: standIn}`.\n  - One test file per route, plus `guard.test.ts`.\n- **Stand-in for the Workflow binding:** the vitest pool will not start while the cross-script binding points at a script that does not exist (\"refers to a service core:user:dev-registry-proxy\"). Overriding `workflows` in the miniflare options doesn't fix it, because the options are merged with wrangler's. The fix is a placeholder worker named `nagara` in the vitest config's `miniflare.workers` (`test/fixtures/pipeline-placeholder.js`, an empty `ItemWorkflow`), so the binding resolves. Each test then passes in the recording stand-in through `env`.\n\n## Row-to-test mapping\n\n| Row | Test |\n|---|---|\n| D1 | enqueue: writes a queued row with the requested voice and creates the item's Workflow |\n| D2 | enqueue: picks a voice from the curated pool when the request names none |\n| D3 | enqueue: refuses a body with no url and writes no row |\n| D4 | enqueue: returns the item failed with the create's error when the Workflow cannot be created |\n| D5 | poll: returns a ready item's timed units without their spoken form, its audio url and duration |\n| D6 | poll: holds a generating item's units back and gives it no audio url |\n| D7 | poll: returns a failed item with its error |\n| D8 | poll: restarts a stale queued item from its restart point without counting a retry |\n| D9 | poll: creates the Workflow for a stale queued item whose instance never ran |\n| D10 | poll: restarts a stale queued item once when two polls arrive together. I removed the claim condition and confirmed the test fails without it. |\n| D11 | poll: leaves a queued item two minutes old alone |\n| D12 | poll: answers 404 for an unknown id |\n| D13 | retry: queues a failed item again and restarts its Workflow from the failed step |\n| D14 | retry: restarts an item that failed in recipe from the lease |\n| D15 | retry: creates the Workflow for an item whose instance was never created |\n| D16 | retry: refuses an item that has used its three retries |\n| D17 | retry: refuses an item that is not failed |\n| D18 | retry: accepts one of two retries sent together and counts it once |\n| D19 | retry: answers 404 for an unknown id |\n| D20 | audio: redirects a ready item to a GET URL signed for its audio key for one hour |\n| D21 | audio: answers 404 for an item still generating |\n| D22 | images: redirects to a GET URL signed for the image's key even before the item is ready |\n| D23 | images: answers 404 for an unknown item |\n| D24 | images: redirects an unknown hash too, leaving the miss to R2 |\n| D25 | guard: answers 401 to each of the 5 `/items` routes without a key |\n| D26 | guard: answers 401 to each of the 5 `/items` routes with a wrong key |\n| D27 | guard: lets /health through without a key |\n\nThe \"by hand\" parts of the `test + manual` rows were not run.\n\n## Check output\n\n```\napi/     biome check . → Checked 33 files … No fixes applied.\n         tsc --noEmit → (clean)\n         vitest run   → Test Files 6 passed (6) · Tests 35 passed (35)\ncommon/  vitest run → Tests 17 passed (17) · tsc --noEmit clean   (rerun because the root lockfile changed)\n```\n\n## Design drift\n\n- **No R2 binding on the API:** `deployment-and-ci.md` and `persistence-and-storage.md` say both Workers bind the R2 bucket. The program design's binding list for `api/` doesn't include one, and the API only signs URLs, so I left it out. If the local-development task wants the API to serve its own local S3 endpoint, it can add the binding then.\n- **The API never writes `workflow_instance_id`:** `item-lifecycle.md` says the Workflow's first step writes it. A row without one is treated as \"never ran\" and gets a `create`.\n- **One extra module, `src/items/restart.ts`:** it holds the create-or-restart logic that requeue and retry share.\n- **One extra module, `src/routes/signed-redirect.ts`:** it holds the presign-and-307 logic that the audio and image routes share.\n- **One extra module, `src/respond.ts`:** a small helper for the `{detail}` error bodies.\n- **`/health` answers plain `ok`:** this follows the program design; the old Python API answered `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`.\n\n## Decisions taken without the user\n\nNone needed the Inbox. These are the choices the notes don't pin down:\n- **D4 status code:** when `create` throws, enqueue still answers `202`, with the item at `failed`.\n- **Error bodies:** they keep FastAPI's `{\"detail\": …}` shape, so clients see no change.\n- **Fields before ready:** `duration` and `audio_url` are `null` until the item is ready, not left out, again so clients see no change.\n- **Retry order:** the retry route claims first and reads the row afterwards. A retry that loses a race then reports the status the winner wrote.\n- **A failing `create` or `restart` during a retry or re-queue:** the error goes up as a 500, and the item stays `queued`, where the 15-minute re-queue picks it up again.\n- **The bucket name `nagara` is my placeholder:** nothing in the notes or the program design settles it.\n\n## Linear\n\n- ASE-80 moved to In Progress, then Done.\n- No tasks created or canceled.\n\n## Not resolved\n\n- **Cassettes:** ASE-80 says the cassettes move to `pipeline/test/cassettes/`, but my brief forbids touching `pipeline/`. They are still under `api/tests/cassettes/`; whoever owns `pipeline/` needs to move them and delete that folder.\n- **Introspection across `script_name`:** whether Workflow introspection works through a cross-script binding is still untested. The API tests don't need it because they use the stand-in.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5d61b82b-e186-42f0-b039-747eb4292a56","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:54:23.174Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"pane_id\":\"w47:p2\",\"status\":\"done\"}\n\n[exited with code 0]\ndone\n# Report: api/ (ASE-80)\n\nThe Python API is replaced by the TypeScript Worker `nagara-api`. All 35 tests pass, and lint and type checks are clean. ASE-80 is in Linear as Done. One part of the task is not done: the cassettes did not move to `pipeline/` (see \"Not resolved\" below).\n\n## Branch and commit\n\n`feat/cloudflare-migration-api`, one commit on top of 624387d, not pushed:\n- `79ed096 feat(api): replace the Python API with the nagara-api Worker`\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Python tree deleted:** `app/`, `migrations/`, `alembic.ini`, `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, Railway files, `.python-version`, `.env.example`, and the tests apart from `tests/cassettes/`. `api/.env` is git-ignored and was never in this worktree, so nothing touched it. The new `api/.gitignore` ignores `.dev.vars`, `.wrangler/` and `node_modules/`; the root `.gitignore` still ignores `.env`.\n- **Config files:**\n  - `api/package.json` is `@nagara/api`, with `dev = wrangler dev --persist-to ../.wrangler-state`.\n  - `tsconfig.json` and `biome.json` are copied from `common/`.\n  - `wrangler.jsonc` sets:\n    - D1 `DB` with the placeholder id `00000000-…` and `migrations_dir ../common/migrations`.\n    - `ITEM_WORKFLOW` as `{name item, class_name ItemWorkflow, script_name nagara}`.\n    - The custom domain `nagara.asermax.com` and dev port 8787.\n    - Vars: `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` (the account's `r2.cloudflarestorage.com` URL), `R2_BUCKET` set to `nagara`, `RETRY_MAX` 3, `REQUEUE_AFTER_MS` 900000.\n  - Secrets are typed in `src/env.d.ts`: `API_KEY`, `R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`.\n  - `wrangler deploy --dry-run` bundles the Worker (28 KiB) and lists 