{"parentUuid":"4da6c88a-20b7-491f-84ee-be6f47a4a31e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv1m61BnED1FwXJ5CVuS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CSG9yhAqqninNmqxthTmUk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p24 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\" | tee /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/impl-ci.md","description":"Collect the CI result"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":363,"cache_read_input_tokens":150138,"output_tokens":223,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":363,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":223,"cache_read_input_tokens":150138,"cache_creation_input_tokens":363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":363},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CSG9yhAqqninNmqxthTmUk":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w30:p24 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\" | tee /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/impl-ci.md","description":"Collect the CI result"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8d26a971-7445-4e2c-9cfc-8e4dca6090e1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfv1m5d7ZYJr4TLs3kZem","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c76b094-620b-4977-8690-b6c33cba1a74","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:56:55.314Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"9c76b094-620b-4977-8690-b6c33cba1a74","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d52732e2-6697-4599-bad0-1df8f92313c9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CSG9yhAqqninNmqxthTmUk","type":"tool_result","content":"done\n# ASE-82 report: one Cloudflare workflow\n\n`cloudflare.yml` now replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`, and `tts.yml` is unchanged. actionlint finds nothing, and walking the job graph by hand shows that a failed `common/` check stops all three deploy jobs. No workflow was triggered and nothing was pushed.\n\n## Commit\n\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `f01debc` | ci: deploy common, pipeline and api from one Cloudflare workflow |\n\nThe commit is on `feat/cloudflare-migration` in the main checkout and touches only `.github/workflows/`.\n\n## What the workflow does\n\n- **Trigger:** a push to `main` that touches `common/**`, `pipeline/**` or `api/**`.\n- **`changes`:** `dorny/paths-filter@v4` sets the outputs `common`, `pipeline` and `api`.\n- **Checks:** every check job installs with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` on Node 24 and runs the script in its tree.\n  - `common-checks` runs only when `common` changed. It is a matrix of five parallel legs: `common` test, lint and types, plus `pipeline` types and `api` types.\n  - `pipeline-checks` and `api-checks` run only when their tree changed. Each is a matrix of test, lint and types.\n  - All matrices use `fail-fast: false`, so one failing leg does not cancel the others.\n- **Deploy chain:** every deploy job is gated on `!failure() && !cancelled()` plus its own trigger.\n\n| Job | `needs` | Runs when | Does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `migrate` | changes, common-checks | `common` changed | `d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` in `common/` |\n| `deploy-pipeline` | changes, common-checks, pipeline-checks, migrate | `pipeline` changed, or migrate succeeded | `pnpm build` in `pipeline/`, then `deploy -c dist/nagara/wrangler.json` |\n| `deploy-api` | changes, all three check jobs, migrate, deploy-pipeline | `api` changed, or deploy-pipeline succeeded | `deploy` in `api/` |\n\nThe deploys use `cloudflare/wrangler-action` with `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`. I kept the action versions the old files already pinned (checkout v7, pnpm/action-setup v4, setup-node v5, wrangler-action v3), because the old `pipeline.yml` deployed successfully with them. pnpm/action-setup reads its version from the root `packageManager`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- **actionlint** 1.7.12, run through `go run`, exits 0 with no findings.\n- **Hand walk of the job graph.** Each deploy job lists every upstream check job in its own `needs`. A failed check therefore stops it directly, without depending on how `failure()` passes through a skipped job in between.\n\n| Push | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `common/` check fails | migrate, deploy-pipeline and deploy-api are all skipped, because `common-checks` failed and sits in each of their `needs` |\n| `pipeline/` check fails | deploy-pipeline and deploy-api are skipped; migrate still runs if `common/` changed |\n| `api/` check fails | only deploy-api is skipped |\n| migrate fails | deploy-pipeline and deploy-api are skipped |\n| only `pipeline/` changed | migrate is skipped (its tree did not change) and that stops nothing; deploy-pipeline runs, then deploy-api |\n| only `common/` changed | checks, then migrate, deploy-pipeline and deploy-api |\n| only `api/` changed | only deploy-api runs |\n| docs only | the workflow does not trigger |\n\n## Design drift\n\n- **A pipeline-only push also redeploys the API.** That follows the program design's rule that a deploy runs when \"its own tree changed or an upstream deploy run\". The note only says such a push \"deploys the pipeline without a migration\" and does not mention the API.\n- **A change to `cloudflare.yml` alone, or to the root `pnpm-lock.yaml` or `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, triggers nothing.** The note filters each tree to its own directory. The old `pipeline.yml` did trigger on its own file.\n- **No `concurrency` group.** The note's warning says nothing serializes two runs, and I kept it that way. The old files' `cancel-in-progress: true` would be unsafe here, because it could cancel a run in the middle of a migration.\n\n## Linear\n\nASE-82 is moved to In Progress and then Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n## Not yet verifiable\n\nThe workflow has never run. The api and pipeline worktrees still have to provide `test`, `lint`, `types` and the pipeline's `build` scripts, and `api/` has to become a workspace package with its own `wrangler.jsonc`. The `nagara` D1 database also still has to be created.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"50d38dbb-d160-4bc9-ae94-eee3cf91e8d5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:56:55.848Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\n# ASE-82 report: one Cloudflare workflow\n\n`cloudflare.yml` now replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`, and `tts.yml` is unchanged. actionlint finds nothing, and walking the job graph by hand shows that a failed `common/` check stops all three deploy jobs. No workflow was triggered and nothing was pushed.\n\n## Commit\n\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `f01debc` | ci: deploy common, pipeline and api from one Cloudflare workflow |\n\nThe commit is on `feat/cloudflare-migration` in the main checkout and touches only `.github/workflows/`.\n\n## What the workflow does\n\n- **Trigger:** a push to `main` that touches `common/**`, `pipeline/**` or `api/**`.\n- **`changes`:** `dorny/paths-filter@v4` sets the outputs `common`, `pipeline` and `api`.\n- **Checks:** every check job installs with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` on Node 24 and runs the script in its tree.\n  - `common-checks` runs only when `common` changed. It is a matrix of five parallel legs: `common` test, lint and types, plus `pipeline` types and `api` types.\n  - `pipeline-checks` and `api-checks` run only when their tree changed. Each is a matrix of test, lint and types.\n  - All matrices use `fail-fast: false`, so one failing leg does not cancel the others.\n- **Deploy chain:** every deploy job is gated on `!failure() && !cancelled()` plus its own trigger.\n\n| Job | `needs` | Runs when | Does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `migrate` | changes, common-checks | `common` changed | `d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` in `common/` |\n| `deploy-pipeline` | changes, common-checks, pipeline-checks, migrate | `pipeline` changed, or migrate succeeded | `pnpm build` in `pipeline/`, then `deploy -c dist/nagara/wrangler.json` |\n| `deploy-api` | changes, all three check jobs, migrate, deploy-pipeline | `api` changed, or deploy-pipeline succeeded | `deploy` in `api/` |\n\nThe deploys use `cloudflare/wrangler-action` with `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`. I kept the action versions the old files already pinned (checkout v7, pnpm/action-setup v4, setup-node v5, wrangler-action v3), because the old `pipeline.yml` deployed successfully with them. pnpm/action-setup reads its version from the root `packageManager`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- **actionlint** 1.7.12, run through `go run`, exits 0 with no findings.\n- **Hand walk of the job graph.** Each deploy job lists every upstream check job in its own `needs`. A failed check therefore stops it directly, without depending on how `failure()` passes through a skipped job in between.\n\n| Push | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `common/` check fails | migrate, deploy-pipeline and deploy-api are all skipped, because `common-checks` failed and sits in each of their `needs` |\n| `pipeline/` check fails | deploy-pipeline and deploy-api are skipped; migrate still runs if `common/` changed |\n| `api/` check fails | only deploy-api is skipped |\n| migrate fails | deploy-pipeline and deploy-api are skipped |\n| only `pipeline/` changed | migrate is skipped (its tree did not change) and that stops nothing; deploy-pipeline runs, then deploy-api |\n| only `common/` changed | checks, then migrate, deploy-pipeline and deploy-api |\n| only `api/` changed | only deploy-api runs |\n| docs only | the workflow does not trigger |\n\n## Design drift\n\n- **A pipeline-only push also redeploys the API.** That follows the program design's rule that a deploy runs when \"its own tree changed or an upstream deploy run\". The note only says such a push \"deploys the pipeline without a migration\" and does not mention the API.\n- **A change to `cloudflare.yml` alone, or to the root `pnpm-lock.yaml` or `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, triggers nothing.** The note filters each tree to its own directory. The old `pipeline.yml` did trigger on its own file.\n- **No `concurrency` group.** The note's warning says nothing serializes two runs, and I kept it that way. The old files' `cancel-in-progress: true` would be unsafe here, because it could cancel a run in the middle of a migration.\n\n## Linear\n\nASE-82 is moved to In Progress and then Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n## Not yet verifiable\n\nThe workflow has never run. The api and pipeline worktrees still have to provide `test`, `lint`, `types` and the pipeline's `build` scripts, and `api/` has to become a workspace package with its own `wrangler.jsonc`. The `nagara` D1 database also still has to be created.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8d26a971-7445-4e2c-9cfc-8e4dca6090e1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"fila