{"parentUuid":"2e1c44e8-b400-4d45-9dc1-b867dfae6c4d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv1vSLYbbRfDA8FgqwNc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V6uPHSWYbCazjiUGNPjFzM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w45:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Your report scrolled out of reach. Repeat it in full as your final message: the review's fixes (uncommitted) and skips with reasons, the checks after the fixes, and the live check results row by row.</supervisor-agent>\"; sleep 10; $H wait w45:p2 --timeout 600000 >/dev/null; $H collect w45:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('message',''))\" | tee /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/review-tts.md","description":"Ask tts subagent to repeat its report and collect"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2124,"cache_read_input_tokens":155388,"output_tokens":367,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":155388,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2124},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01V6uPHSWYbCazjiUGNPjFzM":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w45:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Your report scrolled out of reach. Repeat it in full as your final message: the review's fixes (uncommitted) and skips with reasons, the checks after the fixes, and the live check results row by row.</supervisor-agent>\"; sleep 10; $H wait w45:p2 --timeout 600000 >/dev/null; $H collect w45:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('message',''))\" | tee /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/review-tts.md","description":"Ask tts subagent to repeat its report and collect"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2bee6f56-12f2-4812-9aff-301968b65158","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfv1vRzTeEKoHeiLYQdup","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"713cb97a-14af-4419-8bb6-0b2eeb07b71f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:59:03.843Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"713cb97a-14af-4419-8bb6-0b2eeb07b71f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d1f6318-b025-41a8-a592-6e054078bdf0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V6uPHSWYbCazjiUGNPjFzM","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"pane_id\":\"w45:p2\",\"sent\":true,\"status\":\"working\"}\n# Agentic review and live check: tts/\n\nThe review finished after three rounds; the third round returned no findings. The live check against a `modal serve` dev copy behaved as designed. The review's fixes are uncommitted in `tts/app.py` and `tts/tests/test_endpoints.py`.\n\n**Changeset reviewed:** `git diff feat/cloudflare-migration...HEAD` on `feat/cloudflare-migration-tts` (commit `d9f05bd`), measured against `feat/cloudflare-migration` (fdc0c1a), with `tts/uv.lock` left out.\n\n**Reviewers:** nine in total: reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude, and one conventions reviewer each for these sources:\n- the Modal web-endpoints wiki entry\n- the local cassettes wiki entry\n- the project `CLAUDE.md`\n- your global `CLAUDE.md`\n- the mahou basics \"Code\" rule\n\nI left `.mahou/basics.md` off the conventions list because it only governs how subagents are spawned. Findings files, briefs and the patch for each round are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/agentic-review-tts/`.\n\n## Fixed\n\n**Round 1**\n- **Error responses:** one helper replaces the four inline `JSONResponse(... ErrorBody ...)` constructions in `result` (raised by both simplification and altitude).\n- **Malformed call id:** the check is now `call_id: Annotated[str, Query(pattern=r\"^fc-\")]`. FastAPI answers the 422, and the handwritten branch is gone.\n  - That 422 now carries FastAPI's validation body instead of `{error}`.\n  - I moved the comment explaining the check above the decorator, because the mahou \"Code\" rule keeps comments out of parameter lists.\n- **Double validation:** `result` returns the output dict and lets `response_model=SynthesisResult` validate it, instead of validating it a second time.\n- **Small cleanups:** the `KokoroPipeline` alias is inlined, `encode_opus` has a type hint for `audio` (numpy imported under `TYPE_CHECKING`), and blank lines now sit around `try`, `for` and `if`.\n- **Tests:** type hints on helpers, fixtures and fakes, and blank lines around the loop.\n\n**Round 2**\n- **One path for every non-200 answer:** the helper became `respond(status, body: BaseModel)`, and all five branches use it, including the 202 with `Running()`.\n- **Return types:** `result -> JSONResponse | dict`, `web -> FastAPI`, `Kokoro.synthesize -> dict[str, object]`.\n- **Tests:** every test function has type hints, and the test file is formatted with `ruff format`. I did not format `app.py`, because that would also rewrap the ffmpeg command list, which comes from the base code.\n\n## Skipped\n\n| Finding | Reason |\n|---|---|\n| Delete the `Running` model | The project `CLAUDE.md` wants response shapes as pydantic models |\n| Replace the local HTTP server for the PUT with a patched `httpx.put` | The cassettes wiki prefers real HTTP at that boundary |\n| Make `build_timeline` return `Timing` models | Its existing tests and `read-along-timing.md` use dicts, and both are outside the changeset |\n| Drop the length and last-end checks from the finished-call test | Test row B7 requires them |\n| Build the full audio with one concatenation instead of two | The code was moved from the base, not introduced; the saving is a few MB per item |\n| Upload runs inside the GPU container | The reviewer itself recommended no change |\n| Inline the `call` variable in `start` | It reads better as a variable |\n| Lazy web imports (`image.imports()` or a factory) instead of the web-deps layer in the GPU image | A structural choice; it would change the module's shape. **Open for you to rule on.** |\n| Move `SynthesisResult` to its own module so the model can cross Modal | Needs a new file, which the review's bounds forbid. **Open for you to rule on.** |\n| Deduplicate `/start`, answer 404 instead of 410, add a retryable flag to the 500 | All three contradict what `docs/technical-design/tts-service.md` settled |\n| Add `responses=` entries to the OpenAPI schema | Documentation only; not needed for the contract |\n\n## Checks after the last fix (tts/)\n\n```\nuv run ruff check   All checks passed!\nuv run ty check     All checks passed!\nuv run pytest       19 passed, 1 warning (Starlette's TestClient deprecation about httpx)\n```\n\n## Live check (dev copy at `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run`)\n\n**Setup:**\n- **Upload target:** a local Python PUT receiver behind `cloudflared tunnel --url`; nothing was created in R2.\n- **Input:** two short paragraphs, sent to the uncommitted code above.\n- **Credentials:** a script read the proxy token from `modal-proxy.env`; the token was never printed.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /start` without credentials | 401 |\n| `GET /result?call_id=garbage` | 422, FastAPI's pattern-mismatch body |\n| `GET /result?call_id=fc-01K0000000000000000000000Z` | 422 `{\"error\":\"unknown call id\"}` |\n| `POST /start` with credentials | 200 `{\"call_id\":\"fc-01M4MW01CN57X0X95XS43P5KX2\"}` in 0.8 s |\n| Polling every 5 s | 202, 202, 202, 202, then 200 after 25.5 s |\n| Final result | `{\"format\":\"audio/ogg\",\"duration\":8.575,\"timings\":[{\"start\":0.0,\"end\":4.575},{\"start\":4.575,\"end\":8.575}]}` (the shared boundary is 4.574999999999999 in the raw body); the windows are contiguous and the last end equals the duration |\n| What the receiver got | One PUT to `/audio/itm_livecheck.ogg?X-Amz-Signature=x`, content type `audio/ogg`, 23,834 bytes; ffprobe reads it as Ogg Opus, mono, 8.58 s |\n\n- **GPU image built:** the new layer that adds the web dependencies to the GPU image now builds on Modal and runs.\n- **Not listened to:** I checked the audio with ffprobe but did not play it. Listening is still part of the manual validation the project calls for.\n\n**Cleanup:**\n- **Local processes:** the dev server (uv 735278, modal 735294), the tunnel (735276) and the receiver (735274) were stopped by PID. The modal process needed SIGTERM after SIGINT.\n- **Ephemeral app:** `ap-JRmLHRGFLBoLrxNpSHhv14` was still running after the local process stopped, so I stopped it with `modal app stop -y` on that id. `modal app list` now shows it as stopped, and the deployed `nagara-tts` was not touched.\n- **Leftover files:** I deleted the received audio. Scripts and logs stay in `/tmp/nagara-spike-livecheck/`; none of them contain the token.\n- **Not updated:** I did not edit `status.md`, because the parent session maintains it.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6926a888-25a4-4580-afe8-df33ac80bdde","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:59:44.569Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"pane_id\":\"w45:p2\",\"sent\":true,\"status\":\"working\"}\n# Agentic review and live check: tts/\n\nThe review finished after three rounds; the third round returned no findings. The live check against a `modal serve` dev copy behaved as designed. The review's fixes are uncommitted in `tts/app.py` and `tts/tests/test_endpoints.py`.\n\n**Changeset reviewed:** `git diff feat/cloudflare-migration...HEAD` on `feat/cloudflare-migration-tts` (commit `d9f05bd`), measured against `feat/cloudflare-migration` (fdc0c1a), with `tts/uv.lock` left out.\n\n**Reviewers:** nine in total: reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude, and one conventions reviewer each for these sources:\n- the Modal web-endpoints wiki entry\n- the local cassettes wiki entry\n- the project `CLAUDE.md`\n- your global `CLAUDE.md`\n- the mahou basics \"Code\" rule\n\nI left `.mahou/basics.md` off the conventions list because it only governs how subagents are spawned. Findings files, briefs and the patch for each round are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/agentic-review-tts/`.\n\n## Fixed\n\n**Round 1**\n- **Error responses:** one helper replaces the four inline `JSONResponse(... ErrorBody ...)` constructions in `result` (raised by both simplification and altitude).\n- **Malformed call id:** the check is now `call_id: Annotated[str, Query(pattern=r\"^fc-\")]`. FastAPI answers the 422, and the handwritten branch is gone.\n  - That 422 now carries FastAPI's validation body instead of `{error}`.\n  - I moved the comment explaining the check above the decorator, because the mahou \"Code\" rule keeps comments out of parameter lists.\n- **Double validation:** `result` returns the output dict and lets `response_model=SynthesisResult` validate it, instead of validating it a second time.\n- **Small cleanups:** the `KokoroPipeline` alias is inlined, `encode_opus` has a type hint for `audio` (numpy imported under `TYPE_CHECKING`), and blank lines now sit around `try`, `for` and `if`.\n- **Tests:** type hints on helpers, fixtures and fakes, and blank lines around the loop.\n\n**Round 2**\n- **One path for every non-200 answer:** the helper became `respond(status, body: BaseModel)`, and all five branches use it, including the 202 with `Running()`.\n- **Return types:** `result -> JSONResponse | dict`, `web -> FastAPI`, `Kokoro.synthesize -> dict[str, object]`.\n- **Tests:** every test function has type hints, and the test file is formatted with `ruff format`. I did not format `app.py`, because that would also rewrap the ffmpeg command list, which comes from the base code.\n\n## Skipped\n\n| Finding | Reason |\n|---|---|\n| Delete the `Running` model | The project `CLAUDE.md` wants response shapes as pydantic models |\n| Replace the local HTTP server for the PUT with a patched `httpx.put` | The cassettes wiki prefers real HTTP at that boundary |\n| Make `build_timeline` return `Timing` models | Its existing tests and `read-along-timing.md` use dicts, and both are outside the changeset |\n| Drop the length and last-end checks from the finished-call test | Test row B7 requires them |\n| Build the full audio with one concatenation instead of two | The code was moved from the base, not introduced