{"parentUuid":"70859518-07d6-4eab-be4b-112fa4fc6a1a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv21UPDooVqRcHK8dQPC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":161126,"output_tokens":2134,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":772},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2134,"cache_read_input_tokens":161126,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8116,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"fb7dfcb5-068b-4ede-807a-3a4f62f070ec","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfv21U1eQjaLixzoFefah","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"20a3eed7-2bb4-422e-882a-dbf62e91b3a2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:00:17.096Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"20a3eed7-2bb4-422e-882a-dbf62e91b3a2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv21UPDooVqRcHK8dQPC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BRfaQCkAnWL2nYXVSsBYLW","name":"mcp__plannotator__plannotator_inbox","input":{"action":"send_message","thread":"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator","subject":"tts and api reviews: decisions","body":"The tts and api agentic reviews have both finished. Each left its fixes uncommitted in its worktree, and both suites pass: tts 19 tests with ruff and ty clean, api 35 tests with biome and tsc clean.\n\n**tts live check passed** against a `modal serve` dev copy, with your proxy token, which was never printed:\n- `POST /start` without credentials answers 401.\n- Malformed and unknown call ids answer 422.\n- A start with credentials answers 200 with a `call_id`.\n- Polling gives 202 until 200 after about 25 s, with contiguous timings whose last end equals the duration (8.575 s).\n- The PUT received 23 KB of Ogg Opus, which ffprobe reads as 8.58 s. Nobody listened to it, so that stays a manual row.\n- The dev app is stopped and the deployed `nagara-tts` wasn't touched.\n\nReview fixes: tts gets one `respond()` helper for every non-200 answer, and the malformed-id 422 now comes from FastAPI's `Query(pattern=...)`. api gets `ITEM_STATUS` constants instead of SQL literals, one route table, and the staleness check in one place.\n\nIf you haven't answered by the time the pipeline lands, I'll go with the recommendations so the local validation keeps moving. You can reverse any of them afterwards.\n\n:::question\nCommit the tts and api review fixes on their branches?\n\n- [ ] Yes, commit both\n- [ ] No, discard them\n\nRecommended: Yes, commit both\n:::\n\n:::question\nAPI: re-queue or retry can start a second Workflow instance for the same item. `create` passes no id, and the row only learns the instance id when the first step runs. Example: the pipeline is down for 15 minutes after a successful create, the re-queue creates another instance, and then both run.\n\n- [ ] Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \"restart that instance\"\n- [ ] Keep the program design (Cloudflare picks the id)\n\nRecommended: Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \"restart that instance\"\n:::\n\n:::question\nAPI: when `get()` or `restart()` throws after the claim is written, the route answers 500. A retry then leaves the item `queued` with `retry_count` already counted. A re-queue has already moved `queued_at`.\n\n- [ ] Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\n- [ ] Leave it: 500, and the item waits for the next re-queue\n\nRecommended: Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\n:::\n\n:::question\nAPI: the row insert and the re-queue and retry claims live in `api/src/items/`, as the program design says. A reviewer suggested `common/`, since CLAUDE.md gives `common/` \"the item row's reads and writes\". Only the API uses these three, though, and CLAUDE.md also keeps single-user code out of `common/`.\n\n- [ ] Keep them in `api/`\n- [ ] Move them to `common/src/item-store/`\n\nRecommended: Keep them in `api/`\n:::\n\n:::question\ntts: the GPU image gets an extra layer holding fastapi and httpx, because `app.py` imports them when it loads in every container. It builds and runs on Modal. The alternative is lazy imports, via `image.imports()` or a factory, which changes the module's shape.\n\n- [ ] Keep the extra layer\n- [ ] Switch to lazy imports\n\nRecommended: Keep the extra layer\n:::"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":161126,"output_tokens":2134,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":772},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2134,"cache_read_input_tokens":161126,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2338},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BRfaQCkAnWL2nYXVSsBYLW":{"action":"send_message","thread":"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator","subject":"tts and api reviews: decisions","body":"The tts and api agentic reviews have both finished. Each left its fixes uncommitted in its worktree, and both suites pass: tts 19 tests with ruff and ty clean, api 35 tests with biome and tsc clean.\n\n**tts live check passed** against a `modal serve` dev copy, with your proxy token, which was never printed:\n- `POST /start` without credentials answers 401.\n- Malformed and unknown call ids answer 422.\n- A start with credentials answers 200 with a `call_id`.\n- Polling gives 202 until 200 after about 25 s, with contiguous timings whose last end equals the duration (8.575 s).\n- The PUT received 23 KB of Ogg Opus, which ffprobe reads as 8.58 s. Nobody listened to it, so that stays a manual row.\n- The dev app is stopped and the deployed `nagara-tts` wasn't touched.\n\nReview fixes: tts gets one `respond()` helper for every non-200 answer, and the malformed-id 422 now comes from FastAPI's `Query(pattern=...)`. api gets `ITEM_STATUS` constants instead of SQL literals, one route table, and the staleness check in one place.\n\nIf you haven't answered by the time the pipeline lands, I'll go with the recommendations so the local validation keeps moving. You can reverse any of them afterwards.\n\n:::question\nCommit the tts and api review fixes on their branches?\n\n- [ ] Yes, commit both\n- [ ] No, discard them\n\nRecommended: Yes, commit both\n:::\n\n:::question\nAPI: re-queue or retry can start a second Workflow instance for the same item. `create` passes no id, and the row only learns the instance id when the first step runs. Example: the pipeline is down for 15 minutes after a successful create, the re-queue creates another instance, and then both run.\n\n- [ ] Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \"restart that instance\"\n- [ ] Keep the program design (Cloudflare picks the id)\n\nRecommended: Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \"restart that instance\"\n:::\n\n:::question\nAPI: when `get()` or `restart()` throws after the claim is written, the route answers 500. A retry then leaves the item `queued` with `retry_count` already counted. A re-queue has already moved `queued_at`.\n\n- [ ] Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\n- [ ] Leave it: 500, and the item waits for the next re-queue\n\nRecommended: Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\n:::\n\n:::question\nAPI: the row insert and the re-queue and retry claims live in `api/src/items/`, as the program design says. A reviewer suggested `common/`, since CLAUDE.md gives `common/` \"the item row's reads and writes\". Only the API uses these three, though, and CLAUDE.md also keeps single-user code out of `common/`.\n\n- [ ] Keep them in `api/`\n- [ ] Move them to `common/src/item-store/`\n\nRecommended: Keep them in `api/`\n:::\n\n:::question\ntts: the GPU image gets an extra layer holding fastapi and httpx, because `app.py` imports them when it loads in every container. It builds and runs on Modal. The alternative is lazy imports, via `image.imports()` or a factory, which changes the module's shape.\n\n- [ ] Keep the extra layer\n- [ ] Switch to lazy imports\n\nRecommended: Keep the extra layer\n:::"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fb7dfcb5-068b-4ede-807a-3a4f62f070ec","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfv21U1eQjaLixzoFefah","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9ad4ab71-0229-48a0-b756-38d05c8be4bd","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:00:27.837Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
