apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfv339CjaX6efDpPNj9BT","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb2d4269-c517-4442-bd75-e8adf8fab1ea","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:13:40.819Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"cb2d4269-c517-4442-bd75-e8adf8fab1ea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7ec104d4-e781-47bd-9413-8cacd37a4b7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016PXvH68Z9Pse4y45ymzUDW","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"pane_id\":\"w46:p2\",\"status\":\"done\"}\n\n[exited with code 0]\ndone\n# Report: pipeline/ (ASE-75 to ASE-79)\n\nAll five tasks are done and committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline` (not pushed). Every C1–C28 row has a passing test, and pipeline test, lint, types and `vite build` pass on the final tree.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Hash | Subject | Tasks |\n|---|---|---|\n| `16764e2` | feat(pipeline): run each item through the item Workflow up to its recipe | ASE-75, ASE-76 |\n| `5c59179` | feat(pipeline): acquire the recipe's declared images in the images step | ASE-77 |\n| `cd934c3` | feat(pipeline): describe code blocks and unlabelled images in the describe step | ASE-78 |\n| `6d1f492` | feat(pipeline): synthesize and store each item, and test whole item runs | ASE-79 |\n\nI wrote the code in one pass and then split it into these commits. Each commit typechecks on its own; I checked this on an extracted copy of each commit. The first commit's suite also passes on its own (100 tests). The whole-run tests land in the last commit, which is where the ASE-79 task text puts them.\n\n## What changed, per commit\n\n- **`16764e2` (ASE-75, ASE-76):**\n  - **Package and config:** `@nagara/common` (`workspace:*`), `markdown-it@15.0.2` and `msw@2.15.0` (dev) are added. `wrangler.jsonc` renames the workflow to `item`/`ItemWorkflow` and adds D1 (placeholder id `00000000-…`), R2, `IMAGES`, the new vars and `workers_dev: false`. JobIndex is removed through a `deleted_classes` migration (tag `v2`).\n  - **Removed:** the old extraction-service code (`http/`, `job-index.ts`, `extraction.ts`, `world.ts`) and its tests.\n  - **DomainQueue:** now a lease stored in the synchronous `ctx.storage.kv`, with `acquire`, `release`, `advance` (checks status, sends `lease-granted`, skips an ended waiter) and `alarm`.\n  - **Step wrapper:** writes the status at the start of every attempt; after the last attempt fails, a `<name> failed` step writes `failed` with the step's own error.\n  - **Steps:** fetch (plain-fetch Firecrawl client with the Python SDK's fields), lease (3 waits for `lease-granted`, a recheck after each), recipe (settle → spoken form → drop rule), release.\n  - **Fake agent:** `agents/conversation.ts` reads the `scriptedAgentReplies` setting. When it is unset, the code goes to Flue. The vitest config sets a \"gave up\" default.\n  - **Cassettes:** I `git mv`'d `api/tests/cassettes/test_describe/` to `pipeline/test/cassettes/describe/`, as the api subagent asked. Nothing else under `api/` was touched.\n- **`5c59179` (ASE-77):** semaphores of 2 per host and 10 overall, 10 s timeout, 10 MB streamed cap. SVG scripts and `on*` attributes are stripped with HTMLRewriter. Rasters go through `env.IMAGES` (kept at a shorter side of 200 px or more, re-encoded to WebP) and are stored under `images/<sha256>`.\n  - **Images binding check:** the binding works under the vitest plugin (`info` reports the dimensions, `output` gives WebP), so no stand-in binding was needed.\n- **`cd934c3` (ASE-78):** Gemini through the AI Gateway with structured output, then the sanitize tail. The prompts are generated from the Python strings, and the recorded cassette matches them byte for byte. Each job runs as a child step, they are awaited together with `Promise.allSettled`, and one D1 batch writes the units, degradations and ledger rows.\n- **`6d1f492` (ASE-79):** start synthesis presigns against `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` and hands Modal the URL with `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` in its place. Wait for synthesis polls inside one step: 410 and 422 fail the item at once, 500 fails the attempt. Store joins the timings, fails on a length mismatch, and writes `ready` in one batch.\n  - **Tests:** the whole-run tests, plus 63 spoken-form cases ported from `api/tests/test_extract.py`.\n\n## Row-to-test mapping\n\n| Rows | File | Test |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | `item-workflow.test.ts` | carries an article with code, rasters, an SVG and a repeated image to ready |\n| C2 | `item-workflow.test.ts` | retries a Firecrawl 503 inside the fetch step without ever showing failed |\n| C3 | `item-workflow.test.ts` | fails a page over the HTML cap at once, in fetch |\n| C4 | `item-workflow.test.ts` | fails with fetch's own error once Firecrawl answers 503 on every attempt |\n| C5 | `item-lease.test.ts` | holds a second item of the same domain queued until the first releases after its recipe |\n| C6 | `item-lease.test.ts` | fails in lease after three waits behind a holder that never releases |\n| C20 | `item-lease.test.ts` | restarts a recipe failure from lease, granted again while still the holder, with the current recipe |\n| C7 | `item-recipe.test.ts` | authors the first recipe of a new domain and saves it as version 1 |\n| C8 | `item-recipe.test.ts` | revises a recipe that fails the article and extracts with the new version |\n| C9 | `item-recipe.test.ts` | fails a not-article verdict in one attempt, saves nothing, and the alarm frees the lease |\n| C10 | `item-recipe.test.ts` | fails when the revision gives up and leaves the old version current |\n| C11 | `item-enrichment.test.ts` | drops a small avatar silently and a 404 with a degradation… |\n| C12 | `item-enrichment.test.ts` | fails in images when the page's only unit is an image that 404s |\n| C13 | `item-enrichment.test.ts` | floors a code block whose describe fails and records a cached describe as cached |\n| C14 | `item-enrichment.test.ts` | describes the first 25 of 30 code blocks in document order and floors the rest |\n| C15 | `item-synthesis.test.ts` | fails in start synthesis when Modal answers 503 on every attempt |\n| C16 | `item-synthesis.test.ts` | fails in wait for synthesis when the result answers 500 on every attempt |\n| C17 | `item-synthesis.test.ts` | fails at once in wait for synthesis when the result has expired |\n| C18 | `item-synthesis.test.ts` | fails at once in store when the synthesis returns one window fewer than the units |\n| C19 | `item-synthesis.test.ts` | restarts a failed wait for synthesis without fetching, describing or synthesizing again |\n| C21 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | grants a free lease and arms the alarm |\n| C22 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | refuses a held lease and appends the id to the queue |\n| C23 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | grants the lease again to the instance that holds it |\n| C24 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | keeps a waiter's place when it asks again |\n| C25 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | hands the released lease to the next live waiter, skipping one that ended |\n| C26 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | drops a waiter that releases from the queue and leaves the lease alone |\n| C27 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | sweeps the lease of an ended holder on the alarm and grants the next waiter |\n| C28 | `domain-queue.test.ts` | re-arms the alarm over a holder that is still running |\n\nPer the warning about cassette misses: the tests check outcomes (the described spoken forms, the stored keys, ledger rows, request counts), not only that the item reached `ready`. C1 and C2 check the full status sequence through a D1 trigger created inside the test (not a schema change).\n\n## Check output (pipeline/)\n\n```\npnpm test   Test Files 13 passed (13) · Tests 120 passed | 1 skipped (121)   (stable across 3 runs)\npnpm lint   Checked 76 files in 29ms. No fixes applied.\npnpm types  exit 0\npnpm build  ✓ built; dist wrangler.json has workflow item, IMAGES, DOMAIN_QUEUE + both Flue agents, migration v2\n```\n\nThe skipped test is the existing CPU-limit case, which is run by hand. The pool's stderr also shows miniflare engine messages (\"code had hung\", \"Aborting engine…\"); no test fails because of them.\n\n## Design drift\n\n1. **Step retries:** I set `retries.limit: 2`, which gives 3 attempts. The notes say \"3 attempts\" and C4 confirms 3 Firecrawl calls. The program design's \"limit 3\" would mean 4 attempts.\n2. **Authoring or revision giving up fails the item at once** (NonRetryableError), the same way as not-article. Retrying the step would repeat the agents' own retries and break the bound in `recipes.md` (\"one retry of the whole run, then the item fails\").\n3. **Degradation reasons:** the union only allows `404`, `timeout` and `undecodable`. So any non-2xx status maps to `404`, a network failure or abort to `timeout`, and an oversize, undecodable or binding-failed image to `undecodable`. A 403 or 500 is recorded as `404`. This is a `common/` type question if you want finer reasons.\n4. **`agents/` gained `conversation.ts`** (the configuration factory for the fake agent), although the program design lists `agents/` as unchanged.\n5. **`firecrawl.scrape` returns `html: null`** instead of throwing, so the fetch step can write the ledger row before it throws. The notes require that a failed item still records its credit.\n6. **No `origin` field** in the Firecrawl body. I left out the Python SDK's `origin: \"python-sdk@…\"` because it would mislabel the TS client. So the recorded httpbin Firecrawl cassette does not match, and the tests use fabricated Firecrawl cassettes.\n7. **Relative image `src`** is resolved against the item's URL. The Python code did not do this; it is harmless for absolute URLs.\n8. **SVG stripping** also removes `on*` event-handler attributes, not only `<script>`.\n9. **`wait for synthesis`** sleeps with `setTimeout` inside the step, as the program design describes; it does not use `step.sleep`. The tests set `pollIntervalSeconds: 0` in the vitest config.\n10. **Price vars are new names:** `firecrawlDollarsPerCredit`, `describerDollarsPerCall`, `ttsDollarsPerSecond`, with the old Python values. `MODAL_START_URL` and `MODAL_RESULT_URL` point at `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web.modal.run/{start,result}`, which the tts report derived but has not deployed.\n\n## Decisions taken without the user\n\nNone. No Inbox question was needed.\n\n## Linear\n\nASE-75, ASE-76, ASE-77, ASE-78 and ASE-79 moved to Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n## Not resolved\n\n- **Local development pieces (program design §7) are not built:** `pipeline/.dev.vars.example`, `scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs`, `dev:proxy`, and `persistState` in `vite.config.ts`. They were outside ASE-75 to ASE-79; they need a task if no other part covers them.\n- **Only the code-describe Gemini cassettes moved.** The image describe cannot replay a recording, because the stored WebP bytes come from the Images binding at run time, so image describes are answered by a handler built from the contract. The other `api/tests/cassettes` folders are untouched.\n- **Manual \"by hand\" parts** of C1, C5, C7, C9 and C11 were not run, as the brief asks.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3d4a78d3-d9dc-4205-afec-c9be27cc6e08","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:13:41.576Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"pane_id\":\"w46:p2\",\"status\":\"done\"}\n\n[exited with code 0]\ndone\n# Report: pipeline/ (ASE-75 to ASE-79)\n\nAll five tasks are done and committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline` (not pushed). Every C1–C28 row has a passing test, and pipeline test, lint, types and `vite build` pass on the final tree.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Hash | Subject | Tasks |\n|---|---|---|\n| `16764e2` | feat(pipeline): run each item through the item Workflow up to its recipe | ASE-75, ASE-76 |\n| `5c59179` | feat(pipeline): acquire the recipe's declared images in the images step | ASE-77 |\n| `cd934c3` | feat(pipeline): describe code blocks and unlabelled images in the describe step | ASE-78 |\n| `6d1f492` | feat(pipeline): synthesize and store each item, and test whole item runs | ASE-79 |\n\nI wrote the code in one pass and then split it into these commits. Each commit typechecks on its own; I checked this on an extracted copy of each commit. The first commit's suite also passes on its own 