{"parentUuid":"0aa5500c-1d05-4ebb-b4f3-c97f51cb0bb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv348yrZpJwVLj8KQCAQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01858XGipfSJDmCxP2qg9DTe","name":"mcp__plannotator__plannotator_inbox","input":{"action":"send_message","thread":"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator","subject":"pipeline done (ASE-75 to 79)","body":"The pipeline is done: four commits on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline` (`16764e2`, `5c59179`, `cd934c3`, `6d1f492`). Every row from C1 to C28 has a test, the suite has 120 tests and passes three runs in a row, and lint, types and build are clean. The Images binding works under vitest, so it needs no stand-in. Its agentic review is running now.\n\nDrift it reported, which the docs will be reconciled against:\n- **Step retries:** `retries.limit: 2`, which means 3 attempts. That matches the notes, while the program design's \"limit 3\" would have meant 4.\n- **Agent gives up:** when authoring or revision gives up, the item fails at once with no retry of the step, so the agents' own retry bound from `recipes.md` holds.\n- **Firecrawl failure:** a missing page body comes back as `html: null` instead of a throw, so the credit ledger row is written before the step fails.\n- **Image paths:** relative image `src` values are resolved against the item URL. The Python code didn't do that.\n- **SVG cleanup:** stripping also removes `on*` attributes from SVGs.\n- **Fake agent:** a `conversation.ts` factory in `agents/` makes the agent fake in tests.\n- **Modal URLs:** the vars point at the URLs the not-yet-deployed `nagara-tts` will have. Locally they're overridden with the dev copy.\n\n:::question\nImage degradation reasons. The union in `common/` only allows `404 | timeout | undecodable`, so a 403 or 500 is recorded as `404`. Should the union be widened?\n\n- [ ] Keep the three reasons as they are\n- [ ] Add a reason for the other HTTP statuses (e.g. `http_error`) in `common/`\n\nRecommended: Keep the three reasons as they are\n:::\n\nNext, once the review finishes: merge the four branches, build the local-dev pieces (ASE-81: shared state folder, tunnel proxy, `.dev.vars`), then run the manual rows locally against the Modal dev copy with small articles."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1108,"cache_read_input_tokens":175190,"output_tokens":980,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":128},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1108,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":175190,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1108},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01858XGipfSJDmCxP2qg9DTe":{"action":"send_message","thread":"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator","subject":"pipeline done (ASE-75 to 79)","body":"The pipeline is done: four commits on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline` (`16764e2`, `5c59179`, `cd934c3`, `6d1f492`). Every row from C1 to C28 has a test, the suite has 120 tests and passes three runs in a row, and lint, types and build are clean. The Images binding works under vitest, so it needs no stand-in. Its agentic review is running now.\n\nDrift it reported, which the docs will be reconciled against:\n- **Step retries:** `retries.limit: 2`, which means 3 attempts. That matches the notes, while the program design's \"limit 3\" would have meant 4.\n- **Agent gives up:** when authoring or revision gives up, the item fails at once with no retry of the step, so the agents' own retry bound from `recipes.md` holds.\n- **Firecrawl failure:** a missing page body comes back as `html: null` instead of a throw, so the credit ledger row is written before the step fails.\n- **Image paths:** relative image `src` values are resolved against the item URL. The Python code didn't do that.\n- **SVG cleanup:** stripping also removes `on*` attributes from SVGs.\n- **Fake agent:** a `conversation.ts` factory in `agents/` makes the agent fake in tests.\n- **Modal URLs:** the vars point at the URLs the not-yet-deployed `nagara-tts` will have. Locally they're overridden with the dev copy.\n\n:::question\nImage degradation reasons. The union in `common/` only allows `404 | timeout | undecodable`, so a 403 or 500 is recorded as `404`. Should the union be widened?\n\n- [ ] Keep the three reasons as they are\n- [ ] Add a reason for the other HTTP statuses (e.g. `http_error`) in `common/`\n\nRecommended: Keep the three reasons as they are\n:::\n\nNext, once the review finishes: merge the four branches, build the local-dev pieces (ASE-81: shared state folder, tunnel proxy, `.dev.vars`), then run the manual rows locally against the Modal dev copy with small articles."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"66e8e446-c436-4fdb-8015-e9410f222472","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfv348dmycEuqJA7dvs9z","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"486182cd-02ae-47af-9687-2b78e9454ed1","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:14:01.091Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
