{"parentUuid":"22dc6819-b991-409b-a73f-1958b3539fd2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a8063492-bf9d-4b99-bb12-dd4a7ca042f8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EenXCzrZ8cZ6yw4Ea5j6H6","type":"tool_result","content":"Thread msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX (common subagent blocked on an rm -rf prompt): 12 messages, 3 from the person.\n\n{\n  \"thread\": {\n    \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n    \"project\": {\n      \"id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n      \"key\": \"nagara-ebc7e6\",\n      \"name\": \"nagara\",\n      \"root\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:26:41.628Z\"\n    },\n    \"subject\": \"common subagent blocked on an rm -rf prompt\",\n    \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"messages\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": \"common subagent blocked on an rm -rf prompt\",\n        \"body\": \"The common/ subagent (herdr tab \\\"impl: workspace + common (ASE-73)\\\", pane w30:p24) is blocked on a permission dialog. Your `Bash(rm -rf:*)` ask rule overrides auto mode. It wants to run `rm -rf $T`, where `$T` is a `mktemp -d` folder it just made to test-apply the D1 migrations.\\n\\nFrom now on I'll tell every subagent to avoid `rm -rf` (use `rm -r` on a named path, or leave temp folders in /tmp), so this shouldn't recur.\\n\\n:::question\\nHow should I answer the dialog?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes, let it delete the temp folder\\n- [ ] No, decline it (the child goes on and leaves the temp folder in /tmp)\\n\\nRecommended: Yes, let it delete the temp folder\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:41:14.758Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\",\n        \"person_seen_seq\": 200,\n        \"agent_checked_seq\": 202,\n        \"agent_checked_at\": \"2026-10-11T14:11:21.344Z\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-4ab29a30\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"How should I answer the dialog?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes, let it delete the temp folder\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, decline it (the child goes on and leaves the temp folder in /tmp)\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes, let it delete the temp folder\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"sent\",\n            \"answer\": {\n              \"v\": 1,\n              \"key\": \"q-4ab29a30\",\n              \"kind\": \"single\",\n              \"prompt\": \"How should I answer the dialog?\",\n              \"selected\": [\n                \"Yes, let it delete the temp folder\"\n              ],\n              \"sourceLine\": 6\n            },\n            \"revision\": 33,\n            \"sent_revision\": 33,\n            \"picked_by\": {\n              \"id\": \"person\",\n              \"name\": null\n            },\n            \"picked_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:42:40.712Z\",\n            \"sent_reply_id\": \"msg_01M4MV66KPFA6E6HWGD38A284V\",\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MV66KPFA6E6HWGD38A284V\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"person\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"Answered 1 question.\\n\\n## Answers to your questions\\n\\n1 of 1 question answered.\\n\\n### Q1. How should I answer the dialog? (line 6)\\nAnswer: Yes, let it delete the temp folder (your recommendation)\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:42:46.006Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"delivery\": {\n          \"state\": \"delivered\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-10-11T06:42:46.601Z\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MV6R3S5S87F8J4Z37M33TT\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MV66KPFA6E6HWGD38A284V\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"Done. I answered \\\"Yes\\\" in the dialog and the common/ subagent is working again. It now has the never-`rm -rf` rule too.\\n\\nStatus:\\n- tts (ASE-74) is committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration-tts` and is in the agentic review now.\\n- Its live check against Modal hasn't run, because `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env` still doesn't exist. Whenever you write it, with `MODAL_PROXY_KEY=` and `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET=` lines, the live checks and the local end-to-end runs can use it.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:43:03.929Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": null,\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVJT827QKR6XG6F2S76EDD\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The agentic review of `common/` (ASE-73) finished after three rounds with no findings left. It left four small fixes uncommitted in the main checkout, and none of them changes a `common/` export:\\n\\n- `units.ts`: the paragraph, code and image units build on a shared non-exported `TextUnit` base instead of repeating `display` and `spoken`.\\n- `testing/cassettes.ts`: one shared key comparator, an inlined variable, and a blank line restored.\\n- `presign.ts`: an intermediate variable is inlined.\\n\\nSkipped, with reasons:\\n- **Root configs:** one root biome, tsconfig base and pnpm catalog. They need pipeline/ edits, so they wait until the branches merge.\\n- **Module split:** splitting `row.ts` and `cassettes.ts` into a module per function. The program design names those modules.\\n- **`encodeJson`:** removing it. The Workers will use it.\\n- **`AwsClient`:** reusing one client. It would change `presign`'s signature for a negligible gain.\\n- **vite types:** using `vite/client` types. `common/` doesn't depend on vite.\\n\\nChecks: 17 tests pass, and biome and tsc are clean.\\n\\nIf you haven't answered by the time the manual validation is due, the fixes stay uncommitted in the working tree, and I'll run the validation on the committed code.\\n\\n:::question\\nCommit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\\n- [ ] No, discard them\\n\\nRecommended: Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:49:39.330Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-76254eae\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Commit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, discard them\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"sent\",\n            \"answer\": {\n              \"v\": 1,\n              \"key\": \"q-76254eae\",\n              \"kind\": \"single\",\n              \"prompt\": \"Commit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\",\n              \"selected\": [\n                \"Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\"\n              ],\n              \"note\": \"do the module split; also let's use a better name rather than \\\"row\\\" something more representative to what it refers too\",\n              \"sourceLine\": 19\n            },\n            \"revision\": 120,\n            \"sent_revision\": 120,\n            \"picked_by\": {\n              \"id\": \"person\",\n              \"name\": null\n            },\n            \"picked_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:09.317Z\",\n            \"sent_reply_id\": \"msg_01M4MVQEDXMY84B6N8CPM1493E\",\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MVJT827QKR6XG6F2S76EDD\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVQEDXMY84B6N8CPM1493E\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MVJT827QKR6XG6F2S76EDD\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"person\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"Answered 1 question.\\n\\n## Answers to your questions\\n\\n1 of 1 question answered.\\n\\n### Q1. Commit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`? (line 19)\\nAnswer: Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …` (your recommendation)\\nNote: do the module split; also let's use a better name rather than \\\"row\\\" something more representative to what it refers too\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:11.069Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"delivery\": {\n          \"state\": \"delivered\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:12.153Z\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVRDFEHQ9EJ5CZMVVPF1HZ\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MVQEDXMY84B6N8CPM1493E\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"On it. The common/ subagent commits the four fixes, then splits `row.ts` and `testing/cassettes.ts` into one module per function. The item row's reads and writes go under `common/src/item-store/`: `read-item.ts`, `write-status.ts`, and `json-column.ts` holding the encode/decode pair. The package keeps exporting the same names, so the pipeline and api work in progress isn't affected. I'll tell you if the names it lands on differ.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:42.862Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVWFTS43E3VV31YFVE50HF\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"**common/**\\n- Fixes committed as `349fe2d`.\\n- Split committed as `2cbc866`. `common/src/item-store/` now holds `json-column.ts`, `read-item.ts` and `write-status.ts`. The cassette replay code is in eight small modules under `common/testing/`. The exports haven't changed.\\n- The same subagent is now on ASE-82, the CI workflow.\\n\\n**api/ (ASE-80)**\\n- Done as `79ed096` on `feat/cloudflare-migration-api`: the Python tree is replaced by the `nagara-api` Worker. All 35 tests pass (D1–D27), and lint and types are clean. Its agentic review is running.\\n- Choices the notes left open, which the subagent made itself. Reply if you want any changed:\\n  - When the Workflow can't be created, enqueue still answers 202, with the item `failed`.\\n  - Error bodies keep the FastAPI shape `{\\\"detail\\\": …}`.\\n  - `duration` and `audio_url` are `null` until the item is ready.\\n  - A `create` or `restart` that fails during a retry or re-queue answers 500 and leaves the item `queued`, so the 15-minute re-queue picks it up.\\n  - `/health` answers plain `ok`, as the program design says. The old API answered JSON.\\n- Drift to reconcile in the docs later:\\n  - The API has no R2 binding, because it only signs URLs. `persistence-and-storage`, `deployment-and-ci` and `local-development` say both Workers bind the bucket. The local-dev task settles how the API's presigned GETs reach the local bucket.\\n  - The R2 bucket name `nagara` is a placeholder. Nothing in the notes settles it.\\n\\n**pipeline/ (ASE-75 to 79)** is still running. The tts review and its live check are running too.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:54:56.345Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The tts and api agentic reviews have both finished. Each left its fixes uncommitted in its worktree, and both suites pass: tts 19 tests with ruff and ty clean, api 35 tests with biome and tsc clean.\\n\\n**tts live check passed** against a `modal serve` dev copy, with your proxy token, which was never printed:\\n- `POST /start` without credentials answers 401.\\n- Malformed and unknown call ids answer 422.\\n- A start with credentials answers 200 with a `call_id`.\\n- Polling gives 202 until 200 after about 25 s, with contiguous timings whose last end equals the duration (8.575 s).\\n- The PUT received 23 KB of Ogg Opus, which ffprobe reads as 8.58 s. Nobody listened to it, so that stays a manual row.\\n- The dev app is stopped and the deployed `nagara-tts` wasn't touched.\\n\\nReview fixes: tts gets one `respond()` helper for every non-200 answer, and the malformed-id 422 now comes from FastAPI's `Query(pattern=...)`. api gets `ITEM_STATUS` constants instead of SQL literals, one route table, and the staleness check in one place.\\n\\nIf you haven't answered by the time the pipeline lands, I'll go with the recommendations so the local validation keeps moving. You can reverse any of them afterwards.\\n\\n:::question\\nCommit the tts and api review fixes on their branches?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes, commit both\\n- [ ] No, discard them\\n\\nRecommended: Yes, commit both\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\nAPI: re-queue or retry can start a second Workflow instance for the same item. `create` passes no id, and the row only learns the instance id when the first step runs. Example: the pipeline is down for 15 minutes after a successful create, the re-queue creates another instance, and then both run.\\n\\n- [ ] Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\\n- [ ] Keep the program design (Cloudflare picks the id)\\n\\nRecommended: Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\nAPI: when `get()` or `restart()` throws after the claim is written, the route answers 500. A retry then leaves the item `queued` with `retry_count` already counted. A re-queue has already moved `queued_at`.\\n\\n- [ ] Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\\n- [ ] Leave it: 500, and the item waits for the next re-queue\\n\\nRecommended: Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\nAPI: the row insert and the re-queue and retry claims live in `api/src/items/`, as the program design says. A reviewer suggested `common/`, since CLAUDE.md gives `common/` \\\"the item row's reads and writes\\\". Only the API uses these three, though, and CLAUDE.md also keeps single-user code out of `common/`.\\n\\n- [ ] Keep them in `api/`\\n- [ ] Move them to `common/src/item-store/`\\n\\nRecommended: Keep them in `api/`\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\ntts: the GPU image gets an extra layer holding fastapi and httpx, because `app.py` imports them when it loads in every container. It builds and runs on Modal. The alternative is lazy imports, via `image.imports()` or a factory, which changes the module's shape.\\n\\n- [ ] Keep the extra layer\\n- [ ] Switch to lazy imports\\n\\nRecommended: Keep the extra layer\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:00:27.883Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-4fa64649\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Commit the tts and api review fixes on their branches?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes, commit both\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, discard them\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes, commit both\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-1b99e738\",\n            \"position\": 1,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"API: re-queue or retry can start a second Workflow instance for the same item. `create` passes no id, and the row only learns the instance id when the first step runs. Example: the pipeline is down for 15 minutes after a successful create, the re-queue creates another instance, and then both run.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep the program design (Cloudflare picks the id)\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-55f1499d\",\n            \"position\": 2,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"API: when `get()` or `restart()` throws after the claim is written, the route answers 500. A retry then leaves the item `queued` with `retry_count` already counted. A re-queue has already moved `queued_at`.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Leave it: 500, and the item waits for the next re-queue\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-933f7b37\",\n            \"position\": 3,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"API: the row insert and the re-queue and retry claims live in `api/src/items/`, as the program design says. A reviewer suggested `common/`, since CLAUDE.md gives `common/` \\\"the item row's reads and writes\\\". Only the API uses these three, though, and CLAUDE.md also keeps single-user code out of `common/`.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep them in `api/`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Move them to `common/src/item-store/`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Keep them in `api/`\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-cb065b8f\",\n            \"position\": 4,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"tts: the GPU image gets an extra layer holding fastapi and httpx, because `app.py` imports them when it loads in every container. It builds and runs on Modal. The alternative is lazy imports, via `image.imports()` or a factory, which changes the module's shape.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep the extra layer\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Switch to lazy imports\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Keep the extra layer\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MW6WHPTJ8Y3X18M3ZP1MCB\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The CI review is done too. It left two fixes uncommitted in `cloudflare.yml`, and actionlint still passes:\\n- `wrangler-action` goes up to v4, which the wiki's `cf-cli` entry names.\\n- Each job installs only its own tree, with `pnpm install --filter \\\"{./<dir>}...\\\"`.\\n\\nSkipped:\\n- **Composite setup action:** it would need a new file under `.github/actions/`.\\n- **Merged check jobs:** they would change which deploys a failed check stops.\\n\\n:::question\\nCommit the CI review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes\\n- [ ] No, discard them\\n\\nRecommended: Yes\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:00:37.046Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-18a1c3da\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Commit the CI review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, discard them\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6WHPTJ8Y3X18M3ZP1MCB\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MWZDS43358DQP7H30GMHMZ\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The pipeline is done: four commits on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline` (`16764e2`, `5c59179`, `cd934c3`, `6d1f492`). Every row from C1 to C28 has a test, the suite has 120 tests and passes three runs in a row, and lint, types and build are clean. The Images binding works under vitest, so it needs no stand-in. Its agentic review is running now.\\n\\nDrift it reported, which the docs will be reconciled against:\\n- **Step retries:** `retries.limit: 2`, which means 3 attempts. That matches the notes, while the program design's \\\"limit 3\\\" would have meant 4.\\n- **Agent gives up:** when authoring or revision gives up, the item fails at once with no retry of the step, so the agents' own retry bound from `recipes.md` holds.\\n- **Firecrawl failure:** a missing page body comes back as `html: null` instead of a throw, so the credit ledger row is written before the step fails.\\n- **Image paths:** relative image `src` values are resolved against the item URL. The Python code didn't do that.\\n- **SVG cleanup:** stripping also removes `on*` attributes from SVGs.\\n- **Fake agent:** a `conversation.ts` factory in `agents/` makes the agent fake in tests.\\n- **Modal URLs:** the vars point at the URLs the not-yet-deployed `nagara-tts` will have. Locally they're overridden with the dev copy.\\n\\n:::question\\nImage degradation reasons. The union in `common/` only allows `404 | timeout | undecodable`, so a 403 or 500 is recorded as `404`. Should the union be widened?\\n\\n- [ ] Keep the three reasons as they are\\n- [ ] Add a reason for the other HTTP statuses (e.g. `http_error`) in `common/`\\n\\nRecommended: Keep the three reasons as they are\\n:::\\n\\nNext, once the review finishes: merge the four branches, build the local-dev pieces (ASE-81: shared state folder, tunnel proxy, `.dev.vars`), then run the manual rows locally against the Modal dev copy with small articles.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:14:01.124Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-734de979\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Image degradation reasons. The union in `common/` only allows `404 | timeout | undecodable`, so a 403 or 500 is recorded as `404`. Should the union be widened?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep the three reasons as they are\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Add a reason for the other HTTP statuses (e.g. `http_error`) in `common/`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Keep the three reasons as they are\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MWZDS43358DQP7H30GMHMZ\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MXAH44KKYMKNWEWW3K7ATX\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The machine is low on memory: 14 of 15 GiB used and 5 GiB in swap. The pipeline review's reviewer tabs are the main load. Claude Code stopped my background wait on the pipeline review to free memory, and it tells me not to restart that wait unless you ask. The review itself keeps running in its herdr tab.\\n\\nTo free memory, I closed the idle common/ subagent. Its work is committed. The tts and api subagents stay open, because their worktrees hold the uncommitted review fixes waiting on your answer.\\n\\nUntil you reply, I'm not woken when the review finishes. When you're back, a \\\"go on\\\" (here or in the chat) gets me to collect the review and continue with the merge, local dev and the manual rows. If you'd rather I keep going unattended, start Claude Code with `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BG_SHELL_PRESSURE_REAP=1`.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:20:04.996Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4NMVJ02AW6BSC2GDRY0RWKX\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MXAH44KKYMKNWEWW3K7ATX\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"person\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"continue with the work, clean up anything that's no longer necessary and serialize checks if necessary\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T14:11:20.194Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"delivery\": {\n          \"state\": \"delivered\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-10-11T14:11:21.344Z\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"url\": \"http://localhost:39937/#REDACTED\"\n}"}]},"uuid":"452ce83b-3cc3-4b1d-b039-2cacde337c42","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:11:24.927Z","toolUseResult":"Thread msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX (common subagent blocked on an rm -rf prompt): 12 messages, 3 from the person.\n\n{\n  \"thread\": {\n    \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n    \"project\": {\n      \"id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n      \"key\": \"nagara-ebc7e6\",\n      \"name\": \"nagara\",\n      \"root\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:26:41.628Z\"\n    },\n    \"subject\": \"common subagent blocked on an rm -rf prompt\",\n    \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"messages\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": \"common subagent blocked on an rm -rf prompt\",\n        \"body\": \"The common/ subagent (herdr tab \\\"impl: workspace + common (ASE-73)\\\", pane w30:p24) is blocked on a permission dialog. Your `Bash(rm -rf:*)` ask rule overrides auto mode. It wants to run `rm -rf $T`, where `$T` is a `mktemp -d` folder it just made to test-apply the D1 migrations.\\n\\nFrom now on I'll tell every subagent to avoid `rm -rf` (use `rm -r` on a named path, or leave temp folders in /tmp), so this shouldn't recur.\\n\\n:::question\\nHow should I answer the dialog?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes, let it delete the temp folder\\n- [ ] No, decline it (the child goes on and leaves the temp folder in /tmp)\\n\\nRecommended: Yes, let it delete the temp folder\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:41:14.758Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\",\n        \"person_seen_seq\": 200,\n        \"agent_checked_seq\": 202,\n        \"agent_checked_at\": \"2026-10-11T14:11:21.344Z\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-4ab29a30\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"How should I answer the dialog?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes, let it delete the temp folder\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, decline it (the child goes on and leaves the temp folder in /tmp)\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes, let it delete the temp folder\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"sent\",\n            \"answer\": {\n              \"v\": 1,\n              \"key\": \"q-4ab29a30\",\n              \"kind\": \"single\",\n              \"prompt\": \"How should I answer the dialog?\",\n              \"selected\": [\n                \"Yes, let it delete the temp folder\"\n              ],\n              \"sourceLine\": 6\n            },\n            \"revision\": 33,\n            \"sent_revision\": 33,\n            \"picked_by\": {\n              \"id\": \"person\",\n              \"name\": null\n            },\n            \"picked_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:42:40.712Z\",\n            \"sent_reply_id\": \"msg_01M4MV66KPFA6E6HWGD38A284V\",\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MV66KPFA6E6HWGD38A284V\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"person\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"Answered 1 question.\\n\\n## Answers to your questions\\n\\n1 of 1 question answered.\\n\\n### Q1. How should I answer the dialog? (line 6)\\nAnswer: Yes, let it delete the temp folder (your recommendation)\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:42:46.006Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"delivery\": {\n          \"state\": \"delivered\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-10-11T06:42:46.601Z\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MV6R3S5S87F8J4Z37M33TT\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MV66KPFA6E6HWGD38A284V\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"Done. I answered \\\"Yes\\\" in the dialog and the common/ subagent is working again. It now has the never-`rm -rf` rule too.\\n\\nStatus:\\n- tts (ASE-74) is committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration-tts` and is in the agentic review now.\\n- Its live check against Modal hasn't run, because `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env` still doesn't exist. Whenever you write it, with `MODAL_PROXY_KEY=` and `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET=` lines, the live checks and the local end-to-end runs can use it.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:43:03.929Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": null,\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVJT827QKR6XG6F2S76EDD\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The agentic review of `common/` (ASE-73) finished after three rounds with no findings left. It left four small fixes uncommitted in the main checkout, and none of them changes a `common/` export:\\n\\n- `units.ts`: the paragraph, code and image units build on a shared non-exported `TextUnit` base instead of repeating `display` and `spoken`.\\n- `testing/cassettes.ts`: one shared key comparator, an inlined variable, and a blank line restored.\\n- `presign.ts`: an intermediate variable is inlined.\\n\\nSkipped, with reasons:\\n- **Root configs:** one root biome, tsconfig base and pnpm catalog. They need pipeline/ edits, so they wait until the branches merge.\\n- **Module split:** splitting `row.ts` and `cassettes.ts` into a module per function. The program design names those modules.\\n- **`encodeJson`:** removing it. The Workers will use it.\\n- **`AwsClient`:** reusing one client. It would change `presign`'s signature for a negligible gain.\\n- **vite types:** using `vite/client` types. `common/` doesn't depend on vite.\\n\\nChecks: 17 tests pass, and biome and tsc are clean.\\n\\nIf you haven't answered by the time the manual validation is due, the fixes stay uncommitted in the working tree, and I'll run the validation on the committed code.\\n\\n:::question\\nCommit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\\n- [ ] No, discard them\\n\\nRecommended: Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:49:39.330Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-76254eae\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Commit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, discard them\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"sent\",\n            \"answer\": {\n              \"v\": 1,\n              \"key\": \"q-76254eae\",\n              \"kind\": \"single\",\n              \"prompt\": \"Commit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\",\n              \"selected\": [\n                \"Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …`\"\n              ],\n              \"note\": \"do the module split; also let's use a better name rather than \\\"row\\\" something more representative to what it refers too\",\n              \"sourceLine\": 19\n            },\n            \"revision\": 120,\n            \"sent_revision\": 120,\n            \"picked_by\": {\n              \"id\": \"person\",\n              \"name\": null\n            },\n            \"picked_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:09.317Z\",\n            \"sent_reply_id\": \"msg_01M4MVQEDXMY84B6N8CPM1493E\",\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MVJT827QKR6XG6F2S76EDD\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVQEDXMY84B6N8CPM1493E\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MVJT827QKR6XG6F2S76EDD\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"person\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"Answered 1 question.\\n\\n## Answers to your questions\\n\\n1 of 1 question answered.\\n\\n### Q1. Commit the four review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`? (line 19)\\nAnswer: Yes, commit them as `refactor(common): …` (your recommendation)\\nNote: do the module split; also let's use a better name rather than \\\"row\\\" something more representative to what it refers too\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:11.069Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"delivery\": {\n          \"state\": \"delivered\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:12.153Z\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVRDFEHQ9EJ5CZMVVPF1HZ\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MVQEDXMY84B6N8CPM1493E\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"On it. The common/ subagent commits the four fixes, then splits `row.ts` and `testing/cassettes.ts` into one module per function. The item row's reads and writes go under `common/src/item-store/`: `read-item.ts`, `write-status.ts`, and `json-column.ts` holding the encode/decode pair. The package keeps exporting the same names, so the pipeline and api work in progress isn't affected. I'll tell you if the names it lands on differ.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:52:42.862Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MVWFTS43E3VV31YFVE50HF\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"**common/**\\n- Fixes committed as `349fe2d`.\\n- Split committed as `2cbc866`. `common/src/item-store/` now holds `json-column.ts`, `read-item.ts` and `write-status.ts`. The cassette replay code is in eight small modules under `common/testing/`. The exports haven't changed.\\n- The same subagent is now on ASE-82, the CI workflow.\\n\\n**api/ (ASE-80)**\\n- Done as `79ed096` on `feat/cloudflare-migration-api`: the Python tree is replaced by the `nagara-api` Worker. All 35 tests pass (D1–D27), and lint and types are clean. Its agentic review is running.\\n- Choices the notes left open, which the subagent made itself. Reply if you want any changed:\\n  - When the Workflow can't be created, enqueue still answers 202, with the item `failed`.\\n  - Error bodies keep the FastAPI shape `{\\\"detail\\\": …}`.\\n  - `duration` and `audio_url` are `null` until the item is ready.\\n  - A `create` or `restart` that fails during a retry or re-queue answers 500 and leaves the item `queued`, so the 15-minute re-queue picks it up.\\n  - `/health` answers plain `ok`, as the program design says. The old API answered JSON.\\n- Drift to reconcile in the docs later:\\n  - The API has no R2 binding, because it only signs URLs. `persistence-and-storage`, `deployment-and-ci` and `local-development` say both Workers bind the bucket. The local-dev task settles how the API's presigned GETs reach the local bucket.\\n  - The R2 bucket name `nagara` is a placeholder. Nothing in the notes settles it.\\n\\n**pipeline/ (ASE-75 to 79)** is still running. The tts review and its live check are running too.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T06:54:56.345Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The tts and api agentic reviews have both finished. Each left its fixes uncommitted in its worktree, and both suites pass: tts 19 tests with ruff and ty clean, api 35 tests with biome and tsc clean.\\n\\n**tts live check passed** against a `modal serve` dev copy, with your proxy token, which was never printed:\\n- `POST /start` without credentials answers 401.\\n- Malformed and unknown call ids answer 422.\\n- A start with credentials answers 200 with a `call_id`.\\n- Polling gives 202 until 200 after about 25 s, with contiguous timings whose last end equals the duration (8.575 s).\\n- The PUT received 23 KB of Ogg Opus, which ffprobe reads as 8.58 s. Nobody listened to it, so that stays a manual row.\\n- The dev app is stopped and the deployed `nagara-tts` wasn't touched.\\n\\nReview fixes: tts gets one `respond()` helper for every non-200 answer, and the malformed-id 422 now comes from FastAPI's `Query(pattern=...)`. api gets `ITEM_STATUS` constants instead of SQL literals, one route table, and the staleness check in one place.\\n\\nIf you haven't answered by the time the pipeline lands, I'll go with the recommendations so the local validation keeps moving. You can reverse any of them afterwards.\\n\\n:::question\\nCommit the tts and api review fixes on their branches?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes, commit both\\n- [ ] No, discard them\\n\\nRecommended: Yes, commit both\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\nAPI: re-queue or retry can start a second Workflow instance for the same item. `create` passes no id, and the row only learns the instance id when the first step runs. Example: the pipeline is down for 15 minutes after a successful create, the re-queue creates another instance, and then both run.\\n\\n- [ ] Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\\n- [ ] Keep the program design (Cloudflare picks the id)\\n\\nRecommended: Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\nAPI: when `get()` or `restart()` throws after the claim is written, the route answers 500. A retry then leaves the item `queued` with `retry_count` already counted. A re-queue has already moved `queued_at`.\\n\\n- [ ] Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\\n- [ ] Leave it: 500, and the item waits for the next re-queue\\n\\nRecommended: Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\nAPI: the row insert and the re-queue and retry claims live in `api/src/items/`, as the program design says. A reviewer suggested `common/`, since CLAUDE.md gives `common/` \\\"the item row's reads and writes\\\". Only the API uses these three, though, and CLAUDE.md also keeps single-user code out of `common/`.\\n\\n- [ ] Keep them in `api/`\\n- [ ] Move them to `common/src/item-store/`\\n\\nRecommended: Keep them in `api/`\\n:::\\n\\n:::question\\ntts: the GPU image gets an extra layer holding fastapi and httpx, because `app.py` imports them when it loads in every container. It builds and runs on Modal. The alternative is lazy imports, via `image.imports()` or a factory, which changes the module's shape.\\n\\n- [ ] Keep the extra layer\\n- [ ] Switch to lazy imports\\n\\nRecommended: Keep the extra layer\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:00:27.883Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-4fa64649\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Commit the tts and api review fixes on their branches?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes, commit both\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, discard them\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes, commit both\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-1b99e738\",\n            \"position\": 1,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"API: re-queue or retry can start a second Workflow instance for the same item. `create` passes no id, and the row only learns the instance id when the first step runs. Example: the pipeline is down for 15 minutes after a successful create, the re-queue creates another instance, and then both run.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep the program design (Cloudflare picks the id)\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Create with `id: itemId`; on retry or re-queue, treat `already_exists` as \\\"restart that instance\\\"\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-55f1499d\",\n            \"position\": 2,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"API: when `get()` or `restart()` throws after the claim is written, the route answers 500. A retry then leaves the item `queued` with `retry_count` already counted. A re-queue has already moved `queued_at`.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Leave it: 500, and the item waits for the next re-queue\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Retry writes the item back to `failed` with the error; re-queue only logs, and the item is picked up again after 15 minutes\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-933f7b37\",\n            \"position\": 3,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"API: the row insert and the re-queue and retry claims live in `api/src/items/`, as the program design says. A reviewer suggested `common/`, since CLAUDE.md gives `common/` \\\"the item row's reads and writes\\\". Only the API uses these three, though, and CLAUDE.md also keeps single-user code out of `common/`.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep them in `api/`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Move them to `common/src/item-store/`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Keep them in `api/`\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-cb065b8f\",\n            \"position\": 4,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"tts: the GPU image gets an extra layer holding fastapi and httpx, because `app.py` imports them when it loads in every container. It builds and runs on Modal. The alternative is lazy imports, via `image.imports()` or a factory, which changes the module's shape.\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep the extra layer\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Switch to lazy imports\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Keep the extra layer\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6KKB0Y8BTRMJKFXSXDM3\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MW6WHPTJ8Y3X18M3ZP1MCB\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The CI review is done too. It left two fixes uncommitted in `cloudflare.yml`, and actionlint still passes:\\n- `wrangler-action` goes up to v4, which the wiki's `cf-cli` entry names.\\n- Each job installs only its own tree, with `pnpm install --filter \\\"{./<dir>}...\\\"`.\\n\\nSkipped:\\n- **Composite setup action:** it would need a new file under `.github/actions/`.\\n- **Merged check jobs:** they would change which deploys a failed check stops.\\n\\n:::question\\nCommit the CI review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\\n\\n- [ ] Yes\\n- [ ] No, discard them\\n\\nRecommended: Yes\\n:::\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:00:37.046Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-18a1c3da\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Commit the CI review fixes on `feat/cloudflare-migration`?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Yes\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"No, discard them\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Yes\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MW6WHPTJ8Y3X18M3ZP1MCB\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MWZDS43358DQP7H30GMHMZ\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The pipeline is done: four commits on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline` (`16764e2`, `5c59179`, `cd934c3`, `6d1f492`). Every row from C1 to C28 has a test, the suite has 120 tests and passes three runs in a row, and lint, types and build are clean. The Images binding works under vitest, so it needs no stand-in. Its agentic review is running now.\\n\\nDrift it reported, which the docs will be reconciled against:\\n- **Step retries:** `retries.limit: 2`, which means 3 attempts. That matches the notes, while the program design's \\\"limit 3\\\" would have meant 4.\\n- **Agent gives up:** when authoring or revision gives up, the item fails at once with no retry of the step, so the agents' own retry bound from `recipes.md` holds.\\n- **Firecrawl failure:** a missing page body comes back as `html: null` instead of a throw, so the credit ledger row is written before the step fails.\\n- **Image paths:** relative image `src` values are resolved against the item URL. The Python code didn't do that.\\n- **SVG cleanup:** stripping also removes `on*` attributes from SVGs.\\n- **Fake agent:** a `conversation.ts` factory in `agents/` makes the agent fake in tests.\\n- **Modal URLs:** the vars point at the URLs the not-yet-deployed `nagara-tts` will have. Locally they're overridden with the dev copy.\\n\\n:::question\\nImage degradation reasons. The union in `common/` only allows `404 | timeout | undecodable`, so a 403 or 500 is recorded as `404`. Should the union be widened?\\n\\n- [ ] Keep the three reasons as they are\\n- [ ] Add a reason for the other HTTP statuses (e.g. `http_error`) in `common/`\\n\\nRecommended: Keep the three reasons as they are\\n:::\\n\\nNext, once the review finishes: merge the four branches, build the local-dev pieces (ASE-81: shared state folder, tunnel proxy, `.dev.vars`), then run the manual rows locally against the Modal dev copy with small articles.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:14:01.124Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\",\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"q-734de979\",\n            \"position\": 0,\n            \"kind\": \"single\",\n            \"prompt\": \"Image degradation reasons. The union in `common/` only allows `404 | timeout | undecodable`, so a 403 or 500 is recorded as `404`. Should the union be widened?\",\n            \"context\": null,\n            \"choices\": [\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Keep the three reasons as they are\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": true,\n                \"settled\": false\n              },\n              {\n                \"label\": \"Add a reason for the other HTTP statuses (e.g. `http_error`) in `common/`\",\n                \"description\": null,\n                \"recommended\": false,\n                \"settled\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"recommendation\": \"Keep the three reasons as they are\",\n            \"suggested_text\": null,\n            \"decision_on_answer\": false,\n            \"stopped\": null,\n            \"holds_up\": [],\n            \"asked_by_agent_id\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n            \"orphaned\": false,\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"answer\": null,\n            \"revision\": 0,\n            \"sent_revision\": 0,\n            \"picked_by\": null,\n            \"picked_at\": null,\n            \"sent_reply_id\": null,\n            \"decision_id\": null,\n            \"message_id\": \"msg_01M4MWZDS43358DQP7H30GMHMZ\",\n            \"decision_recording\": false,\n            \"decision_draft\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4MXAH44KKYMKNWEWW3K7ATX\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"name\": \"Claude Code\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"The machine is low on memory: 14 of 15 GiB used and 5 GiB in swap. The pipeline review's reviewer tabs are the main load. Claude Code stopped my background wait on the pipeline review to free memory, and it tells me not to restart that wait unless you ask. The review itself keeps running in its herdr tab.\\n\\nTo free memory, I closed the idle common/ subagent. Its work is committed. The tts and api subagents stay open, because their worktrees hold the uncommitted review fixes waiting on your answer.\\n\\nUntil you reply, I'm not woken when the review finishes. When you're back, a \\\"go on\\\" (here or in the chat) gets me to collect the review and continue with the merge, local dev and the manual rows. If you'd rather I keep going unattended, start Claude Code with `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BG_SHELL_PRESSURE_REAP=1`.\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T07:20:04.996Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": null,\n        \"thread_name\": \"cloudflare-migration: orchestrator\",\n        \"base_path\": \"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"msg_01M4NMVJ02AW6BSC2GDRY0RWKX\",\n        \"project_id\": \"prj_01M4MT8RTWBG0YS9FM3TPQYHBZ\",\n        \"thread_id\": \"msg_01M4MV3DG6QM9Q0V6EJ8E9C0EX\",\n        \"reply_to\": \"msg_01M4MXAH44KKYMKNWEWW3K7ATX\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"kind\": \"person\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": null,\n        \"body\": \"continue with the work, clean up anything that's no longer necessary and serialize checks if necessary\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T14:11:20.194Z\",\n        \"resolved_at\": null,\n        \"idempotency_key\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"delivery\": {\n          \"state\": \"delivered\",\n          \"host\": \"claude-code\",\n          \"session\": \"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-10-11T14:11:21.344Z\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"url\": \"http://localhost:39937/#REDACTED\"\n}","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"22dc6819-b991-409b-a73f-1958b3539fd2","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
