rint(d.get('message',''))\" | tee /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/review-pipeline.md","description":"Check memory, fleet and pipeline review"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"51de29e3-9b75-4ada-b06f-9e99718ca482","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfvau2QwoRac73MiNNEu8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ef46eff-25bc-4478-b4ba-ccc925dee058","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:11:29.912Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"8ef46eff-25bc-4478-b4ba-ccc925dee058","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a8063492-bf9d-4b99-bb12-dd4a7ca042f8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KBvYma1eCPdZ2QebLF4md9","type":"tool_result","content":"               total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available\nMem:            15Gi       6.0Gi       7.7Gi       591Mi       2.6Gi       9.3Gi\nimpl: tts endpoints (ASE-74) idle\nimpl: pipeline (ASE-75..79) done\nimpl: api Worker (ASE-80) done\ndone\nThese notices are for the round-3 reviewers. I had already read their findings and closed their tabs, so nothing new arrived. The report below is the final state of the review.\n\n# Agentic review: pipeline/ on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline`\n\nThe review ran three rounds. Every fix stayed inside `pipeline/` and is uncommitted: 16 modified files, which `git -C /home/agus/.herdr/worktrees/nagara/feat-cloudflare-migration-pipeline diff HEAD` shows in full. After the last fix, tests, types and lint all pass. Several findings need your ruling; they are listed below.\n\n**Scope:** the committed diff `624387d...HEAD`, limited to `pipeline/`. There was no uncommitted or untracked work. I left out the root lockfile and the cassette YAML files, which moved from `api/` unchanged.\n\n**Reviewers:**\n- Four facet reviewers: reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude.\n- One conventions reviewer per source: the project `CLAUDE.md`, your `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, the \"Code\" section of mahou basics, and the wiki entries for workflows, vitest-plugin, durable-objects, images, r2, ai-gateway, flue, firecrawl, gemini svg-input, modal web-endpoints, markdown ast-parsers and the local cassettes-over-mocks entry.\n- `.mahou/basics.md` holds only a rule about subagents, so it had no code conventions to check.\n\nThe findings files are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/agentic-review-pipeline/`.\n\n## Fixed\n\n**Round 1**\n1. `workflow/ledger.ts`: removed the unused `record` export.\n2. `agents/conversation.ts`: `AgentConversation` is now a plain function type instead of an object with one `converse` method.\n3. `recipes/settle.ts` and `steps/recipe.ts`:\n   - `settle` takes the whole `RecipeVersionRow`.\n   - `versionId` replaces `isNew`: it holds the existing version's id, or null for a script the agents just settled.\n   - The recipe step saves with `settled.versionId ?? await saveVersion(...)`.\n   - `agent` is typed as `AgentKind`.\n4. The fetch step returns `{ html, domain }`. lease, recipe and release take the domain as a parameter, so they no longer re-read the item row and the three `extraction_domain ?? \"\"` fallbacks are gone.\n5. `wrapper.ts`: the status parameter is typed `Extract<ItemStatus, \"queued\" | \"generating\">`, and the retries comment says why the limit is 2.\n6. `describe/jobs.ts`: `kind` is typed `Degradation[\"type\"]`.\n7. `steps/describe.ts`: `fallBack` is a closure inside the step that takes only `(job, reason)`.\n8. `images/acquire.ts`:\n   - The per-host semaphore is created without a type cast.\n   - One `Blob` feeds both Images binding calls.\n   - Image units are grouped by anchor with `Map.groupBy` instead of copying an array on every insert.\n   - The global permit also covers decode and store.\n9. `describe/describe-one.ts`: `toBase64` builds its string in 32 KiB chunks.\n10. Tests:\n    - `scenario` saves recipes through the real `saveVersion` and returns the version id, so C1 asserts the returned id. `saveRecipe` is gone.\n    - Introspectors are disposed in an `afterEach` in `test/helpers/item.ts`.\n\n**Round 2**\n\n11. `acquire.ts`: the host permit is taken first and the global permit inside it. Before this, images waiting on a busy host held global permits and blocked images from other hosts.\n12. `acquire.ts`: `hostLimit` writes the per-host semaphore map only when it creates an entry.\n\n**Round 3**\n\n13. `acquire.ts`: `acquireOne` is `async` again. In round 2 I had made it synchronous, which let a src that does not parse as a URL throw out of the `map` and fail the whole images step. That src now becomes its own image's degradation again.\n\n## For you to rule on\n\n**Design or test-design decisions**\n- **The `scriptedAgentReplies` setting in production code.** The test design asked for \"configuration, not an environment branch\". The reviewers want the stand-in moved out of `src/`, behind an injection point or a `mockStepResult` on the recipe step.\n- **Flue dispatch and read share one step.** The flue wiki entry's documented shape is separate `step.do` calls, so the dispatch receipt survives a crash.\n- **Modal result 500 is retried.** The modal entry says a synthesis that fails deterministically answers 500 on every poll, so a retry of the same call never helps. The design says a 500 fails the attempt, not the item (row C16).\n- **Polling inside one step** with `setTimeout` instead of `step.sleep`. The design chose this so `current_step` keeps one name.\n- **The HTML rides as the fetch step's result.** The 1 MiB check measures raw bytes, but the stored result is the JSON-escaped `{ html }`, which is larger. The reviewers propose storing the HTML in R2 and passing its key, or lowering the cap.\n- **Status classification in the HTTP clients.** Firecrawl retries every non-2xx, so a 401 or 402 uses all three attempts. Changing which statuses retry changes behaviour.\n\n**Idempotency when a step runs again**\n- Ledger rows get random ids, so a step that reruns after a deploy writes the cost row twice. A fetch retry is billed again by Firecrawl, so its second row is a real cost.\n- The recipe step can save a second identical version if it reruns after `saveVersion`.\n\n**Outside this pass's bounds**\n- The images and describe steps duplicate the item-row write for units and degradations. The reviewers propose a `writeUnits` helper in `common/`, which this pass could not edit.\n- Your style guide asks for one function per module, but `acquire.ts` and `describe-one.ts` each hold several helpers. Splitting them needs new files, which this pass could not create.\n\n**Image permit layout**\n\nThis was still open after round 3. The host permit now also covers decode and store, so one host's images are decoded and stored one at a time. The alternative holds the host permit only around the download, with a separate permit around store, but then the raw bytes sit between the two permits under no bound. The choice is between memory and throughput.\n\n**Firecrawl billing comment**\n\n`firecrawl/client.ts` says an `auto` proxy escalation bills 5 credits, and so does `docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md`. The firecrawl wiki entry says it costs nothing extra, so the docs or the entry is wrong.\n\n**Cassette fidelity**\n- Modal and image describes are answered by handlers instead of fabricated cassettes. The test design names those handlers, and the image request bytes only exist once the Images binding runs.\n- Firecrawl cassettes are fabricated; recording one needs the real service.\n- No test covers an unreachable service.\n\n**Smaller items I judged not worth changing**\n- A HEAD request before each image PUT.\n- The `TextEncoder` copy in the HTML size check.\n- The one-entry `OPERATOR_GUARDS` map.\n- The two-layer error mapping in `download`. Removing it turns a dropped stream into `undecodable` instead of `timeout`.\n- `report ?? run.report` in `settle`, which exists to satisfy the shared callback's nullable type.\n\n## Checks after the fixes (pipeline/)\n\n```\npnpm test   Test Files 13 passed (13) · Tests 120 passed | 1 skipped (121)\npnpm lint   Checked 76 files. No fixes applied.\npnpm types  exit 0\n```\n\nAll reviewer tabs are closed.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1659d269-f804-47ba-b708-3cc850be118b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:11:30.449Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"               total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available\nMem:            15Gi       6.0Gi       7.7Gi       591Mi       2.6Gi       9.3Gi\nimpl: tts endpoints (ASE-74) idle\nimpl: pipeline (ASE-75..79) done\nimpl: api Worker (ASE-80) done\ndone\nThese notices are for the round-3 reviewers. I had already read their findings and closed their tabs, so nothing new arrived. The report below is the final state of the review.\n\n# Agentic review: pipeline/ on `feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline`\n\nThe review ran three rounds. Every fix stayed inside `pipeline/` and is uncommitted: 16 modified files, which `git -C /home/agus/.herdr/worktrees/nagara/feat-cloudflare-migration-pipeline diff HEAD` shows in full. After the last fix, tests, types and lint all pass. Several findings need your ruling; they are listed below.\n\n**Scope:** the committed diff `624387d...HEAD`, limited to `pipeline/`. There was no uncommitted or untracked work. I left out the root lockfile and the cassette YAML files, which moved from `api/` unchanged.\n\n**Reviewers:**\n- Four facet reviewers: reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude.\n- One conventions reviewer per source: the project `CLAUDE.md`, your `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, the \"Code\" section of mahou basics, and the wiki entries for workflows, vitest-plugin, durable-objects, images, r2, ai-gateway, flue, firecrawl, gemini svg-input, modal web-endpoints, markdown ast-parsers and the local cassettes-over-mocks entry.\n- `.mahou/basics.md` holds only a rule about subagents, so it had no code conventions to check.\n\nThe findings files are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/agentic-review-pipeline/`.\n\n## Fixed\n\n**Round 1**\n1. `workflow/ledger.ts`: removed the unused `record` export.\n2. `agents/conversation.ts`: `AgentConversation` is now a plain function type instead of an object with one `converse` method.\n3. `recipes/settle.ts` and `steps/recipe.ts`:\n   - `settle` takes the whole `RecipeVersionRow`.\n   - `versionId` replaces `isNew`: it holds the existing version's id, or null for a script the agents just settled.\n   - The recipe step saves with `settled.versionId ?? await saveVersion(...)`.\n   - `agent` is typed as `AgentKind`.\n4. The fetch step returns `{ html, domain }`. lease, recipe and release take the domain as a parameter, so they no longer re-read the item row and the three `extraction_domain ?? \"\"` fallbacks are gone.\n5. `wrapper.ts`: the status parameter is typed `Extract<ItemStatus, \"queued\" | \"generating\">`, and the retries comment says why the limit is 2.\n6. `describe/jobs.ts`: `kind` is typed `Degradation[\"type\"]`.\n7. `steps/describe.ts`: `fallBack` is a closure inside the step that takes only `(job, reason)`.\n8. `images/acquire.ts`:\n   - The per-host semaphore is created without a type cast.\n   - One `Blob` feeds both Images binding calls.\n   - Image units are grouped by anchor with `Map.groupBy` instead of copying an array on every insert.\n   - The global permit also covers decode and store.\n9. `describe/describe-one.ts`: `toBase64` builds its string in 32 KiB chunks.\n10. Tests:\n    - `scenario` saves recipes through the real `saveVersion` and returns the version id, so C1 asserts the returned id. `saveRecipe` is gone.\n    - Introspectors are disposed in an `afterEach` in `test/helpers/item.ts`.\n\n**Round 2**\n\n11. `acquire.ts`: the host permit is taken first and the global permit inside it. Before this, images waiting on a busy host held global permits and blocked images from other hosts.\n12. `acquire.ts`: `hostLimit` writes the per-host semaphore map only when it creates an entry.\n\n**Round 3**\n\n13. `acquire.ts`: `acquireOne` is `async` again. In round 2 I had made it synchronous, which let a src that does not parse as a URL throw out of the `map` and fail the whole images step. That src now becomes its own image's degradation again.\n\n## For you to rule on\n\n**Design or test-design decisions**\n- **The `scriptedAgentReplies` setting in production code.** The test design asked for \"configuration, not an environment branch\". The reviewers want the stand-in moved out of `src/`, behind an injection point or a `mockStepResult` on the recipe step.\n- **Flue dispatch and read share one step.** The flue wiki entry's documented shape is separate `step.do` calls, so the dispatch receipt survives a crash.\n- **Modal result 500 is retried.** The modal entry says a synthesis that fails deterministically answers 500 on every poll, so a retry of the same call never helps. The design says a 500 fails the attempt, not the item (row C16).\n- **Polling inside one step** with `setTimeout` instead of `step.sleep`. The design chose this so `current_step` keeps one name.\n- **The HTML rides as the fetch step's result.** The 1 MiB check measures raw bytes, but the stored result is the JSON-escaped `{ html }`, which is larger. The reviewers propose storing the HTML in R2 and passing its key, or lowering the cap.\n- **Status classification in the HTTP clients.** Firecrawl retries every non-2xx, so a 401 or 402 uses all three attempts. Changing which statuses retry changes behaviour.\n\n**Idempotency when a step runs again**\n- Ledger rows get random ids, so a step that reruns after a deploy writes the cost row twice. A fetch retry is billed again by Firecrawl, so its second row is a real cost.\n- The recipe step can save a second identical version if it reruns after `saveVersion`.\n\n**Outside this pass's bounds**\n- The images and describe steps duplicate the item-row write for units and degradations. The reviewers propose a `writeUnits` helper in `common/`, which this pass could not edit.\n- Your style guide asks for one function per module, but `acquire.ts` and `describe-one.ts` each hold several helpers. Splitting them needs new files, which this pass could not create.\n\n**Image permit layout**\n\nThis was still open after round 3. The host permit now also covers decode and store, so one host's images are decoded and stored one at a time. The alternative holds the host permit only around the download, with a separate permit around store, but then the raw bytes sit between the two permits under no bound. The choice is between memory and throughput.\n\n**Firecrawl billing comment**\n\n`firecrawl/client.ts` says an `auto` proxy escalation bills 5 credits, and so does `docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md`. The firecrawl wiki entry says it costs nothing extra, so the docs or the entry is wrong.\n\n**Cassette fidelity**\n- Modal and image describes are answered by handlers instead of fabricated cassettes. The test design names those handlers, and the image request bytes only exist once the Images binding runs.\n- Firecrawl cassettes are fabricated; recording one needs the real service.\n- No test covers an unreachable service.\n\n**Smaller items I judged not worth changing**\n- A HEAD request before each image PUT.\n- The `TextEncoder` copy in the HTML size check.\n- The one-entry `OPERATOR_GUARDS` map.\n- The two-layer error mapping in `download`. Removing it turns a dropped stream into `undecodable` instead of `timeout`.\n- `report ?? run.report` in `settle`, which exists to satisfy the shared callback's nullable type.\n\n## Checks after the fixes (pipeline/)\n\n```\npnpm test   Test Files 13 passed (13) · Tests 120 passed | 1 skipped (121)\npnpm lint   Checked 76 files. No fixes applied.\npnpm types  exit 0\n```\n\nAll reviewer tabs are closed.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"51de29e3-9b75-4ada-b06f-9e99718ca482","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8ef46eff-25bc-4478-b4ba-ccc925dee058","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
