{"parentUuid":"0a669c4d-42f4-49e1-bf05-f8f053e9bc62","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvav9baHpabE9H7aFTxU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015jF6t6xDh7TNMj1JmA4MNS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H close w45:t2; $H prompt w47:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Your review fixes are committed as 9879c02. The user told me to go ahead with my recommendations on the open questions, so implement these two on your branch, with tests, then run biome, tsc and vitest in api/ and commit:\n1. Create each item's Workflow with \\`id: itemId\\`. On a re-queue or retry, a create that fails with an instance that already exists becomes a restart of that instance (\\`get(itemId)\\` then \\`restart\\`). The API then always knows the instance id is the item id.\n2. When \\`get()\\` or \\`restart()\\` throws after a claim was written: on a retry, write the item back to \\`failed\\` with the error (retry_count stays counted) and answer with that item; on a re-queue, log the error and answer the item as it is, so the next poll after 15 minutes tries again.\nThe row insert and claims stay in api/src/items/. Commit as feat(api) or fix(api) as fits, and report the commit, the tests added and the check output in your final message. Note in the report which design notes these two change (they are design drift for the docs).</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Close tts child, send api decisions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":474,"cache_read_input_tokens":199407,"output_tokens":796,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":115},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":474,"ephemeral_5m_i