{"parentUuid":"0925b52f-76ef-4368-b2a7-d14bb8e584ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvb1h5Ye6srHifmFfJr9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_read_input_tokens":202223,"output_tokens":1490,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":70},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1490,"cache_read_input_tokens":202223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7630,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"fd2b58e9-3fa6-4ff4-a844-7fc26018a6c8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfvb1ggVJwDoLcLdsagbU","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f5e50e7-a235-4cac-9327-3dae85607ef3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:13:04.260Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"2f5e50e7-a235-4cac-9327-3dae85607ef3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvb1h5Ye6srHifmFfJr9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've resolved the Inbox thread and told both open subagents to bring questions to me from now on.\n\n## Implementation status\n\nEverything up to the merges is done and committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration`. Nothing is pushed or deployed.\n\n| Part | Task | Status | Tests |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Workspace + `common/` | ASE-73 | Done, reviewed, merged. Includes your `item-store/` split | 17 |\n| tts endpoints | ASE-74 | Done, reviewed, merged. Live check on a Modal dev copy passed | 19 |\n| pipeline | ASE-75 to 79 | Done, reviewed, merged | 120 |\n| api Worker | ASE-80 | Done and reviewed; adding two fixes now, not merged yet | 35 |\n| CI workflow | ASE-82 | Done, reviewed, on the branch | actionlint clean |\n| Local dev setup | ASE-81 | Not started | — |\n| Switchover / deploy | ASE-83 | Tomorrow | — |\n\nOn the merged tree, `common/` and `pipeline/` pass their tests, types and lint again. The api subagent is working right now.\n\n## Decisions I took for you\n\nYour Inbox reply said to continue, but these questions were still unanswered, so I went with my recommendations. Tell me to reverse any of them:\n1. I committed the review fixes for tts, api, pipeline and CI.\n2. The api creates each item's Workflow with the item id as its instance id. On a re-queue or retry, \"already exists\" means restart that instance, so the same item can't get a second instance.\n3. If the Workflow call throws after a retry has claimed the item, the item goes back to `failed`. A re-queue that hits the same error only logs it.\n4. The row insert and the re-queue and retry claims stay in `api/`.\n5. The tts GPU image keeps the extra fastapi/httpx layer.\n6. Image degradation reasons stay `404 | timeout | undecodable`, so a 403 or 500 image is recorded as `404`.\n\n## Open items from the pipeline review\n\nNone of these block local validation:\n- **Fake agent:** the stand-in sits behind a `scriptedAgentReplies` setting in production code. Reviewers want it moved out of `src/`; the test design asked for configuration.\n- **Modal 500s:** a result 500 is retried, but a synthesis that fails deterministically answers 500 on every poll, so the retries can't help.\n- **HTML size:** the HTML passes between steps as the fetch step's result. Its JSON-escaped form can exceed the 1 MiB cap the fetch step checks against raw bytes.\n- **Rerun duplicates:** a step that reruns can write a second ledger row or save a second identical recipe version.\n- **Firecrawl retries:** every non-2xx is retried, so a 401 or 402 uses all three attempts.\n- **Firecrawl billing:** the docs say an `auto` proxy escalation costs 5 credits; the wiki says it costs nothing extra. One of them is wrong.\n\n## Docs that no longer match the code\n\nI'll bring these to you for a docs pass before the manual validation reports:\n- The api has no R2 binding, but three notes say both Workers bind the bucket.\n- Step retries are `limit: 2`, which is 3 attempts.\n- The Workflow instance id is now the item id.\n- The R2 bucket name `nagara` is a placeholder, and so is the D1 id.\n- A push that changes only the pipeline also redeploys the api.\n- Relative image `src` values are resolved against the item URL, and SVG cleaning also strips `on*` attributes.\n\n## Next\n\n1. Merge the api branch once its two fixes land.\n2. ASE-81: the shared `.wrangler-state`, the tunnel proxy, and `.dev.vars` filled from the existing keys.\n3. Run the manual rows locally against a `modal serve` copy, with small articles: B1, C1, C5, C7, C9, C11, D1, D4, D5, D13, D16, D20, D21, D25. You'll need to listen to the audio from C1.\n\n**Still pending:** removing the Modal proxy token tomorrow (it's in `status.md`), and the R2 tokens from the spikes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_read_input_tokens":202223,"output_tokens":1490,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":70},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1490,"cache_read_input_tokens":202223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fd2b58e9-3fa6-4ff4-a844-7fc26018a6c8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfvb1ggVJwDoLcLdsagbU","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"01ce409f-044f-47fc-a9bd-6bdd7f9ad5cd","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:13:10.198Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
