{"parentUuid":"8264138a-335f-439d-883f-a12d080626dc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvb4RiuHP1KNqBGfw7wy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WvCbGMbUusXPGh86QcrF7X","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w47:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\"; cd /home/agus/.herdr/worktrees/nagara/feat-cloudflare-migration-api && git log --oneline -3 && git status --short | head","description":"Collect the api subagent result"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370,"cache_read_input_tokens":204902,"output_tokens":233,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":370,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":233,"cache_read_input_tokens":204902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":370},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WvCbGMbUusXPGh86QcrF7X":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w47:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\"; cd /home/agus/.herdr/worktrees/nagara/feat-cloudflare-migration-api && git log --oneline -3 && git status --short | head","description":"Collect the api subagent result"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"22a380b3-8dc8-46a8-98b3-6f1e55742a10","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfvb4QgeXNitmHnG2RVWD","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"08da608c-e6be-46cd-bd89-beaf16639471","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:13:35.824Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"08da608c-e6be-46cd-bd89-beaf16639471","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0eb95917-9f61-49f9-8df0-359aa75e5dba","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WvCbGMbUusXPGh86QcrF7X","type":"tool_result","content":"done\n# Workflow keyed by item id, and recovery when a restart fails\n\nBoth changes are committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration-api` as `254a3a5 fix(api): key each item's Workflow by its id and recover from failed restarts`. Biome, tsc and vitest pass in `api/`, with 40 tests. The row insert and the claims stay in `api/src/items/`. I've noted that questions now go to you with `<subagent-ask>` and not to the Inbox.\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. The item id is the instance id**\n- Enqueue calls `create({ id: itemId, params: { itemId } })`.\n- When a re-queued or retried row has no `workflow_instance_id`, `restartItem` still calls `create` with the item id.\n- If that `create` throws an error containing `already_exists`, it calls `get(itemId)` and restarts that instance from `restartPoint(current_step)`. That substring is the only part of the error text that local and deployed have in common. Any other error from `create` is passed on.\n- When the row does have an instance id, `get(itemId)` and `restart` run as before.\n\n**2. Errors after a claim**\n- **Retry:** if `restartItem` throws, the route writes the item back to `failed` with `String(error)`, keeps `current_step`, and leaves `retry_count` counted. It answers `202` with the failed item, the same way enqueue answers when its `create` fails.\n- **Re-queue:** if `restartItem` throws, the error is logged with `console.error`, and the poll answers `200` with the item as it is. The claim has already moved `queued_at`, so the next stale poll 15 minutes later tries again.\n\n## Tests\n\n**Added**\n- poll: restarts the instance a stale queued item already has when its first step has not run.\n- poll: answers a stale queued item as it is when its restart throws, leaving it for the next stale poll.\n- retry: restarts the instance an item already has when its first step never ran.\n- retry: writes the item back to failed when `get` throws, with the retry counted.\n- retry: writes the item back to failed when `restart` throws, with the retry counted.\n\n**Updated**\n- The stand-in takes `existingIds` (its `create` then throws an `already_exists` error for those ids), `getError` and `restartError`, and returns an instance under the given id.\n- Every existing `create` assertion now expects `{ id, params: { itemId } }`.\n- The fixtures use the item id as `workflow_instance_id` in place of `wf-1`.\n\n## Checks (in `api/`)\n\n```\nbiome check .  → Checked 33 files … No fixes applied.\ntsc --noEmit   → clean\nvitest run     → Test Files 6 passed (6) · Tests 40 passed (40)\n```\n\n## Design drift for the docs\n\n- **`docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md`:**\n  - The Enqueue paragraph says the instance is created \"with the item's id as the only param\"; the item id is now also the instance id.\n  - The Poll and Retry paragraphs say the API \"creates an instance when the row holds no instance id\"; it now creates one or, when one already exists, restarts it.\n  - The Retry paragraph doesn't say what happens when the restart fails: the item goes back to `failed` and the retry stays counted.\n  - The `workflow_instance_id` row says the first step writes it. That is still true, but the value is now always the item id.\n- **`docs/technical-design/item-contract.md`:**\n  - Under \"What each route does\", the `GET /items/{id}` and `POST /items/{id}/retry` rows, and the 🔁 Retry section, say \"creates one when the row holds no instance id\"; that now covers restarting an instance that already exists.\n  - The retry route can now answer `202` with the item `failed` when the restart throws.\n  - Nothing documents that a re-queue whose restart throws is only logged.\n- **Program design `program-design/nagara.md`:**\n  - §3.1 says \"instance id left to Cloudflare\" for enqueue, and its re-queue and retry callstacks have no `already_exists` fallback and no error handling.\n  - §3.3 describes the re-queue and retry restart without these two behaviours.\n254a3a5 fix(api): key each item's Workflow by its id and recover from failed restarts\n9879c02 refactor(api): share status constants, one route table and one staleness check\n79ed096 feat(api): replace the Python API with the nagara-api Worker\nShell cwd was reset to /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"56061bd5-7584-4a84-ac79-8f8f659b7029","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:13:36.306Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\n# Workflow keyed by item id, and recovery when a restart fails\n\nBoth changes are committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration-api` as `254a3a5 fix(api): key each item's Workflow by its id and recover from failed restarts`. Biome, tsc and vitest pass in `api/`, with 40 tests. The row insert and the claims stay in `api/src/items/`. I've noted that questions now go to you with `<subagent-ask>` and not to the Inbox.\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. The item id is the instance id**\n- Enqueue calls `create({ id: itemId, params: { itemId } })`.\n- When a re-queued or retried row has no `workflow_instance_id`, `restartItem` still calls `create` with the item id.\n- If that `create` throws an error containing `already_exists`, it calls `get(itemId)` and restarts that instance from `restartPoint(current_step)`. That substring is the only part of the error text that local and deployed have in common. Any other error from `create` is passed on.\n- When the row does have an instance id, `get(itemId)` and `restart` run as before.\n\n**2. Errors after a claim**\n- **Retry:** if `restartItem` throws, the route writes the item back to `failed` with `String(error)`, keeps `current_step`, and leaves `retry_count` counted. It answers `202` with the failed item, the same way enqueue answers when its `create` fails.\n- **Re-queue:** if `restartItem` throws, the error is logged with `console.error`, and the poll answers `200` with the item as it is. The claim has already moved `queued_at`, so the next stale poll 15 minutes later tries again.\n\n## Tests\n\n**Added**\n- poll: restarts the instance a stale queued item already has when its first step has not run.\n- poll: answers a stale queued item as it is when its restart throws, leaving it for the next stale poll.\n- retry: restarts the instance an item already has when its first step never ran.\n- retry: writes the item back to failed when `get` throws, with the retry counted.\n- retry: writes the item back to failed when `restart` throws, with the retry counted.\n\n**Updated**\n- The stand-in takes `existingIds` (its `create` then throws an `already_exists` error for those ids), `getError` and `restartError`, and returns an instance under the given id.\n- Every existing `create` assertion now expects `{ id, params: { itemId } }`.\n- The fixtures use the item id as `workflow_instance_id` in place of `wf-1`.\n\n## Checks (in `api/`)\n\n```\nbiome check .  → Checked 33 files … No fixes applied.\ntsc --noEmit   → clean\nvitest run     → Test Files 6 passed (6) · Tests 40 passed (40)\n```\n\n## Design drift for the docs\n\n- **`docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md`:**\n  - The Enqueue paragraph says the instance is created \"with the item's id as the only param\"; the item id is now also the instance id.\n  - The Poll and Retry paragraphs say the API \"creates an instance when the row holds no instance id\"; it now creates one or, when one already exists, restarts it.\n  - The Retry paragraph doesn't say what happens when the restart fails: the item goes back to `failed` and the retry stays counted.\n  - The `workflow_instance_id` row says the first step writes it. That is still true, but the value is now always the item id.\n- **`docs/technical-design/item-contract.md`:**\n  - Under \"What each route does\", the `GET /items/{id}` and `POST /items/{id}/retry` rows, and the 🔁 Retry section, say \"creates one when the row holds no instance id\"; that now covers restarting an instance that already exists.\n  - The retry route can now answer `202` with the item `failed` when the restart throws.\n  - Nothing documents that a re-queue whose restart throws is only logged.\n- **Program design `program-design/nagara.md`:**\n  - §3.1 says \"instance id left to Cloudflare\" for enqueue, and its re-queue and retry callstacks have no `already_exists` fallback and no error handling.\n  - §3.3 describes the re-queue and retry restart without these two behaviours.\n254a3a5 fix(api): key each item's Workflow by its id and recover from failed restarts\n9879c02 refactor(api): share status constants, one route table and one staleness check\n79ed096 feat(api): replace the Python API with the nagara-api Worker","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"22a380b3-8dc8-46a8-98b3-6f1e55742a10","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08da608c-e6be-46cd-bd89-beaf16639471","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","rea