{"parentUuid":"ec823958-4cae-4a92-bdf8-3c76fe31f91c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvb7AbQpdgrYyk53VrHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ch1JNm1LZiJwTtZa7oQzim","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H close w47:t2; cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs; cat > implement-ASE-81.md <<'EOF'\n# ASE-81: local development setup (task for the pipeline subagent)\n\nSame brief and rules as your pipeline brief (`implement-pipeline.md`), with these differences:\n\n- Work in the **main checkout**, `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara`, on `feat/cloudflare-migration`. All four branches are merged there (HEAD 2313182). Do not work in your worktree any more.\n- You may touch `pipeline/`, `api/`, `common/` (its `migrate:local` script) and the root `.gitignore`, as ASE-81 and `docs/technical-design/local-development.md` say.\n- Read ASE-81 in full in Linear and the program design's local-development part (§7).\n\nBuild:\n- the shared state folder `.wrangler-state/` at the repository root (git-ignored), `persistState` in `pipeline/vite.config.ts`, `--persist-to` in api's dev script (already there; check it points at the same folder);\n- `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`;\n- `pipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs` and `pnpm dev:proxy`;\n- the experimental S3 credentials on the pipeline's R2 binding for local dev, as the spike `local-audio-upload/` found;\n- `pipeline/.dev.vars.example` and `api/.dev.vars.example` naming every secret, no values.\n- How the API's presigned GET URLs reach the local bucket: locally the API has no R2 binding and signs against `R2_S3_ENDPOINT`. Make the local value point at the pipeline dev server's local S3 endpoint (`http://localhost:<pipeline port>/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3`) with the same dummy credentials, so a browser can follow the 307. If that cannot work, say so and propose the alternative in a `<subagent-ask>`.\n\nThen fill the real local secret files **by script, never printing values**:\n- `pipeline/.dev.vars`: keep `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY`; add `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` from `api/.env`'s `NAGARA_FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` from `NAGARA_GEMINI_API_KEY`, `MODAL_PROXY_KEY` and `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET` from `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env`, the local dummy R2 PUT keys, and `MODAL_START_URL` / `MODAL_RESULT_URL` pointing at the dev copy `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run/{start,result}`.\n- `api/.dev.vars`: an `API_KEY` you generate locally (write it only to the file), and the dummy R2 GET keys.\n\nSmoke test, small: start both dev servers, the proxy, a quick tunnel and `uv run modal serve app.py` in `tts/` (record every PID). Check `/health`, a 401 without the key, and that `POST /items` writes a queued row and creates the Workflow instance in the pipeline dev server. Do **not** run real articles yet; the manual validation does that next. Stop everything you started, by PID, and stop the ephemeral Modal app.\n\nCommit as `feat(pipeline)`/`chore` as fits, move ASE-81 through its states, and report: commits, the exact launch steps as they now work, the smoke results, and drift against `local-development.md`.\nEOF\n$H prompt w46:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Next task: read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/implement-ASE-81.md.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Close api child and dispatch ASE-81 to the pipeline child"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":497,"cache_read_input_tokens":209718,"output_tokens":1813,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":177},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":497,"ephemer