ine dev server's local S3 endpoint (`http://localhost:<pipeline port>/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3`) with the same dummy credentials, so a browser can follow the 307. If that cannot work, say so and propose the alternative in a `<subagent-ask>`.\n\nThen fill the real local secret files **by script, never printing values**:\n- `pipeline/.dev.vars`: keep `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY`; add `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` from `api/.env`'s `NAGARA_FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` from `NAGARA_GEMINI_API_KEY`, `MODAL_PROXY_KEY` and `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET` from `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env`, the local dummy R2 PUT keys, and `MODAL_START_URL` / `MODAL_RESULT_URL` pointing at the dev copy `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run/{start,result}`.\n- `api/.dev.vars`: an `API_KEY` you generate locally (write it only to the file), and the dummy R2 GET keys.\n\nSmoke test, small: start both dev servers, the proxy, a quick tunnel and `uv run modal serve app.py` in `tts/` (record every PID). Check `/health`, a 401 without the key, and that `POST /items` writes a queued row and creates the Workflow instance in the pipeline dev server. Do **not** run real articles yet; the manual validation does that next. Stop everything you started, by PID, and stop the ephemeral Modal app.\n\nCommit as `feat(pipeline)`/`chore` as fits, move ASE-81 through its states, and report: commits, the exact launch steps as they now work, the smoke results, and drift against `local-development.md`.\nEOF\n$H prompt w46:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Next task: read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/implement-ASE-81.md.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Close api child and dispatch ASE-81 to the pipeline child"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1f166836-0875-4667-9843-00c77be5753e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfvb7ACbEYF9gAu2Y2AjJ","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ace21c2-2ccb-42b9-b6bb-a36e08853527","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:1