{"parentUuid":"cffc1728-f122-4301-a485-7803df8ac55c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvbTtHiqympi9Gaqreh1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XESaJ6PqYdH3gg5xNR9Cjf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara; grep -rn \"1 MiB\\|1MiB\\|maxHtmlBytes\" docs/technical-design/*.md | head -8; echo ---; grep -rn \"creditsUsed\\|credits\" pipeline/src --include=*.ts | head -10; echo ---; grep -rn \"upstream deploy\\|deploy-api\\|redeploy\" .scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md | head -8","description":"Look up the HTML cap, Firecrawl credits and CI rule"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":988,"cache_read_input_tokens":213173,"output_tokens":575,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":304},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":988,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":213173,"cache_creation_input_tokens":988,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":988},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XESaJ6PqYdH3gg5xNR9Cjf":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara; grep -rn \"1 MiB\\|1MiB\\|maxHtmlBytes\" docs/technical-design/*.md | head -8; echo ---; grep -rn \"creditsUsed\\|credits\" pipeline/src --include=*.ts | head -10; echo ---; grep -rn \"upstream deploy\\|deploy-api\\|redeploy\" .scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md | head -8","description":"Look up the HTML cap, Firecrawl credits and CI rule"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"da4752b0-f325-4b3f-b610-d985b451d06d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfvbTsueunXU7ZZYFQSy7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fb67887b-9d42-448d-9a6a-15cb5d0fec07","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:18:56.799Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"fb67887b-9d42-448d-9a6a-15cb5d0fec07","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fee01dd2-023b-45ab-adef-749adc411c6a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XESaJ6PqYdH3gg5xNR9Cjf","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/technical-design/tts-service.md:34:> A Workflow step can return about 1 MiB, and a full article's audio is far larger. Handing Modal a presigned PUT URL keeps the audio out of the result, so the result endpoint answers with timing and metadata alone. The pipeline Worker signs the URL with an R2 API token of its own, using common/'s presigning function and its audio key function (see [common-package](common-package.md)).\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:227:> A step result is capped near 1 MiB, and the Workflow keeps it so a later step, and a restart from a later step, can read it. The fetched HTML is needed only by the recipe step, so it rides as fetch's step result. The units are read and changed by several steps, so they sit on the row, and each step that changes them writes them there.\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:324:- **HTML over the cap**: a fetched page over the 1 MiB a step result can carry fails the fetch step.\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:340:A Workflow instance has no wall-clock limit; the bound is CPU per invocation, tens of seconds by default and configurable upward. The agent loops never approach that bound, because model turns are input-output waits. Step results are each capped near 1 MiB, which bounds the fetched HTML; an item's units, a few hundred kilobytes for a long article, fit well inside. Instance state persists for the retention window, days on the free tier and a month on the paid tier; the poll reads only the row, so an item outlives its instance.\n---\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.ts\n---\n.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md:636:One `cloudflare.yml` replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`: the jobs a tree did not change are skipped, and every deploy job runs on `!failure() && !cancelled()` with its own tree changed or an upstream deploy run, so a pipeline-only push deploys the pipeline without waiting for a migration that never ran, and a failed common check stops everything after it. Three separate workflows cannot wait on each other within one push without polling, which is why this is one file; the docs say three workflows and would change to one workflow with a job group per tree.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d038e2cb-d7e1-4a97-8eb4-41955614a64d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:18:57.277Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/technical-design/tts-service.md:34:> A Workflow step can return about 1 MiB, and a full article's audio is far larger. Handing Modal a presigned PUT URL keeps the audio out of the result, so the result endpoint answers with timing and metadata alone. The pipeline Worker signs the URL with an R2 API token of its own, using common/'s presigning function and its audio key function (see [common-package](common-package.md)).\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:227:> A step result is capped near 1 MiB, and the Workflow keeps it so a later step, and a restart from a later step, can read it. The fetched HTML is needed only by the recipe step, so it rides as fetch's step result. The units are read and changed by several steps, so they sit on the row, and each step that changes them writes them there.\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:324:- **HTML over the cap**: a fetched page over the 1 MiB a step result can carry fails the fetch step.\ndocs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md:340:A Workflow instance has no wall-clock limit; the bound is CPU per invocation, tens of seconds by default and configurable upward. The agent loops never approach that bound, because model turns are input-output waits. Step results are each capped near 1 MiB, which bounds the fetched HTML; an item's units, a few hundred kilobytes for a long article, fit well inside. Instance state persists for the retention window, days on the free tier and a month on the paid tier; the poll reads only the row, so an item outlives its instance.\n---\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.ts\n---\n.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/nagara.md:636:One `cloudflare.yml` replaces `api.yml` and `pipeline.yml`: the jobs a tree did not change are skipped, and every deploy job runs on `!failure() && !cancelled()` with its own tree changed or an upstream deploy run, so a pipeline-only push deploys the pipeline without waiting for a migration that never ran, and a failed common check stops everything after it. Three separate workflows cannot wait on each other within one push without polling, which is why this is one file; the docs say three workflows and would change to one workflow with a job group per tree.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"da4752b0-f325-4b3f-b610-d985b451d06d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/api","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":3},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/api","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fb67887b-9d42-448d-9a6a-15cb5d0fec07","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/hom