{"parentUuid":"84878eb8-dd14-44ed-8b9d-1874a6e8e04d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvbUiAHiCcW3ndoaN8YU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":216343,"output_tokens":1886,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":886},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1249,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1886,"cache_read_input_tokens":216343,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1249},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15966,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"8c861a27-f839-40ea-be93-34343d5f624c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfvbUhkEaNcoJadHXYZxK","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7f4a8a3-3e06-4ad2-8d88-0551a314a8d5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:19:19.271Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/pipeline/src","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"d7f4a8a3-3e06-4ad2-8d88-0551a314a8d5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvbUiAHiCcW3ndoaN8YU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is each annotation, with a proposed fix where one is needed:\n\n**1. Fake agent in production code.** Agreed. I'll have the pipeline subagent take `scriptedAgentReplies` out of `src/` and switch the agent to the fake only through the test setup, for example a test-only Worker entry in the vitest config. That happens once it finishes ASE-81.\n\n**3. The 1 MiB cap.** Cloudflare sets it, not us: a Workflow step's return value is limited to about 1 MiB, and the fetch step returns the HTML as its result. Our cap mirrors that limit, but it measures the raw HTML. The stored result is the JSON-escaped `{html}`, which is larger, so a page just under the cap can still exceed the platform limit. I propose measuring the serialized result against the cap instead. A page near 1 MiB would then fail cleanly in fetch instead of erroring inside the Workflow.\n\n**4. Rerun duplicates.** You're right, and the review overstated it. The recipe step reads the current recipe at the start of every attempt. If a rerun follows a successful save, it finds that version, runs it, and doesn't save again. It only saves a new version if the saved recipe fails and gets revised, and then that new version is legitimate. A duplicate ledger row on a rerun is a real second charge: Firecrawl bills a refetch and the agents bill a rerun. No change needed.\n\n**6. Firecrawl billing.** Firecrawl does return the cost: the ledger row records the response's `creditsUsed`, not an estimate. The \"5 credits on escalation\" claim is only a code comment and a sentence in `article-extraction.md`. I'll drop the claim from both instead of choosing between the comment and the wiki.\n\n**7. API without an R2 binding.** Signing doesn't need one. A presigned URL is computed locally from an R2 API token's S3 key pair; Cloudflare's docs say a binding can't produce presigned URLs. The API never reads or writes the bytes, so a binding would go unused. The docs that say both Workers bind the bucket get corrected.\n\n**11. Pipeline-only push redeploys the API.** That's a side effect of the CI rule \"a deploy runs when its tree changed or an upstream deploy ran\". The rule exists so a migration redeploys both Workers, since both read the schema. A pipeline deploy alone gives the API no reason to redeploy. The cross-script binding names the script and resolves at run time, so the API picks up the new pipeline without one. I propose this condition instead:\n- the pipeline deploys when `pipeline/` changed or the migration ran\n- the API deploys when `api/` changed or the migration ran, and still waits for the pipeline deploy when that one runs\n\nShould I apply these to the code and docs: the fake agent out of `src/`, the serialized-size cap, the Firecrawl comment and doc sentence, and the CI condition? I'll queue them for the pipeline subagent after ASE-81. I'll make the CI change myself in the main checkout."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":216343,"output_tokens":1886,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":886},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1249,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1886,"cache_read_input_tokens":216343,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1249},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8c861a27-f839-40ea-be93-34343d5f624c","apiBlockIndex":1,"reques