{"parentUuid":"5278ffbf-05e2-4fc5-b341-f89ca6bbb658","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvbZyyghrvEZv9agoowU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BKUpcu7obn7jYvfPgcm583","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w46:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\" | tee /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/impl-ASE-81.md","description":"Collect ASE-81 result"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2255,"cache_read_input_tokens":217592,"output_tokens":229,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2255,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":217592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2255},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BKUpcu7obn7jYvfPgcm583":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w46:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\" | tee /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/impl-ASE-81.md","description":"Collect ASE-81 result"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9e57f0fe-3e55-42af-9d49-e654d28d88a7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfvbZyYPqUMNb3YBcvemp","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2a3d3d0-a62e-425d-8666-093351517600","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:20:16.590Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/pipeline/src","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"c2a3d3d0-a62e-425d-8666-093351517600","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4dd0382c-fe1f-426f-a54d-e22edf6b3e7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BKUpcu7obn7jYvfPgcm583","type":"tool_result","content":"done\n# ASE-81: local development setup\n\nBoth Workers now run together locally on one shared state folder, and the smoke test passed. One snag: on this machine port 8787 belongs to an unrelated `bun` process (pid 713), so the smoke ran the API on 8788. I left that process alone.\n\n**Commit:** `e71c820` feat(pipeline): run both Workers locally on one shared state folder, on `feat/cloudflare-migration` in the main checkout, not pushed. ASE-81 is Done in Linear.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Root `.gitignore`:** ignores `.wrangler-state/`.\n- **`pipeline/vite.config.ts`:**\n  - `persistState` points at `../.wrangler-state`, the folder the API's `wrangler dev --persist-to` and `common`'s `migrate:local` already used.\n  - The dev server is fixed at port 5173.\n  - The local bucket gets dummy S3 credentials, only under `vite dev`. A first version also wrote them into the built `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`; now the deploy config carries none, which I checked after a build.\n- **`pipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs` and `pnpm dev:proxy`:**\n  - It listens on 8792 and forwards to 5173, rewriting `/s3/<bucket>/<key>` to `/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/<bucket>/<key>` with `Host: localhost:5173`.\n  - Every other path passes through unchanged.\n- **`pipeline/.dev.vars.example` and `api/.dev.vars.example`:**\n  - They name every secret with an empty value.\n  - Both point `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` at `http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3` and carry the dummy R2 keys. Those keys protect nothing, so they are written out in full.\n  - The pipeline file has a placeholder for `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` and points the Modal URLs at the dev copy.\n- **The real `.dev.vars` files** were filled by script, without printing any value:\n  - `pipeline/.dev.vars`: the secrets copied from `api/.env` and `modal-proxy.env`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` kept, the dummy R2 keys and the dev Modal URLs.\n  - `api/.dev.vars`: a freshly generated `API_KEY` and the dummy R2 keys.\n  - `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` is back to the placeholder, because the tunnel I used is gone.\n\n## Launch steps, as they work now\n\n1. `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`.\n2. `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`.\n3. `cloudflared tunnel --no-autoupdate --url http://localhost:8792`, then put `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<host>.trycloudflare.com/s3` in `pipeline/.dev.vars`.\n4. `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/` (vite, port 5173). Do this after step 3, so the server reads the tunnel's hostname from `.dev.vars` at startup.\n5. `pnpm dev` in `api/` (port 8787, or `pnpm dev --port 8788` when 8787 is taken, as here).\n6. `uv run modal serve app.py` in `tts/`, which serves the dev copy at `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run`.\n\n## Smoke results\n\n- `GET /health` answered 200 `ok`, and a request without the key answered 401.\n- `POST /items` with `https://smoke.invalid/post` answered 202 and wrote a queued row.\n- The Workflow instance ran in the pipeline dev server:\n  - The shared D1 row got `workflow_instance_id`, `extraction_domain = smoke.invalid` and `current_step = fetch`.\n  - It then failed in fetch with \"firecrawl returned no HTML\", as expected for an invalid domain.\n  - This made real Firecrawl calls for the invalid domain, which may have spent a credit.\n- **Storage path:**\n  - A PUT signed for the local endpoint and sent through the tunnel and proxy answered 200.\n  - A GET signed the way the API signs answered 200 with matching bytes; a bad signature answered 403.\n  - The API's image route answered 307 to `http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/nagara/images/…`. So a browser can follow the 307, as long as the pipeline dev server is running.\n- **Modal dev endpoint:** `GET /result` with the proxy keys answered 422 for a bad call id, and 401 without them.\n- **Cleanup:**\n  - I stopped every process I started by its PID (proxy, tunnel, both dev servers, `modal serve`); the ports are free.\n  - I stopped the ephemeral app `ap-kedXg9q8ZX8VSa33mg66p9`; the deployed `nagara-tts` is untouched.\n  - I deleted the smoke row and the test objects from the local state.\n- **Checks:** pipeline lint and types pass, api lint passes, and `vite build` works.\n\n## Drift against `local-development.md`\n\n- **How the API reads audio:** the note says the API \"reads the audio through its own R2 binding\". The API has no R2 binding; it signs GET URLs against `R2_S3_ENDPOINT`. Locally that endpoint is the pipeline dev server's S3 endpoint, so audio and images are readable only while the pipeline dev server runs.\n- **Missing details in the launch steps:**\n  - The proxy's port (8792).\n  - The `--no-autoupdate` flag on the tunnel.\n  - That the pipeline must start after `.dev.vars` names the tunnel.\n  - That `tts/` runs `modal serve` for the dev Modal URLs. The note says local development calls the same Modal app production uses.\n- **Where the S3 credentials live:** the note does not mention the dummy credentials or that both Workers' R2 keys must match them.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bead6682-f938-4239-9872-28d26ecab9a8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:20:17.131Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\n# ASE-81: local development setup\n\nBoth Workers now run together locally on one shared state folder, and the smoke test passed. One snag: on this machine port 8787 belongs to an unrelated `bun` process (pid 713), so the smoke ran the API on 8788. I left that process alone.\n\n**Commit:** `e71c820` feat(pipeline): run both Workers locally on one shared state folder, on `feat/cloudflare-migration` in the main checkout, not pushed. ASE-81 is Done in Linear.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Root `.gitignore`:** ignores `.wrangler-state/`.\n- **`pipeline/vite.config.ts`:**\n  - `persistState` points at `../.wrangler-state`, the folder the API's `wrangler dev --persist-to` and `common`'s `migrate:local` already used.\n  - The dev server is fixed at port 5173.\n  - The local bucket gets dummy S3 credentials, only under `vite dev`. A first version also wrote them into the built `dist/nagara/wrangler.json`; now the deploy config carries none, which I checked after a build.\n- **`pipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs` and `pnpm dev:proxy`:**\n  - It listens on 8792 and forwards to 5173, rewriting `/s3/<bucket>/<key>` to `/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/<bucket>/<key>` with `Host: localhost:5173`.\n  - Every other path passes through unchanged.\n- **`pipeline/.dev.vars.example` and `api/.dev.vars.example`:**\n  - They name every secret with an empty value.\n  - Both point `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` at `http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3` and carry the dummy R2 keys. Those keys protect nothing, so they are written out in full.\n  - The pipeline file has a placeholder for `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` and points the Modal URLs at the dev copy.\n- **The real `.dev.vars` files** were filled by script, without printing any value:\n  - `pipeline/.dev.vars`: the secrets copied from `api/.env` and `modal-proxy.env`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` kept, the dummy R2 keys and the dev Modal URLs.\n  - `api/.dev.vars`: a freshly generated `API_KEY` and the dummy R2 keys.\n  - `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` is back to the placeholder, because the tunnel I used is gone.\n\n## Launch steps, as they work now\n\n1. `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`.\n2. `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/`.\n3. `cloudflared tunnel --no-autoupdate --url http://localhost:8792`, then put `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<host>.trycloudflare.com/s3` in `pipeline/.dev.vars`.\n4. `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/` (vite, port 5173). Do this after step 3, so the server reads the tunnel's hostname from `.dev.vars` at startup.\n5. `pnpm dev` in `api/` (port 8787, or `pnpm dev --port 8788` when 8787 is taken, as here).\n6. `uv run modal serve app.py` in `tts/`, which serves the dev copy at `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run`.\n\n## Smoke results\n\n- `GET /health` answered 200 `ok`, and a request without the key answered 401.\n- `POST /items` with `https://smoke.invalid/post` answered 202 and wrote a queued row.\n- The Workflow instance ran in the pipeline dev server:\n  - The shared D1 row got `workflow_instance_id`, `extraction_domain = smoke.invalid` and `current_step = fetch`.\n  - It then failed in fetch with \"firecrawl returned no HTML\", as expected for an invalid domain.\n  - This made real Firecrawl calls for the invalid domain, which may have spent a credit.\n- **Storage path:**\n  - A PUT signed for the local endpoint and sent through the tunnel and proxy answered 200.\n  - A GET signed the way the API signs answered 200 with matching bytes; a bad signature answered 403.\n  - The API's image route answered 307 to `http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3/nagara/images/…`. So a browser can follow the 307, as long as the pipeline dev server is running.\n- **Modal dev endpoint:** `GET /result` with the proxy keys answered 422 for a bad call id, and 401 without them.\n- **Cleanup:**\n  - I stopped every process I started by its PID (proxy, tunnel, both dev servers, `modal serve`); the ports are free.\n  - I stopped the ephemeral app `ap-kedXg9q8ZX8VSa33mg66p9`; the deployed `nagara-tts` is untouched.\n  - I deleted the smoke row and the test objects from the local state.\n- **Checks:** pipeline lint and types pass, api lint passes, and `vite build` works.\n\n## Drift against `local-development.md`\n\n- **How the API reads audio:** the note says the API \"reads the audio through its own R2 binding\". The API has no R2 binding; it signs GET URLs against `R2_S3_ENDPOINT`. Locally that endpoint is the pipeline dev server's S3 endpoint, so audio and images are readable only while the pipeline dev server runs.\n- **Missing details in the launch steps:**\n  - The proxy's port (8792).\n  - The `--no-autoupdate` flag on the tunnel.\n  - That the pipeline must start after `.dev.vars` names the tunnel.\n  - That `tts/` runs `modal serve` for the dev Modal URLs. The note says local development calls the same Modal app production uses.\n- **Where the S3 credentials live:** the note does not mention the dummy credentials or that both Workers' R2 keys must match them.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9e57f0fe-3e55-42af-9d49-e654d28d88a7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/pipeline/src","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/pipeline/src","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2a3d3d0-a62e-425d-8666-093351517600","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/pipeline/src","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
