{"parentUuid":"5984c935-9297-49ca-ae32-47232f20379b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvbtKr2uc6MS2d9w99pG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014BZCsPyxHc3sboPDnD7vvP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w46:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Next task, in the main checkout on feat/cloudflare-migration (HEAD f93b0c1; I moved the API's local dev port to 8788 because 8787 belongs to a herdr plugin, so use 8788 from now on). The user settled these from your review:\n1. The fake agent must not reach production code. Remove \\`scriptedAgentReplies\\` from \\`pipeline/src/\\` and from the deployed config; the tests get the fake agent through test-only code wired in the vitest config (for example a test-only Worker entry, or a test module the pool substitutes), never through a branch or setting the production bundle carries. Check after a build that \\`dist/\\` contains no trace of it.\n2. The HTML cap measures what the step actually returns: compare the serialized size of the fetch step's result against the cap, not the raw HTML bytes, so a page near 1 MiB fails cleanly in fetch with its own error instead of erroring inside the Workflow. Add or adjust the test.\n3. In \\`firecrawl/client.ts\\`, drop the claim that an auto proxy escalation bills 5 credits; the ledger records the response's creditsUsed. (I fix the doc sentence myself.)\nLeave everything else from the review as it is (Modal 500 retry, Firecrawl retries, rerun ledger rows are accepted). Run pipeline test, lint, types and build; commit as fits; report commits and checks in your final message. Do not start dev servers yet.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Send the code fixes to the pipeline subagent"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens