{"parentUuid":"b498eb15-0ceb-4b4b-ade8-e3e8b4f4e191","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvbu8b8qzSK53gtG7si4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WdjZTpHTKjNEgsTM5w8GG8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs; cat > docs-reconcile.md <<'EOF'\n# Docs reconciliation for the Cloudflare migration implementation\n\nRun `/mahou:write-documentation` in the main checkout `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` (branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`), once, with every amendment below together, weighing the whole `docs/` folder. The user has already approved applying these, so after the unslop and documentation-reviewer passes, write the edits into the notes directly instead of waiting in the chat; do not commit. Touch only `docs/` and, where it repeats a changed fact, the root `CLAUDE.md`. Never print secrets. Never run `rm -rf`.\n\nThe code is the source of truth; read it where a detail matters (`api/src`, `pipeline/src`, `tts/app.py`, `.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml`, `pipeline/vite.config.ts`, `pipeline/scripts/tunnel-proxy.mjs`, the `.dev.vars.example` files). Reports with more detail: `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/` (`impl-api.md`, `impl-ASE-81.md`, `impl-ci.md`, `review-*.md`).\n\n## Amendments\n\n1. **The Workflow instance id is the item id.** Enqueue creates the instance with `id: itemId`. On a re-queue or a retry, when the row holds no instance id the API creates the instance with the item id, and a create that reports the instance already exists becomes a restart of that instance from the restart point. (item-lifecycle: Enqueue, Poll/re-queue, Retry, the `workflow_instance_id` row; item-contract: the GET and retry route rows and the Retry section.)\n2. **A restart that throws after a claim.** On a retry, the item is written back to `failed` with the error, the retry stays counted, and the route answers 202 with the failed item. On a re-queue, the error is logged and the poll answers the item as it is; the next stale poll 15 minutes later tries again. (item-lifecycle, item-contract.)\n3. **The API Worker has no R2 binding.** It only signs GET URLs, with an R2 API token's S3 key pair against `R2_S3_ENDPOINT`; signing a URL needs no binding, and the API never reads or writes bytes. Fix every note that says both Workers bind the bucket (persistence-and-storage, deployment-and-ci, local-development, and any other).\n4. **Step retries:** each step has 3 attempts (`retries.limit: 2`). Check the notes state attempts consistently.\n5. **The HTML cap measures the fetch step's serialized result**, not the raw HTML: a step result is capped near 1 MiB by Cloudflare, and the result is the JSON-serialized `{html, domain}`. (item-lifecycle failure bullets, limits paragraph.)\n6. **CI:** the pipeline deploys when `pipeline/` changed or the migration ran; the API deploys when `api/` changed or the migration ran, after the pipeline deploy when that one runs. A pipeline-only push deploys only the pipeline. The cross-script binding resolves the pipeline by script name at run time, so the API needs no redeploy for it. (deployment-and-ci, and the root CLAUDE.md CI paragraph if it says otherwise.)\n7. **Local development**, as it now works (read `pipeline/vite.config.ts`, `tunnel-proxy.mjs`, the dev scripts):\n   - launch order: `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/`; `pnpm dev:proxy` in `pipeline/` (port 8792); `cloudflared tunnel --no-autoupdate --url http://localhost:8792` and `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://<host>/s3` into `pipeline/.dev.vars`; then `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/` (port 5173; it reads the tunnel host at startup, so it starts after the tunnel); `pnpm dev` in `api/` (port 8788); `uv run modal serve app.py` in `tts/`.\n   - locally the Workers call an ephemeral `modal serve` copy of the TTS app, not the deployed one; the note now says the same Modal app production uses: fix it.\n   - the local bucket carries dummy S3 credentials under vite dev only, and both Workers' local R2 keys are those dummy values; the deployed config carries none.\n   - the API's presigned GETs point at the pipeline dev server's local S3 endpoint, so audio and image links work only while the pipeline dev server runs. Replace \"the API reads the audio through its own R2 binding\".\n   - `.dev.vars.example` in each Worker names the secrets.\n8. **Firecrawl billing:** drop the claim in article-extraction (or wherever) that an `auto` proxy escalation bills 5 credits; the ledger records the `creditsUsed` the response reports.\n9. **Images:** a relative image `src` is resolved against the item's URL; SVG sanitizing strips `<script>` and `on*` event-handler attributes. (article-extraction.)\n10. **Recipe agents giving up** fails the item at once, like a not-article verdict, without retrying the step, so the agents' own retry bound holds. Check recipes.md and item-lifecycle agree.\n11. **tts result endpoint:** the done answer is `{format, duration, timings[{start, end}]}`; 410 and 422 answer `{error}`; an id that is not a call id answers 422. Check tts-service against `tts/app.py`.\n\nWhen done, end with a report: per note, the sections changed, and any amendment you could not land or that the code contradicts.\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"docs: reconcile migration notes\" --model opus --body \"<supervisor-agent>Read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/docs-reconcile.md. It is your full brief.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Spawn the docs reconciliation subagent"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":227172,"output_tokens":3057,"output_toke