{"parentUuid":"590db69b-0536-4e3c-b5f6-95fc44012c5a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- terminal-browser: A real browser running inside the terminal. It splits the human's terminal pane automatically, so you can show a website side by side with the conversation, render HTML to visualize something, and drive whatever tab is open — snapshot, click, fill, eval — with the `terminal-browser action` subcommand.\n- superpowers:mermaid: Loaded to choose, write, style and validate mermaid diagrams (flowcharts, sequence, state, ER and class diagrams). Carries a chart-selection table, one reference per chart type with a default shape and colour palette, the common syntax rules, a bundled validator and the rendering rules the validator cannot catch. Use whenever you generate, write or edit a mermaid code block, and validate every diagram before showing it, even one that looks correct.\n- mahou:test-design-with-canvas: Runs the test-design skill on a canvas instead of in the chat. The candidate roots are drawn on a map of the system for the user to pick, and each branch is drawn as a classification tree with its combination matrix under it; the user corrects with sticky notes or by voice. Use when the user wants to design the test cases and manual validations of a settled change on a canvas.","skillCount":3,"isInitial":false,"names":["terminal-browser","superpowers:mermaid","mahou:test-design-with-canvas"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"68351bb3-921d-4baa-85d5-c4c7f60edcb6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:07.295Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- terminal-browser: A real browser running inside the terminal. It splits the human's terminal pane automatically, so you can show a website side by side with the conversation, render HTML to visualize something, and drive whatever tab is open — snapshot, click, fill, eval — with the `terminal-browser action` subcommand.\n- superpowers:mermaid: Loaded to choose, write, style and validate mermaid diagrams (flowcharts, sequence, state, ER and class diagrams). Carries a chart-selection table, one reference per chart type with a default shape and colour palette, the common syntax rules, a bundled validator and the rendering rules the validator cannot catch. Use whenever you generate, write or edit a mermaid code block, and validate every diagram before showing it, even one that looks correct.\n- mahou:test-design-with-canvas: Runs the test-design skill on a canvas instead of in the chat. The candidate roots are drawn on a map of the system for the user to pick, and each branch is drawn as a classification tree with its combination matrix under it; the user corrects with sticky notes or by voice. Use when the user wants to design the test cases and manual validations of a settled change on a canvas.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
