:"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"28a38391-bf4e-4ea7-a1a8-b553a3ea54fb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:03.026Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"28a38391-bf4e-4ea7-a1a8-b553a3ea54fb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9185824c-72c2-4513-9524-1b50125adfd3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PjVrPcAXHHkPiWABGemZP9","type":"tool_result","content":"done\nAll three changes are committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration` in the main checkout, not pushed, and pipeline test, lint, types and build pass. I started no dev servers.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `236fe51` | refactor(pipeline): keep the scripted agent out of the production bundle |\n| `ae717a6` | fix(pipeline): cap the fetch step's result as it is serialized |\n| `55b7256` | fix(pipeline): drop the stealth-escalation billing claim from the Firecrawl client |\n\n## What changed\n\n1. **The fake agent is out of production code.**\n   - `src/agents/conversation.ts` now only calls the Flue agents (dispatch, then read).\n   - The `scriptedAgentReplies` setting is gone from the code, from `worker-configuration.d.ts` and from the vitest bindings.\n   - A plugin in `vitest.config.ts` redirects every import of `src/agents/conversation.ts` to `test/helpers/scripted-agents.ts`. That test module answers with whatever reply a test sets through `scriptAgents()`, and gives up when none is set.\n   - The redirect reaches the Workflow: the authoring and revision rows (C7, C8) only pass with the scripted replies.\n   - After `pnpm build`, a search of `dist/` for the setting name, the module name, `scriptAgents` and the default reply text found nothing.\n2. **The HTML cap measures what the fetch step returns.** It compares the byte size of the serialized `{ html, domain }`, escaping included, against `maxHtmlBytes`. The new error is \"the fetched page serializes to N bytes, over the 1048576-byte cap\".\n   - **C3 test:** its page is about 600 KB of quote characters, so it is under the cap in raw bytes (the test asserts this) and over it once serialized. The item fails at once in fetch with that error and one Firecrawl ledger row.\n3. **`firecrawl/client.ts`:** the comment no longer claims an auto escalation bills 5 credits; it says a scrape bills the response's `creditsUsed`.\n\n## Checks (pipeline/)\n\n```\npnpm test   Test Files 13 passed (13) · Tests 120 passed | 1 skipped (121)\npnpm lint   Checked 78 files. No fixes applied.\npnpm types  exit 0\npnpm build  ✓ built; no trace of the scripted agent in dist/\n```\n\n## Not mine\n\nFour files under `docs/technical-design/` are modified in the working tree (`deployment-and-ci.md`, `item-contract.md`, `item-lifecycle.md`, `persistence-and-storage.md`). I left them unstaged and untouched.\n55b7256 fix(pipeline): drop the stealth-escalation billing claim from the Firecrawl client\nae717a6 fix(pipeline): cap the fetch step's result as it is serialized\n236fe51 refactor(pipeline): keep the scripted agent out of the production bundle\nf93b0c1 chore(api): serve the local dev server on port 8788\n M docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-contract.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md\n M docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2e222de9-ff25-403a-88d5-320e18d76f26","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:03.900Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\nAll three changes are committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration` in the main checkout, not pushed, and pipeline test, lint, types and build pass. I started no dev servers.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `236fe51` | refactor(pipeline): keep the scripted agent out of the production bundle |\n| `ae717a6` | fix(pipeline): cap the fetch step's result as it is serialized |\n| `55b7256` | fix(pipeline): drop the stealth-escalation billing claim from the Firecrawl client |\n\n## What changed\n\n1. **The fake agent is out of production code.**\n   - `src/agents/conversation.ts` now only calls the Flue agents (dispatch, then read).\n   - The `scriptedAgentReplies` setting is gone from the code, from `worker-configuration.d.ts` and from the vitest bindings.\n   - A plugin in `vitest.config.ts` redirects every import of `src/agents/conversation.ts` to `test/helpers/scripted-agents.ts`. That test module answers with whatever reply a test sets through `scriptAgents()`, and gives up when none is set.\n   - The redirect reaches the Workflow: the authoring and revision rows (C7, C8) only pass with the scripted replies.\n   - After `pnpm build`, a search of `dist/` for the setting name, the module name, `scriptAgents` and the default reply text found nothing.\n2. **The HTML cap measures what the fetch step returns.** It compares the byte size of the serialized `{ html, domain }`, escaping included, against `maxHtmlBytes`. The new error is \"the fetched page serializes to N bytes, over the 1048576-byte cap\".\n   - **C3 test:** its page is about 600 KB of quote characters, so it is under the cap in raw bytes (the test asserts this) and over it once serialized. The item fails at once in fetch with that error and one Firecrawl ledger row.\n3. **`firecrawl/client.ts`:** the comment no longer claims an auto escalation bills 5 credits; it says a scrape bills the response's `creditsUsed`.\n\n## Checks (pipeline/)\n\n```\npnpm test   Test Files 13 passed (13) · Tests 120 passed | 1 skipped (121)\npnpm lint   Checked 78 files. No fixes applied.\npnpm types  exit 0\npnpm build  ✓ built; no trace of the scripted agent in dist/\n```\n\n## Not mine\n\nFour files under `docs/technical-design/` are modified in the working tree (`deployment-and-ci.md`, `item-contract.md`, `item-lifecycle.md`, `persistence-and-storage.md`). I left them unstaged and untouched.\n55b7256 fix(pipeline): drop the stealth-escalation billing claim from the Firecrawl client\nae717a6 fix(pipeline): cap the fetch step's result as it is serialized\n236fe51 refactor(pipeline): keep the scripted agent out of the production bundle\nf93b0c1 chore(api): serve the local dev server on port 8788\n M docs/technical-design/deploym