{"parentUuid":"8a9cf513-ec0b-403d-9cc0-9242d4f76f7b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14987986 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"70c676f2-47db-4610-92a4-79ff414fa267","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:09.356Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14987986 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"70c676f2-47db-4610-92a4-79ff414fa267","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvc6cWyJBZRCS2y5zj4g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SkQhkhpJPhBc8DFKXY362t","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; { cat <<'EOF'\n# Manual validation, run locally (tomorrow's deploy repeats the \"deployed\" ones)\n\nLoad `/mahou:validate` and run the manual rows below through it against the **local** system, in the main checkout `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` on `feat/cloudflare-migration` (HEAD 55b7256 or later). Produce the report artifact `validate` requires, under `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/`. Fix nothing during validation: a failure comes back as a finding, with the evidence. Same safety rules as your pipeline brief (never print secrets, never deploy, stop only your own PIDs, no `rm -rf`). Do not edit `docs/` (another subagent is editing it right now).\n\n## Setup\n\nBring up the local system as `e71c820` set it up, with the API on **port 8788** (8787 belongs to a herdr plugin):\n1. A **fresh** shared state folder: move the current `.wrangler-state/` aside to `/tmp/nagara-wrangler-state-old-<timestamp>` (no deletion), then `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/` (D5's \"fresh local state folder\").\n2. `pnpm dev:proxy`, the quick tunnel, `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` into `pipeline/.dev.vars` by script, `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`, `pnpm dev` in `api/`, `uv run modal serve app.py` in `tts/`. Record every PID. Read the API key from `api/.dev.vars` by script; never print it.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- **Small articles only**: short blog posts or docs pages, a few paragraphs each. Pick real public pages that fit each row (C1: an article with code and images, ideally an SVG; C5: two short articles of the same site enqueued together; C7: an article from a domain with no recipe yet, which on a fresh state is every domain, so the first item of any domain covers it; C9: a site's home page; C11: an article with a broken image, or with a tiny avatar; if no real page has a 404 image, say so and record C11 as partially covered rather than inventing a page). Stay within about 10 real items in total; reuse items across rows (the C7 item can be the D1 item, D20 and D5 read any ready item, D21 needs an item still generating).\n- **D4**: stop the pipeline dev server (by PID), enqueue, see the failed item, start the pipeline again (and the tunnel host still matches `.dev.vars`), retry it to ready.\n- **D13**: a failed item retried reaches ready. If no item fails naturally, make one fail in a later step without code changes (for example stop `modal serve` while an item synthesizes, let it fail, start it again and retry), and say how.\n- **D16**: a fourth retry of a failed item answers 409. Reaching 3 retries cheaply: an item that fails fast (D4-style with the pipeline stopped, or a URL that fails in fetch) retried until the cap.\n- **D20**: open the audio URL in a real browser (`agent-browser` is available) in an audio element, play and seek, and check it works. **Also save one ready item's audio to `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/listen-<id>.ogg` and the item's display text next to it, so the user can listen to it** (the project's \"you have to listen to it\" rule; you cannot hear it).\n- **B1** locally: the audio lands in the local bucket (through the tunnel) and plays. **D25** locally: a poll without the key answers 401.\n- For every ready item, also check the \"seeing it work\" rule from CLAUDE.md: the title and the first units are the actual article, not an error page.\n\n## Rows\n\nEOF\ngrep -E \"^\\| (B1|C1|C5|C7|C9|C11|D1|D4|D5|D13|D16|D20|D21|D25) \" test-design/nagara.md\ncat <<'EOF'\n\n## Ending\n\nStop everything you started by PID, stop the ephemeral Modal app (`modal app list`, then `modal app stop` on its id), set `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` back to the placeholder. Leave the new `.wrangler-state/` in place. Final message: per row, pass/fail/partial with the evidence in one line, the report artifact path, the listen file path, the real URLs used, and every finding.\nEOF\n} > briefs/validate.md; wc -l briefs/validate.md\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w46:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Next task: read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/validate.md.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Write the validation brief and dispatch it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1813,"cache_read_input_tokens":234380,"output_tokens":1907,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1813,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1907,"cache_read_input_tokens":234380,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1813},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SkQhkhpJPhBc8DFKXY362t":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration; { cat <<'EOF'\n# Manual validation, run locally (tomorrow's deploy repeats the \"deployed\" ones)\n\nLoad `/mahou:validate` and run the manual rows below through it against the **local** system, in the main checkout `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` on `feat/cloudflare-migration` (HEAD 55b7256 or later). Produce the report artifact `validate` requires, under `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/`. Fix nothing during validation: a failure comes back as a finding, with the evidence. Same safety rules as your pipeline brief (never print secrets, never deploy, stop only your own PIDs, no `rm -rf`). Do not edit `docs/` (another subagent is editing it right now).\n\n## Setup\n\nBring up the local system as `e71c820` set it up, with the API on **port 8788** (8787 belongs to a herdr plugin):\n1. A **fresh** shared state folder: move the current `.wrangler-state/` aside to `/tmp/nagara-wrangler-state-old-<timestamp>` (no deletion), then `pnpm migrate:local` in `common/` (D5's \"fresh local state folder\").\n2. `pnpm dev:proxy`, the quick tunnel, `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` into `pipeline/.dev.vars` by script, `pnpm dev` in `pipeline/`, `pnpm dev` in `api/`, `uv run modal serve app.py` in `tts/`. Record every PID. Read the API key from `api/.dev.vars` by script; never print it.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- **Small articles only**: short blog posts or docs pages, a few paragraphs each. Pick real public pages that fit each row (C1: an article with code and images, ideally an SVG; C5: two short articles of the same site enqueued together; C7: an article from a domain with no recipe yet, which on a fresh state is every domain, so the first item of any domain covers it; C9: a site's home page; C11: an article with a broken image, or with a tiny avatar; if no real page has a 404 image, say so and record C11 as partially covered rather than inventing a page). Stay within about 10 real items in total; reuse items across rows (the C7 item can be the D1 item, D20 and D5 read any ready item, D21 needs an item still generating).\n- **D4**: stop the pipeline dev server (by PID), enqueue, see the failed item, start the pipeline again (and the tunnel host still matches `.dev.vars`), retry it to ready.\n- **D13**: a failed item retried reaches ready. If no item fails naturally, make one fail in a later step without code changes (for example stop `modal serve` while an item synthesizes, let it fail, start it again and retry), and say how.\n- **D16**: a fourth retry of a failed item answers 409. Reaching 3 retries cheaply: an item that fails fast (D4-style with the pipeline stopped, or a URL that fails in fetch) retried until the cap.\n- **D20**: open the audio URL in a real browser (`agent-browser` is available) in an audio element, play and seek, and check it works. **Also save one ready item's audio to `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/listen-<id>.ogg` and the item's display text next to it, so the user can listen to it** (the project's \"you have to listen to it\" rule; you cannot hear it).\n- **B1** locally: the audio lands in the local bucket (through the tunnel) and plays. **D25** locally: a poll without the key answers 401.\n- For every ready item, also check the \"seeing it work\" rule from CLAUDE.md: the title and the first units are the actual article, not an error page.\n\n## Rows\n\nEOF\ngrep -E \"^\\| (B1|C1|C5|C7|C9|C11|D1|D4|D5|D13|D16|D20|D21|D25) \" test-design/nagara.md\ncat <<'EOF'\n\n## Ending\n\nStop everything you started by PID, stop the ephemeral Modal app (`modal app list`, then `modal app stop` on its id), set `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` back to the placeholder. Leave the new `.wrangler-state/` in place. Final message: per row, pass/fail/partial with the evidence in one line, the report artifact path, the listen file path, the real URLs used, and every finding.\nEOF\n} > briefs/validate.md; wc -l briefs/validate.md\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w46:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Next task: read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/validate.md.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Write the validation brief and dispatch it"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b6ae7193-7065-4e5c-b2e6-11cb9bde2dc3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfvc6bvk2ptpnpcNFiccg","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9f187ccd-8c65-4c06-8679-4a01e79c15b4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:26.519Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
