{"parentUuid":"2362dffc-6cbf-4e07-9a3f-2e3d6f454adf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d41bf66b-27aa-4bab-8364-f3e0c9a5217f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XwDLQNMYAC5cN5XHK3cqfe","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"pane_id\":\"w30:p2Y\",\"sent\":true,\"status\":\"working\"}\nAll eleven amendments are written into the notes under `docs/technical-design/`. Nothing is committed, and the root `CLAUDE.md` is unchanged because nothing in it contradicts the code. The changed diagrams pass the mermaid validator. The documentation-reviewer flagged seven things; I applied five and skipped two (both explained at the end).\n\n**`item-lifecycle.md`**\n- **Modeling table:** the `workflow_instance_id` row says the instance id is the item id, and that the field is empty until the first step runs, even when the instance already exists (amendment 1).\n- **States:**\n  - The diagram's failure labels now include a page over the cap and the agents giving up.\n  - Enqueue creates the instance with `id` set to the item id.\n  - Poll: when the row has no instance id, the API creates the instance; if the create reports it already exists, it restarts it instead. If that throws, the API logs the error, answers the item as it is, and the next stale poll 15 minutes later tries again (amendments 1 and 2).\n  - A new `[!NOTE]` explains why a create can turn into a restart.\n- **The item Workflow's steps:** \"Each step has 3 attempts, the first and two retries\" (amendment 4).\n- **The step wrapper:** the agents giving up fails the recipe step at once, and a page over the cap fails the fetch step the same way (amendments 5 and 10).\n- **Retry:**\n  - Create-or-restart now points back to States instead of repeating it.\n  - A new paragraph covers a restart that throws after the claim: the item is written back to `failed` with the error, the route answers 202 with it, and the retry stays counted (amendment 2).\n- **What a failure names:** a new \"The agents give up\" bullet. \"HTML over the cap\" now measures the fetch step's serialized `{html, domain}` result and fails without retrying.\n- **Platform limits:** the cap applies to the serialized result.\n\n**`item-contract.md`**\n- **What each route does:** the GET row covers create-with-item-id and the logged failure. The retry row adds \"or with the item `failed` again when the restart throws\".\n- **Retry section:** create-with-item-id, plus a new paragraph on the 202 with a failed item (amendments 1 and 2).\n\n**`persistence-and-storage.md`** (amendment 3)\n- **Overview** and **Architecture prose:** both Workers bind D1, and only the pipeline binds the bucket. The API Worker signs GET URLs with an R2 token's S3 key pair against the S3 endpoint.\n- **Architecture:** a new `[!NOTE]` \"Why the API Worker binds no bucket\".\n- **Local paragraph:** the API signs for the local S3 endpoint.\n\n**`deployment-and-ci.md`**\n- **How the Workers deploy:** only the pipeline binds the bucket (amendment 3). The migrations-pipeline-API callout adds that the binding finds the pipeline by script name when called, so a pipeline deploy needs no API redeploy.\n- **Secrets table:** the API row says \"an R2 API token's S3 key pair\".\n- **CI:**\n  - The diagram nodes and the prose carry each job's condition: migrate when `common/` changed; the pipeline when `pipeline/` changed or the migration ran; the API when `api/` changed or the migration ran, after the pipeline deploy when that one runs.\n  - A push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys only the pipeline (amendment 6).\n\n**`local-development.md`** (amendment 7)\n- **Overview:** the Workers call an ephemeral `modal serve` copy of the TTS app.\n- **How to run:**\n  - Each Worker's `.dev.vars.example` names its secrets.\n  - The new order is: migrate, proxy on 8792, `cloudflared tunnel --no-autoupdate`, the pipeline on 5173 (it starts after the tunnel), the API on 8788, then `uv run modal serve app.py`.\n- **Architecture:** a new API → local S3 edge, and the Modal node is labelled as the serve copy.\n- **Modal upload:** the sentence about \"its own R2 binding\" is replaced. The API signs GET URLs for the pipeline dev server's S3 endpoint, so links work only while that server runs. The dummy S3 credentials are added under vite dev only, and the deployed config carries none.\n\n**`article-extraction.md`**\n- **Firecrawl callout:** the 1-or-5-credit claim is replaced by \"the ledger records the response's `creditsUsed`\" (amendment 8).\n- **Acquisition:**\n  - A relative `src` resolves against the item's URL, and a `data:` URI is decoded in place.\n  - SVG stripping names `<script>` and `on*` attributes, with a new `[!NOTE]` on why (amendment 9).\n- **Corrupted text:** I fixed a `\\1` left in the raster-floor sentence by an earlier bad edit, restoring \"measured on the decoded file.\"\n\n**`recipes.md`**: the revision paragraph says an authoring or revision run that gives up fails the item at once, like a not-article verdict, without retrying the recipe step (amendment 10).\n\n**`tts-service.md`**: the result endpoint row gives each status's body, and the local-development sentence names the `modal serve` copy (amendment 11).\n\n**`technical-design/README.md`**: the local-development row names the `modal serve` copy.\n\n**Where the code differs from the brief**\n- **Amendment 11:** the brief says an id that is not a call id answers 422 with `{error}`, but it doesn't. `tts/app.py` rejects it through FastAPI's query `pattern=r\"^fc-\"`, so the 422 body is FastAPI's validation `{detail: [...]}`. Only an unknown `fc-` id answers 422 with `{error}`. The note now states both cases.\n- **CI comment:** the header comment of `.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml` (lines 10–11) still says a deploy runs \"when its own tree changed or the deploy before it ran\". The job conditions say \"or the migration ran\". The notes follow the conditions; I didn't touch the YAML because the brief limits me to `docs/` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n**Reviewer findings skipped**\n- **The `.dev.vars.example` pointer:** it is kept because it tells the reader where the secrets are listed.\n- **CI conditions in both the diagram and the prose:** they are kept because the charter places a diagram beside the prose it illustrates.\n\nFiles are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/`:\n- `reports/docs-reconcile-review.md`\n- `reports/docs-reconcile.diff`\n- `briefs/docs-review-brief.md`\n\nThe diff was taken before the reviewer's fixes, so it is not the final change; `git diff -- docs` shows the full set.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"10feabdb-a497-4b9d-9b11-4a45cce14b31","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:29:48.868Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"pane_id\":\"w30:p2Y\",\"sent\":true,\"status\":\"working\"}\nAll eleven amendments are written into the notes under `docs/technical-design/`. Nothing is committed, and the root `CLAUDE.md` is unchanged because nothing in it contradicts the code. The changed diagrams pass the mermaid validator. The documentation-reviewer flagged seven things; I applied five and skipped two (both explained at the end).\n\n**`item-lifecycle.md`**\n- **Modeling table:** the `workflow_instance_id` row says the instance id is the item id, and that the field is empty until the first step runs, even when the instance already exists (amendment 1).\n- **States:**\n  - The diagram's failure labels now include a page over the cap and the agents giving up.\n  - Enqueue creates the instance with `id` set to the item id.\n  - Poll: when the row has no instance id, the API creates the instance; if the create reports it already exists, it restarts it instead. If that throws, the API logs the error, answers the item as it is, and the next stale poll 15 minutes later tries again (amendments 1 and 2).\n  - A new `[!NOTE]` explains why a create can turn into a restart.\n- **The item Workflow's steps:** \"Each step has 3 attempts, the first and two retries\" (amendment 4).\n- **The step wrapper:** the agents giving up fails the recipe step at once, and a page over the cap fails the fetch step the same way (amendments 5 and 10).\n- **Retry:**\n  - Create-or-restart now points back to States instead of repeating it.\n  - A new paragraph covers a restart that throws after the claim: the item is written back to `failed` with the error, the route answers 202 with it, and the retry stays counted (amendment 2).\n- **What a failure names:** a new \"The agents give up\" bullet. \"HTML over the cap\" now measures the fetch step's serialized `{html, domain}` result and fails without retrying.\n- **Platform limits:** the cap applies to the serialized result.\n\n**`item-contract.md`**\n- **What each route does:** the GET row covers create-with-item-id and the logged failure. The retry row adds \"or with the item `failed` again when the restart throws\".\n- **Retry section:** create-with-item-id, plus a new paragraph on the 202 with a failed item (amendments 1 and 2).\n\n**`persistence-and-storage.md`** (amendment 3)\n- **Overview** and **Architecture prose:** both Workers bind D1, and only the pipeline binds the bucket. The API Worker signs GET URLs with an R2 token's S3 key pair against the S3 endpoint.\n- **Architecture:** a new `[!NOTE]` \"Why the API Worker binds no bucket\".\n- **Local paragraph:** the API signs for the local S3 endpoint.\n\n**`deployment-and-ci.md`**\n- **How the Workers deploy:** only the pipeline binds the bucket (amendment 3). The migrations-pipeline-API callout adds that the binding finds the pipeline by script name when called, so a pipeline deploy needs no API redeploy.\n- **Secrets table:** the API row says \"an R2 API token's S3 key pair\".\n- **CI:**\n  - The diagram nodes and the prose carry each job's condition: migrate when `common/` changed; the pipeline when `pipeline/` changed or the migration ran; the API when `api/` changed or the migration ran, after the pipeline deploy when that one runs.\n  - A push that changes only `pipeline/` deploys only the pipeline (amendment 6).\n\n**`local-development.md`** (amendment 7)\n- **Overview:** the Workers call an ephemeral `modal serve` copy of the TTS app.\n- **How to run:**\n  - Each Worker's `.dev.vars.example` names its secrets.\n  - The new order is: migrate, proxy on 8792, `cloudflared tunnel --no-autoupdate`, the pipeline on 5173 (it starts after the tunnel), the API on 8788, then `uv run modal serve app.py`.\n- **Architecture:** a new API → local S3 edge, and the Modal node is labelled as the serve copy.\n- **Modal upload:** the sentence about \"its own R2 binding\" is replaced. The API signs GET URLs for the pipeline dev server's S3 endpoint, so links work only while that server runs. The dummy S3 credentials are added under vite dev only, and the deployed config carries none.\n\n**`article-extraction.md`**\n- **Firecrawl callout:** the 1-or-5-credit claim is replaced by \"the ledger records the response's `creditsUsed`\" (amendment 8).\n- **Acquisition:**\n  - A relative `src` resolves against the item's URL, and a `data:` URI is decoded in place.\n  - SVG stripping names `<script>` and `on*` attributes, with a new `[!NOTE]` on why (amendment 9).\n- **Corrupted text:** I fixed a `\\1` left in the raster-floor sentence by an earlier bad edit, restoring \"measured on the decoded file.\"\n\n**`recipes.md`**: the revision paragraph says an authoring or revision run that gives up fails the item at once, like a not-article verdict, without retrying the recipe step (amendment 10).\n\n**`tts-service.md`**: the result endpoint row gives each status's body, and the local-development sentence names the `modal serve` copy (amendment 11).\n\n**`technical-design/README.md`**: the local-development row names the `modal serve` copy.\n\n**Where the code differs from the brief**\n- **Amendment 11:** the brief says an id that is not a call id answers 422 with `{error}`, but it doesn't. `tts/app.py` rejects it through FastAPI's query `pattern=r\"^fc-\"`, so the 422 body is FastAPI's validation `{detail: [...]}`. Only an unknown `fc-` id answers 422 with `{error}`. The note now states both cases.\n- **CI comment:** the header comment of `.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml` (lines 10–11) still says a deploy runs \"when its own tree changed or the deploy before it ran\". The job conditions say \"or the migration ran\". The notes follow the conditions; I didn't touch the YAML because the brief limits me to `docs/` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n**Reviewer findings skipped**\n- **The `.dev.vars.example` pointer:** it is kept because it tells the reader where the secrets are listed.\n- **CI conditions in both the diagram and the prose:** they are kept because the charter places a diagram beside the prose it illustrates.\n\nFiles are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/`:\n- `reports/docs-reconcile-review.md`\n- `reports/docs-reconcile.diff`\n- `briefs/docs-review-brief.md`\n\nThe diff was taken before the reviewer's fixes, so it is not the final change; `git diff -- docs` shows the full set.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0bbd8597-f223-4259-967d-5e0d5153521e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":9,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2362dffc-6cbf-4e07-9a3f-2e3d6f454adf","permissi