{"parentUuid":"f06a33d1-ce78-4be8-b8e7-d827d97f59bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvcKB1fUg9hUvRDmUuQt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All eleven doc changes are written across nine notes under `docs/technical-design/`. The subagent ran the unslop and documentation-reviewer checks and applied five of the reviewer's seven findings. The changes are uncommitted; `git diff -- docs` shows them.\n\n- **item-lifecycle and item-contract:** the instance id is the item id. When the instance already exists, a create becomes a restart. A retry whose restart throws goes back to `failed`, and a re-queue logs the error. Every step has 3 attempts. The cap measures the serialized result. Agents that give up fail the item at once.\n- **persistence-and-storage and deployment-and-ci:** only the pipeline binds the bucket; the API signs URLs with an R2 token's S3 key pair. The CI section now states each job's deploy condition.\n- **local-development:** the new launch order and ports (proxy 8792, pipeline 5173, API 8788), the `modal serve` copy, and the dummy S3 credentials. Audio and image links work only while the pipeline dev server runs.\n- **article-extraction:**\n  - the ledger records Firecrawl's `creditsUsed`\n  - relative image `src` values resolve against the item URL\n  - SVG cleaning strips `on*` attributes\n  - a broken `\\1` left by an earlier edit is fixed\n- **recipes:** agents that give up fail the item at once.\n- **tts-service:** each status's body is stated. A malformed call id gets FastAPI's validation body, not `{error}`, which is how the code behaves.\n\nIt also found that the CI workflow's header comment still described the old deploy rule. I corrected it and committed that as `44521c9`.\n\nShould I commit the doc changes as one `docs:` commit? The manual validation is still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":243448,"output_tokens":638,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":57},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":243448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"31aadfb1-eae5-45cb-9b60-198878932c45","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfvcKAacEVdZJmVpt4Aru","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"57c42f4d-e3b1-44e5-8978-5a889df8582d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:06.216Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
