{"parentUuid":"dd11fc56-5658-487b-8f19-df713f2d633d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvcdZvZCWCXyQZ5SS84j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G9u8fSjAyp4dF1moQb8NRH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs; cat > consistency-check.md <<'EOF'\n# Consistency check: code against docs, and leftovers\n\nThe Cloudflare migration of nagara is implemented on `feat/cloudflare-migration` in `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` (HEAD 4101b42 or later). Check the whole repository for leftovers and for inconsistencies between the code and the docs. **Read only: make no edits, no commits.** Another subagent is running a manual validation against local dev servers in this checkout right now, so do not start servers, do not touch `.wrangler-state/`, `.dev.vars` files or running processes. Never print secrets. Never run `rm -rf`.\n\nRead first: the root `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/README.md`, every note under `docs/technical-design/` and `docs/product-design/`, `README.md`. Then sweep the code: `common/`, `api/`, `pipeline/`, `tts/`, `.github/workflows/`, root config files (`package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `.gitignore`, biome and tsconfig files), `.claude/` and `.mahou/` local rules if they describe the code.\n\nLook for:\n1. **Leftovers of what the migration replaced**: the Python API (FastAPI, alembic, Postgres, Railway, `railway.toml`), the extraction service (POST /jobs, GET /jobs, JobIndex, the extraction Workflow, Cloudflare Access, the WORLD_SEAM seam, `CLOUDFLARE_EXTRACTION_URL`), `scriptedAgentReplies`, the old per-tree CI files, old cassettes no test reads (for example under `api/tests/cassettes/`), dead exports, unused dependencies, stale scripts, config keys nothing reads, files no module imports, comments describing removed behaviour.\n2. **Docs that disagree with the code**: every route, status code, body shape, step name, retry count, timeout, cap, binding, var, secret, key layout, migration, CI condition, local-dev step and port that a note states, checked against the code. Also the root `CLAUDE.md` (layout table, commands block, invariants, \"when adding something\") and `README.md`.\n3. **Code that disagrees with itself**: the two Workers' wrangler configs vs `common/wrangler.jsonc` (D1 id, migrations dir, bucket name), the `.dev.vars.example` files vs the secrets the code reads (`env.d.ts`, `worker-configuration.d.ts`), var names used in code vs defined in config, the tts request/response shapes vs what `pipeline/` sends and parses, `common/` types vs what the Workers write.\n4. **Names, comments and tests** that still use the old vocabulary (job, extraction service, Railway) where the thing is now an item, a step or the pipeline Worker.\n\nDo not report style preferences, and do not re-open design decisions the notes record; report only where two things that should agree do not, and things that no longer have a reason to exist.\n\nWrite the findings to `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/consistency-check.md`: one entry per finding with the file and line, what disagrees with what (quote both sides briefly), and the fix you would propose, grouped as Leftovers, Docs vs code, Code vs code, Vocabulary. End your final message with the path and the count per group.\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H spawn --kind claude --label \"consistency check: code vs docs\" --model opus --body \"<supervisor-agent>Read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/consistency-check.md. It is your full brief.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Spawn the consistency check subagent"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"