rring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"6a38985e-2a90-45a6-aee9-961230ba0314","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bef968bc-ddde-4eb2-87c7-308e1c77ded3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UUoapS3K622eApFveQm2gx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Consistency check: code against docs, and leftovers\n2\t\n3\tChecked on `feat/cloudflare-migration` at 4101b42. Read only; no edits were made.\n4\t\n5\t## Leftovers\n6\t\n7\t1. **`api/tests/cassettes/` (31 files)**: vcrpy cassettes from the Python API (`test_extraction_client`, `test_extraction_resolve`, `test_extraction_retry`, `test_extraction_source`, `test_describe_images`, `test_firecrawl_fetch`). No test reads them: the API Worker's suite lives in `api/test/` and imports no cassette. Fix: delete `api/tests/`.\n8\t2. **`pipeline/test/cassettes/describe/test_a_429_retries_then_succeeds.yaml`** and **`test_sanitize_tail_strips_a_marker_from_the_response.yaml`**: no file imports either one. The other two cassettes in that folder are imported (`pipeline/test/helpers/services.ts:7`, `pipeline/test/item-enrichment.test.ts:2`). Fix: delete them, or add the 429-retry and sanitize-tail tests they were recorded for.\n9\t3. **`.mahou/wiki/cloudflare/local-pipeline.md:3`**: \"a job runs through it without the API: `POST /jobs` with `{html, job_id, domain, recipe?}` … then `GET /jobs/<job_id>` until the state is `complete`, `not_article` or `error`\". The pipeline Worker has no public routes now (CLAUDE.md layout table). Line 5 also says \"Durable Object and Workflow state stays local, in `pipeline/.wrangler/`\", but local state now lives in the shared `.wrangler-state/` (`api/package.json` `dev`, `common/package.json` `migrate:local`). Fix: rewrite the entry around enqueueing through the local API (local-development.md), or delete it and leave the gateway-key bullets.\n10\t4. **`.mahou/wiki/testing/cassettes-over-mocks.md:3-9`**: \"The api suite replays … the extraction pipeline, from cassettes\", \"The conftest's matching rules\", \"Mocks stay for … modal's spawn-and-resolve, the gemini describer SDK\", \"minted `itm_` handles\". The conftest, the extraction client and the Modal SDK mocks are gone. Modal is now answered by msw handlers (`pipeline/test/helpers/services.ts:166`), and matching lives in `common/testing/`. Fix: rewrite it for the TypeScript replay library and `common-package.md`'s \"Replaying cassettes in tests\".\n11\t5. **`.gitattributes:15-18`**: the LFS exemption for image fixtures matches `**/tests/fixtures/*`, the Python trees' folder. The TypeScript trees use `test/fixtures`, and `git check-attr` reports `pipeline/test/fixtures/x.png: filter: lfs`. Fix: change the patterns to `**/test/fixtures/*`.\n12\t6. **`.gitignore:14-15`**: \"Runtime & generated data — SQLite DB, …\" and `api/data/` belonged to the Python API; nothing writes `api/data/`. Fix: delete both lines.\n13\t7. **`pipeline/src/runtime/units.ts:141-146`, `pipeline/src/runtime/injection/entry.ts:67-68`**: the runtime gives an image unit `display: unit.alt` and `unitSchema` requires it. The recipe contract defines an image unit with no display (`pipeline/src/agents/prompts.ts:13`: `{ type: \"image\", src, alt, element }`), `markdown-units.md:26` says an image unit carries \"no markdown\", and `toTypedUnits` reads only `src`/`alt` (`pipeline/src/spoken/typed-units.ts:9`). Nothing reads the field. Fix: drop `display` from the image variant in `unitSchema`, `toBoundaryUnit` and `entry.ts`.\n14\t8. **`tts/pyproject.toml:4`**: `description = \"Nagara TTS service — Kokoro-82M on Modal (experiment 001 spike)\"`. The service is the production deployable, not a spike. Fix: drop \"(experiment 001 spike)\".\n15\t9. **`api/.env`** (git-ignored, local only): an env file from the Python API sits next to `api/.dev.vars`; the Worker reads only `.dev.vars`. Contents not read. Fix: the user deletes it locally after checking it holds nothing they still need.\n16\t\n17\t## Docs vs code\n18\t\n19\t1. **`README.md:15-59`**: the whole file still describes the Python API. Line 17: `api/` is \"SQLite/Postgres persistence | FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, uv (Python 3.12)\"; lines 22-25: \"The API invokes it remotely with Modal's own spawn/poll primitives\"; lines 29-44: `uv run uvicorn app.main:app`, `NAGARA_API_KEY`, `dev-key-nagara`, `localhost:8000`; line 49: \"Checks (both trees): `uv run pytest`…\"; lines 53-56: \"Enqueue creates the item as `generating` … Polling resolves the call lazily\". The layout table has no `pipeline/` or `common/` row. In the code, `api/` is a TypeScript Worker, enqueue writes `queued` (`api/src/items/create.ts:15`), the item Workflow does the work, and the local API listens on 8788 (`api/wrangler.jsonc:8`). Fix: rewrite the layout, quick start, checks and \"How it works\" from CLAUDE.md and `local-development.md`.\n20\t2. **`CLAUDE.md` commands block** (\"`pipeline/ … pnpm deploy (prod, via wrangler)`\") and **`deployment-and-ci.md:22`** (\"`pipeline/` deploys with `pnpm deploy`\"): `pnpm deploy` is pnpm's built-in command (\"Usage: pnpm --filter=<deployed project name> deploy <target directory>\"), so it never runs the `deploy` script in `pipeline/package.json:10`. Fix: write `pnpm run deploy`.\n21\t3. **`CLAUDE.md` commands block**: lines for `tts/`, `pipeline/` and `web/`, none for `api/` (`pnpm dev` on 8788, `pnpm run deploy`, test/lint/types) or `common/` (`pnpm migrate:local`, test/lint/types), though both have those scripts. Fix: add an `api/` line and a `common/` line.\n22\t4. **`persistence-and-storage.md:44`, `common-package.md:30` and `:62`, `item-lifecycle.md:245`**: \"Both writers go through the status write in common/\", \"row, queued write\", the API uses it \"for queued and for a failed enqueue\", \"The API uses the same write for `queued` at enqueue and on retry\". The API calls `writeStatus` only with `failed` (`api/src/routes/enqueue.ts:36`, `api/src/routes/retry.ts:28`). Enqueue uses its own `INSERT` (`api/src/items/create.ts:13`), retry its own conditional `UPDATE` (`api/src/items/retry-claim.ts:10`), re-queue its own `UPDATE` (`api/src/items/requeue.ts:18`). The store step writes `ready` in its own SQL (`pipeline/src/workflow/steps/synthesis.ts:71`), and `StatusWrite` excludes `ready` (`common/src/item-store/write-status.ts:5`). Fix: say the API uses the status write only for `failed`, the queued writes are its own INSERT and claim UPDATEs, and the store step writes `ready` itself.\n23\t5. **`common-package.md:68`**: the replay library \"removes the credential headers (authorization, x-api-key and x-goog-api-key)\". `common/testing/request-key.ts:7`: \"Headers never take part in a match\"; no code strips a named list. Fix: \"headers take no part in the match\".\n24\t6. **`common-package.md:77`** (\"This departs from the code style's rule that a payload crossing a service boundary validates at runtime\"): CLAUDE.md's code style now says \"The Workers' types are checked when the code builds, never at runtime\". Fix: remove the sentence, or reword it to say this is what the rule states.\n25\t7. **`item-lifecycle.md:218`**: the lease step's attempt timeout reads \"5 min per wait, up to 3 waits\". The lease step's own attempt runs with `\"1 minute\"` (`pipeline/src/workflow/steps/lease.ts:17`); the 5-minute timeouts belong to the `waitForEvent` calls (`:28`). Fix: \"1 min to ask; then up to 3 waits of 5 min\".\n26\t8. **`item-lifecycle.md:243` and `:326`**: the cases that fail an item at once list the not-article verdict, the agents giving up and HTML over the cap. Two more throw `NonRetryableError` and are missing: the images step's \"no surviving units\" (`pipeline/src/workflow/steps/images.ts:26`) and the store step's timing/unit count mismatch, \"the synthesis returned N timing windows for M units\" (`synthesis.ts:73-77`, invariant 2). Fix: add both to the wrapper paragraph and to \"What a failure names\".\n27\t9. **`item-contract.md:25` and `:28`**: `duration` is \"absent until then\" and `audio_url` is \"present only once ready\". `api/src/response.ts:18` and `:21` always send both keys, `null` before `ready`. Fix: \"`null` until `ready`\".\n28\t10. **`item-contract.md:89`**: the retry cap is \"`retry_max`, default 3\", the old Python setting name. The code reads the `RETRY_MAX` var (`api/wrangler.jsonc:28`, `api/src/env.d.ts:7`). Fix: write `RETRY_MAX`, set to 3 in `api/wrangler.jsonc`.\n29\t11. **`image-and-code-describer.md:123`**: \"`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` is named in the code as the fallback … nothing ever selects it\". The code has only `const MODEL = \"gemini-3.5-flash-lite\"` (`pipeline/src/describe/core.ts:4`); 3.1 appears nowhere. Fix: say no fallback model exists, keeping the reason 3.1 was not adopted, or delete the bullet.\n30\t12. **`markdown-units.md:58`**: \"The runtime has no special handling for a recipe-declared unit that converts to no markdown.\" The validator rejects it: `unit ${position} carries empty markdown` (`pipeline/src/runtime/validate.ts:96-97`), and `recipes.md:31` requires non-empty markdown. Fix: say an empty unit fails validation, or drop the bullet.\n31\t13. **`recipes.md:134`**: \"not-an-article or not-accessible fails the item\". The only verdict is `{ kind: \"not-article\" }` (`pipeline/src/agents/settlement.ts:221`, `pipeline/src/recipes/settle.ts:19`); nothing mentions \"accessible\". Fix: drop \"or not-accessible\".\n32\t14. **`recipes.md:133`**: output units are \"`{ kind, markdown or src+alt }`\". The code uses `{ type: \"paragraph\"|\"code\", display }` or `{ type: \"image\", src, alt, … }` (`pipeline/src/runtime/units.ts:6-17`, `pipeline/src/agents/prompts.ts:10-13`). Fix: `{ type, display or src+alt }`.\n33\t15. **`article-extraction.md:59`** and **`product-design/what-gets-read-aloud.md:28`**: \"The header row gets no line of its own\". A table with no body rows reads its header cells: `if (body.length === 0) { return [asSentence(header.join(\", \"))]; }` (`pipeline/src/spoken/derive.ts:62-63`). Fix: add \"unless the table has no body rows, when its header cells are read as one line\".\n34\t16. **`article-extraction.md:117`**: a degradation carries `\"url\": <origin>`. The code records the src the recipe declared, `url: declaredImages[index].src` (`pipeline/src/images/acquire.ts:69`), which can be relative or a `data:` URI; line 96 of the same note says the src is resolved against the item URL only for the download. Fix: have the note say the declared src, or record the resolved URL in the code.\n35\t17. **`product-design/README.md:16`**: the queue row says a status \"maps directly onto generating, ready, or failed\". `queue.md` lists \"queued, generating, ready, or failed\", and `queued` is a real status. Fix: add `queued`.\n36\t18. **`docs/README.md:12`**: the `technical-design/` row lists \"the item lifecycle, article extraction, read-along timing, the TTS service, the item contract, persistence and storage, authentication, deployment and CI, the invariants\". It leaves out recipes, markdown units, the image and code describer, the common package and local development (`technical-design/README.md:28-38`). Fix: add them.\n37\t\n38\t## Code vs code\n39\t\n40\t1. **`api/wrangler.jsonc:13`, `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:13`, `common/wrangler.jsonc:9`**: all three set `\"database_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"`. The CI migrate job runs `d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` from `common/` (`.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml:125`) and both deploys ship these configs. `deployment-and-ci.md:15` says the configurations \"bind the same D1 database\", and nothing marks the id as a placeholder, so the first deploy targets a database that does not exist. Fix: put the real D1 id in all three, or document the placeholder and when it is replaced.\n41\t2. **`pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:9-14`**: the D1 binding has no `migrations_dir`, while `api/wrangler.jsonc:14` has `\"../common/migrations\"` and `common/wrangler.jsonc:10` has `\"migrations\"`. Only `common/` applies migrations; the API's entry is the outlier (its tests read `../common/migrations` directly in `api/vitest.config.ts:4`). Fix: drop `migrations_dir` from the API config so only `common/` declares it, or add it to the pipeline config too.\n42\t\n43\tThe rest agrees: the `.dev.vars.example` secrets match `api/src/env.d.ts` and `pipeline/worker-configuration.d.ts`; every var in `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc` is read; bucket and database names are `nagara` everywhere; the CI scripts match the `package.json` scripts; the tts `StartRequest`/`StartResponse` shapes, status handling (202/410/422/500), step timeouts, attempts, poll interval and expiry match what `pipeline/src/tts/modal.ts` sends and parses and what `tts-service.md` states. Every dependency in the three `package.json` files is imported.\n44\t\n45\t## Vocabulary\n46\t\n47\t1. **`CLAUDE.md` \"When adding something\"**: \"A new rule for how a job's units become the item's\". There is no job; the units come out of the recipe step. Fix: \"how the recipe step's units become the item's\".\n48\t2. **`CLAUDE.md` \"When adding something\"** (item JSON bullet): \"an in-flight item is read back by a later request than the one that wrote it\". The item is read back by a later Workflow step and by the API's poll. Fix: \"by a later step or request than the one that wrote it\".\n49\t3. **`common/testing/item-id.ts:1-2`**: \"the -N retry suffix stays, so a reminted id never collapses onto the one it replaced\". That describes the extraction service's reminted job handles; item ids are `itm_` plus 8 hex characters with no suffix (`api/src/items/create.ts:5`). Fix: drop the clause.\n50\t4. **`markdown-units.md:53`**: names \"`sanitize_spoken`\", the Python name. The function is `sanitizeSpoken` (`pipeline/src/spoken/sanitize.ts:53`). Fix: rename it in the note.\n51\t5. **`markdown-units.md:11`**: \"The host validates them before anything crosses to the API\". Units no longer cross to the API; the recipe step writes them into the item row. Fix: \"before the recipe step writes them into the item row\".\n52\t6. **`pipeline/src/firecrawl/client.ts:24`**: \"a plain fetch carrying the fields the Python SDK sent\". Fix: state why the fields are set without pointing at the removed SDK.\n53\t7. **`.mahou/spike.md:4`**: \"A spike never changes the production `nagara` Worker\". There are now two production Workers, `nagara` (pipeline) and `nagara-api`. Fix: \"the production `nagara` and `nagara-api` Workers\".\n54\t\n55\tNot reported: the `JobIndex` entries in `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:22-25` stay, because a Durable Object migration tag that was deployed cannot be removed; the \"Python client\" comments in `common/testing/canonical-body.ts` and `common/test/replay-cassettes.test.ts` are accurate, since the cassettes were recorded by the Python client.\n56\t"}]},"uuid":"3924be89-8df6-4453-af21-0103df3389b3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:38:41.452Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/consistency-check.md","content":"# Consistency check: code against docs, and leftovers\n\nChecked on `feat/cloudflare-migration` at 4101b42. Read only; no edits were made.\n\n## Leftovers\n\n1. **`api/tests/cassettes/` (31 files)**: vcrpy cassettes from the Python API (`test_extraction_client`, `test_extraction_resolve`, `test_extraction_retry`, `test_extraction_source`, `test_describe_images`, `test_firecrawl_fetch`). No test reads them: the API Worker's suite lives in `api/test/` and imports no cassette. Fix: delete `api/tests/`.\n2. **`pipeline/test/cassettes/describe/test_a_429_retries_then_succeeds.yaml`** and **`test_sanitize_tail_strips_a_marker_from_the_response.yaml`**: no file imports either one. The other two cassettes in that folder are imported (`pipeline/test/helpers/services.ts:7`, `pipeline/test/item-enrichment.test.ts:2`). Fix: delete them, or add the 429-retry and sanitize-tail tests they were recorded for.\n3. **`.mahou/wiki/cloudflare/local-pipeline.md:3`**: \"a job runs through it without the API: `POST /jobs` with `{html, job_id, domain, recipe?}` … then `GET /jobs/<job_id>` until the state is `complete`, `not_article` or `error`\". The pipeline Worker has no public routes now (CLAUDE.md layout table). Line 5 also says \"Durable Object and Workflow state stays local, in `pipeline/.wrangler/`\", but local state now lives in the shared `.wrangler-state/` (`api/package.json` `dev`, `common/package.json` `migrate:local`). Fix: rewrite the entry around enqueueing through the local API (local-development.md), or delete it and leave the gateway-key bullets.\n4. **`.mahou/wiki/testing/cassettes-over-mocks.md:3-9`**: \"The api suite replays … the extraction pipeline, from cassettes\", \"The conftest's matching rules\", \"Mocks stay for … modal's spawn-and-resolve, the gemini describer SDK\", \"minted `itm_` handles\". The conftest, the extraction client and the Modal SDK mocks are gone. Modal is now answered by msw handlers (`pipeline/test/helpers/services.ts:166`), and matching lives in `common/testing/`. Fix: rewrite it for the TypeScript replay library and `common-package.md`'s \"Replaying cassettes in tests\".\n5. **`.gitattributes:15-18`**: the LFS exemption for image fixtures matches `**/tests/fixtures/*`, the Python trees' folder. The TypeScript trees use `test/fixtures`, and `git check-attr` reports `pipeline/test/fixtures/x.png: filter: lfs`. Fix: change the patterns to `**/test/fixtures/*`.\n6. **`.gitignore:14-15`**: \"Runtime & generated data — SQLite DB, …\" and `api/data/` belonged to the Python API; nothing writes `api/data/`. Fix: delete both lines.\n7. **`pipeline/src/runtime/units.ts:141-146`, `pipeline/src/runtime/injection/entry.ts:67-68`**: the runtime gives an image unit `display: unit.alt` and `unitSchema` requires it. The recipe contract defines an image unit with no display (`pipeline/src/agents/prompts.ts:13`: `{ type: \"image\", src, alt, element }`), `markdown-units.md:26` says an image unit carries \"no markdown\", and `toTypedUnits` reads only `src`/`alt` (`pipeline/src/spoken/typed-units.ts:9`). Nothing reads the field. Fix: drop `display` from the image variant in `unitSchema`, `toBoundaryUnit` and `entry.ts`.\n8. **`tts/pyproject.toml:4`**: `description = \"Nagara TTS service — Kokoro-82M on Modal (experiment 001 spike)\"`. The service is the production deployable, not a spike. Fix: drop \"(experiment 001 spike)\".\n9. **`api/.env`** (git-ignored, local only): an env file from the Python API sits next to `api/.dev.vars`; the Worker reads only `.dev.vars`. Contents not read. Fix: the user deletes it locally after checking it holds nothing they still need.\n\n## Docs vs code\n\n1. **`README.md:15-59`**: the whole file still describes the Python API. Line 17: `api/` is \"SQLite/Postgres persistence | FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, uv (Python 3.12)\"; lines 22-25: \"The API invokes it remotely with Modal's own spawn/poll primitives\"; lines 29-44: `uv run uvicorn app.main:app`, `NAGARA_API_KEY`, `dev-key-nagara`, `localhost:8000`; line 49: \"Checks (both trees): `uv run pytest`…\"; lines 53-56: \"Enqueue creates the item as `generating` … Polling resolves the call lazily\". The layout table has no `pipeline/` or `common/` row. In the code, `api/` is a TypeScript Worker, enqueue writes `queued` (`api/src/items/create.ts:15`), the item Workflow does the work, and the local API listens on 8788 (`api/wrangler.jsonc:8`). Fix: rewrite the layout, quick start, checks and \"How it works\" from CLAUDE.md and `local-development.md`.\n2. **`CLAUDE.md` commands block** (\"`pipeline/ … pnpm deploy (prod, via wrangler)`\") and **`deployment-and-ci.md:22`** (\"`pipeline/` deploys with `pnpm deploy`\"): `pnpm deploy` is pnpm's built-in command (\"Usage: pnpm --filter=<deployed project name> deploy <target directory>\"), so it never runs the `deploy` script in `pipeline/package.json:10`. Fix: write `pnpm run deploy`.\n3. **`CLAUDE.md` commands block**: lines for `tts/`, `pipeline/` and `web/`, none for `api/` (`pnpm dev` on 8788, `pnpm run deploy`, test/lint/types) or `common/` (`pnpm migrate:local`, test/lint/types), though both have those scripts. Fix: add an `api/` line and a `common/` line.\n4. **`persistence-and-storage.md:44`, `common-package.md:30` and `:62`, `item-lifecycle.md:245`**: \"Both writers go through the status write in common/\", \"row, queued write\", the API uses it \"for queued and for a failed enqueue\", \"The API uses the same write for `queued` at enqueue and on retry\". The API calls `writeStatus` only with `failed` (`api/src/routes/enqueue.ts:36`, `api/src/routes/retry.ts:28`). Enqueue uses its own `INSERT` (`api/src/items/create.ts:13`), retry its own conditional `UPDATE` (`api/src/items/retry-claim.ts:10`), re-queue its own `UPDATE` (`api/src/items/requeue.ts:18`). The store step writes `ready` in its own SQL (`pipeline/src/workflow/steps/synthesis.ts:71`), and `StatusWrite` excludes `ready` (`common/src/item-store/write-status.ts:5`). Fix: say the API uses the status write only for `failed`, the queued writes are its own INSERT and claim UPDATEs, and the store step writes `ready` itself.\n5. **`common-package.md:68`**: the replay library \"removes the credential headers (authorization, x-api-key and x-goog-api-key)\". `common/testing/request-key.ts:7`: \"Headers never take part in a match\"; no code strips a named list. Fix: \"headers take no part in the match\".\n6. **`common-package.md:77`** (\"This departs from the code style's rule that a payload crossing a service boundary validates at runtime\"): CLAUDE.md's code style now says \"The Workers' types are checked when the code builds, never at runtime\". Fix: remove the sentence, or reword it to say this is what the rule states.\n7. **`item-lifecycle.md:218`**: the lease step's attempt timeout reads \"5 min per wait, up to 3 waits\". The lease step's own attempt runs with `\"1 minute\"` (`pipeline/src/workflow/steps/lease.ts:17`); the 5-minute timeouts belong to the `waitForEvent` calls (`:28`). Fix: \"1 min to ask; then up to 3 waits of 5 min\".\n8. **`item-lifecycle.md:243` and `:326`**: the cases that fail an item at once list the not-article verdict, the agents giving up and HTML over the cap. Two more throw `NonRetryableError` and are missing: the images step's \"no surviving units\" (`pipeline/src/workflow/steps/images.ts:26`) and the store step's timing/unit count mismatch, \"the synthesis returned N timing windows for M units\" (`synthesis.ts:73-77`, invariant 2). Fix: add both to the wrapper paragraph and to \"What a failure names\".\n9. **`item-contract.md:25` and `:28`**: `duration` is \"absent until then\" and `audio_url` is \"present only once ready\". `api/src/response.ts:18` and `:21` always send both keys, `null` before `ready`. Fix: \"`null` until `ready`\".\n10. **`item-contract.md:89`**: the retry cap is \"`retry_max`, default 3\", the old Python setting name. The code reads the `RETRY_MAX` var (`api/wrangler.jsonc:28`, `api/src/env.d.ts:7`). Fix: write `RETRY_MAX`, set to 3 in `api/wrangler.jsonc`.\n11. **`image-and-code-describer.md:123`**: \"`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` is named in the code as the fallback … nothing ever selects it\". The code has only `const MODEL = \"gemini-3.5-flash-lite\"` (`pipeline/src/describe/core.ts:4`); 3.1 appears nowhere. Fix: say no fallback model exists, keeping the reason 3.1 was not adopted, or delete the bullet.\n12. **`markdown-units.md:58`**: \"The runtime has no special handling for a recipe-declared unit that converts to no markdown.\" The validator rejects it: `unit ${position} carries empty markdown` (`pipeline/src/runtime/validate.ts:96-97`), and `recipes.md:31` requires non-empty markdown. Fix: say an empty unit fails validation, or drop the bullet.\n13. **`recipes.md:134`**: \"not-an-article or not-accessible fails the item\". The only verdict is `{ kind: \"not-article\" }` (`pipeline/src/agents/settlement.ts:221`, `pipeline/src/recipes/settle.ts:19`); nothing mentions \"accessible\". Fix: drop \"or not-accessible\".\n14. **`recipes.md:133`**: output units are \"`{ kind, markdown or src+alt }`\". The code uses `{ type: \"paragraph\"|\"code\", display }` or `{ type: \"image\", src, alt, … }` (`pipeline/src/runtime/units.ts:6-17`, `pipeline/src/agents/prompts.ts:10-13`). Fix: `{ type, display or src+alt }`.\n15. **`article-extraction.md:59`** and **`product-design/what-gets-read-aloud.md:28`**: \"The header row gets no line of its own\". A table with no body rows reads its header cells: `if (body.length === 0) { return [asSentence(header.join(\", \"))]; }` (`pipeline/src/spoken/derive.ts:62-63`). Fix: add \"unless the table has no body rows, when its header cells are read as one line\".\n16. **`article-extraction.md:117`**: a degradation carries `\"url\": <origin>`. The code records the src the recipe declared, `url: declaredImages[index].src` (`pipeline/src/images/acquire.ts:69`), which can be relative or a `data:` URI; line 96 of the same note says the src is resolved against the item URL only for the download. Fix: have the note say the declared src, or record the resolved URL in the code.\n17. **`product-design/README.md:16`**: the queue row says a status \"maps directly onto generating, ready, or failed\". `queue.md` lists \"queued, generating, ready, or failed\", and `queued` is a real status. Fix: add `queued`.\n18. **`docs/README.md:12`**: the `technical-design/` row lists \"the item lifecycle, article extraction, read-along timing, the TTS service, the item contract, persistence and storage, authentication, deployment and CI, the invariants\". It leaves out recipes, markdown units, the image and code describer, the common package and local development (`technical-design/README.md:28-38`). Fix: add them.\n\n## Code vs code\n\n1. **`api/wrangler.jsonc:13`, `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:13`, `common/wrangler.jsonc:9`**: all three set `\"database_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"`. The CI migrate job runs `d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` from `common/` (`.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml:125`) and both deploys ship these configs. `deployment-and-ci.md:15` says the configurations \"bind the same D1 database\", and nothing marks the id as a placeholder, so the first deploy targets a database that does not exist. Fix: put the real D1 id in all three, or document the placeholder and when it is replaced.\n2. **`pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:9-14`**: the D1 binding has no `migrations_dir`, while `api/wrangler.jsonc:14` has `\"../common/migrations\"` and `common/wrangler.jsonc:10` has `\"migrations\"`. Only `common/` applies migrations; the API's entry is the outlier (its tests read `../common/migrations` directly in `api/vitest.config.ts:4`). Fix: drop `migrations_dir` from the API config so only `common/` declares it, or add it to the pipeline config too.\n\nThe rest agrees: the `.dev.vars.example` secrets match `api/src/env.d.ts` and `pipeline/worker-configuration.d.ts`; every var in `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc` is read; bucket and database names are `nagara` everywhere; the CI scripts match the `package.json` scripts; the tts `StartRequest`/`StartResponse` shapes, status handling (202/410/422/500), step timeouts, attempts, poll interval and expiry match what `pipeline/src/tts/modal.ts` sends and parses and what `tts-service.md` states. Every dependency in the three `package.json` files is imported.\n\n## Vocabulary\n\n1. **`CLAUDE.md` \"When adding something\"**: \"A new rule for how a job's units become the item's\". There is no job; the units come out of the recipe step. Fix: \"how the recipe step's units become the item's\".\n2. **`CLAUDE.md` \"When adding something\"** (item JSON bullet): \"an in-flight item is read back by a later request than the one that wrote it\". The item is read back by a later Workflow step and by the API's poll. Fix: \"by a later step or request than the one that wrote it\".\n3. **`common/testing/item-id.ts:1-2`**: \"the -N retry suffix stays, so a reminted id never collapses onto the one it replaced\". That describes the extraction service's reminted job handles; item ids are `itm_` plus 8 hex characters with no suffix (`api/src/items/create.ts:5`). Fix: drop the clause.\n4. **`markdown-units.md:53`**: names \"`sanitize_spoken`\", the Python name. The function is `sanitizeSpoken` (`pipeline/src/spoken/sanitize.ts:53`). Fix: rename it in the note.\n5. **`markdown-units.md:11`**: \"The host validates them before anything crosses to the API\". Units no longer cross to the API; the recipe step writes them into the item row. Fix: \"before the recipe step writes them into the item row\".\n6. **`pipeline/src/firecrawl/client.ts:24`**: \"a plain fetch carrying the fields the Python SDK sent\". Fix: state why the fields are set without pointing at the removed SDK.\n7. **`.mahou/spike.md:4`**: \"A spike never changes the production `nagara` Worker\". There are now two production Workers, `nagara` (pipeline) and `nagara-api`. Fix: \"the production `nagara` and `nagara-api` Workers\".\n\nNot reported: the `JobIndex` entries in `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc:22-25` stay, because a Durable Object migration tag that was deployed cannot be removed; the \"Python client\" comments in `common/testing/canonical-body.ts` and `common/test/replay-cassettes.test.ts` are accurate, since the cassettes were recorded by the Python client.\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6a38985e-2a90-45a6-aee9-961230ba0314","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
