{"parentUuid":"adf34a3d-b983-41fe-8569-38c20cf5a017","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvdiYuJRZsmoETYomRes","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019ELQUaLSxvYfrpughXHMpU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w46:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Two changes from the user:\n1. **D4:** don't wait. Backdate the stranded item's \\`queued_at\\` in the local D1 (wrangler d1 execute nagara --local --persist-to <the shared state folder> from common/, an UPDATE on that one item) to more than 15 minutes ago, then poll it and confirm the re-queue restarts it and it reaches ready. Record D4 as: the enqueue-time failure cannot happen locally (create does not throw with the pipeline stopped; the automated test covers that path), and the local path is the stranded-item re-queue, validated.\n2. **C1 and C11:** build synthetic articles. Write two small static HTML pages in .scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/synthetic/ (served by a local static server you start, exposed through its own quick tunnel so Firecrawl can fetch it; record the PIDs). C1: a short article with an ornament (a decorative divider or icon the recipe should drop), a code block, a raster image of at least 200 px on its short side, an inline SVG or .svg image that contains a <script>, an image with a good descriptive alt, and the same image repeated. C11: a short article with a 40 px avatar and an <img> whose src 404s. Keep the text a few paragraphs, with real prose so the recipe treats it as an article. Each page is its own domain (the tunnel host), so its first run authors a recipe; that is fine. Skip the redirect-to-www part of C1 and say so. Run both through the local API and check each row's expected outcome against the item row, the units and the stored objects. Stop the static server and its tunnel by PID afterwards.\nThen finish as the brief says.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Send D4, C1 and C11 instructions to the validation subagent"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":299,"cache_read_input_tokens":259287,"output_tokens":1074,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":352},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":299,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1074,"cache_read_input_tokens":259287,"cache_creation_input_tokens":299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":299},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019ELQUaLSxvYfrpughXHMpU":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H prompt w46:p2 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Two changes from the user:\n1. **D4:** don't wait. Backdate the stranded item's \\`queued_at\\` in the local D1 (wrangler d1 execute nagara --local --persist-to <the shared state folder> from common/, an UPDATE on that one item) to more than 15 minutes ago, then poll it and confirm the re-queue restarts it and it reaches ready. Record D4 as: the enqueue-time failure cannot happen locally (create does not throw with the pipeline stopped; the automated test covers that path), and the local path is the stranded-item re-queue, validated.\n2. **C1 and C11:** build synthetic articles. Write two small static HTML pages in .scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/synthetic/ (served by a local static server you start, exposed through its own quick tunnel so Firecrawl can fetch it; record the PIDs). C1: a short article with an ornament (a decorative divider or icon the recipe should drop), a code block, a raster image of at least 200 px on its short side, an inline SVG or .svg image that contains a <script>, an image with a good descriptive alt, and the same image repeated. C11: a short article with a 40 px avatar and an <img> whose src 404s. Keep the text a few paragraphs, with real prose so the recipe treats it as an article. Each page is its own domain (the tunnel host), so its first run authors a recipe; that is fine. Skip the redirect-to-www part of C1 and say so. Run both through the local API and check each row's expected outcome against the item row, the units and the stored objects. Stop the static server and its tunnel by PID afterwards.\nThen finish as the brief says.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Send D4, C1 and C11 instructions to the validation subagent"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"952002ad-7a8f-4310-b66c-f15d5c061534","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfvdiXyFHidJTnzLMy9V2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8953753-7c20-48af-9006-f6539a618338","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:48:34.981Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
