{"parentUuid":"cf721dc1-d60c-4ed2-acdc-f027741ebcb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvdjUzgLekUiv52KPdes","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've sent both changes to the validation subagent.\n\n- **D4:** Changing `queued_at` speeds up the re-queue, but it can't force the failure. The failure D4 describes happens when `create` throws at enqueue. Locally, `create` doesn't throw even with the pipeline stopped, so no timestamp makes it fail. The subagent will backdate the stuck item's `queued_at` past 15 minutes, poll it, and confirm it restarts and reaches `ready`. That validates the local path, the re-queue of a stuck item. The enqueue failure itself is covered by the automated D4 test.\n- **C1 and C11:** It will build two small synthetic pages, served from a local static server through their own quick tunnel so Firecrawl can fetch them.\n  - **C1:** an ornament, a code block, a large raster, an SVG containing a `<script>`, an image with a good alt, and a repeated image.\n  - **C11:** a 40 px avatar and an image that returns 404.\n  - **Not covered:** the C1 redirect to `www`. A tunnel hostname can't produce one.\n\nThe question on recording the resolved image URL in degradations is still open."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":259586,"output_tokens":406,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":259586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":