{"parentUuid":"bce3a10b-0ca7-4cfe-8ec4-37d16b968a65","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfve1WVR3mACFjygscaLU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016jru5K5xnksBCiyE1Pfcpe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs; cat > consistency-fixes.md <<'EOF'\n# Apply the consistency-check findings\n\nIn the main checkout `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` on `feat/cloudflare-migration`. Same rules as your pipeline brief. The user approved applying the findings in `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/consistency-check.md`, all of them, with these exceptions and decisions:\n\n- **Code vs code 1 (D1 placeholder id):** leave the id as it is; it is replaced tomorrow when the production database is created. Do mark it: a short comment in each of the three wrangler configs saying the id is a placeholder until the production D1 exists, and keep `deployment-and-ci.md` accurate about it.\n- **Code vs code 2:** drop `migrations_dir` from the API's config, so only `common/` declares it; keep the API tests reading `../common/migrations`.\n- **Leftovers 2 (two unused describe cassettes):** delete them.\n- **Leftovers 9 (`api/.env`):** do not touch it; the user handles it.\n- **Docs vs code 16:** change the code: an image degradation records the **resolved** URL (the src resolved against the item URL), not the declared src. Adjust the test, and keep `article-extraction.md` saying it records the URL.\n- **Leftovers 3, 4 and Vocabulary 7** are under `.mahou/` (the project's local mahou layer): apply them too.\n- **Docs vs code 1 (README.md):** rewrite it from CLAUDE.md and `local-development.md`, keeping its current tone and sections where they still apply.\n\nFor every doc edit, follow `docs/README.md` and the note template rules (callouts, no hard wrapping, present tense). Run `superpowers:unslop` over the changed prose. Run test, lint and types in every tree you touch (`common/`, `api/`, `pipeline/`; `uv run ruff check` in `tts/` if you touch it) and `vite build` in `pipeline/`.\n\nCommit in logical groups with conventional commits: code fixes by tree (`fix(pipeline)`, `chore(api)`, …), cleanup (`chore`), and one `docs:` commit for `docs/`, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, and one `chore:` for `.mahou/`. Final message: the commits, per finding what you did (or why not), and the check output.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the consistency fixes brief"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36,"cache_read_input_tokens":261121,"output_tokens":1021,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":78},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1021,"cache_read_input_tokens":261121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016jru5K5xnksBCiyE1Pfcpe":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs; cat > consistency-fixes.md <<'EOF'\n# Apply the consistency-check findings\n\nIn the main checkout `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` on `feat/cloudflare-migration`. Same rules as your pipeline brief. The user approved applying the findings in `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/consistency-check.md`, all of them, with these exceptions and decisions:\n\n- **Code vs code 1 (D1 placeholder id):** leave the id as it is; it is replaced tomorrow whe