{"parentUuid":"8f7702c4-4933-408c-8ee6-cc80dcf9cc42","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c64b69f2-49ca-4102-a16a-e5e428382fbf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011oSfZQGz7gz5tRdANCn8QS","type":"tool_result","content":"D20-player-playing.png\nD20-player.png\nindex.html\nlisten-itm_d627c989.md\nlisten-itm_d627c989.ogg\nlisten-itm_f76c359c.md\nlisten-itm_f76c359c.ogg\nrows\nsynthetic\nc1\nc11\n\nnagara: local manual validation\nnagara on Cloudflare: manual validation, local\nChange: the Cloudflare migration, branch \nfeat/cloudflare-migration\n in the main checkout, HEAD \n44521c9\n (ci: describe the deploy conditions in the workflow's header). The working tree also carried uncommitted docs edits by another session; no code was uncommitted.\nSystem: brought up as \ne71c820\n set it up, with the API on port 8788: a fresh \n.wrangler-state/\n (the old one moved to \n/tmp/nagara-wrangler-state-old-20261011-113102\n), \npnpm migrate:local\n, \npnpm dev:proxy\n (8792), a quick tunnel, \nR2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\n written into \npipeline/.dev.vars\n by script, \npnpm dev\n in pipeline (vite, 5173), \npnpm dev\n in api (8788), \nuv run modal serve app.py\n in tts (\nhttps://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run\n).\nIdentity: the local \nAPI_KEY\n from \napi/.dev.vars\n, read by script and never printed. Real services: Firecrawl, the AI Gateway (Gemini and the Flue agents' model), Modal's ephemeral dev app.\nSurface: the API over HTTP with curl; D20 also in a real browser (agent-browser).\nSetup and mutations\n.wrangler-state/\n moved aside (no deletion) and recreated by \npnpm migrate:local\n for D5's fresh state.\npipeline/.dev.vars\n: \nR2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\n set by script to the quick tunnel's host for the run, and set back to the placeholder \nhttps://<tunnel-hostname>/s3\n at the end.\nNo database row was written by hand.\nD4, record: \nitems.queued_at\n of itm_57e81442, before \n2026-10-11T14:43:08.864Z\n, mutated to \n2026-10-11T14:20:00.000Z\n with \nwrangler d1 execute nagara --local --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\n from \ncommon/\n. Not reverted: the API's re-queue claim overwrote it with \n2026-10-11T14:48:46.148Z\n, which is the behaviour under test.\nD4, code: one line added before the Workflow \ncreate\n in \napi/src/routes/enqueue.ts\n to force the create to throw, then restored with \ngit checkout -- api/src/routes/enqueue.ts\n (\ngit status --short api/\n empty afterwards).\nB1 start a synthesis with every field, locally: the audio lands in the local bucket through the tunnel and plays\nThe pipeline's start synthesis step called the ephemeral Modal app's \nPOST /start\n with the spoken forms, the voice and a PUT URL signed for \nhttp://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3\n and handed out on the tunnel's host (\nR2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\n). Modal's log:\nPOST /start -> 200 OK  (duration: 4.44 s, execution: 378.1 ms)\nPOST /start -> 200 OK  (duration: 507.4 ms, execution: 374.5 ms)\nGET /result -> 200 OK  (duration: 403.0 ms, execution: 245.9 ms)\nGET /result -> 200 OK  (duration: 379.6 ms, execution: 245.9 ms)\nEach start answered 200 with a call id (the step reached wait for synthesis), and the result endpoint answered 202 while running, then 200. Modal runs in the cloud and could only reach the local bucket through the quick tunnel and the proxy; the object \naudio/itm_f76c359c\n is in the shared local bucket: 735,020 bytes, \naudio/ogg\n, ffprobe reads Ogg of 256.38 s, matching the item's duration 256.375. It plays and seeks in a browser (D20). Same for itm_919a039d (351.175 s).\nResult: \nPASS\n (locally; the deployed half, with a presigned R2 URL, is for the deploy run)\nC1 an article with an ornament, code, a raster, an SVG with a script, a good-alt image and a repeated image\nReal article first: \nhttps://eli.thegreenplace.net/2026/watgo-a-webassembly-toolkit-for-go\n (itm_f76c359c) reached ready, with three code blocks spoken as \nCode: …\n and a raster diagram whose good alt is spoken verbatim and not described. Its title and units are the article's own, and its audio is saved as \nlisten-itm_f76c359c.ogg\n. One spoken-form defect showed: a word starting with a dot loses the space before it (\"designed .wast files\" is spoken \"designed.wast files\"), finding F1.\nNo small real article carried the rest, so a synthetic page was built: \nsynthetic/c1/index.html\n, served by a local static server behind its own quick tunnel, \nhttps://farming-last-roof-donors.trycloudflare.com/\n (itm_d627c989). It holds an ornament paragraph (\n<p class=\"divider\">❦</p>\n), a code block, a 480×320 bar chart, an SVG image (\nflow.svg\n) with a \n<script>\n and an \nonload\n, a red-circle image with a descriptive alt, and the bar chart repeated. The redirect-to-www part was skipped: a quick tunnel cannot redirect to a www host.\nStatus: queued at fetch, then generating recipe (a new domain: the author agent wrote version 1 in 26 s), then describe, wait for synthesis, and ready at 12:03:09.\n{\"title\": \"Caching responses at the edge\", \"status\": \"ready\", \"current_step\": null, \"extraction_domain\": \"farming-last-roof-donors.trycloudflare.com\", \"recipe_version_id\": \"rcp_d19d95d4\", \"degradations\": null, \"duration\": 108.025, \"error\": null}\nUnits (type, image hash, spoken):\nparagraph  | Most of the traffic a small service receives asks for the same few resources over and over. Serving those answers from a cache close to the reader cut\nparagraph  | The flow is short: a client asks the cache, and the cache only goes to the origin when it holds nothing fresh for that request.\nimage 13bc90d1d75f | Image: A diagram shows three connected boxes labeled client, cache, and origin in a horizontal sequence with arrows pointing between them.\nparagraph  | The origin decides how long a response may be reused. A single header carries that decision, and the cache honours it without any further configuratio\ncode  | Code: An HTTP header specifies the duration a response may be reused and sets revalidation rules.\nparagraph  | After a week with the header in place, the share of requests answered by the cache grew steadily, as the chart below shows.\nimage 88d1d9975cad | Image: A bar chart displays four blue vertical bars of increasing height from left to right against blank axes.\nparagraph  | Some responses should never be shared between readers. Anything that depends on who is asking needs a private cache directive, or no caching at all.\nimage 6a251d23a3ba | Image: A red circle centered on a pale yellow background, the warning marker used for private responses\nparagraph  | The same chart, repeated here for the summary, makes the point once more: the cache does most of the work once the origin tells it what is safe to kee\nimage 88d1d9975cad | Image: Four blue vertical bars of increasing heights stand on an axis showing an upward trend.\nparagraph  | That is the whole trick. Decide what may be reused, say so in one header, and let the cache close to the reader take care of the rest.\nOrnament:\n absent from the units. The author agent declared \np.divider\n an ignore (\"decorative separator\"), so the recipe left it out before the pipeline's drop rule could act. The drop rule itself is exercised by the automated tests only.\nCode:\nCode: An HTTP header specifies the duration a response may be reused and sets revalidation rules.\nSVG:\n described from its markup (\"three connected boxes labeled client, cache, and origin\", the text inside the SVG). It is stored as \nimage/svg+xml\n without the \n<script>\n and without \nonload\n:\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"420\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 140\">\n  <title>Request flow: client to cache to origin</title>\n…\nRaster:\n re-encoded to WebP (480×320, \nimage/webp\n) and described.\nGood alt:\n spoken verbatim and not sent to the describer.\nRepeated chart:\n both units carry the same hash \n88d1d997…\n, one object, though each was described on its own: two describer calls, two different sentences, neither answered from the gateway cache.\nLedger:\n{\"types\": \"firecrawl,describer,describer,describer,describer,tts\"}\n (4 describer rows: 3 image, 1 code).\nThe audio landed in the local bucket through the tunnel (108 s). It is saved as \nlisten-itm_d627c989.ogg\n with \nlisten-itm_d627c989.md\n, so the descriptions can be heard.\nResult: \nPASS\n (real article and synthetic page both to ready with the expected units; the www redirect skipped; the ornament was dropped by the recipe's ignore rather than the drop rule)\nC5 two articles of one site enqueued together\nInputs: \nhttps://eli.thegreenplace.net/2026/watgo-a-webassembly-toolkit-for-go\n (itm_f76c359c) and \nhttps://eli.thegreenplace.net/2025/revisiting-lets-build-a-compiler\n (itm_919a039d), posted together at 14:32:15 (both 202 queued).\nStatus timeline from the shared D1, polled every 2 s (local time):\n11:32:16 {\"id\": \"itm_f76c359c\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"current_step\": \"fetch\", \"error\": null}\n11:32:16 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"current_step\": \"fetch\", \"error\": null}\n11:32:20 {\"id\": \"itm_f76c359c\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"current_step\": \"lease\", \"error\": null}\n11:32:20 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"recipe\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:00 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"release\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:03 {\"id\": \"itm_f76c359c\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"recipe\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:03 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"start synthesis\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:10 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"gene","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"094166f0-7638-44bc-9809-c11d388736b2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:05:41.395Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"D20-player-playing.png\nD20-player.png\nindex.html\nlisten-itm_d627c989.md\nlisten-itm_d627c989.ogg\nlisten-itm_f76c359c.md\nlisten-itm_f76c359c.ogg\nrows\nsynthetic\nc1\nc11\n\nnagara: local manual validation\nnagara on Cloudflare: manual validation, local\nChange: the Cloudflare migration, branch \nfeat/cloudflare-migration\n in the main checkout, HEAD \n44521c9\n (ci: describe the deploy conditions in the workflow's header). The working tree also carried uncommitted docs edits by another session; no code was uncommitted.\nSystem: brought up as \ne71c820\n set it up, with the API on port 8788: a fresh \n.wrangler-state/\n (the old one moved to \n/tmp/nagara-wrangler-state-old-20261011-113102\n), \npnpm migrate:local\n, \npnpm dev:proxy\n (8792), a quick tunnel, \nR2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\n written into \npipeline/.dev.vars\n by script, \npnpm dev\n in pipeline (vite, 5173), \npnpm dev\n in api (8788), \nuv run modal serve app.py\n in tts (\nhttps://asermax--nagara-tts-web-dev.modal.run\n).\nIdentity: the local \nAPI_KEY\n from \napi/.dev.vars\n, read by script and never printed. Real services: Firecrawl, the AI Gateway (Gemini and the Flue agents' model), Modal's ephemeral dev app.\nSurface: the API over HTTP with curl; D20 also in a real browser (agent-browser).\nSetup and mutations\n.wrangler-state/\n moved aside (no deletion) and recreated by \npnpm migrate:local\n for D5's fresh state.\npipeline/.dev.vars\n: \nR2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\n set by script to the quick tunnel's host for the run, and set back to the placeholder \nhttps://<tunnel-hostname>/s3\n at the end.\nNo database row was written by hand.\nD4, record: \nitems.queued_at\n of itm_57e81442, before \n2026-10-11T14:43:08.864Z\n, mutated to \n2026-10-11T14:20:00.000Z\n with \nwrangler d1 execute nagara --local --persist-to ../.wrangler-state\n from \ncommon/\n. Not reverted: the API's re-queue claim overwrote it with \n2026-10-11T14:48:46.148Z\n, which is the behaviour under test.\nD4, code: one line added before the Workflow \ncreate\n in \napi/src/routes/enqueue.ts\n to force the create to throw, then restored with \ngit checkout -- api/src/routes/enqueue.ts\n (\ngit status --short api/\n empty afterwards).\nB1 start a synthesis with every field, locally: the audio lands in the local bucket through the tunnel and plays\nThe pipeline's start synthesis step called the ephemeral Modal app's \nPOST /start\n with the spoken forms, the voice and a PUT URL signed for \nhttp://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3\n and handed out on the tunnel's host (\nR2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT\n). Modal's log:\nPOST /start -> 200 OK  (duration: 4.44 s, execution: 378.1 ms)\nPOST /start -> 200 OK  (duration: 507.4 ms, execution: 374.5 ms)\nGET /result -> 200 OK  (duration: 403.0 ms, execution: 245.9 ms)\nGET /result -> 200 OK  (duration: 379.6 ms, execution: 245.9 ms)\nEach start answered 200 with a call id (the step reached wait for synthesis), and the result endpoint answered 202 while running, then 200. Modal runs in the cloud and could only reach the local bucket through the quick tunnel and the proxy; the object \naudio/itm_f76c359c\n is in the shared local bucket: 735,020 bytes, \naudio/ogg\n, ffprobe reads Ogg of 256.38 s, matching the item's duration 256.375. It plays and seeks in a browser (D20). Same for itm_919a039d (351.175 s).\nResult: \nPASS\n (locally; the deployed half, with a presigned R2 URL, is for the deploy run)\nC1 an article with an ornament, code, a raster, an SVG with a script, a good-alt image and a repeated image\nReal article first: \nhttps://eli.thegreenplace.net/2026/watgo-a-webassembly-toolkit-for-go\n (itm_f76c359c) reached ready, with three code blocks spoken as \nCode: …\n and a raster diagram whose good alt is spoken verbatim and not described. Its title and units are the article's own, and its audio is saved as \nlisten-itm_f76c359c.ogg\n. One spoken-form defect showed: a word starting with a dot loses the space before it (\"designed .wast files\" is spoken \"designed.wast files\"), finding F1.\nNo small real article carried the rest, so a synthetic page was built: \nsynthetic/c1/index.html\n, served by a local static server behind its own quick tunnel, \nhttps://farming-last-roof-donors.trycloudflare.com/\n (itm_d627c989). It holds an ornament paragraph (\n<p class=\"divider\">❦</p>\n), a code block, a 480×320 bar chart, an SVG image (\nflow.svg\n) with a \n<script>\n and an \nonload\n, a red-circle image with a descriptive alt, and the bar chart repeated. The redirect-to-www part was skipped: a quick tunnel cannot redirect to a www host.\nStatus: queued at fetch, then generating recipe (a new domain: the author agent wrote version 1 in 26 s), then describe, wait for synthesis, and ready at 12:03:09.\n{\"title\": \"Caching responses at the edge\", \"status\": \"ready\", \"current_step\": null, \"extraction_domain\": \"farming-last-roof-donors.trycloudflare.com\", \"recipe_version_id\": \"rcp_d19d95d4\", \"degradations\": null, \"duration\": 108.025, \"error\": null}\nUnits (type, image hash, spoken):\nparagraph  | Most of the traffic a small service receives asks for the same few resources over and over. Serving those answers from a cache close to the reader cut\nparagraph  | The flow is short: a client asks the cache, and the cache only goes to the origin when it holds nothing fresh for that request.\nimage 13bc90d1d75f | Image: A diagram shows three connected boxes labeled client, cache, and origin in a horizontal sequence with arrows pointing between them.\nparagraph  | The origin decides how long a response may be reused. A single header carries that decision, and the cache honours it without any further configuratio\ncode  | Code: An HTTP header specifies the duration a response may be reused and sets revalidation rules.\nparagraph  | After a week with the header in place, the share of requests answered by the cache grew steadily, as the chart below shows.\nimage 88d1d9975cad | Image: A bar chart displays four blue vertical bars of increasing height from left to right against blank axes.\nparagraph  | Some responses should never be shared between readers. Anything that depends on who is asking needs a private cache directive, or no caching at all.\nimage 6a251d23a3ba | Image: A red circle centered on a pale yellow background, the warning marker used for private responses\nparagraph  | The same chart, repeated here for the summary, makes the point once more: the cache does most of the work once the origin tells it what is safe to kee\nimage 88d1d9975cad | Image: Four blue vertical bars of increasing heights stand on an axis showing an upward trend.\nparagraph  | That is the whole trick. Decide what may be reused, say so in one header, and let the cache close to the reader take care of the rest.\nOrnament:\n absent from the units. The author agent declared \np.divider\n an ignore (\"decorative separator\"), so the recipe left it out before the pipeline's drop rule could act. The drop rule itself is exercised by the automated tests only.\nCode:\nCode: An HTTP header specifies the duration a response may be reused and sets revalidation rules.\nSVG:\n described from its markup (\"three connected boxes labeled client, cache, and origin\", the text inside the SVG). It is stored as \nimage/svg+xml\n without the \n<script>\n and without \nonload\n:\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"420\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 140\">\n  <title>Request flow: client to cache to origin</title>\n…\nRaster:\n re-encoded to WebP (480×320, \nimage/webp\n) and described.\nGood alt:\n spoken verbatim and not sent to the describer.\nRepeated chart:\n both units carry the same hash \n88d1d997…\n, one object, though each was described on its own: two describer calls, two different sentences, neither answered from the gateway cache.\nLedger:\n{\"types\": \"firecrawl,describer,describer,describer,describer,tts\"}\n (4 describer rows: 3 image, 1 code).\nThe audio landed in the local bucket through the tunnel (108 s). It is saved as \nlisten-itm_d627c989.ogg\n with \nlisten-itm_d627c989.md\n, so the descriptions can be heard.\nResult: \nPASS\n (real article and synthetic page both to ready with the expected units; the www redirect skipped; the ornament was dropped by the recipe's ignore rather than the drop rule)\nC5 two articles of one site enqueued together\nInputs: \nhttps://eli.thegreenplace.net/2026/watgo-a-webassembly-toolkit-for-go\n (itm_f76c359c) and \nhttps://eli.thegreenplace.net/2025/revisiting-lets-build-a-compiler\n (itm_919a039d), posted together at 14:32:15 (both 202 queued).\nStatus timeline from the shared D1, polled every 2 s (local time):\n11:32:16 {\"id\": \"itm_f76c359c\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"current_step\": \"fetch\", \"error\": null}\n11:32:16 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"current_step\": \"fetch\", \"error\": null}\n11:32:20 {\"id\": \"itm_f76c359c\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"current_step\": \"lease\", \"error\": null}\n11:32:20 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"recipe\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:00 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"release\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:03 {\"id\": \"itm_f76c359c\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"recipe\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:03 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"generating\", \"current_step\": \"start synthesis\", \"error\": null}\n11:34:10 {\"id\": \"itm_919a039d\", \"status\": \"gene","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a2d86ed6-78de-4892-909f-8af7da33c358","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote"