{"parentUuid":"1324b3fb-5124-4136-8d72-6fcbe9f42b74","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c64b69f2-49ca-4102-a16a-e5e428382fbf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0118HEMNSBimvupg3v8etJLC","type":"tool_result","content":"Findings \n F1, spoken form: the sanitize tail removes the space before a word that starts with a dot: display \"specially designed [.wast files](…)\" and \"harness parses .wast files\" are spoken \"specially designed.wast files\" and \"harness parses.wast files\" (watgo). It needs listening to judge how Kokoro reads it. \n F3, local D1 contention: one fetch attempt failed with D1_ERROR: database is locked: SQLITE_BUSY (D16, retry 1), and one of this run's own D1 reads failed the same way. The shared local D1 is one SQLite file opened by both dev servers and, during this run, a wrangler d1 execute status watcher every 2 s, so the watcher likely contributed. \n F4, local stranded-item recovery: an item enqueued while the pipeline dev server is stopped gets a Workflow instance that errors at once (\"Worker \\\"nagara\\\" not found\"), and the API sees no error. The re-queue after 15 minutes claims the row, its create finds the instance id taken and restarts that instance, the restart is accepted without error, and the instance stays errored, so the item stays queued indefinitely. local-development.md says this re-queue recovers such an item. \n Not covered by hand: C1's redirect to www (a quick tunnel cannot redirect); the drop rule for an ornament and the 200 px floor for an avatar, because the authored recipes excluded both before the pipeline saw them. The automated tests cover all three. \n Left in the local state \n itm_57e81442 and itm_28c60a6f (enqueued with the pipeline stopped) stay queued with errored instances; see F4.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"51e60316-50b2-4c5a-85f3-be5f95d08611","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:05:48.450Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Findings \n F1, spoken form: the sanitize tail removes the space before a word that starts with a dot: display \"specially designed [.wast files](…)\" and \"harness parses .wast files\" are spoken \"specially designed.wast files\" and \"harness parses.wast files\" (watgo). It needs listening to judge how Kokoro reads it. \n F3, local D1 contention: one fetch attempt failed with D1_ERROR: database is locked: SQLITE_BUSY (D16, retry 1), and one of this run's own D1 reads failed the same way. The shared local D1 is one SQLite file opened by both dev servers and, during this run, a wrangler d1 execute status watcher every 2 s, so the watcher likely contributed. \n F4, local stranded-item recovery: an item enqueued while the pipeline dev server is stopped gets a Workflow instance that errors at once (\"Worker \\\"nagara\\\" not found\"), and the API sees no error. The re-queue after 15 minutes claims the row, its create finds the instance id taken and restarts that instance, the restart is accepted without error, and the instance stays errored, so the item stays queued indefinitely. local-development.md says this re-queue recovers such an item. \n Not covered by hand: C1's redirect to www (a quick tunnel cannot redirect); the drop rule for an ornament and the 200 px floor for an avatar, because the authored recipes excluded both before the pipeline saw them. The automated tests cover all three. \n Left in the local state \n itm_57e81442 and itm_28c60a6f (enqueued with the pipeline stopped) stay queued with errored instances; see F4.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8c2a7fe3-2fff-4d9d-91e3-31eaab13a77d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},