{"parentUuid":"193cc5c1-00a5-43cd-a858-8836ca50d772","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvf4Zu1UF81kmco9RANA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The manual validation is done. 13 of 14 rows passed; D4 passed only partly. The full report is `reports/validation/index.html`.\n\n**Rows that passed:**\n- **B1:** Modal uploaded the audio into the local bucket through the tunnel, and the file plays.\n- **C1:** both a real article (Eli Bendersky's watgo post) and the synthetic page reached `ready`, with the expected spoken units.\n  - Code blocks are read as \"Code: …\".\n  - The raster was re-encoded to WebP and described.\n  - The SVG was stored without its `<script>` and `onload`, and described from its markup.\n  - The good alt was read word for word.\n  - The repeated chart is stored as one object.\n- **C5:** the second item from the same site stayed `queued` until the first released its lease, then both reached `ready`.\n- **C7:** an authored recipe was saved as version 1.\n- **C9:** a home page failed with the \"not an article\" verdict.\n- **C11:** the 404 image was dropped, with a degradation recorded.\n- **D1, D5, D13, D16, D20, D21 and D25** passed. D20 played and seeked the audio in a real browser.\n\n**Not checked by hand:**\n- **C1's redirect to `www`:** a tunnel can't produce one.\n- **The ornament and the avatar:** the recipe the agent wrote left both out, so the pipeline's own drop rule and its 200 px floor never ran on them.\n\nThe automated tests cover all three.\n\n**F4, the D4 failure, needs your call.** When an item is enqueued while the pipeline dev server is stopped, its Workflow instance errors straight away with \"Worker nagara not found\". The API doesn't see that error. After 15 minutes the re-queue tries to create the instance, finds the item id already taken, and restarts that instance. Cloudflare accepts the restart, but the instance stays errored, so the item stays `queued` forever.\n\nUsing the item id as the instance id, which I chose for you earlier, caused this. Before that change, the re-queue would have created a fresh instance. In production this needs the pipeline Worker to be missing, which shouldn't happen. Locally it happens whenever you enqueue with the pipeline stopped.\n\nMy recommendation: when the re-queue finds the item's instance errored or terminated, it creates a new instance under a new id, such as `<itemId>-2`. When the instance is still alive, it leaves it alone. That keeps the protection against duplicate instances and still recovers dead ones. The `forced D4` path, an enqueue-time failure retried to `ready`, passed.\n\n**F1 needs your call.** When a word starts with a dot, the spoken form drops the space before it. \"designed .wast files\" is read as \"designed.wast files\". I'd fix the sanitize step so it keeps that space. Listen first and decide whether it matters:\n- `reports/validation/listen-itm_f76c359c.ogg` (watgo) contains the F1 case.\n- `listen-itm_d627c989.ogg` (the synthetic page) lets you hear the image and code descriptions.\n- Each has its text in a `.md` file next to it.\n\n**F3 needs no change.** The shared local D1 was briefly locked. A fetch attempt hit \"database is locked\" and its retry went through. The validation's own status watcher, which polled every 2 seconds, likely caused it.\n\nThe pipeline subagent is applying the consistency fixes now, including recording the resolved image URL. It won't touch F1 or F4 until you decide."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_read_input_tokens":269800,"output_tokens":1157,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations