{"parentUuid":"9d726f19-2b08-4304-a183-65f8d7f5b0ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvfYb8Czw2ueaYkyunyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":272996,"output_tokens":1501,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1134,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1501,"cache_read_input_tokens":272996,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1134},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3409,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"28df7339-5fff-4c6d-96d5-760632cee5dc","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfvfYagug5e5tJGQWcHkx","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b4b6957e-acb9-4e90-82f8-8faedd03aca8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:12:26.625Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"b4b6957e-acb9-4e90-82f8-8faedd03aca8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvfYb8Czw2ueaYkyunyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0155EUV6buFvdg8esHn6vShF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs; cat > f1-f4.md <<'EOF'\n# F1 and F4 from the manual validation\n\nMain checkout, `feat/cloudflare-migration`, same rules as before.\n\n## F4: re-queue checks the instance before restarting it (api/)\n\nIn the re-queue and the retry, when the API reaches an existing instance (the row's `workflow_instance_id`, or the item id after `create` reported it already exists), read the instance's status first:\n- **errored or terminated**: create a new instance under a new id, `<itemId>-<n>` with the next free suffix (n = 2, 3, …; on `already_exists` try the next), and let its first step write it into the row as usual. A restart of an instance that errored before its first step is accepted but does nothing (validation finding F4), which is why it is replaced rather than restarted.\n- **running, queued, waiting or paused**: on a re-queue, leave it alone (it is alive); on a retry, the claim already required `failed`, so restart it as now.\n- **complete**, or anything else: restart from the restart point, as now.\nWrite the tests (the stand-in reports a status per instance). Check what id the pipeline's DomainQueue and the step wrapper rely on: the Workflow reads its own instance id from the event, so a suffixed id must work everywhere the instance id is used (the lease FIFO, `workflow_instance_id`); confirm with a pipeline test if it matters.\n\nThen re-run D4's stranded-item path locally to confirm it recovers: bring up the local system as before (API on 8788), enqueue with the pipeline stopped, start the pipeline, backdate `queued_at` past 15 minutes, poll, and see the item reach ready. Small article. Stop everything by PID afterwards and reset `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The two items stranded in the local state (itm_57e81442, itm_28c60a6f) should recover the same way when polled; check them too.\n\nUpdate `item-lifecycle.md`, `item-contract.md` and `local-development.md` where they describe re-queue and retry restarting an instance (follow the docs rules, unslop the prose).\n\n## F1: keep the space before a word that starts with a dot (pipeline/)\n\nThe sanitize tail removes the space before a token that starts with a dot (\".wast files\" after \"designed\" becomes \"designed.wast files\"). Find why (likely a rule meant for spaces before sentence punctuation) and narrow it so a space before a dot followed by a letter or digit stays. Add spoken-form test cases.\n\nThe user also wonders whether Kokoro reads the dot at all. Do not change the reading yet: with the `modal serve` dev copy, synthesize two short clips, \"The harness parses .wast files from the spec.\" and \"The harness parses dot wast files from the spec.\", save them as `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/f1-dot.ogg` and `f1-dot-word.ogg`, for the user to listen to and decide.\n\n## Ending\n\nRun test, lint and types in api/ and pipeline/, build pipeline/, commit (`fix(api): …`, `fix(pipeline): …`, `docs: …`), and report commits, tests, the D4 rerun result and the clip paths.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the F1 and F4 brief"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":272996,"output_tokens":1501,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1134,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1501,"cache_read_input_tokens":272996,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1134},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0155EUV6buFvdg8esHn6vShF":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs; cat > f1-f4.md <<'EOF'\n# F1 and F4 from the manual validation\n\nMain checkout, `feat/cloudflare-migration`, same rules as before.\n\n## F4: re-queue checks the instance before restarting it (api/)\n\nIn the re-queue and the retry, when the API reaches an existing instance (the row's `workflow_instance_id`, or the item id after `create` reported it already exists), read the instance's status first:\n- **errored or terminated**: create a new instance under a new id, `<itemId>-<n>` with the next free suffix (n = 2, 3, …; on `already_exists` try the next), and let its first step write it into the row as usual. A restart of an instance that errored before its first step is accepted but does nothing (validation finding F4), which is why it is replaced rather than restarted.\n- **running, queued, waiting or paused**: on a re-queue, leave it alone (it is alive); on a retry, the claim already required `failed`, so restart it as now.\n- **complete**, or anything else: restart from the restart point, as now.\nWrite the tests (the stand-in reports a status per instance). Check what id the pipeline's DomainQueue and the step wrapper rely on: the Workflow reads its own instance id from the event, so a suffixed id must work everywhere the instance id is used (the lease FIFO, `workflow_instance_id`); confirm with a pipeline test if it matters.\n\nThen re-run D4's stranded-item path locally to confirm it recovers: bring up the local system as before (API on 8788), enqueue with the pipeline stopped, start the pipeline, backdate `queued_at` past 15 minutes, poll, and see the item reach ready. Small article. Stop everything by PID afterwards and reset `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`. The two items stranded in the local state (itm_57e81442, itm_28c60a6f) should recover the same way when polled; check them too.\n\nUpdate `item-lifecycle.md`, `item-contract.md` and `local-development.md` where they describe re-queue and retry restarting an instance (follow the docs rules, unslop the prose).\n\n## F1: keep the space before a word that starts with a dot (pipeline/)\n\nThe sanitize tail removes the space before a token that starts with a dot (\".wast files\" after \"designed\" becomes \"designed.wast files\"). Find why (likely a rule meant for spaces before sentence punctuation) and narrow it so a space before a dot followed by a letter or digit stays. Add spoken-form test cases.\n\nThe user also wonders whether Kokoro reads the dot at all. Do not change the reading yet: with the `modal serve` dev copy, synthesize two short clips, \"The harness parses .wast files from the spec.\" and \"The harness parses dot wast files from the spec.\", save them as `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/f1-dot.ogg` and `f1-dot-word.ogg`, for the user to listen to and decide.\n\n## Ending\n\nRun test, lint and types in api/ and pipeline/, build pipeline/, commit (`fix(api): …`, `fix(pipeline): …`, `docs: …`), and report commits, tests, the D4 rerun result and the clip paths.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the F1 and F4 brief"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"28df7339-5fff-4c6d-96d5-760632cee5dc","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfvfYagug5e5tJGQWcHkx","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"35f83ec3-15b6-49a9-a121-7effc72e6016","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:12:38.165Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296