{"parentUuid":"94c15ad0-c2b4-48e5-b273-c9839686a6cc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ea88e2f3-115c-4aca-95a1-ae8271c15d9a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bdq1FQkC3XFQbikmpr1Tzt","type":"tool_result","content":"idle\n  1. Rewrote README.md from CLAUDE.md and local-development.md, keeping its sections and tone: layout with pipeline/ and common/, local quick start on 8788, checks, how it works, status.\n  2. CLAUDE.md and deployment-and-ci.md now say pnpm run deploy.\n  3. Added api/ and common/ lines to CLAUDE.md's command block.\n  4. The status-write callers are corrected in persistence-and-storage.md, item-lifecycle.md and common-package.md (diagram label and table):\n     - the API uses the write only for failed;\n     - queued comes from the API's own INSERT and its claim UPDATEs;\n     - the store step writes ready itself.\n  5. common-package.md now says headers take no part in the match.\n  6. common-package.md: the \"departs from the code style\" sentence now states that the code style holds the same rule.\n  7. Lease timeout now reads \"1 min to ask; then up to 3 waits of 5 min\".\n  8. Added \"no surviving units\" and the timing/unit count mismatch to the wrapper paragraph and to \"What a failure names\".\n  9. duration and audio_url are null until ready.\n  10. The retry cap is the RETRY_MAX var.\n  11. The describer note says no fallback model exists, and keeps the reason 3.1 was not adopted.\n  12. An empty declared unit fails validation.\n  13. Dropped \"or not-accessible\".\n  14. Recipe output units are { type, display or src+alt }.\n  15. A table with no body rows reads its header cells as one line, in both notes.\n  16. The code changed, as you decided: a degradation records the src resolved against the item URL, or the src as written when it does not resolve. The C11 test now uses a relative src and\n      expects the resolved URL; article-extraction.md still says it records the URL.\n  17. Added queued to the product index.\n  18. docs/README.md's technical-design row now lists every note.\n\n  Code vs code\n  1. The id is unchanged. A comment marks it as a placeholder in all three wrangler configs, and a WARNING callout in deployment-and-ci.md says the migrate job and both deploys fail until the\n     production id replaces it in all three files.\n  2. Dropped migrations_dir from the API config; its tests still read ../common/migrations.\n\n  Vocabulary\n  1. and 2. Applied in CLAUDE.md.\n  2. Dropped the retry-suffix clause in common/testing/item-id.ts.\n  3. and 5. Applied in markdown-units.md.\n  4. The Firecrawl client comment no longer points at the Python SDK.\n  5. .mahou/spike.md names both nagara and nagara-api.\n\n  The unslop pass ran in two rounds with fresh agents. Round 1 flagged 35 lines and I applied 27. The other 8 fall on older sentences this change didn't touch, so I left them. Round 2 found\n  nothing slipping back.\n\n  Check output\n\n  pipeline  Test Files 13 passed (13) · Tests 120 passed | 1 skipped · lint clean · types 0 · vite build ✓\n  common    Test Files 5 passed (5) · Tests 17 passed · lint clean · types 0\n  api       lint clean · types 0 · tests: 3 fail with my local api/.dev.vars present, 40/40 pass without it\n  tts       uv run ruff check: All checks passed!\n\n  The three API failures come from my local api/.dev.vars, not from these changes. The vitest plugin loads that file, and its local R2_S3_ENDPOINT (http://localhost:5173/cdn-cgi/local/r2/s3)\n  carries a path the audio and image tests don't expect. I moved the file aside for one run (40/40 passed) and put it back. CI has no .dev.vars, so it is unaffected. Pinning those vars in\n  api/vitest.config.ts would make the suite independent of the local file; I left that alone because it is outside these findings.\n\n✻ Baked for 33s · done 12:16 PM\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n❯ pin the R2 vars in api/vitest.config.ts\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  🤖 Opus 5.5 | 🔴 732k/1000k (73%) | 📍 ~/.herdr/worktrees/nagara/feat-cloudflare-migration-pipeline | 🌿 feat/cloudflare-migration-pipeline\n  -- INSERT -- ⏵⏵ auto mode on (shift+tab to cycle)\n\n7f61b5f chore: update the local mahou layer for the Cloudflare pipeline\n26a3f18 docs: align the notes, README and CLAUDE.md with the code\n227b327 chore: remove the Python API's leftovers and mark the placeholder D1 id\nbc571d5 chore(api): leave migrations_dir to common's wrangler config","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e8dd9c52-f618-43aa-99df-cea24a557846","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:16:58.523Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"idle\n  1. Rewrote README.md from CLAUDE.md and local-development.md, keeping its sections and tone: layout with pipeline/ and common/, local quick start on 8788, checks, how it works, status.\n  2. CLAUDE.md and deployment-and-ci.md now say pnpm run deploy.\n  3. Added api/ and common/ lines to CLAUDE.md's command block.\n  4. The status-write callers are corrected in persistence-and-storage.md, item-lifecycle.md and common-package.md (diagram label and table):\n     - the API uses the write only for failed;\n     - queued comes from the API's own INSERT and its claim UPDATEs;\n     - the store step writes ready itself.\n  5. common-package.md now says headers take no part in the match.\n  6. common-package.md: the \"departs from the code style\" sentence now states that the code style holds the same rule.\n  7. Lease timeout now reads \"1 min to ask; then up to 3 waits of 5 min\".\n  8. Added \"no surviving units\" and the timing/unit count mismatch to the wrapper paragraph and to \"What a failure names\".\n  9. duration and audio_url are null until ready.