result"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"304b510f-62be-4f1a-9c65-3eac0ac48fbd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfvga9o87Yhm9QbwdMTpv","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6be1f6da-b6a5-4104-a59b-0e5a9e345367","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:26:01.945Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"6be1f6da-b6a5-4104-a59b-0e5a9e345367","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f0be3d5e-c5d5-4710-9983-44262e6b8e6f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PxqoHeg3DPbSokw8qCdLH6","type":"tool_result","content":"working\nCommitted so far: `f831adc` (test(api) vitest pin), `ca37067` (fix(api) F4, as the brief specified) and `471d885` (fix(pipeline) F1). The F1 clips are saved. The F1 docs line is edited but not yet committed. I've stopped every process I started and the Modal app.\n\nI stopped before the D4 rerun and the F4 docs because the brief's F4 rule breaks retry-from-the-failed-step.\n\n<subagent-ask>\n**F4 as written makes every retry start over from fetch.** When a step runs out of attempts, the pipeline's step wrapper writes `failed` and rethrows (`pipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts`), so the Workflow instance always ends `errored`. Under the brief's rule (\"errored or terminated → create a new instance `<itemId>-<n>`\"), a retry would never restart from `current_step`. It would replace the instance, and the new one runs from the fetch step. That re-fetches the page, and `item-lifecycle.md` (\"Retry does not re-fetch once extraction resolved\") says a retry must avoid this, because Firecrawl's output is non-deterministic. `ca37067` is committed with exactly this behaviour and isn't pushed.\n\nThe F4 finding itself (a restart accepted but nothing runs) applies only to an instance that errored before its first step. The fetch step writes `workflow_instance_id` into the row, so a row without it is exactly the \"never ran its first step\" case.\n\nProposed narrowing:\n- Replace an errored or terminated instance only when the row holds no `workflow_instance_id` (the instance was found through `create`'s `already_exists`).\n- When the row names an instance, an ended instance is restarted from the restart point, as now.\n- A re-queue still leaves a live instance alone, and a retry still restarts it.\n\nThe stranded items itm_57e81442 and itm_28c60a6f have no instance id on their row (if I recall the validation correctly), so they would still recover by replacement.\n\nOptions:\n1. Apply this narrowing and amend `ca37067`.\n2. Keep the brief's rule as written, accepting that a retry re-runs from fetch.\n3. Something else.\n\nI'll continue with the D4 rerun and the docs once you answer.\n</subagent-ask>\n471d885 fix(pipeline): keep the space before a word that starts with a dot\nca37067 fix(api): replace an ended Workflow instance instead of restarting it\nf831adc test(api): pin the S3 endpoint so the suite ignores a local .dev.vars\n7f61b5f chore: update the local mahou layer for the Cloudflare pipeline\n26a3f18 docs: align the notes, README and CLAUDE.md with the code\n227b327 chore: remove the Python API's leftovers and mark the placeholder D1 id\n M docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"19279026-aae0-4298-8847-0671e24f9336","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:26:02.704Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"working\nCommitted so far: `f831adc` (test(api) vitest pin), `ca37067` (fix(api) F4, as the brief specified) and `471d885` (fix(pipeline) F1). The F1 clips are saved. The F1 docs line is edited but not yet committed. I've stopped every process I started and the Modal app.\n\nI stopped before the D4 rerun and the F4 docs because the brief's F4 rule breaks retry-from-the-failed-step.\n\n<subagent-ask>\n**F4 as written makes every retry start over from fetch.** When a step runs out of attempts, the pipeline's step wrapper writes `failed` and rethrows (`pipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts`), so the Workflow instance always ends `errored`. Under the brief's rule (\"errored or terminated → create a new instance `<itemId>-<n>`\"), a retry would never restart from `current_step`. It would replace the instance, and the new one runs from the fetch step. That re-fetches the page, and `item-lifecycle.md` (\"Retry does not re-fetch once extraction resolved\") says a retry must avoid this, because Firecrawl's output is non-deterministic. `ca37067` is committed with exactly this behaviour and isn't pushed.\n\nThe F4 finding itself (a restart accepted but nothing runs) applies only to an instance that errored before its first step. The fetch step writes `workflow_instance_id` into the row, so a row without it is exactly the \"never ran its first step\" case.\n\nProposed narrowing:\n- Replace an errored or terminated instance only when the row holds no `workflow_instance_id` (the instance was found through `create`'s `already_exists`).\n- When the row names an instance, an ended instance is restarted from the restart point, as now.\n- A re-queue still leaves a live instance alone, and a retry still restarts it.\n\nThe stranded items itm_57e81442 and itm_28c60a6f have no instance id on their row (if I recall the validation correctly), so they would still recover by replacement.\n\nOptions:\n1. Apply this narrowing and amend `ca37067`.\n2. Keep the brief's rule as written, accepting that a retry re-runs from fetch.\n3. Something else.\n\nI'll continue with the D4 rerun and the docs once you answer.\n</subagent-ask>\n471d885 fix(pipeline): keep the space before a word that starts with a dot\nca37067 fix(api): replace an ended Workflow instance instead of restarting it\nf831adc test(api): pin the S3 endpoint so the suite ignores a local .dev.vars\n7f61b5f chore: update the local mahou layer for the Cloudflare pipeline\n26a3f18 docs: align the notes, README and CLAUDE.md with the code\n227b327 chore: remove the Python API's leftovers and mark the placeholder D1 id\n M docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"304b510f-62be-4f1a-9c65-3eac0ac48fbd","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default