{"parentUuid":"fd50dd62-1311-4f17-885a-2b2e2bfcce6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvgb5EoWjWN7XKqaGhcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The subagent caught a mistake in my F4 brief. I told it to replace any errored or terminated instance with a fresh one. But the step wrapper rethrows on a step's last attempt, so every failed item's instance ends `errored`. With my rule, every retry would replace the instance and start over from fetch. That re-fetches the page, which retry-from-the-failed-step exists to avoid. That version is already committed as `ca37067` (not pushed).\n\nF4 only covers an instance that errored before its first step ran. The fetch step writes `workflow_instance_id` into the row, so a row without one identifies exactly that case. The subagent proposes narrowing the rule:\n\n- **Row has no `workflow_instance_id`** (the instance was found through `create`'s \"already exists\"): if the instance is errored or terminated, create a new one under `<itemId>-<n>`; if it's alive, leave it alone on a re-queue.\n- **Row names an instance:** restart it from the restart point, as before. A retry from the failed step keeps working.\n\nThe two stuck items have no instance id on their rows, so they would still recover this way.\n\nMy recommendation is to apply the narrowing and amend `ca37067`. It's what you asked for, a status check that recovers instances that never started, without breaking retries. OK to go ahead?\n\nAlready committed besides that:\n- **F1 fix (`471d885`):** the space before a word starting with a dot now stays.\n- **R2 pin (`f831adc`):** the R2 vars are pinned in the API's vitest config, so the suite no longer depends on your local `api/.dev.vars`.\n\nThe F1 clips are ready to listen to:\n- `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/f1-dot.ogg` says \".wast files\"\n- `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/f1-dot-word.ogg` says \"dot wast files\""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1321,"cache_read_input_tokens":285515,"output_tokens":803,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":184},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1321,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":285515,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1321},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4f759624-0846-44c2-b592-376fd49e846a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfvgb4pFrMWczHUvXjtqc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c4c53a7-7b0a-4003-9dbd-8bba9a13886a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:26:11.825Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
