{"parentUuid":"f0ce2fa0-511e-496d-8964-2d3fdfd2b63f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1799270c-0b5b-4a49-aa4e-cb4a1022a600","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WyKQpwhr6xUZBdYmfs8hYV","type":"tool_result","content":"done\nThe number clips are ready in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/`. Recorded durations:\n\n| File | Text | Duration |\n|---|---|---|\n| `num-3.14.ogg` | Version 3.14 shipped today. | 2.85 s |\n| `num-3-point-14.ogg` | Version 3 point 14 shipped today. | 2.825 s |\n| `num-0.5.ogg` | It takes 0.5 seconds. | 2.475 s |\n| `num-0-point-5.ogg` | It takes 0 point 5 seconds. | 2.525 s |\n| `num-leading-.5.ogg` | It takes .5 seconds. | 2.175 s |\n| `num-point-5.ogg` | It takes point 5 seconds. | 2.175 s |\n\n`num-clips.md` beside them maps each file to its text. Each pair is almost the same length, and the \".5\" pair is identical. That hints that Kokoro already says \"point\" for these numbers, but only listening confirms it. The receiver and tunnel for the clips are stopped.\n\nThe D4 rerun is still going:\n- **itm_6059d335** reached `ready` on its replacement instance `itm_6059d335-2`.\n- **itm_28c60a6f** (example.com) ran on `itm_28c60a6f-2` and failed in recipe with \"authoring gave up\". That's expected for a page that isn't an article, so the recovery itself worked.\n- **itm_57e81442** is in `generating`, at the recipe step, on `itm_57e81442-2`.\n\nI haven't touched pipeline code yet. An edit would reload the pipeline dev server, and a running instance never resumes after a reload, so the dot rule for words waits until itm_57e81442 settles. Numbers stay untouched until the user decides.\n\n<subagent-ask>\nThe number clips are ready (`reports/validation/num-*.ogg`, with `num-clips.md`). How should the spoken form treat numbers like \"3.14\", \"0.5\" and \".5\" after the user listens: leave them as written, or write them out with \"point\"? Meanwhile I'll finish D4 and then write the dot rule for words, keeping numbers, sentence punctuation, ellipses and single-letter abbreviations (\"e.g.\", \"U.S.\") as they are.\n</subagent-ask>\nnum-0.5.ogg\nnum-0-point-5.ogg\nnum-3.14.ogg\nnum-3-point-14.ogg\nnum-clips.md\nnum-leading-.5.ogg\nnum-point-5.ogg","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a561dc8b-3ecd-48c2-99a5-3fed3f29964d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:35:44.348Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\nThe number clips are ready in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/`. Recorded durations:\n\n| File | Text | Duration |\n|---|---|---|\n| `num-3.14.ogg` | Version 3.14 shipped today. | 2.85 s |\n| `num-3-point-14.ogg` | Version 3 point 14 shipped today. | 2.825 s |\n| `num-0.5.ogg` | It takes 0.5 seconds. | 2.475 s |\n| `num-0-point-5.ogg` | It takes 0 point 5 seconds. | 2.525 s |\n| `num-leading-.5.ogg` | It takes .5 seconds. | 2.175 s |\n| `num-point-5.ogg` | It takes point 5 seconds. | 2.175 s |\n\n`num-clips.md` beside them maps each file to its text. Each pair is almost the same length, and the \".5\" pair is identical. That hints that Kokoro already says \"point\" for these numbers, but only listening confirms it. The receiver and tunnel for the clips are stopped.\n\nThe D4 rerun is still going:\n- **itm_6059d335** reached `ready` on its replacement instance `itm_6059d335-2`.\n- **itm_28c60a6f** (example.com) ran on `itm_28c60a6f-2` and failed in recipe with \"authoring gave up\". That's expected for a page that isn't an article, so the recovery itself worked.\n- **itm_57e81442** is in `generating`, at the recipe step, on `itm_57e81442-2`.\n\nI haven't touched pipeline code yet. An edit would reload the pipeline dev server, and a running instance never resumes after a reload, so the dot rule for words waits until itm_57e81442 settles. Numbers stay untouched until the user decides.\n\n<subagent-ask>\nThe number clips are ready (`reports/validation/num-*.ogg`, with `num-clips.md`). How should the spoken form treat numbers like \"3.14\", \"0.5\" and \".5\" after the user listens: leave them as written, or write them out with \"point\"? Meanwhile I'll finish D4 and then write the dot rule for words, keeping numbers, sentence punctuation, ellipses and single-letter abbreviations (\"e.g.\", \"U.S.\") as they are.\n</subagent-ask>\nnum-0.5.ogg\nnum-0-point-5.ogg\nnum-3.14.ogg\nnum-3-point-14.ogg\nnum-clips.md\nnum-leading-.5.ogg\nnum-point-5.ogg","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b1a1575f-fba4-45ff-8507-27585c7f858e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0ce2fa0-511e-496d-8964-2d3fdfd2b63f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
