{"parentUuid":"77755c5f-f940-4f26-8b56-bf40f563ffca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwAnSBSvg4zWyRZytLvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The number clips are ready in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/validation/`. Each pair is the same sentence written with the digits and with \"point\" spelled out:\n\n| Written | Spelled out |\n|---|---|\n| `num-3.14.ogg` \"Version 3.14 shipped today.\" | `num-3-point-14.ogg` |\n| `num-0.5.ogg` \"It takes 0.5 seconds.\" | `num-0-point-5.ogg` |\n| `num-leading-.5.ogg` \"It takes .5 seconds.\" | `num-point-5.ogg` |\n\nThe two clips in each pair are almost the same length, and the \".5\" pair is identical. That hints Kokoro already says \"point\", but only listening will tell. Should numbers stay as written, or be spelled out with \"point\"?\n\nThe D4 rerun has recovered all three stuck items on their replacement instances (`<id>-2`):\n- **itm_6059d335** reached `ready`.\n- **itm_28c60a6f** (example.com) ran and failed at the recipe step with \"authoring gave up\". That's the expected outcome for a page that isn't an article.\n- **itm_57e81442** is still in the recipe step.\n\nThe subagent is waiting for that last item before writing the dot rule for words. Editing pipeline code reloads the dev server, and a reload strands any running item."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":293779,"output_tokens":444,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":347,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":293779,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"eph