{"parentUuid":"c869a1f8-6cfb-4af5-aa9e-0aa2ac2f680f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwBLsgWzbgKTVNXNGUfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011Mav9b6QsCEp8vuQFypBwa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w46:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\"; cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara; git log --oneline -5","description":"Collect subagent progress"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":372,"cache_read_input_tokens":295790,"output_tokens":208,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":372,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":295790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":372},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011Mav9b6QsCEp8vuQFypBwa":{"command":"H=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H collect w46:p2 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['status']); print(d.get('message',''))\"; cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara; git log --oneline -5","description":"Collect subagent progress"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"17f43650-b71c-41d9-b3a3-d102f9eb7637","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwBLngduovtKNiSGXGQp","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"24325bc8-ce9f-4e2b-b398-0bdd142311ad","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:43:10.775Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"24325bc8-ce9f-4e2b-b398-0bdd142311ad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"20a5be0d-1e61-4ff7-8c7c-a2227f47c4c5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Mav9b6QsCEp8vuQFypBwa","type":"tool_result","content":"done\nF1 and F4 are done and committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration` (not pushed). The D4 stranded-item path now recovers locally, and all checks pass in `api/` and `pipeline/`. The one open item is how numbers should be read, which waits on the user listening to the number clips.\n\n## Commits (on top of 7f61b5f)\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `f831adc` | test(api): pin the S3 endpoint so the suite ignores a local `.dev.vars` |\n| `ca37067` | fix(api): replace an ended Workflow instance instead of restarting it |\n| `471d885` | fix(pipeline): keep the space before a word that starts with a dot |\n| `0690682` | fix(api): replace only an instance that never ran its first step |\n| `93f56de` | fix(pipeline): read a dot before a letter as the word dot |\n| `d2f165d` | docs: describe the instance check on re-queue and retry, and the spoken dot |\n\n## F4: re-queue and retry (api/)\n- **Rows that name an instance:** the instance has run its fetch step. It is restarted from `current_step` whatever its status, so a retry still resumes from the step that failed. A re-queue leaves a queued, running, waiting or paused instance alone.\n- **Rows that hold no instance id:** the API creates the instance with the item id. If one already exists and is errored or terminated, the API replaces it with a new instance at the next free suffix (`<itemId>-2`, `-3`, …). A live existing instance is left alone on a re-queue and restarted on a retry.\n- **The local-binding difference:** locally, `create` on an id that already exists returns that instance instead of throwing `already_exists`. The API now reads the status of whatever `create` returns. This was the reason the first rerun failed.\n- **Tests:** a retry of an errored or terminated instance that ran a step restarts from `current_step` with no new instance. Replacement is tested both when `create` throws and when it returns the existing instance, along with the next-free-suffix case and leaving a live instance alone.\n- **Pipeline:** no change needed. The Workflow reads the item id from its params, and its own tests already run with instance ids that differ from the item id (`wf-<itemId>`). The domain lease and the agent conversation work with the instance id they are given.\n- **Known gap, local only:** if a `-2` instance also errors before its first step (the pipeline is down again), the next re-queue's `create` of `-2` returns it without throwing, and the item stays queued. On Cloudflare, `already_exists` moves on to `-3`.\n\n## D4 rerun: PASS\n- **How it ran:** itm_6059d335 was enqueued with the pipeline stopped, then the pipeline was started and all three stranded items were polled once. They were already more than 15 minutes stale, so none needed backdating.\n- **itm_6059d335:** `ready` on `itm_6059d335-2` (640 s of audio).\n- **itm_57e81442:** `ready` on `itm_57e81442-2` (681 s).\n- **itm_28c60a6f** (example.com): ran on `itm_28c60a6f-2` and failed in recipe with \"authoring gave up\". That is the right result for a page that isn't an article.\n- The first rerun, on `ca37067` alone, failed for the local-binding reason above. Both reruns, every change made for them and how each was undone are recorded under D4 in `reports/validation/index.html`, with the summary row now PASS.\n- Every process is stopped by PID, all Modal apps show `stopped`, and `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` is back to the placeholder.\n\n## F1: dots (pipeline/)\n- **Cause:** the sanitize tail's `/\\s+([,.;:!?])/` dropped every space before a dot. Now a dot with a digit right after it keeps its space, so \".5\" stays apart from the word before it.\n- **The user's rule:** a dot followed by a letter is spoken as \"dot\" (`93f56de`, `pipeline/src/spoken/dots.ts`, called from the sanitize tail, so the describer's output gets it too):\n  - \".wast\" becomes \"dot wast\" and \".env\" becomes \"dot env\";\n  - \"index.html\" becomes \"index dot html\" and \"example.com\" becomes \"example dot com\";\n  - it applies when the dot comes after a letter, a digit, whitespace, an opening bracket or quote, or the start of a line.\n- **Left as written:** numbers (\"3.14\", \"0.5\", \".5\"), full stops, ellipses, and runs of single letters each followed by a dot (\"e.g.\", \"i.e.\", \"U.S.\"). Each case has a spoken-form test.\n- **Side effect:** an autolink now reads \"a@b dot com\" and \"https://x dot test\". The existing test was updated to match.\n- **Docs:** `article-extraction.md` has a paragraph and a callout on the rule, and `what-gets-read-aloud.md` has a bullet.\n- **Clips:**\n  - `reports/validation/f1-dot.ogg` and `f1-dot-word.ogg`: \".wast\" against \"dot wast\", which the user has already chosen between.\n  - `reports/validation/num-*.ogg`, listed in `num-clips.md`: \"3.14\", \"0.5\" and \".5\", each next to the same sentence with \"point\" written out. Each pair is nearly the same length, and the \".5\" pair is identical, but only listening settles how Kokoro reads them.\n\n## Other\n- **api vitest:** `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` is pinned in `api/vitest.config.ts`. The R2 GET keys were already pinned. The suite passes with the local `api/.dev.vars` present.\n- **Docs:** `item-lifecycle.md`, `item-contract.md` and `local-development.md` describe the status check and the replacement. Unslop round 1 found 15 issues and I applied 11; the other 4 are in older sentences this change doesn't touch. Round 2 found nothing that slipped back.\n\n## Checks\n```\napi       Tests 56 passed (6 files) · lint clean · types 0   (with api/.dev.vars present)\npipeline  Tests 136 passed | 1 skipped (13 files) · lint clean · types 0 · vite build ✓\n```\n\n<subagent-ask>\nHow should the spoken form treat numbers (\"3.14\", \"0.5\", \".5\") once the user has listened to `reports/validation/num-*.ogg`: leave them as written, or write out \"point\"? Until then numbers stay as written.\n</subagent-ask>\nd2f165d docs: describe the instance check on re-queue and retry, and the spoken dot\n93f56de fix(pipeline): read a dot before a letter as the word dot\n0690682 fix(api): replace only an instance that never ran its first step\n471d885 fix(pipeline): keep the space before a word that starts with a dot\nca37067 fix(api): replace an ended Workflow instance instead of restarting it","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e069acdf-46e2-4412-b8af-219a8a800afd","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:43:11.283Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\nF1 and F4 are done and committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration` (not pushed). The D4 stranded-item path now recovers locally, and all checks pass in `api/` and `pipeline/`. The one open item is how numbers should be read, which waits on the user listening to the number clips.\n\n## Commits (on top of 7f61b5f)\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `f831adc` | test(api): pin the S3 endpoint so the suite ignores a local `.dev.vars` |\n| `ca37067` | fix(api): replace an ended Workflow instance instead of restarting it |\n| `471d885` | fix(pipeline): keep the space before a word that starts with a dot |\n| `0690682` | fix(api): replace only an instance that never ran its first step |\n| `93f56de` | fix(pipeline): read a dot before a letter as the word dot |\n| `d2f165d` | docs: describe the instance check on re-queue and retry, and the spoken dot |\n\n## F4: re-queue and retry (api/)\n- **Rows that name an instance:** the instance has run its fetch step. It is restarted from `current_step` whatever its status, so a retry still resumes from the step that failed. A re-queue leaves a queued, running, waiting or paused instance alone.\n- **Rows that hold no instance id:** the API creates the instance with the item id. If one already exists and is errored or terminated, the API replaces it with a new instance at the next free suffix (`<itemId>-2`, `-3`, …). A live existing instance is left alone on a re-queue and restarted on a retry.\n- **The local-binding difference:** locally, `create` on an id that already exists returns that instance instead of throwing `already_exists`. The API now reads the status of whatever `create` returns. This was the reason the first rerun failed.\n- **Tests:** a retry of an errored or terminated instance that ran a step restarts from `current_step` with no new instance. Replacement is tested both when `create` throws and when it returns the existing instance, along with the next-free-suffix case and leaving a live instance alone.\n- **Pipeline:** no change needed. The Workflow reads the item id from its params, and its own tests already run with instance ids that differ from the item id (`wf-<itemId>`). The domain lease and the agent conversation work with the instance id they are given.\n- **Known gap, local only:** if a `-2` instance also errors before its first step (the pipeline is down again), the next re-queue's `create` of `-2` returns it without throwing, and the item stays queued. On Cloudflare, `already_exists` moves on to `-3`.\n\n## D4 rerun: PASS\n- **How it ran:** itm_6059d335 was enqueued with the pipeline stopped, then the pipeline was started and all three stranded items were polled once. They were already more than 15 minutes stale, so none needed backdating.\n- **itm_6059d335:** `ready` on `itm_6059d335-2` (640 s of audio).\n- **itm_57e81442:** `ready` on `itm_57e81442-2` (681 s).\n- **itm_28c60a6f** (example.com): ran on `itm_28c60a6f-2` and failed in recipe with \"authoring gave up\". That is the right result for a page that isn't an article.\n- The first rerun, on `ca37067` alone, failed for the local-binding reason above. Both reruns, every change made for them and how each was undone are recorded under D4 in `reports/validation/index.html`, with the summary row now PASS.\n- Every process is stopped by PID, all Modal apps show `stopped`, and `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` is back to the placeholder.\n\n## F1: dots (pipeline/)\n- **Cause:** the sanitize tail's `/\\s+([,.;:!?])/` dropped every space before a dot. Now a dot with a digit right after it keeps its space, so \".5\" stays apart from the word before it.\n- **The user's rule:** a dot followed by a letter is spoken as \"dot\" (`93f56de`, `pipeline/src/spoken/dots.ts`, called from the sanitize tail, so the describer's output gets it too):\n  - \".wast\" becomes \"dot wast\" and \".env\" becomes \"dot env\";\n  - \"index.html\" becomes \"index dot html\" and \"example.com\" becomes \"example dot com\";\n  - it applies when the dot comes after a letter, a digit, whitespace, an opening bracket or quote, or the start of a line.\n- **Left as written:** numbers (\"3.14\", \"0.5\", \".5\"), full stops, ellipses, and runs of single letters each followed by a dot (\"e.g.\", \"i.e.\", \"U.S.\"). Each case has a spoken-form test.\n- **Side effect:** an autolink now reads \"a@b dot com\" and \"https://x dot test\". The existing test was updated to match.\n- **Docs:** `article-extraction.md` has a paragraph and a callout on the rule, and `what-gets-read-aloud.md` has a bullet.\n- **Clips:**\n  - `reports/validation/f1-dot.ogg` and `f1-dot-word.ogg`: \".wast\" against \"dot wast\", which the user has already chosen between.\n  - `reports/validation/num-*.ogg`, listed in `num-clips.md`: \"3.14\", \"0.5\" and \".5\", each next to the same sentence with \"point\" written out. Each pair is nearly the same length, and the \".5\" pair is identical, but only listening settles how Kokoro reads them.\n\n## Other\n- **api vitest:** `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` is pinned in `api/vitest.config.ts`. The R2 GET keys were already pinned. The suite passes with the local `api/.dev.vars` present.\n- **Docs:** `item-lifecycle.md`, `item-contract.md` and `local-development.md` describe the status check and the replacement. Unslop round 1 found 15 issues and I applied 11; the other 4 are in older sentences this change doesn't touch. Round 2 found nothing that slipped back.\n\n## Checks\n```\napi       Tests 56 passed (6 files) · lint clean · types 0   (with api/.dev.vars present)\npipeline  Tests 136 passed | 1 skipped (13 files) · lint clean · types 0 · vite build ✓\n```\n\n<subagent-ask>\nHow should the spoken form treat numbers (\"3.14\", \"0.5\", \".5\") once the user has listened to `reports/validation/num-*.ogg`: leave them as written, or write out \"point\"? Until then numbers stay as written.\n</subagent-ask>\nd2f165d docs: describe the instance check on re-queue and retry, and the spoken dot\n93f56de fix(pipeline): read a dot before a letter as the word dot\n0690682 fix(api): replace only an instance that never ran its first step\n471d885 fix(pipeline): keep the space before a word that starts with a dot\nca37067 fix(api): replace an ended Workflow instance instead of restarting it","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"17f43650-b71c-41d9-b3a3-d102f9eb7637","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"24325bc8-ce9f-4e2b-b398-0bdd142311ad","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f