{"parentUuid":"088d4abb-6813-44c7-8e17-0951aabeb963","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwBM8GrgwaifFE6DApgc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"F1 and F4 are done and committed, and D4 now passes locally.\n\n**F4**\n- **Commits:** the narrowed rule is `0690682`, its docs are in `d2f165d`.\n- **Row names an instance:** the item is always restarted from the step that failed.\n- **Row has no instance id:** an instance that errored or was terminated before its first step is replaced with `<itemId>-2`, `-3` and so on.\n- **Local difference:** locally, `create` on an existing id hands back that instance instead of throwing \"already exists\", so the API reads the status of whatever `create` returns. One gap remains, locally only: if the `-2` instance also dies before its first step, that item stays stuck. On Cloudflare it moves on to `-3`.\n- **D4 rerun:** all three stuck items recovered. Two reached `ready`. example.com failed in the recipe step with \"authoring gave up\", which is the right result for a page that isn't an article.\n\n**F1**\n- **Commits:** `471d885` and `93f56de`.\n- **Space before the dot:** it's kept again. The cause was a sanitize regex that removed every space before a dot.\n- **Dot read as \"dot\":**\n  - A dot before a letter is read as \"dot\": \"dot wast\", \"index dot html\", \"example dot com\".\n  - Numbers, full stops, ellipses and \"e.g.\" / \"i.e.\" / \"U.S.\" are left as written.\n  - The rule also applies to the describer's output.\n  - Side effect: autolinks now read \"https://x dot test\" and \"a@b dot com\".\n- **Docs:** `article-extraction.md` and `what-gets-read-aloud.md` describe the rule.\n\n**Checks:**\n- api: 56 tests pass, with your local `.dev.vars` present, since the R2 vars are now pinned.\n- pipeline: 136 tests pass, and build is clean.\n\nThe number question is still yours: `num-*.ogg` against `num-*-point-*.ogg`. Should numbers stay as written, or be spelled out with \"point\"? After that, all that's left is closing the subagent and deleting its stale worktree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2570,"cache_read_input_tokens":296162,"output_tokens":738,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":47},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2570,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":296162,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2570},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d60c012c-3451-4d24-8de4-df492d1a28b8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwBM7cRAecQwZP6jtJHr","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c4eb9854-5eba-4f32-8dad-6903d1ec3e7f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:43:19.576Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
