{"parentUuid":"c0ba5bc2-cd6a-4d01-905c-8a030bd2a24b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwCwC4czfF3MVgAFHGpR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JS9RHhisrdn8wfoRGegbHu","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research drizzle with D1","subagent_type":"mahou:researcher","prompt":"Question: how does Drizzle ORM (current stable versions of drizzle-orm and drizzle-kit as of October 2026) work with Cloudflare D1 from Workers, for a pnpm monorepo where a source-only TypeScript package `@nagara/common` (no build step) holds the schema and query functions used by two Workers, and drizzle-kit generates the SQL migrations that `wrangler d1 migrations apply` then applies (locally with --local --persist-to, remotely in CI)?\n\nReport facts with sources (official docs, release notes, GitHub issues), no recommendation:\n1. Current stable versions of drizzle-orm and drizzle-kit; any v1 beta status and whether D1 support differs between 0.x and 1.x.\n2. The D1 driver: `drizzle(env.DB)` import path, how to pass the schema, relational queries (`db.query.x.findFirst`) support on D1, `db.batch([...])` support and its atomicity on D1, transactions (D1 has no interactive transactions: what drizzle does with `db.transaction` on D1).\n3. Schema for SQLite: `sqliteTable`, text/integer/real columns, `integer({mode: 'boolean'})`, `text({mode: 'json'}).$type<T>()` for JSON columns stored as TEXT, CHECK constraints (`check()` support and whether drizzle-kit emits them), unique constraints, indexes, foreign keys, `$defaultFn`, enums via `text({enum: [...]})` (does it emit a CHECK?). Whether `json_valid` CHECK constraints can be expressed.\n4. drizzle-kit `generate` with `dialect: 'sqlite'` and `driver: 'd1-http'` or none: the output folder layout (SQL files plus `meta/_journal.json` and snapshots), file naming, and whether `wrangler d1 migrations apply` reads that folder correctly (it applies `*.sql` in order and tracks them in `d1_migrations`); known issues with the `meta/` folder, statement breakpoints (`--> statement-breakpoint`) and wrangler. Custom migration names (`--name`).\n5. Conditional updates: expressing `UPDATE ... WHERE status = 'failed' AND retry_count < ?` returning whether a row changed (`.returning()` on D1, or `meta.changes`), and an `INSERT ... SELECT COALESCE(MAX(version),0)+1 ...` (insert-select support in drizzle for SQLite, or `sql` template fallback).\n6. Using drizzle in tests under `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` with migrations applied from the drizzle folder via `readD1Migrations`/`applyD1Migrations` (does readD1Migrations handle the `--> statement-breakpoint` markers and the `meta/` folder?).\n7. Bundle size impact on a Worker, and any Workers/workerd compatibility caveats.\nKeep the answer under 900 words, each fact with its source URL.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1608,"cache_read_input_tokens":310946,"output_tokens":1232,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":94},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1608,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1232,"cache_read_input_tokens":310946,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1608,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1608},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JS9RHhisrdn8wfoRGegbHu":{"description":"Research drizzle with D1","subagent_type":"mahou:researcher","prompt":"Question: how does Drizzle ORM (current stable versions of drizzle-orm and drizzle-kit as of October 2026) work with Cloudflare D1 from Workers, for a pnpm monorepo where a source-only TypeScript package `@nagara/common` (no build step) holds the schema and query functions used by two Workers, and drizzle-kit generates the SQL migrations that `wrangler d1 migrations apply` then applies (locally with --local --persist-to, remotely in CI)?\n\nReport facts with sources (official docs, release notes, GitHub issues), no recommendation:\n1. Current stable versions of drizzle-orm and drizzle-kit; any v1 beta status and whether D1 support differs between 0.x and 1.x.\n2. The D1 driver: `drizzle(env.DB)` import path, how to pass the schema, relational queries (`db.query.x.findFirst`) support on D1, `db.batch([...])` support and its atomicity on D1, transactions (D1 has no interactive transactions: what drizzle does with `db.transaction` on D1).\n3. Schema for SQLite: `sqliteTable`, text/integer/real columns, `integer({mode: 'boolean'})`, `text({mode: 'json'}).$type<T>()` for JSON columns stored as TEXT, CHECK constraints (`check()` support and whether drizzle-kit emits them), unique constraints, indexes, foreign keys, `$defaultFn`, enums via `text({enum: [...]})` (does it emit a CHECK?). Whether `json_valid` CHECK constraints can be expressed.\n4. drizzle-kit `generate` with `dialect: 'sqlite'` and `driver: 'd1-http'` or none: the output folder layout (SQL files plus `meta/_journal.json` and snapshots), file naming, and whether `wrangler d1 migrations apply` reads that folder correctly (it applies `*.sql` in order and tracks them in `d1_migrations`); known issues with the `meta/` folder, statement breakpoints (`--> statement-breakpoint`) and wrangler. Custom migration names (`--name`).\n5. Conditional updates: expressing `UPDATE ... WHERE status = 'failed' AND retry_count < ?` returning whether a row changed (`.returning()` on D1, or `meta.changes`), and an `INSERT ... SELECT COALESCE(MAX(version),0)+1 ...` (insert-select support in drizzle for SQLite, or `sql` template fallback).\n6. Using drizzle in tests under `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` with migrations applied from the drizzle folder via `readD1Migrations`/`applyD1Migrations` (does readD1Migrations handle the `--> statement-breakpoint` markers and the `meta/` folder?).\n7. Bundle size impact on a Worker, and any Workers/workerd compatibility caveats.\nKeep the answer under 900 words, each fact with its source URL.","run_in_background":"true"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cff91dee-e9e1-4b20-8a1d-e2b237f89269","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwCwBd5z8iQpo3JZMuAz","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:program-design-with-canvas","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2e75317-4f1c-4e7e-997a-b8708c9c026a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:04:12.642Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
