{"parentUuid":"47d46c97-76b0-44a3-bc23-f17e76c1f358","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwD9uUqqkHvGnsP76MpD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bu5NiSZD4KcnJ2e14b6Mhe","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/drizzle.md","content":"# Program design: D1 through drizzle\n\nRepository `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara`, branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`. Covers moving every D1 read and write into `common/` as drizzle queries, with drizzle-kit generating the migrations from a schema in `common/`. Leaves out the DomainQueue's Durable Object storage (not D1) and every non-database module.\n\n## 1 common/ package\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  ws@{ shape: doc, label: \"pnpm workspace\" }\n  common[\"common/<br/>@nagara/common<br/>source only\"]\n  kit[\"drizzle-kit 0.31.11<br/>dev dependency\"]\n  orm[\"drizzle-orm 0.45.4<br/>dependency\"]\n  mig@{ shape: doc, label: \"common/migrations/<br/>0000_initial.sql<br/>meta/\" }\n  api[\"api/<br/>nagara-api\"]\n  pipe[\"pipeline/<br/>nagara\"]\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1 nagara\" }\n  ws --- common\n  ws --- api\n  ws --- pipe\n  common -->|\"uses\"| orm\n  kit -->|\"generates from<br/>the schema\"| mig\n  api -->|\"imports the queries\"| common\n  pipe -->|\"imports the queries\"| common\n  mig -->|\"wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply\"| d1\n  classDef pkg fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class common,api,pipe pkg\n  class d1 store\n  class kit,orm,mig tool\n```\n\n`common/` gains `drizzle-orm` 0.45.4 as a dependency and `drizzle-kit` 0.31.11 as a dev dependency, both the npm `latest` tags. The 1.0 release candidate is not used: it writes each migration into its own timestamped subfolder, and both `wrangler d1 migrations apply` and the tests' `readD1Migrations` read only top-level `.sql` files, so neither would find a migration. A trial of 0.31.11's output (a `0000_initial.sql` with `--> statement-breakpoint` comments and a `meta/` folder of snapshots) applied cleanly with `wrangler d1 migrations apply --local`, CHECKs and `json_valid` included.\n\n`common/drizzle.config.ts` names the dialect `sqlite`, the schema `src/db/schema.ts` and the output `migrations/`. A new script `db:generate` runs `drizzle-kit generate`. `migrate:local` stays as it is. Nothing is built: the Workers bundle `drizzle-orm` from `common/`'s source, about 20 KB gzipped.\n\n### 1.2 How a schema change reaches D1\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  edit[\"edit src/db/schema.ts\"]\n  gen[\"pnpm db:generate<br/>(drizzle-kit generate)\"]\n  file@{ shape: doc, label: \"migrations/<br/>NNNN_name.sql + meta/\" }\n  review{\"SQL reviewed<br/>and committed\"}\n  local[\"pnpm migrate:local<br/>.wrangler-state\"]\n  tests[\"readD1Migrations<br/>in both test configs\"]\n  ci[\"CI common-checks:<br/>generate, then<br/>git diff --exit-code\"]\n  remote[\"CI migrate job:<br/>d1 migrations apply --remote\"]\n  edit --> gen --> file --> review\n  review --> local\n  review --> tests\n  review --> ci\n  ci -->|\"schema and SQL agree\"| remote\n  ci -.->|\"a schema edit with<br/>no migration fails\"| edit\n```\n\nThe SQL is generated, then reviewed and committed like code; wrangler applies it everywhere it does today. CI adds one leg to `common-checks`: run `drizzle-kit generate` and fail when it leaves a new or changed file, so a schema edit without its migration never deploys. The current `0001_initial.sql` is replaced by a generated `0000_initial.sql`: the production database does not exist yet, so there is no applied history to keep. The local `.wrangler-state/` records `0001_initial.sql` as applied, so it is reset once (moved aside, then `pnpm migrate:local`).\n\n### 1.3 Schema and queries\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n  class items {\n    id text PK\n    url text\n    title text?\n    voice text\n    status ItemStatus CHECK\n    created_at text\n    updated_at text\n    queued_at text\n    workflow_instance_id text?\n    current_step Step?\n    extraction_domain text?\n    recipe_version_id text? FK\n    retry_count integer = 0\n    duration real?\n    audio_format text?\n    units json Unit[]? CHECK json_valid\n    degradations json Degradation[]? CHECK json_valid\n    error text?\n  }\n  class recipe_versions {\n    id text PK\n    domain text\n    version integer\n    script text\n    created_at text\n    UNIQUE domain, version\n  }\n  class cost_entries {\n    id text PK\n    item_id text FK\n    type CostType CHECK\n    quantity real\n    unit CostUnit CHECK\n    dollars real\n    cached boolean = false\n    detail json? CHECK json_valid\n    created_at text\n    INDEX item_id\n  }\n  items --> recipe_versions : recipe_version_id\n  cost_entries --> items : item_id\n```\n\nThe schema keeps every table, column, CHECK, foreign key and index of `0001_initial.sql`, with the column keys in snake_case so the row types keep their field names. The status, cost type and cost unit columns are `text({ enum })` typed from `ITEM_STATUS`, `COST_TYPE` and `COST_UNIT`, plus an explicit `check()`, because drizzle's enum emits no CHECK. JSON columns are `text({ mode: \"json\" }).$type<…>()`, so drizzle encodes and decodes them and `json-column.ts` goes. `cached` becomes `integer({ mode: \"boolean\" })`, so the row reads back a boolean instead of 0 or 1.\n\nThe row types derive from the schema: `ItemRow`, `RecipeVersionRow` and `CostEntryRow` become `typeof table.$inferSelect`, replacing the hand-written types in `item.ts`, `recipe.ts` and `ledger.ts`; the constant maps stay where they are.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph store [\"common/src/db\"]\n    direction TB\n    db[\"database(d1)<br/>drizzle with the schema\"]\n    read[\"readItem\"]\n    status[\"writeStatus\"]\n    insert[\"insertQueued\"]\n    claimR[\"claimRetry\"]\n    claimQ[\"claimRequeue\"]\n    fetched[\"recordFetch\"]\n    extracted[\"recordExtraction\"]\n    unitsW[\"writeUnits\"]\n    ready[\"writeReady\"]\n    cost[\"costEntry\"]\n    current[\"currentRecipe\"]\n    save[\"saveRecipeVersion\"]\n  end\n  api[\"api/ routes\"]\n  pipe[\"pipeline/ steps\"]\n  api --> db\n  api --> read\n  api --> status\n  api --> insert\n  api --> claimR\n  api --> claimQ\n  pipe --> db\n  pipe --> read\n  pipe --> status\n  pipe --> fetched\n  pipe --> extracted\n  pipe --> unitsW\n  pipe --> ready\n  pipe --> cost\n  pipe --> current\n  pipe --> save\n```\n\n| Query | Answers | Replaces |\n|---|---|---|\n| `database(d1)` | the drizzle client over a D1 binding, with the schema | `env.DB.prepare` everywhere |\n| `readItem(db, id)` | the item row or null | `common` `readItem` (raw SELECT, manual JSON decode) |\n| `writeStatus(db, id, write)` | queued or generating with a step; failed with a step and an error | `common` `writeStatus` |\n| `insertQueued(db, {url, voice})` | the new item's id | `api/src/items/create.ts` |\n| `claimRetry(db, id, retryMax)` | whether this call claimed the retry (one conditional UPDATE, `.returning({ id })`, claimed when a row comes back) | `api/src/items/retry-claim.ts` |\n| `claimRequeue(db, id, staleBefore)` | whether this call claimed the re-queue, same shape | the UPDATE inside `api/src/items/requeue.ts` |\n| `recordFetch(db, id, {instanceId, domain})` | the fetch step's write of the instance id and domain | the UPDATE in `fetch.ts` |\n| `recordExtraction(db, id, {title, units, recipeVersionId})` | the recipe step's write | the UPDATE in `recipe.ts` |\n| `writeUnits(db, id, {units, degradations})` | the units and degradations write the images and describe steps share | the two duplicated UPDATEs in `images.ts` and `describe.ts` |\n| `writeReady(db, id, {units, duration, format})` | the store step's ready write | the UPDATE in `synthesis.ts` |\n| `costEntry(db, entry)` | one cost ledger row | `pipeline/src/workflow/ledger.ts` |\n| `currentRecipe(db, domain)` | the domain's latest recipe version or null | `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts` |\n| `saveRecipeVersion(db, domain, script)` | the new version's id; one `INSERT … SELECT COALESCE(MAX(version), 0) + 1` through `db.insert().select()` | `saveVersion` in `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts` |\n\nEvery write returns the drizzle query without awaiting it. A caller awaits it alone, or hands several to `db.batch([...])` where today's code batches (fetch: `recordFetch` and the Firecrawl `costEntry`; describe: `writeUnits` and the describer entries; store: `writeReady` and the TTS entry). D1 runs a batch as one transaction. `db.transaction` is not used: D1 rejects `BEGIN` from a binding.\n\n### 1.4 Module list\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  subgraph new [\"new\"]\n    direction TB\n    n1[\"common/drizzle.config.ts\"]\n    n2[\"common/src/db/schema.ts<br/>the three tables\"]\n    n3[\"common/src/db/database.ts\"]\n    n4[\"common/src/db/items/<br/>read-item, write-status,<br/>insert-queued, claim-retry,<br/>claim-requeue, record-fetch,<br/>record-extraction,<br/>write-units, write-ready\"]\n    n5[\"common/src/db/cost-entry.ts\"]\n    n6[\"common/src/db/recipes/<br/>current-recipe,<br/>save-recipe-version\"]\n    n7[\"common/migrations/<br/>0000_initial.sql, meta/\"]\n  end\n  subgraph touched [\"touched\"]\n    direction TB\n    t1[\"common/package.json<br/>deps, db:generate\"]\n    t2[\"common/src/item.ts,<br/>ledger.ts, recipe.ts<br/>row types from schema\"]\n    t3[\"common/src/index.ts\"]\n    t4[\"api/src/routes/*,<br/>api/src/items/*<br/>call common\"]\n    t5[\"pipeline/src/workflow/<br/>steps/*, recipe step<br/>call common\"]\n    t6[\"test helpers in api/,<br/>pipeline/, common/<br/>seed through drizzle\"]\n    t7[\".github/workflows/<br/>cloudflare.yml<br/>schema check leg\"]\n  end\n  subgraph deleted [\"deleted\"]\n    direction TB\n    d1[\"common/src/item-store/\"]\n    d2[\"common/migrations/<br/>0001_initial.sql\"]\n    d3[\"api/src/items/create.ts,<br/>retry-claim.ts\"]\n    d4[\"pipeline/src/workflow/<br/>ledger.ts\"]\n    d5[\"saveVersion, currentRecipe<br/>in pipeline/src/recipes/<br/>store.ts\"]\n  end\n  classDef n fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef t fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef d fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,n6,n7 n\n  class t1,t2,t3,t4,t5,t6,t7 t\n  class d1,d2,d3,d4,d5 d\n```\n\nThe queries go under `common/src/db/`, grouped by table, one function per module. `item-store/` is folded into `db/items/`, because it held the same kind of code. `domainFromUrl` stays in `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts`: it parses a URL and touches no table. `api/src/items/requeue.ts` and `restart.ts` stay: they decide when to claim and how to restart the Workflow, and call `claimRequeue`. The ids keep their prefixes and are minted inside the query that inserts the row (`itm_`, `rcp_`, `cst_`).\n\n## 2 api/ and pipeline/ callers\n\n### 2.1 Callstack: the retry route\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  req[\"POST /items/:id/retry\"]\n  db[\"database(env.DB)\"]\n  read[\"readItem\"]\n  missing{\"row?\"}\n  r404([\"404\"])\n  claim[\"claimRetry(db, id, RETRY_MAX)\"]\n  won{\"claimed?\"}\n  r409([\"409, the item<br/>as it is\"])\n  restart[\"restartItem<br/>(Workflow)\"]\n  threw{\"threw?\"}\n  fail[\"writeStatus failed<br/>with the error\"]\n  r202([\"202 with readItem\"])\n  req --> db --> read --> missing\n  missing -->|\"no\"| r404\n  missing -->|\"yes\"| claim --> won\n  won -->|\"no\"| r409\n  won -->|\"yes\"| restart --> threw\n  threw -->|\"yes\"| fail --> r202\n  threw -->|\"no\"| r202\n  classDef q fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef ok fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef bad fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class db,read,claim,fail q\n  class r202 ok\n  class r404,r409 bad\n```\n\nEvery route builds the client once per request with `database(env.DB)` and passes it down; no route or step writes SQL. Enqueue calls `insertQueued`, then `readItem`; poll calls `readItem` and, through `requeueIfStale`, `claimRequeue`. Each pipeline step builds the client from its env the same way and calls the step's query, batching where it does today. The behaviour of every route and step is unchanged; the API and pipeline suites pass unmodified apart from their seeding helpers.\n\n## 3 Standards\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  claude@{ shape: doc, label: \"CLAUDE.md\" }\n  inv@{ shape: doc, label: \"invariants.md\" }\n  notes@{ shape: doc, label: \"docs/technical-design\" }\n  wiki@{ shape: doc, label: \"mahou wiki\" }\n  g1[\"code style: every D1<br/>read and write is a drizzle<br/>query in common/src/db,<br/>even when one Worker uses it\"]\n  g2[\"invariant 7: the schema is<br/>common/src/db/schema.ts;<br/>drizzle-kit generates the<br/>migration, reviewed and<br/>committed\"]\n  g3[\"common-package,<br/>persistence-and-storage,<br/>deployment-and-ci,<br/>local-development\"]\n  g4[\"new entry: drizzle on D1<br/>(0.x layout, no transaction,<br/>enum emits no CHECK)\"]\n  claude --> g1\n  inv --> g2\n  claude --> g2\n  notes --> g3\n  wiki --> g4\n```\n\nThe CLAUDE.md code-style rule that keeps single-Worker code out of `common/` gains an exception for the database: every D1 read and write is a drizzle query in `common/src/db/`. Invariant 7 changes from hand-written SQL to SQL generated by drizzle-kit from the schema, reviewed and committed. \"When adding something\" gets a line: a schema change edits `schema.ts` and runs `pnpm db:generate`. The notes that describe the item row's reads and writes, the migrations, CI and the local reset are updated. The local wiki gains an entry for drizzle on D1 with what the trial and the research found.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3677,"cache_read_input_tokens":328915,"output_tokens":5889,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":83},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3677,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5889,"cache_read_input_tokens":328915,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3677},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Bu5NiSZD4KcnJ2e14b6Mhe":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/drizzle.md","content":"# Program design: D1 through drizzle\n\nRepository `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara`, branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`. Covers moving every D1 read and write into `common/` as drizzle queries, with drizzle-kit generating the migrations from a schema in `common/`. Leaves out the DomainQueue's Durable Object storage (not D1) and every non-database module.\n\n## 1 common/ package\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  ws@{ shape: doc, label: \"pnpm workspace\" }\n  common[\"common/<br/>@nagara/common<br/>source only\"]\n  kit[\"drizzle-kit 0.31.11<br/>dev dependency\"]\n  orm[\"drizzle-orm 0.45.4<br/>dependency\"]\n  mig@{ shape: doc, label: \"common/migrations/<br/>0000_initial.sql<br/>meta/\" }\n  api[\"api/<br/>nagara-api\"]\n  pipe[\"pipeline/<br/>nagara\"]\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1 nagara\" }\n  ws --- common\n  ws --- api\n  ws --- pipe\n  common -->|\"uses\"| orm\n  kit -->|\"generates from<br/>the schema\"| mig\n  api -->|\"imports the queries\"| common\n  pipe -->|\"imports the queries\"| common\n  mig -->|\"wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply\"| d1\n  classDef pkg fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class common,api,pipe pkg\n  class d1 store\n  class kit,orm,mig tool\n```\n\n`common/` gains `drizzle-orm` 0.45.4 as a dependency and `drizzle-kit` 0.31.11 as a dev dependency, both the npm `latest` tags. The 1.0 release candidate is not used: it writes each migration into its own timestamped subfolder, and both `wrangler d1 migrations apply` and the tests' `readD1Migrations` read only top-level `.sql` files, so neither would find a migration. A trial of 0.31.11's output (a `0000_initial.sql` with `--> statement-breakpoint` comments and a `meta/` folder of snapshots) applied cleanly with `wrangler d1 migrations apply --local`, CHECKs and `json_valid` included.\n\n`common/drizzle.config.ts` names the dialect `sqlite`, the schema `src/db/schema.ts` and the output `migrations/`. A new script `db:generate` runs `drizzle-kit generate`. `migrate:local` stays as it is. Nothing is built: the Workers bundle `drizzle-orm` from `common/`'s source, about 20 KB gzipped.\n\n### 1.2 How a schema change reaches D1\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  edit[\"edit src/db/schema.ts\"]\n  gen[\"pnpm db:generate<br/>(drizzle-kit generate)\"]\n  file@{ shape: doc, label: \"migrations/<br/>NNNN_name.sql + meta/\" }\n  review{\"SQL reviewed<br/>and committed\"}\n  local[\"pnpm migrate:local<br/>.wrangler-state\"]\n  tests[\"readD1Migrations<br/>in both test configs\"]\n  ci[\"CI common-checks:<br/>generate, then<br/>git diff --exit-code\"]\n  remote[\"CI migrate job:<br/>d1 migrations apply --remote\"]\n  edit --> gen --> file --> review\n  review --> local\n  review --> tests\n  review --> ci\n  ci -->|\"schema and SQL agree\"| remote\n  ci -.->|\"a schema edit with<br/>no migration fails\"| edit\n```\n\nThe SQL is generated, then reviewed and committed like code; wrangler applies it everywhere it does today. CI adds one leg to `common-checks`: run `drizzle-kit generate` and fail when it leaves a new or changed file, so a schema edit without its migration never deploys. The current `0001_initial.sql` is replaced by a generated `0000_initial.sql`: the production database does not exist yet, so there is no applied history to keep. The local `.wrangler-state/` records `0001_initial.sql` as applied, so it is reset once (moved aside, then `pnpm migrate:local`).\n\n### 1.3 Schema and queries\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n  class items {\n    id text PK\n    url text\n    title text?\n    voice text\n    status ItemStatus CHECK\n    created_at text\n    updated_at text\n    queued_at text\n    workflow_instance_id text?\n    current_step Step?\n    extraction_domain text?\n    recipe_version_id text? FK\n    retry_count integer = 0\n    duration real?\n    audio_format text?\n    units json Unit[]? CHECK json_valid\n    degradations json Degradation[]? CHECK json_valid\n    error text?\n  }\n  class recipe_versions {\n    id text PK\n    domain text\n    version integer\n    script text\n    created_at text\n    UNIQUE domain, version\n  }\n  class cost_entries {\n    id text PK\n    item_id text FK\n    type CostType CHECK\n    quantity real\n    unit CostUnit CHECK\n    dollars real\n    cached boolean = false\n    detail json? CHECK json_valid\n    created_at text\n    INDEX item_id\n  }\n  items --> recipe_versions : recipe_version_id\n  cost_entries --> items : item_id\n```\n\nThe schema keeps every table, column, CHECK, foreign key and index of `0001_initial.sql`, with the column keys in snake_case so the row types keep their field names. The status, cost type and cost unit columns are `text({ enum })` typed from `ITEM_STATUS`, `COST_TYPE` and `COST_UNIT`, plus an explicit `check()`, because drizzle's enum emits no CHECK. JSON columns are `text({ mode: \"json\" }).$type<…>()`, so drizzle encodes and decodes them and `json-column.ts` goes. `cached` becomes `integer({ mode: \"boolean\" })`, so the row reads back a boolean instead of 0 or 1.\n\nThe row types derive from the schema: `ItemRow`, `RecipeVersionRow` and `CostEntryRow` become `typeof table.$inferSelect`, replacing the hand-written types in `item.ts`, `recipe.ts` and `ledger.ts`; the constant maps stay where they are.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph store [\"common/src/db\"]\n    direction TB\n    db[\"database(d1)<br/>drizzle with the schema\"]\n    read[\"readItem\"]\n    status[\"writeStatus\"]\n    insert[\"insertQueued\"]\n    claimR[\"claimRetry\"]\n    claimQ[\"claimRequeue\"]\n    fetched[\"recordFetch\"]\n    extracted[\"recordExtraction\"]\n    unitsW[\"writeUnits\"]\n    ready[\"writeReady\"]\n    cost[\"costEntry\"]\n    current[\"currentRecipe\"]\n    save[\"saveRecipeVersion\"]\n  end\n  api[\"api/ routes\"]\n  pipe[\"pipeline/ steps\"]\n  api --> db\n  api --> read\n  api --> status\n  api --> insert\n  api --> claimR\n  api --> claimQ\n  pipe --> db\n  pipe --> read\n  pipe --> status\n  pipe --> fetched\n  pipe --> extracted\n  pipe --> unitsW\n  pipe --> ready\n  pipe --> cost\n  pipe --> current\n  pipe --> save\n```\n\n| Query | Answers | Replaces |\n|---|---|---|\n| `database(d1)` | the drizzle client over a D1 binding, with the schema | `env.DB.prepare` everywhere |\n| `readItem(db, id)` | the item row or null | `common` `readItem` (raw SELECT, manual JSON decode) |\n| `writeStatus(db, id, write)` | queued or generating with a step; failed with a step and an error | `common` `writeStatus` |\n| `insertQueued(db, {url, voice})` | the new item's id | `api/src/items/create.ts` |\n| `claimRetry(db, id, retryMax)` | whether this call claimed the retry (one conditional UPDATE, `.returning({ id })`, claimed when a row comes back) | `api/src/items/retry-claim.ts` |\n| `claimRequeue(db, id, staleBefore)` | whether this call claimed the re-queue, same shape | the UPDATE inside `api/src/items/requeue.ts` |\n| `recordFetch(db, id, {instanceId, domain})` | the fetch step's write of the instance id and domain | the UPDATE in `fetch.ts` |\n| `recordExtraction(db, id, {title, units, recipeVersionId})` | the recipe step's write | the UPDATE in `recipe.ts` |\n| `writeUnits(db, id, {units, degradations})` | the units and degradations write the images and describe steps share | the two duplicated UPDATEs in `images.ts` and `describe.ts` |\n| `writeReady(db, id, {units, duration, format})` | the store step's ready write | the UPDATE in `synthesis.ts` |\n| `costEntry(db, entry)` | one cost ledger row | `pipeline/src/workflow/ledger.ts` |\n| `currentRecipe(db, domain)` | the domain's latest recipe version or null | `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts` |\n| `saveRecipeVersion(db, domain, script)` | the new version's id; one `INSERT … SELECT COALESCE(MAX(version), 0) + 1` through `db.insert().select()` | `saveVersion` in `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts` |\n\nEvery write returns the drizzle query without awaiting it. A caller awaits it alone, or hands several to `db.batch([...])` where today's code batches (fetch: `recordFetch` and the Firecrawl `costEntry`; describe: `writeUnits` and the describer entries; store: `writeReady` and the TTS entry). D1 runs a batch as one transaction. `db.transaction` is not used: D1 rejects `BEGIN` from a binding.\n\n### 1.4 Module list\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  subgraph new [\"new\"]\n    direction TB\n    n1[\"common/drizzle.config.ts\"]\n    n2[\"common/src/db/schema.ts<br/>the three tables\"]\n    n3[\"common/src/db/database.ts\"]\n    n4[\"common/src/db/items/<br/>read-item, write-status,<br/>insert-queued, claim-retry,<br/>claim-requeue, record-fetch,<br/>record-extraction,<br/>write-units, write-ready\"]\n    n5[\"common/src/db/cost-entry.ts\"]\n    n6[\"common/src/db/recipes/<br/>current-recipe,<br/>save-recipe-version\"]\n    n7[\"common/migrations/<br/>0000_initial.sql, meta/\"]\n  end\n  subgraph touched [\"touched\"]\n    direction TB\n    t1[\"common/package.json<br/>deps, db:generate\"]\n    t2[\"common/src/item.ts,<br/>ledger.ts, recipe.ts<br/>row types from schema\"]\n    t3[\"common/src/index.ts\"]\n    t4[\"api/src/routes/*,<br/>api/src/items/*<br/>call common\"]\n    t5[\"pipeline/src/workflow/<br/>steps/*, recipe step<br/>call common\"]\n    t6[\"test helpers in api/,<br/>pipeline/, common/<br/>seed through drizzle\"]\n    t7[\".github/workflows/<br/>cloudflare.yml<br/>schema check leg\"]\n  end\n  subgraph deleted [\"deleted\"]\n    direction TB\n    d1[\"common/src/item-store/\"]\n    d2[\"common/migrations/<br/>0001_initial.sql\"]\n    d3[\"api/src/items/create.ts,<br/>retry-claim.ts\"]\n    d4[\"pipeline/src/workflow/<br/>ledger.ts\"]\n    d5[\"saveVersion, currentRecipe<br/>in pipeline/src/recipes/<br/>store.ts\"]\n  end\n  classDef n fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef t fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef d fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,n6,n7 n\n  class t1,t2,t3,t4,t5,t6,t7 t\n  class d1,d2,d3,d4,d5 d\n```\n\nThe queries go under `common/src/db/`, grouped by table, one function per module. `item-store/` is folded into `db/items/`, because it held the same kind of code. `domainFromUrl` stays in `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts`: it parses a URL and touches no table. `api/src/items/requeue.ts` and `restart.ts` stay: they decide when to claim and how to restart the Workflow, and call `claimRequeue`. The ids keep their prefixes and are minted inside the query that inserts the row (`itm_`, `rcp_`, `cst_`).\n\n## 2 api/ and pipeline/ callers\n\n### 2.1 Callstack: the retry route\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  req[\"POST /items/:id/retry\"]\n  db[\"database(env.DB)\"]\n  read[\"readItem\"]\n  missing{\"row?\"}\n  r404([\"404\"])\n  claim[\"claimRetry(db, id, RETRY_MAX)\"]\n  won{\"claimed?\"}\n  r409([\"409, the item<br/>as it is\"])\n  restart[\"restartItem<br/>(Workflow)\"]\n  threw{\"threw?\"}\n  fail[\"writeStatus failed<br/>with the error\"]\n  r202([\"202 with readItem\"])\n  req --> db --> read --> missing\n  missing -->|\"no\"| r404\n  missing -->|\"yes\"| claim --> won\n  won -->|\"no\"| r409\n  won -->|\"yes\"| restart --> threw\n  threw -->|\"yes\"| fail --> r202\n  threw -->|\"no\"| r202\n  classDef q fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef ok fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef bad fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class db,read,claim,fail q\n  class r202 ok\n  class r404,r409 bad\n```\n\nEvery route builds the client once per request with `database(env.DB)` and passes it down; no route or step writes SQL. Enqueue calls `insertQueued`, then `readItem`; poll calls `readItem` and, through `requeueIfStale`, `claimRequeue`. Each pipeline step builds the client from its env the same way and calls the step's query, batching where it does today. The behaviour of every route and step is unchanged; the API and pipeline suites pass unmodified apart from their seeding helpers.\n\n## 3 Standards\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  claude@{ shape: doc, label: \"CLAUDE.md\" }\n  inv@{ shape: doc, label: \"invariants.md\" }\n  notes@{ shape: doc, label: \"docs/technical-design\" }\n  wiki@{ shape: doc, label: \"mahou wiki\" }\n  g1[\"code style: every D1<br/>read and write is a drizzle<br/>query in common/src/db,<br/>even when one Worker uses it\"]\n  g2[\"invariant 7: the schema is<br/>common/src/db/schema.ts;<br/>drizzle-kit generates the<br/>migration, reviewed and<br/>committed\"]\n  g3[\"common-package,<br/>persistence-and-storage,<br/>deployment-and-ci,<br/>local-development\"]\n  g4[\"new entry: drizzle on D1<br/>(0.x layout, no transaction,<br/>enum emits no CHECK)\"]\n  claude --> g1\n  inv --> g2\n  claude --> g2\n  notes --> g3\n  wiki --> g4\n```\n\nThe CLAUDE.md code-style rule that keeps single-Worker code out of `common/` gains an exception for the database: every D1 read and write is a drizzle query in `common/src/db/`. Invariant 7 changes from hand-written SQL to SQL generated by drizzle-kit from the schema, reviewed and committed. \"When adding something\" gets a line: a schema change edits `schema.ts` and runs `pnpm db:generate`. The notes that describe the item row's reads and writes, the migrations, CI and the local reset are updated. The local wiki gains an entry for drizzle on D1 with what the trial and the research found.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c622585a-4399-416e-b969-65654b710780","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwD9tvbdtcFmNHaYtYy2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae136789-555b-4f97-82cc-7add0cdca9d5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:07:41.986Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"ae136789-555b-4f97-82cc-7add0cdca9d5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"80fda331-2e00-4fae-8db7-abe6c474de14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bu5NiSZD4KcnJ2e14b6Mhe","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/drizzle.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"477303e2-8fc9-409e-8f27-ff0cdabb539b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:07:42.043Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/drizzle.md","content":"# Program design: D1 through drizzle\n\nRepository `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara`, branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`. Covers moving every D1 read and write into `common/` as drizzle queries, with drizzle-kit generating the migrations from a schema in `common/`. Leaves out the DomainQueue's Durable Object storage (not D1) and every non-database module.\n\n## 1 common/ package\n\n### 1.1 Package layout\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  ws@{ shape: doc, label: \"pnpm workspace\" }\n  common[\"common/<br/>@nagara/common<br/>source only\"]\n  kit[\"drizzle-kit 0.31.11<br/>dev dependency\"]\n  orm[\"drizzle-orm 0.45.4<br/>dependency\"]\n  mig@{ shape: doc, label: \"common/migrations/<br/>0000_initial.sql<br/>meta/\" }\n  api[\"api/<br/>nagara-api\"]\n  pipe[\"pipeline/<br/>nagara\"]\n  d1@{ shape: cyl, label: \"D1 nagara\" }\n  ws --- common\n  ws --- api\n  ws --- pipe\n  common -->|\"uses\"| orm\n  kit -->|\"generates from<br/>the schema\"| mig\n  api -->|\"imports the queries\"| common\n  pipe -->|\"imports the queries\"| common\n  mig -->|\"wrangler d1<br/>migrations apply\"| d1\n  classDef pkg fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef store fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#ea580c\n  classDef tool fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#4b5563\n  class common,api,pipe pkg\n  class d1 store\n  class kit,orm,mig tool\n```\n\n`common/` gains `drizzle-orm` 0.45.4 as a dependency and `drizzle-kit` 0.31.11 as a dev dependency, both the npm `latest` tags. The 1.0 release candidate is not used: it writes each migration into its own timestamped subfolder, and both `wrangler d1 migrations apply` and the tests' `readD1Migrations` read only top-level `.sql` files, so neither would find a migration. A trial of 0.31.11's output (a `0000_initial.sql` with `--> statement-breakpoint` comments and a `meta/` folder of snapshots) applied cleanly with `wrangler d1 migrations apply --local`, CHECKs and `json_valid` included.\n\n`common/drizzle.config.ts` names the dialect `sqlite`, the schema `src/db/schema.ts` and the output `migrations/`. A new script `db:generate` runs `drizzle-kit generate`. `migrate:local` stays as it is. Nothing is built: the Workers bundle `drizzle-orm` from `common/`'s source, about 20 KB gzipped.\n\n### 1.2 How a schema change reaches D1\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  edit[\"edit src/db/schema.ts\"]\n  gen[\"pnpm db:generate<br/>(drizzle-kit generate)\"]\n  file@{ shape: doc, label: \"migrations/<br/>NNNN_name.sql + meta/\" }\n  review{\"SQL reviewed<br/>and committed\"}\n  local[\"pnpm migrate:local<br/>.wrangler-state\"]\n  tests[\"readD1Migrations<br/>in both test configs\"]\n  ci[\"CI common-checks:<br/>generate, then<br/>git diff --exit-code\"]\n  remote[\"CI migrate job:<br/>d1 migrations apply --remote\"]\n  edit --> gen --> file --> review\n  review --> local\n  review --> tests\n  review --> ci\n  ci -->|\"schema and SQL agree\"| remote\n  ci -.->|\"a schema edit with<br/>no migration fails\"| edit\n```\n\nThe SQL is generated, then reviewed and committed like code; wrangler applies it everywhere it does today. CI adds one leg to `common-checks`: run `drizzle-kit generate` and fail when it leaves a new or changed file, so a schema edit without its migration never deploys. The current `0001_initial.sql` is replaced by a generated `0000_initial.sql`: the production database does not exist yet, so there is no applied history to keep. The local `.wrangler-state/` records `0001_initial.sql` as applied, so it is reset once (moved aside, then `pnpm migrate:local`).\n\n### 1.3 Schema and queries\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n  class items {\n    id text PK\n    url text\n    title text?\n    voice text\n    status ItemStatus CHECK\n    created_at text\n    updated_at text\n    queued_at text\n    workflow_instance_id text?\n    current_step Step?\n    extraction_domain text?\n    recipe_version_id text? FK\n    retry_count integer = 0\n    duration real?\n    audio_format text?\n    units json Unit[]? CHECK json_valid\n    degradations json Degradation[]? CHECK json_valid\n    error text?\n  }\n  class recipe_versions {\n    id text PK\n    domain text\n    version integer\n    script text\n    created_at text\n    UNIQUE domain, version\n  }\n  class cost_entries {\n    id text PK\n    item_id text FK\n    type CostType CHECK\n    quantity real\n    unit CostUnit CHECK\n    dollars real\n    cached boolean = false\n    detail json? CHECK json_valid\n    created_at text\n    INDEX item_id\n  }\n  items --> recipe_versions : recipe_version_id\n  cost_entries --> items : item_id\n```\n\nThe schema keeps every table, column, CHECK, foreign key and index of `0001_initial.sql`, with the column keys in snake_case so the row types keep their field names. The status, cost type and cost unit columns are `text({ enum })` typed from `ITEM_STATUS`, `COST_TYPE` and `COST_UNIT`, plus an explicit `check()`, because drizzle's enum emits no CHECK. JSON columns are `text({ mode: \"json\" }).$type<…>()`, so drizzle encodes and decodes them and `json-column.ts` goes. `cached` becomes `integer({ mode: \"boolean\" })`, so the row reads back a boolean instead of 0 or 1.\n\nThe row types derive from the schema: `ItemRow`, `RecipeVersionRow` and `CostEntryRow` become `typeof table.$inferSelect`, replacing the hand-written types in `item.ts`, `recipe.ts` and `ledger.ts`; the constant maps stay where they are.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph store [\"common/src/db\"]\n    direction TB\n    db[\"database(d1)<br/>drizzle with the schema\"]\n    read[\"readItem\"]\n    status[\"writeStatus\"]\n    insert[\"insertQueued\"]\n    claimR[\"claimRetry\"]\n    claimQ[\"claimRequeue\"]\n    fetched[\"recordFetch\"]\n    extracted[\"recordExtraction\"]\n    unitsW[\"writeUnits\"]\n    ready[\"writeReady\"]\n    cost[\"costEntry\"]\n    current[\"currentRecipe\"]\n    save[\"saveRecipeVersion\"]\n  end\n  api[\"api/ routes\"]\n  pipe[\"pipeline/ steps\"]\n  api --> db\n  api --> read\n  api --> status\n  api --> insert\n  api --> claimR\n  api --> claimQ\n  pipe --> db\n  pipe --> read\n  pipe --> status\n  pipe --> fetched\n  pipe --> extracted\n  pipe --> unitsW\n  pipe --> ready\n  pipe --> cost\n  pipe --> current\n  pipe --> save\n```\n\n| Query | Answers | Replaces |\n|---|---|---|\n| `database(d1)` | the drizzle client over a D1 binding, with the schema | `env.DB.prepare` everywhere |\n| `readItem(db, id)` | the item row or null | `common` `readItem` (raw SELECT, manual JSON decode) |\n| `writeStatus(db, id, write)` | queued or generating with a step; failed with a step and an error | `common` `writeStatus` |\n| `insertQueued(db, {url, voice})` | the new item's id | `api/src/items/create.ts` |\n| `claimRetry(db, id, retryMax)` | whether this call claimed the retry (one conditional UPDATE, `.returning({ id })`, claimed when a row comes back) | `api/src/items/retry-claim.ts` |\n| `claimRequeue(db, id, staleBefore)` | whether this call claimed the re-queue, same shape | the UPDATE inside `api/src/items/requeue.ts` |\n| `recordFetch(db, id, {instanceId, domain})` | the fetch step's write of the instance id and domain | the UPDATE in `fetch.ts` |\n| `recordExtraction(db, id, {title, units, recipeVersionId})` | the recipe step's write | the UPDATE in `recipe.ts` |\n| `writeUnits(db, id, {units, degradations})` | the units and degradations write the images and describe steps share | the two duplicated UPDATEs in `images.ts` and `describe.ts` |\n| `writeReady(db, id, {units, duration, format})` | the store step's ready write | the UPDATE in `synthesis.ts` |\n| `costEntry(db, entry)` | one cost ledger row | `pipeline/src/workflow/ledger.ts` |\n| `currentRecipe(db, domain)` | the domain's latest recipe version or null | `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts` |\n| `saveRecipeVersion(db, domain, script)` | the new version's id; one `INSERT … SELECT COALESCE(MAX(version), 0) + 1` through `db.insert().select()` | `saveVersion` in `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts` |\n\nEvery write returns the drizzle query without awaiting it. A caller awaits it alone, or hands several to `db.batch([...])` where today's code batches (fetch: `recordFetch` and the Firecrawl `costEntry`; describe: `writeUnits` and the describer entries; store: `writeReady` and the TTS entry). D1 runs a batch as one transaction. `db.transaction` is not used: D1 rejects `BEGIN` from a binding.\n\n### 1.4 Module list\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  subgraph new [\"new\"]\n    direction TB\n    n1[\"common/drizzle.config.ts\"]\n    n2[\"common/src/db/schema.ts<br/>the three tables\"]\n    n3[\"common/src/db/database.ts\"]\n    n4[\"common/src/db/items/<br/>read-item, write-status,<br/>insert-queued, claim-retry,<br/>claim-requeue, record-fetch,<br/>record-extraction,<br/>write-units, write-ready\"]\n    n5[\"common/src/db/cost-entry.ts\"]\n    n6[\"common/src/db/recipes/<br/>current-recipe,<br/>save-recipe-version\"]\n    n7[\"common/migrations/<br/>0000_initial.sql, meta/\"]\n  end\n  subgraph touched [\"touched\"]\n    direction TB\n    t1[\"common/package.json<br/>deps, db:generate\"]\n    t2[\"common/src/item.ts,<br/>ledger.ts, recipe.ts<br/>row types from schema\"]\n    t3[\"common/src/index.ts\"]\n    t4[\"api/src/routes/*,<br/>api/src/items/*<br/>call common\"]\n    t5[\"pipeline/src/workflow/<br/>steps/*, recipe step<br/>call common\"]\n    t6[\"test helpers in api/,<br/>pipeline/, common/<br/>seed through drizzle\"]\n    t7[\".github/workflows/<br/>cloudflare.yml<br/>schema check leg\"]\n  end\n  subgraph deleted [\"deleted\"]\n    direction TB\n    d1[\"common/src/item-store/\"]\n    d2[\"common/migrations/<br/>0001_initial.sql\"]\n    d3[\"api/src/items/create.ts,<br/>retry-claim.ts\"]\n    d4[\"pipeline/src/workflow/<br/>ledger.ts\"]\n    d5[\"saveVersion, currentRecipe<br/>in pipeline/src/recipes/<br/>store.ts\"]\n  end\n  classDef n fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef t fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n  classDef d fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,n6,n7 n\n  class t1,t2,t3,t4,t5,t6,t7 t\n  class d1,d2,d3,d4,d5 d\n```\n\nThe queries go under `common/src/db/`, grouped by table, one function per module. `item-store/` is folded into `db/items/`, because it held the same kind of code. `domainFromUrl` stays in `pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts`: it parses a URL and touches no table. `api/src/items/requeue.ts` and `restart.ts` stay: they decide when to claim and how to restart the Workflow, and call `claimRequeue`. The ids keep their prefixes and are minted inside the query that inserts the row (`itm_`, `rcp_`, `cst_`).\n\n## 2 api/ and pipeline/ callers\n\n### 2.1 Callstack: the retry route\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  req[\"POST /items/:id/retry\"]\n  db[\"database(env.DB)\"]\n  read[\"readItem\"]\n  missing{\"row?\"}\n  r404([\"404\"])\n  claim[\"claimRetry(db, id, RETRY_MAX)\"]\n  won{\"claimed?\"}\n  r409([\"409, the item<br/>as it is\"])\n  restart[\"restartItem<br/>(Workflow)\"]\n  threw{\"threw?\"}\n  fail[\"writeStatus failed<br/>with the error\"]\n  r202([\"202 with readItem\"])\n  req --> db --> read --> missing\n  missing -->|\"no\"| r404\n  missing -->|\"yes\"| claim --> won\n  won -->|\"no\"| r409\n  won -->|\"yes\"| restart --> threw\n  threw -->|\"yes\"| fail --> r202\n  threw -->|\"no\"| r202\n  classDef q fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef ok fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef bad fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class db,read,claim,fail q\n  class r202 ok\n  class r404,r409 bad\n```\n\nEvery route builds the client once per request with `database(env.DB)` and passes it down; no route or step writes SQL. Enqueue calls `insertQueued`, then `readItem`; poll calls `readItem` and, through `requeueIfStale`, `claimRequeue`. Each pipeline step builds the client from its env the same way and calls the step's query, batching where it does today. The behaviour of every route and step is unchanged; the API and pipeline suites pass unmodified apart from their seeding helpers.\n\n## 3 Standards\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  claude@{ shape: doc, label: \"CLAUDE.md\" }\n  inv@{ shape: doc, label: \"invariants.md\" }\n  notes@{ shape: doc, label: \"docs/technical-design\" }\n  wiki@{ shape: doc, label: \"mahou wiki\" }\n  g1[\"code style: every D1<br/>read and write is a drizzle<br/>query in common/src/db,<br/>even when one Worker uses it\"]\n  g2[\"invariant 7: the schema is<br/>common/src/db/schema.ts;<br/>drizzle-kit generates the<br/>migration, reviewed and<br/>committed\"]\n  g3[\"common-package,<br/>persistence-and-storage,<br/>deployment-and-ci,<br/>local-development\"]\n  g4[\"new entry: drizzle on D1<br/>(0.x layout, no transaction,<br/>enum emits no CHECK)\"]\n  claude --> g1\n  inv --> g2\n  claude --> g2\n  notes --> g3\n  wiki --> g4\n```\n\nThe CLAUDE.md code-style rule that keeps single-Worker code out of `common/` gains an exception for the database: every D1 read and write is a drizzle query in `common/src/db/`. Invariant 7 changes from hand-written SQL to SQL generated by drizzle-kit from the schema, reviewed and committed. \"When adding something\" gets a line: a schema change edits `schema.ts` and runs `pnpm db:generate`. The notes that describe the item row's reads and writes, the migrations, CI and the local reset are updated. The local wiki gains an entry for drizzle on D1 with what the trial and the research found.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae136789-555b-4f97-82cc-7add0cdca9d5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
