{"parentUuid":"2c6660ee-d876-477b-b2e3-ea52ff7870f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwDF3SxqkEeowoYUabce","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NdM9zPjvux9Xf5eLr9iUT6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/dzcanvas && cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,json\nmd=open('program-design/drizzle.md').read()\nparts=[];branch=None;part=None;buf=[];fence=None;code=[]\ndef flush():\n    global buf\n    if part is None: buf=[];return\n    text='\\n'.join(buf).strip()\n    for para in re.split(r'\\n\\s*\\n',text):\n        para=para.strip()\n        if not para: continue\n        if para.startswith('|'):\n            rows=[r for r in para.split('\\n') if not re.match(r'^\\|[-| ]+\\|$',r)]\n            cells=[[c.strip().replace('`','') for c in r.strip('|').split('|')] for r in rows]\n            part['blocks'].append({'kind':'mono','text':'\\n'.join(f\"{c[0]}\\n    {c[1]}\\n    replaces: {c[2]}\" for c in cells[1:])})\n        else:\n            part['blocks'].append({'kind':'prose','text':para.replace('\\n',' ').replace('`','').replace('**','')})\n    buf=[]\nfor line in md.split('\\n'):\n    if fence:\n        if line.startswith('```'):\n            part['blocks'].append({'kind':'mermaid' if fence=='mermaid' else 'mono','text':'\\n'.join(code)});fence=None;code=[]\n        else: code.append(line)\n        continue\n    if line.startswith('```'):\n        flush();fence=line[3:].strip() or 'text';continue\n    m=re.match(r'^## (\\d+) (.*)',line)\n    if m: flush();branch=(m[1],m[2]);part=None;continue\n    m=re.match(r'^### (\\d+\\.\\d+) (.*)',line)\n    if m: flush();part={'branch':branch[0],'branchTitle':branch[1],'n':m[1],'title':m[2],'blocks':[]};parts.append(part);continue\n    if line.startswith('# '): continue\n    buf.append(line)\nflush()\n# standards branch has no ### part: make one\nfor p in parts: pass\ntree=\"\"\"Program design: D1 through drizzle\n└─ nagara                                                     proposed\n   ├─ 1 common/ package                                       proposed\n   │  ├─ 1.1 Package layout\n   │  ├─ 1.2 How a schema change reaches D1\n   │  ├─ 1.3 Schema and queries\n   │  └─ 1.4 Module list\n   ├─ 2 api/ and pipeline/ callers                            proposed\n   │  └─ 2.1 Callstack: the retry route\n   └─ 3 Standards                                             proposed\n      └─ 3.1 Sources and what they govern\n\"\"\"\nnote=\"\"\"The whole drizzle program design is proposed at once. Each branch is a column and each part an area under it; the text record is program-design/drizzle.md in the scratch folder. Put a sticky note on anything that does not match your idea, or say it by voice, then click Send to Claude.\n\nPoints to check:\n- drizzle-orm 0.45.4 and drizzle-kit 0.31.11, not the 1.0 release candidate: the RC writes each migration into a subfolder that wrangler and readD1Migrations never read. A trial of 0.31.11's output applied cleanly with wrangler, CHECKs and json_valid included (1.1).\n- The generated 0000_initial.sql replaces 0001_initial.sql: production D1 does not exist yet. The local .wrangler-state is reset once (1.2).\n- CI fails when the schema changed without its migration: common-checks runs drizzle-kit generate and git diff --exit-code (1.2).\n- Row types derive from the schema; cached reads back as a boolean; drizzle encodes the JSON columns, so json-column.ts goes (1.3).\n- Every query lives in common/src/db, one per module, including the ones only the API or only the pipeline runs. CLAUDE.md's rule that single-Worker code stays in its Worker gets a database exception (1.4, 3.1).\n- Writes return the query unawaited so steps can batch them as today; db.transaction is not used because D1 rejects BEGIN from a binding (1.3).\"\"\"\nopen('/tmp/dzcanvas/spec.json','w').write(json.dumps({'tree':tree,'parts':parts,'note':note}))\nprint([ (p['n'],[b['kind'][0] for b in p['blocks']]) for p in parts])\nEOF","description":"Build the canvas spec from the record"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13850,"cache_read_input_tokens":341170,"output_tokens":2177,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":570},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13850,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2177,"cache_read_input_tokens":341170,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13850},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NdM9zPjvux9Xf5eLr9iUT6":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/dzcanvas && cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,json\nmd=open('program-design/drizzle.md').read()\nparts=[];branch=None;part=None;buf=[];fence=None;code=[]\ndef flush():\n    global buf\n    if part is None: buf=[];return\n    text='\\n'.join(buf).strip()\n    for para in re.split(r'\\n\\s*\\n',text):\n        para=para.strip()\n        if not para: continue\n        if para.startswith('|'):\n            rows=[r for r in para.split('\\n') if not re.match(r'^\\|[-| ]+\\|$',r)]\n            cells=[[c.strip().replace('`','') for c in r.strip('|').split('|')] for r in rows]\n            part['blocks'].append({'kind':'mono','text':'\\n'.join(f\"{c[0]}\\n    {c[1]}\\n    replaces: {c[2]}\" for c in cells[1:])})\n        else:\n            part['blocks'].append({'kind':'prose','text':para.replace('\\n',' ').replace('`','').replace('**','')})\n    buf=[]\nfor line in md.split('\\n'):\n    if fence:\n        if line.startswith('```'):\n            part['blocks'].append({'kind':'mermaid' if fence=='mermaid' else 'mono','text':'\\n'.join(code)});fence=None;code=[]\n        else: code.append(line)\n        continue\n    if line.startswith('```'):\n        flush();fence=line[3:].strip() or 'text';continue\n    m=re.match(r'^## (\\d+) (.*)',line)\n    if m: flush();branch=(m[1],m[2]);part=None;continue\n    m=re.match(r'^### (\\d+\\.\\d+) (.*)',line)\n    if m: flush();part={'branch':branch[0],'branchTitle':branch[1],'n':m[1],'title':m[2],'blocks':[]};parts.append(part);continue\n    if line.startswith('# '): continue\n    buf.append(line)\nflush()\n# standards branch has no ### part: make one\nfor p in parts: pass\ntree=\"\"\"Program design: D1 through drizzle\n└─ nagara                                                     proposed\n   ├─ 1 common/ package                                       proposed\n   │  ├─ 1.1 Package layout\n   │  ├─ 1.2 How a schema change reaches D1\n   │  ├─ 1.3 Schema and queries\n   │  └─ 1.4 Module list\n   ├─ 2 api/ and pipeline/ callers                            proposed\n   │  └─ 2.1 Callstack: the retry route\n   └─ 3 Standards                                             proposed\n      └─ 3.1 Sources and what they govern\n\"\"\"\nnote=\"\"\"The whole drizzle program design is proposed at once. Each branch is a column and each part an area under it; the text record is program-design/drizzle.md in the scratch folder. Put a sticky note on anything that does not match your idea, or say it by voice, then click Send to Claude.\n\nPoints to check:\n- drizzle-orm 0.45.4 and drizzle-kit 0.31.11, not the 1.0 release candidate: the RC writes each migration into a subfolder that wrangler and readD1Migrations never read. A trial of 0.31.11's output applied cleanly with wrangler, CHECKs and json_valid included (1.1).\n- The generated 0000_initial.sql replaces 0001_initial.sql: production D1 does not exist yet. The local .wrangler-state is reset once (1.2).\n- CI fails when the schema changed without its migration: common-checks runs drizzle-kit generate and git diff --exit-code (1.2).\n- Row types derive from the schema; cached reads back as a boolean; drizzle encodes the JSON columns, so json-column.ts goes (1.3).\n- Every query lives in common/src/db, one per module, including the ones only the API or only the pipeline runs. CLAUDE.md's rule that single-Worker code stays in its Worker gets a database exception (1.4, 3.1).\n- Writes return the query unawaited so steps can batch them as today; db.transaction is not used because D1 rejects BEGIN from a binding (1.3).\"\"\"\nopen('/tmp/dzcanvas/spec.json','w').write(json.dumps({'tree':tree,'parts':parts,'note':note}))\nprint([ (p['n'],[b['kind'][0] for b in p['blocks']]) for p in parts])\nEOF","description":"Build the canvas spec from the record"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a49f95fd-0f17-43b2-a539-2e70a4df6386","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwDF2m3BFXDakS6hMdca","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15c99208-2568-4c9a-a831-6981abbc8c51","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:08:21.005Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
