{"parentUuid":"e079ecbd-ec73-4429-9921-d15a512254bf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6fe5d878-ed9d-4814-b2fe-38653acae53f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>b92meu7z3</task-id>\n<summary>Monitor event: \"drizzle canvas: Send to Claude clicks and voice messages\"</summary>\n<event>voice: is this the usual approach with Drizzle or is there a different pattern recommended of using the models directly or something like that I want to avoid using Raw SQL and also adding any extra layer of complexity if possible I'm not sure if the drizzle usage recommends using repositories or using the models directly or what the current best approaches | selected: shape:X0Sw3KL4KqmrPv_2fBSGI (mock mermaid)</event>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"1ee3cf57-5070-4741-a972-dce3de0fb74f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:12:33.814Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":106,"turnIndex":307},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"1ee3cf57-5070-4741-a972-dce3de0fb74f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwDb4ABSn64SXwZau8QT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":365812,"output_tokens":1600,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":775},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1600,"cache_read_input_tokens":365812,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7871,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"668958a2-8f07-41ca-8941-ca2e87e93b26","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwDb3LZjtg9K7nYNsi2u","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"159d5acc-9111-41d2-8a49-475a01d65bcf","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:12:43.441Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"159d5acc-9111-41d2-8a49-475a01d65bcf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwDb4ABSn64SXwZau8QT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Drizzle has no models or active-record layer. A table defined with `sqliteTable` is the model: it carries the column types and gives you `typeof items.$inferSelect` for the row type. You query it directly with `db.select().from(items).where(eq(items.id, id))`, `db.update(items).set({...}).where(...)`, or the relational form `db.query.items.findFirst({ where: ... })`. The docs prescribe no repository pattern; their examples call the query builder where the data is needed. The query functions I proposed in 1.3 are a repository layer of our own on top, the extra layer you want to avoid.\n\nThe simpler shape:\n- **`common/src/db/`** holds `schema.ts` (tables, CHECKs, indexes), the `database(d1)` client and the row types derived from the schema. Nothing else.\n- **Routes and steps** call drizzle inline: enqueue does `db.insert(items).values(...)`, the store step does `db.batch([db.update(items).set(...), db.insert(costEntries).values(...)])`, and so on. The 13 one-call wrapper functions go away.\n\n**Raw SQL.** Two places in my proposal still used the `sql` template, and both can be plain drizzle:\n- **The recipe save:** `COALESCE(MAX(version), 0) + 1` becomes a select of the current `version` followed by an insert at version + 1. The `UNIQUE(domain, version)` constraint already turns a concurrent save into an error, so nothing is lost.\n- **The retry claim:** `retry_count = retry_count + 1` becomes `set({ retry_count: row.retry_count + 1 })` with `where(eq(items.retry_count, row.retry_count), lt(items.retry_count, max), eq(items.status, \"failed\"))`. A concurrent retry finds the count already moved and claims nothing, the same guarantee as today.\n\nThe only `sql` left is inside the schema's CHECK constraints (`json_valid`, the status list), because drizzle has no other way to express a CHECK. That's schema definition, not a query.\n\nOne judgment call on duplication:\n- `writeStatus` is called by the API and by the step wrapper.\n- The units and degradations write is shared by the images and describe steps.\n\nInline, each of those becomes a two-line `db.update(items).set(...)` repeated at its callers. I'd keep inline drizzle everywhere and accept that small repetition.\n\nShould I redraw 1.3 and 1.4 with inline drizzle and no query layer?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":365812,"output_tokens":1600,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":775},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1600,"cache_read_input_tokens":365812,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"668958a2-8f07-41ca-8941-ca2e87e93b26","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwDb3LZjtg9K7nYNsi2u","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2397733-96d2-4d64-a491-baaf5152be2c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:12:51.577Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
