{"parentUuid":"ff2b0635-60a7-4858-88bb-31b12f62b650","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwDe6vSuVe8kWPhV7Nu4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HgXMVWTLZ5oTrGSi6knEiS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/dzcanvas/note.txt <<'EOF'\nAnswer to your voice question (is a query layer the usual drizzle approach?):\n\nDrizzle has no models or active-record layer. A table defined with sqliteTable is the model: it carries the column types and gives the row type (typeof items.$inferSelect). You query it directly: db.select().from(items).where(eq(items.id, id)), db.update(items).set({...}).where(...), or db.query.items.findFirst(...). The docs prescribe no repository pattern; their examples call the query builder where the data is needed. The query functions proposed in 1.3 are a repository layer of our own, the extra layer you want to avoid.\n\nThe simpler shape:\n- common/src/db holds schema.ts (tables, CHECKs, indexes), the database(d1) client and the row types derived from the schema. Nothing else.\n- Routes and steps call drizzle inline: enqueue does db.insert(items).values(...), the store step does db.batch([db.update(items).set(...), db.insert(costEntries).values(...)]). The 13 wrapper functions go.\n\nNo raw SQL in queries:\n- Recipe save: read the domain's current version, insert at version + 1. UNIQUE(domain, version) already turns a concurrent save into an error.\n- Retry claim: set({ retry_count: row.retry_count + 1 }) where status is failed, retry_count equals the value read and is under the cap. A concurrent retry finds the count moved and claims nothing.\nThe only sql left is in the schema's CHECK constraints (json_valid, the status list): drizzle has no other way to write a CHECK.\n\nDuplication: writeStatus (the API and the step wrapper) and the units write (images and describe) become a two-line db.update repeated at their callers. I'd accept that.\n\nShould I redraw 1.3 and 1.4 with inline drizzle and no query layer? Answer with a sticky note or by voice.\nEOF\nagent-browser eval \"(() => { const n = editor.getCurrentPageShapes().find(s => s.type==='geo' && s.props.dash==='dashed' && s.props.color==='grey'); editor.updateShape({ id: n.id, type: 'geo', props: { richText: tldraw.toRichText($(python3 -c 'import json;print(json.dumps(open(\"/tmp/dzcanvas/note.txt\").read()))')) } }); return n.id })()\" ; sleep 1; agent-browser eval \"(() => { const n = editor.getCurrentPageShapes().find(s => s.type==='geo' && s.props.dash==='dashed' && s.props.color==='grey'); const el=document.querySelector('[data-shape-id=\\\"'+n.id+'\\\"] .tl-rich-text'); const z=editor.getZoomLevel(); editor.updateShape({id:n.id,type:'geo',props:{h: el.getBoundingClientRect().height/z + 60}}); editor.zoomToBounds(editor.getShapePageBounds(n.id), {inset: 40}); return 'ok' })()\"; sleep 1; agent-browser screenshot /tmp/dzcanvas/s2.png >/dev/null","description":"Write the answer into the Claude note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1641,"cache_read_input_tokens":366198,"output_tokens":1190,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":52},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1641,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1190,"cache_read_input_tokens":366198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1641},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HgXMVWTLZ5oTrGSi6knEiS":{"command":"cat > /tmp/dzcanvas/note.txt <<'EOF'\nAnswer to your voice question (is a query layer the usual drizzle approach?):\n\nDrizzle has no models or active-record layer. A table defined with sqliteTable is the model: it carries the column types and gives the row type (typeof items.$inferSelect). You query it directly: db.select().from(items).where(eq(items.id, id)), db.update(items).set({...}).where(...), or db.query.items.findFirst(...). The docs prescribe no repository pattern; their examples call the query builder where the data is needed. The query functions proposed in 1.3 are a repository layer of our own, the extra layer you want to avoid.\n\nThe simpler shape:\n- common/src/db holds schema.ts (tables, CHECKs, indexes), the database(d1) client and the row types derived from the schema. Nothing else.\n- Routes and steps call drizzle inline: enqueue does db.insert(items).values(...), the store step does db.batch([db.update(items).set(...), db.insert(costEntries).values(...)]). The 13 wrapper functions go.\n\nNo raw SQL in queries:\n- Recipe save: read the domain's current version, insert at version + 1. UNIQUE(domain, version) already turns a concurrent save into an error.\n- Retry claim: set({ retry_count: row.retry_count + 1 }) where status is failed, retry_count equals the value read and is under the cap. A concurrent retry finds the count moved and claims nothing.\nThe only sql left is in the schema's CHECK constraints (json_valid, the status list): drizzle has no other way to write a CHECK.\n\nDuplication: writeStatus (the API and the step wrapper) and the units write (images and describe) become a two-line db.update repeated at their callers. I'd accept that.\n\nShould I redraw 1.3 and 1.4 with inline drizzle and no query layer? Answer with a sticky note or by voice.\nEOF\nagent-browser eval \"(() => { const n = editor.getCurrentPageShapes().find(s => s.type==='geo' && s.props.dash==='dashed' && s.props.color==='grey'); editor.updateShape({ id: n.id, type: 'geo', props: { richText: tldraw.toRichText($(python3 -c 'import json;print(json.dumps(open(\"/tmp/dzcanvas/note.txt\").read()))')) } }); return n.id })()\" ; sleep 1; agent-browser eval \"(() => { const n = editor.getCurrentPageShapes().find(s => s.type==='geo' && s.props.dash==='dashed' && s.props.color==='grey'); const el=document.querySelector('[data-shape-id=\\\"'+n.id+'\\\"] .tl-rich-text'); const z=editor.getZoomLevel(); editor.updateShape({id:n.id,type:'geo',props:{h: el.getBoundingClientRect().height/z + 60}}); editor.zoomToBounds(editor.getShapePageBounds(n.id), {inset: 40}); return 'ok' })()\"; sleep 1; agent-browser screenshot /tmp/dzcanvas/s2.png >/dev/null","description":"Write the answer into the Claude note"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fa73750f-305a-4382-9a27-1d63ec7911a6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwDe6Pwz9S4ZzkTTDjLf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15143def-c585-4f54-bd5d-b0d1e584b8fb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:13:26.045Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
