{"parentUuid":"f84cebeb-a39f-4938-b93b-3e126d072c45","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwDtKsDMwg7irHBwM5sb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U2QHa1MmJVrNT5vDgkqRFY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/dzcanvas/q1.txt <<'EOF'\n❓ Q1 · The query layer\n\nThe queries diagram and table beside this card propose one function per query in common/src/db, a layer of our own on top of drizzle. You asked whether drizzle's usual pattern is different, and whether a generic repository like api-toolkit's fits. The Claude note below has the findings.\n\nWhich shape should the queries take?\n- Inline drizzle at the callers: common/src/db holds only the schema, the client and the row types.\n- A small generic repository in common/src/db: get, create and updateWhere over any table, each returning the unexecuted query so steps can batch.\nEOF\nagent-browser eval \"(() => {\nconst { createShapeId, toRichText } = tldraw\nconst shapes = editor.getCurrentPageShapes()\nconst area = shapes.find(s => s.type==='mock' && s.props.kind==='area' && String(s.props.data.label).includes('· 1.3 '))\nconst ab = editor.getShapePageBounds(area.id)\nconst inside = shapes.filter(s => s.id!==area.id && s.type!=='arrow' && (() => { const b=editor.getShapePageBounds(s.id); return b.minX>=ab.minX && b.maxX<=ab.maxX && b.minY>=ab.minY && b.maxY<=ab.maxY })())\nconst mers = inside.filter(s => s.type==='mock' && s.props.kind==='mermaid').map(s=>({s,b:editor.getShapePageBounds(s.id)})).sort((a,b)=>a.b.minY-b.b.minY)\nconst target = mers[1].b\nconst right = Math.max(...inside.map(s=>editor.getShapePageBounds(s.id).maxX))\nconst x = right + 80\nconst qid = createShapeId()\neditor.createShape({ id:qid, type:'geo', x, y: target.minY, props:{ geo:'rectangle', w:1000, h:200, color:'violet', fill:'semi', dash:'solid', font:'draw', size:'s', align:'start', verticalAlign:'start', richText: toRichText($(python3 -c 'import json;print(json.dumps(open(\"/tmp/dzcanvas/q1.txt\").read()))')) } })\nconst n = shapes.find(s => s.type==='geo' && s.props.dash==='dashed' && s.props.color==='grey')\nconst label = shapes.find(s=>s.type==='text' && JSON.stringify(s.props.richText).includes('\\\"Claude\\\"'))\nwindow.__q1 = { qid, nid: n.id, lid: label && label.id, x, area: area.id }\nreturn 'ok'\n})()\" ; sleep 1; agent-browser eval \"(() => {\nconst { qid, nid, lid, x, area } = window.__q1\nconst z = editor.getZoomLevel()\nconst fit = (id) => { const el=document.querySelector('[data-shape-id=\\\"'+id+'\\\"] .tl-rich-text'); editor.updateShape({id, type:'geo', props:{h: el.getBoundingClientRect().height/z + 60}}) }\nfit(qid)\nconst qb = editor.getShapePageBounds(qid)\neditor.updateShape({ id:nid, type:'geo', x, y: qb.maxY + 80, props:{ w:1000 } })\nif (lid) editor.updateShape({ id:lid, type:'text', x, y: qb.maxY + 40 })\nreturn 'ok'\n})()\"; sleep 1; agent-browser eval \"(() => {\nconst { qid, nid, area } = window.__q1\nconst z = editor.getZoomLevel()\nconst el=document.querySelector('[data-shape-id=\\\"'+nid+'\\\"] .tl-rich-text'); editor.updateShape({id:nid, type:'geo', props:{h: el.getBoundingClientRect().height/z + 60}})\nconst ab = editor.getShapePageBounds(area)\nconst nb = editor.getShapePageBounds(nid)\neditor.updateShape({ id: area, type:'mock', props:{ w: nb.maxX - ab.minX + 40, h: Math.max(ab.h, nb.maxY - ab.minY + 40) } })\nconst nab = editor.getShapePageBounds(area)\nconst others = editor.getCurrentPageShapes().filter(s=>s.type==='mock'&&s.props.kind==='area'&&s.id!==area).map(s=>editor.getShapePageBounds(s.id)).filter(o=>o.minX<nab.maxX&&o.maxX>nab.minX&&o.minY<nab.maxY&&o.maxY>nab.minY)\neditor.zoomToBounds(nab,{inset:40})\nreturn JSON.stringify({overlaps: others.length})\n})()\"; sleep 1; agent-browser screenshot /tmp/dzcanvas/s5.png >/dev/null","description":"Move the discussion inside part 1.3 as a question card and note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_us