{"parentUuid":"131ed943-7b3b-4099-a0df-224e79db5c7b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwETyv6yP1s1czGfBixi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KcuQwWpPgrEDZr52oKGZc5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('drizzle.md').read()\na=s.index('```mermaid\\nflowchart LR\\n  subgraph store')\nb=s.index('### 1.4 Module list')\nnew='''```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph itemsT [\"common/src/db/items\"]\n    direction TB\n    gi[\"getItem\"]\n    ci[\"createItem\"]\n    ui[\"updateItem\"]\n    ws[\"writeStatus\"]\n    cr[\"claimRetry\"]\n    cq[\"claimRequeue\"]\n  end\n  subgraph recipesT [\"common/src/db/recipe-versions\"]\n    direction TB\n    gr[\"getLatestRecipeVersion\"]\n    crv[\"createRecipeVersion\"]\n  end\n  subgraph costsT [\"common/src/db/cost-entries\"]\n    direction TB\n    cc[\"createCostEntry\"]\n  end\n  db[\"database(d1)\"]\n  api[\"api/ routes\"]\n  pipe[\"pipeline/ steps\"]\n  api --> db\n  pipe --> db\n  api --> itemsT\n  pipe --> itemsT\n  pipe --> recipesT\n  pipe --> costsT\n```\n\nEach table gets a folder of functions named by one pattern: `get<Model>`, `list<Models>`, `create<Model>`, `update<Model>`, `delete<Model>`, plus a conditional write named for what it does when a plain update cannot express it. Only the functions a caller uses exist; no route or step lists or deletes rows today, so `list` and `delete` are added under the same names when one does. Every function takes the drizzle client first and returns the drizzle query unawaited, except where it has to read before it writes.\n\n| Function | Answers | Replaces |\n|---|---|---|\n| `database(d1)` | the drizzle client over a D1 binding, with the schema | `env.DB.prepare` everywhere |\n| `getItem(db, id)` | the item row or null | `readItem` |\n| `createItem(db, {url, voice})` | the insert of a queued item; mints the `itm_` id and the timestamps, and returns the id with the query | `insertQueued` in `api/src/items/create.ts` |\n| `updateItem(db, id, changes)` | an update of the given columns by id, `updated_at` set | the UPDATEs in the fetch, recipe, images, describe and store steps |\n| `writeStatus(db, id, write)` | the status write in its two forms (queued or generating with a step; failed with a step and an error), built on `updateItem` | `writeStatus` |\n| `claimRetry(db, row, retryMax)` | whether this call claimed the retry: one UPDATE to queued with `retry_count` = the row's count + 1, where the item is still failed, still at the count read and under the cap; claimed when `.returning({ id })` gives a row back | `api/src/items/retry-claim.ts` |\n| `claimRequeue(db, id, staleBefore)` | whether this call claimed the re-queue, same shape: `queued_at` moved where the item is still queued and stale | the UPDATE in `api/src/items/requeue.ts` |\n| `getLatestRecipeVersion(db, domain)` | the domain's highest version or null | `currentRecipe` |\n| `createRecipeVersion(db, {domain, script})` | reads the latest version and inserts at the next number, minting the `rcp_` id; `UNIQUE(domain, version)` turns a concurrent save into an error | `saveVersion` |\n| `createCostEntry(db, entry)` | the insert of one cost row, minting the `cst_` id | `ledgerInsert` |\n\nNo query uses the `sql` template; it appears only in the schema's CHECK constraints. The retry route reads the item before it claims, because the claim compares the count it read. A caller awaits a returned query alone or hands several to `db.batch([...])` where today's code batches (fetch: `updateItem` and the Firecrawl `createCostEntry`; describe: `updateItem` and the describer entries; store: `updateItem` and the TTS entry). D1 runs a batch as one transaction. `db.transaction` is not used: D1 rejects `BEGIN` from a binding.\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\n# module list\na=s.index('    n4[\"common/src/db/items/')\nb=s.index('    n7[\"common/migrations/')\ns=s[:a]+'''    n4[\"common/src/db/items/<br/>get-item, create-item,<br/>update-item, write-status,<br/>claim-retry, claim-requeue\"]\n    n5[\"common/src/db/cost-entries/<br/>create-cost-entry\"]\n    n6[\"common/src/db/recipe-versions/<br/>get-latest-recipe-version,<br/>create-recipe-version\"]\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"The queries go under `common/src/db/`, grouped by table, one function per module.\",\"The queries go under `common/src/db/`, one folder per table, one function per module.\")\ns=s.replace(\"call `claimRequeue`. The ids keep their prefixes and are minted inside the query that inserts the row (`itm_`, `rcp_`, `cst_`).\",\"call `claimRequeue`. The ids keep their prefixes and are minted by the create function of their table (`itm_`, `rcp_`, `cst_`).\")\nopen('drizzle.md','w').write(s)\nimport re,subprocess\nfor i,blk in enumerate(re.findall(r\"```mermaid\\n(.*?)```\",s,re.S)):\n    r=subprocess.run(['bash','/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/superpowers/skills/mermaid/scripts/validate-mermaid.sh'],input=blk,capture_output=True,text=True)\n    print(i,'ok' if r.returncode==0 else r.stdout[:300])\nEOF\ngrep -n \"claimRetry\\|readItem\" drizzle.md | head","description":"Rewrite parts 1.3 and 1.4 with per-table functions","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":384222,"output_tokens":3641,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1506},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3641,"cache_read_input_tokens":384222,"cache_creation_input_tokens":413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413},"ty