{"parentUuid":"7f8410df-2bff-4a04-8ff7-7d0df77cc3a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwEWehYp8Q2s4LQWvUXL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PMEZHhDui8zegDjL4cQ5Za","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('drizzle.md').read()\na=s.index('### 2.1 Callstack: the retry route')\nb=s.index('## 3 Standards')\nnew='''### 2.1 Callstack: the retry route\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  req[\"POST /items/:id/retry\"]\n  db[\"database(env.DB)\"]\n  read[\"getItem\"]\n  missing{\"row?\"}\n  r404([\"404\"])\n  claim[\"claimRetry<br/>(db, row, RETRY_MAX)\"]\n  won{\"claimed?\"}\n  reread[\"getItem again\"]\n  r409([\"409: at the cap,<br/>or not failed\"])\n  restart[\"restartItem<br/>(Workflow)\"]\n  threw{\"threw?\"}\n  fail[\"writeStatus failed<br/>with the error\"]\n  r202([\"202 with the item\"])\n  req --> db --> read --> missing\n  missing -->|\"no\"| r404\n  missing -->|\"yes\"| claim --> won\n  won -->|\"no\"| reread --> r409\n  won -->|\"yes\"| restart --> threw\n  threw -->|\"yes\"| fail --> r202\n  threw -->|\"no\"| r202\n  classDef q fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef ok fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef bad fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class db,read,claim,reread,fail q\n  class r202 ok\n  class r404,r409 bad\n```\n\nEvery route builds the client once per request with `database(env.DB)` and passes it down; no route or step writes SQL. The retry route now reads before it claims, because the claim compares the count it read; a retry that loses reads again so its 409 names the status the winner wrote. Enqueue calls `createItem`, then `getItem`; poll calls `getItem` and, through `requeueIfStale`, `claimRequeue`. Each pipeline step builds the client from its env the same way and calls `updateItem`, `writeStatus` and the create functions, batching where it does today. The behaviour of every route and step is otherwise unchanged; the API and pipeline suites pass unmodified apart from their seeding helpers.\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\nopen('drizzle.md','w').write(s)\nimport re,subprocess\nblk=re.findall(r\"```mermaid\\n(.*?)```\",new,re.S)[0]\nr=subprocess.run(['bash','/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/superpowers/skills/mermaid/scripts/validate-mermaid.sh'],input=blk,capture_output=True,text=True); print(r.returncode)\nEOF","description":"Rewrite the retry callstack for the new functions","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4140,"cache_read_input_tokens":384635,"output_tokens":1118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":62},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4140,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":384635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4140},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PMEZHhDui8zegDjL4cQ5Za":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('drizzle.md').read()\na=s.index('### 2.1 Callstack: the retry route')\nb=s.index('## 3 Standards')\nnew='''### 2.1 Callstack: the retry route\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  req[\"POST /items/:id/retry\"]\n  db[\"database(env.DB)\"]\n  read[\"getItem\"]\n  missing{\"row?\"}\n  r404([\"404\"])\n  claim[\"claimRetry<br/>(db, row, RETRY_MAX)\"]\n  won{\"claimed?\"}\n  reread[\"getItem again\"]\n  r409([\"409: at the cap,<br/>or not failed\"])\n  restart[\"restartItem<br/>(Workflow)\"]\n  threw{\"threw?\"}\n  fail[\"writeStatus failed<br/>with the error\"]\n  r202([\"202 with the item\"])\n  req --> db --> read --> missing\n  missing -->|\"no\"| r404\n  missing -->|\"yes\"| claim --> won\n  won -->|\"no\"| reread --> r409\n  won -->|\"yes\"| restart --> threw\n  threw -->|\"yes\"| fail --> r202\n  threw -->|\"no\"| r202\n  classDef q fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb\n  classDef ok fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\n  classDef bad fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n  class db,read,claim,reread,fail q\n  class r202 ok\n  class r404,r409 bad\n```\n\nEvery route builds the client once per request with `database(env.DB)` and passes it down; no route or step writes SQL. The retry route now reads before it claims, because the claim compares the count it read; a retry that loses reads again so its 409 names the status the winner wrote. Enqueue calls `createItem`, then `getItem`; poll calls `getItem` and, through `requeueIfStale`, `claimRequeue`. Each pipeline step builds the client from its env the same way and calls `updateItem`, `writeStatus` and the create functions, batching where it does today. The behaviour of every route and step is otherwise unchanged; the API and pipeline suites pass unmodified apart from their seeding helpers.\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\nopen('drizzle.md','w').write(s)\nimport re,subprocess\nblk=re.findall(r\"```mermaid\\n(.*?)```\",new,re.S)[0]\nr=subprocess.run(['bash','/home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/superpowers/skills/mermaid/scripts/validate-mermaid.sh'],input=blk,capture_output=True,text=True); print(r.returncode)\nEOF","description":"Rewrite the retry callstack for the new functions","timeout":120000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01PMEZHhDui8zegDjL4cQ5Za":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f355d98f-9903-408e-8de4-388797488529","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwEWeJUe4VQPjPS8iHt3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d58dbfc0-38b3-45a4-872c-d1a325ab2efc","timestamp":"2