{"parentUuid":"be76b06d-4d75-4027-9044-fa27c4b601ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwEb6fc5qBGGLW3iVdXV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've applied your decision on Q1 to the canvas and to the record, `program-design/drizzle.md`.\n\n- **1.3 Schema and queries:** each table gets a folder in `common/src/db/` with functions named by one pattern: `get`, `list`, `create`, `update` and `delete`, plus conditional writes named for what they do. There's no generic repository.\n  - `items`: `getItem`, `createItem`, `updateItem`, `writeStatus` (built on `updateItem`), `claimRetry`, `claimRequeue`\n  - `recipe_versions`: `getLatestRecipeVersion`, `createRecipeVersion`\n  - `cost_entries`: `createCostEntry`\n  - Only the functions a caller uses exist. Nothing lists or deletes rows yet, so `list` and `delete` get added under those names when something does.\n  - No query uses raw SQL. The `sql` template appears only in the schema's CHECK constraints.\n- **1.4 Module list:** updated to match.\n- **2.1 Retry callstack:** the retry route now reads the item before it claims it, because the claim checks the retry count it read. A retry that loses the race reads again, so its 409 shows the status the winning retry wrote.\n\nThe question card is gone. A Claude note inside 1.3 lists what changed. Check those three parts and confirm, or put a sticky note on whatever doesn't match."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1199,"cache_read_input_tokens":394742,"output_tokens":525,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":63},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1199,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":525,"cache_read_input_tokens":394742