{"parentUuid":"3588d13f-3c07-4dfd-9d53-64a64e069595","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwF5ec1ZcmzDYwhbrig8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fq8jTSETBMk6a951B4tc7f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs\ncp implement-common.md implement-ASE-84.md; cat >> implement-ASE-84.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Your part: D1 through drizzle (ASE-84)\n\nTask: ASE-84 in Linear. Work in the **main checkout** `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` on `feat/cloudflare-migration` (HEAD d2f165d or later). No other subagent touches code; a docs subagent edits `docs/`, `CLAUDE.md` and `.mahou/` at the same time, so do not edit those (the \"Never edit files under docs/\" rule above stands, and CLAUDE.md is theirs too). The safety rules above apply; also never `rm -rf`.\n\nThe settled program design is `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/drizzle.md`. Follow it exactly: package layout (drizzle-orm 0.45.4, drizzle-kit 0.31.11, `drizzle.config.ts`, `db:generate`), the schema (every table, column, CHECK, FK, index of today's `common/migrations/0001_initial.sql`; snake_case keys; enums typed from the constant maps plus explicit `check()`; JSON columns `text({mode: \"json\"}).$type<…>()`; `cached` as boolean), row types derived from the schema, the per-table functions in 1.3 with their exact names and semantics, the module list in 1.4, the retry route reading before it claims (2.1), and the CI leg that fails when the schema changed without its migration. No query uses the `sql` template; it may appear only in the schema's CHECKs. `db.transaction` is not used. Writes return the unawaited query so the fetch, describe and store steps keep their `db.batch`.\n\nThe researcher's facts and the trial behind the design: drizzle 0.31.11 output (`0000_initial.sql`, `--> statement-breakpoint`, `meta/`) applies with `wrangler d1 migrations apply --local`; `readD1Migrations` reads top-level `.sql` files and splits statements with wrangler's splitter: verify it handles the breakpoint comments under both Workers' vitest configs. Verify `.returning()` on D1 for the claims and the insert-select is no longer needed (createRecipeVersion reads the latest version, then inserts at the next).\n\nSteps:\n1. Schema, client, functions, generated migration replacing `0001_initial.sql`; diff the generated SQL against the old file and keep them equivalent (constraint names may differ; say how).\n2. Port every caller in `api/` and `pipeline/`; delete what the module list deletes. Test seeding helpers in all three trees go through drizzle too (the one test-only D1 trigger in the pipeline's whole-run tests may use drizzle's `db.run(sql\\`…\\`)`).\n3. Tests: the existing suites must pass with their assertions unchanged (behaviour is unchanged). Port `common/`'s item-store tests to the new functions, and add tests in `common/` for `claimRetry` (claimed, lost to a concurrent claim, at the cap, not failed), `claimRequeue` (claimed, not stale, already claimed), `createRecipeVersion` (first version, next version, concurrent save fails on the unique pair) and `updateItem` setting `updated_at`.\n4. CI leg in `.github/workflows/cloudflare.yml`; actionlint it.\n5. Reset the local state: move `.wrangler-state/` aside to `/tmp/nagara-wrangler-state-pre-drizzle-<timestamp>`, run `pnpm migrate:local`, and smoke one small real item end to end as before (API on 8788, the tunnel, `modal serve`), stopping everything by PID afterwards and resetting `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT`.\n6. Run test, lint, types in `common/`, `api/`, `pipeline/`, and the pipeline build. Commit in logical steps (`feat(common)`, `refactor(api)`, `refactor(pipeline)`, `ci`). Move ASE-84 to In Progress at the start and Done at the end.\n\nQuestions go to me with `<subagent-ask>…</subagent-ask>`. Your final message is the full report.\nEOF\ncat > docs-drizzle.md <<'EOF'\n# Docs for D1 through drizzle\n\nRun `/mahou:write-documentation` once in the main checkout `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara` (branch `feat/cloudflare-migration`) with the amendments below. The user approved documenting the change, so after the unslop and documentation-reviewer passes, write the edits directly. Do not commit. Touch only `docs/`, the root `CLAUDE.md` and `.mahou/`; an implementation subagent is changing code at the same time, so do not touch code. Never print secrets. Never `rm -rf`.\n\nThe settled program design is `/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/program-design/drizzle.md`; read it first. It is the source; the code is being written from it now.\n\nAmendments:\n1. **CLAUDE.md, code style**: the rule that code only one Worker uses stays in that Worker gains a database exception: every D1 read and write is a drizzle query function in `common/src/db/`, one folder per table, named by one pattern (`get`, `list`, `create`, `update`, `delete`, plus conditional writes named for what they do), even when one Worker uses it. The layout table's `common/` row says it holds the drizzle schema, the queries and the generated migrations.\n2. **Invariant 7** (CLAUDE.md and `docs/technical-design/invariants.md`): a schema change is a migration; the schema is `common/src/db/schema.ts` and drizzle-kit generates the SQL migration from it, reviewed and committed; migrations apply before either Worker deploys; the tests build their schema from the same migrations. Keep the \"what it buys\" reasoning in invariants.md accurate.\n3. **CLAUDE.md \"When adding something\"**: a schema change edits `schema.ts` and runs `pnpm db:generate` in `common/`; the existing \"a change to the item JSON\" bullet's migration clause follows the same wording.\n4. **`common-package.md`**: the item row's reads and writes become the per-table functions over drizzle (1.3's table), the row types derive from the schema, the JSON codec is gone, and the migrations are generated. Mermaid diagrams updated.\n5. **`persistence-and-storage.md`**: how the Workers reach D1 (drizzle client over the binding, batches as transactions, no interactive transactions) and the write ownership paragraphs.\n6. **`deployment-and-ci.md`**: the `common-checks` leg that fails when the schema changed without its migration.\n7. **`item-contract.md` / `item-lifecycle.md`**: only where they name the old functions or files (`readItem`, `writeStatus` stays, `insertQueued`, `retry-claim`), or the retry route's order (it now reads the item before claiming).\n8. **Local wiki**: a new entry under `.mahou/wiki/` for drizzle on D1 (versions 0.45.4 / 0.31.11 and why not the 1.0 RC: per-migration subfolders invisible to wrangler and `readD1Migrations`; `text({enum})` emits no CHECK so add `check()`; JSON columns via `mode: \"json\"`; `db.batch` is D1's transaction, `db.transaction` is rejected by D1 from a binding; 0.x qualifies columns inside CHECKs). Add its line to the right `INDEX.md`, following the existing entries' shape.\n\nEnd with a report: per file, the sections changed, and anything you could not land.\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper\n$H spawn --kind claude --label \"impl: drizzle (ASE-84)\" --model opus --body \"<supervisor-agent>Read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/implement-ASE-84.md. It is your full brief.</supervisor-agent>\"\n$H spawn --kind claude --label \"docs: drizzle\" --model opus --body \"<supervisor-agent>Read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/docs-drizzle.md. It is your full brief.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Write briefs and spawn the drizzle implementation and docs subagents"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1713,"