{"parentUuid":"c2d09b24-6ac2-4143-8dbd-9fcaa51227b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwFGawYYZvJfrkiBPXTT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":406736,"output_tokens":2762,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2762,"cache_read_input_tokens":406736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":21211,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d4b217bb-b62f-4dfc-872b-bcb817aa486c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwFGaWW38ajU4vvHXA5S","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:learn","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"207519bf-f5b8-4eb8-985e-b29b45457d08","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:35:02.498Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"207519bf-f5b8-4eb8-985e-b29b45457d08","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwFGawYYZvJfrkiBPXTT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Below is everything new since the last compaction that could become something reusable. For each item: the job it does and where it would land. Correct the reading here before I draft anything.\n\n**1. Questions on the canvas go inside the branch (program-design-with-canvas iteration)**\nYou corrected this twice. Answers and questions belong inside the part being discussed, next to the items they're about, not in a note at the top. A question gets a violet card, and the findings go in a Claude note under it, as in design-with-canvas. When the question closes, the card is deleted and the part is redrawn. Lands in `mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, as a new \"Questions\" section.\n\n**2. Full report in the subagent's final message (implement iteration)**\n`collect` returns only a subagent's last message. Several reports were lost because a later short message, such as \"these notifications are stale\", replaced them. Every brief and follow-up prompt says the final message holds the full report. Lands in the \"How to answer\" bullet of `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`.\n\n**3. Compact a reused subagent between tasks (implement iteration)**\nWhen the same subagent takes on a further task (review, local dev, validation, fixes) and its context is high, run `/compact` with a list of what to keep, after its current turn and before the next brief. You asked for this when it reached 73%. Lands in \"Dispatch and collect\" of `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`.\n\n**4. Consistency check after implementation (new agent plus an implement step)**\nA read-only subagent sweeps the whole repository and writes findings grouped as Leftovers, Docs vs code, Code vs code and Vocabulary, each with file and line, both sides quoted and a proposed fix. The user settles the findings, and an implementation subagent applies them. Lands in `mahou/agents/consistency-checker.md`, plus a step in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md` between design reconciliation and manual validation.\n\n**5. Covering rows that real inputs can't reach (validate iteration)**\n- **Synthetic page:** when no real input has what a row needs, the subagent builds a small synthetic one, served locally through a tunnel the system under test can reach.\n- **Forced failure:** to reach an error path, it changes code temporarily, runs the row, restores the file with `git checkout`, and confirms with `git status` that it is clean.\n- **Backdated timestamp:** to skip a wait, it backdates a timestamp in the local database, and records the change in the report.\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/validate/SKILL.md`.\n\n**6. Comparison clips for spoken-form decisions (local, nagara)**\nWhen a question about how the TTS reads something comes up (dots, numbers), the subagent synthesizes short A/B clips with the `modal serve` dev copy, writes an index of which clip says what, and lets the user listen before changing anything. Lands in `.mahou/` in nagara.\n\n**7. Test doubles never reach the production bundle (local, nagara)**\nYou ruled that the fake agent must not be in production code. Test doubles get wired in through the vitest config, and a build check confirms `dist/` holds no trace of them. Lands in nagara's `CLAUDE.md` code style, or in `.mahou/`.\n\n**8. Rules for subagents while you're away (implement, local or global)**\n- **Questions through the Inbox:** subagents send their questions through the Plannotator Inbox, keep working on whatever doesn't depend on the answer, and take the most reversible option consistent with the design when they're blocked.\n- **No `rm -rf`:** your `Bash(rm -rf:*)` ask rule turns any `rm -rf` into a dialog that blocks a subagent, so briefs forbid it.\n\n**Open points to settle before drafting:**\n1. Which of items 1–8 to keep.\n2. Item 4: the agent name (`consistency-checker`, or another), and whether implement always runs it or only when you ask.\n3. Item 7: nagara's `CLAUDE.md` or `.mahou/`.\n4. Item 8, the Inbox part: a global implement option for when you step away, or local to nagara.\n5. Item 8, the `rm -rf` part: your global `CLAUDE.md`, mahou basics, or local to nagara."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":406736,"output_tokens":2762,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2762,"cache_read_input_tokens":406736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d4b217bb-b62f-4dfc-872b-bcb817aa486c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwFGaWW38ajU4vvHXA5S","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:learn","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"c065f937-7c8c-436c-a422-d7b896dc5056","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:35:09.641Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
