he drizzle docs result"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ae298e8b-06a9-433f-8488-4996b37af609","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwFczs2ToE5ZP4q8xuff","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"755173a2-1ff8-44c3-93ce-346c53c77e73","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:39:18.159Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"755173a2-1ff8-44c3-93ce-346c53c77e73","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"400f1f2c-2c82-40fe-a468-5c63dc156957","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LCjJtXqttR6b4P4pPYLKGU","type":"tool_result","content":"done\nThe drizzle docs edits are written to disk and nothing is committed. Both unslop rounds and the documentation reviewer ran, and I applied their findings. I touched only `docs/`, `CLAUDE.md` and `.mahou/`. I wrote from the program design, then compared it with the code the implementation child had landed so far: the function names, `common/src/db/`, `0000_initial.sql` and `db:generate` match. The table-qualified columns inside CHECKs show up in the generated migration.\n\n**`CLAUDE.md`**\n- **Layout table:** the `common/` row now says it holds the drizzle schema, a query function for every read and write, and the migrations generated from the schema.\n- **Commands block:** added `pnpm db:generate` to the `common/` line.\n- **Invariant 7:** the schema is `common/src/db/schema.ts`; drizzle-kit generates the migration, which the developer reviews and commits; migrations apply before either Worker deploys; the tests build their schema from the same migrations.\n- **Code style:** new bullet for the database exception. Every D1 read and write is a drizzle query function in `common/src/db/`, one folder per table, even when only one Worker uses it. Functions are named `get`, `list`, `create`, `update`, `delete`, plus conditional writes named for what they do, and no route or step writes SQL.\n- **\"When adding something\":**\n  - New \"A schema change\" bullet: edit `schema.ts`, run `pnpm db:generate`, commit the reviewed SQL, and write the query functions the change needs.\n  - The item-JSON bullet's migration clause uses the same wording. It also says a backfill on its own goes into an empty migration from `pnpm db:generate --custom`; that is my addition, beyond the brief's wording.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/common-package.md`**\n- **Summary and overview:** now name the schema, the query functions and the generated migrations, plus the database exception.\n- **Architecture:** the diagram shows schema → row types and query functions, and drizzle-kit → migrations → D1. The prose says the schema is the single source for all three.\n- **\"What it holds\":** the row types derive from the schema. New rows for the D1 schema and the query functions. The migrations row says they are generated. The JSON codec row is removed.\n- **New section \"🗄️ Reading and writing D1\":**\n  - What `database(d1)` does, the naming pattern, and a diagram of the per-table folders.\n  - A table of the nine functions with what each answers and who calls it.\n  - The CHECK, JSON and boolean column notes.\n  - Queries are returned unawaited, and the steps that batch are named.\n  - Two callouts: a TIP that rejects interactive transactions, and a NOTE on why the queries live in `common/`.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md`**\n- **Summary:** migrations are now \"generated from the schema\".\n- **Write-ownership paragraph:** the API writes `queued` through `createItem`, `claimRetry` and `claimRequeue`.\n- **JSON columns paragraph:** drizzle encodes and decodes the columns, they carry `json_valid` CHECKs, and the row type derives from the schema.\n- **\"🗃️ How the schema changes\":** new diagram from schema edit through generate, review, local apply, tests, the CI check and the remote apply. The prose covers the generated files, `meta/` and the CI failure.\n- **Architecture:** Workers reach D1 only through the query functions, with a link to `common-package` for batching. I kept the batching detail out of this note because the reviewer flagged it as repeated.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md`**\n- The `common/` deploy paragraph says the migrations are generated.\n- The CI diagram node and prose describe the extra `common/` check: run `pnpm db:generate` and fail on a new or changed file under `common/migrations/`.\n- A failed schema check stops the whole chain.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/invariants.md`**\n- Row 7 is rewritten to match. It keeps \"the suite exercises the migration path\" and adds that CI fails a schema change with no migration.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/item-contract.md` and `item-lifecycle.md`**\n- **Retry route:** reads the item, then claims it.\n- **Claim callouts:** the claim gates on the count the route read, and a retry that loses reads the row again so its `409` names the status the other retry wrote. I also replaced the unclear \"the cap would read tighter than it is\" with what actually happens: the item can be retried more times than the cap allows.\n- **`item-lifecycle.md` status-write paragraph:** names `createItem` and the claims instead of `INSERT`/`UPDATE`.\n\n**Beyond the brief's list:**\n- `docs/technical-design/README.md`: the index rows for `common-package` and `persistence-and-storage` no longer say \"hand-written\" migrations or \"item row's reads and writes\".\n- `recipes.md`: one sentence now says the `recipe_versions` table comes from the schema.\n\n**`.mahou/wiki/`**\n- New `cloudflare/drizzle-on-d1.md` covering:\n  - the versions 0.45.4 / 0.31.11, and why not the 1.0 RC (wrangler and `readD1Migrations` can't see its subfolders)\n  - `text({enum})` emits no CHECK, so add `check()`\n  - JSON columns via `mode: \"json\"`, plus their `json_valid` CHECK\n  - booleans via `integer({ mode: \"boolean\" })`\n  - `db.batch` is D1's transaction and `db.transaction` is rejected from a binding\n  - 0.x qualifies columns inside CHECKs, as the generated SQL shows\n- It has a line in `cloudflare/INDEX.md`, and the root `INDEX.md` line for `cloudflare` mentions it.\n\n**Left alone:**\n- The documentation reviewer asked to turn the \"this note\" cells into links. The existing cassette row already uses \"this note\", so I kept that.\n- Unslop flagged older sentences outside the brief's scope, such as \"Deploys are not made twice…\" and \"with `409`; `404` for an unknown id\". I didn't change them.\n- `local-development.md` already describes the schema correctly. I didn't document the one-time `.wrangler-state` reset, since it isn't a standing mechanism.\n\n**Could not land:** nothing.\n\nThe review and unslop reports are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/docs-drizzle/`.\n M .mahou/wiki/INDEX.md\n M .mahou/wiki/cloudflare/INDEX.md\n M CLAUDE.md\nD  api/src/items/create.ts\n M api/src/items/requeue.ts\nD  api/src/items/retry-claim.ts\n M api/src/routes/audio.ts\n M api/src/routes/enqueue.ts\n M api/src/routes/images.ts\n M api/src/routes/poll.ts\n M api/src/routes/retry.ts\n M api/test/audio.test.ts\n M api/test/enqueue.test.ts\n M api/test/guard.test.ts\n M api/test/helpers/items.ts\n M api/test/images.test.ts\n M api/test/poll.test.ts\n M api/test/retry.test.ts\n M common/biome.json\nD  common/migrations/0001_initial.sql\n M common/package.json\n M common/src/index.ts\nD  common/src/item-store/json-column.ts\nD  common/src/item-store/read-item.ts\nD  common/src/item-store/write-status.ts\n M common/src/item.ts\n M common/src/ledger.ts\n M common/src/recipe.ts\nD  common/test/item-store/insert-item.ts\nD  common/test/item-store/read-item.test.ts\nD  common/test/item-store/write-status.test.ts\n M common/tsconfig.json\n M docs/technical-design/README.md\n M docs/technical-design/common-package.md\n M docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md\n M docs/technical-design/invariants.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-contract.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md\n M docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md\n M docs/technical-design/recipes.md\n M pipeline/package.json\n M pipeline/src/recipes/store.ts\nD  pipeline/src/workflow/ledger.ts\n M pipeline/src/workflow/require-item.ts\n M pipeline/src/workflow/steps/describe.ts\n M pipeline/src/workflow/steps/fetch.ts\n M pipeline/src/workflow/steps/images.ts\n M pipeline/src/workflow/steps/recipe.ts\n M pipeline/src/workflow/steps/synthesis.ts\n M pipeline/src/workflow/wrapper.ts\n M pipeline/test/helpers/item.ts\n M pipeline/test/helpers/scenario.ts\n M pipeline/test/item-enrichment.test.ts\n M pipeline/test/item-lease.test.ts\n M pipeline/test/item-recipe.test.ts\n M pnpm-lock.yaml\n?? .mahou/wiki/cloudflare/drizzle-on-d1.md\n?? common/drizzle.config.ts\n?? common/migrations/\n?? common/src/db/\n?? common/test/db/","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"23082828-5104-4e75-9214-c03298de592e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:39:18.727Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\nThe drizzle docs edits are written to disk and nothing is committed. Both unslop rounds and the documentation reviewer ran, and I applied their findings. I touched only `docs/`, `CLAUDE.md` and `.mahou/`. I wrote from the program design, then compared it with the code the implementation child had landed so far: the function names, `common/src/db/`, `0000_initial.sql` and `db:generate` match. The table-qualified columns inside CHECKs show up in the generated migration.\n\n**`CLAUDE.md`**\n- **Layout table:** the `common/` row now says it holds the drizzle schema, a query function for every read and write, and the migrations generated from the schema.\n- **Commands block:** added `pnpm db:generate` to the `common/` line.\n- **Invariant 7:** the schema is `common/src/db/schema.ts`; drizzle-kit generates the migration, which the developer reviews and commits; migrations apply before either Worker deploys; the tests build their schema from the same migrations.\n- **Code style:** new bullet for the database exception. Every D1 read and write is a drizzle query function in `common/src/db/`, one folder per table, even when only one Worker uses it. Functions are named `get`, `list`, `create`, `update`, `delete`, plus conditional writes named for what they do, and no route or step writes SQL.\n- **\"When adding something\":**\n  - New \"A schema change\" bullet: edit `schema.ts`, run `pnpm db:generate`, commit the reviewed SQL, and write the query functions the change needs.\n  - The item-JSON bullet's migration clause uses the same wording. It also says a backfill on its own goes into an empty migration from `pnpm db:generate --custom`; that is my addition, beyond the brief's wording.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/common-package.md`**\n- **Summary and overview:** now name the schema, the query functions and the generated migrations, plus the database exception.\n- **Architecture:** the diagram shows schema → row types and query functions, and drizzle-kit → migrations → D1. The prose says the schema is the single source for all three.\n- **\"What it holds\":** the row types derive from the schema. New rows for the D1 schema and the query functions. The migrations row says they are generated. The JSON codec row is removed.\n- **New section \"🗄️ Reading and writing D1\":**\n  - What `database(d1)` does, the naming pattern, and a diagram of the per-table folders.\n  - A table of the nine functions with what each answers and who calls it.\n  - The CHECK, JSON and boolean column notes.\n  - Queries are returned unawaited, and the steps that batch are named.\n  - Two callouts: a TIP that rejects interactive transactions, and a NOTE on why the queries live in `common/`.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md`**\n- **Summary:** migrations are now \"generated from the schema\".\n- **Write-ownership paragraph:** the API writes `queued` through `createItem`, `claimRetry` and `claimRequeue`.\n- **JSON columns paragraph:** drizzle encodes and decodes the columns, they carry `json_valid` CHECKs, and the row type derives from the schema.\n- **\"🗃️ How the schema changes\":** new diagram from schema edit through generate, review, local apply, tests, the CI check and the remote apply. The prose covers the generated files, `meta/` and the CI failure.\n- **Architecture:** Workers reach D1 only through the query functions, with a link to `common-package` for batching. I kept the batching detail out of this note because the reviewer flagged it as repeated.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md`**\n- The `common/` deploy paragraph says the migrations are generated.\n- The CI diagram node and prose describe the extra `common/` check: run `pnpm db:generate` and fail on a new or changed file under `common/migrations/`.\n- A failed schema check stops the whole chain.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/invariants.md`**\n- Row 7 is rewritten to match. It keeps \"the suite exercises the migration path\" and adds that CI fails a schema change with no migration.\n\n**`docs/technical-design/item-contract.md` and `item-lifecycle.md`**\n- **Retry route:** reads the item, then claims it.\n- **Claim callouts:** the claim gates on the count the route read, and a retry that loses reads the row again so its `409` names the status the other retry wrote. I also replaced the unclear \"the cap would read tighter than it is\" with what actually happens: the item can be retried more times than the cap allows.\n- **`item-lifecycle.md` status-write paragraph:** names `createItem` and the claims instead of `INSERT`/`UPDATE`.\n\n**Beyond the brief's list:**\n- `docs/technical-design/README.md`: the index rows for `common-package` and `persistence-and-storage` no longer say \"hand-written\" migrations or \"item row's reads and writes\".\n- `recipes.md`: one sentence now says the `recipe_versions` table comes from the schema.\n\n**`.mahou/wiki/`**\n- New `cloudflare/drizzle-on-d1.md` covering:\n  - the versions 0.45.4 / 0.31.11, and why not the 1.0 RC (wrangler and `readD1Migrations` can't see its subfolders)\n  - `text({enum})` emits no CHECK, so add `check()`\n  - JSON columns via `mode: \"json\"`, plus their `json_valid` CHECK\n  - booleans via `integer({ mode: \"boolean\" })`\n  - `db.batch` is D1's transaction and `db.transaction` is rejected from a binding\n  - 0.x qualifies columns inside CHECKs, as the generated SQL shows\n- It has a line in `cloudflare/INDEX.md`, and the root `INDEX.md` line for `cloudflare` mentions it.\n\n**Left alone:**\n- The documentation reviewer asked to turn the \"this note\" cells into links. The existing cassette row already uses \"this note\", so I kept that.\n- Unslop flagged older sentences outside the brief's scope, such as \"Deploys are not made twice…\" and \"with `409`; `404` for an unknown id\". I didn't change them.\n- `local-development.md` already describes the schema correctly. I didn't document the one-time `.wrangler-state` reset, since it isn't a standing mechanism.\n\n**Could not land:** nothing.\n\nThe review and unslop reports are in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/docs-drizzle/`.\n M .mahou/wiki/INDEX.md\n M .mahou/wiki/cloudflare/INDEX.md\n M CLAUDE.md\nD  api/src/items/create.ts\n M api/src/items/requeue.ts\nD  api/src/items/retry-claim.ts\n M api/src/routes/audio.ts\n M api/src/routes/enqueue.ts\n M api/src/routes/images.ts\n M api/src/routes/poll.ts\n M api/src/routes/retry.ts\n M api/test/audio.test.ts\n M api/test/enqueue.test.ts\n M api/test/guard.test.ts\n M api/test/helpers/items.ts\n M api/test/images.test.ts\n M api/test/poll.test.ts\n M api/test/retry.test.ts\n M common/biome.json\nD  common/migrations/0001_initial.sql\n M common/package.json\n M common/src/index.ts\nD  common/src/item-store/json-column.ts\nD  common/src/item-store/read-item.ts\nD  common/src/item-store/write-status.ts\n M common/src/item.ts\n M common/src/ledger.ts\n M common/src/recipe.ts\nD  common/test/item-store/insert-item.ts\nD  common/test/item-store/read-item.test.ts\nD  common/test/item-store/write-status.test.ts\n M common/tsconfig.json\n M docs/technical-design/README.md\n M docs/technical-design/common-package.md\n M docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md\n M docs/technical-design/invariants.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-contract.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md\n M docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md\n M docs/technical-design/recipes.md\n M pipeline/package.jso