{"parentUuid":"6ad23178-468f-4815-9f90-dd2e139ab263","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a77ed1ac-4d2e-4568-98f6-e2f8885d205b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"\n\n<pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n# Annotations on claude · last message\n\n## Annotation 1 (lines 3–4)\nComment on: \"**1. Questions on the canvas go inside the branch (program-design-with-canvas iteration)** You corrected this twice. Answers and questions belong inside the part being discussed, next to the items they're about, not in a note at the top. A question gets a violet card, and the findings go in a Claude note under it, as in design-with-canvas. When the question closes, the card is deleted and the part is redrawn. Lands in `mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, as a new \"Questions\" section.\"\n> this isn't properly defined on the canvas skill? does it belong here?\n\n## Annotation 2 (lines 6–7)\nLooks good: \"**2. Full report in the subagent's final message (implement iteration)** `collect` returns only a subagent's last message. Several reports were lost because a later short message, such as \"these notifications are stale\", replaced them. Every brief and follow-up prompt says the final message holds the full report. Lands in the \"How to answer\" bullet of `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`.\"\n\n## Annotation 3 (lines 9–10)\nComment on: \"**3. Compact a reused subagent between tasks (implement iteration)** When the same subagent takes on a further task (review, local dev, validation, fixes) and its context is high, run `/compact` with a list of what to keep, after its current turn and before the next brief. You asked for this when it reached 73%. Lands in \"Dispatch and collect\" of `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`.\"\n> sounds good, we should keep an eye for when we get around 50% and only compact after completing a task and before taking a new one, never when working on a task\n\n## Annotation 4 (lines 12–13)\nComment on: \"**4. Consistency check after implementation (new agent plus an implement step)** A read-only subagent sweeps the whole repository and writes findings grouped as Leftovers, Docs vs code, Code vs code and Vocabulary, each with file and line, both sides quoted and a proposed fix. The user settles the findings, and an implementation subagent applies them. Lands in `mahou/agents/consistency-checker.md`, plus a step in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md` between design reconciliation and manual validation.\"\n> hmm this should be part of design reconciliation actually; also the validation should happen before the reconciliation\n\n## Annotation 5 (line 20)\nLooks good: \"Lands in `mahou/skills/validate/SKILL.md`.\"\n\n## Annotation 6 (lines 22–23)\nRemove this:\n```\n**6. Comparison clips for spoken-form decisions (local, nagara)**\nWhen a question about how the TTS reads something comes up (dots, numbers), the subagent synthesizes short A/B clips with the `modal serve` dev copy, writes an index of which clip says what, and lets the user listen before changing anything. Lands in `.mahou/` in nagara.\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 7 (lines 25–26)\nLooks good: \"**7. Test doubles never reach the production bundle (local, nagara)** You ruled that the fake agent must not be in production code. Test doubles get wired in through the vitest config, and a build check confirms `dist/` holds no trace of them. Lands in nagara's `CLAUDE.md` code style, or in `.mahou/`.\"\n\n</pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n"},"uuid":"94eaa845-e320-402b-b2a0-a20cfa3f3e66","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:40:19.127Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":109,"turnIndex":317},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
