tion (new agent plus an implement step)** A read-only subagent sweeps the whole repository and writes findings grouped as Leftovers, Docs vs code, Code vs code and Vocabulary, each with file and line, both sides quoted and a proposed fix. The user settles the findings, and an implementation subagent applies them. Lands in `mahou/agents/consistency-checker.md`, plus a step in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md` between design reconciliation and manual validation.\"\n> hmm this should be part of design reconciliation actually; also the validation should happen before the reconciliation\n\n## Annotation 5 (line 20)\nLooks good: \"Lands in `mahou/skills/validate/SKILL.md`.\"\n\n## Annotation 6 (lines 22–23)\nRemove this:\n```\n**6. Comparison clips for spoken-form decisions (local, nagara)**\nWhen a question about how the TTS reads something comes up (dots, numbers), the subagent synthesizes short A/B clips with the `modal serve` dev copy, writes an index of which clip says what, and lets the user listen before changing anything. Lands in `.mahou/` in nagara.\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 7 (lines 25–26)\nLooks good: \"**7. Test doubles never reach the production bundle (local, nagara)** You ruled that the fake agent must not be in production code. Test doubles get wired in through the vitest config, and a build check confirms `dist/` holds no trace of them. Lands in nagara's `CLAUDE.md` code style, or in `.mahou/`.\"\n\n## Annotation 8 (line 28)\nComment on: \"Rules for subagents while you're away (implement, local or global)\"\n> this should be a genera rule for subagents\n\n## Annotation 9 (line 29)\nRemove this:\n```\n- **Questions through the Inbox:** subagents send their questions through the Plannotator Inbox, keep working on whatever doesn't depend on the answer, and take the most reversible option consistent with the design when they're blocked.\n```\n> I don't want this.\n\n## Annotation 10 (line 30)\nComment on: \"- **No `rm -rf`:** your `Bash(rm -rf:*)` ask rule turns any `rm -rf` into a dialog that blocks a subagent, so briefs forbid it.\"\n> don't forbid, ask to avoid it if possible\n\n</pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n"},"uuid":"ce7fc56e-d973-403b-9128-e4565caf7015","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:40:55.785Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":110,"turnIndex":318},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
