{"parentUuid":"a7b7312d-3a2b-4698-a564-83f71ad764c2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"43392324-2db6-4e56-97a3-bcf3a6f6789f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bm3DGTLTH4eMaaStZ2MCr7","type":"tool_result","content":"126\t- **A new rule for how the recipe step's units become the item's** (the spoken form, the drop) → a function\n127\t  at the end of the item Workflow's recipe step in `pipeline/`, beside the spoken-form derivation, and a\n128\t  test case, plus a section or callout in\n129\t  `docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md`.\n130\t- **A change to the item JSON** → `docs/technical-design/item-contract.md`, **and a migration in\n131\t  `common/` when the persisted shape needs a backfill**: a column change edits\n132\t  `common/src/db/schema.ts` and runs `pnpm db:generate` in `common/`, and a backfill alone is SQL\n133\t  written into the empty migration `pnpm db:generate --custom` creates. Write the backfill\n134\t  because the item Workflow persists the display list across the async gap: a later step or request\n135\t  reads the in-flight item back, and that reader is not the step that wrote the row. **A new member of the unit union needs neither**: the item row's `units` is a JSON column, so the union\n136\t  is not schema and there is no DDL to write, and rows persisted before the new kind existed carry none\n137\t  of it and stay readable unchanged.\n138\t- **A schema change** → an edit to `common/src/db/schema.ts` and `pnpm db:generate` in `common/`,\n139\t  with the generated SQL reviewed and committed beside it (invariant 7), plus the query functions in"}]},"uuid":"954a2ee4-da7f-4c04-8dbe-932c79bcb559","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:41:51.423Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/CLAUDE.md","content":"- **A new rule for how the recipe step's units become the item's** (the spoken form, the drop) → a function\n  at the end of the item Workflow's recipe step in `pipeline/`, beside the spoken-form derivation, and a\n  test case, plus a section or callout in\n  `docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md`.\n- **A change to the item JSON** → `docs/technical-design/item-contract.md`, **and a migration in\n  `common/` when the persisted shape needs a backfill**: a column change edits\n  `common/src/db/schema.ts` and runs `pnpm db:generate` in `common/`, and a backfill alone is SQL\n  written into the empty migration `pnpm db:generate --custom` creates. Write the backfill\n  because the item Workflow persists the display list across the async gap: a later step or request\n  reads the in-flight item back, and that reader is not the step that wrote the row. **A new member of the unit union needs neither**: the item row's `units` is a JSON column, so the union\n  is not schema and there is no DDL to write, and rows persisted before the new kind existed carry none\n  of it and stay readable unchanged.\n- **A schema change** → an edit to `common/src/db/schema.ts` and `pnpm db:generate` in `common/`,\n  with the generated SQL reviewed and committed beside it (invariant 7), plus the query functions in","numLines":14,"startLine":126,"totalLines":163}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a7b7312d-3a2b-4698-a564-83f71ad764c2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
