{"parentUuid":"70d21730-5617-4fbd-9491-e3b1628e075e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"769a7d9a-4c76-4466-ad6f-542f4a0e9fa9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"\n\n<pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n# Annotations on claude · last message\n\n## Annotation 1 (lines 6–7)\nLooks good: \"- **Chat or canvas:** program-design-with-canvas never says which one to use, so I answered in the chat until you told me otherwise. - **The question card:** the violet `❓ Q<n>` card, the Claude note under it, and deleting the card when the question closes are defined only in design-with-canvas. Program design now uses them too.\"\n\n## Annotation 2 (lines 10–11)\nComment on: \"- **(a) program-design-with-canvas:** a short section that names the canvas as the place to talk, and copies the question card from design-with-canvas. - **(b) the canvas skill:** a question-card subsection under \"Talking on the canvas\", read by every loading skill. Design-with-canvas would point to it instead of defining the card, and program-design-with-canvas would add only \"talk on the canvas\".\"\n> let's do it on program-design-with-canvas; does any of the other with-canvas skill require this too?\n\n</pasted_content id=\"bfba\">\n"},"uuid":"0279a4ac-61c4-4185-81b9-c4cc6ba9646e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:43:04.457Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":112,"turnIndex":320},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
