ose. When a branch settles, draw its representation and prose in its section and ask the user to approve it there.\n36:## Questions\n38:Questions go in the open branch, on its right side, under its write-up. The branch's Claude note goes under the questions.\n40:- **A question is a violet card**: a rectangle with violet border and fill, titled `❓ Q<n> · <title>`, then the body, which gives the situation and ends with the question. Add a diagram, drawn with tldraw shapes, when the question is about where something runs, in what order or across which boundary.\n41:- **Follow-ups stay inside the base question's card**, one at a time, until the question branch closes. The card holds, top to bottom: the base question and its diagram, a summary box, one Claude note, and the current follow-up as a violet card of its own.\n42:- **The summary box**, a solid grey rectangle labelled `Summary · Q<n> so far`, holds what the question branch has settled and the findings that bear on it. Rewrite it each round; never add a line per answer.\n43:- **When the question branch closes**, delete the card, update the branch's leaves on the left, and update its write-up.\n44:- **Keep two questions open for the user to answer.** A question waiting on a spike, a prototype or a lookup does not count toward the two, so there are three while one waits. Open the next question from the frontier as soon as one closes.\n48:Everything you would say in the chat goes on the canvas: how you read an answer, research and spike results, status, and requests to approve a branch. Write it as a Claude note: a grey dashed rectangle labelled `Claude`, in the branch or the question it is about. Keep one Claude note per place and replace its text each round. When a branch is done, delete its note.\n52:When the tree is complete, stop the canvas and continue with `design`'s Recording section in the chat.\n== program-design-with-canvas\n== test-design-with-canvas\n3:description: Runs the test-design skill on a canvas