{"parentUuid":"5acf123f-481e-45da-a3f6-9ab43d2f9c86","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwG7zz2FQA9EyKo8cEBH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing the drafts for the learn items to the scratch folder, then running the unslop pass on them before showing you."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":435211,"output_tokens":4035,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4035,"cache_read_input_tokens":435211,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"25cbd3d2-d1f3-4c20-95e5-7d4aa946b97f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwG7zARKm9VN337fWXfW","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"77cd7f7c-42d9-4260-9fb0-32af4ef2d682","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:45:52.077Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"77cd7f7c-42d9-4260-9fb0-32af4ef2d682","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwG7zz2FQA9EyKo8cEBH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KW8jqy2iiJmis5DsSuq9Fi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round4/drafts.md","content":"# Learn round 4: drafts\n\n## 1. program-design-with-canvas: talk on the canvas, questions inside the part\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, two new sections after \"The canvas\", before \"Mockups\".\n\n```markdown\n## Questions\n\nA question goes inside the part it is about, on the right side of the part's area, next to the items it discusses. The part's Claude note goes under the questions.\n\n- **A question is a violet card**: a rectangle with violet border and fill, titled `❓ Q<n> · <title>`, then the body, which gives the situation and ends with the question. Add a diagram, drawn with tldraw shapes, when the question is about where something runs, in what order or across which boundary.\n- **Follow-ups stay inside the base question's card**, one at a time, until the question closes. The card holds, top to bottom: the base question and its diagram, a summary box, one Claude note, and the current follow-up as a violet card of its own.\n- **The summary box**, a solid grey rectangle labelled `Summary · Q<n> so far`, holds what the question has settled and the findings that bear on it. Rewrite it each round; never add a line per answer.\n- **When the question closes**, delete the card, redraw the part with what it settled, and update the record.\n\n## Messages from Claude\n\nEverything you would say in the chat goes on the canvas: how you read an answer, research results, status, and requests to approve a part. Write it as a Claude note: a grey dashed rectangle labelled `Claude`, in the part or the question it is about. Keep one Claude note per place and replace its text each round. When a part settles, delete its note.\n```\n\n## 1b. test-design-with-canvas: questions inside the branch\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/test-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`. The \"Messages from Claude\" section is replaced, and a \"Questions\" section goes before it.\n\nOld:\n\n```markdown\n## Messages from Claude\n\nWrite what you would say in the chat as one Claude note at the top of the canvas: how to read the drawing, the open questions, and the implementation tasks the trees surfaced. Replace its text each round.\n```\n\nNew:\n\n```markdown\n## Questions\n\nA question goes inside the branch it is about, beside the classification, partition or row it discusses. A question about a root goes beside its card on the map. The branch's Claude note goes under the questions.\n\n- **A question is a card with a violet border and no fill**, titled `❓ Q<n> · <title>`, then the body, which gives the situation and ends with the question. The missing fill keeps it apart from the filled violet classification boxes.\n- **Follow-ups stay inside the base question's card**, one at a time, until the question closes. The card holds, top to bottom: the base question, a summary box, one Claude note, and the current follow-up as a card of its own.\n- **The summary box**, a solid grey rectangle labelled `Summary · Q<n> so far`, holds what the question has settled. Rewrite it each round; never add a line per answer.\n- **When the question closes**, delete the card, redraw the branch with what it settled, and update the record.\n\n## Messages from Claude\n\nEverything you would say in the chat goes on the canvas, as a Claude note: a grey dashed rectangle labelled `Claude`, in the branch, tree or question it is about. One note at the top of the canvas says how to read the drawing and lists the implementation tasks the trees surfaced. Keep one Claude note per place and replace its text each round.\n```\n\n## 2. implement: the full report in the final message\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"The brief\", the \"How to answer\" bullet.\n\nOld: \"**How to answer.** A report in the shape mahou:report gives: the branch, the commits, a summary per change, the row-to-test mapping, the linter and test output tail, and what it could not resolve. A design ambiguity that changes the outcome is a question back through the subagent's question channel, not a guess.\"\n\nNew: \"**How to answer.** A report in the shape mahou:report gives: the branch, the commits, a summary per change, the row-to-test mapping, the linter and test output tail, and what it could not resolve. The report is the whole of the subagent's final message, because collecting a result reads only that message: a shorter message sent after the report replaces it. Every later instruction to the subagent repeats this. A design ambiguity that changes the outcome is a question back through the subagent's question channel, not a guess.\"\n\n## 3. implement: compact a reused subagent between tasks\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"Dispatch and collect\", a new paragraph after \"Release a subagent…\".\n\n\"A subagent kept for further work, such as the review, a fix round or the manual validation, carries every earlier task in its context. Check its context use whenever it finishes a task. When it is near half, have it run `/compact` with a list of what to keep, such as the checkout it works in, the safety rules and where the briefs live, then send the next task. Compact only between tasks: never while it is working on one.\"\n\n## 4. consistency-checker agent, and the implement order\n\nNew file `mahou/agents/consistency-checker.md`:\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: consistency-checker\ndescription: Sweeps one repository after a change lands for leftovers of what the change replaced and for places where the code and the docs, or two parts of the code, disagree. Writes findings to a file and returns the path. Makes no edits.\ntools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash(git:*), Skill(mahou:docs)\nmodel: opus\n---\n\n# Consistency checker\n\nChecks one repository against itself once a change has landed. You edit nothing, and you start no servers or processes.\n\nYou are given the repository's absolute path, a summary of what the change replaced, and the path to write the findings to. Use `git -C <repo-path>` and absolute paths for everything. Never `cd`.\n\n## Read first\n\nLoad mahou:docs. Read the project's `CLAUDE.md`, the docs charter and every note the change touches, then the code: every package, the CI files, the root configuration and the project's local rule files when they describe the code.\n\n## What to look for\n\n1. **Leftovers**: files, dependencies, scripts, configuration keys, exports, test fixtures and comments that belonged to what the change replaced, or that nothing reads or imports any more.\n2. **Docs vs code**: every route, status code, body shape, step, retry count, timeout, limit, binding, variable, secret, key layout, migration, CI condition, local step and port a note or `CLAUDE.md` states, checked against the code.\n3. **Code vs code**: configuration files that must agree (bindings, ids, folders), the secrets an example file names against the ones the code reads, the shapes one service sends against the ones the other parses, shared types against what the code writes.\n4. **Vocabulary**: names, comments and tests that still use the replaced system's words for something that is now called differently.\n\nReport only where two things that should agree do not, and things that no longer have a reason to exist. No style preferences, and no reopening of decisions the notes record. When something looks wrong but has a recorded reason to stay, leave it out and list it under \"Not reported\" with the reason.\n\n## Output\n\nWrite the findings file with four sections, Leftovers, Docs vs code, Code vs code and Vocabulary. Each finding gets the file and line, the two sides that disagree quoted briefly, and the fix you would propose. Return the path and the count per section in your final message.\n```\n\n`mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`: the \"Manual validation\" section moves before \"Design reconciliation\", and \"Design reconciliation\" becomes:\n\nOld: \"The code that lands is what was actually built, and the notes drift from it the moment a child deviates, simplifies, or meets a platform fact. When a repository's implementation and review are done, collect the drift: every flag a subagent raised about a design mismatch, every pointing callout in a touched note whose condition has now landed, and every diagram that renders a shape the change altered. The user settles each one, and the agreed updates run through mahou:write-documentation once, with the whole documentation in view, before the manual validation reports the system as finished.\"\n\nNew: \"The code that lands is what was actually built, and the notes drift from it the moment a child deviates, simplifies, or meets a platform fact. When the manual validation has reported, collect the drift: every flag a subagent raised about a design mismatch, every pointing callout in a touched note whose condition has now landed, and every diagram that renders a shape the change altered. Then dispatch a `mahou:consistency-checker` per repository, with a summary of what the change replaced, for the leftovers and disagreements no flag named. The user settles each item. An implementation subagent applies the agreed code fixes, and the agreed documentation updates run through mahou:write-documentation once, with the whole documentation in view.\"\n\nIn \"Manual validation\", \"The next repository starts when the previous one has reported.\" stays, and nothing else changes.\n\n`mahou/README.md`, \"Agents\", a new line after `documentation-reviewer`:\n\n\"- `consistency-checker`: one repository after a change lands, for leftovers and for code that disagrees with the docs or with itself, dispatched by `implement` during design reconciliation.\"\n\nThe `implement` line in the skills list changes \"then runs `agentic-review` per repository and `validate` one repository at a time.\" to \"then runs `agentic-review` per repository, `validate` one repository at a time, and a consistency check before the docs are reconciled.\"\n\n## 5. validate: synthetic inputs and forced failures\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/validate/SKILL.md`, \"Mutating data to reach a row\".\n\nAfter the paragraph beginning \"Some rows need an error the system does not produce on its own\", add:\n\n\"A temporary code change can force the failure when no input or configuration reaches it: make the smallest change that produces the error, run the row, then restore the file with `git checkout -- <file>` and confirm with `git status` that it is clean before the next row. Run it while nothing else is in flight on the system, because the change reloads the server that runs the code. Record the change and its restore in the report like any other mutation.\"\n\nNew paragraph at the end of the section:\n\n\"When no real input has what a row needs, such as a page with every element the row combines, build a synthetic input: the smallest artifact that has those elements and reads like the real thing, kept in the change's scratch folder and served locally, behind a tunnel when the system under test runs remotely and must reach it. Say in the row which parts of the expected outcome it could not cover.\"\n\n## 7. nagara: test doubles stay out of the production bundle\n\nLands in nagara's `CLAUDE.md`, \"Code style\", a new bullet, or in `.mahou/implement.md` (the choice is open):\n\n\"- **A test double never reaches the production bundle.** The tests wire a fake in through the vitest configuration, such as a module the config substitutes, never through a setting or a branch the deployed code carries. After a build, `dist/` holds no trace of it.\"\n\n## 8. implement: avoid rm -rf\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"The brief\", the \"Repository rules\" bullet, appended:\n\n\"Avoid `rm -rf` when another way works, such as `rm -r` on a named path or leaving temporary files in `/tmp`: a permission rule can turn it into a dialog that blocks the subagent until the user answers.\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":435211,"output_tokens":4035,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4035,"cache_read_input_tokens":435211,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KW8jqy2iiJmis5DsSuq9Fi":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round4/drafts.md","content":"# Learn round 4: drafts\n\n## 1. program-design-with-canvas: talk on the canvas, questions inside the part\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, two new sections after \"The canvas\", before \"Mockups\".\n\n```markdown\n## Questions\n\nA question goes inside the part it is about, on the right side of the part's area, next to the items it discusses. The part's Claude note goes under the questions.\n\n- **A question is a violet card**: a rectangle with violet border and fill, titled `❓ Q<n> · <title>`, then the body, which gives the situation and ends with the question. Add a diagram, drawn with tldraw shapes, when the question is about where something runs, in what order or across which boundary.\n- **Follow-ups stay inside the base question's card**, one at a time, until the question closes. The card holds, top to bottom: the base question and its diagram, a summary box, one Claude note, and the current follow-up as a violet card of its own.\n- **The summary box**, a solid grey rectangle labelled `Summary · Q<n> so far`, holds what the question has settled and the findings that bear on it. Rewrite it each round; never add a line per answer.\n- **When the question closes**, delete the card, redraw the part with what it settled, and update the record.\n\n## Messages from Claude\n\nEverything you would say in the chat goes on the canvas: how you read an answer, research results, status, and requests to approve a part. Write it as a Claude note: a grey dashed rectangle labelled `Claude`, in the part or the question it is about. Keep one Claude note per place and replace its text each round. When a part settles, delete its note.\n```\n\n## 1b. test-design-with-canvas: questions inside the branch\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/test-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`. The \"Messages from Claude\" section is replaced, and a \"Questions\" section goes before it.\n\nOld:\n\n```markdown\n## Messages from Claude\n\nWrite what you would say in the chat as one Claude note at the top of the canvas: how to read the drawing, the open questions, and the implementation tasks the trees surfaced. Replace its text each round.\n```\n\nNew:\n\n```markdown\n## Questions\n\nA question goes inside the branch it is about, beside the classification, partition or row it discusses. A question about a root goes beside its card on the map. The branch's Claude note goes under the questions.\n\n- **A question is a card with a violet border and no fill**, titled `❓ Q<n> · <title>`, then the body, which gives the situation and ends with the question. The missing fill keeps it apart from the filled violet classification boxes.\n- **Follow-ups stay inside the base question's card**, one at a time, until the question closes. The card holds, top to bottom: the base question, a summary box, one Claude note, and the current follow-up as a card of its own.\n- **The summary box**, a solid grey rectangle labelled `Summary · Q<n> so far`, holds what the question has settled. Rewrite it each round; never add a line per answer.\n- **When the question closes**, delete the card, redraw the branch with what it settled, and update the record.\n\n## Messages from Claude\n\nEverything you would say in the chat goes on the canvas, as a Claude note: a grey dashed rectangle labelled `Claude`, in the branch, tree or question it is about. One note at the top of the canvas says how to read the drawing and lists the implementation tasks the trees surfaced. Keep one Claude note per place and replace its text each round.\n```\n\n## 2. implement: the full report in the final message\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"The brief\", the \"How to answer\" bullet.\n\nOld: \"**How to answer.** A report in the shape mahou:report gives: the branch, the commits, a summary per change, the row-to-test mapping, the linter and test output tail, and what it could not resolve. A design ambiguity that changes the outcome is a question back through the subagent's question channel, not a guess.\"\n\nNew: \"**How to answer.** A report in the shape mahou:report gives: the branch, the commits, a summary per change, the row-to-test mapping, the linter and test output tail, and what it could not resolve. The report is the whole of the subagent's final message, because collecting a result reads only that message: a shorter message sent after the report replaces it. Every later instruction to the subagent repeats this. A design ambiguity that changes the outcome is a question back through the subagent's question channel, not a guess.\"\n\n## 3. implement: compact a reused subagent between tasks\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"Dispatch and collect\", a new paragraph after \"Release a subagent…\".\n\n\"A subagent kept for further work, such as the review, a fix round or the manual validation, carries every earlier task in its context. Check its context use whenever it finishes a task. When it is near half, have it run `/compact` with a list of what to keep, such as the checkout it works in, the safety rules and where the briefs live, then send the next task. Compact only between tasks: never while it is working on one.\"\n\n## 4. consistency-checker agent, and the implement order\n\nNew file `mahou/agents/consistency-checker.md`:\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: consistency-checker\ndescription: Sweeps one repository after a change lands for leftovers of what the change replaced and for places where the code and the docs, or two parts of the code, disagree. Writes findings to a file and returns the path. Makes no edits.\ntools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash(git:*), Skill(mahou:docs)\nmodel: opus\n---\n\n# Consistency checker\n\nChecks one repository against itself once a change has landed. You edit nothing, and you start no servers or processes.\n\nYou are given the repository's absolute path, a summary of what the change replaced, and the path to write the findings to. Use `git -C <repo-path>` and absolute paths for everything. Never `cd`.\n\n## Read first\n\nLoad mahou:docs. Read the project's `CLAUDE.md`, the docs charter and every note the change touches, then the code: every package, the CI files, the root configuration and the project's local rule files when they describe the code.\n\n## What to look for\n\n1. **Leftovers**: files, dependencies, scripts, configuration keys, exports, test fixtures and comments that belonged to what the change replaced, or that nothing reads or imports any more.\n2. **Docs vs code**: every route, status code, body shape, step, retry count, timeout, limit, binding, variable, secret, key layout, migration, CI condition, local step and port a note or `CLAUDE.md` states, checked against the code.\n3. **Code vs code**: configuration files that must agree (bindings, ids, folders), the secrets an example file names against the ones the code reads, the shapes one service sends against the ones the other parses, shared types against what the code writes.\n4. **Vocabulary**: names, comments and tests that still use the replaced system's words for something that is now called differently.\n\nReport only where two things that should agree do not, and things that no longer have a reason to exist. No style preferences, and no reopening of decisions the notes record. When something looks wrong but has a recorded reason to stay, leave it out and list it under \"Not reported\" with the reason.\n\n## Output\n\nWrite the findings file with four sections, Leftovers, Docs vs code, Code vs code and Vocabulary. Each finding gets the file and line, the two sides that disagree quoted briefly, and the fix you would propose. Return the path and the count per section in your final message.\n```\n\n`mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`: the \"Manual validation\" section moves before \"Design reconciliation\", and \"Design reconciliation\" becomes:\n\nOld: \"The code that lands is what was actually built, and the notes drift from it the moment a child deviates, simplifies, or meets a platform fact. When a repository's implementation and review are done, collect the drift: every flag a subagent raised about a design mismatch, every pointing callout in a touched note whose condition has now landed, and every diagram that renders a shape the change altered. The user settles each one, and the agreed updates run through mahou:write-documentation once, with the whole documentation in view, before the manual validation reports the system as finished.\"\n\nNew: \"The code that lands is what was actually built, and the notes drift from it the moment a child deviates, simplifies, or meets a platform fact. When the manual validation has reported, collect the drift: every flag a subagent raised about a design mismatch, every pointing callout in a touched note whose condition has now landed, and every diagram that renders a shape the change altered. Then dispatch a `mahou:consistency-checker` per repository, with a summary of what the change replaced, for the leftovers and disagreements no flag named. The user settles each item. An implementation subagent applies the agreed code fixes, and the agreed documentation updates run through mahou:write-documentation once, with the whole documentation in view.\"\n\nIn \"Manual validation\", \"The next repository starts when the previous one has reported.\" stays, and nothing else changes.\n\n`mahou/README.md`, \"Agents\", a new line after `documentation-reviewer`:\n\n\"- `consistency-checker`: one repository after a change lands, for leftovers and for code that disagrees with the docs or with itself, dispatched by `implement` during design reconciliation.\"\n\nThe `implement` line in the skills list changes \"then runs `agentic-review` per repository and `validate` one repository at a time.\" to \"then runs `agentic-review` per repository, `validate` one repository at a time, and a consistency check before the docs are reconciled.\"\n\n## 5. validate: synthetic inputs and forced failures\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/validate/SKILL.md`, \"Mutating data to reach a row\".\n\nAfter the paragraph beginning \"Some rows need an error the system does not produce on its own\", add:\n\n\"A temporary code change can force the failure when no input or configuration reaches it: make the smallest change that produces the error, run the row, then restore the file with `git checkout -- <file>` and confirm with `git status` that it is clean before the next row. Run it while nothing else is in flight on the system, because the change reloads the server that runs the code. Record the change and its restore in the report like any other mutation.\"\n\nNew paragraph at the end of the section:\n\n\"When no real input has what a row needs, such as a page with every element the row combines, build a synthetic input: the smallest artifact that has those elements and reads like the real thing, kept in the change's scratch folder and served locally, behind a tunnel when the system under test runs remotely and must reach it. Say in the row which parts of the expected outcome it could not cover.\"\n\n## 7. nagara: test doubles stay out of the production bundle\n\nLands in nagara's `CLAUDE.md`, \"Code style\", a new bullet, or in `.mahou/implement.md` (the choice is open):\n\n\"- **A test double never reaches the production bundle.** The tests wire a fake in through the vitest configuration, such as a module the config substitutes, never through a setting or a branch the deployed code carries. After a build, `dist/` holds no trace of it.\"\n\n## 8. implement: avoid rm -rf\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"The brief\", the \"Repository rules\" bullet, appended:\n\n\"Avoid `rm -rf` when another way works, such as `rm -r` on a named path or leaving temporary files in `/tmp`: a permission rule can turn it into a dialog that blocks the subagent until the user answers.\"\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"25cbd3d2-d1f3-4c20-95e5-7d4aa946b97f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfwG7zARKm9VN337fWXfW","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9587e4fe-033f-4a85-911b-5a9a4dfe019b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:46:23.012Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"9587e4fe-033f-4a85-911b-5a9a4dfe019b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a494df3b-a977-4017-be9c-129fddc17163","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KW8jqy2iiJmis5DsSuq9Fi","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round4/drafts.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"579f185b-0951-4d50-8c1f-a70c254ea573","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:46:23.093Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round4/drafts.md","content":"# Learn round 4: drafts\n\n## 1. program-design-with-canvas: talk on the canvas, questions inside the part\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/program-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`, two new sections after \"The canvas\", before \"Mockups\".\n\n```markdown\n## Questions\n\nA question goes inside the part it is about, on the right side of the part's area, next to the items it discusses. The part's Claude note goes under the questions.\n\n- **A question is a violet card**: a rectangle with violet border and fill, titled `❓ Q<n> · <title>`, then the body, which gives the situation and ends with the question. Add a diagram, drawn with tldraw shapes, when the question is about where something runs, in what order or across which boundary.\n- **Follow-ups stay inside the base question's card**, one at a time, until the question closes. The card holds, top to bottom: the base question and its diagram, a summary box, one Claude note, and the current follow-up as a violet card of its own.\n- **The summary box**, a solid grey rectangle labelled `Summary · Q<n> so far`, holds what the question has settled and the findings that bear on it. Rewrite it each round; never add a line per answer.\n- **When the question closes**, delete the card, redraw the part with what it settled, and update the record.\n\n## Messages from Claude\n\nEverything you would say in the chat goes on the canvas: how you read an answer, research results, status, and requests to approve a part. Write it as a Claude note: a grey dashed rectangle labelled `Claude`, in the part or the question it is about. Keep one Claude note per place and replace its text each round. When a part settles, delete its note.\n```\n\n## 1b. test-design-with-canvas: questions inside the branch\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/test-design-with-canvas/SKILL.md`. The \"Messages from Claude\" section is replaced, and a \"Questions\" section goes before it.\n\nOld:\n\n```markdown\n## Messages from Claude\n\nWrite what you would say in the chat as one Claude note at the top of the canvas: how to read the drawing, the open questions, and the implementation tasks the trees surfaced. Replace its text each round.\n```\n\nNew:\n\n```markdown\n## Questions\n\nA question goes inside the branch it is about, beside the classification, partition or row it discusses. A question about a root goes beside its card on the map. The branch's Claude note goes under the questions.\n\n- **A question is a card with a violet border and no fill**, titled `❓ Q<n> · <title>`, then the body, which gives the situation and ends with the question. The missing fill keeps it apart from the filled violet classification boxes.\n- **Follow-ups stay inside the base question's card**, one at a time, until the question closes. The card holds, top to bottom: the base question, a summary box, one Claude note, and the current follow-up as a card of its own.\n- **The summary box**, a solid grey rectangle labelled `Summary · Q<n> so far`, holds what the question has settled. Rewrite it each round; never add a line per answer.\n- **When the question closes**, delete the card, redraw the branch with what it settled, and update the record.\n\n## Messages from Claude\n\nEverything you would say in the chat goes on the canvas, as a Claude note: a grey dashed rectangle labelled `Claude`, in the branch, tree or question it is about. One note at the top of the canvas says how to read the drawing and lists the implementation tasks the trees surfaced. Keep one Claude note per place and replace its text each round.\n```\n\n## 2. implement: the full report in the final message\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"The brief\", the \"How to answer\" bullet.\n\nOld: \"**How to answer.** A report in the shape mahou:report gives: the branch, the commits, a summary per change, the row-to-test mapping, the linter and test output tail, and what it could not resolve. A design ambiguity that changes the outcome is a question back through the subagent's question channel, not a guess.\"\n\nNew: \"**How to answer.** A report in the shape mahou:report gives: the branch, the commits, a summary per change, the row-to-test mapping, the linter and test output tail, and what it could not resolve. The report is the whole of the subagent's final message, because collecting a result reads only that message: a shorter message sent after the report replaces it. Every later instruction to the subagent repeats this. A design ambiguity that changes the outcome is a question back through the subagent's question channel, not a guess.\"\n\n## 3. implement: compact a reused subagent between tasks\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"Dispatch and collect\", a new paragraph after \"Release a subagent…\".\n\n\"A subagent kept for further work, such as the review, a fix round or the manual validation, carries every earlier task in its context. Check its context use whenever it finishes a task. When it is near half, have it run `/compact` with a list of what to keep, such as the checkout it works in, the safety rules and where the briefs live, then send the next task. Compact only between tasks: never while it is working on one.\"\n\n## 4. consistency-checker agent, and the implement order\n\nNew file `mahou/agents/consistency-checker.md`:\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: consistency-checker\ndescription: Sweeps one repository after a change lands for leftovers of what the change replaced and for places where the code and the docs, or two parts of the code, disagree. Writes findings to a file and returns the path. Makes no edits.\ntools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash(git:*), Skill(mahou:docs)\nmodel: opus\n---\n\n# Consistency checker\n\nChecks one repository against itself once a change has landed. You edit nothing, and you start no servers or processes.\n\nYou are given the repository's absolute path, a summary of what the change replaced, and the path to write the findings to. Use `git -C <repo-path>` and absolute paths for everything. Never `cd`.\n\n## Read first\n\nLoad mahou:docs. Read the project's `CLAUDE.md`, the docs charter and every note the change touches, then the code: every package, the CI files, the root configuration and the project's local rule files when they describe the code.\n\n## What to look for\n\n1. **Leftovers**: files, dependencies, scripts, configuration keys, exports, test fixtures and comments that belonged to what the change replaced, or that nothing reads or imports any more.\n2. **Docs vs code**: every route, status code, body shape, step, retry count, timeout, limit, binding, variable, secret, key layout, migration, CI condition, local step and port a note or `CLAUDE.md` states, checked against the code.\n3. **Code vs code**: configuration files that must agree (bindings, ids, folders), the secrets an example file names against the ones the code reads, the shapes one service sends against the ones the other parses, shared types against what the code writes.\n4. **Vocabulary**: names, comments and tests that still use the replaced system's words for something that is now called differently.\n\nReport only where two things that should agree do not, and things that no longer have a reason to exist. No style preferences, and no reopening of decisions the notes record. When something looks wrong but has a recorded reason to stay, leave it out and list it under \"Not reported\" with the reason.\n\n## Output\n\nWrite the findings file with four sections, Leftovers, Docs vs code, Code vs code and Vocabulary. Each finding gets the file and line, the two sides that disagree quoted briefly, and the fix you would propose. Return the path and the count per section in your final message.\n```\n\n`mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`: the \"Manual validation\" section moves before \"Design reconciliation\", and \"Design reconciliation\" becomes:\n\nOld: \"The code that lands is what was actually built, and the notes drift from it the moment a child deviates, simplifies, or meets a platform fact. When a repository's implementation and review are done, collect the drift: every flag a subagent raised about a design mismatch, every pointing callout in a touched note whose condition has now landed, and every diagram that renders a shape the change altered. The user settles each one, and the agreed updates run through mahou:write-documentation once, with the whole documentation in view, before the manual validation reports the system as finished.\"\n\nNew: \"The code that lands is what was actually built, and the notes drift from it the moment a child deviates, simplifies, or meets a platform fact. When the manual validation has reported, collect the drift: every flag a subagent raised about a design mismatch, every pointing callout in a touched note whose condition has now landed, and every diagram that renders a shape the change altered. Then dispatch a `mahou:consistency-checker` per repository, with a summary of what the change replaced, for the leftovers and disagreements no flag named. The user settles each item. An implementation subagent applies the agreed code fixes, and the agreed documentation updates run through mahou:write-documentation once, with the whole documentation in view.\"\n\nIn \"Manual validation\", \"The next repository starts when the previous one has reported.\" stays, and nothing else changes.\n\n`mahou/README.md`, \"Agents\", a new line after `documentation-reviewer`:\n\n\"- `consistency-checker`: one repository after a change lands, for leftovers and for code that disagrees with the docs or with itself, dispatched by `implement` during design reconciliation.\"\n\nThe `implement` line in the skills list changes \"then runs `agentic-review` per repository and `validate` one repository at a time.\" to \"then runs `agentic-review` per repository, `validate` one repository at a time, and a consistency check before the docs are reconciled.\"\n\n## 5. validate: synthetic inputs and forced failures\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/validate/SKILL.md`, \"Mutating data to reach a row\".\n\nAfter the paragraph beginning \"Some rows need an error the system does not produce on its own\", add:\n\n\"A temporary code change can force the failure when no input or configuration reaches it: make the smallest change that produces the error, run the row, then restore the file with `git checkout -- <file>` and confirm with `git status` that it is clean before the next row. Run it while nothing else is in flight on the system, because the change reloads the server that runs the code. Record the change and its restore in the report like any other mutation.\"\n\nNew paragraph at the end of the section:\n\n\"When no real input has what a row needs, such as a page with every element the row combines, build a synthetic input: the smallest artifact that has those elements and reads like the real thing, kept in the change's scratch folder and served locally, behind a tunnel when the system under test runs remotely and must reach it. Say in the row which parts of the expected outcome it could not cover.\"\n\n## 7. nagara: test doubles stay out of the production bundle\n\nLands in nagara's `CLAUDE.md`, \"Code style\", a new bullet, or in `.mahou/implement.md` (the choice is open):\n\n\"- **A test double never reaches the production bundle.** The tests wire a fake in through the vitest configuration, such as a module the config substitutes, never through a setting or a branch the deployed code carries. After a build, `dist/` holds no trace of it.\"\n\n## 8. implement: avoid rm -rf\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/implement/SKILL.md`, \"The brief\", the \"Repository rules\" bullet, appended:\n\n\"Avoid `rm -rf` when another way works, such as `rm -r` on a named path or leaving temporary files in `/tmp`: a permission rule can turn it into a dialog that blocks the subagent until the user answers.\"\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9587e4fe-033f-4a85-911b-5a9a4dfe019b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
