 \"Do not report style preferences or reopen decisions the notes record.\"\n  - L105: \"…per repository, with a summary of what the change replaced, for the leftovers and disagreements no flag named.\" → \"…per repository with a summary of what the change replaced. It finds the leftovers and disagreements that no flag named.\"\n  - L113: \"and a consistency check before the docs are reconciled.\" → \"and `consistency-checker` per repository before it reconciles the docs.\"\n  - L121: \"reaches it: make the smallest change\" → \"reaches it. Make the smallest change\"\n  - L121: \"while nothing else is in flight on the system\" → \"while nothing else is running on the system\"\n  - L125: \"build a synthetic input: the smallest artifact … reads like the real thing, kept in the change's scratch folder and served locally, …\" → \"build a synthetic input, the smallest artifact … looks like the real thing. Keep it in the change's scratch folder and serve it locally, …\"\n  - L131: \"`dist/` holds no trace of it.\" → \"`dist/` contains none of the fake's code.\"\n  - L137: \"`/tmp`: a permission rule can turn it into a dialog\" → \"`/tmp`, because a permission rule can turn `rm -rf` into a dialog\"\n  \n  Rejected:\n  - L12, rule 16, \"**A question is a violet card**: …\": this lead-in names the item and plainly states its shape, so it is not a slogan. It also matches the sibling bullet in section 1b, and rewriting it as an instruction would change the bold lead-in structure.\n  - L79, rule 35, \"Checks one repository against itself once a change has landed.\": the subagent receives the agent body as its prompt, but the frontmatter description is for the dispatcher. The body's opening line is therefore not a repeat for the agent that reads it.\n  - L111, rule 33, the README line \"`consistency-checker`: one repository after a change lands, …\": it follows the form of the existing Agents lines in mahou/README.md, such as \"`documentation-reviewer`: one draft against the project's charter and template, dispatched by …\".\n</agent-message>"}
