{"parentUuid":"72b38bf0-7c64-406e-9976-019dbea83ec7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dcb8d19d-de3f-4377-8be6-a364947d38f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GEb22xVHg7wpPQP55ndUyc","type":"tool_result","content":"done\n# ASE-84 report: D1 through drizzle\n\nEvery D1 read and write now goes through drizzle query functions in `common/src/db/`. Test, lint and types pass in `common/`, `api/` and `pipeline/`, and the pipeline build works. You removed the Modal key mid-run, so the live smoke stopped at `start synthesis` and the store step was never run live. ASE-84 is Done in Linear.\n\n## Branch and commits\nBranch `feat/cloudflare-migration` in the main checkout. Nothing pushed. The docs subagent's edits were left unstaged.\n\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `90515d1` | feat(common): read and write D1 through drizzle |\n| `3381616` | refactor(api): call common's drizzle queries |\n| `d9864da` | refactor(pipeline): call common's drizzle queries |\n| `8d2ca24` | ci: fail common checks when the schema changed without its migration |\n\nThe api and pipeline commits are separate, so the Workers don't compile at `90515d1` alone.\n\n## Changes\n- **`common/`:**\n  - Added drizzle-orm 0.45.4 and the dev dependency drizzle-kit 0.31.11, both pinned.\n  - Added `drizzle.config.ts` and a `db:generate` script.\n  - `src/db/schema.ts` defines the three tables with snake_case keys. The enum columns are typed from `ITEM_STATUS`, `COST_TYPE` and `COST_UNIT`, each with an explicit `check()`. The JSON columns use `text({mode:\"json\"}).$type<…>()`, and `cached` is `integer({mode:\"boolean\"})`.\n  - `database.ts` holds the client.\n  - The query functions are `getItem`, `createItem` (returns `{ id, query }`), `updateItem`, `writeStatus`, `claimRetry`, `claimRequeue`, `getLatestRecipeVersion`, `createRecipeVersion` and `createCostEntry`, one module each. Writes return the query unawaited.\n  - `ItemRow`, `RecipeVersionRow` and `CostEntryRow` are now derived with `$inferSelect`.\n  - Deleted `item-store/` and `0001_initial.sql`.\n  - `biome.json` now ignores `migrations/meta`, which holds drizzle-kit's generated JSON.\n- **`api/`:**\n  - Each route builds `database(env.DB)` once.\n  - `requeueIfStale(env, db, row)` calls `claimRequeue`.\n  - The retry route reads the item, claims with `claimRetry(db, row, RETRY_MAX)`, then reads again. The second read is how the 409 names the status the winner wrote and how the 202 carries the new count, as before.\n  - Deleted `create.ts` and `retry-claim.ts`.\n- **`pipeline/`:**\n  - The steps use `updateItem`, `writeStatus` and the create functions. The batches in the fetch, describe and store steps are kept as `db.batch`.\n  - Deleted `workflow/ledger.ts`, plus `currentRecipe` and `saveVersion` from `recipes/store.ts`; `domainFromUrl` stays.\n  - drizzle-orm is a dev dependency, for the test helpers only.\n- **Test helpers:** all three trees seed and read through drizzle.\n  - The `status_log` table and trigger use `db.run(sql…)`.\n  - The status log is read through a test-only `sqliteTable`.\n- **CI:** a new `common-checks` leg runs `db:generate` and fails when `git status --porcelain -- migrations` is not empty. actionlint 1.7.12 passes it. I checked it would catch a real case: adding a column without regenerating made generate write a new migration.\n\n## Checks I ran\n- **Generated SQL against the old migration:** I loaded both into sqlite3 and compared the columns, foreign keys and indexes, then inserted bad values against each constraint.\n  - Every CHECK, the unique pair and every foreign key reject the same inserts in both.\n  - The CHECKs are now named (`items_status_check` and so on), so the error message gives the name instead of the expression.\n  - `UNIQUE(domain, version)` is now the named unique index `recipe_versions_domain_version_unique`.\n  - The primary keys are now `NOT NULL` explicitly, which is stricter than SQLite's default and harmless.\n  - `cached` defaults to `false`, which SQLite stores as 0.\n  - The tables are created in a different order; SQLite accepts a foreign key to a table created later.\n- **Migrations in the tests:** `readD1Migrations` handles the `--> statement-breakpoint` comments under both Workers' vitest configs.\n- **`.returning()` on D1:** works for both claims.\n- **Concurrent recipe saves:** the test where two saves race passed 5 runs out of 5.\n\n## Row-to-test mapping (new `common/` tests)\n| Case | Test |\n|---|---|\n| claimRetry: claimed | `claimRetry › claims a failed item under the cap…` |\n| claimRetry: lost to a concurrent claim | `› loses to a concurrent claim made from the same read` |\n| claimRetry: at the cap | `› refuses an item at the cap` |\n| claimRetry: not failed | `› refuses an item that is not failed` |\n| claimRequeue: claimed | `claimRequeue › claims a queued item queued before the cutoff…` |\n| claimRequeue: not stale | `› refuses an item queued after the cutoff` |\n| claimRequeue: already claimed | `› refuses a second claim once the first moved queued_at` |\n| createRecipeVersion: first version | `createRecipeVersion › saves a domain's first script as version 1` |\n| createRecipeVersion: next version | `› saves the next script at the next version, counted per domain` |\n| createRecipeVersion: concurrent save | `› fails one of two concurrent saves on the unique domain and version` |\n| updateItem sets `updated_at` | `updateItem › writes the given columns, sets updated_at…` |\n\nThe ported tests are `getItem` (3, from `readItem`) and `writeStatus` (3).\n\n## Output tails\n- **common:** Tests 28 passed (28) · biome: no fixes applied · tsc exit 0\n- **api:** Tests 56 passed (56) · biome: no fixes applied · tsc exit 0\n- **pipeline:** Tests 136 passed, 1 skipped (137) · biome: no fixes applied · tsc exit 0 · `vite build` exit 0, with only the existing \"use agent\" directive warnings\n\n## Test edits beyond seeding helpers\n- **`item-enrichment.test.ts`:** expects `cached: true` instead of `1`. The program design makes `cached` read back as a boolean, so this assertion had to change.\n- **`api/test/poll.test.ts`:** the seed `current_step: \"synthesize\"` is not a real step, and the typed helper rejects it. It is now `\"start synthesis\"`, which doesn't change what the test checks.\n- **Seed values:** the poll tests seed `units` as arrays instead of `JSON.stringify(...)`.\n- **enqueue's row count:** now read with `$count`.\n\n## Design drift\n- **`common/src/db/mint-id.ts`:** a small module the three create functions share to mint ids. It isn't in the program design's module list.\n- **Order of the two reads in the retry route:** the design reads, claims and then reads again only on a lost claim. I also read again after a won claim, because today's 202 returns the item as the claim left it (queued, count raised). Behaviour is unchanged.\n- **Schema output:** the CHECK names and the unique pair now being a named index, as described under \"Checks I ran\".\n- No notes under `docs/` disagree that I know of; the docs subagent was editing them at the same time.\n\n## Local reset and smoke\n- **Reset:** the old state was moved to `/tmp/nagara-wrangler-state-pre-drizzle-20261011194109`. `pnpm migrate:local` applied `0000_initial.sql` with wrangler: 6 commands, ✅.\n- **What ran live:** I enqueued `https://eli.thegreenplace.net/2026/watgo-a-webassembly-toolkit-for-go` as `itm_a75022c0`. With the API on 8788, the tunnel and `modal serve` running, these writes all landed correctly:\n  - the enqueue's insert;\n  - the fetch step's batch of the item update and the Firecrawl cost entry;\n  - the author agent's recipe saved as version 1;\n  - the units JSON;\n  - the describe step's batch, with 3 describer entries;\n  - the status writes.\n- **Where it stopped:** the item failed at `start synthesis` with \"modal start answered 401\", because you had removed the Modal key.\n- **Retry route:** a live retry claimed (`retry_count` 1), restarted from `start synthesis`, and failed again the same way.\n- **Not covered:** the store step was never run live, per your instruction.\n- **Cleanup:**\n  - Every process I started was stopped by its recorded process group: proxy, tunnel, both dev servers and `modal serve`.\n  - `modal serve` left its ephemeral app running, so I stopped it by id (`ap-qLmnCJjJ8l5EImclas8Avg`). The deployed `nagara-tts` was not touched.\n  - `R2_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT` is back to its `https://<tunnel-hostname>/s3` placeholder.\n  - The failed smoke item, its recipe version and its cost rows are still in the local D1.\n\n## Decisions taken without the user\nNone. No question was sent to the Plannotator inbox.\n\n## Linear\nASE-84 went from Todo to In Progress to Done. No tasks were created or canceled.\n\n## Unresolved\nNone.\n8d2ca24 ci: fail common checks when the schema changed without its migration\nd9864da refactor(pipeline): call common's drizzle queries\n3381616 refactor(api): call common's drizzle queries\n90515d1 feat(common): read and write D1 through drizzle\nd2f165d docs: describe the instance check on re-queue and retry, and the spoken dot\n93f56de fix(pipeline): read a dot before a letter as the word dot\n0690682 fix(api): replace only an instance that never ran its first step\n471d885 fix(pipeline): keep the space before a word that starts with a dot\n M .mahou/wiki/INDEX.md\n M .mahou/wiki/cloudflare/INDEX.md\n M CLAUDE.md\n M docs/technical-design/README.md\n M docs/technical-design/common-package.md\n M docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md\n M docs/technical-design/invariants.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-contract.md\n M docs/technical-design/item-lifecycle.md\n M docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"abb2c590-6bad-4baf-8890-a1530f79c5cc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:49:32.491Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\n# ASE-84 report: D1 through drizzle\n\nEvery D1 read and write now goes through drizzle query functions in `common/src/db/`. T