{"parentUuid":"848b3071-f58d-4fd1-8244-27ab0430efe7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwGfdBVwS4oiDB67nBKD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written every approved mahou change in claude-plugins. Nothing is committed.\n\n- **program-design-with-canvas:** two new sections. \"Questions\" puts a violet card inside the part, next to the items it discusses, with follow-ups, a summary box, and the card deleted when the question closes. \"Messages from Claude\" says to talk on the canvas, in the part or question being discussed.\n- **test-design-with-canvas:** the single note at the top of the canvas is replaced. Questions now sit inside the branch, as violet-bordered cards with no fill, so they don't look like the classification boxes. Claude notes go in the place they're about, and one note at the top keeps the reading guide and the implementation tasks.\n- **implement:**\n  - The full report must be the subagent's final message.\n  - Compact a reused subagent between tasks once its context nears half.\n  - Manual validation now runs before design reconciliation, and reconciliation dispatches a `consistency-checker` per repository.\n  - The repository rules say to avoid `rm -rf` when another way works.\n- **validate:** a temporary code change can force a failure, restored with `git checkout` and checked with `git status`. When no real input has what a row needs, the subagent builds a synthetic one.\n- **New agent:** `mahou/agents/consistency-checker.md`. It's listed in `mahou/README.md`, and the README's implement line mentions it.\n- **claude-plugins `CLAUDE.md`:** I added the new agent and the new implement order. This wasn't in the drafts. It also notes that `consistency-checker` runs on opus, while every other agent there runs on sonnet.\n\nItem 7 lands in nagara's `CLAUDE.md`, not in mahou, so I haven't written it yet. Should I add that bullet to nagara's `CLAUDE.md`? That file already holds the uncommitted Drizzle doc edits.\n\nThe agentic review of ASE-84 is still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":872,"cache_read_input_tokens":465479,"output_tokens":637,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":872,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":465479,"cache_creation_input_tokens":872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":872},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9c8999ac-ec52-48d0-bc83-0bc3772775a5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwGfciDrbUxRY4XekW9A","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3107c70f-a496-401b-a20c-a2227eed2205","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:53:04.217Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
