{"parentUuid":"590f54d8-8caa-4357-8ece-ba2bfa0f47a6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b4539a27-3dad-4a2a-9c7a-fa360e1c69df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxbhbrJby43xGBV7WnS2hT","type":"tool_result","content":"8:    gen[\"pnpm db:generate<br/>in common/\"]\n13:    ci[\"CI common checks:<br/>generate, then fail<br/>on a new or changed file\"]\n14:    remote[\"CI migrate job:<br/>wrangler d1 migrations<br/>apply --remote\"]\n18:    review --> ci\n19:    ci -->|\"schema and SQL agree\"| remote\n20:    ci -.->|\"a schema edit with<br/>no migration fails\"| edit\n23:The schema is `common/src/db/schema.ts` in [common/](common-package.md), and the migrations are SQL files drizzle-kit generates from it into `common/migrations/`, beside a `meta/` folder of schema snapshots that the next generation diffs against. The developer reviews and commits each generated file like code, and CI fails a change whose schema edit has no migration beside it. The Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job applies them to D1 with wrangler before the pipeline Worker and the API Worker deploy, in the same workflow, so neither Worker ever runs against a schema older than its code (see [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md)). Deploys are not made twice in quick succession, so two migration runs never overlap. Locally, the developer applies the same migrations with wrangler to the D1 database in the shared state folder (see [local-development](local-development.md)), and the Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying them too.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bf36fd9e-08cd-4af0-a9f6-d7b25263725c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:01:52.900Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"8:    gen[\"pnpm db:generate<br/>in common/\"]\n13:    ci[\"CI common checks:<br/>generate, then fail<br/>on a new or changed file\"]\n14:    remote[\"CI migrate job:<br/>wrangler d1 migrations<br/>apply --remote\"]\n18:    review --> ci\n19:    ci -->|\"schema and SQL agree\"| remote\n20:    ci -.->|\"a schema edit with<br/>no migration fails\"| edit\n23:The schema is `common/src/db/schema.ts` in [common/](common-package.md), and the migrations are SQL files drizzle-kit generates from it into `common/migrations/`, beside a `meta/` folder of schema snapshots that the next generation diffs against. The developer reviews and commits each generated file like code, and CI fails a change whose schema edit has no migration beside it. The Cloudflare CI workflow's migrate job applies them to D1 with wrangler before the pipeline Worker and the API Worker deploy, in the same workflow, so neither Worker ever runs against a schema older than its code (see [deployment-and-ci](deployment-and-ci.md)). Deploys are not made twice in quick succession, so two migration runs never overlap. Locally, the developer applies the same migrations with wrangler to the D1 database in the shared state folder (see [local-development](local-development.md)), and the Workers' tests build their D1 schema by applying them too.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"425dd3a2-0be4-4303-8561-69ea1e171fe1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":11,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"590f54d8-8caa-4357-8ece-ba2bfa0f47a6",