d write rolls back the first, if D1 under the vitest plugin lets you provoke one, otherwise say so), and keep the API and pipeline suites' assertions unchanged. Run test, lint, types in `common/`, `api/`, `pipeline/`, the pipeline build and `pnpm db:check`. Commit as `refactor(common): …` / `refactor(api): …` / `refactor(pipeline): …`.\n\n## Docs\n\nThen run `/mahou:write-documentation` once for this change, with the user's approval to write directly after the unslop and documentation-reviewer passes: the CLAUDE.md code-style database bullet (per-table functions plus functions for atomic writes across tables, all executing and returning rows; the Workers only pass the client), `common-package.md`'s \"Reading and writing D1\" section and its functions table (no unexecuted queries; the atomic functions and which step calls each), and anywhere else that says writes return unawaited queries or that the steps call `db.batch` (`persistence-and-storage.md`, `item-lifecycle.md`, the local wiki entry `.mahou/wiki/cloudflare/drizzle-on-d1.md`). Commit as `docs: …` (and `chore: …` for `.mahou/`).\nEOF\nH=/home/agus/.claude/plugins/cache/herdr-subagents/herdr-subagents/0.10.0/bin/herdr-helper; $H read w30:p33 --lines 3 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['screen'])\" | grep -o \"([0-9]*%)\"; $H prompt w30:p33 --body \"<supervisor-agent>Next task: read and follow /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/briefs/ase84-orm-followups.md. Your final message holds the full report.</supervisor-agent>\"","description":"Write the ORM follow-up brief and send it to the ASE-84 subagent"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cf96228e-2dd3-4986-a542-423d5b612fb9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwHXf9xkiHr8CWhjPZEE","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3701b68c-5272-4ec2-a2d1-8f7c96d52ca7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:04:36.573Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14ba