 git status --short | head","description":"Collect the ORM follow-ups result"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6eae0fce-b086-433e-9611-24c7c78abcf4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwJGA2CP2qeZfShx7zTd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f3543604-3b9b-48d6-aae3-706a9a692530","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:13:55.962Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"f3543604-3b9b-48d6-aae3-706a9a692530","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1ddc0482-37ac-4748-9ad5-2aafe67ae460","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ZhzC59VTvYMzFht25poFX","type":"tool_result","content":"done\n# ASE-84 ORM follow-ups\n\nEvery write in `common/src/db/` now runs and returns its row. The Workers only build the drizzle client and pass it to those functions; no route or step calls `db.batch`. Test, lint and types pass in `common/`, `api/` and `pipeline/`. The pipeline build works, and `pnpm db:check` leaves the migration unchanged. Everything is committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration`, not pushed, and the tree is clean.\n\n## Commits\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `827574f` | refactor(common): run every write and return its row |\n| `bc647ec` | refactor(api): answer with the rows the writes return |\n| `28c5711` | refactor(pipeline): record the batched writes through common's operations |\n| `c7a1aee` | docs: describe the D1 functions as running and returning rows, and the atomic writes |\n| `da7b32e` | chore: record returning, batch rollback and runtime defaults in the drizzle wiki entry |\n\n## Code\n- **Creates and updates return the row.** They all run through `.returning()`:\n  - `createItem` returns the item.\n  - `createRecipeVersion` and `createCostEntry` return their rows.\n  - `updateItem` returns the row, or null for an unknown id. `writeStatus` is built on it, so it returns the same.\n- **Atomic writes** live in `common/src/db/operations/`, one function per module. Each takes `(db, itemId, changes, cost or costs)`, runs one `db.batch` and returns the item row.\n\n  | Function | Writes | Called by |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | `recordFetch` | the instance id and domain, plus the Firecrawl cost row | fetch step |\n  | `recordDescriptions` | the units and degradations, plus one describer cost row per description | describe step |\n  | `recordAudio` | `ready`, `current_step` and error cleared, timed units, duration and format, plus the TTS cost row | store step |\n\n  A new `ItemCost` type (a cost entry without `item_id`) sits next to `NewCostEntry`.\n- **Claims** return the claimed row, or null when the call lost.\n  - The retry route reads the item, then claims. A win answers 202 with the claimed row. A loss reads once more to build the 409 message.\n  - The `?? read` fallback is gone.\n  - The re-queue check tests the claim against null.\n- **Schema defaults:**\n  - Each id gets `$defaultFn` with `mintId` and its prefix (`itm_`, `rcp_`, `cst_`), so `mint-id.ts` stays.\n  - `created_at` and `queued_at` get `$defaultFn`, and `updated_at` gets `$defaultFn` and `$onUpdate`.\n  - The claims still set `queued_at` themselves, because moving it is what a claim does.\n  - Runtime defaults emit no SQL, so the migration is unchanged.\n- **Enqueue** answers with the created item, without reading it back. When the Workflow create fails, it answers with the row `writeStatus` returns.\n- **CHECK helpers** stay in `schema.ts`, with a one-line comment that only the schema's CHECKs use them. The three seeding helpers stay separate.\n\n## Behaviour notes\n- **Fallbacks:** when the status write after a failed Workflow create or restart returns null, enqueue answers with the created item and retry with the claimed row (`failed ?? item`, `failed ?? claimed`). Null would mean the row was deleted mid-request.\n- **Row deleted after a lost retry claim:** the route now answers 404 where it used to fall back to the row it read first.\n- **Timestamps can differ by a millisecond.** A new item's `created_at`, `updated_at` and `queued_at` come from separate default calls, and a claim's `queued_at` and `updated_at` can differ the same way. Before, each write used one shared time.\n- **`createCostEntry` has no caller in either Worker.** Only the tests use it, because the steps write cost rows through the operations. The brief asked for it to return its row, so I kept it.\n\n## Tests\n- **Existing `common/` tests:** adjusted to the new return shapes.\n  - The claims return the row or null.\n  - `createRecipeVersion` and `updateItem` return rows, and `updateItem` answers null for an unknown id.\n  - In the two claim tests that asserted `updated_at` equals `queued_at`, both are now checked to be later than the seeded time, because the two now come from separate clock reads.\n- **New tests:**\n  - `createItem`: the minted id, the timestamps and the queued status.\n  - `createCostEntry`: the minted id and `cached` defaulting to false.\n  - One test file per operation: both writes land, and a failing second write rolls back the first.\n  - `recordDescriptions` also gets an empty-costs case.\n- **Rollback can be provoked under the vitest plugin.** A cost entry with an invalid `type` fails its CHECK, and the earlier update in the same batch does not land.\n- **API and pipeline assertions are unchanged.** Two pipeline test seeds take `.id` from `createRecipeVersion`'s row.\n\n| Tree | Test | Lint | Types |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `common/` | 38 passed (38) | no fixes applied | exit 0 |\n| `api/` | 56 passed (56) | no fixes applied | exit 0 |\n| `pipeline/` | 136 passed, 1 skipped (137) | no fixes applied | exit 0 |\n\nThe pipeline build exits 0. `pnpm db:check` prints \"No schema changes, nothing to migrate\" and exits 0.\n\n## Docs (`/mahou:write-documentation`)\nThe draft went through two unslop rounds and the documentation reviewer before landing; it is in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/docs-orm-followups/`.\n- **Unslop round 1:** 12 findings, 9 applied. I skipped 3 because they flag the house form the notes already use: the colon in the claims' table cells and \"the finished state\".\n- **Unslop round 2:** nothing had slipped back.\n- **Documentation reviewer:** 3 form findings, all applied.\n  - Two callouts: \"Why ids and timestamps are schema defaults\" and \"Why a claim returns the row\".\n  - Two dashed diagram edges from the operations to the tables they write.\n\nWhat changed in each file:\n- **`CLAUDE.md`, code-style database bullet:** each table has a folder of functions, and cross-table atomic writes live in `common/src/db/operations/`, named for what they record. Every function runs its query and returns the row; the Workers only pass the client.\n- **`common-package.md`, \"Reading and writing D1\":**\n  - The first paragraph names the operations folder.\n  - The diagram has an `operations` subgraph.\n  - The functions table gives the new return shapes and adds the three operations, with the step that calls each.\n  - There is a paragraph on the schema defaults, and the \"unawaited query\" paragraph is replaced with the run-and-return rule and the batch atomicity.\n- **`item-lifecycle.md`:** one sentence: the store step writes `ready` through `recordAudio`.\n- **`.mahou/wiki/cloudflare/drizzle-on-d1.md`:** the \"returns the query unawaited\" bullet is replaced with three facts:\n  - how `.returning()` behaves on D1 and inside a batch;\n  - that the batch rollback is provoked in the `common/` tests;\n  - that `$defaultFn` and `$onUpdate` emit no SQL.\n- **`persistence-and-storage.md`:** left untouched. It mentions neither unawaited queries nor `db.batch`, and its description of the writes is still correct.\n\nThe two callouts were written on your behalf:\n> **Why ids and timestamps are schema defaults:** A function cannot forget `updated_at` or mint an id under the wrong prefix when no function sets them. drizzle computes these defaults in the Worker when drizzle builds the statement, so the migrations contain none of them.\n\n> **Why a claim returns the row:** The route that made the claim learns the outcome and the row it wrote from one statement, so a won retry answers with the claimed row without reading it again.\n\n## Linear\nI moved, created and canceled no tasks. ASE-84 stays Done, and the brief named no task for this work.\n\n## Decisions taken without the user\nNone.\nda7b32e chore: record returning, batch rollback and runtime defaults in the drizzle wiki entry\nc7a1aee docs: describe the D1 functions as running and returning rows, and the atomic writes\n28c5711 refactor(pipeline): record the batched writes through common's operations\nbc647ec refactor(api): answer with the rows the writes return","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c1981996-c30a-4b85-91b3-7590469cff50","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:13:56.515Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"done\n# ASE-84 ORM follow-ups\n\nEvery write in `common/src/db/` now runs and returns its row. The Workers only build the drizzle client and pass it to those functions; no route or step calls `db.batch`. Test, lint and types pass in `common/`, `api/` and `pipeline/`. The pipeline build works, and `pnpm db:check` leaves the migration unchanged. Everything is committed on `feat/cloudflare-migration`, not pushed, and the tree is clean.\n\n## Commits\n| Hash | Subject |\n|---|---|\n| `827574f` | refactor(common): run every write and return its row |\n| `bc647ec` | refactor(api): answer with the rows the writes return |\n| `28c5711` | refactor(pipeline): record the batched writes through common's operations |\n| `c7a1aee` | docs: describe the D1 functions as running and returning rows, and the atomic writes |\n| `da7b32e` | chore: record returning, batch rollback and runtime defaults in the drizzle wiki entry |\n\n## Code\n- **Creates and updates return the row.** They all run through `.returning()`:\n  - `createItem` returns the item.\n  - `createRecipeVersion` and `createCostEntry` return their rows.\n  - `updateItem` returns the row, or null for an unknown id. `writeStatus` is built on it, so it returns the same.\n- **Atomic writes** live in `common/src/db/operations/`, one function per module. Each takes `(db, itemId, changes, cost or costs)`, runs one `db.batch` and returns the item row.\n\n  | Function | Writes | Called by |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | `recordFetch` | the instance id and domain, plus the Firecrawl cost row | fetch step |\n  | `recordDescriptions` | the units and degradations, plus one describer cost row per description | describe step |\n  | `recordAudio` | `ready`, `current_step` and error cleared, timed units, duration and format, plus the TTS cost row | store step |\n\n  A new `ItemCost` type (a cost entry without `item_id`) sits next to `NewCostEntry`.\n- **Claims** return the claimed row, or null when the call lost.\n  - The retry route reads the item, then claims. A win answers 202 with the claimed row. A loss reads once more to build the 409 message.\n  - The `?? read` fallback is gone.\n  - The re-queue check tests the claim against null.\n- **Schema defaults:**\n  - Each id gets `$defaultFn` with `mintId` and its prefix (`itm_`, `rcp_`, `cst_`), so `mint-id.ts` stays.\n  - `created_at` and `queued_at` get `$defaultFn`, and `updated_at` gets `$defaultFn` and `$onUpdate`.\n  - The claims still set `queued_at` themselves, because moving it is what a claim does.\n  - Runtime defaults emit no SQL, so the migration is unchanged.\n- **Enqueue** answers with the created item, without reading it back. When the Workflow create fails, it answers with the row `writeStatus` returns.\n- **CHECK helpers** stay in `schema.ts`, with a one-line comment that only the schema's CHECKs use them. The three seeding helpers stay separate.\n\n## Behaviour notes\n- **Fallbacks:** when the status write after a failed Workflow create or restart returns null, enqueue answers with the created item and retry with the claimed row (`failed ?? item`, `failed ?? claimed`). Null would mean the row was deleted mid-request.\n- **Row deleted after a lost retry claim:** the route now answers 404 where it used to fall back to the row it read first.\n- **Timestamps can differ by a millisecond.** A new item's `created_at`, `updated_at` and `queued_at` come from separate default calls, and a claim's `queued_at` and `updated_at` can differ the same way. Before, each write used one shared time.\n- **`createCostEntry` has no caller in either Worker.** Only the tests use it, because the steps write cost rows through the operations. The brief asked for it to return its row, so I kept it.\n\n## Tests\n- **Existing `common/` tests:** adjusted to the new return shapes.\n  - The claims return the row or null.\n  - `createRecipeVersion` and `updateItem` return rows, and `updateItem` answers null for an unknown id.\n  - In the two claim tests that asserted `updated_at` equals `queued_at`, both are now checked to be later than the seeded time, because the two now come from separate clock reads.\n- **New tests:**\n  - `createItem`: the minted id, the timestamps and the queued status.\n  - `createCostEntry`: the minted id and `cached` defaulting to false.\n  - One test file per operation: both writes land, and a failing second write rolls back the first.\n  - `recordDescriptions` also gets an empty-costs case.\n- **Rollback can be provoked under the vitest plugin.** A cost entry with an invalid `type` fails its CHECK, and the earlier update in the same batch does not land.\n- **API and pipeline assertions are unchanged.** Two pipeline test seeds take `.id` from `createRecipeVersion`'s row.\n\n| Tree | Test | Lint | Types |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `common/` | 38 passed (38) | no fixes applied | exit 0 |\n| `api/` | 56 passed (56) | no fixes applied | exit 0 |\n| `pipeline/` | 136 passed, 1 skipped (137) | no fixes applied | exit 0 |\n\nThe pipeline build exits 0. `pnpm db:check` prints \"No schema changes, nothing to migrate\" and exits 0.\n\n## Docs (`/mahou:write-documentation`)\nThe draft went through two unslop rounds and the documentation reviewer before landing; it is in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/reports/docs-orm-followups/`.\n- **Unslop round 1:** 12 findings, 9 applied. I skipped 3 because they flag the house form the notes already use: the colon in the claims' table cells and \"the finished state\".\n- **Unslop round 2:** nothing had slipped back.\n- **Documentation reviewer:** 3 form findings, all applied.\n  - Two callouts: \"Why ids and timestamps are schema defaults\" and \"Why a claim returns the row\".\n  - Two dashed diagram edges from the operations to the tables they write.\n\nWhat changed in each file:\n- **`CLAUDE.md`, code-style database bullet:** each table has a folder of functions, and cross-table atomic writes live in `common/src/db/operations/`, named for what they record. Every function runs its query and returns the row; the Workers only pass the client.\n- **`common-package.md`, \"Reading and writing D1\":**\n  - The first paragraph names the operations folder.\n  - The diagram has an `operations` subgraph.\n  - The functions table gives the new return shapes and adds the three operations, with the step that calls each.\n  - There is a paragraph on the schema defaults, and the \"unawaited query\" paragraph is replaced with the run-and-return rule and the batch atomicity.\n- **`item-lifecycle.md`:** one sentence: the store step writes `ready` through `recordAudio`.\n- **`.mahou/wiki/cloudflare/drizzle-on-d1.md`:** the \"returns the query unawaited\" bullet is replaced with three facts:\n  - how `.returning()` behaves on D1 and inside a batch;\n  - that the batch rollback is provoked in the `common/` tests;\n  - that `$defaultFn` and `$onUpdate` emit no SQL.\n- **`persistence-and-storage.md`:** left untouched. It mentions neither unawaited queries nor `db.batch`, and its description of the writes is still correct.\n\nThe two callouts were written on your behalf:\n> **Why ids and timestamps are schema defaults:** A function cannot forget `updated_at` or mint an id under the wrong prefix when no function sets them. drizzle computes these defaults in the Worker when drizzle builds the statement, so the migrations contain none of them.\n\n> **Why a claim returns the row:** The route that made the claim learns the outcome and the row it wrote from one statement, so a won retry answers with the claimed row without reading it again.\n\n## Linear\nI moved, created and canceled no tasks. ASE-84 stays Done, and the brief named no task for this work.\n\n## Decisions taken without the user\nNone.\nda7b32e chore: record returning, batch rollback and runtime defaults in the drizzle wiki entry\nc7a1aee docs: describe the D1 functions as running and returning rows, and the atomic writes\n28c5711 refactor(pipeline): record the batched writes through common's operations\nbc647ec refactor(api): answer with the rows the writes return","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6eae0fce-b086-433e-9611-24c7c78abcf4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f3543604-3b9b-48d6-aae3-706a9a692530","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
