{"parentUuid":"67ff7665-a4e1-4253-b9c8-39a5776bbb45","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwbygqEAf28pMuWwJLMw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm writing the deployment checklist into ASE-83 now. The account has no D1 databases and no R2 buckets yet, and wrangler is logged in."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":80445,"output_tokens":1972,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":139},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1972,"cache_read_input_tokens":80445,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ef0a9943-96d8-444b-bef3-9815188d7cff","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwbygTfcJSfnAVXPohhA","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0785084e-77ac-43fc-a028-fa8e772d4996","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:06:13.650Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"0785084e-77ac-43fc-a028-fa8e772d4996","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwbygqEAf28pMuWwJLMw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018rZZ8Ke8CUJzpLNq455exB","name":"mcp__linear-server__save_issue","input":{"id":"ASE-83","state":"In Progress","description":"Bring the migrated stack up in production and remove what it replaces. The first deploy is manual. The API runs on its workers.dev URL until the end-to-end test passes. Only then does `nagara.asermax.com` move to it and Railway get deleted.\n\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md`, `docs/technical-design/authentication.md`, `docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md`.\n\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`.\n\n## 1. Credentials (user)\n\nEach one goes into `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/prod-secrets.env`, keyed by name, and never into the chat.\n\n- [ ] `API_KEY`: the clients' key. Reuse Railway's or create a new one.\n- [ ] `R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read only, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the API.\n- [ ] `R2_PUT_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_PUT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read & Write, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the pipeline.\n- [ ] `MODAL_PROXY_KEY` / `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET`: a new Modal proxy auth token. The local-validation token was revoked.\n- [ ] `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` (AI Gateway token): copied from `pipeline/.dev.vars` unless production should use separate keys.\n\n## 2. Cloudflare resources\n\n- [ ] `wrangler d1 create nagara`, then put its id in place of the all-zero placeholder in `common/`, `api/` and `pipeline/` `wrangler.jsonc`, and commit.\n- [ ] `wrangler r2 bucket create nagara`.\n- [ ] Create the two R2 tokens from step 1, which needs the bucket to exist.\n\n## 3. Deploy\n\n- [ ] tts: `uv run modal deploy app.py` in `tts/`. This replaces the `nagara-tts` app that Railway calls, so Railway stops synthesizing from this point.\n- [ ] Check that `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web.modal.run/{start,result}` answers 401 without proxy auth. Fix `MODAL_START_URL`/`MODAL_RESULT_URL` if the URL differs.\n- [ ] Migrations: `wrangler d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` from `common/`.\n- [ ] Pipeline: `pnpm run deploy` in `pipeline/`, then `wrangler secret put` for its 7 secrets. This replaces the old extraction-service `nagara` Worker. The v2 tag deletes JobIndex.\n- [ ] API: `pnpm run deploy` in `api/` with the custom-domain route removed locally and `workers_dev: true`. The change stays uncommitted. Then `wrangler secret put` for its 3 secrets.\n\n## 4. End-to-end test against workers.dev\n\nUse small articles, and listen to every audio.\n\n- [ ] `/health` answers 200. D25: a poll without the key gets 401.\n- [ ] D1: enqueue with a voice, and the item goes queued → generating → ready.\n- [ ] C7: the first article of a new domain authors version 1 of its recipe.\n- [ ] B1 / D20: the audio sits in R2, and the 307 URL plays and seeks in a browser.\n- [ ] D21: the audio route of a generating item answers 404.\n- [ ] D13: force a describe failure with a temporarily wrong `GEMINI_API_KEY`, restore the key, retry, and the item reaches ready.\n- [ ] D16: a fourth retry answers 409.\n- [ ] C1, C5, C9 and C11 where a real page reaches them.\n\n## 5. Cutover (only after step 4 passes)\n\n- [ ] Restore the custom-domain route, deploy the API, and point `nagara.asermax.com` at the API Worker.\n- [ ] Remove the Cloudflare Access application and its service token from the pipeline.\n- [ ] Delete the Railway API service, Postgres and bucket. Nothing is copied over.\n- [ ] Add the GitHub secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, then merge, so CI deploys.\n\n## 6. Cleanup\n\n- [ ] Revoke the R2 tokens from the spikes.\n- [ ] Delete the stopped Modal apps `nagara-tts-spike` and `nagara-spike-upload`.\n- [ ] Delete `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env` and `prod-secrets.env`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":80445,"output_tokens":1972,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":139},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1972,"cache_read_input_tokens":80445,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018rZZ8Ke8CUJzpLNq455exB":{"id":"ASE-83","state":"In Progress","description":"Bring the migrated stack up in production and remove what it replaces. The first deploy is manual. The API runs on its workers.dev URL until the end-to-end test passes. Only then does `nagara.asermax.com` move to it and Railway get deleted.\n\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md`, `docs/technical-design/authentication.md`, `docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md`.\n\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`.\n\n## 1. Credentials (user)\n\nEach one goes into `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/prod-secrets.env`, keyed by name, and never into the chat.\n\n- [ ] `API_KEY`: the clients' key. Reuse Railway's or create a new one.\n- [ ] `R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read only, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the API.\n- [ ] `R2_PUT_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_PUT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read & Write, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the pipeline.\n- [ ] `MODAL_PROXY_KEY` / `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET`: a new Modal proxy auth token. The local-validation token was revoked.\n- [ ] `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` (AI Gateway token): copied from `pipeline/.dev.vars` unless production should use separate keys.\n\n## 2. Cloudflare resources\n\n- [ ] `wrangler d1 create nagara`, then put its id in place of the all-zero placeholder in `common/`, `api/` and `pipeline/` `wrangler.jsonc`, and commit.\n- [ ] `wrangler r2 bucket create nagara`.\n- [ ] Create the two R2 tokens from step 1, which needs the bucket to exist.\n\n## 3. Deploy\n\n- [ ] tts: `uv run modal deploy app.py` in `tts/`. This replaces the `nagara-tts` app that Railway calls, so Railway stops synthesizing from this point.\n- [ ] Check that `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web.modal.run/{start,result}` answers 401 without proxy auth. Fix `MODAL_START_URL`/`MODAL_RESULT_URL` if the URL differs.\n- [ ] Migrations: `wrangler d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` from `common/`.\n- [ ] Pipeline: `pnpm run deploy` in `pipeline/`, then `wrangler secret put` for its 7 secrets. This replaces the old extraction-service `nagara` Worker. The v2 tag deletes JobIndex.\n- [ ] API: `pnpm run deploy` in `api/` with the custom-domain route removed locally and `workers_dev: true`. The change stays uncommitted. Then `wrangler secret put` for its 3 secrets.\n\n## 4. End-to-end test against workers.dev\n\nUse small articles, and listen to every audio.\n\n- [ ] `/health` answers 200. D25: a poll without the key gets 401.\n- [ ] D1: enqueue with a voice, and the item goes queued → generating → ready.\n- [ ] C7: the first article of a new domain authors version 1 of its recipe.\n- [ ] B1 / D20: the audio sits in R2, and the 307 URL plays and seeks in a browser.\n- [ ] D21: the audio route of a generating item answers 404.\n- [ ] D13: force a describe failure with a temporarily wrong `GEMINI_API_KEY`, restore the key, retry, and the item reaches ready.\n- [ ] D16: a fourth retry answers 409.\n- [ ] C1, C5, C9 and C11 where a real page reaches them.\n\n## 5. Cutover (only after step 4 passes)\n\n- [ ] Restore the custom-domain route, deploy the API, and point `nagara.asermax.com` at the API Worker.\n- [ ] Remove the Cloudflare Access application and its service token from the pipeline.\n- [ ] Delete the Railway API service, Postgres and bucket. Nothing is copied over.\n- [ ] Add the GitHub secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, then merge, so CI deploys.\n\n## 6. Cleanup\n\n- [ ] Revoke the R2 tokens from the spikes.\n- [ ] Delete the stopped Modal apps `nagara-tts-spike` and `nagara-spike-upload`.\n- [ ] Delete `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env` and `prod-secrets.env`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ef0a9943-96d8-444b-bef3-9815188d7cff","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfwbygTfcJSfnAVXPohhA","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b7186388-c843-475c-81e8-a1a55eee69f2","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:06:26.849Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
