Tests \u001b[22m \u001b[1m\u001b[32m136 passed\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\u001b[2m | \u001b[22m\u001b[33m1 skipped\u001b[39m\u001b[90m (137)\u001b[39m\n\u001b[2m   Start at \u001b[22m 00:12:01\n\u001b[2m   Duration \u001b[22m 24.49s\u001b[2m (transform 81.75s, setup 218.09s, import 21.63s, tests 5.39s, environment 2ms)\u001b[22m","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":9,"newStart":14,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," Both Workers deploy with wrangler. Their configurations bind the same D1 database, named `nagara`, and only the pipeline Worker's binds the R2 bucket (see [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)). The API Worker's configuration binds the item Workflow by the pipeline Worker's script name. `nagara.asermax.com` points at the API Worker, the only Worker clients reach."," ","-> [!WARNING] The D1 database id is a placeholder until the production database exists","-> `pipeline/wrangler.jsonc`, `api/wrangler.jsonc` and `common/wrangler.jsonc` carry the all-zero `database_id` `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000`, which local development and the tests use as is. No D1 database has that id, so the migrate job and both deploys fail against the real account until the production database exists and its id replaces the placeholder in all three files.","-"," > [!NOTE] Why the pipeline Worker has no public routes"," > The API Worker creates and restarts the item Workflow through the cross-script Workflow binding, and nothing else calls the pipeline. With no route to reach, the pipeline Worker carries no authentication of its own and no edge policy guards it."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a9080c1e-3ed9-41c6-9f4d-fcf9023f318a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd