{"parentUuid":"3d249546-8e7f-461a-b5e0-b48f391c3b43","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwd6nYLWXoghq8GV88hh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No. `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` is a Cloudflare API token, not the Access service token.\n\n- **What it's for:** the pipeline uses it to authenticate to the `nagara` AI Gateway. The Flue agents send it to reach Workers AI through the gateway (`pipeline/src/agents/model-provider.ts`). Describe sends it as `cf-aig-authorization` when it calls Gemini through the gateway (`pipeline/src/describe/core.ts:27`).\n- **The Access service token** is a client id and secret pair. Clients sent it to reach the old pipeline through Cloudflare Access. The new pipeline has no public routes, so nothing uses it. It's on the step 5 list to delete.\n\nThe deployed `nagara` Worker already has a `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` secret. The new pipeline deploys under the same Worker name, and `wrangler deploy` keeps the secrets already set, so production doesn't need the value again. `pipeline/.dev.vars` also has a value set (53 characters), which local validation used against the same gateway. I can't read a deployed secret, so I can't confirm the two are the same token.\n\nYou can leave `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` empty in `prod-secrets.env`, and I'll skip it and keep the deployed one. If the D13 or C7 tests fail with a gateway 401, I'll overwrite it with the `.dev.vars` value.\n\nShould I go ahead with the Modal TTS deploy and the D1 migrations while you create the R2 tokens?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":100009,"output_tokens":627,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":106},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":590,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":627,"cache_read_input_tokens":100009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":590},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1a0fa45f-2bdc-4b14-a413-2fd7560e3b44","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfwd6n9momozKChNu8whp","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d59e29a1-69be-474f-8276-ecacf69fcc9c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:21:00.732Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/pipeline","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
