{"parentUuid":"11d1def1-2dd5-4983-987f-11b33e8e134a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfweKn7H1eVrYaXLcj8pj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"D13 passes. Item B (`itm_dc5289f5`) was retried with the real secret and reached `ready`, with `retry_count` 1 and duration 59.35 s. Its ledger has one Firecrawl row and one describer row, so the retry restarted at start synthesis and didn't fetch or describe again. That describer row is also the first Gemini call through the gateway in production, and it worked. Item A stays failed at the cap, with `retry_count` 3.\n\nOn provider keys: yes, it fits. With BYOK, you store the Gemini key on the `nagara` gateway (AI Gateway → `nagara` → Provider Keys, held in Secrets Store), and a request sends only `cf-aig-authorization`. The gateway then adds the provider credential itself.\n\nWhat it changes:\n- **Fewer copies of the key.** `GEMINI_API_KEY` leaves the pipeline's secrets, `pipeline/.dev.vars`, the example file and the env types. The key lives in one place, and rotating it never touches a deploy.\n- **Local dev uses the same key.** It already goes through the same gateway, so it would use the stored key too.\n- **The code change is small.** The describer drops the `x-goog-api-key` header. The vitest config's test value, the docs (`image-and-code-describer.md`, `deployment-and-ci.md`) and the pipeline secrets table change with it.\n- **Every Gemini call depends on the gateway.** That's already true today.\n\nThe Flue agents call Workers AI, which needs no provider key, so they're unaffected.\n\nIt's independent of the cutover. You can do it now, before the remaining rows, or as a separate Linear task after the switch. Which do you want? The test rows still open are C1, C5 (partly covered: item B waited `queued` while A held the `sive.rs` lease), C9 and C11."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":841,"cache_read_input_tokens":138884,"output_tokens":879,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":272},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":138884,"cache_creation_input_tokens":841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a1a45dca-5d10-4ca2-ab20-870bdcfcc611","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfweKmjhq4pVJkE8hvs2F","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1aab932a-b3fe-46c9-9c7b-5ae3e406d5d0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:37:07.403Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/common","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
