0f70","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfweXUSDzDQgkE5PVpk5v","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9a4d130-270d-4e68-b778-543f292f85f7","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:39:41.208Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"a9a4d130-270d-4e68-b778-543f292f85f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"846cd608-f589-4070-ab03-34264ca2b2e0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EAhKas54YBCCHZnEy2HLZH","type":"tool_result","content":"13:    \"types\": \"pnpm build:bundle && tsc --noEmit\"\n37:    \"typescript\": \"7.0.2\",\ndeclare namespace Cloudflare {\n  interface Exports {\n    default: {\n      fetch(request: Request, env?: unknown): Promise<Response>;\n    };\n> [!WARNING] Waiting for a connection counts toward a step's timeout\n> All the child steps start together, but their calls run 6 at a time, and the time a child waits for a free connection counts toward its 1-minute timeout. In the spike that measured it, the last of 25 five-second calls finished 26 s after the fan-out started. A slow gateway or a full budget of large SVGs can push the last children in the queue past their timeout, and each such child fails that attempt.\n\n**Retry policy.** The describe step has 3 attempts of 5 minutes each, and each child step has 3 attempts of 1 minute each. A retry of the describe step runs every child again as new steps, so a repeated describe goes back to AI Gateway, whose response cache answers a request identical to one that already succeeded.\n\n**A failed description degrades the unit and never fails the item.** A unit whose child step failed gets a `describe failed` degradation and floors (code) or keeps the fallback (image). The describe phase never fails the item, even when every description failed: a code-bearing item whose Gemini calls all failed reaches `ready` with every code block on the floor `\"Code with no description.\"` and a degradation for each.\n\nThe pipeline Worker holds the Gemini key and the AI Gateway token as secrets. A failed or capped unit made no billable call, so only a successful describe writes a ledger row.\n\n## ⏩ What is not built yet\n\n3:summary: \"The Gemini describer, reached through AI Gateway with its response cache: one generated sentence for a block a listener can't see, reused by the code path and the image path, floored and capped against one shared per-item budget.\"\n12:Gives a listener one spoken sentence for a block they cannot see: a code block, or an image with no author-written text. It is a reusable core with two callers: the code path and the image path both reach the same Gemini call, layered under a fan-out that floors, caps, and fails per unit. It never speaks what a block *means*, only what it *is* or *shows*: meaning comes from the author, and the describer only makes the block visible. It runs as the item Workflow's describe step, which starts one child step per description (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)), and every call goes through AI Gateway with the gateway's response cache on.\n30:The core call makes one call to `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` through AI Gateway, parses the JSON, and runs the value through the shared sanitize tail. The response schema is a JSON object with one required string field, `spoken`.\n45:### 🗄️ The gateway's response cache\n47:AI Gateway answers an identical request from its response cache without calling Gemini, and reports the hit in the `cf-aig-cache-status` response header. A describe repeated with the same prompt and the same image, such as a code snippet two articles share, costs no model call. Each successful describe writes one ledger row at the flat describe price, whether Gemini or the cache answered, and sets the row's cached flag when the header reports a hit (see [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)).\n113:> All the child steps start together, but their calls run 6 at a time, and the time a child waits for a free connection counts toward its 1-minute timeout. In the spike that measured it, the last of 25 five-second calls finished 26 s after the fan-out started. A slow gateway or a full budget of large SVGs can push the last children in the queue past their timeout, and each such child fails that attempt.\n115:**Retry policy.** The describe step has 3 attempts of 5 minutes each, and each child step has 3 attempts of 1 minute each. A retry of the describe step runs every child again as new steps, so a repeated describe goes back to AI Gateway, whose response cache answers a request identical to one that already succeeded.\n119:The pipeline Worker holds the Gemini key and the AI Gateway token as secrets. A failed or capped unit made no billable call, so only a successful describe writes a ledger row.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f7947135-ea34-4c06-879c-5dbc1ca0a4c8","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:39:41.592Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"13:    \"types\": \"pnpm build:bundle && tsc --noEmit\"\n37:    \"typescript\": \"7.0.2\",\ndeclare namespace Cloudflare {\n  interface Exports {\n    default: {\n      fetch(request: Request, env?: unknown): Promise<Response>;\n    };\n> [!WARNING] Waiting for a connection counts toward a step's timeout\n> All the child steps start together, but their calls run 6 at a time, and the time a child waits for a free connection counts toward its 1-minute timeout. In the spike that measured it, the last of 25 five-second calls finished 26 s after the fan-out started. A slow gateway or a full budget of large SVGs can push the last children in the queue past their timeout, and each such child fails that attempt.\n\n**Retry policy.** The describe step has 3 attempts of 5 minutes each, and each child step has 3 attempts of 1 minute each. A retry of the describe step runs every child again as new steps, so a repeated describe goes back to AI Gateway, whose response cache answers a request identical to one that already succeeded.\n\n**A failed description degrades the unit and never fails the item.** A unit whose child step failed gets a `describe failed` degradation and floors (code) or keeps the fallback (image). The describe phase never fails the item, even when every description failed: a code-bearing item whose Gemini calls all failed reaches `ready` with every code block on the floor `\"Code with no description.\"` and a degradation for each.\n\nThe pipeline Worker holds the Gemini key and the AI Gateway token as secrets. A failed or capped unit made no billable call, so only a successful describe writes a ledger row.\n\n## ⏩ What is not built yet\n\n3:summary: \"The Gemini describer, reached through AI Gateway with its response cache: one generated sentence for a block a listener can't see, reused by the code path and the image path, floored and capped against one shared per-item budget.\"\n12:Gives a listener one spoken sentence for a block they cannot see: a code block, or an image with no author-written text. It is a reusable core with two callers: the code path and the image path both reach the same Gemini call, layered under a fan-out that floors, caps, and fails per unit. It never speaks what a block *means*, only what it *is* or *shows*: meaning comes from the author, and the describer only makes the block visible. It runs as the item Workflow's describe step, which starts one child step per description (see [item-lifecycle](item-lifecycle.md)), and every call goes through AI Gateway with the gateway's response cache on.\n30:The core call makes one call to `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` through AI Gateway, parses the JSON, and runs the value through the shared sanitize tail. The response schema is a JSON object with one required string field, `spoken`.\n45:### 🗄️ The gateway's response cache\n47:AI Gateway answers an identical request from its response cache without calling Gemini, and reports the hit in the `cf-aig-cache-status` response header. A describe repeated with the same prompt and the same image, such as a code snippet two articles share, costs no model call. Each successful describe writes one ledger row at the flat describe price, whether Gemini or the cache answered, and sets the row's cached flag when the header reports a hit (see [persistence-and-storage](persistence-and-storage.md)).\n113:> All the child steps start together, but their calls run 6 at a time, and the time a child waits for a free connection counts toward its 1-minute timeout. In the spike that measured it, the last of 25 five-second calls finished 26 s after the fan-out started. A slow gateway or a full budget of large SVGs can push the last children in the queue past their timeout, and each such child fails that attempt.\n115:**Retry policy.** The describe step has 3 attempts of 5 minutes each, and each child step has 3 attempts of 1 minute each. A retry of the describe step runs every child again as new steps, so a repeated describe goes back to AI Gateway, whose response cache answers a request identical to one that already succeeded.\n119:The pipeline Worker holds the Gemini key and the AI Gateway token as secrets. A failed or capped unit made no billable call, so only a successful describe writes a ledger row.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0ed82d50-5e0e-4ae3-a8f8-0ec1b6db0f70","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","branch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"asermax/nagara","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"filadd/cc-plugin-marketplace","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a9a4d130-270d-4e68-b778-543f292f85f7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"feat/cloudflare-migration","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
