{"parentUuid":"3250f274-9c1c-42f0-8368-5508afc7233a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b0783bda-2a1f-4b85-9a2b-5ec970e5ef3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TBPYbNeeD142EryYJbaW8i","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"ASE-83\",\"uuid\":\"88a75223-8f1b-4fdd-bc3a-206276da0f5f\",\"title\":\"Switch nagara over to Cloudflare and retire Railway\",\"description\":\"Bring the migrated stack up in production and remove what it replaces. The first deploy is manual. The API runs on its [workers.dev](<http://workers.dev>) URL until the end-to-end test passes. Only then does `nagara.asermax.com` move to it and Railway get deleted.\\n\\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md`, `docs/technical-design/authentication.md`, `docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md`.\\n\\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`.\\n\\n## 1. Credentials (user)\\n\\nEach one goes into `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/prod-secrets.env`, keyed by name, and never into the chat.\\n\\n- [X] `API_KEY`: the clients' key. Reuse Railway's or create a new one.\\n- [X] `R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read only, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the API.\\n- [X] `R2_PUT_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_PUT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read & Write, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the pipeline.\\n- [X] `MODAL_PROXY_KEY` / `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET`: a new Modal proxy auth token. The local-validation token was revoked.\\n- [X] `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` (AI Gateway token). `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` keeps the value the old `nagara` Worker already had.\\n\\n## 2. Cloudflare resources\\n\\n- [X] `wrangler d1 create nagara` (id `bdc5b6b3-724f-47df-8733-640fd263cd2f`, region ENAM), then put its id in place of the all-zero placeholder in `common/`, `api/` and `pipeline/` `wrangler.jsonc`, and commit.\\n- [X] `wrangler r2 bucket create nagara`.\\n- [X] Create the two R2 tokens from step 1, which needs the bucket to exist.\\n\\n## 3. Deploy\\n\\n- [X] tts: `uv run modal deploy app.py` in `tts/`. This replaces the `nagara-tts` app that Railway calls, so Railway stops synthesizing from this point.\\n- [X] Check that `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web.modal.run/{start,result}` answers 401 without proxy auth. Fix `MODAL_START_URL`/`MODAL_RESULT_URL` if the URL differs.\\n- [X] Migrations: `wrangler d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` from `common/`.\\n- [X] Pipeline: `pnpm run deploy` in `pipeline/`, then `wrangler secret put` for its 7 secrets. This replaces the old extraction-service `nagara` Worker. The v2 tag deletes JobIndex.\\n- [X] API (`https://nagara-api.asermax.workers.dev`): `pnpm run deploy` in `api/` with the custom-domain route removed locally and `workers_dev: true`. The change stays uncommitted. Then `wrangler secret put` for its 3 secrets.\\n\\n## 4. End-to-end test against [workers.dev](<http://workers.dev>)\\n\\nUse small articles, and listen to every audio.\\n\\n- [X] `/health` answers 200. D25: a poll without the key gets 401.\\n- [X] D1: enqueue with a voice, and the item goes queued → generating → ready (`itm_961ed933`, [sive.rs/hellyeah](<http://sive.rs/hellyeah>), about 90 s).\\n- [X] C7: the first article of a new domain authors version 1 of its recipe.\\n- [X] B1 / D20: the audio sits in R2, and the 307 URL plays and seeks in a browser.\\n- [X] D21: the audio route of a generating item answers 404.\\n- [X] D13: force a start-synthesis failure with a temporarily wrong `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET`, restore the secret, retry, and the item reaches ready. A wrong Gemini key only degrades describe, so it can't fail the item.\\n- [X] D16: a fourth retry answers 409.\\n- [X] C1, C5, C9 and C11, using real pages and the synthetic pages behind quick tunnels. On the synthetic C1 page the authored recipe typed the `pre` block as a paragraph, so it was spoken as \\\"Code sample.\\\" without a description. The real article's 3 code blocks came out as `code` units.\\n- [X] The Gemini key moved to the gateway as a provider key (BYOK). The describer no longer sends `x-goog-api-key`, and the `GEMINI_API_KEY` secret is deleted.\\n\\n## 5. Cutover (only after step 4 passes)\\n\\n- [X] Restore the custom-domain route, deploy the API, and point `nagara.asermax.com` at the API Worker. Railway's DNS record was deleted by hand, since wrangler can't attach a custom domain over an existing record.\\n- [ ] Remove the Cloudflare Access application and its service token from the pipeline.\\n- [ ] Delete the Railway API service, Postgres and bucket. Nothing is copied over.\\n- [ ] Add the GitHub secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, then merge, so CI deploys.\\n\\n## 6. Cleanup\\n\\n- [ ] Revoke the R2 tokens from the spikes.\\n- [ ] Delete the stopped Modal apps `nagara-tts-spike` and `nagara-spike-upload`.\\n- [ ] Delete `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env` and `prod-secrets.env`.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"1f715c70-f21d-466d-92a3-ef263db6955e\",\"name\":\"Cloudflare migration\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/asermax/issue/ASE-83/switch-nagara-over-to-cloudflare-and-retire-railway\",\"gitBranchName\":\"asermax/ase-83-switch-nagara-over-to-cloudflare-and-retire-railway\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-11T06:01:48.076Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-12T03:51:13.014Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-12T03:06:28.786Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"labels\":[\"Improvement\"],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Agustin Carrasco\",\"createdById\":\"c8b03f1c-0b66-413e-85b8-f11067346ca8\",\"project\":\"nagara\",\"projectId\":\"14d108e2-6712-4129-b37d-e021d5aa2f0b\",\"team\":\"Asermax\",\"teamId\":\"c821b24b-23d9-403e-9038-23d9024a2110\"}"}]}]},"uuid":"92fd611e-d9ff-4560-a997-9bb75160d3d9","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:51:13.823Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"ASE-83\",\"uuid\":\"88a75223-8f1b-4fdd-bc3a-206276da0f5f\",\"title\":\"Switch nagara over to Cloudflare and retire Railway\",\"description\":\"Bring the migrated stack up in production and remove what it replaces. The first deploy is manual. The API runs on its [workers.dev](<http://workers.dev>) URL until the end-to-end test passes. Only then does `nagara.asermax.com` move to it and Railway get deleted.\\n\\nNotes: `docs/technical-design/deployment-and-ci.md`, `docs/technical-design/authentication.md`, `docs/technical-design/persistence-and-storage.md`.\\n\\nBranch: `feat/cloudflare-migration`.\\n\\n## 1. Credentials (user)\\n\\nEach one goes into `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/prod-secrets.env`, keyed by name, and never into the chat.\\n\\n- [X] `API_KEY`: the clients' key. Reuse Railway's or create a new one.\\n- [X] `R2_GET_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_GET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read only, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the API.\\n- [X] `R2_PUT_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `R2_PUT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: an R2 API token with Object Read & Write, scoped to the `nagara` bucket. Used by the pipeline.\\n- [X] `MODAL_PROXY_KEY` / `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET`: a new Modal proxy auth token. The local-validation token was revoked.\\n- [X] `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` (AI Gateway token). `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` keeps the value the old `nagara` Worker already had.\\n\\n## 2. Cloudflare resources\\n\\n- [X] `wrangler d1 create nagara` (id `bdc5b6b3-724f-47df-8733-640fd263cd2f`, region ENAM), then put its id in place of the all-zero placeholder in `common/`, `api/` and `pipeline/` `wrangler.jsonc`, and commit.\\n- [X] `wrangler r2 bucket create nagara`.\\n- [X] Create the two R2 tokens from step 1, which needs the bucket to exist.\\n\\n## 3. Deploy\\n\\n- [X] tts: `uv run modal deploy app.py` in `tts/`. This replaces the `nagara-tts` app that Railway calls, so Railway stops synthesizing from this point.\\n- [X] Check that `https://asermax--nagara-tts-web.modal.run/{start,result}` answers 401 without proxy auth. Fix `MODAL_START_URL`/`MODAL_RESULT_URL` if the URL differs.\\n- [X] Migrations: `wrangler d1 migrations apply nagara --remote` from `common/`.\\n- [X] Pipeline: `pnpm run deploy` in `pipeline/`, then `wrangler secret put` for its 7 secrets. This replaces the old extraction-service `nagara` Worker. The v2 tag deletes JobIndex.\\n- [X] API (`https://nagara-api.asermax.workers.dev`): `pnpm run deploy` in `api/` with the custom-domain route removed locally and `workers_dev: true`. The change stays uncommitted. Then `wrangler secret put` for its 3 secrets.\\n\\n## 4. End-to-end test against [workers.dev](<http://workers.dev>)\\n\\nUse small articles, and listen to every audio.\\n\\n- [X] `/health` answers 200. D25: a poll without the key gets 401.\\n- [X] D1: enqueue with a voice, and the item goes queued → generating → ready (`itm_961ed933`, [sive.rs/hellyeah](<http://sive.rs/hellyeah>), about 90 s).\\n- [X] C7: the first article of a new domain authors version 1 of its recipe.\\n- [X] B1 / D20: the audio sits in R2, and the 307 URL plays and seeks in a browser.\\n- [X] D21: the audio route of a generating item answers 404.\\n- [X] D13: force a start-synthesis failure with a temporarily wrong `MODAL_PROXY_SECRET`, restore the secret, retry, and the item reaches ready. A wrong Gemini key only degrades describe, so it can't fail the item.\\n- [X] D16: a fourth retry answers 409.\\n- [X] C1, C5, C9 and C11, using real pages and the synthetic pages behind quick tunnels. On the synthetic C1 page the authored recipe typed the `pre` block as a paragraph, so it was spoken as \\\"Code sample.\\\" without a description. The real article's 3 code blocks came out as `code` units.\\n- [X] The Gemini key moved to the gateway as a provider key (BYOK). The describer no longer sends `x-goog-api-key`, and the `GEMINI_API_KEY` secret is deleted.\\n\\n## 5. Cutover (only after step 4 passes)\\n\\n- [X] Restore the custom-domain route, deploy the API, and point `nagara.asermax.com` at the API Worker. Railway's DNS record was deleted by hand, since wrangler can't attach a custom domain over an existing record.\\n- [ ] Remove the Cloudflare Access application and its service token from the pipeline.\\n- [ ] Delete the Railway API service, Postgres and bucket. Nothing is copied over.\\n- [ ] Add the GitHub secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, then merge, so CI deploys.\\n\\n## 6. Cleanup\\n\\n- [ ] Revoke the R2 tokens from the spikes.\\n- [ ] Delete the stopped Modal apps `nagara-tts-spike` and `nagara-spike-upload`.\\n- [ ] Delete `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/modal-proxy.env` and `prod-secrets.env`.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"1f715c70-f21d-466d-92a3-ef263db6955e\",\"name\":\"Cloudflare migration\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/asermax/issue/ASE-83/switch-nagara-over-to-cloudflare-and-retire-railway\",\"gitBranchName\":\"asermax/ase-83-switch-nagara-over-to-cloudflare-and-retire-railway\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-11T06:01:48.076Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-12T03:51:13.014Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-12T03:06:28.786Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"labels\":[\"Improvement\"],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Agustin Carrasco\",\"createdById\":\"c8b03f1c-0b66-413e-85b8-f11067346ca8\",\"project\":\"nagara\",\"projectId\":\"14d108e2-6712-4129-b37d-e021d5aa2f0b\",\"team\":\"Asermax\",\"teamId\":\"c821b24b-23d9-403e-9038-23d9024a2110\"}"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"36b5dbf2-5ee0-4699-bf6a-f710f581f5e6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/worksp