{"parentUuid":"6b17ab03-ecae-44c7-8d88-0acd8d514eb6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwfwbzvjL6qN38uEPnpz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `cloudflare` run's checks all passed, but the `migrate` job failed, so the deploy jobs never ran. Cloudflare's D1 API rejected the CI token with `The given account is not valid or is not authorized to access this service [code: 7403]`. The token dates from the extraction-service CI, which never used D1, so it most likely lacks D1 permission. The 7403 code can also mean the stored account id doesn't match, but the token is the likelier cause.\n\nProduction is unaffected. CI would deploy the same commit I deployed by hand, so nothing is out of date.\n\nTo fix it, open **My Profile → API Tokens** in the Cloudflare dashboard and edit the token behind `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`. Add these permissions:\n- **Account → D1 → Edit**, for the migrate job.\n- **Zone → Workers Routes → Edit** on `asermax.com`, which the API deploy needs to attach the custom domain.\n\nThe token should already have Workers Scripts Edit, since it deployed the old pipeline.\n\nWhen you've saved it, tell me and I'll run `gh run rerun 38201565758 --failed` and watch the three deploy jobs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":183809,"output_tokens":553,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":701,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":553,"cache_read_input_tokens":183809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":701},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null