{"parentUuid":"fb8f7b99-a09c-49b7-adbf-4c425863585b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwgRKUJGrM9Soti8yJsG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49,"cache_read_input_tokens":194811,"output_tokens":1116,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":352},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":194811,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3792,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"84f12f13-f595-4b8e-b6e6-f853780dc980","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwgRJgfGi1Nv3tepxUaN","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f40ccd2f-189a-42eb-93fd-c8681e6d4881","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:04:30.733Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"f40ccd2f-189a-42eb-93fd-c8681e6d4881","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwgRKUJGrM9Soti8yJsG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain gets a recipe: a small script the author agent writes. It turns the page's HTML elements into units and labels each one with a type, such as `paragraph`, `code` or `image`. The pipeline uses that label to decide what a unit gets. A `code` unit goes to the describer, and the listener hears \"Code: <one sentence about the code>\".\n\nFor the synthetic C1 page, the agent's script handled `pre` in the same branch as `p`:\n\n```js\nc.find(\"p, pre, figure\").each((_, el) => {\n  if (el.tagName === \"figure\") { units.push({ type: \"image\", ... }) }\n  else { units.push({ type: \"paragraph\", display: toMarkdown(e.clone()), ... }) }\n});\n```\n\nSo the code block came out as a unit labelled `paragraph`, holding a fenced block:\n\n- **Display:** still correct. A reader sees the code, because `toMarkdown` turns the `pre` into a fence.\n- **Spoken form:** the paragraph text goes through the usual spoken-form derivation, which turns any fenced block into the placeholder \"Code sample.\".\n- **Describe:** skipped, because the describer only runs on units labelled `code`. \"Code sample.\" is never replaced.\n\nSo the listener hears \"Code sample.\" where they should hear something like \"Code: An HTTP header specifies how long a response may be reused.\" Nothing fails and the item reaches `ready`, so only listening reveals it.\n\nIt isn't a deploy problem. Locally the agent wrote a recipe for the same page that labelled the `pre` as `code`, and the real eli article's three code blocks were all labelled `code` in production. The agent produced a weaker recipe this time, and nothing downstream caught it. The recipe stays saved for that domain, so every later article from the domain gets the same treatment until a revision changes it.\n\nIt could be caught in three places:\n- **At runtime:** treat a `paragraph` unit whose display is only a fenced block as `code`. This is the cheapest fix and works for recipes already saved.\n- **At authoring:** have the check the agent runs on its draft recipe reject a `pre` labelled as `paragraph`, so the agent fixes it before the recipe is saved.\n- **In the prompt:** state more firmly that `pre` must become `code`. This lowers the odds but guarantees nothing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49,"cache_read_input_tokens":194811,"output_tokens":1116,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":352},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":194811,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"84f12f13-f595-4b8e-b6e6-f853780dc980","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwgRJgfGi1Nv3tepxUaN","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"91718592-ac9c-45e8-bc68-2952d90cae62","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:04:38.395Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
