6-10-12T04:05:40.965Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Directed mode\n\nUsed when `learn` is invoked with arguments. The user has already decided what the session should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take.\n\n1. **Map the state the ask touches.** Read the skills, agents, wiki entries and local files the ask names or would change, and find every reference to them across the plugin. Report what exists, what references what, and what the ask would leave dangling.\n\n2. **Restate each item of the ask** in your own words, as the job it does and where it lands. The user corrects the reading here, before anything is drafted.\n\n3. **Settle what the ask leaves open** before drafting: names, scope (global or local), which existing pieces stay, which docs change. Ask these together, as questions with no preference stated. Do not decide any of them.\n\n4. Continue with **Drafting** in `SKILL.md`, in the order the user gave the items.\nbasics.md\nimplement.md\nspike.md\ntasks.md\nwiki\n# References\n\n- [`cloudflare`](cloudflare/INDEX.md): running jobs, gates, agents, containers and data on Cloudflare's platform\n- [`firecrawl`](firecrawl/INDEX.md): calling Firecrawl from runtimes its SDK does not support\n- [`gemini`](gemini/INDEX.md): what the Gemini API accepts as input and how it describes it\n- [`markdown`](markdown/INDEX.md): parsing markdown into a syntax tree outside a renderer\n- [`modal`](modal/INDEX.md): calling Modal functions from outside its Python client\n- [`node`](node/INDEX.md): running and distributing a Node program\n- [`testing`](testing/INDEX.md): how test runners are built and what they expose","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3f6a0ed9-fdd1-4081-a62d-788b8ccd3928","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration","root":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/