{"parentUuid":"1c392ea0-8376-4bbf-a825-b5ed46ce4470","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwgXrNaTXv7h1m9qdaR9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1604,"cache_read_input_tokens":200462,"output_tokens":1663,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":762},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1604,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1663,"cache_read_input_tokens":200462,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1604},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13340,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"c6b15a50-fa6f-48d4-b692-93e7e0fbf7fe","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwgXqx1y8MzAFubZHkkJ","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:learn","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"95f77589-5348-439c-876f-5b6ad0ac803a","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:06:08.972Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"95f77589-5348-439c-876f-5b6ad0ac803a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwgXrNaTXv7h1m9qdaR9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"These are the candidates from the deploy leg. Before listing them, I checked that the wiki doesn't already cover them.\n\n**Wiki entries (Cloudflare, global)**\n\n1. **`cloudflare/ai-gateway.md` gains a section on provider keys.** A key stored on the gateway as a provider key (BYOK) means the caller drops the provider's own auth header and sends only `cf-aig-authorization`. Workers AI calls through the gateway also authenticate with that header alone. Today the entry covers `cf-aig-authorization` and caching, but not provider keys.\n2. **A new entry, `cloudflare/workers-deploy.md`, on deploying Workers with wrangler.** Its facts, all seen in this leg:\n   - A custom domain can't attach to a hostname that already has DNS records. The error is code `100117`, and the record has to be deleted first.\n   - Wrangler has no DNS commands, and its OAuth login token has only `zone (read)`.\n   - When the custom domain fails, the deploy reports \"partially updated\" and doesn't roll back. If the config doesn't set `workers_dev`, that deploy also turns workers.dev off, so the Worker is left with no URL.\n   - `wrangler secret bulk` reads JSON from stdin, so several secrets are set in one deployment without printing them.\n   - Secrets survive `wrangler deploy` when the Worker keeps its name.\n   - A new workers.dev hostname can answer 404 for a short time after it's first enabled.\n   - In CI, a D1 error with code `7403` means the token lacks D1 Edit. A deploy that attaches a custom domain also needs Workers Routes Edit on the zone.\n\n**Skill iterations (global)**\n\n3. **`mahou:validate` adds a way to force a failure on a deployed system.** Temporarily set a secret to a wrong value. Then restore it from the file that holds the real value, never by retyping it, and record both steps in the report. It sits next to the existing paragraph on forcing a failure with a temporary code change.\n4. **A credentials template, in the secrets rules of `mahou:basics` or `mahou:spike`.** When several credentials are needed, write a file with every key empty, a comment per key naming where its value comes from, and a note for keys that keep their current value. The user fills it in, and the values are copied by key name. Today only `mahou:spike` has the rule that the user writes a credential to a scratch file with `!`, and it covers one credential.\n\nI left one fact out because the session never verified it: that the local D1 state is filed under the `database_id`, so a new id starts with an empty database.\n\nWhich of these do you want drafted? For item 4, should it land in `basics` so every skill follows it, or in `spike`?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1604,"cache_read_input_tokens":200462,"output_tokens":1663,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":762},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1604,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1663,"cache_read_input_tokens":200462,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1604},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c6b15a50-fa6f-48d4-b692-93e7e0fbf7fe","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwgXqx1y8MzAFubZHkkJ","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"mahou:learn","attributionPlugin":"mahou","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ed40e55-b92b-40e6-b3a4-b718f1f30742","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:06:10.902Z","advisorModel":"c