{"parentUuid":"8797829d-a264-402a-a06d-e804724aec7d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwgedUcuSv9cEMv7EJSM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QWWNqvYcZ14BYjeaeZRzS7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round5/drafts.md","content":"# Learn round 5: drafts\n\n## 1. Wiki: AI Gateway provider keys\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/ai-gateway.md`.\n\n`verified: 2026-10-10` becomes `verified: 2026-10-12`.\n\nThe \"Answers\" paragraph, old: \"Answers what changes when a Worker calls a model provider through Cloudflare AI Gateway instead of directly: authentication, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, and from the AI Gateway docs.\"\n\nNew: \"Answers what changes when a Worker calls a model provider through Cloudflare AI Gateway instead of directly: authentication, provider keys, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, from a production Worker that calls Gemini and Workers AI through one gateway, and from the AI Gateway docs.\"\n\nAfter the bullet \"A gateway with authentication on requires a `cf-aig-authorization` header on every request.\", two new bullets:\n\n- A provider key stored on the gateway (BYOK) takes the provider's credential out of the caller. The request carries only `cf-aig-authorization`, and the gateway adds the stored key before forwarding. A Gemini call through `google-ai-studio` with no `x-goog-api-key` header succeeded this way from a deployed Worker, so the Worker needs no provider secret.\n- A Workers AI model reached through the gateway's `workers-ai` provider authenticated with `cf-aig-authorization` alone, with no `Authorization` header.\n\nNew line in \"Sources\": \"- Production run, 2026-10-12: Gemini through `google-ai-studio` with a stored provider key, and Workers AI through `workers-ai`, from a deployed Worker\"\n\n`cloudflare/INDEX.md`, old: \"- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\"\n\nNew: \"- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, provider keys, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\"\n\n## 2. Wiki: deploying Workers with wrangler\n\nNew file `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/workers-deploy.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Workers deploy: custom domains, secrets and CI tokens with wrangler\n\nverified: 2026-10-12\n\nAnswers what needs care when a Worker is deployed with wrangler: attaching a custom domain, what a failed trigger update leaves behind, setting secrets, creating resources from a script, and the permissions a CI token needs. Distilled from a manual production deploy of two Workers, a D1 database and an R2 bucket with wrangler 4.135, and from the first CI deploy after it.\n\n## Knowledge\n\n- A custom domain (`routes: [{ \"pattern\": \"<host>\", \"custom_domain\": true }]`) does not attach to a hostname that already has DNS records. The deploy fails with `Hostname '<host>' already has externally managed DNS records (A, CNAME, etc). Delete them first or try a different hostname. [code: 100117]`. Delete the record and deploy again. Between the two, the hostname has no record.\n- wrangler has no command for DNS records, and the OAuth token from `wrangler login` carries `zone (read)` only. Delete a record in the dashboard, or with an API token that has Zone DNS Edit.\n- A failed trigger update is not rolled back. wrangler reports `Trigger configuration for \"<worker>\" was only partially updated` and the new version stays live. A config with `routes` and no `workers_dev` key turns workers.dev off on that deploy. A Worker moved from workers.dev to a custom domain that then fails to attach is reachable at no URL until a deploy succeeds.\n- Right after workers.dev was first enabled for a Worker, a request to it answered 404. The same request answered normally a few seconds later.\n- `wrangler secret bulk --name <worker>` reads a JSON object from stdin when no file is given, and sets every key in one new version. A script that builds the JSON from the file holding the values keeps them out of the terminal. `wrangler secret put <KEY> --name <worker>` also reads the value from stdin. Every secret change deploys a new version at once.\n- Secrets survive `wrangler deploy`. A Worker redeployed under the same name keeps every secret it had, including those the new code does not read, until `wrangler secret delete`.\n- `wrangler d1 create` and `wrangler r2 bucket create` work with the OAuth token. In a non-interactive shell they print the binding snippet and leave the config alone (`Using fallback value in non-interactive context: no`). `wrangler d1 migrations apply <db> --remote` in a non-interactive shell answers its own \"continue?\" prompt with yes.\n- In CI, D1 calls failed with `The given account is not valid or is not authorized to access this service [code: 7403]` when the API token had no D1 permission. Once the token had Account D1 Edit and Zone Workers Routes Edit on the domain's zone, the migrations and both deploys passed, one of them attaching a custom domain.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Custom domains: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/routing/custom-domains/\n- Secrets: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/secrets/\n- Production deploy, 2026-10-12: two Workers, D1 and R2 created and deployed by hand, a custom domain moved off an existing DNS record, then the first CI deploy\n```\n\n`cloudflare/INDEX.md`, a new line between `vitest-plugin` and `workflows`:\n\n\"- [`workers-deploy`](workers-deploy.md): deploying with wrangler: a custom domain over existing DNS records, partial trigger updates, secrets from stdin, and CI token permissions\"\n\n## 3. learn: pick the mode from the ask\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/learn/SKILL.md`, with edits to its two references and the plugin README.\n\n`SKILL.md`, \"Two modes\", old:\n\n```markdown\n## Two modes\n\nRoute on the arguments.\n\n- **No arguments.** Discovery. Follow `references/discover.md`. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\n- **Arguments given.** Directed. Follow `references/directed.md`. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\n\nBoth modes continue with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\n```\n\nNew:\n\n```markdown\n## Modes\n\nPick the mode from what the user asks, not from whether there are arguments.\n\n- **Discovery.** Follow `references/discover.md` when the user gives nothing to go on, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\n- **Directed.** Follow `references/directed.md` when the user names what to build. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\n- **Mixed.** When the user names some items and also asks what else there is, work the named items as directed and run discovery over the part of the session the ask points at.\n\nSay which mode you are following, and for a mix which items go each way, before starting. Every mode continues with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\n```\n\n`SKILL.md` frontmatter `description`, old: \"The author's tool for growing the plugin from real sessions. Without arguments it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks. With arguments it works the user's ask directly from the current context. Produces new or iterated skills, agents, wiki entries and local .mahou files.\"\n\nNew: \"The author's tool for growing the plugin from real sessions. Depending on what the user asks, it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks; or it works the user's ask directly from the current context; or both. Produces new or iterated skills, agents, wiki entries and local .mahou files.\"\n\n`references/discover.md`, first line, old: \"Used when `learn` is invoked without arguments.\"\n\nNew: \"Used when the user gives nothing to go on, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. In a mixed ask, it covers only the part of the session the ask points at.\"\n\n`references/directed.md`, first line, old: \"Used when `learn` is invoked with arguments. The user has already decided what the session should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take.\"\n\nNew: \"Used when the user names what to build, alone or as the named part of a mixed ask. The user has already decided what those items should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take on them.\"\n\n`mahou/README.md`, the `mahou:learn` line, old: \"Collects the points where a session generated friction (or takes your ask directly), and proposes…\"\n\nNew: \"Collects the points where a session generated friction, takes your ask directly, or both, and proposes…\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_read_input_tokens":206361,"output_tokens":5655,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2443},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5655,"cache_read_input_tokens":206361,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QWWNqvYcZ14BYjeaeZRzS7":{"file_path":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round5/drafts.md","content":"# Learn round 5: drafts\n\n## 1. Wiki: AI Gateway provider keys\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/ai-gateway.md`.\n\n`verified: 2026-10-10` becomes `verified: 2026-10-12`.\n\nThe \"Answers\" paragraph, old: \"Answers what changes when a Worker calls a model provider through Cloudflare AI Gateway instead of directly: authentication, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, and from the AI Gateway docs.\"\n\nNew: \"Answers what changes when a Worker calls a model provider through Cloudflare AI Gateway instead of directly: authentication, provider keys, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, from a production Worker that calls Gemini and Workers AI through one gateway, and from the AI Gateway docs.\"\n\nAfter the bullet \"A gateway with authentication on requires a `cf-aig-authorization` header on every request.\", two new bullets:\n\n- A provider key stored on the gateway (BYOK) takes the provider's credential out of the caller. The request carries only `cf-aig-authorization`, and the gateway adds the stored key before forwarding. A Gemini call through `google-ai-studio` with no `x-goog-api-key` header succeeded this way from a deployed Worker, so the Worker needs no provider secret.\n- A Workers AI model reached through the gateway's `workers-ai` provider authenticated with `cf-aig-authorization` alone, with no `Authorization` header.\n\nNew line in \"Sources\": \"- Production run, 2026-10-12: Gemini through `google-ai-studio` with a stored provider key, and Workers AI through `workers-ai`, from a deployed Worker\"\n\n`cloudflare/INDEX.md`, old: \"- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\"\n\nNew: \"- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, provider keys, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\"\n\n## 2. Wiki: deploying Workers with wrangler\n\nNew file `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/workers-deploy.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Workers deploy: custom domains, secrets and CI tokens with wrangler\n\nverified: 2026-10-12\n\nAnswers what needs care when a Worker is deployed with wrangler: attaching a custom domain, what a failed trigger update leaves behind, setting secrets, creating resources from a script, and the permissions a CI token needs. Distilled from a manual production deploy of two Workers, a D1 database and an R2 bucket with wrangler 4.135, and from the first CI deploy after it.\n\n## Knowledge\n\n- A custom domain (`routes: [{ \"pattern\": \"<host>\", \"custom_domain\": true }]`) does not attach to a hostname that already has DNS records. The deploy fails with `Hostname '<host>' already has externally managed DNS records (A, CNAME, etc). Delete them first or try a different hostname. [code: 100117]`. Delete the record and deploy again. Between the two, the hostname has no record.\n- wrangler has no command for DNS records, and the OAuth token from `wrangler login` carries `zone (read)` only. Delete a record in the dashboard, or with an API token that has Zone DNS Edit.\n- A failed trigger update is not rolled back. wrangler reports `Trigger configuration for \"<worker>\" was only partially updated` and the new version stays live. A config with `routes` and no `workers_dev` key turns workers.dev off on that deploy. A Worker moved from workers.dev to a custom domain that then fails to attach is reachable at no URL until a deploy succeeds.\n- Right after workers.dev was first enabled for a Worker, a request to it answered 404. The same request answered normally a few seconds later.\n- `wrangler secret bulk --name <worker>` reads a JSON object from stdin when no file is given, and sets every key in one new version. A script that builds the JSON from the file holding the values keeps them out of the terminal. `wrangler secret put <KEY> --name <worker>` also reads the value from stdin. Every secret change deploys a new version at once.\n- Secrets survive `wrangler deploy`. A Worker redeployed under the same name keeps every secret it had, including those the new code does not read, until `wrangler secret delete`.\n- `wrangler d1 create` and `wrangler r2 bucket create` work with the OAuth token. In a non-interactive shell they print the binding snippet and leave the config alone (`Using fallback value in non-interactive context: no`). `wrangler d1 migrations apply <db> --remote` in a non-interactive shell answers its own \"continue?\" prompt with yes.\n- In CI, D1 calls failed with `The given account is not valid or is not authorized to access this service [code: 7403]` when the API token had no D1 permission. Once the token had Account D1 Edit and Zone Workers Routes Edit on the domain's zone, the migrations and both deploys passed, one of them attaching a custom domain.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Custom domains: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/routing/custom-domains/\n- Secrets: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/secrets/\n- Production deploy, 2026-10-12: two Workers, D1 and R2 created and deployed by hand, a custom domain moved off an existing DNS record, then the first CI deploy\n```\n\n`cloudflare/INDEX.md`, a new line between `vitest-plugin` and `workflows`:\n\n\"- [`workers-deploy`](workers-deploy.md): deploying with wrangler: a custom domain over existing DNS records, partial trigger updates, secrets from stdin, and CI token permissions\"\n\n## 3. learn: pick the mode from the ask\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/learn/SKILL.md`, with edits to its two references and the plugin README.\n\n`SKILL.md`, \"Two modes\", old:\n\n```markdown\n## Two modes\n\nRoute on the arguments.\n\n- **No arguments.** Discovery. Follow `references/discover.md`. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\n- **Arguments given.** Directed. Follow `references/directed.md`. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\n\nBoth modes continue with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\n```\n\nNew:\n\n```markdown\n## Modes\n\nPick the mode from what the user asks, not from whether there are arguments.\n\n- **Discovery.** Follow `references/discover.md` when the user gives nothing to go on, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\n- **Directed.** Follow `references/directed.md` when the user names what to build. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\n- **Mixed.** When the user names some items and also asks what else there is, work the named items as directed and run discovery over the part of the session the ask points at.\n\nSay which mode you are following, and for a mix which items go each way, before starting. Every mode continues with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\n```\n\n`SKILL.md` frontmatter `description`, old: \"The author's tool for growing the plugin from real sessions. Without arguments it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks. With arguments it works the user's ask directly from the current context. Produces new or iterated skills, agents, wiki entries and local .mahou files.\"\n\nNew: \"The author's tool for growing the plugin from real sessions. Depending on what the user asks, it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks; or it works the user's ask directly from the current context; or both. Produces new or iterated skills, agents, wiki entries and local .mahou files.\"\n\n`references/discover.md`, first line, old: \"Used when `learn` is invoked without arguments.\"\n\nNew: \"Used when the user gives nothing to go on, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. In a mixed ask, it covers only the part of the session the ask points at.\"\n\n`references/directed.md`, first line, old: \"Used when `learn` is invoked with arguments. The user has already decided what the session should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take.\"\n\nNew: \"Used when the user names what to build, alone or as the named part of a mixed ask. The user has already decided what those items should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take on them.\"\n\n`mahou/README.md`, the `mahou:learn` line, old: \"Collects the points where a session generated friction (or takes your ask directly), and proposes…\"\n\nNew: \"Collects the points where a session generated friction, takes your ask directly, or both, and proposes…\"\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e73566c3-a56d-4bd1-a531-83e4fa021453","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfwged4L6LtRhoWwjCz37","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7aa72240-86be-4c25-a682-e212bb2a29d2","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:08:14.410Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"7aa72240-86be-4c25-a682-e212bb2a29d2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ceba04d9-a0e6-47f8-b87e-eaa86737ebf8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QWWNqvYcZ14BYjeaeZRzS7","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round5/drafts.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"a6a02f0e-91e8-48e5-88be-6db5ed9b7faf","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:08:14.507Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round5/drafts.md","content":"# Learn round 5: drafts\n\n## 1. Wiki: AI Gateway provider keys\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/ai-gateway.md`.\n\n`verified: 2026-10-10` becomes `verified: 2026-10-12`.\n\nThe \"Answers\" paragraph, old: \"Answers what changes when a Worker calls a model provider through Cloudflare AI Gateway instead of directly: authentication, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, and from the AI Gateway docs.\"\n\nNew: \"Answers what changes when a Worker calls a model provider through Cloudflare AI Gateway instead of directly: authentication, provider keys, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, from a production Worker that calls Gemini and Workers AI through one gateway, and from the AI Gateway docs.\"\n\nAfter the bullet \"A gateway with authentication on requires a `cf-aig-authorization` header on every request.\", two new bullets:\n\n- A provider key stored on the gateway (BYOK) takes the provider's credential out of the caller. The request carries only `cf-aig-authorization`, and the gateway adds the stored key before forwarding. A Gemini call through `google-ai-studio` with no `x-goog-api-key` header succeeded this way from a deployed Worker, so the Worker needs no provider secret.\n- A Workers AI model reached through the gateway's `workers-ai` provider authenticated with `cf-aig-authorization` alone, with no `Authorization` header.\n\nNew line in \"Sources\": \"- Production run, 2026-10-12: Gemini through `google-ai-studio` with a stored provider key, and Workers AI through `workers-ai`, from a deployed Worker\"\n\n`cloudflare/INDEX.md`, old: \"- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\"\n\nNew: \"- [`ai-gateway`](ai-gateway.md): calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, provider keys, the cache header, no cost returned, no CLI\"\n\n## 2. Wiki: deploying Workers with wrangler\n\nNew file `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/workers-deploy.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Workers deploy: custom domains, secrets and CI tokens with wrangler\n\nverified: 2026-10-12\n\nAnswers what needs care when a Worker is deployed with wrangler: attaching a custom domain, what a failed trigger update leaves behind, setting secrets, creating resources from a script, and the permissions a CI token needs. Distilled from a manual production deploy of two Workers, a D1 database and an R2 bucket with wrangler 4.135, and from the first CI deploy after it.\n\n## Knowledge\n\n- A custom domain (`routes: [{ \"pattern\": \"<host>\", \"custom_domain\": true }]`) does not attach to a hostname that already has DNS records. The deploy fails with `Hostname '<host>' already has externally managed DNS records (A, CNAME, etc). Delete them first or try a different hostname. [code: 100117]`. Delete the record and deploy again. Between the two, the hostname has no record.\n- wrangler has no command for DNS records, and the OAuth token from `wrangler login` carries `zone (read)` only. Delete a record in the dashboard, or with an API token that has Zone DNS Edit.\n- A failed trigger update is not rolled back. wrangler reports `Trigger configuration for \"<worker>\" was only partially updated` and the new version stays live. A config with `routes` and no `workers_dev` key turns workers.dev off on that deploy. A Worker moved from workers.dev to a custom domain that then fails to attach is reachable at no URL until a deploy succeeds.\n- Right after workers.dev was first enabled for a Worker, a request to it answered 404. The same request answered normally a few seconds later.\n- `wrangler secret bulk --name <worker>` reads a JSON object from stdin when no file is given, and sets every key in one new version. A script that builds the JSON from the file holding the values keeps them out of the terminal. `wrangler secret put <KEY> --name <worker>` also reads the value from stdin. Every secret change deploys a new version at once.\n- Secrets survive `wrangler deploy`. A Worker redeployed under the same name keeps every secret it had, including those the new code does not read, until `wrangler secret delete`.\n- `wrangler d1 create` and `wrangler r2 bucket create` work with the OAuth token. In a non-interactive shell they print the binding snippet and leave the config alone (`Using fallback value in non-interactive context: no`). `wrangler d1 migrations apply <db> --remote` in a non-interactive shell answers its own \"continue?\" prompt with yes.\n- In CI, D1 calls failed with `The given account is not valid or is not authorized to access this service [code: 7403]` when the API token had no D1 permission. Once the token had Account D1 Edit and Zone Workers Routes Edit on the domain's zone, the migrations and both deploys passed, one of them attaching a custom domain.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Custom domains: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/routing/custom-domains/\n- Secrets: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/secrets/\n- Production deploy, 2026-10-12: two Workers, D1 and R2 created and deployed by hand, a custom domain moved off an existing DNS record, then the first CI deploy\n```\n\n`cloudflare/INDEX.md`, a new line between `vitest-plugin` and `workflows`:\n\n\"- [`workers-deploy`](workers-deploy.md): deploying with wrangler: a custom domain over existing DNS records, partial trigger updates, secrets from stdin, and CI token permissions\"\n\n## 3. learn: pick the mode from the ask\n\nLands in `mahou/skills/learn/SKILL.md`, with edits to its two references and the plugin README.\n\n`SKILL.md`, \"Two modes\", old:\n\n```markdown\n## Two modes\n\nRoute on the arguments.\n\n- **No arguments.** Discovery. Follow `references/discover.md`. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\n- **Arguments given.** Directed. Follow `references/directed.md`. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\n\nBoth modes continue with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\n```\n\nNew:\n\n```markdown\n## Modes\n\nPick the mode from what the user asks, not from whether there are arguments.\n\n- **Discovery.** Follow `references/discover.md` when the user gives nothing to go on, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\n- **Directed.** Follow `references/directed.md` when the user names what to build. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\n- **Mixed.** When the user names some items and also asks what else there is, work the named items as directed and run discovery over the part of the session the ask points at.\n\nSay which mode you are following, and for a mix which items go each way, before starting. Every mode continues with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\n```\n\n`SKILL.md` frontmatter `description`, old: \"The author's tool for growing the plugin from real sessions. Without arguments it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks. With arguments it works the user's ask directly from the current context. Produces new or iterated skills, agents, wiki entries and local .mahou files.\"\n\nNew: \"The author's tool for growing the plugin from real sessions. Depending on what the user asks, it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks; or it works the user's ask directly from the current context; or both. Produces new or iterated skills, agents, wiki entries and local .mahou files.\"\n\n`references/discover.md`, first line, old: \"Used when `learn` is invoked without arguments.\"\n\nNew: \"Used when the user gives nothing to go on, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. In a mixed ask, it covers only the part of the session the ask points at.\"\n\n`references/directed.md`, first line, old: \"Used when `learn` is invoked with arguments. The user has already decided what the session should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take.\"\n\nNew: \"Used when the user names what to build, alone or as the named part of a mixed ask. The user has already decided what those items should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take on them.\"\n\n`mahou/README.md`, the `mahou:learn` line, old: \"Collects the points where a session generated friction (or takes your ask directly), and proposes…\"\n\nNew: \"Collects the points where a session generated friction, takes your ask directly, or both, and proposes…\"\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7aa72240-86be-4c25-a682-e212bb2a29d2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
