{"parentUuid":"ee2a34d3-389c-4cc1-bbd8-73d03a57b0e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwgqQTqt9e3VvVK3ooKX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4011,"cache_read_input_tokens":229911,"output_tokens":1820,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":80},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4011,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1820,"cache_read_input_tokens":229911,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4011},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6527,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"11c76d74-307c-43e1-a7f8-ea45b7d6f7a1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwgqQ4XqnxrijkbcTZvA","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad175b59-0319-4137-9331-d5704f355e6b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:10:00.349Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"ad175b59-0319-4137-9331-d5704f355e6b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwgqQTqt9e3VvVK3ooKX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Unslop is done. The second round found no fix had slipped back, so the three drafts below are final, and all three are saved in `.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round5/drafts.md`. Approve, correct or drop each one separately.\n\n## 1. Wiki: AI Gateway provider keys\n\nThis edits `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/ai-gateway.md`.\n\n- The `verified` date changes from 2026-10-10 to 2026-10-12.\n- The opening paragraph adds \"provider keys\" to the topics the entry covers. It also names a new source: a production Worker that calls Gemini and Workers AI through one gateway.\n- Two new bullets go after the `cf-aig-authorization` bullet:\n  - With a provider key stored on the gateway (BYOK), the caller holds no provider credential. The request carries only `cf-aig-authorization`, and the gateway adds the stored key before forwarding. A Gemini call through `google-ai-studio` with no `x-goog-api-key` header succeeded this way from a deployed Worker.\n  - A Workers AI model reached through the gateway's `workers-ai` provider authenticated with `cf-aig-authorization` alone, with no `Authorization` header.\n- The Sources list gains \"Production run, 2026-10-12: Gemini through `google-ai-studio` with a stored provider key, and Workers AI through `workers-ai`, from a deployed Worker.\"\n- The entry's line in `cloudflare/INDEX.md` adds \"provider keys\" to its list.\n\n## 2. Wiki: deploying Workers with wrangler\n\nThis is a new file, `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/workers-deploy.md`, verified 2026-10-12. It covers the following:\n\n- **Custom domain over existing DNS records:** the deploy fails with error `100117` and the record has to be deleted first. The hostname has no DNS record until the next deploy succeeds.\n- **No DNS from wrangler:** it has no DNS command, and its OAuth token has only `zone (read)`.\n- **Partial trigger updates:** a failed trigger update is not rolled back. A config with `routes` and no `workers_dev` key turns workers.dev off, so a domain that fails to attach leaves the Worker with no URL.\n- **New workers.dev hostnames** answered 404 for a few seconds after being enabled.\n- **Secrets from stdin:** `wrangler secret bulk` and `secret put` read from stdin. Every secret change deploys a new version.\n- **Secrets survive `wrangler deploy`** under the same Worker name, until `wrangler secret delete`.\n- **Non-interactive shells:** `d1 create` and `r2 bucket create` print the binding snippet and don't edit the config. `d1 migrations apply --remote` confirms its own prompt.\n- **CI token permissions:** CI error `7403` came from a token with no D1 permission. After the token got D1 Edit and Workers Routes Edit, everything passed.\n\nThe Sources list has the custom domains docs, the secrets docs, and the 2026-10-12 production deploy.\n\n`cloudflare/INDEX.md` gets a new line between `vitest-plugin` and `workflows`: \"`workers-deploy`: deploying with wrangler: a custom domain over existing DNS records, partial trigger updates, secrets from stdin, and CI token permissions\".\n\n## 3. learn: pick the mode from the ask\n\nThis edits `mahou/skills/learn/SKILL.md`. The section \"Two modes\" becomes \"Modes\":\n\n> Pick the mode from what the user asks, not from whether there are arguments.\n>\n> - **Discovery.** Follow `references/discover.md` when the user asks for nothing specific, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\n> - **Directed.** Follow `references/directed.md` when the user names what to build. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\n> - **Mixed.** When the user names some items and also asks what else there is, work the named items as directed and run discovery over the part of the session the ask points at.\n>\n> Before starting, tell the user which mode you are following. For a mixed ask, list the items you work as directed and the part of the session discovery covers. Every mode continues with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\n\nThe edits that go with it:\n- **Skill description:** \"Without arguments… With arguments…\" becomes \"When the user asks what the session has to teach, it collects… When the user names what to build, it works that ask directly from the current context. A mixed ask gets both.\"\n- **`discover.md`, first line:** \"Used when the user asks for nothing specific, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. In a mixed ask, it covers only the part of the session the ask points at.\"\n- **`directed.md`, first line:** \"Used when the user names what to build, alone or as the named part of a mixed ask. The user has already decided what those items should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take on them.\"\n- **README, the `mahou:learn` line:** \"Collects the points where a session generated friction, takes your ask directly, or both, and proposes…\""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4011,"cache_read_input_tokens":229911,"output_tokens":1820,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":80},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4011,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1820,"cache_read_input_tokens":229911,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4011},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"11c76d74-307c-43e1-a7f8-ea45b7d6f7a1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwgqQ4XqnxrijkbcTZvA","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b449dda9-62dc-4097-9d6b-66a2884d895c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:10:07.582Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
