{"parentUuid":"92713db9-dda2-4a59-9853-b005bd91b123","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwhDvi8gGqxYb9dQfKM9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XKvks49RSKz9YrvDQuC9p1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins/mahou && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:60]); s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nW='skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/'\nedit(W+'ai-gateway.md',[\n(\"verified: 2026-10-10\",\"verified: 2026-10-12\"),\n(\"instead of directly: authentication, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, and from the AI Gateway docs.\",\n \"instead of directly: authentication, provider keys, caching, what the caller learns about cost, and what can be managed from the CLI. Distilled from a spike that called Gemini through a gateway from a deployed Worker, from a production Worker that calls Gemini and Workers AI through one gateway, and from the AI Gateway docs.\"),\n(\"- A gateway with authentication on requires a `cf-aig-authorization` header on every request.\\n\",\n \"- A gateway with authentication on requires a `cf-aig-authorization` header on every request.\\n- With a provider key stored on the gateway (BYOK), the caller holds no provider credential. The request carries only `cf-aig-authorization`, and the gateway adds the stored key before forwarding. A Gemini call through `google-ai-studio` with no `x-goog-api-key` header succeeded this way from a deployed Worker.\\n- A Workers AI model reached through the gateway's `workers-ai` provider authenticated with `cf-aig-authorization` alone, with no `Authorization` header.\\n\"),\n(\"- Spike, 2026-10-04: Gemini image description from a deployed Worker through a gateway, with the SDK and with plain `fetch`\",\n \"- Spike, 2026-10-04: Gemini image description from a deployed Worker through a gateway, with the SDK and with plain `fetch`\\n- Production run, 2026-10-12: Gemini through `google-ai-studio` with a stored provider key, and Workers AI through `workers-ai`, from a deployed Worker\"),\n])\nedit(W+'INDEX.md',[\n(\"calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, the cache header,\",\"calling a provider through a gateway: authentication, provider keys, the cache header,\"),\n(\"- [`workflows`]\",\"- [`workers-deploy`](workers-deploy.md): deploying with wrangler: a custom domain over existing DNS records, partial trigger updates, secrets from stdin, and CI token permissions\\n- [`workflows`]\"),\n])\nd=open('/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/cloudflare-migration/learn/round5/drafts.md').read()\nentry=d.split(\"New file `mahou/skills/wiki/references/cloudflare/workers-deploy.md`:\\n\\n```markdown\\n\")[1].split(\"\\n```\\n\")[0]+\"\\n\"\nopen(W+'workers-deploy.md','w').write(entry)\nL='skills/learn/'\nmodes=d.split(\"New:\\n\\n```markdown\\n## Modes\")[1].split(\"\\n```\\n\")[0]\nedit(L+'SKILL.md',[\n(\"## Two modes\\n\\nRoute on the arguments.\\n\\n- **No arguments.** Discovery. Follow `references/discover.md`. Collect the friction points, report each with a take, and wait for the user to pick what to keep.\\n- **Arguments given.** Directed. Follow `references/directed.md`. No summary and no take. The user has said what they want. Map the state their ask touches and work toward it.\\n\\nBoth modes continue with Drafting once there is an item to draft.\",\n \"## Modes\"+modes),\n(\"Without arguments it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks. With arguments it works the user's ask directly from the current context.\",\n \"When the user asks what the session has to teach, it collects the points where the session generated friction or changed the behavior of the flow that was running, gives a take on each, and drafts what the user picks. When the user names what to build, it works that ask directly from the current context. A mixed ask gets both.\"),\n])\nedit(L+'references/discover.md',[(\"Used when `learn` is invoked without arguments.\",\"Used when the user asks for nothing specific, or asks what the session, or a part of it, has to teach. In a mixed ask, it covers only the part of the session the ask points at.\")])\nedit(L+'references/directed.md',[(\"Used when `learn` is invoked with arguments. The user has already decided what the session should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take.\",\"Used when the user names what to build, alone or as the named part of a mixed ask. The user has already decided what those items should become. Do not summarize the session and do not give a take on them.\")])\nedit('README.md',[(\"Collects the points where a session generated friction (or takes your ask directly), and proposes\",\"Collects the points where a session generated friction, takes your ask directly, or both, and proposes\")])\nEOF\ngit -C /home/agus/workspace/asermax/claude-plugins status --short; sed -n '/^## Modes/,/^## Fidelity/p' skills/learn/SKILL.md","description":"Write the three approved learn items"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":238142,"output_tokens":1880,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1880,"cache_read_input_tokens":238142,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephem