092Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch","sessionId":"f14bad90-e61e-4c27-a38f-bf7cbc76465e","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"atomic-stirring-rossum"}
{"parentUuid":"a7b17744-3337-4478-a9f5-ffafce0685d7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"53e9dddf-02b3-4d2f-8ed3-cefa6eaaf42e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NPATrNSB4q5gNVu7AQBFrz","type":"tool_result","content":"learn-architecture-exploration/exploration.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/iterations.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/SKILL.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-new-rules.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-round1.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-round2b.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-round2.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-ruletest.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-sync.md\n\nlearn-architecture-exploration:\nexploration.md\niterations.md\nSKILL.md\nunslop-new-rules.md\nunslop-round1.md\nunslop-round2b.md\nunslop-round2.md\nunslop-ruletest.md\nunslop-sync.md\nwiki\n\nlearn-architecture-exploration/wiki:\ncloudflare\nmodal\nworkflows-iteration.md\n\nmarkdown-and-lists:\nbrief-api.md\nbrief-pipeline.md\n==> markdown-and-lists/brief-api.md <==\n<supervisor-agent>\n# Implement: markdown and lists, api/\n\n## The change\nRead first: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/article-extraction.md, the-describer.md, docs/product-design/what-gets-read-aloud.md (on this branch), and the settled design at /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/markdown-and-lists/design.md (branches 4 and 5, and program architecture 5).\nSummary: in api/app/service/extract.py, `to_spoken(display)` returns one string per unit with a newline between blocks (today the markdown-it walk joins inline tokens with \"\" so paragraphs and list items fuse: '- First item\\n- Second item' -> 'First itemSecond item'). Headings, quotes and the title unit ('# <title>', an ordinary paragraph unit the pipeline now prepends) read as their words; every paragraph and list item on its own line, no full stop added; an ordered item keeps its number at the start of its line ('3. Write the interface', honouring the list's start); nesting depth is not announced (nested lines in document order, inner numbering its own); an empty list item (a split list's resumed part, rendered compactly like '2.  3.  Item B.3') has no line; task checkboxes [x]/[ ] removed; strikethrough parsed (enable it in the MarkdownIt instance) and read as its words; a pipe table's header row on its own line, then each body row as 'Header: cell, …' on its own line; a soft wrap inside one paragraph stays a space. `sanitize_spoken` (shared with the describer, describe.py:91, and the table linearizer) keeps newlines (whitespace collapses only within a line), removes an emphasis/code marker only where it touches text (an asterisk between spaces, e.g. 'value_0 * 2', stays; run-in '**review.**Agents' still becomes 'review. Agents'), reduces tag shapes ('<software>', '</div>') to their word as today, then replaces operator sequences with words, longest match first: '<=' less than or equal to, '>=' greater than or equal to, '->' to, '=>' to, '<-' from, '<<' much less than, '>>' much greater than, '<3' heart, '<' less than, '>' greater than. The drop rule (is_unspeakable over the whole unit) and everything downstream (images, describer, TTS input list[str], timing) are unchanged; no migration.\nOut of scope: pipeline/, tts/, operators inside inline code, [x]/[ ] in prose, re-deriving stored items.\nReference only: the spike's spoken script at /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/markdown-and-lists/spikes/markdown-fidelity/spoken/.\n\n## Tasks, in order\n1. ASE-69: sanitize tail keeps newlines, strips only markers touching text, speaks operators (the walk's newline rules depend on the tail keeping newlines).\n2. ASE-68: line-based spoken derivation.\n\n## Test rows (verbatim)\n## B·1 the poll that resolves a completed job\n\n==> markdown-and-lists/brief-pipeline.md <==\n<supervisor-agent>\n# Implement: markdown and lists, pipeline/\n\n## The change\nRead first: /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/docs/technical-design/markdown-units.md, recipes.md, extraction-service.md (on this branch), and the settled design + program architecture at /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/markdown-and-lists/design.md.\nSummary: every recipe's `toMarkdown(element)` serializes the element WITH its own tag (today it uses cheerio `.html()`, the inner HTML, which drops the h2/blockquote/ol/table tag), wraps the content of a `<pre>` without a `<code>` child in `<code>`, and runs Turndown with the fixed config plus `@truto/turndown-plugin-gfm` (add it next to turndown 7.2.4; it reaches the sandbox through scripts/build-injection-bundle.mjs). In the SAME sandbox call, after the recipe returns, the runtime splits every declared paragraph unit whose element is an <ol>/<ul> holding a <pre>, <img>, <figure>, <picture> or <svg> at any depth into list part / code or image unit / list part in document order (each list part a clone in its own <ol>/<ul>, converted with the same converter; the part after continues start on ordered levels and opens with an empty <li> at each enclosing level so resumed items keep depth; an item whose only content was the block is not repeated; image unit src/alt read as the element carries them), then prepends a paragraph unit '# <title>' when the extracted title is not empty. The sandbox reply carries the title, the declared units (with paths, as today) and the flattened units. The host validates the DECLARED units exactly as today plus a new check: a declared unit whose own element is an <li> is a problem whose line names the unit (position and path), the list it belongs to, and the rule that a recipe hands a list over whole. Clean -> runRecipe returns the flattened units (the workflow and the agent extract tool both get them); problems -> the report, flattened discarded. The shared RECIPE_CONTRACT (pipeline/src/agents/prompts.ts, embedded by both author and revision instructions) gains these plain rules: markdown is GFM and the whole element goes to toMarkdown; a list is one unit even when it holds code or images; the runtime may split a unit into several and the extract tool shows the split result; a formula is its alttext as plain text with no delimiter; attributions (blockquote footer/cite), <dl>, footnotes, heading self-links and any heading repeating the title are left out through the recipe's includes and ignores; task-list checkboxes are kept.\nOut of scope: api/, tts/, the four stored recipes (ASE-70), lazy-load src resolution for split images, figure captions, a split that throws, empty list parts.\nReference only (never copy wholesale; build it clean): the spike's split at /home/agus/workspace/asermax/nagara/.scratch/markdown-and-lists/spikes/markdown-fidelity/runner/split.mjs and its findings-round-5.md (it hit a bug: a whitespace-only text node left after pulling a nested list out of an item became a spurious empty <li>).\n\n## Tasks, in order\n1. ASE-64: converter keeps the element's own tag, wraps a bare <pre>, GFM plugin in the bundle.\n2. ASE-65: list split, title unit, two-list sandbox reply, host returns flattened after validating declared.\n3. ASE-66: orphaned-<li> validator check.\n4. ASE-67: RECIPE_CONTRACT rules.\n\n\n==> markdown-and-lists/charter-review.md <==\n# Charter review: docs-draft\n\nScope: `technical-design/markdown-units.md` (new note, full review) and the six other files `CHANGES.md`\nlists as touched, diffed against their current `docs/` versions. Compared against\n`docs/README.md` (the charter), `docs/_templates/note.md`, and both folder `README.md` indexes.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"794c5bbb-e0c3-4816-be87-5c201805cea9","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.171Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"learn-architecture-exploration/exploration.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/iterations.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/SKILL.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-new-rules.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-round1.md\nlearn-architecture-exploration/unslop-round2b.md